window.QUESTIONS=[{"id":"P1","cat":"Product & definition","sub":"Definition","weight":"critical","q":"Does the one-sentence definition still call frontmatter a markdown editor, or does the noun change?","lede":"The noun names the one part of the codebase we did not write, and every page, demo and price is written against it.","visual":{"kind":"arch","layers":[{"label":"Owned","items":["src/modules/mdmax — 3,614 lines, 13 files","19 construct detectors, the splice writer"],"side":"1 symbol reaches product code","tone":"accent"},{"label":"Unbuilt","items":[".frontmatter/review.jsonl","per-span hash, reviewed-by, reviewed-at"],"side":"MVP-0","tone":"warn"},{"label":"Forked","items":["src/modules/editor, src/modules/app-shell","41 of 43 files byte-identical to sgnk-md"],"side":"0 files unique to us","tone":"sunk"}],"note":"Counts from docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:223 and the fix-first table at :217.","caption":"What the product owns, bottom-up. The noun names the top layer."},"stakes":"Pick the wrong noun and every downstream artefact points at a forked shell we do not own and cannot promise quality for.","state":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:20 defines it as \"a markdown editor for repositories whose documents are written by agents\".","41 of 43 editor and app-shell files are byte-identical to the sibling repo sgnk-md, and none is unique to frontmatter (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:223).","`src/modules/mdmax` is the only owned module, and one symbol from one of its thirteen files reaches product code (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:217).","Editing itself is now table stakes four times over: a free working-tree diff shipped in Claude Code, Antigravity, Codex and the VS Code Agents window."],"path":["The noun was chosen when the shell looked like an asset — \"88.6% of a shipping editor exists\" (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:557).","The 2026-09-08 round measured it and found a fork, with 25 of 226 files across `src/` already diverged (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:223).","The form factor underneath the noun, standalone or extension, is called the largest unreasoned decision in the plan (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:48)."],"tension":["The sentence promises editing quality a fork cannot guarantee and omits the engine, which is the only thing we wrote.","Keeping \"editor\" means paying a divergence tax that no exhibit carries a number for; it is prose at :223 and priced nowhere.","Changing the noun re-points every screen, price and channel, and \"review layer\" is a category with no search demand."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"What the codebase owns, re-counted in the tree 2026-09-09","items":[["Editor + app-shell files byte-identical to sgnk-md","41 of 43","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:223"],["Editor + app-shell files unique to frontmatter","0","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:223"],["Files across src/ already diverged from the sibling","25 of 226 (181 still identical)","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:223"],["Lines in src/modules/mdmax, the only owned module","3,614 across 13 files","verified: find src/modules/mdmax -name '*.ts' | wc -l → 13; cat | wc -l → 3614"],["Files outside mdmax that import it","2","verified: grep -rn 'modules/mdmax' src/ excluding the module itself"],["Distinct mdmax symbols reaching product code","1 (decodeStrict)","src/modules/vault/application/get-snapshot.ts:13 and src/modules/vault/infrastructure/search-index.ts:16"]]},{"type":"table","title":"The definition sentence, four versions in eleven days","cols":["Where","The noun and the claim","Status"],"rows":[["docs/DECIDE.md:59","\"a markdown editor for people who build software with AI\" — byte-exact editing","Superseded; byte-exactness refuted as a pitch, docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:174"],["docs/BRIEF.md:125","\"a markdown editor that knows which bytes a machine wrote\"","Superseded; authorship did not sell as a consumer feature, docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:175"],["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:20","\"a markdown editor for repositories whose documents are written by agents\"","Current, and labelled a failing hypothesis on line 22"],["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:27","\"nobody persists review state across people and across tools on a working tree with no pull request\"","What survived the attack; not yet the headline"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Keep \"markdown editor\" and budget the fork tax as a line item","what":"The sentence stays as written and the divergence between the two repos becomes a costed, tracked item.","gains":["Familiar noun; the free-editor distribution story survives intact","Nothing downstream has to be rewritten this week"],"costs":["Every table-stakes day is a fork tax or an upstream merge, and neither is estimated","Promises the one thing we did not build"],"system":"No change to code; adds a recurring merge obligation against sgnk-md.","screens":"None.","money":"Unpriced engineering time on a shell that is not the product."},{"k":"b","label":"Change the noun to the engine and the state, shipped inside an editor","what":"\"A review layer for markdown written by agents\" — the editor becomes the shell, not the promise.","gains":["Names the only owned code and stops selling editing quality","Survives the fork finding and the narrowing in P2 together"],"costs":["An unfamiliar category with no search demand","Weakens the free-editor funnel argument in the product family"],"system":"No engine change; the sidecar becomes the headline object.","screens":"First-run copy and the landing pages are rewritten.","money":"None directly; slower organic search."},{"k":"c","label":"Merge sgnk-md and frontmatter into one codebase, then write the sentence","what":"One repo, one name, one shell, and the editor noun becomes honest again.","gains":["Removes the divergence tax at source","Makes \"editor\" a claim we can stand behind"],"costs":["A merge before any user-facing work, at 1.21 engineering days per week (:227)","The merge itself has never been estimated"],"system":"One codebase; the Tauri identity fix at fix-first item 9 folds into it.","screens":"None immediately.","money":"Unknown weeks before anything is shown to anyone."},{"k":"d","label":"Defer the noun until the form-factor decision resolves","what":"No sentence is written until standalone-versus-extension is settled.","gains":["Avoids writing the same sentence twice","Form factor genuinely determines the noun"],"costs":["Nothing downstream can be written, and the weeks 1–2 pages need copy now","Defers rather than decides"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None built.","money":"None."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["The sentence should name what we own, and we own the engine and the sidecar, not the shell.","One symbol from one of thirteen owned files reaches product code today — a gap to close, not an asset to sell (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:217).","Option b keeps the editor as the container without making editing the promise, which is the only reading that survives both the fork finding and P2's narrowing."],"flip":"If the merge in option c is genuinely one week, do it first and \"editor\" becomes honest again. Ask what it costs before the room votes.","linked":["P2"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:20","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:27","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:223","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:557","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:48","docs/DECIDE.md:59","docs/BRIEF.md:125","src/modules/vault/application/get-snapshot.ts:13","src/modules/vault/infrastructure/search-index.ts:16"],"dupes":{"dropped":["G13"],"why":"Is 'markdown editor' the product's noun. P1(a)=G13(b) keep it, P1(b)=G13(c) change the category noun; recs b vs a. Product & definition owns the definition. G13's public-versus-internal split is a sub-answer, not a separate decision."}},{"id":"P2","cat":"Product & definition","sub":"Definition","weight":"critical","q":"Does review state stay the headline, narrow to per-span state kept in the repo, or does something else lead?","lede":"Three of the four claims became table stakes in nine weeks, and the read-receipt half of this one has a corpse with $45M behind it.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":150,"cols":[{"title":"See what the agent changed","tone":"stop"},{"title":"Know what nobody reviewed","tone":"warn"},{"title":"Which text the agent wrote","tone":"accent"}],"rows":[{"label":"Shipped free by","cells":["Claude Code, Antigravity, Codex, VS Code","VS Code, per file, merged 2026-07-03","Nobody"]},{"label":"Dated","cells":["v2.1.260, published 2026-09-03","Milestone 1.128.0, undocumented","One extension, 88 installs"]},{"label":"Precedent","cells":["petergyang/human-review: 1,241 stars in 6 weeks","Almanac sold it, raised $45M, shut 2025-01-31","iA Writer 8: typed versus pasted, personal docs"]},{"label":"Left to us","cells":["Nothing","Per-span, in the repo, across tools and machines","The whole claim, and we cannot deliver it yet"]}],"note":"Almanac totals are from a podcast summary, not the founder's own writing.","caption":"Where each of the four claims stands on 9 September 2026."},"stakes":"Lead with a sentence four free tools already satisfy and the first person in the room refutes it by opening their own editor.","state":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:20 leads with review state; line 22 labels it a hypothesis whose test has already gone against it.","\"See what the agent changed\" is free in four places, the newest being Claude Code v2.1.260, published 2026-09-03.","VS Code merged a per-file review/unreview operation on 2026-07-03, milestone 1.128.0, gated behind a setting and absent from its public docs.","What survives is narrow and already written at docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:27: state that persists across people and across tools on a working tree with no pull request."],"path":["Review state was synthesised from the refutations of the previous three headlines and was never itself attacked (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:21).","The 2026-09-08 round attacked it and came back negative with one narrowed survivor (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:124).","Almanac shipped this whole feature sentence, read receipts and approvals included, raised $45M, and switched off on 2025-01-31.","Three headline arms were named for the weeks 1–2 test at :296 and none carries a pass mark (merged from P22)."],"tension":["The general document form is Almanac's and is dead; the narrow form is unclaimed and has never been shown to anyone.","Thirteen purpose-built markdown-review extensions sum to 1,217 installs, ceiling 400 (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:24).","Attribution is the only one of the four claims nobody shipped, and it is the one we cannot deliver until writes carry provenance (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:65).","Three arms split a ten-person sample three ways, which decides nothing without a number written in advance."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"What the attack returned, 2026-09-08","items":[["Reactions on the request cited as the demand signal","266","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:23 — anthropics/claude-code#33932"],["Of its 36 texts, how many ask for anything to persist","0","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:23"],["Of its 36 texts, how many name a tool that already does it","18","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:23"],["Times \"markdown\" appears in those 36 texts","1","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:23"],["Purpose-built markdown-review VS Code extensions that already exist","13, summing to 1,217 installs, ceiling 400","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:24"],["Installs of mddiff, which is this sentence shipped 2026-06-03","74","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:24"],["Corpus discrepancy to settle before quoting the reaction count","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:23 says 266; docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:21 says 262 for the same issue","Pick one and re-check the issue before it goes on a slide"]]},{"type":"bars","title":"Obsidian forum, one population, one metric, read 2026-09-08","note":"The closest existing request to review state, against the rendering bug the plan treats as a week-2 channel. docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:25 and :410.","data":[["Review state request — likes",0],["\"Tracking changes within notes\" — likes",1],["\"Suggestion mode like Google Docs\" — likes",3],["Nested-construct rendering bug — likes",501]],"unit":"forum likes"},{"type":"table","title":"The arms and what already stands behind each","cols":["Arm","Supporting evidence","Contradicting evidence"],"rows":[["See what the AI wrote","None found for consumers","iA Writer 7 shipped it 2023; 208-download Obsidian port; best VS Code extension 366 installs; 0 asks in the top twenty Reddit posts — docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:175, :296"],["See what the agent changed without asking","The upvoted pain matches it — docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:296","The 266-reaction request asks for a per-session panel; 18 of 36 texts name a tool that already does it — docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:23"],["Know what nobody has reviewed yet","The upvoted pain matches it; it is the narrowed survivor — docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:27","Obsidian forum: closest request 0 likes, 1 post in nearly three years — docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:410"],["Your checklist is green because the agent ticked it","354 of 355 boxes ticked by the agent across a 20-file sample; population 49,664; reviewer-owned checklist 11× rarer","Untested as a headline — docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:306"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"What the weeks 1–2 tests currently specify","items":[["Developers shown the review mock in both framings","10","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:352"],["Landing pages","3","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:352"],["Team conversations on seats and gating","20","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:352"],["People shown the S2 screenshot for five seconds","5","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:352"],["Kill signal stated for the product","Under 4 of 10 unprompted","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:321"],["Kill signal stated per arm","None","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:296"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Confirm review state as the headline and test it unchanged","what":"The plan stands and the weeks 1–2 pages carry today's sentence.","gains":["Every downstream artefact stays usable","No copy work this week"],"costs":["Page one of the plan carries a refutation of itself","Thirteen shipped products at a 400-install ceiling say the market was tested"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Narrow it: per-span state kept in the repo, across people, tools and machines","what":"The claim shrinks to the one shape nothing observed reaches, and the sidecar in the repository is the differentiator.","gains":["True, checkable, and unoccupied by any incumbent","Stops the pitch colliding with GitHub Viewed, Google's blue dot and VS Code's marker"],"costs":["A much smaller statement, invisible without a second person and a second tool","The pilot's ten strangers may have neither"],"system":"The sidecar must survive an out-of-band write, which is still open (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:146).","screens":"The review panel becomes a cross-person list, not a per-session diff.","money":"None today; it is what a team seat would be sold on."},{"k":"c","label":"Lead with attribution — which text the agent wrote","what":"Authorship of spans becomes the headline and review state the mechanism beneath it.","gains":["The only one of the four claims nobody has shipped","Google sells the span-level half today, at our intended tier"],"costs":["We can only show what the write carried; prompts need F11 MCP, MVP-1 and untested (:65)","Reverses a documented demotion made on consumer evidence"],"system":"Forces F11 MCP and commit-trailer readers forward from MVP-1.","screens":"The hover card becomes the primary surface, not a detail.","money":"Puts a live paid precedent behind the team tier."},{"k":"d","label":"Demote review state and lead with spec-kit self-certification","what":"\"Your checklist is green because the agent ticked it\" becomes the entry line.","gains":["Built on a measured fact: 354 of 355 boxes ticked by the agent (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:306)","Needs no feature that is not already planned"],"costs":["Points at one toolchain of 11,072 repos (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:148)","Needs a different demo and a different first screen"],"system":"No change.","screens":"The launcher leads with the scan, not the tint.","money":"None."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["Option b is the only version the 2026-09-08 round left standing, and the plan already writes it that way at :27 and :559.","Narrowing costs nothing today because nothing is built.","Per-span, stored in the repository rather than in editor workspace state, is the one shape nothing observed reaches — including VS Code's own marker.","Whichever sentence leads, write the pass mark before the test runs; the exit measure has one at docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:22 and the headline test has none."],"flip":"If fewer than 4 of 10 developers name unreviewed agent edits unprompted, the kill line at docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:321, then c or d becomes the honest lead.","linked":["F3","G1","MK27","P11","P24"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:22","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:23","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:24","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:27","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:321","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:363","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:410","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:559","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:21","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:124","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:138","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:175","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:296","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:306","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:352","docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:22","merged: P22","https://raw.githubusercontent.com/anthropics/claude-code/main/CHANGELOG.md","https://get.almanac.io/go-forward","https://api.github.com/repos/petergyang/human-review"],"dupes":{"dropped":["MK1"],"why":"Does review state stay the headline, narrow to per-span state kept in the repo, or step aside for authorship. Near-verbatim, both rec (b). Product & definition owns the one-sentence definition."}},{"id":"P11","cat":"Product & definition","sub":"Demo","weight":"critical","q":"Which demo do we build, and does it run on a repository the viewer chose?","lede":"The plan and the critique specify two different demos, and the current one opens a file we generated in a repo we control.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":150,"cols":[{"title":"Fifteen-second tint","tone":"warn"},{"title":"Rejection, byte-identical","tone":"stop"},{"title":"Their own repo","tone":"accent"}],"rows":[{"label":"Whose file","cells":["One we generated moments before","One we prepared","Theirs, unstaged"]},{"label":"What it proves","cells":["Review state exists","A rejected hunk is byte-identical","Their folder has named problems"]},{"label":"Cost","cells":["18 days: store, render, revert, panel","0 for us; Zed ships it","No new capability needed"]},{"label":"Who already ships it","cells":["Four free agent tools show the diff","Zed, per hunk, documented","Nobody"]},{"label":"Survives the falsifier","cells":["Unknown","No","It is the falsifier"]}],"note":"Costs from docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:56; the third demo from docs/CRITIQUE.md:715 and docs/PRODUCT.md:900.","caption":"Three demos, and the only one nobody else can run."},"stakes":"A demo that works only on prepared files fails at week 12 for a reason it was designed to hide.","state":["The plan's demo begins \"Run the agent's spec command\", so the file is generated by the demonstrator (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:45).","It is the week 8–9 deliverable and costs 18 days of store, rendering, revert and panel (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:356, :56).","docs/CRITIQUE.md:715 proposed the alternative: point it at the prospect's own repo and print what will not survive.","No rule about demo files exists anywhere in the plan (merged from P12)."],"path":["The earlier demo was a rejection — reject a hunk, show the file is byte-identical (docs/DECIDE.md:75).","That one was refuted because Zed ships per-hunk accept and reject verbatim (docs/CRITIQUE.md:408).","docs/CRITIQUE.md:386 wrote the falsifier: ten strangers, their own repositories, unstaged, and 6 of 10 must notice a difference unprompted."],"tension":["The differentiation is real and conditional on an adversarial file, so demonstrating it means handing over a file crafted to break a competitor (docs/CRITIQUE.md:382).","The exit test at :357 uses ten strangers with their own repos, where no prepared files exist.","The falsifier sits at day 41 and the critique says run it at day 5 with a rough prototype."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"Three demos, and what each proves","cols":["Demo","Where specified","What it proves","What it costs"],"rows":[["Fifteen-second tint","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:45","That review state exists on a spec the demo just generated","Store 6d, rendering 5d, revert 3d, panel 4d = 18d — docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:56"],["Rejection / byte-identical","docs/DECIDE.md:75","That a rejected hunk is byte-identical","Shipped by Zed verbatim; \"0 days for the demo\" for them — docs/CRITIQUE.md:408"],["Import / verification report on the prospect's own repo","docs/CRITIQUE.md:715, docs/PRODUCT.md:900","That their existing folder has named, countable problems","Needs NF-1, the splice return shape and a padEnd fix — no new capability, per docs/PRODUCT.md:900"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"What the demo has to overcome","items":[["Purpose-built markdown-review extensions already shipping the tint idea","13, summing to 1,217 installs, ceiling 400","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:24"],["Zed's shipped per-hunk accept/reject","\"accept or reject each individual change hunk\"","docs/CRITIQUE.md:377"],["git add -p installs inside Obsidian alone","3,075,875","docs/CRITIQUE.md:379"],["Falsifier already written","≥6 of 10 strangers notice a difference on their own repo, unstaged, no CRLF setup","docs/CRITIQUE.md:386"],["Files the byte claim is verified against","8,513, of which one wiki is 77%","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:296, :514"],["The counter-argument the corpus states against itself","Deterministic projections out-install every AI capability combined by 7.25×, and the import-report cut puts boards and calendars fourth","docs/PRODUCT.md:902"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"The falsifier already written into the corpus, and when it is scheduled","items":[["The test","Hand ten strangers their own real repository and the binary, unstaged, with no CRLF setup","docs/CRITIQUE.md:386"],["Pass condition","≥6 of 10 spontaneously notice a difference from their current tool, without being shown the corrupted-file comparison","docs/CRITIQUE.md:386"],["Where it currently sits","DECIDE §9's day-41 test; the critique says run it at day 5 with a prototype instead","docs/CRITIQUE.md:386"],["Where the plan puts the equivalent","Weeks 10–12, ten strangers, 6 of 10 by the week-0 measure","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:357"],["What the pilot's ten users bring","Their own repos and their own agents — no prepared files exist","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:231"],["Corpus the fidelity claims rest on","Seven Obsidian vaults; one wiki is 77% of 8,513 files","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:514"]]},{"type":"table","title":"What each demo needs from the file, and whether the pilot supplies it","cols":["Demo","File it needs to land","Does a stranger's repo supply it?"],"rows":[["Fifteen-second tint (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:45)","A spec the agent just generated, in our repo","No — the stranger's agent must have written something they have not read"],["Rejection / byte-identical (docs/DECIDE.md:75)","Any file, but the difference is invisible unless it is CRLF or deeply nested","Sometimes — and only 83% of foreign vaults hit a refusal at all (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:214)"],["Repo report (docs/CRITIQUE.md:715)","Any existing folder of markdown","Yes — that is the whole design"],["Any of them, on a file we prepared","A file crafted to break the competitor","Not applicable — and docs/CRITIQUE.md:382 says the room knows"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Build the fifteen-second tint demo as specified","what":"Generate a spec, open it, show every paragraph tinted, revert one, show the panel.","gains":["Shows the headline feature directly","If P2 confirms review state, this is the only demo that matches the pitch"],"costs":["18 days before there is anything to show","Runs on a file we generated in a repo we control"],"system":"Needs the store, rendering, revert and panel complete.","screens":"S2 tint and S4 review panel.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Build the repo report first, on the viewer's own folder, and adopt it as a rule","what":"Open the stranger's repository and print what is stale, broken, missing and what will not render the same.","gains":["Checkable in five seconds against a folder they already own","Needs no model and no new capability (docs/PRODUCT.md:900)"],"costs":["Demonstrates the scan, not review state, so headline and demo point at different features","Some repos will show nothing and we have to say so"],"system":"Needs NF-1, the splice return shape and the padEnd fix.","screens":"S13 repo docs scan becomes the cold open.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Build both: the report as cold open, the tint as the second beat","what":"The report earns attention and the tint carries the claim.","gains":["Attention and claim in one sitting","Covers the case where P2 confirms the headline"],"costs":["Largest scope, at 1.21 engineering days per calendar week","No longer fifteen seconds, and the weaker half is remembered"],"system":"Both paths must be finished.","screens":"S13 then S2.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Build no demo until weeks 1–2 pick the headline; test on mocks","what":"The S2 screenshot and the three landing pages carry the tests.","gains":["Avoids building a demo for a headline that may be demoted","Mock tests are already scheduled at :352"],"costs":["Defers a decision rather than making one","The demo is already a week 8–9 item, so little changes"],"system":"No change.","screens":"Mocks only.","money":"None."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["The one demo nobody else can run opens the prospect's own repository and says something specific and unflattering about it.","The corpus argued for it twice independently (docs/CRITIQUE.md:715, docs/PRODUCT.md:900) and it needs no new capability.","Adopting it as a rule changes what gets built, because the product then has to be visible on ordinary files rather than adversarial ones.","It also aligns the demo with the exit test at :357, where no prepared files exist."],"flip":"If P2 confirms review state unchanged, the demo must show the headline and c becomes the requirement rather than the luxury.","linked":["F7","P2"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:24","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:45","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:56","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:356","docs/DECIDE.md:75","docs/CRITIQUE.md:377","docs/CRITIQUE.md:386","docs/CRITIQUE.md:408","docs/CRITIQUE.md:715","docs/PRODUCT.md:900","docs/PRODUCT.md:902","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:214","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:231","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:357","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:514","docs/CRITIQUE.md:382","merged: P12"]},{"id":"P13","cat":"Product & definition","sub":"Projection law","weight":"critical","q":"Does the projection law survive the review sidecar, and how many stores outside the file are allowed?","lede":"The founding law says every view owns no state; the headline feature is a store beside the file, and six stores have accumulated.","visual":{"kind":"arch","layers":[{"label":"Contradicted","items":["shares store: firestore.rules, public route"],"side":"delete under P8","tone":"stop"},{"label":"Ours","items":["control plane: identity, teams, entitlements, billing"],"side":"one","tone":"neutral"},{"label":"Theirs, in the repo","items":[".frontmatter/review.jsonl · usage.jsonl",".frontmatter/state.json · comments sidecar"],"side":"one directory","tone":"accent"},{"label":"The file","items":["the document bytes, the only source of truth"],"side":"the law","tone":"sunk"}],"note":"Introduced at docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:135, :64, :133, docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:20 and docs/THESIS.md:837.","caption":"Every store outside the document, counted together for the first time."},"stakes":"By our own admission gate the headline feature fails the law we also use as the category sentence.","state":["The law: every app-like thing is a projection \"owning no state of its own\" (docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:267).","The G2 gate fails a feature that \"needs a sidecar, an index, a `.base`-equivalent, or a row in the control plane\" (docs/THESIS.md:820).","F2 is specified as `.frontmatter/review.jsonl` beside the files (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:135).","Six stores now exist across the plan and the tree, each introduced separately and never added up (merged from P14)."],"path":["The law was written when the product was an editor with projections, before review state became the headline.","The record already conceded a sidecar once, for tree sort state (docs/THESIS.md:837).","Putting the state in the file is ruled out on evidence: every in-file annotation syntax renders as garbage on GitHub (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:64)."],"tension":["Either the law is amended in writing or the product ships in violation of a law it also sells as a category sentence.","The differentiator is precisely that the state is in the repository rather than in editor workspace state, so the sidecar is the point, not a lapse.","Without a stated cap, the seventh store is added the way the first six were."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"The law, the gate, and the feature","cols":["Artefact","What it says","Citation"],"rows":[["The law","Every app-like thing is a projection \"owning no state of its own\"","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:267"],["G2, the entailment gate","Fails if it \"needs a sidecar, an index, a `.base`-equivalent, or a row in the control plane\"","docs/THESIS.md:820"],["Dashboards, refused under the law","\"a view with no file behind it — the exact thing the projection law forbids\"","docs/THESIS.md:857"],["Saved searches, redesigned by G2","Admitted only because the saved search is itself a .md file whose frontmatter holds the query","docs/THESIS.md:836"],["Sort/group on the tree, admitted anyway","Passes only as palette plus `.frontmatter/state.json` — a sidecar already conceded once","docs/THESIS.md:837"],["F2 review state","Per-span hashes in `.frontmatter/review.jsonl` beside the files","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:135"],["Why not in the file","\"every in-file syntax renders as garbage on GitHub\"","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:64"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"What the sidecar is and what is still unknown about it","items":[["Format","One JSON line per span: path, byte start, byte end, content hash, reviewed-by, reviewed-at, and when known author, model, prompt","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:135"],["Anchor","Byte range plus content hash, relocated by the splice locator on every edit","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:135"],["Why the journal cannot be the anchor","\"git, other editors and agents bypass it\"","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:135"],["Nearest shipped pattern","SpecKit Companion's .spec-context.json, 9,367 installs","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:135"],["Whether the anchor survives an out-of-band write","Still open after round 2 — \"the only scenario the product exists for\"","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:146"]]},{"type":"table","title":"Every store outside the document, as currently planned or shipped","cols":["Store","What it holds","Where introduced","Status"],"rows":[[".frontmatter/review.jsonl","Per-span hash, reviewed-by, reviewed-at, and when known author, model, prompt","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:135","Planned, MVP-0, unbuilt"],[".frontmatter/usage.jsonl","Days opened, docs opened, spans reviewed, proposals accepted","docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:20","Drafted, week 0"],["Comments sidecar","Comments anchored to spans, never in the file","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:64","Planned, MVP-1"],[".frontmatter/state.json","Sort and group state on the tree","docs/THESIS.md:837","Ratified in the record, absent from the plan"],["Control plane","Identity, team membership, entitlements, billing, GitHub App installation id","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:133; docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:49","Planned"],["shares / public slug","Slug, title, content snapshot, visibility","firestore.rules:78; src/app/(public)/[slug]/page.tsx","Rules committed, route wired and live"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"What the architecture claims, against what the tree does","items":[["Plan's claim","\"The control plane holds… no document bytes\"","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:133"],["Week-0 draft's claim","\"No document byte ever passes through a Zephyrus server\"","docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:35"],["Shipped reality","Public page reads the repo server-side with one operator token","src/container/dependency-container.ts:140, src/config/env.ts:85"],["Stores counted together anywhere in the plan","0 — no exhibit lists them","verified: no such exhibit in docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Amend the law and cap the stores at two: one repo directory, one control plane","what":"Content has one source of truth; exactly one plain-text sidecar directory may hold review state, and one control plane holds the account.","gains":["The headline feature becomes legal under a named, bounded exception","States honestly in one sentence what each side holds"],"costs":["The category sentence gains a clause, and the clause is what a competitor quotes back","Presumes P8 removes the shares store"],"system":"A CI check that no new persistent store is added outside the two.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Keep the law absolute and put review state in the file","what":"No sidecar, no exception, no clause.","gains":["The law stays as written","Nothing new to explain"],"costs":["Ruled out on measured evidence: in-file syntax renders as garbage on GitHub (:64)","Breaks the still-renders-everywhere rule at :527"],"system":"An in-file annotation syntax the engine must write and strip.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Drop the projection law from the product's language; keep it as engineering","what":"The contradiction disappears because the law stops being a public claim.","gains":["Costs no engineering and removes the contradiction entirely","No clause for a competitor to quote"],"costs":["Loses the category sentence at docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:297","Removes the only sentence that puts the product in a category"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Re-run the G2 gate on F2 formally and publish the result either way","what":"The record's own process is applied to the feature it was written before.","gains":["Honest, and it is the process designed for this case","Settles it on the record rather than by assertion"],"costs":["On the text at :820 F2 fails, which puts the meeting back at Decision 1 with no headline","Costs a round with no product change"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["The law is worth keeping, because it is the only sentence that puts the product in a category, and the amendment is small and testable.","One sidecar directory, plain text; deleting it loses review state and no content.","Two stores is the smallest number that stays true once billing exists, and it turns into a CI check the repo has to build anyway.","The record already conceded a sidecar once at :837, so this formalises a breach rather than opening one."],"flip":"If the anchor cannot survive an out-of-band write, still open at docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:146, the sidecar projects nothing and c is honest.","linked":["F1","L1","P2"],"sources":["docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:267","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:297","docs/THESIS.md:820","docs/THESIS.md:836","docs/THESIS.md:837","docs/THESIS.md:857","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:64","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:135","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:527","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:146","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:133","docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:20","docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:35","docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:49","firestore.rules:78","src/config/env.ts:85","src/container/dependency-container.ts:140","merged: P14"]},{"id":"P3","cat":"Product & definition","sub":"Abandoned headlines","weight":"high","q":"Does byte-exactness come back into the pitch, stay a silent mechanism, or leave the copy entirely?","lede":"The only claim a stranger can check in five seconds against their own folder, and no vendor has taught a buyer to want it.","visual":{"kind":"ba","before":{"title":"A tool that reformats on write","lines":[{"t":"line 12: the requested change","mark":"="},{"t":"line 40: blank line doubled","mark":"+"},{"t":"every line: carriage return destroyed","mark":"-"}]},"after":{"title":"A byte-range splice","lines":[{"t":"line 12: the requested change","mark":"="},{"t":"every other byte identical","mark":"="}]},"via":"splice, or refuse","note":"Cursor staff call the left-hand column a known issue they are tracking (docs/DECIDE.md:35).","caption":"Real, invisible on an ordinary file, and below the category's floor."},"stakes":"Promote it and the demo needs a file crafted to break a named competitor; drop it and the only checkable claim goes.","state":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:174 rules it \"Mechanism, not pitch\" on 4 complaints in 12,556.","It survives as a proof line under whichever headline wins: `git diff` after an edit shows the change and nothing else (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:296).","Nobody in the thirty-year redlining category sells below word level; Word's own API offers character and word and stops there.","Word-level prose diff has been free in git since 2006 as `--color-words`."],"path":["It was the founding headline (docs/DECIDE.md:59) and was refuted on demand: 1 formatting-caused switch found in eleven years (docs/DECIDE.md:27).","docs/DECIDE.md:35 confirmed the defect is real and admitted by an incumbent's own staff.","docs/CRITIQUE.md:382 then priced the demo: the difference is invisible unless the file is adversarial."],"tension":["Demand is 0.03% of the measured complaint base and the defect is real and on the record in a competitor's words.","Byte granularity is genuinely below the floor the category sells at, so there is no buyer trained to ask for it.","Publishing any fidelity number drags the 83% refusal rate along with it, by the plan's own rule at :516."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"Demand for byte-exactness, counted","items":[["Complaints about mangled formatting in editor comments","4 of 12,556","docs/DECIDE.md:27"],["In launch comments","1 of 3,749","docs/DECIDE.md:27"],["\"line endings\" in GitHub issue titles","1 of 43,656","docs/DECIDE.md:27"],["Formatting-caused switches found in eleven years","1","docs/DECIDE.md:27"],["Files the byte-exactness claim is verified on each release","8,513, of which one wiki is 77%","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:296, :514"],["The incumbents' admitted defect","Cursor staff: doubled blank lines and destroyed CRs on CRLF, \"a known issue we're tracking\"","docs/DECIDE.md:35"]]},{"type":"table","title":"Where the mechanism is visible and where it is not","cols":["Session-one file","What frontmatter shows","What the user already has"],"rows":[["LF, ASCII, flat, 2 hunks","a reviewable diff","Zed: accept or reject each individual change hunk — docs/CRITIQUE.md:377"],["Same, inside Obsidian","nothing new","4,165,249 cumulative downloads across four AI plugins — docs/CRITIQUE.md:378"],["Same, in a git repo","a byte-identical rejected file","git diff / git add -p, installed 3,075,875 times inside Obsidian alone — docs/CRITIQUE.md:379"],["CRLF, or nested fence-in-callout-in-list, or a 6-file change","a real, unmatched difference","nothing equivalent — docs/CRITIQUE.md:380"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Keep it where it is — one proof line under the headline, never the headline","what":"One sentence under whatever leads, with the corpus caveat attached.","gains":["Costs nothing and keeps the one five-second checkable claim","Matches the demand evidence exactly"],"costs":["A proof line nobody reads does no work","Leaves the strongest engineering unsold"],"system":"No change.","screens":"One line on the landing page.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Promote it to a co-headline for the technical audience","what":"Lead the developer-facing page with corruption, paired with the incumbents' admitted defect.","gains":["A claim no competitor can make","The defect is documented in their own words"],"costs":["A defect claim about named companies","Demand for it is 4 complaints in 12,556 (docs/DECIDE.md:27)"],"system":"No change.","screens":"A second landing page for the technical arm.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Remove it from user-facing copy; keep it as a constraint and a test","what":"The engine property stays; the sentence goes.","gains":["Shortens the pitch and drops a claim nobody asks for","No exposure on a fidelity number"],"costs":["Loses the only claim a stranger can check against their own folder","Leaves the demo with nothing verifiable in it"],"system":"No change; the corpus test stays in CI.","screens":"One line removed.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Keep it, and publish fidelity and refusal rate as one fraction","what":"The claim is re-scoped to the constructs it is measured on and the refusal rate sits beside it.","gains":["Defensible against the first person who checks","Already required by the plan's own rule at :516"],"costs":["Publishing an 83% refusal rate next to a fidelity claim (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:214)","Both numbers are properties of seven Obsidian vaults (:514)"],"system":"The corpus run has to emit both numbers together.","screens":"A methodology note beside the claim.","money":"None."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["The measurement is real, the demand is not, and the plan already put it in the right slot.","One sentence preserves the only claim a stranger can check against their own folder.","Option d is not really optional: the moment any fidelity number is published, :516 says the refusal rate goes next to it."],"flip":"If every headline arm fails in weeks 1–2 and corruption is what people react to, option b is the fallback.","linked":["E5","P11"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:174","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:214","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:296","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:514","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:516","docs/DECIDE.md:27","docs/DECIDE.md:35","docs/DECIDE.md:59","docs/CRITIQUE.md:377","docs/CRITIQUE.md:382","https://www.diffchecker.com/pricing/"]},{"id":"P7","cat":"Product & definition","sub":"Boundary","weight":"high","q":"Which refusal list is the public one, and does each refusal carry a published reversal price?","lede":"Refusals are the positioning, and the plan's list and the record's list are different lists that have never been laid side by side.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":170,"cols":[{"title":"Plan §1, line 43","tone":"warn"},{"title":"Record §103.3","tone":"accent"}],"rows":[{"label":"Plugins, code execution","cells":["Refused, no price","Refused; reverses at 1,000 paying users"]},{"label":"Project management","cells":["Refused, no price","Refused; nothing reverses it"]},{"label":"Chat sidebar","cells":["Refused, no price","Refused; under 20% acceptance at 90 days"]},{"label":"Hosting user content","cells":["Refused","Not listed — and a public route ships today"]},{"label":"Live cursors, multiplayer","cells":["Missing","Refused; 3 of first 20 teams cancel on presence"]},{"label":"Mobile editor","cells":["Refused in v1","Admitted, with its own budget of 4 controls"]}],"note":"Record entries at docs/THESIS.md:852–858; mobile admitted at :843.","caption":"Two lists, one contradiction, and four missing reversal prices."},"stakes":"A refusal announced and then quietly reversed costs more than never announcing it.","state":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:43 states six refusals; docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:298 makes the list the positioning.","The record's list is seven, each with a written reversal condition (docs/THESIS.md:852–858), and the plan carries none of them.","Mobile is refused by the plan and admitted by the record with its own budget (docs/THESIS.md:843).","Two of the plan's own additions are contradicted by artefacts in the tree today (P8)."],"path":["Each refusal was decided in its own section, against its own evidence, months apart.","The record's seven were ratified as the feature-admission rule with numeric reversal prices attached.","The plan's six-item line was assembled later and independently, keeping three and dropping four (merged from P17)."],"tension":["Some items are company identity and some are roadmap, and the list presents them as one kind of thing.","Publishing a reversal price names the number at which a principle is for sale, which a competitor can quote back.","Not publishing one lets the first hard customer conversation decide the order for us."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"The two refusal lists, compared","cols":["Refusal","In plan §1 line 43","In record §103.3","Reversal condition on record"],"rows":[["Plugins / code execution","Yes","Yes (:853)","Capability model with no fs/network/eval, plus a published audit; not before 1,000 paying users"],["Project management","Yes","Yes (:852)","\"Nothing reverses it\" — a company-identity constraint, to be said publicly"],["Chat sidebar","Yes","Yes (:855)","<20% strong acceptance across all verbs at 90 days"],["Hosting user content","Yes","Not listed","None written — and the code ships a wired public route (P8)"],["Vendor database of document bytes","Yes","Not listed","None written — and firestore.rules designs one (P9)"],["Mobile editor in v1","Yes","Admitted, not refused (:843: ADMIT with its own V0 ≤ 4)","Direct conflict between the two documents"],["Live cursors / real-time multiplayer","Missing","Yes (:854)","≥3 of the first 20 paying teams cancel citing presence by name"],["Template galleries","Missing","Yes (:856)","\"Where do I get templates\" a top-3 support string for two quarters — and even then the answer is a git repo"],["Dashboards","Missing","Yes (:857)","Never as a screen; a dashboard file is already legal today"],["Anything with its own configuration surface","Missing","Yes (:858)","Only a default wrong for a majority cohort"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"What one refusal is worth as deflection, measured on the closest analogue","items":[["Obsidian forum topics tagged to the plugin surface","7,076 of 31,048 tagged topics = 22.79%","docs/BUSINESS.md:808"],["Just dataview + templater, the two that require code execution","4,243 topics = 13.67%","docs/BUSINESS.md:809"],["Support load per install, code-execution plugins vs ecosystem average","2.78×","docs/BUSINESS.md:811"],["Warning attached to that number by its own author","Do not quote 22.79% as a share of our future tickets — it establishes the class exists and is large, not its size for us","docs/BUSINESS.md:819"]]},{"type":"table","title":"Each refusal, what it costs us, and what would reverse it","cols":["Refusal","Measured cost of keeping it","Written reversal condition"],"rows":[["Plugins / code execution","Forecloses the category's only demonstrated community moat; the competitor's registry is 143,290,675 downloads deep","Capability model with no fs/network/eval plus a published audit; not before 1,000 paying users — docs/THESIS.md:853"],["Project management","Refuses a whole adjacent category","\"Nothing reverses it\" — a company-identity constraint, to be stated publicly — docs/THESIS.md:852"],["Chat sidebar","Refuses the surface every AI product ships","<20% strong acceptance across all verbs at 90 days — docs/THESIS.md:855"],["Live cursors / multiplayer","HackMD and Docmost lead with it","≥3 of the first 20 paying teams cancel citing presence by name — docs/THESIS.md:854"],["Hosting user content","\"a byte-preserving engine whose output nobody can see is a claim without a demonstration\"","None written; PRD v2 recommends shipping it — docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:4206"],["Mobile editor in v1","About 15% of complaints","No condition — the record simply ADMITS mobile with its own V0 ≤ 4 budget — docs/THESIS.md:843, docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:539"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"What the strongest refusal buys, and what the weakest one costs","items":[["Share of Obsidian tagged forum topics touching the plugin surface","22.79% — but explicitly not to be quoted as a share of our tickets","docs/BUSINESS.md:808, :819"],["Support load per install for code-execution plugins","2.78× the ecosystem average","docs/BUSINESS.md:811"],["Support cost at 10,000 users, already modelled","about 90 founder-hours a month","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:137"],["Permanent duty publishing creates","24-hour acknowledgement, no size floor, personal, never ends","docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:4208"],["Incumbents that shipped a hide-all-AI switch only after backlash","Zed (412 reactions), VS Code (30), Telegram (181)","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:382"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"One reconciled list, with each entry's reversal price published","what":"The record's seven plus hosting and the vendor database, mobile settled either way, prices shown.","gains":["One artefact instead of two that disagree","Distinguishes principle from roadmap, which is what makes a refusal credible"],"costs":["Publicly refusing multiplayer, galleries and dashboards, untested with any buyer","Cannot be published until P8 settles two of the entries"],"system":"The list becomes the feature-admission gate in one place.","screens":"A refusals section on the site and in the pitch.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Keep the plan's six as public copy, the record's seven as the internal gate","what":"Short public line, strict private admission rule.","gains":["Copy stays short and the gate stays strict","Nothing new to publish"],"costs":["Mobile stays a live contradiction between the two documents","Nobody reading both can tell which governs"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Publish only the three that are identity, and treat the rest as roadmap","what":"No plugins, no code execution, no project management, no chat sidebar — nothing else is announced.","gains":["Only refuses what will never be reversed, so it stays credible under pressure","No published price to be quoted back"],"costs":["Loses \"we never hold your files\", the strongest trust claim in the plan","The architecture argument rests on the item being dropped"],"system":"No change.","screens":"A shorter positioning line.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Stop publishing a refusal list; keep it as the internal admission gate","what":"Refusals govern what gets built and are never used as copy.","gains":["No risk of a visible reversal","The gate keeps working"],"costs":["Gives up the positioning at :298","That line is the only differentiated copy not resting on an unproven feature"],"system":"No change.","screens":"The positioning line goes.","money":"None."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["One list, or the two documents keep diverging — they already disagree about mobile.","The record did the hard part by attaching a number to every entry; publishing them makes the permanent refusals stronger by contrast.","\"Nothing reverses it\" reads differently next to \"reversed at 1,000 paying users\", and that contrast is the whole value of the list."],"flip":"If the founders will not publicly refuse multiplayer, galleries and dashboards, fall back to c and keep only the three that are identity.","linked":["P10"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:43","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:298","docs/THESIS.md:843","docs/THESIS.md:852","docs/THESIS.md:853","docs/THESIS.md:854","docs/THESIS.md:855","docs/THESIS.md:856","docs/THESIS.md:857","docs/THESIS.md:858","docs/BUSINESS.md:808","docs/BUSINESS.md:819","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:137","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:382","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:539","docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:4206","docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:4208","merged: P17"],"dupes":{"dropped":["G14"],"why":"Which refusals may be stated publicly. Both rec publishing only the subset that is true and differentiating today. Product & definition owns the boundary; refusals are the positioning."}},{"id":"P10","cat":"Product & definition","sub":"Boundary","weight":"high","q":"Does the plugin ban stay absolute, or does the data-only exception the record ratified go into the product?","lede":"The ban is the first refusal in the positioning, and the record found it forecloses the only community moat this category has shown.","visual":{"kind":"arch","layers":[{"label":"Banned outright","items":["third-party code in our process","eval, filesystem, network"],"side":"the ban","tone":"stop"},{"label":"The record's exception","items":["declarative render profiles","out-of-process import and export adapters"],"side":"unbuilt","tone":"warn"},{"label":"Already planned","items":["MCP server: agents write through the engine"],"side":"F11, MVP-1","tone":"neutral"},{"label":"The real boundary","items":["the bytes on disk, not the process"],"side":"docs/BUSINESS.md:902","tone":"accent"}],"note":"A sandbox protects the machine and does nothing for byte preservation.","caption":"What a ban on the process protects, and what it does not."},"stakes":"Claim a community moat while banning the only mechanism that produces one and the first informed reader stops believing the rest.","state":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:43 refuses plugins and code execution outright, repeated as a security rule at :551.","docs/BUSINESS.md:906 records a different verdict: the ban stands with one named exception, a data-only, no-code contribution surface.","docs/BUSINESS.md:846 states there is no example of a durable community moat in this category without third-party code."],"path":["The ban was decided on security and support grounds: our boundary is the bytes, not the process (docs/BUSINESS.md:902).","§86 then priced what the ban costs and found the cost is the category's only proven community mechanism.","docs/CRITIQUE.md:398 sharpened it: the registry we are excluded from is a competitor's distribution engine, 143,290,675 downloads deep."],"tension":["A sandbox protects the machine and does nothing for byte preservation, so the ban is correct on its own terms.","The moat claim stacked on top of it is what fails, and the cheapest fix is to drop the claim rather than the ban.","A declarative surface acquires conditionals and becomes a language nobody designed or budgeted (docs/BUSINESS.md:914)."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"What the ban costs, measured 2026-08-30","items":[["Obsidian community registry, cumulative downloads","143,290,675","docs/CRITIQUE.md:350"],["Registry entries","7,139 plugins (docs/CRITIQUE.md:350) — note docs/BUSINESS.md:827 counts 7,119 on the same date; reconcile before quoting","plus 717 themes, docs/BUSINESS.md:827"],["Cumulative downloads across four AI plugins inside Obsidian","4,165,249","docs/CRITIQUE.md:378"],["Claudian: one developer, elapsed time, stars","269 days, 15,064 stars, no CI, no PRD, no corpus","docs/CRITIQUE.md:409"],["VS Code Marketplace extensions","135,646","docs/BUSINESS.md:825"]]},{"type":"table","title":"What the ban buys, and what the exception would cost","cols":["Measure","Value","Source"],"rows":[["Share of Obsidian tagged topics touching the plugin surface","22.79% (7,076 of 31,048)","docs/BUSINESS.md:808"],["Support load per install, code-execution plugins vs average","2.78×","docs/BUSINESS.md:811"],["Top 20 Obsidian plugins that are core roadmap, not code engines","18 of 20","docs/BUSINESS.md:864"],["Templater's irreducible arbitrary-code share of active installs","0.701%","docs/BUSINESS.md:864"],["Plugins whose best-ever single version never passed 1,000 downloads","4,763 of 7,085 = 67.2%","docs/BUSINESS.md:857"],["Predicted failure of a declarative surface","It grows conditionals, then loops, then an escape hatch — Dataview shipped DQL then dataviewjs","docs/BUSINESS.md:914"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Keep the ban absolute and say so in the positioning","what":"No third-party code, no exception, stated publicly.","gains":["Simplest to state and defend","The largest single support deflection available to one person"],"costs":["Forecloses the category's only demonstrated community moat","The product family then has no third-party contribution surface"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Ship the exception: declarative render profiles and out-of-process adapters","what":"A contribution surface that cannot execute code, conformance-tested by the certificate.","gains":["Contribution without touching the byte guarantee","Gives the certificate a job beyond selling"],"costs":["The record's own warning: a declarative surface becomes a language (:914)","Unestimated work on a 37-to-58-week schedule"],"system":"A profile format, a conformance runner, and a registry to host them.","screens":"A profiles list in settings.","money":"None; a support surface with no revenue."},{"k":"c","label":"Keep the ban and demote community from moat number one","what":"The documentation changes, not the product.","gains":["Resolves it as a writing fix, which the record names as the available one (:916)","Costs nothing and nothing breaks"],"costs":["Gives up a moat claim in every deck with nothing in its place","Leaves the question of what the moat actually is"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Keep the ban and make the MCP server the sanctioned third-party surface","what":"Agents and tools integrate without running code in our process.","gains":["F11 is already planned for MVP-1","Integration without a sandbox"],"costs":["MCP is explicitly untested as a route agents will take (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:65)","An integration surface is not a community one"],"system":"F11 gains a published contract and a compatibility promise.","screens":"An integrations page.","money":"None."}],"rec":"c","recCase":["The ban is correct and should not move: the security boundary is the bytes, and a sandbox does not protect bytes.","What is wrong is the claim stacked on top, and the honest fix is the cheap one the record already identified.","Option b can follow later with a written stop rule: three constructs of conditionals and it is a language. It is not MVP-0 work."],"flip":"docs/BUSINESS.md:922 already sets it: if \"I need X and you won't build it\" crosses 15% of support volume on a rolling quarter, the data-only surface is forced.","linked":["FF12","P7"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:43","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:65","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:551","docs/BUSINESS.md:825","docs/BUSINESS.md:827","docs/BUSINESS.md:846","docs/BUSINESS.md:902","docs/BUSINESS.md:906","docs/BUSINESS.md:914","docs/BUSINESS.md:916","docs/BUSINESS.md:922","docs/CRITIQUE.md:350","docs/CRITIQUE.md:398","docs/CRITIQUE.md:409"],"dupes":{"dropped":["MK9"],"why":"Does the no-plugins ban stay absolute or admit the data-only/out-of-process exception. Same four options; recs c vs b. Product & definition owns the refusal."}},{"id":"P24","cat":"Product & definition","sub":"Definition","weight":"high","q":"Is the claim that review catches defects, or that it tells you what changed?","lede":"The plan never says which job the review surface does, and the two promises have different evidence and different failure modes.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":160,"cols":[{"title":"Catch what the agent broke","tone":"stop"},{"title":"Know what changed","tone":"accent"}],"rows":[{"label":"What the evidence says","cells":["Defects were 78 of 570 review comments, 14%","Reviewers told the origin validated better"]},{"label":"What we must prove","cells":["That our surface finds errors","That a person can see the change at all"]},{"label":"Failure mode","cells":["Missed one, so the tool failed","Ignored it, so the tool is noise"]},{"label":"Precedent","cells":["Clinical alerts: 55–98% override","GitHub Viewed, Google's blue dot"]},{"label":"Demo","cells":["Needs a planted defect","Opens their own repository"]}],"note":"Microsoft's 14% is from ICSE 2013; the override range is 34 drug-interaction studies. Both are transferred from other domains.","caption":"Two jobs, one surface, and only one of them is defensible."},"stakes":"Promise defect-catching and the first missed error is our fault; promise orientation and the surface has to earn attention every day.","state":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:20 promises that every span changed since a person last read it is tinted, and never says what the reading is for.","The one measured argument in the plan is orientation: reviewers told which code was machine-written validated better, at higher workload (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:409 area, §16).","In the review literature defects were 78 of 570 comments, fourth of nine categories.","No evidence exists anywhere about reviewing AI-written prose; every finding is transferred from code review, clinical alerting or fact-checking."],"path":["The claim moved from bytes to authorship to answering markers to review state in two days (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:13).","Each move changed the sentence and none of them stated the job the person is doing when they read a tinted span.","The retention argument at :427 assumes a count going to zero, which is an orientation job, not a defect job."],"tension":["A defect claim is falsifiable by one missed error and is the claim every code-review tool that died was making.","An orientation claim is honest and weak: it competes with a free diff panel that four tools already open automatically.","The two jobs imply different surfaces — a ranked findings list against an exhaustible change list."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"What the review and alerting literature measures","items":[["Defects as a share of code review comments","78 of 570 (14%), fourth of nine categories","sback.it ICSE 2013"],["Drug-interaction alert override rate across 34 studies","55–98%","pubmed 35673040"],["One hospital: alerts overridden, and reasons that were meaningless","12,659 of 14,612 (86.6%); 88.3%","pubmed 38658357"],["The one system that achieved acceptance","31 rules firing in 0.19% of 500,274 sessions, 57.5% accepted","pubmed 34450669"],["Developer review budget, and median change size","3.2 h/week; 24 lines","sback.it ICSE 2018 SEIP"],["Evidence about reviewing AI-written prose","None found","self-declared gap"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Claim defect detection: the tool finds what the agent got wrong","what":"The surface ranks findings and the promise is that errors surface.","gains":["The strongest promise available and the easiest to sell","Matches what a liable buyer says they want"],"costs":["Falsified by one missed defect","Every product that made this claim in code review is dead or discontinued"],"system":"Needs a judgement layer the engine does not have.","screens":"A ranked findings list replaces the change list.","money":"Justifies a higher price and a support obligation."},{"k":"b","label":"Claim orientation: you can see what changed and who wrote it","what":"The surface is a ledger, and the promise is visibility rather than judgement.","gains":["The one thing measured: knowing the origin improved validation","Nothing to be falsified by a missed error"],"costs":["Weaker than a buyer wants to hear","Competes with a free diff panel four tools now open automatically"],"system":"No judgement layer; the sidecar is enough.","screens":"An exhaustible change list and the tint.","money":"Prices like a utility, not like a guarantee."},{"k":"c","label":"Claim the record: a durable ledger for whoever is answerable","what":"The promise is that the reading is recorded, not that it was any good.","gains":["Matches the regulated buyer's actual need and the sidecar's actual shape","Survives every attention finding, because it does not require attention"],"costs":["A compliance sale, and no regulation opened requires per-span review","Nobody buys a record for themselves"],"system":"Retention of the sidecar becomes a feature, which no F-row builds today.","screens":"An export of who read what, when.","money":"Team tier only; no individual buys this."},{"k":"d","label":"Claim no job; show the state and let people decide what it is for","what":"The product presents review state and makes no promise about outcomes.","gains":["Nothing to be wrong about","Keeps every buyer's interpretation open"],"costs":["A pitch with no verb does not survive one meeting","Leaves the demo without a point"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["Orientation is the only job with a measurement behind it, and it is the one the plan's own attention section already argues for.","A defect claim is what four dead review products made, and one missed error refutes it in front of the person who found it.","Option c is the honest team-tier framing and should sit under b, not replace it — nobody buys a record for themselves.","Saying the job out loud also settles what the surface is: an exhaustible list, not a ranked set of findings."],"flip":"If the five people who bill for documents say they need errors caught rather than changes shown, c becomes the sale and b becomes the free tier.","linked":["P11","P2"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:20","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:427","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:13","https://sback.it/publications/icse2013.pdf","https://sback.it/publications/icse2018seip.pdf","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/35673040/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38658357/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34450669/"]},{"id":"P15","cat":"Product & definition","sub":"Surface budget","weight":"medium","q":"Which budget governs — concepts and controls at rest — and what is displaced to fit inside it?","lede":"The plan cites a seven-concept budget that appears once in the corpus, in the plan itself, and nothing enforces any of the numbers.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":150,"cols":[{"title":"Record §18.2","tone":"neutral"},{"title":"THESIS §103.4","tone":"accent"},{"title":"Plan v15","tone":"warn"}],"rows":[{"label":"Concepts","cells":["3","4","\"seven\", never enumerated"]},{"label":"The nouns","cells":["file, folder, view","plus prompt, paid for at :864","at least 10 introduced"]},{"label":"Controls at rest","cells":["9, enumerated","9, unchanged","tabs, 4 modes, counter, bars"]},{"label":"Enforced by","cells":["A CI DOM assertion","The same","Nothing: no .github directory"]}],"note":"docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:1848 and :1881; docs/THESIS.md:862; docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:429.","caption":"Three budgets in three documents, none of them enforced."},"stakes":"A budget nobody can trace and nothing enforces is a mood, and accretion is the stated failure mode.","state":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:429 cites \"the seven-concept budget\"; the string occurs once in the whole corpus, at that line.","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:1848 sets three concepts; docs/THESIS.md:862 raises it to four and pays for the fourth at :864.","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:1881 pins nine controls visible at rest and enumerates them from :1883.","F1 ships tabs, four modes and a properties panel (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:55), and the review counter and tree bars are added at :409 (merged from P16)."],"path":["The nine were set with a CI DOM assertion attached (docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:1845).","THESIS is blunt about the concept number: \"four is a budget we chose, not a number the literature gives\" (docs/THESIS.md:877).","The v15 feature list was written from market evidence, not from either budget, and the two were never laid side by side."],"tension":["The two things the product most needs seen, the tint and the unreviewed counter, have no slots left.","Raising a budget for our own favourite feature is the exact failure the budget exists to prevent.","Nothing is enforced: verified 2026-09-09, the repo has no `.github` directory at all."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"Three different budgets in three documents","cols":["Document","Number","The nouns","Citation"],"rows":[["Record §18.2","C ≤ 3","file, folder, view","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:1848"],["THESIS §103.4","4","file, folder, view, prompt — the fourth bought and paid for at :864","docs/THESIS.md:862"],["Plan v15 §17","\"seven-concept\"","Not enumerated anywhere; the phrase occurs once in the whole corpus","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:429"],["What v15 actually introduces","At least 10","file, folder, mode/view, span, review state, sidecar, attribution, proposal, scan, key","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:20, :55–62, :135"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"What the budget rests on, and what it does not","items":[["NN/g progressive disclosure","Bounds disclosure DEPTH, not breadth — \"beyond 2 disclosure levels typically have low usability\"","docs/THESIS.md:872"],["Feature Fatigue (Thompson, Hamilton & Rust, JMR 2005)","Gives a direction for subscription businesses, not a count; Crossref metadata only, the paper is paywalled and was not opened","docs/THESIS.md:873"],["Arc, first-party adoption data","5.52% of DAUs use more than one Space; 4.17% Live Folders; 0.4% Calendar Preview on Hover","docs/THESIS.md:874"],["Note-app abandonment studies found","None; the circulated Obsidian claim is refuted at source","docs/THESIS.md:875, docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:1867"],["Hick's law","Not cited — the attached DOI resolves to Hyman 1953, a reaction-time study, not adoption","docs/THESIS.md:877"]]},{"type":"table","title":"The nine at rest, and what v15 wants to add","cols":["Slot","Record's at-rest list (docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:1883–1891)","v15 addition"],"rows":[["1–2","The text, full-bleed; file tree collapsed to a rail, folder names only","Tree gains unreviewed bars — docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:409"],["3","Breadcrumb path, also the rename affordance","Tab strip — docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:55"],["4","One mode control: three-state segment Edit · Read · Split","Four modes: Live, Edit, Split, Read — docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:55"],["5","One view control: projection selector","—"],["6","Save/sync state as text, three states only","—"],["7","Word count","Review counter, top-left of the panel — docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:409"],["8","Search entry point","—"],["9","Right-pane toggle that cycles","Properties panel for frontmatter — docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:55"],["+","Explicitly not visible at rest: no AI button, no export button, no share button","ShareMenu, AIMenu and ExportMenu are all wired into the editor header today — src/modules/editor/presentation/EditorPane.tsx:905–907"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"The counters, and what the code shows today","items":[["V0 target","≤ 9, pinned by a DOM assertion in CI","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:1845"],["Repo has no CI at all","Verified 2026-09-09: no .github directory exists","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:216 records \"No CI; four gates have reported green while blind\""],["Palette commands in the record","14","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:1865"],["Palette commands counted in the tree today","13 fixed, plus dynamic \"Insert template: …\" entries per template file","src/modules/app-shell/presentation/CommandPalette.tsx"],["Slash commands today","14, capped at 16","src/modules/editor/presentation/slash-commands.ts:34–51; docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:1901"],["Buttons wired into the editor header today","ShareMenu, AIMenu, ExportMenu — all three on the record's not-visible-at-rest list","src/modules/editor/presentation/EditorPane.tsx:905–907"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Four concepts, nine controls, and displace to fit","what":"Adopt the record's numbers, drop the tab strip and fold Live into the mode control, buying two slots.","gains":["Both numbers are traceable and already argued","Displacement is what makes a budget real"],"costs":["No tab strip, cushioned only by quick-switch on mod+k (docs/CRITIQUE.md:612)","Review state, span and sidecar are then not first-session nouns"],"system":"Build the DOM assertion first; there is no CI to hang it on.","screens":"S2 loses the tab strip and one mode.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Raise both numbers and pin them with the assertion","what":"Five concepts and eleven controls, written down and checked.","gains":["The headline feature can be named on the first-run screen","Honest and checkable"],"costs":["A counter that moves for our own feature stops being a constraint","Concedes the argument the budget exists to win"],"system":"The DOM assertion is written against the new numbers.","screens":"S2 keeps tabs and gains the counter.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Keep nine for the document surface and give the review panel its own budget","what":"Two budgets, as mobile was given one at docs/THESIS.md:843.","gains":["Precedent exists in the record","The document surface stays clean"],"costs":["Two budgets are harder to enforce than one","Unlike mobile, the panel shares a screen with the surface it is exempt from"],"system":"Two DOM assertions, scoped by region.","screens":"The panel grows independently.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Delete the counters and review the at-rest screenshot instead","what":"No numbers; judgement at review time.","gains":["Stops citing a number with no source, which is the immediate defect","Nothing false is published"],"costs":["Loses the only enforceable check on surface growth in the corpus","Accretion is the stated failure mode"],"system":"No assertion.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["Four is the only concept number with an argument attached, and THESIS labels it chosen rather than derived, which is the honest form.","Adopting it forces the useful question: can the tint teach itself without the phrase \"review state\" on the first screen? The five-second test at :411 measures exactly that.","The \"seven-concept budget\" phrase should be struck this week either way, because a reader who greps for it finds only itself.","None of this is enforced today, so the first action is building the DOM assertion, not winning the argument."],"flip":"If the five-second test shows people cannot read the tint without a label, buy the slot explicitly under b and name what it displaced.","linked":[],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:411","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:429","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:1848","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:1867","docs/THESIS.md:862","docs/THESIS.md:864","docs/THESIS.md:872","docs/THESIS.md:873","docs/THESIS.md:874","docs/THESIS.md:877","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:55","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:216","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:409","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:1845","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:1865","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:1881","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:1901","docs/THESIS.md:843","docs/THESIS.md:905","docs/CRITIQUE.md:612","docs/CRITIQUE.md:614","src/modules/editor/presentation/EditorPane.tsx:905","merged: P16"]},{"id":"FF1","cat":"Form factor & surfaces","sub":"Core choice","weight":"critical","q":"Do we ship a standalone editor, a VS Code extension, or one core behind both, and which ships first?","lede":"Every estimate in the plan prices a standalone shell. No line anywhere prices an extension, and the meeting must choose between them.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":26,"cols":[{"title":"Standalone shell","tone":"neutral"},{"title":"VS Code extension","tone":"accent"},{"title":"One core, both","tone":"neutral"}],"rows":[{"label":"Population in reach","cells":["Show HN median 3 points across 386 launches","24.89M Claude Code installs in that store","Both, in sequence"]},{"label":"Review niche there","cells":["Not applicable","13 extensions, 1,217 installs, ceiling 400","Same 400 ceiling"]},{"label":"Live mode","cells":["Yes","No view-zone API, so no","Two diverging feature sets"]},{"label":"Table stakes","cells":["14.5 to 20.5 days, unbudgeted","Host supplies about 6.5 of 17.5 days","Paid once, on the shell"]},{"label":"The name","cells":["Free","Owned by an 82,265-install incumbent","Two names to explain"]},{"label":"Elapsed to MVP-0","cells":["57.9 weeks at 1.21 days a week","No estimate exists","No estimate exists"]}],"note":"Rows read from the plan and re-measured 2026-09-09.","caption":"Three surfaces, and the row nobody has costed"},"stakes":"Choosing the shell commits about 58 calendar weeks before a stranger has been asked anything.","state":["Decision 6 offers three options and carries an estimate for none of them (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:364).","All thirteen features and all eleven fixes budget the standalone shell only (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:55, :214).","The engine is 3,614 lines with no DOM, and one symbol of thirteen files reaches product code (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:217, :223).","Round 2 measured a byte-exact write from an extension twice, at 94/94 and 156/156 bytes (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:125)."],"path":["The gap register called this the largest unreasoned decision in the plan on 2026-09-08 (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:48).","Round 2 measured the mechanics and left the choice to the founders (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:125).","Microsoft merged a review/unreview operation into the Agents window on 2026-07-03, milestone 1.128.0, and documented none of it (api.github.com, PR 324218)."],"tension":["The host reaches three orders of magnitude more people and has now built the per-file half of our marker itself.","Free working-tree diff of agent changes shipped in four places between 2026-08-24 and 2026-09-03: Antigravity, Notion, Codex and Claude Code v2.1.260.","Only the engine is ours. 41 of 43 editor files are byte-identical to the sibling repo (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:141).","What nobody has shipped is review state stored in the repository, per span, surviving a machine change."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"What round 2 actually measured","items":[["Extension byte-exact write, harness 1","94 / 94 bytes","VS Code 1.135.0 — PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:364"],["Extension byte-exact write, harness 2","156 / 156 bytes","independent second harness — GAPS:125"],["Engine that would port","3,614 lines, 13 files, no DOM","re-verified in src/modules/mdmax, 2026-09-09"],["Engine symbols reaching product code today","1 symbol from 1 of 13 files","decodeStrict, exactly 2 import sites — re-verified"],["Extension engineering estimate in the plan","none","no line in Exhibit 1 or §9"]]},{"type":"table","title":"Population against niche","cols":["Surface","Installs","Source"],"rows":[["Copilot Chat","78.06M","GAPS-2026-09-08.md:48"],["Claude Code VS Code extension","24.89M","GAPS:48; PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:150"],["markdown-all-in-one (10.6x co-recommendation lift with Copilot)","14.45M","GAPS:48"],["git-ai","61,517","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:151"],["SpecKit Companion (nearest sidecar pattern)","9,367","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:152"],["All 13 markdown-review extensions, combined","1,217","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:9, :24"],["Best of those 13 — the ceiling","400","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:24"],["mddiff, our own sentence, shipped 2026-06-03","74","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:24"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Standalone editor only, as the plan is written","what":"Build the four-mode shell, pay the table-stakes bill, ship nothing inside another editor.","gains":["Keeps Live mode, the free-editor story and the Obsidian audience","One codebase, one set of estimates, no host to depend on"],"costs":["57.9 calendar weeks to MVP-0 at the measured 1.21 days a week","Pays table stakes on a shell that is 41 of 43 files someone else's code","Show HN median is 3 points across 386 markdown-editor launches"],"system":"No change. The fix list and the sequence stand as written.","screens":"All nine prototype screens survive unchanged.","money":"Two certificates a year: $99 Apple, $150-400 Windows."},{"k":"b","label":"VS Code extension only","what":"Ship review state and attribution as an extension and stop building the shell.","gains":["Meets the population that already runs the agents","The host supplies about 6.5 of the 17.5 table-stakes days free"],"costs":["No view-zone API, so Live mode cannot exist","A niche of 13 extensions totalling 1,217 installs, ceiling 400","The name is owned there by an 82,265-install incumbent"],"system":"Engine ports unchanged. The shell and all Tauri work are abandoned.","screens":"S0, the S2 mode tabs and S11 die. S4 becomes a host view.","money":"No certificates, no web hosting, no store fee."},{"k":"c","label":"One core, extension first, standalone shell second","what":"Extract the engine as the product, ship the thin extension, keep the shell for later.","gains":["Puts the tint in front of a real population inside the test window","Keeps the shell open as an option without paying for it yet"],"costs":["Two shells to maintain later, at 1.21 engineering days a week","The extension still has no estimate anywhere in the plan"],"system":"Engine becomes a package with two hosts and one sidecar format.","screens":"S2 and S4 ship twice, in two idioms, from one spec.","money":"Extension cost unknown. Nobody has priced it."},{"k":"d","label":"One core, standalone first, extension at MVP-1","what":"Keep the current build order and add the extension after the pilot exits.","gains":["No re-planning today; every estimate in the plan stays valid","Lets the pilot run on the surface that already partly exists"],"costs":["Defers the population question by 57.9 calendar weeks","By then the host may have documented what it merged in July"],"system":"No change.","screens":"No change.","money":"None."}],"rec":"c","recCase":["Only the engine is ours: 3,614 lines, no DOM, portable by measurement rather than by hope (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:223).","The shell is not an asset. 41 of 43 editor files are byte-identical to sgnk-md (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:141).","Building it first spends 57.9 calendar weeks before anyone outside the session has been asked anything (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:227).","Take it with FF12, because the package route may be cheaper still, and with FF14, which binds both."],"flip":"If the contention test in FF4 loses a byte inside the host, the extension is out and (d) is the answer.","linked":["F5","FF11","FF12","FF14","FF3","FF4"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:364","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:9","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:24","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:55","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:214","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:217","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:223","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:227","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:48","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:125","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:141","docs/CRITIQUE.md:441","src/modules/mdmax","https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode/pulls/324218"],"dupes":{"dropped":["MK2"],"why":"Standalone editor / VS Code extension / one core behind both, and which ships first. Verbatim the same question and the same rec (c). Form factor & surfaces owns it."}},{"id":"FF3","cat":"Form factor & surfaces","sub":"The fork","weight":"critical","q":"The editor shell is a fork of sgnk-md. Do we merge back into it, freeze it, hard-fork it, or delete it?","lede":"The same fork appears once as a strength and once as a liability in one document, and nobody has resolved which it is.","visual":{"kind":"arch","layers":[{"label":"Splice engine, src/modules/mdmax","items":["3,614 lines","13 files, no DOM","1 symbol reaches product code"],"side":"ours","tone":"accent"},{"label":"Editor and app shell","items":["41 of 43 files byte-identical","0 unique to frontmatter"],"side":"forked","tone":"sunk"},{"label":"The rest of src/","items":["202 identical, 25 diverged","20 unique, 13 of them the engine"],"side":"forked","tone":"sunk"},{"label":"src-tauri desktop shell","items":["productName sgnk-md","identifier ai.sgnk.md"],"side":"sibling's","tone":"stop"}],"note":"Re-measured 2026-09-09 against the sibling repo.","caption":"What this product owns, by layer: 14.2% of 25,407 lines"},"stakes":"Every table-stakes day the plan does not budget is a fork tax paid twice or an upstream merge nobody scheduled.","state":["§9 fix #0 calls the shell a fork, not an asset, and attaches no engineering days (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:223).","§23 lists the same fact as a strength: 88.6% of a shipping editor exists (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:557).","The plan states the whole-repo count two ways: 181 of 226 at line 223, 202 of 228 at line 479.","src-tauri still carries the sibling's identity in the committed config (src-tauri/tauri.conf.json:3, :5)."],"path":["Round 2 found it. It is finding 4 of the five that changed most (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:141).","It had never appeared in any earlier plan.","Nobody has asked whether sgnk-md has users (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:105)."],"tension":["Merging needs an answer about sgnk-md's users that nobody has requested.","Hard-forking commits 14.5 to 20.5 table-stakes days the measured rate cannot pay (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:227).","Deleting the shell is correct only if FF1 resolves to a host surface.","The divergence has not moved since the plan was written. The extra file counted today is a .DS_Store."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"Re-measured 2026-09-09 against the sibling repo at ~/Desktop/GitHub/md","cols":["Scope","Byte-identical","Diverged","Unique to frontmatter"],"rows":[["src/modules/editor + src/modules/app-shell (all files)","41","2","0"],["src/ — all files, including non-code","202","26 (one is .DS_Store)","20"],["src/ — .ts, .tsx, .css only","183","25","20"],["Of those 20 unique files","—","—","13 engine, 5 Firebase auth, 1 DI container, 1 splice-frontmatter"],["The plan says, at line 223","181 of 226","25","0 in editor + app-shell"],["The plan also says, at line 479","202 of 228","—","—"]],"note":"The 41-of-43 editor figure reproduces exactly. The whole-repo figure does not: line 223 and line 479 disagree with each other and both disagree with measurement. On like-for-like code files the divergence count is still 25, not 26 — the extra file is a macOS .DS_Store artifact, so nothing has actually drifted since the plan was written."},{"type":"stat","title":"What is actually owned","items":[["Total source, .ts and .tsx","25,407 lines","re-measured 2026-09-09; matches CRITIQUE.md:52"],["Engine","3,614 lines = 14.2%","re-measured, 13 files"],["Everything else","21,793 lines","CRITIQUE.md:52 calls it an Obsidian clone"],["Engine reaching product code","1 symbol, 2 import sites","decodeStrict from shape-gate.ts"],["src-tauri identity","productName sgnk-md, id ai.sgnk.md","src-tauri/tauri.conf.json:3, :5"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Merge back: one codebase, frontmatter as a mode of sgnk-md","what":"Stop maintaining two trees and ship frontmatter as a mode inside the sibling product.","gains":["Ends the divergence tax outright","Inherits whatever user base sgnk-md already has"],"costs":["Needs to know whether sgnk-md has users, which nobody has asked","Two products then share one release and one name"],"system":"One tree, one build, a feature flag where they differ.","screens":"The launcher becomes a mode switch inside sgnk-md.","money":"One set of certificates instead of two."},{"k":"b","label":"Freeze the shell: new work goes to the engine and one surface","what":"No further investment in the forked shell; the engine and one surface get every day.","gains":["Stops paying the tax without needing a migration","Requires no answer we do not already have"],"costs":["The shell stays at its current quality","Every table-stakes gap in the eight-item list stays open"],"system":"No upstream tracking. Engine work continues.","screens":"No new screens. Existing ones stop improving.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Hard-fork and own it: stop tracking the sibling, budget the table stakes","what":"Declare the shell ours and put the table-stakes days into the plan.","gains":["Honest about what maintaining an editor costs","Removes the ambiguity in fix #0"],"costs":["14.5 to 20.5 engineering days of table stakes before any novel feature","The measured rate of 1.21 days a week cannot pay that"],"system":"The shell becomes a first-class codebase with its own tests.","screens":"Table editing, paste-to-markdown and a keymap editor arrive.","money":"Roughly four months of the measured rate spent on parity."},{"k":"d","label":"Delete the shell; ship the engine inside someone else's shell","what":"Keep the 14.2% that is ours and let a host supply the editor.","gains":["Keeps only what is genuinely this product's","Matches the FF1 extension route and the FF12 package route"],"costs":["Loses 21,793 lines and the free-editor story","Live mode and the four-mode promise go with it"],"system":"Engine becomes a package. No shell to build or sign.","screens":"S0, S2 and S11 are retired.","money":"No certificates, no web hosting."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["Freezing is the only option that needs no answer we do not have today.","Merging needs to know whether sgnk-md has users, and nobody has asked (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:105).","Hard-forking commits 14.5 to 20.5 table-stakes days the measured 1.21 days a week cannot pay (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:227).","Fix the two conflicting whole-repo counts in the same edit, so the meeting is not shown two numbers for one fact."],"flip":"If sgnk-md has ten reachable users, merging is the best deal in the plan and (a) wins.","linked":["FF1","FF14","FF8"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:223","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:227","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:479","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:557","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:105","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:141","docs/CRITIQUE.md:52","src-tauri/tauri.conf.json:3","src-tauri/tauri.conf.json:5","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r24-v1-table-stakes.md:87"],"dupes":{"dropped":["B11","PL11"],"why":"Merge back / vendor / freeze / hard-fork / delete the sgnk-md editor shell. Same option set; recs split b/a/b. Form factor & surfaces owns which shell we ship. P1 is not a duplicate: it decides the definition noun, not the codebase."}},{"id":"FF8","cat":"Form factor & surfaces","sub":"Web vs desktop","weight":"critical","q":"The desktop app described in the plan does not exist. Do we build it, ship web-only, or make it the paid tier?","lede":"Every desktop-only promise rests on a Tauri shell that points at the sibling product's website and holds no filesystem permission.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":26,"cols":[{"title":"Web app today","tone":"accent"},{"title":"Desktop shell today","tone":"stop"},{"title":"Desktop as promised","tone":"neutral"}],"rows":[{"label":"Open a local file","cells":["Chrome and Edge, per folder","No fs permission at all","Any folder, full read and write"]},{"label":"MCP server (F11)","cells":["No","No","Yes, a local process"]},{"label":"Offline","cells":["Cached open files","Nothing; it loads a remote URL","Everything except the model"]},{"label":"Signing","cells":["Not applicable","signingIdentity null; dmg and app","Notarised dmg, signed exe, AppImage"]},{"label":"Identity","cells":["frontmatter","productName sgnk-md, id ai.sgnk.md","frontmatter"]},{"label":"Cost to close the gap","cells":["Built","Plan budgets 1 day","Measured at 4 to 8 weeks"]}],"note":"Right column is Exhibit 2. Middle column is the committed config, read 2026-09-09.","caption":"What the plan promises on desktop against what is committed"},"stakes":"Four to eight weeks of shell work buys the ten pilot strangers nothing they would notice.","state":["§3 describes a Tauri app containing the editor, engine, git client, MCP server and search index (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:104).","§9 fix #9 budgets one day for the whole problem (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:222).","The committed window url, devUrl and frontendDist all point at the sibling product's site (src-tauri/tauri.conf.json:3).","The capability set contains no fs permission of any kind (src-tauri/capabilities/default.json)."],"path":["The offline-or-online research measured the shell on 2026-08-31 and called it a chrome-less browser in an app icon (docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r19-p2-offline-or-online.md:11).","It priced the real build at four to eight weeks (docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r19-p2-offline-or-online.md:18).","That finding never reached the plan."],"tension":["Exhibit 2's whole desktop column is promised on a shell that cannot open a file (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:92).","The File System Access API exists only in desktop Chrome and Edge, so web-only refuses about one in five desktop visitors (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:102).","MCP needs a local process, so pulling F11 into MVP-0 makes the desktop app mandatory (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:65).","At 1.21 engineering days a week, four to eight weeks of shell work is most of a quarter (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:227)."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"src-tauri/tauri.conf.json and capabilities/default.json, read 2026-09-09","cols":["What the plan says","What the committed config says"],"rows":[["Contains the editor, engine, git client, MCP server, search index (line 104)","window url, devUrl and frontendDist all = https://md.sgnk.ai — the sibling product's website"],["Full local read/write; offline everything except the model (Exhibit 2)","zero fs permissions. The set is: core, event, window, webview, shell, os, process, clipboard read/write, dialog"],[".dmg notarised, Windows .exe code-signed, Linux AppImage (line 104)","targets: [dmg, app]; signingIdentity: null; entitlements: null"],["Product identity re-labelled in 1 day (fix #9)","productName sgnk-md, identifier ai.sgnk.md — against a measured 4-8 weeks to go from remote wrapper to real (r19-p2 §91.2, option B)"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"What each route costs and forecloses","items":[["File System Access API support","desktop Chrome and Edge only","none of Firefox, Safari, iOS, Android — PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:102, caniuse 2026-09-08"],["Users refused on a non-Chromium browser","about 1 in 5 desktop visitors","r19-p2 §91.3, explicitly tagged [derived], not measured"],["Desktop certificates","$99/yr Apple; $150-400/yr Windows plus a hardware token","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:104, :231"],["Real Tauri build","4-8 weeks","r19-p2 §91.2"],["Measured engineering rate","1.21 days per calendar week","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:227, independently reproduced"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Build the real Tauri app now","what":"Bundle the frontend, declare scoped fs, shell out to git, run the engine locally.","gains":["Delivers MCP, local git, the watcher and true offline","The strongest legal posture, since bytes never transit"],"costs":["Four to eight weeks of shell work before any stranger sees the product","Two certificates, an update server and a per-OS bug matrix"],"system":"Scoped fs capability, bundled frontend, local git and index.","screens":"No new screens. Exhibit 2's desktop column becomes true.","money":"$99/yr Apple plus $150-400/yr Windows and a hardware token."},{"k":"b","label":"Ship web-only for MVP-0 and rewrite Exhibit 2 to describe what exists","what":"The pilot runs in the browser against a GitHub repo or a Chrome and Edge folder.","gains":["The pilot runs on what is already built","No certificates, no installer, no update channel"],"costs":["Loses MCP, local git, the watcher and offline beyond cached files","Refuses about one in five desktop visitors on Firefox and Safari"],"system":"No Tauri work. The filesystem adapter stays browser-only.","screens":"Exhibit 2's desktop column is deleted, not deferred.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Web-only free; the desktop app becomes the paid tier","what":"Charge for the installed app and its local capabilities rather than for seats.","gains":["Gives the paid tier a concrete offer instead of a thin one","Puts the desktop work behind a signal that someone will pay"],"costs":["Prices a product that has not been built","The four to eight weeks arrive before the first rupee"],"system":"Entitlement check in the desktop build.","screens":"An upgrade path in S11.","money":"A price on an unbuilt artefact."},{"k":"d","label":"Desktop primary, web as a read-only viewer","what":"The installed app is the product; the browser shows documents and nothing more.","gains":["Best offline and legal posture in the record","Documents never transit, so the legal surface shrinks"],"costs":["An install cliff in front of a funnel that needs roughly 1.26M cumulative visitors","Every desktop cost arrives first and all at once"],"system":"Two builds with sharply different capability sets.","screens":"The web app loses editing, so most screens become read-only.","money":"Certificates plus an update server, before revenue."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["The exit test is ten strangers in twelve weeks, and shell work buys those ten nothing they would notice (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:227).","The web app already delivers F1 through F8 against a repo or a local folder on Chrome and Edge (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:92).","Exhibit 2's desktop column is currently a specification of a product rather than a description of one (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:104).","Fix #9's one day is against a measured four to eight weeks, so correct the estimate in the same edit."],"flip":"If MCP is pulled into MVP-0 the desktop app becomes mandatory, so decide F11's tier in the same sitting.","linked":["AC12","AC19","AC8","FF14","FF3","FF7"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:65","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:92","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:102","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:104","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:222","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:227","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:231","src-tauri/tauri.conf.json:3","src-tauri/capabilities/default.json","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r19-p2-offline-or-online.md:11","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r19-p2-offline-or-online.md:18","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r19-p2-offline-or-online.md:67","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r19-p2-offline-or-online.md:78"],"dupes":{"dropped":["AC2"],"why":"Is MVP-0 the web app or a desktop build, and which one do the ten strangers get. AC2's b/c/d map 1:1 onto FF8's options and both rec (b) web-only. AC2's option (a), pricing the access layer into the schedule, is a schedule action and belongs with PL2."}},{"id":"FF14","cat":"Form factor & surfaces","sub":"Capacity","weight":"critical","q":"How many surfaces is one person allowed at 1.21 engineering days a week, and which are deleted today?","lede":"The plan names or still references eight surfaces on a commit record showing one author and a rate that puts one surface at 58 weeks.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":28,"cols":[{"title":"One surface","tone":"accent"},{"title":"Two surfaces","tone":"neutral"},{"title":"Keep all eight","tone":"stop"}],"rows":[{"label":"Elapsed to MVP-0","cells":["57.9 weeks at 1.21 days a week","No second estimate exists","No estimate exists"]},{"label":"Surfaces deleted today","cells":["Seven","Six","None"]},{"label":"Stale references fixed","cells":["Nine, in one edit","Nine, in one edit","Nine left standing"]},{"label":"Channels retained","cells":["None from the surface list","One","All of them"]},{"label":"What decides it","cells":["FF1, in the same sitting","FF1 plus a second choice","Nothing"]}],"note":"Rate measured over 2026-07-13 to 2026-09-08 and reproduced 2026-09-09.","caption":"Surface count against a measured 1.21 engineering days a week"},"stakes":"Nothing in the plan says how many surfaces one person may have, and that number binds every other decision here.","state":["§9 measures 10 of 58 calendar days touching src, src-tauri or test, which is 1.21 engineering days a week (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:227).","MVP-0 is about 70 engineering days, so 57.9 calendar weeks at that rate (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:227).","The resources note records one author on every commit, open since 2026-08-31 (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:231).","Two surfaces are cut and still appear in nine places (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:304, :310)."],"path":["Round 2 measured the velocity and withdrew both the ten-week schedule and the 2.5x correction (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:130).","The surface list was never re-cut against the new rate.","Free working-tree agent diffs shipped in four products between 2026-08-24 and 2026-09-03, so the window is not static."],"tension":["Two cut surfaces, one undecided, one that does not exist in the code, and one needing a local process nobody has built.","Surface count is the binding constraint and the one variable the plan never budgets.","The 0.23 per week figure is computed on a narrower path set than the headline it sits beside, which makes the collapse look worse.","If a second person is real, every density figure has to be re-derived before the sequence is quoted again."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"Surfaces named or still referenced in the v15 plan","cols":["Surface","Stated status","Where"],"rows":[["Web app","MVP-0","Exhibit 6, line 203"],["Desktop app (Tauri)","MVP-0 — but the shell points at md.sgnk.ai with zero fs permissions","line 104; src-tauri/tauri.conf.json"],["VS Code extension","undecided","decision 6, line 364"],["Obsidian plugin","CUT — still referenced in 6 places","lines 204, 338, 428, 464, 477, 524 (cut at 304)"],["Chrome extension","CUT — still referenced in 3 places","lines 203, 464, 477 (cut at 310)"],["MCP server","MVP-1; needs a local process","F11, line 65"],["mdmax cert GitHub Action","Max tier; the CLI exits 1 today","lines 224, 462"],["?src= URL parameter","named once, in no tier or sequence","line 310"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"The rate that binds all of it — independently reproduced 2026-09-09","items":[["Measured engineering days per calendar week","1.21","10 of 58 calendar days on src + src-tauri + test — reproduces exactly"],["Best rate ever observed on the sibling repo","1.91 per week","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:227"],["Last 30 days, same path basis as the headline","3 of 30 days = 0.70 per week","re-measured. The plan's \"0.23/week\" is src/ alone — a different denominator from its own headline, which makes the collapse look 3x worse than like-for-like"],["MVP-0 estimate, one surface","about 70 engineering days","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:227"],["Elapsed at the measured rate","57.9 calendar weeks","70 / 1.21, recomputed"],["Authors on the commit record","1 — now 82 of 82 on this repo (the plan says 80 of 80; two commits have landed since)","re-measured 2026-09-09"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"One surface for MVP-0, named today; every other surface deleted from the plan","what":"Pick the surface in the same sitting as FF1 and remove the rest from the document.","gains":["Makes the plan match the measured rate","Removes maintenance commitments nobody decided to make"],"costs":["Removes the free-plugin and browser channels from the pilot","Forces FF1, FF2 and FF7 to be answered in one sitting"],"system":"One build target, one release path.","screens":"One screen set; the family diagram loses three boxes.","money":"Fewer certificates and no store fees."},{"k":"b","label":"Two surfaces: the web app plus one host surface","what":"Keep the trial in the browser and add one extension or plugin as a channel.","gains":["Keeps a trial and a distribution channel","Matches the FF1 one-core recommendation"],"costs":["Roughly doubles maintenance against a rate that needs 58 weeks for one","No estimate exists for the second surface"],"system":"One engine, two hosts, one sidecar format.","screens":"Two screen idioms to keep in step.","money":"One store listing."},{"k":"c","label":"Keep the current list and accept the elapsed time","what":"Change nothing in the surface list or the sequence.","gains":["No re-planning today","The nine stale references can be fixed later, in isolation"],"costs":["The plan's own arithmetic puts MVP-0 in late 2027","Nine stale references stay in a document going to a founder meeting"],"system":"No change.","screens":"No change.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Resolve the second founder first; choose the surface count after","what":"Answer whether the team is one person or two, then re-derive the rate.","gains":["The only option that changes the rate rather than the scope","Answers a contradiction the plan has carried since 2026-08-31"],"costs":["Blocks every other form-factor decision until the answer exists","The contradiction has been open since 2026-08-31"],"system":"No change.","screens":"No change.","money":"None."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["The rate was measured and reproduces: 10 of 58 days, 1.21 a week, 70 days is 57.9 calendar weeks (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:227).","Two of the eight surfaces are cut and still carry commitments in nine places (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:304, :310).","Name one surface, delete the rest in the same edit, and let the deletions be visible.","Fix the 0.23 figure while you are there. It uses a narrower path set than the headline beside it."],"flip":"If a second person is real and named, re-derive the rate before quoting any sequence, because the density figures are not additive.","linked":["B1","FF1","FF12","FF2","FF7","FF8"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:65","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:203","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:227","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:231","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:304","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:310","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:364","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:462","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:130","src-tauri/tauri.conf.json:3","src-tauri/capabilities/default.json"]},{"id":"FF2","cat":"Form factor & surfaces","sub":"The rendering bet","weight":"high","q":"Do we chase rendering fidelity, meaning Live mode in MVP-0 and an Obsidian surface, or cut both?","lede":"The only demand signal with a vote behind it points at a feature the cheap surface cannot host, through a channel already cut.","visual":{"kind":"flow","perRow":4,"nodes":[{"label":"501 likes, 117 posts","note":"Obsidian's nested-construct render bug","tone":"neutral"},{"label":"Fix needs live preview","note":"nested constructs inside list items","tone":"neutral","edge":"needs"},{"label":"Obsidian plugin is cut","note":"the Live Preview tree is depth-1","tone":"stop","edge":"so"},{"label":"Only route left is Live mode","note":"inside our own shell","tone":"warn","edge":"then"},{"label":"No view-zone API in VS Code","note":"Live is standalone-only","tone":"stop","edge":"but"},{"label":"Standalone shell has to go first","note":"57.9 weeks at 1.21 days a week","tone":"stop","edge":"so"},{"label":"Or cut Live and Obsidian","note":"one feature set on either surface","tone":"accent","edge":"or"}],"note":"Every step was measured. Only the last is a choice.","caption":"How one forum vote forces the most expensive surface"},"stakes":"Keeping Live forces the standalone shell first and forecloses the cheaper surface.","state":["F1 lists Live, Edit, Split and Read as MVP-0 (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:55).","Decision 6 records there is no view-zone API, so Live is standalone-only (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:364).","The Obsidian plugin is cut at Exhibit 17 and still referenced in six places (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:304, :204, :338, :428, :464, :477).","§21 still promises the 501-like fix ships first as the free plugin (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:524)."],"path":["Live preview and the plugin arrived together with the Obsidian bet.","Round 2 killed the plugin on three grounds, including a depth-1 parse tree (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:127).","The nearest measured analogue landed 115 installs in fourteen days against our own 200 kill line (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:304)."],"tension":["In the only population with a vote, rendering fidelity beats review state 501 to 0 (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:25).","What that population wants is what a plugin cannot deliver, and what a plugin can deliver scored zero in three years.","Obsidian shipped the neighbouring nested-in-list fix twice in 2026, which shrinks the window further (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:304).","Obsidian core shipped no AI, agent, diff or review feature across its last twenty releases, so the shelf beside us is empty too."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"The vote, and the window","items":[["Obsidian forum, nested-construct rendering bug","501 likes, 117 posts, 18,331 views","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:25"],["Obsidian forum, closest review-state request","0 likes, 251 views, 1 post in three years","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:25, :410"],["Obsidian releases 2025-26 mentioning live preview","51 hits across 142 releases","CRITIQUE.md:362 (M13)"],["Obsidian shipped the neighbouring nested-in-list fix","twice in 2026","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:304"],["View-zone API in VS Code","none — Live is standalone-only","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:364"]]},{"type":"table","title":"Where the cut plugin still lives in the same document","cols":["Location","Line","What it still says"],"rows":[["Exhibit 17, the cut","304","CUT — the parse is unreachable, 115 installs against a 200 kill line"],["Exhibit 6, MVP-0 channels","204","\"Free Obsidian live-preview plugin, week 2; kill: under 200 installs in 14 days\""],["§14 ninety-day flowchart, the no-go branch","338","\"Stop: free plugin, services, engine\""],["Exhibit 24, retention lever","428","\"The plugin ... stays installed in a vault the user already opens daily\""],["§19 family diagram","464","\"Chrome extension · Obsidian plugin\""],["Exhibit 26, family members","477","\"Free; channels — MVP-1, week 2\""],["§21 rendering rules","524","the 501-like fix \"shipped first as the free plugin\""]]},{"type":"stat","title":"What that population votes for","items":[["Nested-construct rendering bug","501 likes","the thing a plugin cannot fix — PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:25"],["Closest review-state request","0 likes, 1 post in three years","the thing a plugin could ship — PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:25"],["Closest measured analogue, first 14 days","115 installs","against our own 200-install kill line — PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:304"],["Extensions and plugins already sitting in this niche","13 VS Code, 7 Obsidian, none above 1,540 downloads","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:559"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Keep Live in MVP-0 and ship the additive Obsidian review-state plugin","what":"Chase the rendering audience on both surfaces, with the 200-install kill line intact.","gains":["Keeps the only feature in the corpus with a 501-vote demand signal","Reuses the CodeMirror work either shell needs anyway"],"costs":["Forces the standalone shell first, at 57.9 calendar weeks","The plugin ships the feature that population scored 0 likes on"],"system":"A live-preview renderer plus a CodeMirror decoration layer over the sidecar.","screens":"S2 keeps all four mode tabs. A plugin settings pane is added.","money":"None. Both surfaces are free."},{"k":"b","label":"Cut Live from MVP-0, cut Obsidian, delete the six stale references","what":"Ship Edit, Split and Read, and say nothing about Obsidian anywhere in the plan.","gains":["Both surfaces can carry one feature set, so the extension stays viable","Removes six contradictions from a twenty-three-section document"],"costs":["Drops the only feature with a measured demand signal","Loses the Exhibit 24 retention lever and the flowchart's fallback branch"],"system":"No live-preview renderer, no CodeMirror plugin build.","screens":"S2 loses the Live tab. The family diagram loses a box.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Keep Live in the standalone shell only; no Obsidian surface","what":"Live returns if the shell wins FF1; the extension ships tint, revert and panel.","gains":["Preserves both audiences without promising a third-party surface","Lets FF1 decide rather than pre-empting it"],"costs":["Two divergent feature sets to document, test and support","Still forces the shell if the rendering audience is the buyer"],"system":"One engine, two renderers, one sidecar.","screens":"S2 differs between surfaces, which the prototype does not show.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Hold until the five-second screenshot test in weeks 1-2","what":"Show five people the S2 screenshot and decide after they answer.","gains":["Cheap and honest, and it is already scheduled for weeks 1-2","Costs nothing, and the five people are already scheduled"],"costs":["Blocks the form factor for two weeks","The test measures the tint, not Live mode"],"system":"No change.","screens":"No change.","money":"None."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["The 501 likes are Obsidian users complaining about Obsidian, and the plugin that would have met them there is cut (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:127).","Reaching them now needs them to install a second editor, which is the hardest ask in this plan.","Live is the most expensive mode to get right and the one that closes the cheaper surface (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:364).","Delete the six references in the same edit, line 338 first, because it makes the cut plugin the fallback if the product test fails."],"flip":"If the ten pilot strangers turn out to be Obsidian users, Live is the product and the extension is dead.","linked":["D8","FF1","FF14","G2"],"sources":["merged: FF6","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:25","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:55","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:204","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:304","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:338","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:364","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:410","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:428","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:464","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:477","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:524","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:559","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:127","docs/CRITIQUE.md:362"]},{"id":"FF4","cat":"Form factor & surfaces","sub":"Gates before the choice","weight":"high","q":"Which measurements must land before the surface is chosen, and with what pre-registered kill lines?","lede":"Neither surface has been tested at the moment the product exists for, and every engine number comes from vaults, not repos.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":30,"cols":[{"title":"Standalone shell","tone":"neutral"},{"title":"VS Code extension","tone":"neutral"}],"rows":[{"label":"Quiet write, nobody typing","cells":["0 throws across 1,354 blocks that proceeded","94/94 and 156/156 bytes, two harnesses"]},{"label":"Agent writes while a human types","cells":["unmeasured","unmeasured, named as a data-loss path"]},{"label":"Anchor after an out-of-band write","cells":["unmeasured","unmeasured"]},{"label":"Host save on a dirty buffer","cells":["not applicable","rewrites the file"]},{"label":"Refusal rate on Obsidian vaults","cells":["83.01% of 7,969 blocks","same engine, same number"]},{"label":"Refusal rate on repo markdown","cells":["unmeasured","unmeasured"]}],"note":"Cells read 2026-09-09 from the plan and the round-2 harnesses.","caption":"Six scenarios, two surfaces, five cells nobody has filled"},"stakes":"Choosing a surface on evidence that excludes the founding scenario means finding out after the shell is built.","state":["Decision 6 records an untested data-loss path on the extension's raw-write bypass (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:364).","Round 2's still-open list carries the contended write and the out-of-band anchor (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:146).","SOURCES.json is seven Obsidian vaults, and one wiki is 77% of the 8,513 files (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:514).","NF-1 is four days and the first item in the whole fix list (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:214)."],"path":["The round-2 harnesses proved byte-exactness in a quiet editor and stopped there (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:125).","The corpus was pinned on 2026-08-29, when Obsidian was the channel.","The buyer moved to the repo developer across four direction changes and the corpus did not move with it."],"tension":["The 83.01% refusal is 6,613 blocks from one cause: a hyphen item at column zero, an Obsidian tag habit (docs/ENGINE.md:146, :51).","If the buyer is the repo developer, NF-1's four days may repair a defect that buyer never hits.","Each test defers decision 6, and three deferrals are already queued in front of it.","A verifier written after the fact certified the quiet case while the loud one went unmeasured."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"What has been tested, per surface","cols":["Scenario","Standalone shell","VS Code extension","Status"],"rows":[["Quiet write, no human in the buffer","0 throws, 0 corruptions across the 1,354 frontmatter blocks that proceeded of 7,969 (ENGINE.md:146)","94/94 and 156/156 bytes","measured"],["Agent writes while a human is typing","unmeasured","unmeasured — named as a data-loss path","GAPS:146"],["Review anchor survives an out-of-band write","unmeasured","unmeasured","GAPS:146"],["Host save pipeline on a dirty buffer","not applicable","rewrites the file","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:364"]]},{"type":"bars","title":"Corpus composition, test/corpus/foreign/SOURCES.json, read 2026-09-09","note":"Seven Obsidian vaults, 8,513 markdown files, pinned 2026-08-29. Zero repo-shaped sources: no spec-kit specs, no docs/ folders, no agent-written specs. File counts reproduce exactly against the manifest.","unit":"markdown files","data":[["community-archive/obsidian-hub",6586],["oldwinter/knowledge-garden",961],["quanru/obsidian-example-lifeos",540],["s-blu/obsidian_dataview_example_vault",264],["kepano/kepano-obsidian",103],["erazlogo/obsidian-history-vault",40],["CyanVoxel/Obsidian-Vault-Template",19]]},{"type":"stat","title":"What that corpus produced","items":[["Splice writer refusals","6,615 of 7,969 frontmatter blocks = 83.01%","ENGINE.md:146"],["Of those, one cause","6,613 — a `-` item at column zero","ENGINE.md:146, :51"],["NF-1 budget, first item in the fix list","4 engineering days","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:214"],["Unaddressable top-level keys (NF-4)","2,447 of 29,288 across 937 of 7,969 files","ENGINE.md:213 — includes CJK keys from the same vaults"],["Refusal rate on repo-shaped markdown","unmeasured","no repo source is pinned"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Decide the form factor at the meeting; run neither test","what":"Take decision 6 on the evidence already in the plan and start building.","gains":["Keeps the schedule and unblocks every downstream decision today","Removes three deferrals sitting in front of decision 6"],"costs":["Chooses a surface on evidence that excludes the founding scenario","Risks spending the first four days on a defect the chosen buyer never hits"],"system":"No change.","screens":"No change.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Run the contention test only, with a one-byte kill written first","what":"Test an agent writing while a human types, on both surfaces, and nothing else.","gains":["Covers the only scenario the product exists for","Cheapest of the gating options"],"costs":["Leaves the engine's headline number measured on the wrong audience","The spike is unestimated, because no extension work has been estimated"],"system":"A contended-write harness for both surfaces.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Run both: contention test and a repo-shaped corpus, kills written first","what":"Gate decision 6 on two measurements with kill lines agreed before either runs.","gains":["Answers whether the surface is safe and whether NF-1 is aimed at the right buyer","Converts two opinions into gates before they can be argued away"],"costs":["Delays decision 6 by the length of two spikes","Assembling and pinning a new corpus is real work, not one command"],"system":"A contended-write harness plus a second pinned corpus in test/corpus.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Run both, but decide the surface anyway; results feed build order","what":"Take decision 6 now and let the measurements change what gets built first.","gains":["Keeps momentum and still produces the evidence","The kill lines can still be written, just not enforced"],"costs":["Risks discovering the losing surface after the shell is built","A result that arrives after the choice tends to be re-argued"],"system":"Same two harnesses, no gate.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"c","recCase":["The whole claim is that bytes survive when a machine writes into a document a person is reading, and that case is untested on both surfaces (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:146).","The corpus question is among the cheapest on the list and it gates the most expensive one (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:514).","One repo-corpus run says whether NF-1, four days and first in the plan, matters to the chosen buyer (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:214).","Write both kill lines before either test runs, so the answer cannot be re-argued once it is inconvenient."],"flip":"If the two spikes together cost more than a week, run the contention test alone and record the corpus as unmeasured in the meeting notes.","linked":["FF1","FF11"],"sources":["merged: FF10","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:214","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:216","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:364","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:514","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:125","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:146","docs/ENGINE.md:51","docs/ENGINE.md:146","docs/ENGINE.md:213","test/corpus/foreign/SOURCES.json"]},{"id":"FF5","cat":"Form factor & surfaces","sub":"Name and store","weight":"high","q":"Does the marketplace name collision veto the extension, or does the extension ship under the engine's name?","lede":"If form factor resolves toward VS Code, the name is already owned in that store by an extension alive since 2019.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":26,"cols":[{"title":"Keep frontmatter","tone":"neutral"},{"title":"mdmax in the store","tone":"accent"},{"title":"Rename the product","tone":"neutral"}],"rows":[{"label":"VS Code store name","cells":["Second to an 82,265-install incumbent","Free","Free"]},{"label":"npm name","cells":["Taken; @frontmatter is theirs","mdmax is free, HTTP 404","Depends on the new name"]},{"label":"Cost in conversation","cells":["\"Not the VS Code one\", forever","Two names to explain","One name, once"]},{"label":"What it unblocks","cells":["Nothing","FF12's package surface","Every surface, later"]},{"label":"What it costs","cells":["A permanent qualifier","A two-name story","Every internal reference"]}],"note":"Store and npm states read from the record, 2026-08-29 to 2026-09-07.","caption":"Three name strategies against the store, npm and the conversation"},"stakes":"Ship into the store under a taken name and every search result belongs to someone else.","state":["The collision appears at the key figures and inside decision 6, with no resolution proposed (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:13, :364).","Round 2 found it worse than recorded: 82,265 installs, alive at v10.12.0 on 2026-08-21 (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:132).","\"Frontmatter Studio\" was taken on 2026-09-07, and the @frontmatter npm scope is the incumbent's (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:132).","npm `mdmax` and `frontmatter-cert` are both free, at HTTP 404 (docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:1403)."],"path":["The record flagged 80,605 installs on 2026-08-29 and the plan did not mention it until v15 (docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:4799).","The gap register called the name untreated (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:50).","The record already priced the tax: not the VS Code one, in every conversation (docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:5632)."],"tension":["The collision taxes the package surface as well as the store, so it constrains FF12, not only FF1.","A rename is one decision now and a hundred edits later.","The FRONTMATTER EU word mark was reported but never reproduced across five blocked registries (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:146).","The record itself says the naming decision and the positioning decision are one decision (docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:5632)."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"The incumbent, and what names are left","items":[["Front Matter CMS, VS Code installs","82,265","GAPS:132, alive at v10.12.0 on 2026-08-21"],["Same, read nine days earlier","80,605","RECORD:4799, read 2026-08-29"],["npm `frontmatter`","taken (HTTP 200) — a dead 2022 0.0.3 YAML parser","RECORD:1403, :4827"],["npm `@frontmatter` scope","the incumbent's","GAPS:132"],["npm `mdmax`","free (HTTP 404)","RECORD:1403"],["npm `frontmatter-cert`","free (HTTP 404)","RECORD:1403"],["\"Frontmatter Studio\"","taken 2026-09-07","GAPS:132"],["gray-matter, the generic-name substrate","about 35.8M downloads a month (derived: 8,352,860 weekly x 4.28)","RECORD:9297, read 2026-08-30; CRITIQUE.md:1728 gives 35,124,859 for 2026-08-31 — same order, different day"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Rename the whole product before any store listing","what":"Pick one free name and use it on the app, the store, npm and the site.","gains":["Removes the tax on every surface at once","One decision, taken before anything is published"],"costs":["Discards whatever recognition the name has built across the record","Every internal document and repo reference changes"],"system":"Package name, repo name and bundle identifier all change.","screens":"Every screen's title bar and the launcher wordmark.","money":"A domain, and the time to re-check five registries."},{"k":"b","label":"Ship the extension as mdmax; keep frontmatter for the app","what":"The engine's name goes to the store and npm; the app keeps the product name.","gains":["Uses the one name that is free on npm and in the store","Describes what the extension is, which is the engine"],"costs":["A two-name story to explain in every conversation","Search splits between two words"],"system":"Package published as mdmax; the app keeps its identifier.","screens":"The extension's marketplace page carries a different wordmark.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Keep the name everywhere and pay the tax","what":"Ship as frontmatter in the store and accept second place in search.","gains":["One brand across every surface and every document","No rework in the record, the repo or the prototype"],"costs":["A permanent qualifier against an 82,265-install incumbent","Seven years of search history belongs to them"],"system":"No change.","screens":"No change.","money":"Paid in acquisition, not in cash."},{"k":"d","label":"Stay out of the marketplace; the collision becomes a search problem","what":"No store listing at all, so the collision only affects web search.","gains":["Sidesteps the store collision entirely","Leaves the name open until a surface is actually chosen"],"costs":["Forecloses the option FF1 exists to weigh","Leaves the npm collision unsolved for FF12"],"system":"No extension build.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["The engine is what would ship into the store, it is already called mdmax, and mdmax is free on npm where frontmatter is not (docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:1403).","That makes the two-name story a description rather than an apology.","It unblocks FF12, which needs a free npm name and has only this one.","The EU word mark is still unreproduced, so the legal half of this is unsettled either way (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:146)."],"flip":"If the founders want one brand on every surface, this becomes a rename and the answer is (a), decided before the first listing.","linked":["FF1","FF11","FF12"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:13","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:364","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:50","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:132","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:146","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:1403","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:4799","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:4827","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:5632","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:9297","docs/CRITIQUE.md:1728"],"dupes":{"dropped":["G21"],"why":"Does the marketplace name collision veto the extension or does the extension ship under the engine's name. Recs b vs a — one says ship as mdmax, the other says rename the product first. Form factor & surfaces owns extension scope; N1/N4 carry the naming half."}},{"id":"FF11","cat":"Form factor & surfaces","sub":"Extension scope","weight":"high","q":"If an extension ships, what is inside it, where is it published, and does it carry its own key?","lede":"Decision 6 names an extension without saying what is in it, and the answer moves the cost by an order of magnitude.","visual":{"kind":"screen","title":"The extension inside VS Code","panes":[{"label":"Host supplies","w":32,"rows":[{"label":"Explorer, palette, keymap, outline","meta":"free","tone":"sunk"},{"label":"Model picker and MCP registration","meta":"unverified on forks","tone":"warn"},{"label":"Multi-file diff, review and unreview","meta":"merged 2026-07-03","tone":"warn"}]},{"label":"Thin version adds","w":38,"rows":[{"label":"Tint per span, read from the sidecar","meta":"our claim","tone":"accent"},{"label":"One-key revert","meta":"byte range","tone":"accent"},{"label":"Review panel, state kept in the repo","meta":"the differentiator","tone":"accent"}]},{"label":"Only if thick","w":30,"rows":[{"label":"Idea mode and decision flow","meta":"F5, F6","tone":"neutral"},{"label":"Repo docs scan","meta":"F7","tone":"neutral"},{"label":"Table editing","meta":"5-8 d, host gives none","tone":"stop"}]}],"note":"The host now ships a per-file reviewed marker of its own, gated and undocumented.","caption":"What the host gives, what thin adds, what only thick adds"},"stakes":"A thick extension is a second product with no estimate, built by one person at 1.21 days a week.","state":["Decision 6 says only VS Code extension, with no scope, no feature list and no estimate (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:364).","It claims the host's model picker deletes fix #6, three days of BYO-key work (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:219, :364).","Whether Cursor and other forks honour the VS Code model APIs is still open (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:146).","No store is named anywhere in the plan; open-vsx.org appears once, as a probed host."],"path":["The extension was measured as a mechanism in round 2 and never scoped as a product (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:125).","Stack Overflow 2025 puts VS Code at 75.9% and Cursor at 17.9% of IDE usage (docs/CRITIQUE.md:363).","Microsoft merged a per-file review and unreview operation into the Agents window on 2026-07-03, milestone 1.128.0 (api.github.com, PR 324218)."],"tension":["Thin tests the one surviving claim and lands in a niche whose measured ceiling is 400 installs (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:24).","The host now ships the per-file version of that marker, behind a setting and absent from its public docs.","What the host has not shipped is state stored in the repository, per span, surviving a machine change.","Three days of BYO-key work is deleted on an assumption never tested on a single fork."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"IDE usage, Stack Overflow 2025 (n=49k+, CRITIQUE.md:363 and :431)","cols":["Editor","Usage","Store it pulls from"],"rows":[["VS Code","75.9%","Microsoft Marketplace"],["Cursor","17.9%","not established in our record"],["Sublime Text","10.5%","not a VS Code host"],["Claude Code","9.7%","runs inside a host"],["Zed","7.3%","not a VS Code host"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"What rides on the unverified claim","items":[["Extensions in the Microsoft Marketplace","135,646","RECORD:9176, read 2026-08-30"],["BYO key, fix #6","3 engineering days — \"deleted\" by the host model picker","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:219, :364"],["Model-picker support on Cursor and other forks","unmeasured","GAPS:146"],["Which registry the forks serve extensions from","not established in the corpus","only open-vsx.org as a probed host, COMPLETE-RECORD:20787"],["Consequence if absent","no AI on about a quarter of the host population, or fix #6 comes back","derived from the two rows above"]]},{"type":"table","title":"Table-stakes gaps in the standalone shell, and whether the host supplies them (r24-v1, eight ranked gaps)","cols":["Gap","Cost","Host supplies it?"],"rows":[["Heading hotkeys, link, list/quote/task toggles, move line","0.5 d","Yes (markdown-all-in-one, 14.45M installs)"],["Outline hotkey and fuzzy heading jump","0.5 d","Yes"],["Command palette that indexes everything","1-2 d","Yes"],["Quick-switcher deltas","0.5 d","Yes"],["HTML paste to markdown","2-3 d","Partly"],["Table editing: Tab nav, add/remove row and column, alignment","5-8 d","No"],["Splice-backed table writes","+2 d","No"],["Customisable keymap","3-4 d","Yes"]],"note":"Sums to 14.5-20.5 days; mid-point 17.5. The five host-supplied rows are about 6.5 of those days at their mid-points."},{"type":"stat","title":"The niche the thin version enters","items":[["All 13 markdown-review extensions combined","1,217 installs","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:9, :24"],["Ceiling of the best one","400 installs","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:24"],["mddiff, our sentence shipped 2026-06-03","74 installs in three months","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:24"],["Nearest sidecar pattern, SpecKit Companion","9,367 installs","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:152"],["git-ai, commit-level attribution","61,517 installs","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:151"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Thin, on the host model picker, Microsoft Marketplace only","what":"Tint, revert and panel over the sidecar; the host supplies the AI; one listing.","gains":["Cheapest instrument for the one claim that survived round 1","Keeps fix #6's three days deleted"],"costs":["No AI on forks that do not honour the model API","Gives up roughly a quarter of the measured IDE population"],"system":"No key UI, no keychain, no second registry.","screens":"S11's key field never ships in the extension.","money":"Saves 3 engineering days if the assumption holds."},{"k":"b","label":"Thin first, own key, both stores, widening line written before publishing","what":"Same scope, plus a BYO-key fallback, published to Open VSX as well.","gains":["AI works on every host, using the key work the shell needs anyway","A pre-registered line decides widening instead of an argument"],"costs":["Costs the three days decision 6 claimed to save","A second listing on a registry we have not confirmed the forks use"],"system":"BYO key and keychain shared between extension and shell.","screens":"S11's key field ships on both surfaces.","money":"3 engineering days, never wasted."},{"k":"c","label":"Thick: F1 through F8 inside the host","what":"Rebuild the product as an extension, including generation and the docs scan.","gains":["Competes above the 400-install niche, where git-ai sits at 61,517","Answers the table-stakes gap and the review claim on one surface"],"costs":["A second product with no estimate anywhere in the plan","The host supplies none of the 5-8 days of table editing"],"system":"Every feature ported to the host's APIs.","screens":"All nine screens rebuilt in the host idiom.","money":"Unpriced."},{"k":"d","label":"No extension","what":"Standalone only, so the question does not arise.","gains":["One surface to maintain at 1.21 engineering days a week","No store listing, no host API to depend on, no name collision"],"costs":["Removes the only measured route to the population that has the problem","Leaves decision 6 with two live options instead of three"],"system":"No change.","screens":"No change.","money":"None."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["The saving being protected is three days; the risk is AI silently failing for a quarter of the hosts (docs/CRITIQUE.md:363).","The key work is the same work the standalone shell needs, so it is never wasted (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:219).","Thin is right on the evidence: SpecKit Companion at 9,367 and git-ai at 61,517 are both single-purpose (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:151, :152).","Set the widening line honestly. mddiff took three months to reach 74 installs (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:24)."],"flip":"If the fork test shows the model API is honoured, drop the fallback from the extension and keep it in the app.","linked":["FF1","FF12","FF5"],"sources":["merged: FF13","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:9","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:24","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:151","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:152","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:219","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:364","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:125","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:146","docs/CRITIQUE.md:363","docs/CRITIQUE.md:431","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:9176","docs/FRONTMATTER-COMPLETE-RECORD-2026-08-30.md:20787","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r24-v1-table-stakes.md:87","https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode/pulls/324218"]},{"id":"FF12","cat":"Form factor & surfaces","sub":"Package and CLI","weight":"high","q":"Do we add a fourth option to decision 6, the engine as an npm package, MCP server and agent plugin, and run it first?","lede":"The repo's own critique recommends a form factor decision 6 does not list, prices it at a week, and pre-registers its kill number.","visual":{"kind":"flow","perRow":3,"nodes":[{"label":"Splice engine, 3,614 lines","note":"14.2% of source, the only thing owned","tone":"accent"},{"label":"npm package","note":"mdmax is free; frontmatter is not","tone":"accent","edge":"ship as"},{"label":"MCP server","note":"agents write through the engine","tone":"accent","edge":"and"},{"label":"Agent plugin","note":"runs inside Claude Code or Codex","tone":"accent","edge":"and"},{"label":"Thirty days of installs","note":"about one week of work to get here","tone":"neutral","edge":"then"},{"label":"Under 100 installs, stop","note":"kill number written before the run","tone":"stop","edge":"if"}],"note":"The critique's own recommendation, absent from decision 6.","caption":"One week and one number, before 58 weeks go into a shell"},"stakes":"Committing 58 weeks to a shell without running the one-week instrument that could have predicted the outcome.","state":["Decision 6 offers exactly three options and no package route (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:364).","The family diagram lists mdmax cert as a Max-tier GitHub Action (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:462).","§9 fix #10 records that the cert CLI exits 1 with ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND and is not among the 26 scripts (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:224).","The critique recommends the package route outright, at about one week (docs/CRITIQUE.md:163)."],"path":["The record lists npm, VS Code and CLI as the genuinely unexplored option (docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:9439).","Neither the record nor the critique reached decision 6.","A free markdown agent-review skill for Claude Code and Codex, petergyang/human-review, went from 0 to 1,241 stars and 98 forks in six weeks after 2026-07-27 (api.github.com)."],"tension":["The corpus's strongest recommendation is missing from the decision the founders are being asked to make.","The shape is already shipping: dealfluence/adeu is MIT, 149 stars, and converged on the same refuse-on-ambiguity engine for .docx (docs/CRITIQUE.md:1700).","The nearest free comparator reached 1,241 stars in six weeks, which sizes the attention and says nothing about payment.","Giving the engine away MIT forecloses selling it, and an independent team already shipped the mechanism MIT."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"The unlisted fourth option","items":[["Engine share of the codebase","3,614 of 25,407 lines = 14.2%","re-measured 2026-09-09"],["Cost of the package + MCP + plugin route","about one week, against a 240-day plan","CRITIQUE.md:163"],["Pre-registered kill number","fewer than 100 installs in 30 days","CRITIQUE.md:163"],["Information yield, per the critique","\"higher than rounds 21-25 combined\"","CRITIQUE.md:163"],["gray-matter, the substrate","about 35.8M npm downloads a month","RECORD:9297, read 2026-08-30"],["npm name `mdmax`","free (HTTP 404)","RECORD:1403"],["Competitor already shipping this shape","dealfluence/adeu, MIT, 149 stars, pushed 2026-08-30","CRITIQUE.md:33, :1700 — for .docx"],["`mdmax cert` today","exits 1, ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND; not among the 26 scripts","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:224, re-verified"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Add it as a fourth option and run it first, with the 100-install kill","what":"Publish the engine as an MIT package, an MCP server and an agent plugin.","gains":["One week buys an installs number before 58 weeks go into any shell","The one channel whose ceiling matches the funnel's requirement"],"costs":["Gives the engine away, which forecloses selling it as a library","A free comparator already holds the attention this would compete for"],"system":"Engine extracted, CLI fixed, MCP server built.","screens":"None. This surface has no screens.","money":"None in, about one week out."},{"k":"b","label":"Fix the CLI only, one day, and keep it internal","what":"Make mdmax cert runnable and leave it as a Max-tier gate.","gains":["Makes the certificate real and closes fix #10","Closes fix #10, broken for 37 days after the commit that claimed it landed"],"costs":["Produces no external signal and no installs","Leaves the fourth option unmodelled"],"system":"Extensions and the alias fixed; cert added to package.json.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Leave the package surface unmodelled, as the plan has it","what":"Decision 6 keeps three options and the engine stays internal.","gains":["Keeps the meeting to three choices","No licence decision, and the engine is not given away"],"costs":["Leaves the cheapest instrument in the plan unrun","The record's own strongest recommendation stays untested"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Ship the package after MVP-0 exits","what":"Sequence it behind the ten-stranger test.","gains":["No new work before the pilot","The pilot keeps every engineering day between now and the exit test"],"costs":["If the pilot fails, the instrument that could have predicted it was never run","An MIT competitor is already in this shape and moving"],"system":"Deferred.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["A one-week test with a written kill number, run before a 58-week build, is the best information trade in the plan (docs/CRITIQUE.md:163).","The critique reached that conclusion independently, and it never reached decision 6 (docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:9439).","The exclusivity being protected is thin. An independent team already shipped the same refuse-on-ambiguity mechanism MIT (docs/CRITIQUE.md:1700).","Run the five-regex linter comparison before pricing Max on the certificate (docs/ENGINE.md:899)."],"flip":"If the founders intend to sell the engine as a licensed library, run it source-available instead and keep the same kill number.","linked":["E24","F26","FF1","FF11","FF14","FF5"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:224","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:364","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:462","docs/CRITIQUE.md:33","docs/CRITIQUE.md:163","docs/CRITIQUE.md:1700","docs/ENGINE.md:899","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:1403","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:9297","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:9439","https://api.github.com/repos/petergyang/human-review"],"dupes":{"dropped":["E31","F14","PL14","MK11"],"why":"Five areas independently ask whether the splice engine ships free as an npm package + MCP server as a pre-build demand probe. Option sets map 1:1 (ship now with a pre-registered install kill / ship after the engine fixes / keep it inside the editor / don't publish). Recs disagree five ways: FF12 run it first, E31 after NF-1+NF-4, F14 both package and integration, PL14 MIT this month, MK11 make it the launch. Form factor & surfaces owns it because FF12 frames it correctly as a fourth option to the surface decision; the licence rider survives in E24/L20."}},{"id":"FF7","cat":"Form factor & surfaces","sub":"Browser","weight":"medium","q":"Does the `?src=` URL parameter ship in MVP-0, and do the three stale Chrome-extension references get deleted?","lede":"The cheapest surface in the plan costs hours, sits behind a surface already cut, and appears in no tier and no sequence.","visual":{"kind":"flow","perRow":3,"nodes":[{"label":"A public .md URL","note":"raw.githubusercontent.com","tone":"neutral"},{"label":"access-control-allow-origin: *","note":"no extension needed to read it","tone":"good","edge":"sends"},{"label":"?src=<raw url>","note":"one parameter on the web app","tone":"accent","edge":"so"},{"label":"Rendered, with review state","note":"the reader installs nothing","tone":"accent","edge":"gives"},{"label":"Chrome extension","note":"store listing, Manifest V3, already cut","tone":"stop","edge":"instead of"}],"note":"The CORS header is what killed the extension.","caption":"The cut surface, and the parameter that replaces it in hours"},"stakes":"Leaving the only hours-long distribution surface unscheduled is a choice nobody made deliberately.","state":["Exhibit 17 cuts the Chrome extension and names `?src=` as the replacement (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:310).","Exhibit 6 still lists the Chrome extension as an MVP-1 surface (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:203).","So do the family diagram and Exhibit 26 (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:464, :477).","`?src=` appears once in the whole document, in no tier and no sequence (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:310)."],"path":["Round 2 killed the extension on the CORS header alone (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:134).","The 1.5M reader figure summed a 500,000-user reader with a 1,000,000-user clipper (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:310).","The real reading population is about 647,000, and its leader has not shipped a store build in over two years (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:310)."],"tension":["Three places promise a surface one place killed.","The replacement is the only surface measured in hours, and it has no owner and no tier.","If FF8 goes desktop-primary, `?src=` becomes a viewer feature rather than a channel."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"The cut, and what replaces it","items":[["Claimed browser reader population","1.5M","refuted — two products summed, one a clipper"],["Real reading population","about 647,000","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:310"],["Market leader's last store build","over two years ago","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:310"],["raw.githubusercontent.com CORS header","access-control-allow-origin: *","no extension needed — PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:310"],["Cost of the `?src=` replacement","hours","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:310"],["Times `?src=` appears in the plan","1 (line 310 only)","verified 2026-09-09"],["Places the cut extension still appears","3 (lines 203, 464, 477)","verified 2026-09-09"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Ship `?src=` in MVP-0 and delete the Chrome extension from all three places","what":"One URL parameter in the pilot, and a plan that says one thing about the browser.","gains":["Gives the web app a shareable entry point before the first Show HN","Costs hours, needs no store listing and no Manifest V3"],"costs":["Adds a surface to a plan FF14 says is already over-committed","Read-only until a repo is connected"],"system":"A query parameter and a fetch path in the web app.","screens":"A read-only variant of S2, with no tree and no tabs.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Ship `?src=` at MVP-1, as Exhibit 17 implies","what":"Keep the current sequence and add the parameter after the pilot.","gains":["Nothing changes in the ninety-day sequence","The parameter still ships, so the surface is not lost"],"costs":["Leaves the cheapest surface out of the window where the ten strangers are watching","Three stale references stay in a document going to a founder meeting"],"system":"Deferred.","screens":"Deferred.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Reinstate the Chrome extension","what":"Build and list a Manifest V3 extension that opens .md URLs in frontmatter.","gains":["A store listing is a channel with its own search surface","It could show review state on a file the reader does not own"],"costs":["Requires overturning two measured findings","Targets about 647,000 readers whose leader has not shipped in two years"],"system":"A Manifest V3 build and a store review cycle.","screens":"An extension popup nobody has designed.","money":"A one-off store registration fee."},{"k":"d","label":"No browser-link surface at all","what":"Neither the extension nor the parameter; the web app opens repos and folders only.","gains":["Simplest to maintain and to document","One fewer surface on a plan FF14 says is already over-committed"],"costs":["Removes the only way a person who has installed nothing can see the product","Contradicts Exhibit 17, which already named the replacement"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["It costs hours, needs no store, and is the only path by which someone who has installed nothing sees the product (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:310).","The three stale references cost nothing to delete and are the difference between a plan that reads as decided and one that reads as unedited.","Delete them in the same edit as FF2's six, so the surface list is corrected once."],"flip":"If FF8 resolves to desktop-primary, `?src=` is a viewer feature rather than a channel and its priority drops.","linked":["FF14","FF8"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:203","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:310","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:464","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:477","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:134"],"dupes":{"dropped":["G25"],"why":"Does the ?src= URL parameter ship, and when. Recs conflict outright: FF7 ships it in MVP-0, G25 builds it only as the demo surface. Form factor & surfaces owns surfaces; the channel claim follows."}},{"id":"FF9","cat":"Form factor & surfaces","sub":"Mobile","weight":"medium","q":"Is mobile a stated permanent non-goal, a read-only reviewer at MVP-1, or left undecided?","lede":"The plan cuts mobile from every tier while its own critique classes it Must-be and ranks it the top churn risk.","visual":{"kind":"screen","title":"A read-only mobile reviewer, if it ships","panes":[{"label":"Unreviewed","w":38,"rows":[{"label":"specs/auth.md, 4 spans","meta":"agent, 2h ago","mark":"4","tone":"warn"},{"label":"docs/AGENTS.md, 1 span","meta":"agent, today","mark":"1","tone":"warn"},{"label":"README.md","meta":"clear","mark":"","tone":"good"}]},{"label":"Span","w":62,"rows":[{"label":"Tinted paragraph, rendered read-only","meta":"hash matched","tone":"accent"},{"label":"Mark read","meta":"one tap","tone":"good"},{"label":"Revert","meta":"not offered on mobile","tone":"sunk"},{"label":"Attribution: prompt not recorded","meta":"from the commit trailer","tone":"neutral"}]}],"note":"Reading and marking only. No editing, no revert, no file tree.","caption":"What a mobile reviewer would contain, and what it refuses"},"stakes":"If review state is the product, the reviewer is the person most often away from a laptop.","state":["§22 says mobile is about 15% of complaints, not in v1, later a reader and reviewer (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:539).","Exhibit 6 lists mobile in the Absent row for both MVP-0 and MVP-1 (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:205).","Exhibit 2 gives mobile browsers repo connect only (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:92).","The three statements do not agree with each other."],"path":["The critique classed it Kano Must-be on the ground that every product opened has a first-class mobile story (docs/CRITIQUE.md:203).","It also ranked it the number one churn-risk gap, present but cut from every stage (docs/CRITIQUE.md:680).","The record's own counter-analysis is tagged inference, not measurement (docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:2067)."],"tension":["The web app already renders documents in a mobile browser, so a read-only reviewer is scope rather than a new build.","FF14 says surface count is the binding constraint, and this adds one.","The record's counter-evidence, the 1/32 and 7:1 ratios, is inference and cannot settle it (docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:2067)."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"Two sources pulling opposite ways","items":[["Kano class","MUST-BE","CRITIQUE.md:203"],["Ranked churn risk","#1 gap, cut from every stage","CRITIQUE.md:680; RECORD:10836"],["The record's own verdict on sequencing","\"an MVP-2 item that will feel like an MVP-1 item\"","RECORD:10836"],["Tiers mobile appears in","0 of 3","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:205"],["Markdown-native mobile vs the OS notes app","about 1/32 the size — tagged [inference] in the record, not measured","RECORD:2067"],["Capture-shaped vs authoring-shaped markdown apps","about 7:1 — same [inference] tag","RECORD:2067"],["Named mobile complaint in that thread","\"Make Obsidian Sync work in background (on Mobile)\", 124 posts","RECORD:2067"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"State mobile as a permanent non-goal, on the page","what":"Write it down as a refusal alongside plugins, hosting and code execution.","gains":["Honest, cheap, and it makes the plan say one thing","Removes a Must-be from the churn list by declaring it out of scope"],"costs":["Accepts a Must-be absence in a category where every competitor has a mobile story","The reviewer job is the one most likely to happen away from a desk"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None. The mobile row leaves Exhibit 2.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Non-goal for MVP-0; a read-only mobile reviewer at MVP-1","what":"Mobile shows unreviewed spans and lets a person mark them read. No editing.","gains":["Matches the product's own logic: the reviewer is mobile, the author is not","The web app already renders, so this is scope rather than a new build"],"costs":["Adds a surface to a plan whose binding constraint is surface count","Marking read on a phone is the weakest form of review"],"system":"Responsive layout plus a mobile write path for review.jsonl.","screens":"One new narrow-viewport screen; S4 collapses to a list.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Leave it undecided","what":"Keep the current wording across §22, Exhibit 2 and Exhibit 6.","gains":["Nothing is committed today","Nothing is foreclosed while the pilot runs"],"costs":["The plan keeps saying three different things about one surface","A Must-be gap stays unranked and unowned"],"system":"No change.","screens":"No change.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Mobile-first review, desktop-first editing","what":"Reviewing is designed for the phone and editing is designed for the desk.","gains":["The strongest expression of the review-state thesis","Reviewing on a phone is the behaviour the counter exists to trigger"],"costs":["Doubles the surface count before anyone has been asked whether they want review state","Two design systems on 1.21 engineering days a week"],"system":"Two layouts and two interaction models over one sidecar.","screens":"A full mobile screen set alongside the desktop nine.","money":"None."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["Reviewing is the one job here that genuinely happens away from a laptop.","The web app already renders in a mobile browser, so this is a scope decision rather than a build (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:92).","Saying non-goal for MVP-0 and naming MVP-1 turns three inconsistent sentences into one commitment.","The counter-evidence is weaker than it looks: the 1/32 and 7:1 ratios are tagged inference (docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:2067)."],"flip":"If the twenty team conversations say reviewers review at their desks, mobile drops to (a) and the plan is simpler for it.","linked":["FF14","FF8"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:92","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:205","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:539","docs/CRITIQUE.md:203","docs/CRITIQUE.md:680","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:2067","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:10836"],"dupes":{"dropped":["F28"],"why":"Is mobile a permanent non-goal, a read-only reviewer at MVP-1, or undecided. Recs b vs c. Form factor & surfaces owns surfaces."}},{"id":"F1","cat":"Features","sub":"Review state","weight":"critical","q":"Do we prove the review anchor survives an out-of-band write before spending the eighteen days on the store?","lede":"Review state is the largest row in MVP-0, and its anchor has never been tested against the one write it exists for.","visual":{"kind":"flow","perRow":3,"nodes":[{"label":"Agent rewrites the file","note":"Claude Code, Cursor, git checkout","tone":"neutral"},{"label":"Bytes move, hashes change","tone":"neutral"},{"label":"The journal never saw it","note":"git, other editors and agents bypass it","tone":"warn"},{"label":"Splice locator relocates spans","tone":"accent"},{"label":"Tint lands on the right span","tone":"good"},{"label":"Tint is wrong in its own demo","tone":"stop","dashed":true}],"note":"Never run. This is the only scenario the product exists for.","caption":"The out-of-band write, and the two ways the anchor can end"},"stakes":"If relocation fails on an agent's rewrite, the tint is wrong exactly when the demo needs it right.","state":["Exhibit 1 budgets store 6d, rendering 5d, revert 3d, panel 4d, all in MVP-0 (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:56).","Spans are anchored by byte range plus content hash; the journal is deliberately not the anchor (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:135).","No store exists in `src/` today. `.frontmatter/` appears only in the mdmax cert contract.","A content-hash prototype on one spec-kit and one superpowers repo is already scheduled for weeks 3–4 (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:354)."],"path":["Review state became the headline after bytes, authorship and answer-in-place were each refuted.","The 2026-09-08 round attacked it too; what survived is across people and across tools, on a working tree with no pull request (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:124).","Nothing was built to test the tool-agnostic anchor, which is that claim's only mechanism."],"tension":["Eighteen days at the measured 1.21 engineering days per week is about fifteen calendar weeks (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:227).","Whether the anchor survives an out-of-band write is still open after round 2 (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:146).","Paragraph anchoring relocates more reliably and gives up per-span; blob anchoring gives up the working-tree case."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"F2 as specified, against the measured rate","items":[["Store, rendering, revert, panel","18 engineering days","Exhibit 1, PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:56"],["Measured engineering days per calendar week","1.21","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:227 — 10 of 58 calendar days touched src/, src-tauri/ or test/"],["F2 alone at that rate","about 15 calendar weeks","derived: 18 ÷ 1.21"],["Evidence class in the plan's own table","Untested","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:188"],["Review-state store in src/ today","None — no .frontmatter/review.jsonl writer, no per-span hash store, no review module","measured: src/modules/ holds ai, ai-tools, app-shell, auth, drafts, editor, export, graph, mdmax, preview, repository, share, vault"]]},{"type":"bars","title":"Purpose-built markdown-review extensions, VS Code Marketplace, 2026-09-08","note":"PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:24. mddiff, published 2026-06-03, is this product's own sentence already shipped.","data":[["All 13 extensions, summed",1217],["Largest single extension",400],["mddiff",74]],"unit":"installs"},{"type":"bars","title":"Obsidian forum, one population, one metric, 2026-09-08","note":"PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:410. The rendering bug the plan treats as a channel, against the closest existing request for review state.","data":[["Nested code block rendering bug",501],["Suggestion Mode like Google Docs/Word",3],["Tracking changes within notes",1],["List of changes since last view",0]],"unit":"likes"},{"type":"stat","title":"What is built and what is assumed","items":[["Review-state store in src/ today","None — .frontmatter/ appears only in src/modules/mdmax/domain/cert-contract.ts, not as a store","measured: grep for review.jsonl / sidecar / .frontmatter/ over src/"],["Anchor design","byte range + content hash, relocated by the splice locator","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:56"],["Tested against an agent write","No","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:146 — listed as still open after round 2"],["Nearest shipped pattern","SpecKit Companion .spec-context.json, 9,367 installs","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:135"]]},{"type":"table","title":"Writers that bypass the journal, per the plan's own sidecar note","cols":["Writer","Reaches the file","Reaches the journal"],"rows":[["frontmatter's own splice","Yes","Yes"],["The user's agent (Claude Code, Cursor)","Yes","No"],["git checkout, merge, rebase","Yes","No"],["Any other editor","Yes","No"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Prove relocation on a real agent rewrite first, then commit the eighteen days","what":"Two to three days of prototype on one spec-kit repo and one superpowers repo before any store code.","gains":["Answers the load-bearing assumption for a sixth of one feature's cost","It is already a scheduled milestone, so no new week is invented"],"costs":["Delays the first visible tint by two to three days","A prototype can become the product and the store never gets budgeted"],"system":"Exercises the splice locator against files we did not write; no store schema yet.","screens":"None. The prototype is a script and a diff.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Build store and rendering now (11d), treat relocation failures as a later fix","what":"The tint ships on files frontmatter wrote, and out-of-band relocation is patched when it breaks.","gains":["The tint is on screen seven engineering days earlier","The pilot has something to look at inside the quarter"],"costs":["A structural failure surfaces around week 9 with eleven days sunk","Revert stays a git operation, so the one-key demo beat is missing"],"system":"Store and rendering land on top of an unproven locator.","screens":"S2 tint and the unreviewed bars in the tree.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Narrow the anchor to whole paragraphs","what":"Review state is recorded per paragraph rather than per span, which relocates more reliably.","gains":["Fewer false relocations on ordinary agent rewrites","Smaller store, simpler rendering"],"costs":["Gives up per-span, the half Google actually charges for","Weakens attribution in F3 at the same time"],"system":"The span table becomes a paragraph table; the hash key changes.","screens":"Tint blocks get coarser and the hover card loses byte ranges.","money":"Drops the one granularity a comparable is paid for."},{"k":"d","label":"Demote review state to a feature and lead with spec-kit self-certification","what":"The tint still ships, but the plan stops selling it as the reason the product exists.","gains":["Honest to the round-2 result","Frees eighteen days for the engine and the scan"],"costs":["The plan then has no headline","Most of the other twelve rows were justified by sitting inside this loop"],"system":"Store still needed, smaller and unrushed.","screens":"S4 stops being the front door.","money":"Pro loses the capability its price was anchored to."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["The surviving claim is across tools on a working tree with no pull request, and a tool-agnostic anchor is its only mechanism.","Two to three days against eighteen, on a milestone the plan already schedules for weeks 3–4 (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:354).","The failure it catches cannot be patched later. Options c and d each surrender one half of the claim."],"flip":"If the prototype shows relocation is unreliable on ordinary agent rewrites, option c is the honest retreat and the span-level pitch goes with it.","linked":["E22","F26","F3","F33","P13","PR1"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:24","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:56","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:188","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:227","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:354","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:363","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:410","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:124","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:135","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:146","merged: F2"],"dupes":{"dropped":["R2"],"why":"Do we prove the review anchor survives an out-of-band write before committing the eighteen days. R2's options are purely when to run that test; F1's (a)/(b) are the same fork plus two product options. Recs a vs c. Features owns review state."}},{"id":"F3","cat":"Features","sub":"Attribution","weight":"critical","q":"Do we reopen attribution as a paid claim, given no platform has shipped span-level authorship?","lede":"It is the only one of our four claims nobody occupies, and the demotion that killed it rested on the wrong comparison.","visual":{"kind":"matrix","x":["file level","span level"],"y":["free","paid"],"points":[{"label":"Google Docs blue dot","x":0.1,"y":0.05},{"label":"git-ai commit trailers","x":0.22,"y":0.05},{"label":"Workspace part-level authorship","x":0.62,"y":0.82},{"label":"iA Writer 8 authorship","x":0.72,"y":0.34},{"label":"claude-edits-scm, 88 installs","x":0.88,"y":0.05},{"label":"frontmatter F3","x":0.95,"y":0.55,"us":true}],"note":"The only span-level implementation found anywhere has 88 installs.","caption":"Who marks authorship, at what granularity, and who charges"},"stakes":"Give this away and we hand over the one half of the loop a live comparable is paid for.","state":["F3 is a reader for commit trailers and git-ai notes, 3 days, MVP-0, free inside F1–F8 (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:57, docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:287).","The vocabulary audit still records it as demoted: shown when available, never the headline (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:175).","Most MVP-0 hover cards would read prompt not recorded, because no write path carries a prompt until MCP (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:247)."],"path":["The demotion rested on iA Writer 7 and a 208-download Obsidian port, which is consumer authorship marking in a personal document.","Round 2 found Google selling the span-level half at Business Standard and above while the file-level dot stays free (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:139).","Nine weeks of platform releases absorbed the other three claims. Attribution is the one nobody took."],"tension":["An unoccupied claim is either an unmet need or a proven non-need, and 88 installs does not separate the two.","Gating it requires billing, and MVP-0 has none.","The gated half stays thin until a write carries a prompt, which is F14."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"Authorship marking: what sold and what did not","cols":["Product","Form","Price","Result"],"rows":[["iA Writer 7 (2023)","Consumer authorship marking","Paid app","Obsidian port: 208 downloads; best VS Code extension: 366 installs"],["Google Docs","File-level blue dot","Free","Every tier"],["Google Workspace","See who changed a part of a document","Business Standard and above","Sold today, verified 2026-09-08"],["frontmatter F3 as planned","Span-level, from trailers and notes","Free","Untested"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"What F3 costs and where it sits","items":[["Build","3 engineering days (readers only)","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:57"],["Stage","MVP-0 readers, MVP-1 prompts via MCP","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:57"],["Price today","Free — Individual gets F1 to F8","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:287"],["Pro tier price it would join","$4 to $5 per user per month","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:288"],["What the MVP-0 card usually says","prompt not recorded — no write path carries a prompt until F11","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:247"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Keep F3 free and in MVP-0 as a hover card","what":"Attribution shows whatever the write carried, at every tier, with no gate.","gains":["Simplest, and it matches the free-editor story","No billing surface to build in MVP-0"],"costs":["Gives away the half a live comparable charges for","Leaves the only unoccupied claim unsold"],"system":"No change.","screens":"Hover card on S2, as drawn.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Split it Google's way: file-level author free, span-level author paid","what":"Everyone sees who last touched the file; seats see which spans each author wrote.","gains":["Copies a live priced split at our own price band","Costs no build days now, only a gate when billing exists"],"costs":["Adds a gating surface to a product with no billing in MVP-0","The paid half is thin until F14 carries prompts"],"system":"Two readers instead of one, with an entitlement check between them.","screens":"Hover card gains a locked state for the span-level half.","money":"Puts a capability a comparable is paid for behind the seat price."},{"k":"c","label":"Lead with attribution and rebuild the pitch around it","what":"Which text the machine wrote becomes the headline, and review state becomes the feature under it.","gains":["The only claim four platforms did not absorb in nine weeks","It uses the engine's real strength, which is spans"],"costs":["Reverses a demotion the corpus made on measured evidence","Attribution is absent on most real writes until MCP ships"],"system":"F3 stops being a 3-day reader and becomes the surface everything else hangs off.","screens":"S2 leads with authorship; the review panel demotes to a counter.","money":"Reprices both tiers on an untested claim."},{"k":"d","label":"Cut F3 from MVP-0 and ship it with the MCP write path","what":"No attribution until a write actually carries a prompt.","gains":["Saves three days now","The pilot never sees a card reading prompt not recorded"],"costs":["The pilot never sees attribution at all","Concedes the unoccupied claim for a quarter"],"system":"F3 collapses into F14.","screens":"Hover card ships with change time and byte range only.","money":"None."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["Google is the only company on record selling this, it sells the span-level half, and it prices in our band.","The demotion was made against a consumer app in a personal document, which is the wrong comparison and should be struck from Exhibit 4.","Copying a live split costs nothing today; it decides which reader is gated once billing exists."],"flip":"If the twenty team conversations say teams read authorship out of git blame and consider it solved, keep F3 free and drop it from the Pro pitch.","linked":["D6","F1","F33","P2"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:57","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:175","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:247","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:287","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:288","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:139","https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=dfarkash.claude-edits-scm"],"dupes":{"dropped":["MK15","P4"],"why":"Is attribution free, split Google's way (file-level free, span-level paid), or the headline. Near-verbatim option sets and all three rec (b), so the merge is lossless. Features owns the row that carries the days and the source dependency; 'promote to headline' is already an option inside P2."}},{"id":"F10","cat":"Features","sub":"AI panel","weight":"critical","q":"Is bring-your-own key a hard gate before any stranger touches the product?","lede":"Every AI request in the shipped code bills the operator, and ten strangers are scheduled for weeks 10 to 12.","visual":{"kind":"arch","layers":[{"label":"User's machine","items":["Editor","Splice engine","No key field yet"],"tone":"neutral"},{"label":"Zephyrus server","items":["Six live /api/ai routes","Five operator keys read at request time","Vercel AI Gateway fallback"],"side":"billed to us","tone":"stop"},{"label":"Model provider","items":["Google, Groq, Cerebras, Mistral, OpenRouter"],"tone":"sunk"}],"note":"The plan says the request goes from the user's machine to their provider.","caption":"The middle layer the architecture claims does not exist"},"stakes":"An unbounded model bill owed by a company funded from consulting hours.","state":["Fix #6 records no bring-your-own key and every AI request billing the operator, 3 days, blocking (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:219).","The gateway reads five operator environment keys and falls back to the Vercel AI Gateway (src/modules/ai/infrastructure/gateway-client.ts:34).","The cost rules assume model cost is zero because all AI is on the user's key (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:231)."],"path":["The gateway was inherited from sgnk-md, which was a single-operator app.","The risk register already answers this: BYO key before any stranger (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:328).","Five features depend on a model, and the pilot depends on those features."],"tension":["Three days sit in front of the whole schedule and have not been sequenced against generation or the panel.","A stranger with no key of their own sees a smaller product than the plan describes.","A cap enforced in policy is not a cap; a cap enforced in code is another thing to build correctly."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"The current AI cost path","items":[["Bring-your-own key","Not built","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:219; fix #6, 3 days"],["Operator keys read at request time","5 providers — Google, Groq, Cerebras, Mistral, OpenRouter","src/modules/ai/infrastructure/gateway-client.ts:34-53"],["Fallback when none set","Vercel AI Gateway, credit-gated","src/modules/ai/infrastructure/gateway-client.ts:66"],["Live AI routes exposed","6","measured: src/app/api/ai/"],["Model cost the plan assumes","Zero — all AI on the user's key","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:231"],["Strangers scheduled","10, weeks 10 to 12","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:357"]]},{"type":"table","title":"Features that cannot be shown to a stranger without it","cols":["Feature","Needs a model","Blocked without BYO key"],"rows":[["F5 idea mode","Yes","Yes"],["F6 decision flow","Yes","Yes"],["F7 generation half","Yes","Yes — the scan itself is model-free"],["F8 AI panel","Yes","Yes"],["Ghost text (shipped, off by default)","Yes","Yes"],["F2 review state","No","No"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Hard gate: no AI route is reachable by a non-founder until the key UI ships","what":"The keychain and key field land before the pilot, and unkeyed users get the editor and the tint.","gains":["Bounded spend and the architecture claim becomes true","Three days inside a 24-day block that already exists"],"costs":["Strangers without a key see a smaller product","Key entry is friction in the first session"],"system":"Key UI, keychain, and every route reading the user's key.","screens":"S11 gains the key field the prototype already draws.","money":"Model cost goes to zero, as the cost rules assume."},{"k":"b","label":"Run the pilot on operator keys with a per-user cap enforced in code","what":"We pay for the ten strangers' model use, with a hard ceiling per account.","gains":["Ten strangers see the whole product immediately","No key friction in the first session"],"costs":["Contradicts the plan's own cost rule and risk response","The cap is unbudgeted work that must be right first time"],"system":"Metering, per-user ceilings and a refusal path when the ceiling is hit.","screens":"A quota state nobody has drawn.","money":"A real model bill, bounded only by code we have not written."},{"k":"c","label":"Ship BYO key and keep a metered operator fallback as paid hosted AI","what":"Both paths exist from day one, with hosted AI metered and capped.","gains":["The upsell moment is real and observable","Users with no key still see everything"],"costs":["Hosted AI was MVP-1 and off by default, so this widens cost and legal surface early","It is the one path where document text reaches a model through us"],"system":"Key UI plus metering plus billing, all before the pilot.","screens":"S11 key field plus a usage and billing surface.","money":"Revenue and cost both start before there is a paying tier."},{"k":"d","label":"Cut every model-dependent feature from MVP-0 and pilot review state alone","what":"The pilot tests one thing and no AI route is exposed.","gains":["No key problem, no spend, no metering","The exit measure becomes unambiguous"],"costs":["Removes generation and the panel from the demo","Leaves a first-time user nothing to do in an empty folder"],"system":"Routes stay unreachable behind a build flag.","screens":"S11 loses the AI section entirely.","money":"None."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["The plan's own risk table already says BYO key before any stranger, and the architecture claim is false until it lands.","Three days is small against the 24-day fix-first block it already sits inside.","The failure mode is an unbounded bill against consulting revenue, which is the worst-shaped risk here."],"flip":"Option b is acceptable only with a spend cap enforced in code rather than in a policy, and nothing short of that.","linked":["AC13","F27","F5","F8","L10"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:219","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:231","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:328","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:357","src/modules/ai/infrastructure/gateway-client.ts:34"]},{"id":"F19","cat":"Features","sub":"Share","weight":"critical","q":"Does the shipped public-share page stay, get gated, or get deleted before anyone outside sees the build?","lede":"The plan says frontmatter hosts nothing; the code serves any shared note to anonymous readers today.","visual":{"kind":"flow","perRow":3,"nodes":[{"label":"Anonymous visitor","tone":"neutral"},{"label":"/p/[slug] on our server","note":"unauthenticated server component","tone":"warn"},{"label":"Server reads the note from GitHub","tone":"stop"},{"label":"Rendered page served to anyone","tone":"stop"},{"label":"public_slug spliced into the file","note":"907 of 907 files byte-identical","tone":"sunk"}],"note":"Section 1 lists no hosting of user content among the things not in the product.","caption":"The path the plan says does not exist, live in the tree"},"stakes":"A public route serving user content confers intermediary status and the obligations that follow it.","state":["Section 1 and Exhibit 6 both put hosting outside the product (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:43, docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:205).","The share module is 1,407 lines across 16 files and serves `/p/[slug]` to unauthenticated visitors (src/modules/share/application/resolve-public-note.ts).","The share writer's splice is measured clean: 907 of 907 files byte-identical (src/modules/share/infrastructure/share-writer.ts:22).","Decision 3 is scheduled for week 2 and written as though nothing exists (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:367)."],"path":["Publishing came with the sgnk-md fork, where it was a feature rather than a contradiction.","Round 2 found three committed files disagreeing about whether we hold documents (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:142).","The PRD prices shipping publishing safely at 74 founder-hours (docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:4194)."],"tension":["Decision 3 is not a greenfield choice, because one of its two options is already built.","No operating rule can be written until one of the three contradicting files is deleted.","A flag is a decision deferred, and flags ship on."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"What is actually shipped","items":[["Share module","1,407 lines across 16 files","measured: src/modules/share/"],["Public route","/p/[slug], unauthenticated Server Component","src/app/(public)/p/[slug]/page.tsx"],["Byte path","Server reads the note from GitHub and renders it","src/modules/share/application/resolve-public-note.ts:36"],["What is written into the user's file","public_slug, spliced into the YAML frontmatter","src/modules/share/infrastructure/share-writer.ts"],["Splice fidelity, measured on the pinned corpus","907 of 907 files byte-identical after a no-op publish/unpublish cycle; the regenerating path left 33 of 907","src/modules/share/infrastructure/share-writer.ts:22"],["Founder-hours the PRD prices for shipping it safely","74","FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:4194"]]},{"type":"table","title":"Four artefacts, three positions","cols":["Source","Position on holding documents"],"rows":[["PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:43","No hosting of user content"],["PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:205","Hosting absent from MVP-0"],["FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:4295 and :4204","We hold user documents; ship publishing in v1, narrow surface, 74 founder-hours of obligations first"],["firestore.rules, committed, 419 lines","900,000-byte note bodies, revisions with allow delete: if false, and UNAUTHENTICATED GET for visibility==public (line 83)"],["src/app/(public)/p/[slug]","Shipped and serving"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Delete the share module and the public route before any external build","what":"The 1,407 lines come out and the plan and the code agree.","gains":["The legal section can be finalised this month","No intermediary status to argue about"],"costs":["Deletes the only way to show a document to a non-user","Deletes a splice path measured clean on 907 files"],"system":"Removes a module, a public route and a writer path.","screens":"The share control and the public page disappear.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Keep it and rewrite the operating rules around hosting","what":"We say plainly that we host published pages, and take the obligations.","gains":["Keeps a real capability that already works","Publishing is a distribution surface nothing else replaces"],"costs":["Every legal rule has to be rewritten around intermediary status","Grievance, takedown and abuse handling all become live work"],"system":"No code change; substantial policy and process work.","screens":"The public page becomes a supported surface.","money":"74 founder-hours by the PRD's own estimate."},{"k":"c","label":"Disable the route in the build, keep the code, decide in week 2","what":"Nothing serves user content while the hosting question is open.","gains":["Nothing deleted and nothing served","One build-flag change, reversible either way"],"costs":["A flag is a deferred decision and flags ship on","The contradiction stays in the tree for another fortnight"],"system":"A build flag over the public route.","screens":"Share control hidden.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Replace it with permalink plus export","what":"A link opens the file in the reader's own frontmatter; we host nothing.","gains":["Matches the promise and the architecture","No state and no obligations"],"costs":["Does nothing for a private repo or a plain folder","Requires the reader to have the product"],"system":"A URL parameter over the existing web app.","screens":"Share becomes a copy-link action.","money":"None."}],"rec":"c","recCase":["This cannot be settled as a feature question, because the hosting decision governs it and that decision is scheduled.","What can be settled today is that nothing serves user content to anonymous readers while it is open.","That is a build-flag change, not a deletion, and it keeps a clean splice path available."],"flip":"If the founders confirm we never hold documents, delete the module rather than flagging it, and finish the operating rules the same week.","linked":["F16","L1"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:43","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:205","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:365","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:367","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:142","docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:4194","firestore.rules:83","src/modules/share/application/resolve-public-note.ts:36"],"dupes":{"dropped":["G10","MK18"],"why":"Does the shipped public-share route stay, and in what shape. Three different answers to one question: F19 disable in the build, G10 keep with noindex, MK18 permalink plus export. Features owns it because the share module is shipped code. L6 is NOT a duplicate — it decides governance (founder-only, noindex, system slugs) once the route survives."}},{"id":"F21","cat":"Features","sub":"Cut and inherited","weight":"critical","q":"Do we delete the table editor and ghost text this week, given each refutes a claim the pitch rests on?","lede":"Two inherited surfaces are in the tree, and between them they falsify byte-exactness and the byte path.","visual":{"kind":"ba","via":"table-edit.ts","before":{"title":"A 4-line CRLF table, before one cell edit","lines":[{"t":"100 bytes","mark":"kept"},{"t":"4 carriage returns","mark":"kept"},{"t":"5 lines untouched","mark":"kept"}]},"after":{"title":"After the shipped table editor","lines":[{"t":"84 bytes","mark":"lost"},{"t":"1 carriage return","mark":"lost"},{"t":"3 of 5 lines rewritten","mark":"lost"}]},"note":"Ghost text is the same class: it posts the prefix to our own route on a timer.","caption":"The counterexample to the pitch, measured in our own code"},"stakes":"A prospect who edits a table, or turns ghost text on, finds the counterexample in ten seconds.","state":["`table-edit.ts` is 190 lines and regenerates rows; editing one cell in a 4-line CRLF table rewrites 3 lines and destroys 3 carriage returns (docs/DECIDE.md:216).","The decision layer already said delete the UI and keep the measurement as a test, dated 2026-08-31.","Ghost text posts the prefix before the cursor to `/api/ai/complete` after 650 ms idle, off by default (src/modules/editor/presentation/ghost-text.ts:133, src/modules/editor/presentation/editor-settings.ts:41).","Neither appears in Exhibit 1."],"path":["Both came from sgnk-md, where byte preservation and the byte path were not claims.","The table editor was slated for deletion on 2026-08-31 and is still shipping.","The share writer shows the alternative: a splice that left 907 of 907 files byte-identical, against a regenerating path that left 33."],"tension":["Table editing is a table-stakes capability, and the splice-backed replacement is unbudgeted.","Ghost text is off by default, which mitigates but does not resolve the contradiction.","Deleting is half a day; rebuilding table editing on the splice writer is a week or more."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"What the table editor does to a file","items":[["Lines rewritten on a one-cell edit","3 of 5","r26-c4-features.md finding R3, module executed in Node"],["Bytes","100 to 84","r26-c4-features.md finding R3"],["Carriage returns on a CRLF file","4 to 1 (3 destroyed)","DECIDE.md:216; r26-c4-features.md finding R3"],["Status in the decision layer","Dead code, already slated for deletion","DECIDE.md:216, dated 2026-08-31"],["Status in the tree","Present, 190 lines","src/modules/preview/presentation/table-edit.ts"],["Contrast: the share writer's splice","907 of 907 files byte-identical; the regenerating path left 33 of 907","src/modules/share/infrastructure/share-writer.ts:22"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"Ghost text against three stated rules","items":[["Rule 1","No document byte passes through a Zephyrus server","WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:35"],["Rule 2","The AI panel is one collapsed line; nothing runs until asked","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:247"],["Rule 3","The AI request goes from the user's machine to their provider","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:133"],["What ghost text does","POSTs the whole prefix before the cursor to /api/ai/complete after 650 ms idle","src/modules/editor/presentation/ghost-text.ts:121, :133"],["Default","Off","src/modules/editor/presentation/editor-settings.ts:41"],["In the feature exhibit","Absent","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:55-67"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Delete both this week and keep the table measurement as a regression test","what":"The two contradicting surfaces leave the tree, and the measurement becomes evidence for the pitch.","gains":["Turns the worst artefact in the repo into the most persuasive one","Three stated AI rules stop being contradicted by shipped code"],"costs":["Inline table editing is gone until a splice-backed version exists","One of six live AI routes goes with it"],"system":"Removes 190 lines, one CodeMirror compartment and one route.","screens":"Preview-pane table editing and the ghost-text setting disappear.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Rebuild both correctly before deleting anything","what":"Table writes go through the splice writer, and completion calls the user's provider directly.","gains":["No capability lost","Completion becomes consistent with the byte path once keys ship"],"costs":["The table UI is 5 to 8 days plus 2 for splice-backed writes, none of it budgeted","The counterexample ships until the rebuild lands"],"system":"Splice-backed table writes; a direct-to-provider completion path.","screens":"Same screens, different behaviour.","money":"Removes a route we pay for."},{"k":"c","label":"Keep both and disclose the limitations in the UI","what":"A note says this control rewrites your file, and another says completion sends text to our server.","gains":["Zero work","Nothing is hidden"],"costs":["A disclosure that says this control rewrites your file is worse copy than no control","It is a written admission inside the product that the pitch is conditional"],"system":"No change.","screens":"Two disclosure strings.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Make tables read-only in preview and gate ghost text behind the hide-all switch","what":"One line for tables, and completion survives only for users who leave AI on.","gains":["Cheapest way to make the byte claim true","No deletion, so nothing is lost if the fork is merged"],"costs":["Editing a table in source is the friction markdown editors exist to remove","The byte-path contradiction persists for everyone who turns AI on"],"system":"A read-only flag and a switch dependency.","screens":"Tables become read-only in the preview pane.","money":"None."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["The table decision was already made on 2026-08-31 and has not been executed; only the date is still open.","Ghost text breaks all three stated AI rules at once, is absent from the plan, and is off by default, so nobody relies on it.","Keeping the table measurement as a regression test converts the counterexample into a working demonstration of what regenerating costs."],"flip":"If the founders want completion as a differentiator, ghost text must be rebuilt to call the user's provider directly, which is option b for that half only.","linked":["F18","F9"],"sources":["docs/DECIDE.md:216","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r26-c4-features.md","src/modules/preview/presentation/table-edit.ts","src/modules/share/infrastructure/share-writer.ts:22","docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:35","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:133","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:247","src/modules/editor/presentation/ghost-text.ts:133","src/modules/editor/presentation/editor-settings.ts:41","merged: F22"]},{"id":"F5","cat":"Features","sub":"Generation","weight":"high","q":"Does generation ship in MVP-0 on founder evidence that has never been attached?","lede":"Idea mode and the decision flow are eight days between them, and both rest on the same statement in chat.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":190,"cols":[{"title":"spec-kit, Kiro, plan mode"},{"title":"Standalone PRD tools","tone":"sunk"},{"title":"F5 + F6","tone":"accent"}],"rows":[{"label":"Asks the clarifying questions","cells":["Yes, all three","No","Yes, from the LLM port"]},{"label":"Where the answers land","cells":["In chat, or outside the repo","n/a","Frontmatter keys in the file"]},{"label":"Price","cells":["Free","Free","Free, 8 engineering days"]},{"label":"Traction","cells":["The toolchains people already run","Top repo 57 stars of 512","Founder test, no notes attached"]},{"label":"Survives with AI hidden","cells":["n/a","n/a","No: needs a key and a network"]}],"note":"Claude Code plan mode writes to ~/.claude/plans and deletes after 30 days.","caption":"The clarify-then-generate step, and who already performs it free"},"stakes":"Eight days and an evidence label both go if the founder test does not replicate.","state":["Idea mode exists as code: generate-document, five prompt kinds, `/api/ai/generate-doc`, needing structured output 2d and a from-repo input 2d (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:59).","The decision flow is 4 days on top, shipping inside idea mode in MVP-0 (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:60).","Both are blocked by the LLM port returning a bare string (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:220).","The gap register rates the evidence High severity: a statement in chat, no notes, no participants, no protocol (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:23)."],"path":["The founders reported testing both with users, and the plan admitted them on that basis.","Public evidence for standalone generators is weak, and the reconciliation offered was that generation is fine inside the review loop.","Round 2 recorded that this points at a buyer who does not run an agent, contradicting the recommended first buyer (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:52)."],"tension":["The stated difference is where the answers land, and that has been asserted, never measured.","Kiro already stages line comments at the point of need, so a second editor is worse than the key they press (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:307).","Without generation, a first-time user has nothing to do in an empty folder."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"F5's evidence and cost","items":[["Evidence class","Founder user test, reported","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:59"],["Notes, participants, protocol attached","None","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:23, severity High"],["Public evidence, standalone PRD generators","512 repos; top repo 57 stars","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:59"],["Code that exists","generate-document, 5 prompt kinds, /api/ai/generate-doc","src/modules/ai/application/doc-prompts.ts:10"],["Remaining build","2d structured output + 2d from-repo input","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:59"],["Blocked by","LLM port returns a bare string; JSON is sliced between brackets","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:220"]]},{"type":"table","title":"The five document kinds already coded","cols":["Kind","Sections the prompt fixes"],"rows":[["prd","Overview / Problem, Goals and non-goals, Target users, User stories, Functional requirements, UX and flows, Success metrics, Risks and open questions, Milestones"],["frd","Functional requirements document"],["brd","Business requirements document"],["product-note","TL;DR, Problem, Proposed solution, Why now, Open questions, Next steps"],["spec","Summary, Goals and non-goals, Architecture, Data model, API, Key flows, Edge cases and failure modes, Testing plan, Rollout, Open questions"]]},{"type":"table","title":"Who already asks the clarifying questions","cols":["Tool","The step","Where the answer lives","Price"],"rows":[["spec-kit","/speckit.clarify","In chat","Free"],["Kiro","Spec clarification at phase checkpoints","In the tool, as line comments at the point of need","Free"],["Claude Code plan mode","Plan mode questions","~/.claude/plans/<slug>.md, outside the repo, deleted after 30 days","Free"],["frontmatter F6","Structured question list from the LLM port","Frontmatter keys in the user's file","Free, 4 engineering days"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"F6's dependencies and class","items":[["Build","4 engineering days","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:60"],["Blocked by","F5 structured output; the LLM port returns a bare string today","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:220"],["Web without install","Yes, with the user's key","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:60"],["Desktop offline","No","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:60"],["Evidence class","Founder user test, reported","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:187"],["Where the incumbents' files land","Verified on a scratch repo in round 2","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:126"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Ship both in MVP-0 as planned, eight days","what":"The generated document arrives with its assumptions written into the file and tinted.","gains":["The strongest founder-evidenced feature is in the pilot","Most of idea mode is already written"],"costs":["Doubles the exposure to one unattached claim","Four of the eight days duplicate a step three free tools perform"],"system":"Structured output in the LLM port, plus a question-list contract.","screens":"S0 launcher cards and the generation flow.","money":"Needs a key, so it needs BYO key first."},{"k":"b","label":"Attach the founder notes first, then ship both","what":"Participants, what they were asked and what they did go into the plan before a day is spent.","gains":["One founder hour closes a High-severity gap","The exhibit's evidence column becomes true as published"],"costs":["If no notes exist, the label has to change before the meeting","It blocks eight days behind a task only the founders can do"],"system":"No change.","screens":"No change.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Ship idea mode, defer the decision flow to MVP-1","what":"Generation happens in one shot; the strangers say whether they wanted to be asked first.","gains":["Halves the exposure and buys four days","Sequences the two so one informs the other"],"costs":["A one-shot generator is the configuration the public evidence says has no traction","Drops the part the founders say they actually tested"],"system":"Structured output only; no question contract.","screens":"S0 cards without a question step.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Cut both and let the user's agent generate","what":"frontmatter reads the frontmatter keys it finds and tints what arrives.","gains":["Zero build, and it matches the reading-surface story","Removes the buyer contradiction round 2 named"],"costs":["The empty folder stays empty on first run","Removes the only two features with any user contact behind them"],"system":"Deletes the generate routes and the prompt kinds.","screens":"S0 becomes blank plus templates only.","money":"None."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["This is the cheapest open item in the plan: the founders either have notes or they do not, and one hour settles it.","Shipping is probably right either way, because the code is mostly written and both are already in the ten-stranger pilot with a stated measure (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:325).","What cannot stand is an evidence column that says founder user test when no protocol exists."],"flip":"If no notes exist, relabel both untested and ship idea mode alone, which is option c.","linked":["F10","F27","F7","FF1"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:59","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:69","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:220","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:325","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:23","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:52","src/modules/ai/application/doc-prompts.ts:10","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:60","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:187","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:307","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:126","merged: F6"],"dupes":{"dropped":["P6","PL1"],"why":"Does the generation block (idea mode, decision flow) ship in MVP-0 on founder evidence never attached. Recs b/a/b. Features owns the rows and the day counts; PL1's 'settle the form factor first' rider survives as an edge from FF1."}},{"id":"F7","cat":"Features","sub":"Repo docs scan","weight":"high","q":"Does the docs scan ship its commodity half first, or the staleness heuristic that is the only novel check?","lede":"Ten days, and two of its three checks are already free in the editor the buyer already has open.","visual":{"kind":"screen","title":"S13 repo docs scan","panes":[{"label":"Proposals","w":2,"rows":[{"label":"Stale section: doc older than the code it cites","meta":"4d, unspecified","tone":"accent"},{"label":"Broken link","meta":"free in VS Code, off by default","tone":"sunk"},{"label":"Missing AGENTS.md or CHANGELOG","meta":"2d","tone":"neutral"}]},{"label":"What was read","w":1,"rows":[{"label":"41 markdown files","tone":"sunk"},{"label":"package.json scripts","tone":"sunk"},{"label":"git dates","tone":"sunk"},{"label":"zero source files","tone":"sunk"}]}],"note":"No model call in the scan. Generation reuses idea mode and the user's key.","caption":"The screen, and which of its three checks nobody else ships"},"stakes":"Six of the ten days rebuild something the buyer's editor already ships and turns off by default.","state":["Staleness heuristic 4d, missing-doc templates 2d, S13 UI 4d, all MVP-0, evidence class founder direction (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:61).","Link resolution already exists in the codebase as `link-doctor` (src/modules/ai/application/link-doctor.ts).","The scan is also the diagnostic that briefs a Zephyrus engagement (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:478)."],"path":["The differentiator line was that Vale and markdownlint lint but propose nothing.","VS Code then turned out to ship markdown link validation itself, off by default, which is that class's honest verdict.","The retention plan leans on the scan as the second reason to return, independent of AI use (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:426)."],"tension":["The staleness rule has never been written down beyond doc-older-than-the-code-it-cites.","The evidence rail is what makes S13 credible, and it is most credible about a check nobody else runs.","False positives in a linter destroy trust, which is why the incumbent ships its own version off."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"The three checks and who already does them free","cols":["Check","Incumbent","Reach","What frontmatter adds"],"rows":[["Broken links","VS Code built-in markdown link validation; marksman language server","Bundled with the editor, OFF by default","Proposals with review state"],["Prose and markdown lint","Vale; markdownlint","6,087 and 6,326 stars","Not attempted"],["Missing standard docs","readme-md-generator","11,131 stars, abandoned 2022","AGENTS.md and CHANGELOG templates"],["Stale section (doc older than the code it cites)","None found in the corpus","—","The actual differentiator, 4 days, unspecified"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"F7 cost and class","items":[["Staleness heuristic","4 engineering days","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:61"],["Missing-doc templates","2 engineering days","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:61"],["S13 UI","4 engineering days","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:61"],["Model calls in the scan","Zero — git dates, package.json scripts, link resolution","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:61"],["Evidence class","Founder direction","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:61"],["Second role","The diagnostic that briefs a Zephyrus engagement","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:478"],["What the S13 evidence rail lists","41 markdown files, package.json scripts, git dates, zero source files","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:253"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Ship all ten days as specified","what":"Stale sections, broken links and missing docs all land together with the evidence rail.","gains":["S13 is the most complete screen in the prototype","It doubles as the services funnel"],"costs":["Six of ten days rebuild two commodity checks","No written rule for the novel half before it is coded"],"system":"Git dates, script parsing and link resolution behind one scan.","screens":"S13 complete.","money":"Feeds the fixed-scope engagement."},{"k":"b","label":"Ship links and missing docs first (6d), hold staleness for a written rule","what":"The commodity half ships fast, reusing link-doctor, and the differentiator waits.","gains":["Fastest visible screen, and most of it is already written","Nothing ships before its rule exists"],"costs":["The screen demos as markdownlint with a nicer rail","It competes with a bundled check the incumbent disables by default"],"system":"Reuses link-doctor; no new heuristic.","screens":"S13 without the stale rail.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Ship staleness first (4d plus UI) and cite VS Code for link checking","what":"The only check nobody else runs goes on screen first, and we point at the editor for links.","gains":["Puts the novel check in front of the first stranger","Forces the staleness rule to be written before it is coded"],"costs":["Loses the completeness that makes the evidence rail persuasive","Pointing at a competitor's feature inside our own screen is awkward"],"system":"Git dates and code references only.","screens":"S13 with one proposal class.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Cut it from MVP-0 and keep it as the consultancy's diagnostic script","what":"The scan is a studio tool that produces a brief, not a product surface.","gains":["Ten days back for the review loop","No public surface to keep correct"],"costs":["Retention loses its one lever that does not depend on AI use","The funnel from scan to engagement then needs a founder to run it"],"system":"No product code.","screens":"S13 leaves the exhibit.","money":"Keeps the engagement, loses the self-serve path to it."}],"rec":"c","recCase":["The evidence rail is what makes the screen credible, and it is most credible about a check no incumbent runs.","Building the commodity half first produces a screen that looks like a linter, against an incumbent that ships its own off by default.","Write the staleness rule as a rule before it is coded, then add link checking on top."],"flip":"If the week-1 conversations with people who bill for documents name broken links as the pain and never mention staleness, invert to option b.","linked":["F31","F5","G18","P11"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:61","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:253","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:426","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:478","docs/FRONTMATTER-COMPLETE-RECORD-2026-08-30.md:13331","docs/FRONTMATTER-COMPLETE-RECORD-2026-08-30.md:13371","src/modules/ai/application/link-doctor.ts"],"dupes":{"dropped":["P19"],"why":"Does the repo docs scan ship its commodity half, its staleness heuristic, or leave MVP-0 as the consultancy's diagnostic. Recs c vs b. Features owns the row; the services-funnel consequence links to G18."}},{"id":"F8","cat":"Features","sub":"AI panel","weight":"high","q":"Does the AI panel ship the two verbs the plan specifies, or the eight the code already has?","lede":"The plan and the shipped product disagree about how much AI is in the editor, by a factor of four.","visual":{"kind":"screen","title":"The AI surface, plan against code","panes":[{"label":"At rest","w":1,"rows":[{"label":"One collapsed line, nothing runs until asked","tone":"accent"}]},{"label":"Menu in the code","w":1,"rows":[{"label":"Refine selection / note","tone":"neutral"},{"label":"Summarize note","tone":"neutral"},{"label":"Expand, Shorten","tone":"warn"},{"label":"Professional tone, Casual tone, Translate","tone":"warn"},{"label":"Suggest wikilinks","tone":"warn"}]},{"label":"Menu in the plan","w":1,"rows":[{"label":"Fix this selection","tone":"good"},{"label":"Critique this selection","meta":"does not exist","tone":"stop"},{"label":"Summarise this file","tone":"good"}]}],"note":"Exhibit 1 prices this row at 3 days for the key UI and keychain only.","caption":"Eight shipped verbs, three specified, one of them unbuilt"},"stakes":"Either working code gets deleted or the positioning's restraint stops being true.","state":["Exhibit 1 defines the row as two verbs, collapsed by default, with a hide-all switch (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:62).","The shipped menu has eight items and none of them is critique (src/modules/editor/presentation/AIMenu.tsx:248).","Six AI routes are live: complete, generate-doc, link-doctor, refine, suggest-links, summarize."],"path":["Two verbs were derived from the finding that editing supplied text is 10.6% of ChatGPT messages, and that incumbents hide AI until invoked (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:381).","The eight verbs were inherited from sgnk-md, which was built to a different brief.","Nobody has decided whether shipping means deleting six or writing one."],"tension":["Critique is the only verb on either list that belongs to a review product rather than a writing product.","Deleting working code costs days that buy no capability.","Five palette entries are still five things a user can find, so demotion is not deletion."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"Plan against code","cols":["Verb","In the plan (PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:62)","In the code (AIMenu.tsx:248-255)"],"rows":[["Fix this selection","Yes","Yes — Refine selection / note"],["Critique this selection","Yes","No"],["Summarise this file","Yes","Yes — Summarize note"],["Expand","No","Yes"],["Shorten","No","Yes"],["Change tone: professional","No","Yes"],["Change tone: casual","No","Yes"],["Translate to English","No","Yes"],["Suggest wikilinks","No","Yes"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"What F8 is priced at, and what exists","items":[["F8 build in Exhibit 1","3 days — BYO key UI plus keychain","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:62"],["Verbs in the shipped menu","8","src/modules/editor/presentation/AIMenu.tsx:248-255"],["Live AI routes","6 — complete, generate-doc, link-doctor, refine, suggest-links, summarize","measured: src/app/api/ai/"],["Ghost text, handled separately","Shipped, off by default, absent from Exhibit 1","see F22"],["Public evidence cited for two verbs","Editing supplied text is 10.6% of ChatGPT messages","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:62"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Cut to the two specified verbs and write critique","what":"Six menu items are deleted and one new verb is built.","gains":["The shipped product matches the plan and the positioning","The smallest AI surface anyone could claim"],"costs":["Deletes working code and adds an unbudgeted build","Six deletions become merge conflicts with the sibling repo"],"system":"Removes five routes' entry points; adds one prompt kind.","screens":"The AI menu shrinks to three items.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Ship the eight that exist and drop the two-verb line from the plan","what":"The menu stays as inherited, collapsed at rest, and the plan is corrected.","gains":["Zero build","Nothing in the product contradicts the document"],"costs":["The AI panel becomes the largest surface in a product that leads with restraint","Eight verbs is a writing assistant, which is what the pitch disclaims"],"system":"No change.","screens":"No change.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Ship three verbs; move the other five behind the palette","what":"Refine, summarise and a new critique are on the menu; the rest are reachable by search only.","gains":["Keeps the collapsed-at-rest promise and keeps the code","One verb to build, five to demote rather than delete"],"costs":["Five palette entries are still five findable features","Critique is unbudgeted work in a row priced at three days"],"system":"Routing change plus one prompt kind.","screens":"Menu of three; palette gains five entries.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Ship two by promoting refine and summarise, and defer critique","what":"The plan's sentence survives with one word changed and nothing is built.","gains":["No build at all","Smallest surface without deleting anything"],"costs":["Loses the verb that fits a review product best","Still leaves five inherited verbs undecided"],"system":"No change.","screens":"Menu of two.","money":"None."}],"rec":"c","recCase":["Critique is the one verb that belongs to a review product, so it is worth the build.","The other five are working code, and demoting them to the palette costs an afternoon against deleting them.","This keeps the collapsed-at-rest promise, which is what the incumbent evidence actually supports (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:381)."],"flip":"If the five-second screenshot test shows people reading the AI panel before the tint, cut to two and take the surface off the screen.","linked":["F10","F21","F9"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:62","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:202","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:381","src/modules/editor/presentation/AIMenu.tsx:248"]},{"id":"F11","cat":"Features","sub":"Refactor","weight":"high","q":"Does vault-wide refactor move into MVP-0 as the one capability with a counted public vote?","lede":"It is the only feature in the exhibit whose demand was measured as votes on a specific request.","visual":{"kind":"file","name":"a spec in the vault","lines":[{"t":"---","note":"frontmatter block"},{"t":"tags: [review-state]","mark":"rename"},{"t":"---"},{"t":"See [[review-state]] for the anchor.","mark":"rename"},{"t":"```md"},{"t":"tags: [review-state]","mark":"refuse","note":"inside a fence"},{"t":"```"},{"t":"...and review-state in prose.","mark":"refuse","note":"ambiguous, not a target"}],"note":"Two renames, two refusals, every hunk shown before it is written.","caption":"What a vault rename splices, and what it declines to guess"},"stakes":"The best-evidenced capability waits behind six features with weaker evidence.","state":["Rename a tag, heading or key across the vault, every hunk reviewable, 8 days, MVP-1 (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:63).","Its evidence line is 86 likes on broken-links-on-rename (docs/DECIDE.md:105).","The engine that does it exists; non-locality is listed as an improvement still to make rather than a shipped refusal (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:510)."],"path":["The 2026-08-31 decision layer called this byte-exactness sold as a capability rather than a promise.","It was placed in MVP-1 when MVP-0 was defined as the review loop alone.","MVP-0 now contains six rows whose evidence class is founder-reported or untested."],"tension":["The eight days are mostly multi-file apply and per-hunk review, both of which reuse the review surface.","It depends on fix #4, the engine wired behind every write (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:217).","If review state is confirmed as the headline, MVP-0 should say one thing and this is a second thing."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"F9's evidence against the MVP-0 rows","items":[["F9 broken-links-on-rename","86 likes","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:63; DECIDE.md:105"],["F2 review state","Untested as a product","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:188"],["F5 idea mode","Founder user test, no notes attached","GAPS-2026-09-08.md:23"],["F6 decision flow","Founder user test, no notes attached","GAPS-2026-09-08.md:23"],["F7 repo docs scan","Founder direction","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:61"],["F9 build","8 engineering days","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:63"],["F9 stage today","MVP-1","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:63"]]},{"type":"table","title":"What F9 needs that already exists","cols":["Requirement","Status"],"rows":[["Byte-range splice across a file","Built — mdmax, 3,614 lines across 13 files, byte-exactness measured on 8,513 real files (PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:492, :498)"],["Refusal on fenced or ambiguous matches","Designed; non-locality is listed as an improvement still to make, not a shipped refusal (PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:510)"],["Multi-file apply with per-hunk review","Not built — this is the 8 days"],["Engine wired behind product writes","Not built — fix #4, 8 days (PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:217)"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Leave it in MVP-1 as planned","what":"MVP-0 stays the review loop and the refactor follows the paid tier.","gains":["MVP-0 says one thing to ten strangers","No new dependency on fix #4 in the pilot"],"costs":["The best-evidenced capability waits behind six weaker ones","The engine's real strength is not in the pilot"],"system":"No change.","screens":"S8 stays MVP-1.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Move it into MVP-0 and drop the decision flow to MVP-1 to pay for it","what":"Eight days of counted demand replace four days of founder-reported demand.","gains":["Trades a weaker evidence class for a stronger one","Reuses the review panel for hunks, so part is already paid for"],"costs":["MVP-0 grows by four days net","It still needs fix #4 to land first"],"system":"Multi-file apply on top of the splice writer.","screens":"S8 refactor preview enters MVP-0.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Ship the single-file half in MVP-0, the vault-wide half in MVP-1","what":"Rename a key or tag in the open file, with refusals shown, and defer the multi-file apply.","gains":["Demonstrates the mechanism cheaply","Reuses the review surface with no new apply path"],"costs":["A single-file rename is not what the 86 likes asked for","It demos as a find-and-replace with manners"],"system":"Splice across one file only.","screens":"A hunk list inside the editor rather than S8.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Ship it first, before review state, as the MVP-0 demo","what":"The pilot leads with a refactor that refuses rather than guesses.","gains":["Leads with the strongest evidence and the engine's actual strength","Refusal becomes visible rather than asserted"],"costs":["Abandons review state as the headline, which is a decision that must come first","The review surface is what makes hunks reviewable, so it would be built anyway"],"system":"Engine-first sequencing.","screens":"S8 becomes the front door.","money":"None."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["Every day in MVP-0 currently buys an untested hypothesis or a founder report; this buys a counted request from the target population.","The engine to serve it already exists, so most of the eight days are the apply path and the hunk list.","The trade against the decision flow is close to even in days and strongly positive in evidence class."],"flip":"If review state is confirmed as the headline and the weeks 1–2 tests support it, leave this in MVP-1, because MVP-0 should then say one thing.","linked":["F1","F5"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:63","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:188","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:217","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:492","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:510","docs/DECIDE.md:105","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:23"]},{"id":"F15","cat":"Features","sub":"Sync","weight":"high","q":"Does sync stay on the roadmap at fifteen-plus days, or become conflict surfacing over the user's own git?","lede":"Sync is the one price individuals are proven to pay, and the largest single build in the plan.","visual":{"kind":"arch","layers":[{"label":"The user's files","items":["A folder, or a git repo"],"tone":"neutral"},{"label":"Git","items":["Already syncs a repo, free, for the buyer we target"],"tone":"sunk"},{"label":"Conflict surfacing","items":["Splice journal, compare-and-swap, never a CRDT"],"side":"settled","tone":"accent"},{"label":"Sync service","items":["15+ days, MVP-2","Obsidian sells this at about $4"],"tone":"warn"}],"note":"Zed staked the opposite architecture on CRDTs in public on 2026-09-01.","caption":"Which layer owns multi-device, and which is already free"},"stakes":"Fifteen days for an audience the product does not currently target.","state":["Sync is git merge, never a CRDT, conflicts surfaced never guessed, 15-plus days, MVP-2 (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:66).","The comparison table lists Obsidian Sync at about $4 as the one proven individual price (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:159).","The architecture is already settled as git merge plus splice journal plus compare-and-swap (docs/DECIDE.md:171)."],"path":["The 2026-08-31 decision layer ranked sync #1 loved, #3 hated and #1 switching trigger, on 1,251 of 43,656 issues (docs/DECIDE.md:107).","That population's vaults are folders, not repositories.","Zed's Delta committed publicly to CRDTs on 2026-09-01, so the never-a-CRDT position now needs a written rebuttal naming them."],"tension":["For a repo user, git already syncs, free.","The measured demand comes from the audience the VS Code route would abandon.","Conflict surfacing is much smaller than a sync service, and it does not carry the $4 price."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"Sync, as the record measures it","items":[["Rank among loved attributes","#1","DECIDE.md:107"],["Rank among hated attributes","#3","DECIDE.md:107"],["Rank as a switching trigger","#1","DECIDE.md:107"],["Issues touching it","1,251 of 43,656","DECIDE.md:107"],["The proven individual price","About $4, Obsidian Sync","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:159"],["F12 build","15+ engineering days, MVP-2","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:66"],["Settled architecture, may not be reopened","git merge plus splice journal plus compare-and-swap, never a CRDT","DECIDE.md:171"]]},{"type":"table","title":"Who needs sync, and whether they already have it","cols":["User","Documents live in","Already synced"],"rows":[["Developer with a repo","git","Yes, free"],["Obsidian user with a vault","A folder","No — this is who pays $4"],["Web-app user on Chrome, local folder","A folder","No"],["Team on MVP-1","A repo","Yes, plus the sidecar"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Keep it in MVP-2 at fifteen-plus days as planned","what":"A real multi-device sync service, later, at the price the category proves.","gains":["Preserves the one individual price anyone here is proven to pay","Serves folder users if the pilot brings them"],"costs":["Fifteen days sit on a roadmap for an audience we do not target","It is the largest row and the last scheduled"],"system":"A sync service with its own storage and conflict rules.","screens":"Multi-device and conflict views.","money":"The only proven individual price, if the audience is right."},{"k":"b","label":"Cut it and state plainly that git is the sync","what":"The desktop app commits and pushes, and there is no sync product.","gains":["Removes the largest build in the plan","Matches the repo-first buyer exactly"],"costs":["Gives up the only individual price in the category","Folder users get nothing across devices"],"system":"A git client and a watcher, both already planned.","screens":"A commit and push affordance.","money":"No individual revenue line."},{"k":"c","label":"Reframe it as conflict surfacing over the user's existing git","what":"We show and never guess conflicts on the sidecar and the file, on top of whatever they already run.","gains":["Much smaller build, and it is what the settled architecture already says","Extends to folder users later without redesign"],"costs":["It is not what the $4 buys elsewhere, so it does not carry the price","The name sync then has to leave the roadmap"],"system":"Compare-and-swap plus a merge driver for the sidecar.","screens":"A conflict view, which MVP-1 already lists.","money":"No new price; it protects the team tier instead."},{"k":"d","label":"Hold until the first-buyer decision is made","what":"The row waits on whether we serve the developer or the person liable for the document.","gains":["Correct dependency order","No design committed to the wrong audience"],"costs":["The roadmap keeps a fifteen-day row with no owner","The CRDT rebuttal stays unwritten while Zed publishes"],"system":"No change.","screens":"No change.","money":"None."}],"rec":"c","recCase":["The architecture was already settled as git merge plus splice journal plus compare-and-swap, which is conflict surfacing rather than a service.","Mostly this is writing down what was decided and pricing it honestly.","It keeps the door open: if the pilot brings folder users, the same machinery extends."],"flip":"If the first-buyer decision picks the non-developer whose documents are not in a repo, sync becomes a real product and the fifteen days must be scheduled.","linked":["E35"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:66","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:159","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:366","docs/DECIDE.md:107","docs/DECIDE.md:171","https://zed.dev/blog/agentic-xanadu"],"dupes":{"dropped":["MK26"],"why":"Does sync stay a fifteen-plus-day MVP-2 build, move earlier as the merge only, or become conflict surfacing over the user's own git. Recs c vs b are the same answer worded twice. Features owns the row."}},{"id":"F16","cat":"Features","sub":"Export","weight":"high","q":"Does the server PDF route get cut to keep the zero-document-bytes promise, and does folder-to-one-PDF get built?","lede":"Export is 945 lines nobody has run, and two of its five menu items send the document to our server.","visual":{"kind":"screen","title":"Export, shipped and missing","panes":[{"label":"Menu today","w":2,"rows":[{"label":"Download .md","meta":"browser","tone":"good"},{"label":"Export HTML","meta":"browser","tone":"good"},{"label":"Export Word (.doc)","meta":"browser","tone":"good"},{"label":"Open PDF (print)","meta":"our server","tone":"stop"},{"label":"Download PDF","meta":"our server","tone":"stop"}]},{"label":"Not built","w":1,"rows":[{"label":"Folder to one PDF","meta":"4d, 79 reactions","tone":"accent"},{"label":"Copy as HTML","meta":"0 occurrences","tone":"sunk"},{"label":"Browser print path","meta":"assumed, absent","tone":"warn"}]}],"note":"Whether any of the shipped code runs is still on the open list.","caption":"Five shipped items, two of which leave the machine"},"stakes":"The zero-document-bytes claim carries the architecture, the legal section and the positioning.","state":["Export is listed as already built and never run, 945 lines across 8 files, 0 days plus one hour to verify (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:67).","Both PDF items call the same authenticated server route, which reads the note's bytes and renders them.","Folder-to-one-PDF is 4 days in MVP-1, with docusaurus#969 at 79 reactions open since 2018.","The week-0 byte path says no document byte passes through a Zephyrus server (docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:35)."],"path":["The whole export module was inherited from sgnk-md and never re-examined against frontmatter's architecture claim.","Export survived the cut that removed decks and sites, on a 4.8:1 VS Code install ratio.","Round 2 noted the cut used Obsidian download ratios, which measure note-takers rather than this buyer (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:60)."],"tension":["Both cannot be true: the menu ships a server render and the plan promises no document bytes leave.","Removing the PDF items means writing a browser print path, which is small but not the zero the row implies.","The one export leg with a counted request is the leg that is not built."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"The five shipped export menu items, against the architecture promise","cols":["Menu item","Where it runs","Document bytes reach our server","Works offline"],"rows":[["Download .md","Browser","No","Yes"],["Export HTML","Browser","No","Yes"],["Export Word (.doc), HTML-based","Browser","No","Yes"],["Open PDF (print)","Opens the server-rendered PDF in a new tab","Yes","No"],["Download PDF","Server route, authenticated, puppeteer-core + @sparticuz/chromium","Yes","No"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"What exists and what is unverified","items":[["Lines of export code","945 across 8 files","measured: src/modules/export/ + src/app/api/export/ + export-vault-zip.ts"],["Menu items","5","src/modules/export/presentation/ExportMenu.tsx:156-160"],["Of those, server-side","2 — both PDF paths call serverPdfUrl()","ExportMenu.tsx:101-116"],["Wired at","EditorPane.tsx:907","src/modules/editor/presentation/EditorPane.tsx:907"],["Ever run","Unverified","GAPS-2026-09-08.md:146"],["Cost to verify","1 hour","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:67"],["Not built","copy-as-HTML (0 occurrences in src/); folder-to-HTML/PDF","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:67"],["Export vs decks, VS Code installs","4,107,590 vs 851,533 = 4.8:1","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:67"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"Export demand, as counted","items":[["Export vs decks, VS Code installs","4,107,590 vs 851,533","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:67"],["Folder-to-one-PDF request","docusaurus#969, 79 reactions, open since 2018","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:67"],["Single-document export","Already built, never run, 945 lines","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:67"],["Folder-to-one-PDF build","4 engineering days, MVP-1","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:67"],["Whole-vault ZIP","Already built, 70 lines","src/modules/vault/application/export-vault-zip.ts"]]},{"type":"table","title":"Export legs and their status","cols":["Leg","Built","Demand evidence"],"rows":[["Single doc to .md, HTML, Word","Yes, unverified","Category table stakes"],["Single doc to PDF (server, two menu items)","Yes, unverified","Category table stakes"],["Whole vault to ZIP","Yes","None recorded"],["Copy as HTML","No — 0 occurrences in src/","None recorded"],["Folder to one PDF or HTML","No","79 reactions, open 8 years"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Verify all five, keep them, and narrow the promise to the desktop app","what":"Nothing is deleted, and zero-document-bytes becomes a desktop-only claim.","gains":["No capability lost and no build days spent","Server-rendered mermaid keeps PDF fidelity"],"costs":["The strongest line in the positioning becomes conditional","The legal section depends on that line, so it reopens too"],"system":"Keeps the puppeteer route and its chromium binary.","screens":"Menu unchanged.","money":"A server render cost per PDF."},{"k":"b","label":"Verify the browser formats, cut the server PDF route, write a print path","what":"PDF becomes a browser print, and no export path touches our server.","gains":["The promise holds everywhere, including the web app","Three formats are free and already written"],"costs":["Loses server-rendered mermaid fidelity in PDF","The print path is unbudgeted, if small"],"system":"Deletes the pdf route and the chromium dependency.","screens":"Two menu items replaced by one print action.","money":"Removes a per-render cost."},{"k":"c","label":"Keep the server PDF behind explicit per-use consent","what":"One named exception, shown at the moment it applies.","gains":["Honest, and it keeps fidelity for the one case that needs it","No code deleted"],"costs":["A named exception in a section that reads better with none","It keeps a document-bytes path open while the hosting decision is unresolved"],"system":"Consent state plus the existing route.","screens":"A consent step in the export flow.","money":"Per-render cost, bounded by use."},{"k":"d","label":"Cut export from MVP-0 and build folder-to-one-PDF first in MVP-1","what":"Nothing ships until the leg with counted demand is built and everything is verified together.","gains":["No unverified claim on the page","Builds the one leg with an eight-year-old request behind it"],"costs":["The one feature that costs zero days disappears from the exhibit","Four days in a tier that is already thin"],"system":"Folder walk plus a single render path.","screens":"Export returns in MVP-1, complete.","money":"Fits the client-handover case the services line sells."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["The zero-document-bytes claim is worth more than server-rendered mermaid in a PDF.","The three browser formats are already written and consistent with the promise; verify them in the hour the row already budgets.","Build folder-to-one-PDF afterwards on whatever render path survives, rather than on top of a route being deleted."],"flip":"If the verification hour shows the browser formats do not run either, this stops being an export decision and becomes a fix-first row.","linked":["AC14","F13","F19"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:67","docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:35","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:146","src/modules/editor/presentation/EditorPane.tsx:907","src/modules/export/presentation/ExportMenu.tsx:156","src/app/api/export/pdf/[...path]/route.ts:36","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:60","src/modules/vault/application/export-vault-zip.ts","merged: F17"],"dupes":{"dropped":["P20","PL16"],"why":"Verify the 945 lines of unrun export, decide what happens to the server PDF route, and whether export stays an MVP-0 row. PL16(b)=F16(d), PL16(c)=F16(b), P20(c)=F16(d). Recs b/b/c. Features owns the row; AC14 stays separate as the byte-claim exception."}},{"id":"F23","cat":"Features","sub":"Rendering","weight":"high","q":"Does nested-construct rendering become a feature row in our own editor, now that the plugin is cut?","lede":"The most-voted request in the only population with a vote has no owner, no estimate and no stage.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":210,"cols":[{"title":"Our own Live mode","tone":"accent"},{"title":"Additive Obsidian extension"},{"title":"Drop the claim"}],"rows":[{"label":"Serves the 501-like rendering bug","cells":["Yes","No, it serves review state","No"]},{"label":"Cost","cells":["Unknown; live preview is core rendering","Decoration over sidecar ranges","Zero"]},{"label":"Fixes the three contradicting sections","cells":["Yes","Partly","Yes"]},{"label":"Re-entry into a vault opened daily","cells":["No","Yes","No"]},{"label":"Writes into the user's files","cells":["No","No","No"]}],"note":"Obsidian's Live Preview tree is depth-1 by construction, verified twice.","caption":"Three ways to answer the strongest demand signal in the corpus"},"stakes":"The plan states a rendering rule it has no work behind, in three places that disagree.","state":["Section 21 still says nested constructs render correctly, shipped first as the free plugin (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:524).","Section 12 cut that plugin as unbuildable (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:304), and the channels row still lists it for week 2 (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:204).","Exhibit 1 has no row for it."],"path":["The plan intended to fix Obsidian's rendering as a free plugin and inherit the fidelity claim.","Round 2 proved the plugin cannot work: the Live Preview tree is depth-1 by construction (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:127).","The attention section states the consequence: rendering fidelity outranks review state by two orders of magnitude in that population (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:410)."],"tension":["Live preview is core rendering, so the estimate is unknown until someone scopes it.","It is the single strongest demand signal in the corpus, in the same forum where our headline scored zero.","A certificate that says your file renders wrong in our own editor is not defensible."],"evidence":[{"type":"bars","title":"Obsidian forum, one population, one metric, 2026-09-08","note":"PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:410. The rendering bug against the closest existing requests for review state.","data":[["Nested code block rendering bug",501],["Suggestion Mode like Google Docs/Word",3],["Tracking changes within notes",1],["List of changes since last view",0]],"unit":"likes"},{"type":"table","title":"What three sections of the plan say about the same thing","cols":["Section","Statement"],"rows":[["Section 21 rendering rules (line 524)","Nested constructs render correctly — shipped first as the free plugin"],["Section 12 channels (line 304)","The free Obsidian plugin is CUT; the parse is unreachable"],["Exhibit 6 channels row (line 204)","Free Obsidian live-preview plugin, week 2; kill under 200 installs in 14 days"],["Exhibit 1 (lines 55-67)","No feature row for nested-construct rendering"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Make it a feature row in our own editor, with an estimate and a stage","what":"Nested constructs in list items render correctly in Live mode, and it is scheduled like everything else.","gains":["The strongest counted demand in the corpus gets an owner","Our Live mode gets a claim no incumbent can make"],"costs":["Live preview is core rendering and the estimate is unknown","It competes with the review loop for the same weeks"],"system":"Our own CodeMirror parse, where we control containment.","screens":"Live mode changes; no new screen.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Ship the additive Obsidian surface instead","what":"Review state as a CodeMirror extension over the sidecar's byte ranges, inside Obsidian.","gains":["The plan already names this as the viable Obsidian path","Re-entry from a surface they open daily"],"costs":["It serves review state, so the 501 likes stay unserved","A second surface to maintain with no rendering claim"],"system":"A decoration layer over the sidecar; no re-parse.","screens":"An Obsidian pane, not one of ours.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Drop the rendering claim and fix the three contradicting sections","what":"The plan stops asserting fidelity it has not built.","gains":["The document stops contradicting itself in three places","No unowned promise on the page"],"costs":["Gives up the only demand signal measured at this magnitude","Live mode loses its most concrete differentiator"],"system":"No change.","screens":"No change.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Keep it as an engine-only claim through the certificate","what":"mdmax certifies how a construct renders elsewhere; our renderer makes no promise.","gains":["Consistent with the certificate story","No renderer work"],"costs":["A certificate about rendering, issued by an editor that renders it wrong, is indefensible","It leaves the three sections still contradicting each other"],"system":"Detector work only.","screens":"A certificate output.","money":"None."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["If the 501-against-0 finding is taken seriously at all, it has to appear as work rather than as a sentence.","Our CodeMirror Live mode is the one surface where we control the parse, which is precisely what the Obsidian plugin lacked.","Fix the three contradicting sections in the same pass, whichever option wins."],"flip":"If scoping shows the fix needs a parser rewrite rather than a containment fix, option c is the honest answer and the claim comes off the page.","linked":[],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:204","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:304","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:410","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:524","docs/DECIDE.md:106","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:127"]},{"id":"F26","cat":"Features","sub":"Agent writes","weight":"high","q":"Do we ship a control over which files an agent may write, or refuse the job in writing?","lede":"The product exists to adjudicate agent writes and has no way to say which files an agent may touch.","visual":{"kind":"flow","perRow":3,"nodes":[{"label":"Agent writes anywhere in the repo","tone":"warn"},{"label":"No scope rule exists","note":"0 hits across 163 inventory rows","tone":"stop"},{"label":"frontmatter sees it afterwards","tone":"neutral"},{"label":"Panel groups unreviewed by path","tone":"accent"},{"label":"An MCP write path could refuse","note":"binds only agents that use it","tone":"sunk","dashed":true}],"note":"Review after the fact is not the same as scope before the fact.","caption":"Where a scope rule could live, and what exists instead"},"stakes":"A review product that cannot scope a write invites the obvious question in the first demo.","state":["Nothing in Exhibit 1 mentions write scope, and the greps over the 163-row inventory return zero rows (docs/PRODUCT.md:655).","The security rules cover plugins, code execution and ambient access, not write scope (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:551).","The only place a scope rule we own could live is the MCP write path, which is 6 days and untested (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:65)."],"path":["The mental model was that the agent writes wherever it writes and frontmatter shows what changed.","Scope was never raised, because the review surface was assumed to be the control.","Non-locality is already listed as a refusal condition the engine does not declare (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:510)."],"tension":["Prevention requires a write path we control, and we may never have one.","Noticing requires a group-by in a panel already being built.","The omission is larger than several features that were listed with no evidence at all."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"Scope control, searched for","items":[["Feature rows in the inventory","163","PRODUCT.md:655-862"],["Rows mentioning allowlist, denylist, scope control, which files, permission to write or gitignore","0","r26-c4-features.md, finding R1"],["Rows in Exhibit 1 mentioning it","0","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:55-67"],["Rows in the inventory whose evidence column reads NONE","36 of 163 (22.1%)","r26-c4-features.md, finding F1"],["Where a scope rule would naturally live","F11 MCP server, 6 days, MVP-1, untested","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:65"]]},{"type":"table","title":"What the product controls today, and what it does not","cols":["Control","Present"],"rows":[["See what changed since a person last read it (F2)","Planned, MVP-0"],["Revert one span (F2)","Planned, MVP-0"],["Refuse an ambiguous splice (engine)","Partly — non-locality is listed as an improvement still to make (PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:510)"],["Say which paths an agent may write","Nowhere in the plan or the inventory"],["Ceilings per file (4 MB, 200,000 lines)","Stated in the operating rules (PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:551)"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Ship a repo-level write-scope file enforced at the MCP write path","what":"Paths an agent may and may not touch, checked when the write comes through us.","gains":["The scope story becomes real where writes actually pass through us","It gives the MCP server a second reason to exist"],"costs":["Binds only agents that use our server, which is itself untested","A control a user can walk around reads worse than none"],"system":"A scope file, a parser and a refusal path in the MCP server.","screens":"A scope editor, or a file the user writes by hand.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Refuse it in writing: we review writes, we do not police them","what":"The plan says plainly that the user's agent has its own permissions.","gains":["Honest, free, and consistent with the no-ambient-access posture","One more refusal for the positioning"],"costs":["A prospect may reasonably ask why a review product cannot scope a write","It concedes the question rather than answering it"],"system":"No change.","screens":"No change.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Surface it read-only: group unreviewed spans by path","what":"The review panel shows which paths were touched, so out-of-scope writes are obvious.","gains":["Close to zero cost inside a panel already being built","Answers the real question: did it touch something I did not expect"],"costs":["Notices after the fact rather than preventing","It is a weaker answer than a permissions system sounds"],"system":"A group-by in the review panel.","screens":"S4 gains a path grouping.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Defer until the agent-write-authority decision is settled","what":"Nothing is built or refused until that decision lands.","gains":["Correct dependency order","No design committed to the wrong model"],"costs":["The gap stays in the plan while outsiders read it","It is the kind of omission a reviewer finds first"],"system":"No change.","screens":"No change.","money":"None."}],"rec":"c","recCase":["Prevention needs a write path we control and may never have; noticing needs a group-by in a panel already funded.","Grouping unreviewed spans by path answers the real question at close to zero cost.","It leaves option a available if the MCP probe proves the write path out."],"flip":"If the twenty team conversations name write scope as the reason they would pay, option a becomes the offer and the MCP server becomes the gate.","linked":["F1","FF12"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:65","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:510","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:551","docs/PRODUCT.md:655","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r26-c4-features.md"]},{"id":"F33","cat":"Features","sub":"Review state","weight":"high","q":"Is a span tinted because it changed, or because a machine wrote it?","lede":"The general form of this feature is Almanac's, and Almanac raised $45M and switched it off in January 2025.","visual":{"kind":"timeline","items":[{"when":"2025-01-31","label":"Almanac shuts down","note":"read receipts, approvals, doc history","tone":"stop"},{"when":"2026-07-03","label":"VS Code merges review/unreview","note":"agents window, experimental, undocumented","tone":"warn"},{"when":"2026-08-24","label":"Antigravity ships Agent Edits","note":"Uncommitted and Branch panes","tone":"warn"},{"when":"2026-08-28","label":"Notion ships per-change approval","note":"agent edits approved one at a time","tone":"warn"},{"when":"2026-09-03","label":"Claude Code v2.1.260 diff panel","note":"opens itself, three scopes, no reviewed mark","tone":"warn"}],"note":"Everything dated 2026 ships the agent-scoped form free.","caption":"Nine weeks of absorption, and the corpse underneath the general form"},"stakes":"Tint everything and we rebuild a feature with a $45M failure behind it.","state":["The feature as specified tints every span changed since a person last read it, whatever wrote it (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:56).","Attribution is a separate row that reads authorship when the write carried it (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:57).","Nothing in the plan restricts the tint to machine-authored spans."],"path":["Round 2 narrowed the claim to across people and across tools on a working tree with no pull request (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:124).","Today's research narrows it further: the general-document form was Almanac's whole feature list, and Almanac shut down on 2025-01-31.","Four platforms shipped the agent-scoped diff free between 2026-07-03 and 2026-09-03."],"tension":["Tinting everything is honest and cheap, and it is also the shape with a dead precedent behind it.","Scoping to agent writes requires knowing who wrote a span, which is attribution, which is unbuilt.","This repo alone holds 4,446,724 markdown words, so a whole-repo unreviewed surface is a debt nobody clears."],"evidence":[],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Tint every changed span, as specified","what":"Any span that changed since a person last read it is tinted, whatever wrote it.","gains":["No dependency on attribution","Simplest rule to explain and to implement"],"costs":["It is the shape Almanac sold, at scale, before shutting down","On a large repo it produces a surface nobody works through"],"system":"Hash per span; no author field required.","screens":"S2 and S4 as drawn.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Tint every span; sort and default the panel to agent-authored spans","what":"The store stays general, the surface leads with what a machine wrote.","gains":["Keeps the cheap store and takes the surviving claim","Degrades gracefully when authorship is unknown"],"costs":["Two behaviours to explain in one feature","The default is only as good as the attribution behind it"],"system":"An author field on the span record, read when present.","screens":"S4 gains a default filter and an ordering rule.","money":"Ties the surface to the paid attribution split."},{"k":"c","label":"Tint only spans a machine wrote","what":"Human edits are plain text; only machine-authored spans carry state.","gains":["Exactly the claim nothing observed occupies","The smallest possible review surface, which is what the attention evidence wants"],"costs":["Useless wherever the write carried no authorship, which is most writes today","It makes review state depend entirely on an unbuilt row"],"system":"Author becomes a required field, so unknown authorship means no tint.","screens":"S2 shows fewer tints and needs a state for unknown.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Ship a and decide scope after the five-second screenshot test","what":"The general tint ships and the scoping question waits for the test already scheduled.","gains":["No dependency and no delay","The test is scheduled for weeks 1–2 anyway"],"costs":["The store schema is set before the question is asked","Retrofitting an author field into a shipped store is more expensive than adding it now"],"system":"General store; author added later.","screens":"No change now.","money":"None."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["Keeping the store general costs nothing and keeps every span recoverable; the choice belongs in the surface.","Leading the panel with agent-authored spans is the only version of this claim nothing observed reaches.","It also makes the attribution split worth paying for, which is the same argument as F3."],"flip":"If the anchor prototype shows authorship is absent on most real agent writes, option b collapses into a and the scoping claim has to be dropped.","linked":["F1","F3"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:56","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:57","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:124","https://get.almanac.io/go-forward","https://www.notion.com/releases","https://raw.githubusercontent.com/anthropics/claude-code/main/CHANGELOG.md","https://antigravity.google/blog/vcs-and-terminal"]},{"id":"F4","cat":"Features","sub":"Answer in place","weight":"medium","q":"Does answer-in-place stay in MVP-0 now that its Q-to-A half is cut and the live population is about 1,400 files?","lede":"It was briefly the headline; it is now a two-day feature aimed at one toolchain's marker syntax.","visual":{"kind":"funnel","steps":[{"label":"Public spec.md files carrying the marker","n":3368,"unit":"files","tone":"neutral"},{"label":"Live after reading 50 files hit by hit","n":1415,"unit":"files","tone":"accent"}],"note":"42% of a read-every-hit sample, spec-kit syntax only.","caption":"The addressable population after both corrections"},"stakes":"Two days spent on a demo beat that survives because it used to be the headline.","state":["It detects the NEEDS CLARIFICATION marker and splices into its byte range, 2 days, MVP-0 (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:58).","The Q-to-A half is cut: spec-kit appends that bullet only after the user has answered.","It is the smallest row in Exhibit 1 and the only one whose demand was counted by reading every hit."],"path":["An earlier plan claimed 62,976 unanswered markers; 49,408 were spec-kit's own checklist line (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:178).","A fresh count on 2026-09-08 read a 50-file sample and put the live share at 42%.","The round-2 scratch-repo run found `specify init` writes 30 files and zero specs (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:126)."],"tension":["It is cheap enough to be below the noise floor of any schedule this plan can defend.","It serves one toolchain, and that toolchain may clear its markers in chat before a file is opened.","Generalising the detector adds a configuration surface, which the admission test scores as an automatic fail."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"The marker population, after two corrections","items":[["Public spec.md files carrying the marker","3,368","measured 2026-09-08, PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:58"],["Sample read hit-by-hit","50 files","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:58"],["Genuinely live in that sample","42%","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:58"],["Estimated live files","about 1,400","derived: 3,368 x 0.42 = 1,415"],["Earlier claim, withdrawn","62,976 markers, of which 49,408 were spec-kit's own checklist line","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:178"],["Build","2 engineering days","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:58"]]},{"type":"table","title":"Which half survives","cols":["Half","Status","Reason"],"rows":[["NEEDS CLARIFICATION marker","Kept","3,368 files carry it; 42% live"],["Q: to A: bullet","CUT","spec-kit appends the bullet only after acceptance, so it is a closed record by construction"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Keep it in MVP-0 at two days as specified","what":"One marker syntax, detected and spliced, with the honest denominator kept on the page.","gains":["Cheapest row in the exhibit and it demos in one keystroke","The only demand figure in the plan derived by reading every hit"],"costs":["Serves one toolchain and about 1,400 public files","Adds a row nobody has asked for by name"],"system":"Marker detector over the splice writer. No new store.","screens":"S3 answer in place, as drawn.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Generalise the detector to any marker the user configures","what":"Bracketed TODO and open-question markers become configurable patterns.","gains":["Serves far more files than one toolchain's syntax","Survives spec-kit losing its audience"],"costs":["A configuration surface, which the admission test fails on sight","Every false positive lands inside the product's own review claim"],"system":"Pattern registry plus settings persistence.","screens":"A settings row in S11 that did not exist.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Move it to MVP-1 and spend the two days on the anchor prototype","what":"The marker feature waits until the review loop is proven.","gains":["Buys two days for the question that gates everything else","MVP-0 says one thing"],"costs":["Loses a demo beat that reads well in fifteen seconds","Nothing else fills the empty-folder moment"],"system":"No change.","screens":"S3 leaves MVP-0.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Cut it and fold marker answering into the file-scoped AI panel","what":"A generic verb answers the marker with no special handling of its byte range.","gains":["One fewer row to specify and maintain","No toolchain-specific code"],"costs":["The distinctive part is the exact byte range, and that disappears","The panel needs a key, so the marker case dies with no key"],"system":"Deletes the detector; the panel carries it.","screens":"S3 is absorbed into the AI panel.","money":"None."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["Two days is below the resolution of this schedule, and the row's demand was counted honestly rather than summed from a search.","Keep the denominator on the page, about 1,400 files and spec-kit only, so nobody re-inflates it later."],"flip":"If the week-3 toolchain runs show spec-kit users clearing markers in chat before a file is ever opened, cut it.","linked":["F5","F8"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:58","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:178","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:126"],"dupes":{"dropped":["P5"],"why":"Does answer-in-place stay in MVP-0 now its Q-to-A half is cut. Same options, both rec (a) keep at two days. Features owns the row."}},{"id":"F9","cat":"Features","sub":"AI panel","weight":"medium","q":"What does the hide-all-AI switch actually hide, and does it ship on day one as the positioning promises?","lede":"The switch is named in the positioning as a lead refusal, and no code for it exists.","visual":{"kind":"ba","via":"one switch","before":{"title":"Today: no switch at all","lines":[{"t":"AI menu, eight verbs","mark":"on"},{"t":"Ghost text on a 650 ms idle timer","mark":"on"},{"t":"Idea mode in the launcher","mark":"on"},{"t":"Generate half of the docs scan","mark":"on"}]},"after":{"title":"Switch on, all or nothing","lines":[{"t":"Every AI surface","mark":"off"},{"t":"Editor, tree, modes","mark":"on"},{"t":"Review state and revert","mark":"on"},{"t":"First run from a generated document","mark":"off"}]},"note":"Five booleans exist in settings today; none of them is a global AI switch.","caption":"What is left when the switch is on: the editor and the tint"},"stakes":"A switch that leaves three AI surfaces running is the kind of thing that gets found and posted.","state":["The plan puts the switch in S11 on day one and names it in the positioning (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:298, docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:382).","The shipped settings object has five booleans and no global AI switch (src/modules/editor/presentation/editor-settings.ts:12).","Nobody has written down what the switch hides."],"path":["Zed, VS Code and Telegram each shipped a global off switch only after a public issue.","The plan reads that as a chance to lead with the refusal instead of retrofitting it.","The scope was never specified, because the AI surfaces were counted from the plan rather than the code."],"tension":["If it hides everything, a first-run user who turns it on can no longer start from a generated document.","If it hides only the panel, the promise is thinner than a reader of the positioning would assume.","Per-surface toggles are a configuration surface, which the admission test scores as an automatic fail."],"evidence":[{"type":"bars","title":"Reactions on the issue that forced each incumbent's off switch","note":"PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:382. Each switch shipped after the issue, not before.","data":[["Zed disable_ai",412],["Telegram AI button",181],["VS Code chat.disableAIFeatures",30]],"unit":"reactions"},{"type":"stat","title":"The settings surface that exists today","items":[["Booleans in the shipped settings","5 — vimMode, lineNumbers, spellcheck, focusMode, aiGhostText","src/modules/editor/presentation/editor-settings.ts:12-16"],["Global AI switch","Not present","measured: grep for hideAI / disableAI / hideAllAI over src/ returns nothing"],["Where the plan puts it","S11 settings, day one, named in the positioning","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:382"],["Features that would have to respect it","F5, F6, F7 generation, F8, ghost text","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:200-202"],["Admission-test constraint","A configuration surface is an automatic fail, not a trade (gate G5)","r20-q6-feature-discipline.md, 103.1"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"One switch that hides every AI surface","what":"Panel, ghost text, idea mode, decision flow and the generate half of the scan all disappear.","gains":["The strongest version of the promise and the easiest to state in one line","Cheapest to build: one flag, checked in five places"],"costs":["A first-run user with it on cannot start from a generated document","The product with it on is the editor plus the tint"],"system":"One setting, read by every AI entry point.","screens":"S11 gains one row; S0 loses its generator cards when on.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Hide the panel and ghost text only; generation stays reachable","what":"The switch covers the always-present surfaces, not the ones the user opens deliberately.","gains":["Less disruptive to the first-run flow","Keeps the launcher useful with AI mostly off"],"costs":["The switch does not mean what the positioning implies","That gap is exactly what gets screenshotted"],"system":"One setting, narrower scope.","screens":"S11 row with a qualifier under it.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Per-surface toggles instead of one switch","what":"Each AI surface gets its own boolean in settings.","gains":["Precise control for the user who wants some of it","No forced trade between generation and quiet"],"costs":["Five booleans become ten, which the admission test fails outright","No single sentence to put in the positioning"],"system":"Five settings and their persistence.","screens":"S11 grows a section.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Drop the switch from the positioning until it is built","what":"The claim comes off the page and returns when the code exists.","gains":["Nothing false on the page","No scope argument to settle this week"],"costs":["Gives up the one refusal three incumbents proved people ask for loudly","The positioning's lead-with-refusals section loses its sharpest item"],"system":"No change.","screens":"No change.","money":"None."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["The all-or-nothing version is the cheapest to build and the only one that can be stated in one line.","It describes a product the plan already argues is the free tier: the editor and review state, with no model.","Its scope shrinks if ghost text is deleted, so settle F21 first."],"flip":"If the pilot shows first-run users reaching idea mode before anything else, the switch has to spare the launcher and option b becomes the honest scope.","linked":["F21","F27","F8"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:202","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:298","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:382","src/modules/editor/presentation/editor-settings.ts:12","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r20-q6-feature-discipline.md"]},{"id":"F13","cat":"Features","sub":"Teams","weight":"medium","q":"Do comments live only in the sidecar, or do we also export an interchange format?","lede":"A sidecar comment is invisible to everyone not running frontmatter, which is where reviewers are.","visual":{"kind":"file","name":"spec.md and its sidecar","lines":[{"t":"The API returns 200 on failure.","mark":"span"},{"t":"","note":"three ways to attach a comment"},{"t":".frontmatter/review.jsonl","mark":"sidecar","note":"renders nowhere, reads everywhere"},{"t":"{>>needs a source<<}","mark":"critic","note":"toolkit last committed 2021-02-27"},{"t":"> [!comment] needs a source","mark":"in-file","note":"writes into the user's file"}],"note":"The oldest constraint: nothing is added to markdown that breaks it elsewhere.","caption":"Three carriers for one comment, and what each costs the file"},"stakes":"Pick the in-file carrier and the product breaks its own rule in its own feature.","state":["Comments are specified as a sidecar too, never in the file, because every in-file syntax renders as garbage on GitHub (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:64).","The rendering rules repeat it: review state and comments in the plain-text sidecar (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:528).","An earlier plan carried CriticMarkup and pandoc track-changes in both directions (docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:1043)."],"path":["The no-breakage rule is the product's oldest constraint and an in-file comment syntax is its clearest violation.","The record's own verdict was to materialise to JSON always, and treat CriticMarkup as a byte format we own (docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:3306).","criticmarkup.com is a parked domain and the toolkit has been still since 2021."],"tension":["Sidecar-only reproduces the isolation the plan criticises SpecKit Companion for.","Exporting into a dead standard answers an objection more than it serves a workflow.","Making comments visible on GitHub means writing into the user's file, which is refused everywhere else."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"The interchange option, measured","items":[["criticmarkup.com","Parked domain","FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:3306, fetched"],["CriticMarkup/CriticMarkup-toolkit","848 stars, last commit 2021-02-27","FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:3306, fetched"],["Google Docs public API","Cannot create suggestions at all","FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:178, fetched"],["The record's own earlier verdict","Materialise to JSON always; CriticMarkup optionally and only as a byte format we own","FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:3306"],["An earlier plan's position","CriticMarkup plus pandoc --track-changes, both directions","FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:1043"],["Current plan's position","Sidecar only, never in the file","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:64"]]},{"type":"table","title":"What each carrier costs the user","cols":["Carrier","Renders on GitHub","Readable without frontmatter","Survives a byte-exact edit"],"rows":[["Sidecar .frontmatter/","Not shown","Yes — plain JSONL","Yes"],["CriticMarkup in the file","Renders as literal braces","Yes, ugly","The comment is bytes, so edits move it"],["HTML comment in the file","Hidden","Yes","Same"],["Callout block in the file","Renders as a callout","Yes","Same"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Sidecar only, as specified","what":"Comments live in `.frontmatter/`, plain text, anchored by byte range and hash.","gains":["Every touched file still renders everywhere","One carrier to keep correct"],"costs":["Invisible to a reviewer who opens the file on GitHub","Reproduces the lock-in objection we raise about others"],"system":"No change.","screens":"Comments live in S4 and the hover card.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Sidecar as the source of truth, with an export to CriticMarkup on demand","what":"A command writes a copy carrying comments as CriticMarkup, leaving the original untouched.","gains":["Answers the lock-in objection in one sentence","Never touches the file under review"],"costs":["Exports into a format whose toolkit has been still since 2021","One more output to keep correct for a rare case"],"system":"A serialiser over the sidecar; no writer change.","screens":"An entry in the export menu.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Sidecar plus an optional in-file callout for open comments","what":"Open comments can be materialised as callouts so they render on GitHub.","gains":["Comments become visible where reviewers already are","Callouts have no closing marker to lose"],"costs":["Writes into the user's file, which the product refuses everywhere else","The exception has to be written into the rendering rules"],"system":"A writer path that adds bytes on purpose.","screens":"A materialise control next to each comment.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Defer comments to MVP-2 and ship shared read-state alone","what":"No carrier decision is made, and the team feature is who has read what.","gains":["Removes the decision and shrinks the team build by about half","Read state is the half with a comparable behind it"],"costs":["Teams asking for comments get nothing","Read state alone is what GitHub bundles at $4"],"system":"No comment schema.","screens":"S4 without a comment thread.","money":"Thins the team offer further."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["Sidecar-only is the right default, and the export is cheap insurance that never touches the file.","Treat CriticMarkup as a byte format we own rather than a standard we join, which is what the record already concluded (docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:3306)."],"flip":"If the twenty team conversations say reviewers will not leave GitHub, option c becomes worth pricing and the rendering rules need their exception written.","linked":["F16"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:64","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:528","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:178","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:3306","docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:1043"]},{"id":"F18","cat":"Features","sub":"Cut and inherited","weight":"medium","q":"Do bookmarks and graph view get deleted, demoted to the palette, or left as they are?","lede":"Both are shipped, both are unchosen, and one of them holds a third of the product's global hotkeys.","visual":{"kind":"state","states":[{"label":"Inherited","meta":"41 of 43 editor files","via":"fork","tone":"sunk"},{"label":"Visible now","meta":"bookmark control, mod+g","via":"no decision","tone":"warn","current":true},{"label":"Palette only","meta":"no pixel, no hotkey","via":"demote","tone":"accent"},{"label":"Deleted","meta":"685 + 33 lines","via":"fork call","tone":"neutral"}],"note":"The plan tells a reader bookmarks do not exist; the status bar disagrees.","caption":"The four states an inherited surface can be in"},"stakes":"The published plan describes a product that differs from the build in reachable controls.","state":["The gap register puts bookmarks under what the product should not have, confidence class E (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:81).","The code ships `useBookmarks` wired into the editor pane, persisted under `sgnk-md-bookmarks` (src/modules/editor/presentation/bookmarks.ts:31, src/modules/editor/presentation/EditorPane.tsx:53).","Graph view is 685 lines and holds one of exactly three global hotkeys (src/modules/app-shell/presentation/KnowledgeUI.tsx:58; docs/FEATURE-GAP-REPORT.md:41).","Neither appears in Exhibit 1 and neither has a stage."],"path":["Both came with the sgnk-md fork, so neither arrived through a decision.","The admission test failed graph view on gate one, recording 0 of 89 feature requests mentioning it, and prescribed demotion.","The same fork leaks the sibling's identity into storage keys and the Tauri bundle id (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:222)."],"tension":["Deleting working code to satisfy a one-word entry on a refusal list is a poor trade.","A visible control and a global hotkey compete for the at-rest attention the tint needs.","Every deletion is a future merge conflict with the sibling repo, which the fork decision has not settled."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"Bookmarks: plan against code","items":[["Plan's position","Should not have — confidence E","GAPS-2026-09-08.md:81"],["Code","useBookmarks, 33 lines, wired into EditorPane","src/modules/editor/presentation/bookmarks.ts; EditorPane.tsx:53"],["Storage key","sgnk-md-bookmarks","src/modules/editor/presentation/bookmarks.ts:31"],["Same leak elsewhere","sgnk-md-editor-settings; src-tauri productName sgnk-md, id ai.sgnk.md","editor-settings.ts:46; PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:222"],["Evidence in the earlier inventory","Bear pin-notes [fetched]; size column reads ∅","PRODUCT.md:659, row 6"],["Files in editor plus app-shell","43, of which 41 byte-identical to sgnk-md","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:223"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"Graph view, run through the admission test","items":[["Feature requests mentioning it","0 of 89","r20-q6-feature-discipline.md, 103.2 row 6"],["Internal graph size","3,848 nodes","r20-q6-feature-discipline.md, 103.2 row 6"],["Transclusions it produced","45, all of them documentation of the feature","r20-q6-feature-discipline.md, 103.2 row 6"],["Verdict of that test","Fails gate 1; demote to Invoked, never marketed; delete if mentions stay at 0 for two quarters","r20-q6-feature-discipline.md, 103.2 row 6"],["In Exhibit 1","Absent","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:55-67"],["Built","Yes — 685 lines, force-graph, tag-coloured, hover-focus","src/modules/graph/; FEATURE-GAP-REPORT.md:41"],["Global hotkeys in the whole app","3 — mod+k, mod+p, mod+g","src/modules/app-shell/presentation/KnowledgeUI.tsx:56-58"]]},{"type":"table","title":"Where attention is supposed to go on S2","cols":["Element","Position in the predicted scan path"],"rows":[["Top bar and left rail — tabs, tree, unreviewed bars","First"],["Document heading and opening lines","Second"],["Right rail","Last"],["AI panel","Off the path, collapsed"],["Graph view","Not in the plan's scan model at all"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Delete both surfaces and their stores","what":"Bookmarks and the graph module come out of the tree this week.","gains":["The shipped product matches the plan exactly","Less inherited surface to maintain"],"costs":["Deletes 685 plus 33 lines of working code","Graph view is the cheapest familiarity signal for an Obsidian migrant"],"system":"Two modules removed; divergence from the sibling grows.","screens":"A status-bar control and a hotkey disappear.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Keep both, remove the refusal line, and rename the storage keys","what":"The plan is corrected to describe the product that exists.","gains":["No deletion risk and the sibling identity leak is fixed","Obsidian migrants keep what they expect"],"costs":["The refusal list gets shorter and less credible","Restraint stops being visibly true at rest"],"system":"Storage key rename only.","screens":"No change.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Demote both to the command palette and release the hotkey","what":"No visible control, no global key, still reachable by search.","gains":["Follows the admission test's own verdict for graph view","Keeps the code and buys back a pixel and a hotkey"],"costs":["It is a third state the refusal list has no word for","They stay as maintenance nobody has budgeted"],"system":"Routing change; `mod+g` freed for the editing floor.","screens":"Two palette entries replace a control and a hotkey.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Leave both until the fork decision is made","what":"Nothing moves until merge, vendor or fork-and-own is settled.","gains":["No work now, and it is the correct dependency","One decision settles many instances at once"],"costs":["The published plan keeps describing a different product","The hotkey stays spent"],"system":"No change.","screens":"No change.","money":"None."}],"rec":"c","recCase":["Demotion is the reversible move: it costs a routing change and buys back the at-rest attention the tint needs.","The admission test already reached this verdict for graph view, with a counted number behind it.","Rename the storage keys either way; it is the same sibling-identity leak as the Tauri bundle id."],"flip":"If the fork decision goes to merge rather than fork-and-own, deletion becomes free and option a is better.","linked":["F21"],"sources":["docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:81","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:222","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:223","docs/PRODUCT.md:659","src/modules/editor/presentation/bookmarks.ts:31","src/modules/editor/presentation/EditorPane.tsx:53","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:413","docs/FEATURE-GAP-REPORT.md:41","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r20-q6-feature-discipline.md","src/modules/app-shell/presentation/KnowledgeUI.tsx:58","merged: F29"]},{"id":"F25","cat":"Features","sub":"Search","weight":"medium","q":"Where does the search index live, given the byte path forbids the server index the plan asks for?","lede":"Two sections of the plan prescribe opposite fixes for the same measured problem.","visual":{"kind":"arch","layers":[{"label":"Repo bytes","items":["Fetched in the browser with the user's token"],"tone":"neutral"},{"label":"Index","items":["Per open file, lazily","Client worker over the whole repo","Server index, closed off by the byte path"],"side":"the choice","tone":"accent"},{"label":"Query","items":["Title, tag and folder scopes over MiniSearch today"],"tone":"sunk"}],"note":"77 MB is parsed per cold start today, on the inherited implementation.","caption":"Which layer holds the index, and what that costs the promise"},"stakes":"Search over unopened files is most of a stranger's vault on day one.","state":["Section 9 prescribes server full-text search in the web app with a local index on desktop (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:233).","The week-0 byte path says a server index is off the table and section 9's line must change (docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:44, docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:50).","Search is not a feature row; it is one word inside the editor row (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:55).","The current implementation is MiniSearch over the vault snapshot (docs/FEATURE-GAP-REPORT.md:45)."],"path":["The 77 MB figure was measured against the inherited implementation, which loads the whole snapshot.","The byte-path decision was drafted afterwards and closes off the obvious fix.","The contradiction is unreconciled in the shipped plan."],"tension":["A lazily built per-file index is either slow or incomplete on a cold vault, and nobody has said which is acceptable.","A worker-built index costs a first-connect wait that can at least be shown as progress.","A server index reopens the hosting question and the whole legal section with it."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"Search, as measured and as prescribed","items":[["Parsed per cold start today","77 MB","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:233"],["Section 9's fix","Server full-text search in the web app; local index on desktop","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:233"],["Week-0 byte path's fix","Index lazily per open file in the client; server index off the table","WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:44, :50"],["Current implementation","MiniSearch over the vault snapshot with title, tag and folder scopes","docs/FEATURE-GAP-REPORT.md:45"],["Feature row for search","None; one word inside F1","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:55"],["Published performance measures promised","Time to first keystroke cold; typing latency on a 10,000-word document","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:233"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Client-only, lazily indexed per open file","what":"Only opened files are searchable, and section 9 is corrected to say so.","gains":["The zero-document-bytes claim holds everywhere","Cheapest to build and to reason about"],"costs":["Search over unopened files is degraded, which is most of a new vault","It is a visible regression against every competitor"],"system":"Index on open; no snapshot load.","screens":"Search results carry a scope caveat.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Client index built in a worker over the whole repo, cached in IndexedDB","what":"Whole-vault search with no server, paid for once at first connect.","gains":["Full search and the promise both hold","The wait is shown as progress, which is normal after connecting a repo"],"costs":["First connect on a large repo is slow","Browser memory bounds it, and the web app is the trial"],"system":"A worker, a persistence layer and an invalidation rule.","screens":"A first-connect progress state.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Server index as section 9 says, with the promise narrowed","what":"Document text is indexed on our server for the web app.","gains":["Best search on any repo size","No client memory ceiling"],"costs":["Puts document text on our server, which reopens the hosting decision","The legal section changes with it"],"system":"An index service and its retention rules.","screens":"No visible difference.","money":"Infrastructure cost that the plan currently assumes away."},{"k":"d","label":"Full search on desktop only; the web app searches open files","what":"The trial is honestly worse than the download, and says so.","gains":["Simple and true","No worker, no server"],"costs":["Makes the trial visibly worse, which is the opposite of a trial's job","The web app is where a stranger meets the product first"],"system":"Two implementations.","screens":"A stated limitation in the web app.","money":"None."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["A worker-built client index keeps the promise and still gives whole-vault search.","The cost is a first-connect wait, which is a normal thing for an app that has just connected to a repository.","Section 9's server line has to be corrected either way, because a later decision already overrides it."],"flip":"If first-connect indexing measures badly on a repo the size of this one, option a is the fallback and the limitation goes on the page.","linked":["AC1","F19"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:55","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:233","docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:44","docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:50","docs/FEATURE-GAP-REPORT.md:45"],"dupes":{"dropped":["AC15"],"why":"Client index or server index for search. Same four options; recs b vs a differ only on how eagerly the client index is built. Features owns search; the byte-path constraint reaches it as an edge from AC1."}},{"id":"F27","cat":"Features","sub":"Onboarding","weight":"medium","q":"Are the launcher's four templates files or generator prompts, and does Handover survive having no standard?","lede":"The launcher cards are the first thing a new user sees, and nobody has said what happens when one is clicked.","visual":{"kind":"screen","title":"S0 launcher","panes":[{"label":"The four cards","w":2,"rows":[{"label":"Blank document","meta":"file"},{"label":"Spec","meta":"file"},{"label":"Decision record","meta":"MADR"},{"label":"Handover","meta":"no published standard","tone":"warn"},{"label":"Changelog","meta":"Keep a Changelog 1.1.0"}]},{"label":"If they are prompts","w":1,"rows":[{"label":"Needs a key","tone":"stop"},{"label":"Needs a network","tone":"stop"},{"label":"Dead with AI hidden","tone":"stop"}]}],"note":"First-run promise: open a folder, edit in thirty seconds, no account.","caption":"Two different products behind the same four cards"},"stakes":"A stranger with no key opens the product and finds four dead cards.","state":["Exhibit 7 shows the launcher as blank, four templates, and existing edits sorted unreviewed-first (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:239).","The prototype draws Blank, Spec, Decision record, Handover and Changelog, matching the recurring types the register names (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:95).","The rendering rules already commit to labelling an offered structure as offered (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:526)."],"path":["Templates entered through the earlier record as the strongest onboarding lever, specifically templates in the vault rather than a gallery.","The launcher screen was drawn from that; the click behaviour was left open.","Three of the four cards cite a published standard and Handover cites none (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:525)."],"tension":["A template file needs no model, no key and no network; a generator prompt needs all three.","The generator is the feature the founders say they tested, and the launcher is where it would show first.","Two card types in one row is more to explain than a first session can carry."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"The two possible meanings of a template card","cols":["","Template file","Generator prompt (F5)"],"rows":[["Needs a model","No","Yes"],["Needs the user's key","No","Yes"],["Works with hide-all-AI on","Yes","No"],["Works offline in the desktop app","Yes","No"],["Build cost","Near zero — four .md files","Already built, needs structured output (2d) and BYO key (3d)"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"What the record says about the document types","items":[["Recurring types named","spec, decision record, handover, changelog","GAPS-2026-09-08.md:95"],["What the prototype draws","Blank document, Spec, Decision record (MADR), Handover, Changelog (Keep a Changelog 1.1.0)","docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html, S0 launcher"],["Standards named in the rendering rules","MADR and Nygard decision records; RFC 7322; Keep a Changelog 1.1.0","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:525"],["No standard body","Runbooks and PRDs; a structure is offered and labelled as such","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:526"],["Handover standard","None named anywhere in the plan","measured: PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:525-526"],["F5's five kinds already coded","prd, frd, brd, product-note, spec","src/modules/ai/application/doc-prompts.ts:10"],["Onboarding evidence","Templates in the vault, not a gallery","r20-q6-feature-discipline.md, 103.3"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Four template files, with Handover labelled a house structure","what":"Clicking a card writes a markdown file into the folder and opens it.","gains":["Works offline, with no key, and with AI hidden","Three of four cite a real standard"],"costs":["First run never shows the AI capability the founders tested","A file is a thin thing to call a template"],"system":"Four `.md` files and a copy action.","screens":"S0 as drawn, with one label change.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Four generator prompts running idea mode","what":"Clicking a card generates a document from the repo and the user's answers.","gains":["Shows the strongest founder-evidenced feature first","Every card produces something specific to this repo"],"costs":["A stranger with no key sees four dead cards","BYO key has to land before the pilot"],"system":"Launcher wired to the generate route.","screens":"S0 cards gain a key requirement state.","money":"Model cost lands on the first click."},{"k":"c","label":"Two of each, with the generator cards visibly requiring a key","what":"Two files and two prompts, distinguished on the card.","gains":["Covers both paths and teaches the key requirement early","Nothing is dead for an unkeyed user"],"costs":["Four cards become two concepts in a first session","It is the most explaining for the least commitment"],"system":"Two behaviours behind one card component.","screens":"S0 gains a second card style.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Swap Handover for AGENTS.md","what":"Every card cites something external, reusing the docs scan's missing-doc template.","gains":["No unstandardised card on the first screen","Reuses work the scan already needs"],"costs":["Drops the one recurring type no other feature covers","Handover is the type this studio itself writes most"],"system":"Shares a template with the docs scan.","screens":"One card renamed.","money":"None."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["Only template files keep the first-run promise for a user with no key (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:429).","The four drawn in the prototype already match the record's own list of recurring types.","Handover must be labelled an offered structure, the way the rendering rules already require."],"flip":"If BYO key lands early and the pilot shows first-run users reaching for generation, option c becomes affordable without a dead first click.","linked":["F10","F5","F9"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:239","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:429","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:525","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:526","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:95","docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html","src/modules/ai/application/doc-prompts.ts:10","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r20-q6-feature-discipline.md"]},{"id":"F31","cat":"Features","sub":"Import","weight":"medium","q":"Does import get a feature row, given migration from Notion is already sold as a service?","lede":"The product sells a migration service and ships a plain markdown file picker.","visual":{"kind":"flow","perRow":3,"nodes":[{"label":"Notion export .zip","tone":"neutral"},{"label":"UUID filenames, broken links","tone":"warn"},{"label":"Our importer: .md picker only","note":"101 lines, no zip, no rewriting","tone":"stop"},{"label":"A founder does it by hand","note":"inside a fixed-scope engagement","tone":"warn"},{"label":"Or an internal tool the studio runs","tone":"accent"}],"note":"The counted importer demand is Obsidian's population, not this buyer.","caption":"What a migration actually costs when no importer exists"},"stakes":"Every migration costs founder hours in a business argued to sell without them.","state":["Exhibit 1 has no import row.","Migration from Notion sits inside the Zephyrus services engagement (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:478).","The code ships an ImportModal of 101 lines taking `.md`, `.markdown` and `.txt`, with no zip handling and no link rewriting (src/modules/app-shell/presentation/ImportModal.tsx)."],"path":["Format-aware import was cut with everything that was not the review loop.","The services angle was written later and reintroduced migration as a human deliverable.","The earlier inventory lists import as a gap for Notion and Obsidian (docs/FEATURE-GAP-REPORT.md:99)."],"tension":["Selling migration by hand contradicts the argument that the product does the selling the studio cannot afford by hand.","The counted importer demand is measured on Obsidian's users, who are not this plan's buyer.","Notion exports are messy, so a supported public importer is a long-lived maintenance commitment."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"Importer demand, as counted","items":[["Open issues in the Obsidian importer repo that are Import from X requests for formats with no importer","47 of 58 (81%)","r1-migration-fidelity.md:35"],["notion-labelled issues in that repo","58 total, 55 closed (94.8%) — the most-churned importer there","r1-migration-fidelity.md:36"],["notion-to-md npm downloads","1.36M per month","r1-migration-fidelity.md:187"],["Import rows in Exhibit 1","0","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:55-67"],["What ships today","ImportModal, 101 lines: .md/.markdown/.txt file picker, no zip, no link rewriting","src/modules/app-shell/presentation/ImportModal.tsx"],["Where migration appears in the plan","A services deliverable","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:478"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Ship a Notion-zip importer as a feature row in MVP-1","what":"Zip handling, UUID filename cleanup and link rewriting, in the product.","gains":["The services migration becomes a button, which is the plan's own funnel theory","It is the one import path with counted demand anywhere"],"costs":["One more format to keep correct as Notion changes its export","The demand was counted on a different population"],"system":"A zip reader, a filename normaliser and a link rewriter.","screens":"The import modal grows a format path.","money":"Removes founder hours from each migration."},{"k":"b","label":"Keep migration as a service and build an internal tool","what":"The studio runs the importer; there is no public surface.","gains":["Serves the paying case at a fraction of the cost","No support burden and no format promise"],"costs":["Every migration still costs founder hours","The tool has no users, so it stays fragile"],"system":"A script, not a module.","screens":"None.","money":"Migration stays billable and stays manual."},{"k":"c","label":"Keep the file picker and document the Notion export path","what":"We say how to get from an export to a folder, and change no code.","gains":["Near zero cost","Nothing promised that is not delivered"],"costs":["Does not fix UUID filenames or broken links, which is the actual pain","It reads as advice where a tool was expected"],"system":"No change.","screens":"A documentation page.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"No import at all; frontmatter opens folders and repos","what":"The file picker goes and import leaves the product.","gains":["Smallest surface","Consistent with the reading-surface story"],"costs":["Contradicts a service the plan is already selling","Deletes working code for no gain"],"system":"Removes a modal.","screens":"The import control disappears.","money":"None."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["The migration case is real and priced, and it belongs to the fixed-scope engagement rather than a free editor's feature list.","An internal tool serves it at a fraction of the cost of a supported public importer.","The counted demand is Obsidian's importer, whose users are not this buyer, which is the same population caveat the plan applies to its engine numbers."],"flip":"If two or more pilot users arrive from Notion and stall on the export, the importer earns a product row and option a follows.","linked":["F16","F7"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:478","docs/FEATURE-GAP-REPORT.md:99","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-29-r11/r1-migration-fidelity.md:35","src/modules/app-shell/presentation/ImportModal.tsx"]},{"id":"FL4","cat":"Flow & interaction","sub":"Review fatigue","weight":"critical","q":"Do we run the 40-hunk head-to-head against `git add -p` in weeks 1-2, before building the review surface?","lede":"The record holds a costed argument that the review interaction is theatre on any change big enough to need it, and a written falsifier.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":126,"cols":[{"title":"frontmatter review surface","tone":"accent"},{"title":"`git add -p`, free"}],"rows":[{"label":"Keystrokes on 40 hunks","cells":["80 minimum","80 minimum"]},{"label":"Words to read to judge","cells":["about 4,400","about 4,400"]},{"label":"Total review","cells":["17-25 min","17-25 min"]},{"label":"Against agent generation","cells":["about 60 s, so 17-25x","same ratio"]},{"label":"Hunk grain","cells":["word","line"]},{"label":"Works on an unsaved buffer","cells":["yes","no"]}],"note":"What survives the comparison is word grain, dirty buffers and the hash line.","caption":"The same 40 hunks, in the paid surface and the free one."},"stakes":"Eighteen engineering days of review-state build rest on an interaction that may collapse to accept-all on any change large enough to matter.","state":["Weeks 1-2 lists six items and the 40-hunk comparison is not among them (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:352`).","One of those six, the Obsidian plugin, is cut ten lines earlier (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:304`).","Review state is priced at 18 engineering days: store 6, rendering 5, revert 3, panel 4 (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:56`).","The falsifier is already written with thresholds (`docs/CRITIQUE.md:643`)."],"path":["The comparison was made in the 2026-08-31 critique, against an earlier version of the interaction.","The plan has been rewritten four times since and the falsifier was never carried forward."],"tension":["Review to generation runs 17-25x on a 40-hunk change, and worsens as agents produce larger changes (`docs/CRITIQUE.md:637`).","Cisco measured no useful review above 250 lines and a 60-minute wear-out. That is source code, and the mapping onto markdown spans is an analogy.","Google measured a 3.2-hour weekly review budget against a 24-line median change.","What genuinely survives is narrow: word-grain hunks, hunks in a dirty buffer, and the hash line (`docs/CRITIQUE.md:641`)."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"The 40-hunk review, costed (CRITIQUE.md:626-635)","items":[["Keystrokes, minimum","80","40 × (1 nav + 1 decision)"],["Words to read to judge","~4,400","40 hunks × ~110 words"],["Careful review @200 wpm","22 min","4,400 / 200"],["Total review","17–25 min","reading + 3 s/hunk decision"],["Agent generation","~60 s","same change"],["Review : generation","17–25×","CRITIQUE.md:637 — \"the product's structural problem\""]]},{"type":"table","title":"What already ships free, and what does not","cols":["Capability","Where","Cost to user"],"rows":[["Per-hunk discard of uncommitted agent changes","`git restore -p`, `git checkout -p`, `git add -p`, git 2.50.1 (CRITIQUE.md:639)","free, offline, for years"],["Accept or reject each hunk in an editor","Zed agent panel, re-verified live 2026-08-31 (CRITIQUE.md:622)","$0"],["Word-grain hunks, hunks in a dirty buffer, the hash line","frontmatter only (CRITIQUE.md:641)","the whole delta"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Run the head-to-head in weeks 1-2, before the 18 days of build","what":"Ten strangers review one prepared 40-hunk agent change in both surfaces.","gains":["The only test in the record that can refute 18 days cheaply","Both outcomes are actionable, so nothing is wasted"],"costs":["Needs a prepared 40-hunk change and a script","The corpus states the falsifier and never costs it"],"system":"No change. A mock and a terminal.","screens":"Needs one review mock good enough to walk 40 hunks.","money":"Ten conversations on top of the 35 already scheduled."},{"k":"b","label":"Build the surface, then compare at the ten-stranger pilot","what":"The comparison happens in weeks 10-12 against the real thing.","gains":["Tests the product, not a mock","No extra week-1 load"],"costs":["If it fails, 18 days are already spent","The MVP-0 exit test fails with it"],"system":"No change.","screens":"No change.","money":"18 days at risk."},{"k":"c","label":"Change the unit so the comparison does not apply — file or section, not hunk","what":"Review is marked at file or section level, as GitHub's Viewed state is.","gains":["Sidesteps the ratio entirely","Matches the free incumbent's shape"],"costs":["Gives up the per-span claim, which is the differentiator","Changes the counter, the tree bars and the panel"],"system":"The sidecar unit changes from span to file or heading.","screens":"The panel becomes a file list.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Accept the ratio and design for skim — file level by default, hunks on demand","what":"The default surface is coarse and the span detail is opened deliberately.","gains":["Honest about how a large change is actually read","Keeps the per-span store under a coarse default"],"costs":["Two units on every surface","Pre-empts the counter decision before it is taken"],"system":"Store stays per span; the default projection is coarser.","screens":"Adds a level switch to the panel.","money":"None."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["It is the cheapest way to refute 18 days of build, and the thresholds are already written, so there is nothing to design.","A pass justifies the surface; a fail redirects to (c) or (d) before any code is written.","The comparison also decides the review unit, which four other decisions here inherit."],"flip":"If the ten-developer mock test returns fewer than 4 of 10 unprompted asks for review state, the week-3 kill fires first and this test never runs.","linked":["FL19","FL5","FL6"],"sources":["docs/CRITIQUE.md:626","docs/CRITIQUE.md:637","docs/CRITIQUE.md:639","docs/CRITIQUE.md:641","docs/CRITIQUE.md:643","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:352","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:304","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:56","https://static1.smartbear.co/support/media/resources/cc/book/code-review-cisco-case-study.pdf","https://sback.it/publications/icse2018seip.pdf"]},{"id":"FL12","cat":"Flow & interaction","sub":"First run","weight":"critical","q":"What does a stranger meet in the first thirty seconds, and does the 83% scan refusal gate the pilot?","lede":"Five of six flows open with a folder scan that refuses 83% of real vaults, and none of the nine prototype screens is a first run.","visual":{"kind":"flow","perRow":4,"nodes":[{"label":"Launch","note":"no folder, no sidecar, nothing scanned","tone":"neutral"},{"label":"Templates first, as drawn","note":"Open folder is a toolbar icon","tone":"warn"},{"label":"Open a folder","note":"the ordering specified twice in the record","tone":"accent"},{"label":"Scan walks the tree","tone":"neutral"},{"label":"6,613 of 6,614 files refused","note":"zero-indent block sequences","tone":"stop"},{"label":"Apology or guarantee line","note":"same scan, two readings","tone":"warn"},{"label":"Sandbox of real .md files","note":"the fallback when the repo refuses","tone":"accent"}],"note":"Review state needs no frontmatter write, so a write-path refusal need not block a read.","caption":"The first thirty seconds, which no screen has drawn."},"stakes":"The first thirty seconds is the product's worst number, and the state a pilot stranger actually meets has never been drawn.","state":["The launcher leads with a blank document and four templates (`docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:291`); Open folder is a small toolbar button (`:286`).","The PRD's step 1 and the flow research both put Open an existing folder first with a sandbox second (`docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:1763`, `r21-s7-flow-design.md:37`).","NF-1 is 4 days and NF-3 is 3 days at the front of fix-first (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:214`, `:215`); Z is 17% today against a 99.9% target.","No prototype screen is a first run; the launcher opens onto 3 projects and 128 documents (`prototype:302`)."],"path":["The launcher was drawn as a returning-user home screen and then used as the first screen.","The refusal was measured against seven Obsidian vaults where one wiki is 77% of 8,513 files (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:514`)."],"tension":["The product has no import problem, because the corpus is already `.md` on disk and import collapses to pointing at a folder.","Across the four closest products, first run teaches one mechanic on content the product supplies (`c4-onboarding-activation.md:62`).","Review state needs no frontmatter write, so a construct the writer cannot address has no business blocking the reader.","The flow research says ship none of these flows until NF-1 and NF-3 land (`r21-s7-flow-design.md:169`)."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"Documented first-run orderings","cols":["Product","Order","Source"],"rows":[["Obsidian","Two choices only: \"Create new vault\" or \"Open folder as vault\" — recorded as \"co-equal, not buried\"; import is step 5 of 6","c4-onboarding-activation.md:50-51"],["Obsidian sandbox","A real disposable vault, opened deliberately from Help — \"Not shown automatically at first run\"","c4:82"],["Linear","Demo workspace first, create workspace second","c4:55"],["Pattern across Obsidian, Linear, Raycast, Vercel","First run teaches one mechanic on content the product supplies, and defers the user's own corpus","c4:62"],["PRD v2 step 1","Open an existing folder — primary; sandbox second","FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2:1763"],["r21-s7 Flow 1 step 1","Open an existing folder (primary), Try a sandbox (secondary)","r21-s7:37"],["frontmatter prototype","Blank + 4 templates first; existing edits below; Open folder in the toolbar","prototype:291, :302, :286"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"First-run constraints already written down","items":[["First-run screens in the prototype","0 of 9","prototype:282-687"],["K1, keystrokes to first value","≤ 3","FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2:1846"],["C, concepts to learn","≤ 3 — file, folder, view","FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2:1848"],["V0, visible controls at rest","≤ 9","FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2:1845"],["Walkthrough, tour, What's New modal","banned","FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2:1764, NN/g"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"The scan, measured","items":[["Foreign files refused","6,613 of 6,614","zero-indent block sequences, FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2:1814"],["Aggregate vault refusal","83%","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:214"],["Z target","≥ 99.9%","FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2:1851; today 17%"],["Flows that open with the scan","5 of 6","r21-s7:169"],["Ten folders tried → refusals met","8.3","r21-s7:9, derived from 83%"],["Corpus composition","7 Obsidian vaults, one wiki = 77% of 8,513 files","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:514"],["NF-1 + NF-3","7 engineering days","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:214-215"]]},{"type":"table","title":"The two status lines available for the same scan","cols":["Version","Text","Line"],"rows":[["Apology (today's behaviour, undrawn)","\"163 of 1,040 files could not be read.\"","r21-s7:39"],["Guarantee","\"1,040 files open. 163 use a list style the editor will not edit yet. None have been modified.\"","r21-s7:47"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Folder primary, sandbox second, and split the read path from the write path","what":"Open a folder leads, a disposable sandbox of real files is the visible second, and a write-path refusal never blocks reading.","gains":["Keeps the no-importer advantage and answers the defer-the-corpus pattern","Turns most of the 83% into a write-tier footnote"],"costs":["A sandbox corpus to build and maintain","The read/write seam is unestimated anywhere in the record"],"system":"Adds a seam the engine does not have between the reader and the writer.","screens":"Draws the missing first-run screen and demotes the template row.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Gate: no stranger until NF-1 and NF-3 land","what":"Human testing waits for the corpus refusal to fall under the falsifier's line.","gains":["The first impression is the product working","It is what the flow research instructs"],"costs":["Seven days of fix-first in front of every human test","On a schedule the plan itself calls unfalsifiable until day 7"],"system":"No new seam. The scheduled fixes land first.","screens":"No change beyond the missing first-run screen.","money":"Delays every week-1 signal."},{"k":"c","label":"Ship as drawn — templates first, with a guarantee-shaped status line","what":"The launcher keeps its ordering and the scan reports what opened rather than what failed.","gains":["Demonstrates refuse-rather-than-guess at the first possible moment","No build cost"],"costs":["A stranger whose repo is 83% unreadable does not wait","Templates first reads as another markdown editor"],"system":"No change.","screens":"One status line; the launcher is untouched.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Curate the pilot to spec-kit and superpowers repos the engine handles","what":"Recruit ten strangers whose repositories are agent-toolchain output.","gains":["Removes the failure from the pilot","Matches the channel strategy"],"costs":["The exit test proves nothing about the vault population","That population is where the corpus and the free tier are aimed"],"system":"No change.","screens":"No change.","money":"None."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["MVP-0's loop is read, tint, revert, and a revert writes bytes the file already had rather than splicing frontmatter.","Splitting the paths converts the worst number into a footnote for the tier that ships first, and the fix still lands behind it.","Both documents that specify a first run say folder first, and a sandbox is how the four closest products defer a stranger's own corpus.","A template row leading the screen makes the first impression another markdown editor, at the moment the product needs to look like something else."],"flip":"If the read and write split costs more than the seven days NF-1 and NF-3 cost, take the schedule hit and gate instead.","linked":["E1","FL14","FL18"],"sources":["docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:291","docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:286","docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:302","docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:1763","docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:1814","docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:1845","docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:1851","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-29-r11/c4-onboarding-activation.md:51","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-29-r11/c4-onboarding-activation.md:62","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-29-r11/c4-onboarding-activation.md:82","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r21-s7-flow-design.md:37","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r21-s7-flow-design.md:47","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r21-s7-flow-design.md:169","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:214","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:215","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:514","merged: FL13"]},{"id":"FL14","cat":"Flow & interaction","sub":"Cold start","weight":"critical","q":"On first open of a repo we have never seen, what is the baseline, and which surface is the pilot tested on?","lede":"The ten strangers bring their own repos, and the plan says neither what their first document looks like nor where a later write is noticed.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":138,"cols":[{"title":"Fresh agent output, the demo"},{"title":"Stranger's existing repo, the pilot","tone":"accent"}],"rows":[{"label":"Everything unreviewed","cells":["Every paragraph tinted, as intended","Every paragraph tinted, the stated failure"]},{"label":"Baseline at first open","cells":["Nothing tinted until the agent writes","Nothing tinted, counter reads zero"]},{"label":"Baseline at the last commit","cells":["The fresh spec is tinted","Only uncommitted work is tinted"]},{"label":"Notices a write while open","cells":["Desktop only, no watcher in the web app","Desktop only"]},{"label":"Works with no git","cells":["No, it degrades to first-open baseline","No"]},{"label":"Anchor survives another tool's write","cells":["Untested","Untested"]}],"note":"The anchor question is still open after two adversarial rounds, and both other rows depend on it.","caption":"Three cold-start rules against the two scenarios that matter."},"stakes":"Either a stranger's first document is entirely tinted, which is the stated test failure, or the counter reads zero and nothing is demonstrated.","state":["The demo is every paragraph tinted on a spec the agent has just written (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:45`).","The sidecar is created on first use and no cold-start rule is stated anywhere (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:135`).","Local git, the background watcher and the search index are desktop-only (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:100`).","Whether the anchor survives an out-of-band write is still open after two rounds (`docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:146`)."],"path":["The demo was designed around a file an agent had just written, where every span genuinely is new.","The pilot scenario, ten strangers bringing their own repos, was never separated from it (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:231`)."],"tension":["The working tree with no pull request is the container section 1 claims nobody covers, and it supplies the only natural baseline.","That baseline needs git, which the access model puts on desktop only, so it covers no plain folder and no drag-in session.","The web app is the trial and the desktop app is the daily surface (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:106`), and the exit test runs on one of them.","The week 3-4 test already opens a spec-kit and a superpowers repo (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:354`), so adding an out-of-band write costs almost nothing."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"The two cold-start rules and what each first screen looks like","cols":["Rule","Fresh agent output (the demo)","Stranger's existing 3,000-word repo (the pilot)"],"rows":[["Everything unreviewed","Every paragraph tinted — the intended demo","Every paragraph tinted — reads as \"highlighted\", the stated test failure"],["Baseline at first open","Nothing tinted until the agent writes again","Nothing tinted; counter reads 0; nothing to show"],["Baseline at last commit, uncommitted work unreviewed","The agent's fresh spec is tinted","Only what changed since the last commit is tinted — usually a little, sometimes nothing"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"What is fixed, and what is open","items":[["Sidecar unit","one JSON line per span: path, byte start, byte end, content hash, reviewed-by, reviewed-at","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:135"],["Cold-start rule stated anywhere","no","grep of PRODUCT-BRIEF, GAPS, WEEK0"],["Pilot users bringing their own repos","10 of 10","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:231"],["Five-second test failure words","\"highlighted\" or \"error\"","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:411"],["GitHub Viewed state","free at every tier, per file, auto-unmarked on change, private to each reviewer","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:56"],["Local git","desktop only","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:100"]]},{"type":"table","title":"What each surface can do for the core loop (PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:92-100)","cols":["Capability","Web, GitHub repo","Web, local folder (Chrome/Edge)","Desktop"],"rows":[["Review state (F2)","Yes; sidecar committed","Yes","Yes"],["Background watcher","No","No","Yes"],["Local git","No","No","Yes"],["Notices an agent write while the file is open","No (derived from the watcher row)","No (derived)","Yes"],["MCP server — writes that carry the prompt","No","No","Yes"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"The untested mechanism","items":[["Out-of-band anchor survival","still open after 2 adversarial rounds","GAPS-2026-09-08.md:146"],["Anchor design","byte range + content hash, relocated by the splice locator","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:135"],["Journal as anchor","explicitly rejected — \"git, other editors and agents bypass it\"","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:135"],["Week 3–4 test in the plan","tint works on files frontmatter did not write, on one spec-kit and one superpowers repo","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:354"],["Review-state code in src/ today","none","grep for review.jsonl / unreviewed / reviewState → 0 files"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Baseline at the last commit; pilot on desktop","what":"Anything uncommitted at first open is unreviewed, and the ten strangers use the surface where git and the watcher exist.","gains":["Uses the container the product claims as its differentiator","The demo and the pilot behave the same way"],"costs":["Puts the Tauri build, notarisation and the identity fix on the critical path","Covers no plain folder and no web session"],"system":"The cold-start rule reads git; it degrades to first-open baseline without it.","screens":"No new screen; the tint's meaning changes on first open.","money":"Apple and Windows certificates before week 10."},{"k":"b","label":"Everything unreviewed at first open; pilot on either surface","what":"A repo we have never seen is entirely unread until someone reads it.","gains":["The counter is honest: nobody has read this","No git dependency, so every surface behaves alike"],"costs":["A stranger's first document is fully tinted","That is the exact five-second-test failure mode"],"system":"Simplest rule; no git read.","screens":"The first open looks like a highlighted document.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Baseline at first open; pilot on the web app with a focus refresh","what":"The repo as it stands is treated as read, and the web app re-reads on window focus and tab activation.","gains":["Clean first screen and every later tint is real signal","No install, which the access model says the trial needs"],"costs":["The first session may demonstrate nothing at all","A focus refresh is not a watcher and is uncosted"],"system":"Adds a re-read on focus in the web shell.","screens":"No new screen.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Anchor test in weeks 3-4, then last-commit baseline, pilot on desktop","what":"Add an out-of-band write to the existing week 3-4 test, then commit to the last-commit rule and the desktop surface.","gains":["Answers the one mechanism the gap register calls the only scenario the product exists for","Costs almost nothing, because the test already opens both repos"],"costs":["The surface choice is unsettled for two more weeks","A failure changes the sidecar design entirely"],"system":"No change until the test returns.","screens":"No change until the test returns.","money":"None."}],"rec":"d","recCase":["Both the baseline and the surface are downstream of a mechanism that has never been run.","The week 3-4 test already opens a spec-kit and a superpowers repo, so adding let the agent write again and check the anchors is one line.","Landing on the last-commit rule uses the container section 1 claims, and it degrades to first-open baseline for a folder with no git, which is explainable.","Then the web app is the trial and the desktop app carries the exit test, which is what the access model already says."],"flip":"If the anchor does not survive a write by another tool, the sidecar design changes and this question is replaced by a much larger one.","linked":["FF8","FL12","FL18"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:45","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:135","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:231","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:411","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:100","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:106","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:354","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:56","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:146","merged: FL15"]},{"id":"FL18","cat":"Flow & interaction","sub":"Lifecycle","weight":"critical","q":"Does a span have a seen state between changed and reviewed, or only the two?","lede":"The sidecar records reviewed-by and reviewed-at and nothing else, so scrolling past a span and judging it are the same event or neither.","visual":{"kind":"state","states":[{"label":"Untouched","meta":"hash matches","tone":"sunk"},{"label":"Changed","meta":"hash differs","via":"a write","tone":"warn","current":true},{"label":"Seen","meta":"scrolled into view","via":"scroll","tone":"accent"},{"label":"Reviewed","meta":"accept, revert or skip","via":"a key","tone":"good"}],"note":"Only Untouched and Reviewed exist in the sidecar today. Seen is the state the store cannot express.","caption":"The review lifecycle, and the missing middle."},"stakes":"Without a seen state, the bulk-clear gate, the exit measure and any dismissal rate all read the same single boolean.","state":["The sidecar line is path, byte start, byte end, content hash, reviewed-by, reviewed-at (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:135`). One state, no kind.","The drawer already offers three acts, accept, revert and skip, and the sidecar spec names none of them (`docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:459`).","The exit measure counts spans reviewed, meaning accept, revert or skip (`docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:19`).","The demo has a span clear on reading: read one, it clears (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:45`)."],"path":["The store was specified before any interaction was drawn, so it holds an outcome and not an act.","The prototype then drew a skip button, a Mark all read button and a hover card, which are three acts the store cannot tell apart."],"tension":["The demo sells clearing by reading, and the pilot gate needs proof that reading happened.","A gated bulk clear needs viewport tracking the code does not have, and viewport tracking is a seen state by another name.","Clinical alerting is what one boolean looks like at scale: 12,659 of 14,612 alerts overridden, 88.3% of the reasons meaningless.","Three states cost one field in the sidecar and one more transition in the renderer."],"evidence":[],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Three states, and the sidecar records which act cleared a span","what":"Changed, seen and reviewed, with an action kind on every line: scrolled, accepted, reverted, skipped, bulk.","gains":["The exit measure can tell a reader from a clicker","A dismissal rate and a gated bulk clear both become possible"],"costs":["One field and one transition to build","Viewport tracking the code does not have today"],"system":"The sidecar grows an action kind; the renderer grows a seen transition.","screens":"The tint can fade at seen and clear at reviewed, which is two treatments rather than one.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Two states, and only an explicit act clears a span","what":"Scrolling never clears anything. A key or a button does.","gains":["The counter means judged, not passed over","No viewport tracking at all"],"costs":["Contradicts the fifteen-second demo, where reading clears","Every span costs a keystroke, which is the fatigue path"],"system":"No change.","screens":"The demo has to be re-cut.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Two states, and scrolling past a span clears it","what":"The demo's reading model: what passed under the eye is read.","gains":["Matches the fifteen-second demo exactly","Zero friction on a long document"],"costs":["Scrolling fast clears a whole file","The exit measure then counts scrolling"],"system":"Needs viewport tracking anyway, for the wrong purpose.","screens":"No panel act is required at all.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Two states now, with an action-kind field reserved in the sidecar","what":"Ship the boolean, write the field into the format, fill it later.","gains":["No behaviour to build in MVP-0","Readers written now do not break later"],"costs":["Every MVP-0 measurement is taken on the boolean","The pilot cannot tell a reader from a clicker"],"system":"Format grows a field nothing writes.","screens":"No change.","money":"None."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["The demo and the exit measure disagree today: one says reading clears a span, the other counts explicit acts.","Three states settle that disagreement without choosing between them, because the tint can fade at seen and clear at reviewed.","The sidecar has to learn an action kind for the bulk-clear decision regardless, so the marginal cost is the seen transition alone.","Every downstream measurement here, the exit gate, a dismissal rate and a gated bulk clear, needs the distinction to exist."],"flip":"If the pilot's local counts show seen and reviewed within a few per cent of each other, the extra state buys nothing and (b) is enough.","linked":["E37","FL11","FL19","FL20","FL5","FL6"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:135","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:45","docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:459","docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:19","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38658357/"]},{"id":"FL19","cat":"Flow & interaction","sub":"The review surface","weight":"critical","q":"Is the primary surface an exhaustible list of every changed span, or only the spans a rule selects?","lede":"Every review product converged on an exhaustible list, and every measurement of one says it stops being read long before it ends.","visual":{"kind":"funnel","steps":[{"label":"Prescribing sessions","n":500274,"unit":"sessions","tone":"sunk"},{"label":"Sessions where any of 31 rules fired","n":935,"unit":"sessions","tone":"accent"},{"label":"Of those alerts, accepted","n":57.5,"unit":"per cent","tone":"good"}],"note":"The comparison: enumerated alerting is overridden 55-98% across 34 studies.","caption":"The alerting system that earned acceptance fired in 0.19% of sessions."},"stakes":"The plan's panel is an exhaustible list, and the only measured systems that keep acceptance fire almost never.","state":["F2 ships a review panel with a counter, and the tree carries unreviewed bars (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:56`).","The panel is designed as a persistent list rather than a per-session diff (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:383`).","The drawer headline counts unreviewed spans in this file, walked one at a time (`docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:458`).","Nothing in the plan caps how many spans are surfaced in one sitting."],"path":["The list is the affordance the category converged on: GitHub's file list, Zed's agent panel, the diff pane in four editors.","The attention evidence arrived afterwards and runs the other way."],"tension":["Cisco found no useful review above 250 lines and a 60-minute wear-out. That is source code, and the mapping onto markdown spans is an analogy.","Google measured a 3.2-hour weekly review budget against a 24-line median change.","The one clinical system that earned acceptance fired 31 rules in 0.19% of 500,274 sessions, at 57.5% acceptance.","Suppression means ranking, and a ranking is state the projection law says must be derivable from the file alone."],"evidence":[],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Suppression by default, with the full list one click away","what":"The panel opens on a filtered set, and the rule is a deterministic function of the file.","gains":["Matches every measured system that kept acceptance","Nothing is hidden, only deferred behind one click"],"costs":["A rule that is wrong hides the thing that mattered","The rule has to be explainable in one sentence"],"system":"The filter must be derivable from the bytes, or the projection law breaks.","screens":"The panel gains a filtered default and a show-everything control.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Enumeration as today: every changed span, in document order","what":"The panel lists everything and the person works down it.","gains":["No rule to explain and nothing can be hidden","Matches what the category has converged on"],"costs":["The list stops being read long before it ends","Every override measurement in the evidence is against it"],"system":"No change.","screens":"No change.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"A budget rather than a filter: a fixed number of spans a sitting","what":"The surface offers a capped batch and defers the rest to the next sitting.","gains":["Respects the measured wear-out without ranking anything","No judgement about which span matters"],"costs":["An arbitrary number nobody has measured for prose","Deferred spans still accumulate"],"system":"A counter and a cut-off; no ranking state.","screens":"The panel gains an end-of-batch state.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Enumeration, plus a dismissal rate that retires a span class","what":"Show everything, and stop surfacing a class of change once it is ignored past a stated rate.","gains":["The suppression is learned rather than guessed","Tricorder's probation threshold is a precedent"],"costs":["Needs live counts before it does anything","The first weeks are pure enumeration"],"system":"Per-class dismissal counts in the local usage file.","screens":"No new screen; classes quietly stop appearing.","money":"None."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["Every measured review system that keeps acceptance fires rarely, and every one that enumerates is overridden between 55% and 98%.","The filter can be a deterministic function of the file, so the projection law holds and no ranking is stored.","The full list one click away means nothing is hidden, which is the difference between suppression and omission.","MHRA already permits an audit trail to be reviewed by exception reporting rather than as a full list, so the compliance reading survives."],"flip":"If the 40-hunk test shows strangers finishing an exhaustive list without reaching accept-all, enumeration is not the problem and (b) stands.","linked":["D4","FL11","FL18","FL4","FL6"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:56","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:383","docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:458","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34450669/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/35673040/","https://static1.smartbear.co/support/media/resources/cc/book/code-review-cisco-case-study.pdf","https://sback.it/publications/icse2018seip.pdf","https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5aa2b9ede5274a3e391e37f3/MHRA_GxP_data_integrity_guide_March_edited_Final.pdf"],"dupes":{"dropped":["D24"],"why":"Does the review surface enumerate every changed span or suppress to an exception list. Same four poles (suppress / enumerate / budget / enumerate-plus-dismissal-rate) and both rec suppression. Flow & interaction owns the review surface."}},{"id":"FL2","cat":"Flow & interaction","sub":"Keyboard","weight":"high","q":"Which keyboard model ships for review — single letters, modifier keys, or single letters scoped to the drawer?","lede":"Three incompatible key maps for one act sit in the corpus, none is in the code, and single letters carry a level-A duty nobody costed.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":118,"cols":[{"title":"r21-s6 walk-and-act"},{"title":"r24-v4 Tab and y/n"},{"title":"Prototype drawer","tone":"accent"}],"rows":[{"label":"Walk","cells":["j / k","Tab / Shift-Tab","j / k, per the hint chip"]},{"label":"Accept","cells":["a","y, Enter accepts all","a"]},{"label":"Reject or revert","cells":["r means reject","n","r means revert"]},{"label":"Third verb","cells":["e, edit then accept","Esc discards","s, skip; absent from the hint"]},{"label":"WCAG 2.2 SC 2.1.4","cells":["fires under a screen reader","clear, modifiers only","fires under a screen reader"]}],"note":"r means reject in one map and revert in another. Those are opposite acts on one span.","caption":"Three maps for one decision, none of them in the code."},"stakes":"`r` means reject in one map and revert in another, which are opposite acts on the same span.","state":["The code types the world as `mod+k | mod+p | mod+g` (`src/modules/app-shell/presentation/use-hotkey.ts:5`) plus three authoring keys.","No review key exists, and there is no review-state code in `src/` at all.","The plan says one key reverts any span (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:20`) and never names the key."],"path":["Each research round designed a map against its own surface: a proposal render, then a located AI edit, then the review drawer.","The prototype then disagreed with itself. The drawer's buttons offer accept, revert and skip; its hint chip omits skip (`docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:458`)."],"tension":["Single letters are the fast map and the one WCAG 2.2 SC 2.1.4 flags at level A (`k4-accessibility.md:106`).","The recorded remedies are a remap screen, a modifier requirement, or restricting the keys to focus.","A remap screen is priced at 3-4 days for two founders (`r24-v1-table-stakes.md:36`) and no exhibit carries it.","A reader's caret usually sits in the document, not in the drawer, so focus scoping costs reach."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"Four keyboard models in the corpus for one decision","cols":["Source","Walk","Accept","Reject / revert","Other"],"rows":[["r21-s6:87","j / k","a","r = reject","e = edit-then-accept"],["r24-v4:146","Tab / Shift-Tab","y, Enter = accept all","n","Esc = discard"],["prototype:459 (S4 drawer buttons)","—","a · accept","r · revert","s · skip"],["prototype:458 (same drawer, hint chip)","j k","a","r","`s` missing from the hint"],["prototype:387 (S2 hover card)","—","\"Mark reviewed\"","\"Revert · ⌘⇧Z\"","—"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"What exists in the code today","items":[["Global hotkeys bound","3","use-hotkey.ts:5 — mod+k, mod+p, mod+g"],["Authoring keys bound","3","CodeMirrorEditor.tsx:224-226 — Mod-b/i/e"],["Review keys bound","0","no review-state code in src/ (grep: review.jsonl, reviewState, unreviewed → 0 files)"],["Customisable keymap","none","r24-v1:36 costs it at 3–4 days and names this exact line: \"`use-hotkey.ts:5` literally types the world as…\""],["WCAG remedy on record","remap, modifier, or focus-scope","k4-accessibility.md:106, SC 2.1.4, level A"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Single letters everywhere, with a remap screen in MVP-0","what":"j and k walk, a, r and s act, anywhere in the app, and Settings lets you rebind them.","gains":["Fastest map for a keyboard-fluent reviewer","Matches the drawer as it is already drawn"],"costs":["Adds the SC 2.1.4 remap UI to MVP-0 at 3-4 days","No exhibit carries that cost today"],"system":"A keymap store and a rebinding surface the code has nowhere else.","screens":"Adds a Settings hotkeys screen; the drawer is unchanged.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Modifier keys only: j and k walk, Cmd-Enter accepts, Cmd-Shift-Z reverts","what":"No single letter ever acts, so the WCAG criterion is met without a remap screen.","gains":["Clears SC 2.1.4 with no remap UI","Keeps the revert key the hover card already promises"],"costs":["Slower per hunk on a long change","The drawer's buttons have to be redrawn"],"system":"No new store. One keymap table.","screens":"Redraws the drawer's hint chip and buttons.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Single letters, active only while the review drawer has focus","what":"The keys fire in the drawer and nowhere else, so the criterion's focus exemption applies.","gains":["The speed of single letters and no remap screen","Forces one meaning for r, because the drawer names the act"],"costs":["A focus-management rule the code has nowhere else","Keys stop working with the caret in the document"],"system":"One focus-scope rule around the drawer.","screens":"The drawer becomes a focus container; the hover card keeps modifier keys.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"No review keyboard in MVP-0 — buttons only","what":"Every review act is a click until after the pilot.","gains":["Removes a decision and costs nothing","No accessibility exposure"],"costs":["Makes a 40-hunk review mouse-driven","That is the slowest version of the thing being sold"],"system":"No change.","screens":"The hint chip comes off the drawer.","money":"None."}],"rec":"c","recCase":["Focus scoping gives the speed of single letters and the compliance of modifiers for the price of one rule.","k4's own note records that the criterion allows active-focus-only shortcuts, so no remap screen is required.","Scoping settles the verb collision by force: whatever the drawer calls the act is what the key does."],"flip":"If review acts are to be driven from the document body, by hover card or caret, focus scoping does not apply and only the modifier map is compliant.","linked":["D15","FL18","FL19","FL3"],"sources":["src/modules/app-shell/presentation/use-hotkey.ts:5","src/modules/app-shell/presentation/KnowledgeUI.tsx:56","src/modules/editor/presentation/CodeMirrorEditor.tsx:224","docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:458","docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:459","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r21-s6-renders-that-earn-it.md:87","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r24-v4-ai-native-editing.md:146","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r24-v1-table-stakes.md:36","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-29-r12/k4-accessibility.md:106","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:20"]},{"id":"FL3","cat":"Flow & interaction","sub":"Interaction floor","weight":"high","q":"Do the table-stakes interaction days go into MVP-0, and does Cmd-K move to insert-link with them?","lede":"The sequence spends 69 of about 70 engineering days before it reaches the line that reads table stakes and polish.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":132,"cols":[{"title":"Whole floor"},{"title":"Cheap half","tone":"accent"},{"title":"Ship as is"}],"rows":[{"label":"Engineering days added","cells":["13-21, midpoint 17.5","2.5-3.5","0"]},{"label":"MVP-0 total","cells":["about 87","about 73","about 70"]},{"label":"Cmd-K","cells":["insert link","insert link","file switcher"]},{"label":"Palette, outline key, switcher","cells":["done","done","as inherited"]},{"label":"Table editing, HTML paste","cells":["done","not done","not done"]},{"label":"Extra calendar weeks at 1.21 d/wk","cells":["about 14","about 3","0"]}],"note":"Day counts are r24-v1's, stated as days for two founders against a one-author commit record.","caption":"What each amount of floor buys, and what it costs in weeks."},"stakes":"The exit test is whether six of ten strangers keep it, and a stranger who cannot bold a heading never forms a view on review state.","state":["Six named blocks in the sequence sum to 69 days against a stated total of about 70 (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:227`).","The measured floor is eight items at 13-21 days, midpoint 17.5, and none of them is scheduled (`docs/CRITIQUE.md:602`).","`insertLink` is written and reachable only by mouse (`src/modules/editor/presentation/toolbar-transforms.ts:234`, `Toolbar.tsx:102`).","Cmd-K opens the note switcher (`src/modules/app-shell/presentation/KnowledgeUI.tsx:56`); the prototype's status bar says a third thing (`prototype:315`)."],"path":["The editor shell came from sgnk-md, where 41 of 43 editor files are byte-identical. Nobody chose these bindings for this product.","The floor was measured by reading the code against the published key maps of Obsidian, Typora, Bear, iA Writer, Zed and VS Code."],"tension":["In Typora, Bear, iA Writer, Obsidian and VS Code, Cmd-K is insert-link (`docs/CRITIQUE.md:614`). Here it opens a file switcher.","r24-v1 prices the floor in days for two founders; the commit record is 80 of 80 by one author (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:231`).","At the measured 1.21 engineering days a calendar week, 17.5 more days is roughly fourteen more weeks.","A VS Code extension inherits the whole floor and the keymap from the host and deletes this decision (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:364`)."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"The sequence, added up (PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:227)","items":[["Fix-first","24 days","NF-1, NF-3, CI, engine wiring, byte budget, BYO key, structured output"],["Review state F2","18 days","store 6 + rendering 5 + revert 3 + panel 4"],["F3 attribution + F4 answer in place","6 days",""],["F5 idea mode + F6 decision flow","8 days",""],["F7 repo docs scan","10 days",""],["F8 AI panel","3 days",""],["Named blocks, total","69 days","against a stated ~70 for MVP-0"],["Left for table stakes and polish","~1 day","derived: 70 − 69"]]},{"type":"table","title":"The measured floor, and whether it is scheduled (CRITIQUE.md:602-610)","cols":["Item","Cost (two founders, per r24-v1:31)","In any MVP stage"],"rows":[["⌘1–6, ⌘K link, list/quote/task toggles, checkbox, move-line","0.5 d","No"],["Outline hotkey + fuzzy heading jump","0.5 d","No"],["Palette that indexes everything and shows hotkeys","1–2 d","No"],["Quick-switcher deltas: recents-on-empty, create-on-miss, ⌘⏎ new tab","0.5 d","No"],["HTML paste → markdown","2–3 d","No"],["Table editing: Tab nav, add/remove row and column, alignment","5–8 d","No"],["Splice-backed table writes","+2 d","No"],["Customisable keymap","3–4 d","No"],["Total","13–21 d, midpoint 17.5","0 of 8"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"Re-measured against the current plan","items":[["Occurrences of \"hotkey\" in PRODUCT-BRIEF.md","0","grep"],["Occurrences of \"keymap\" or \"table editing\"","0","grep"],["Occurrences of \"palette\"","1","line 55, as an existing F1 capability, not as scheduled work"],["Command palette today","14 static commands, no hotkey column, no recents, no pinning","r24-v1:37"],["17.5 days in calendar terms","70 calendar days as person-days; 104–140 as pair-days","CRITIQUE.md:616"]]},{"type":"table","title":"⌘K across the three artefacts and the field","cols":["Where","⌘K does","⌘P does","Insert link"],"rows":[["frontmatter code","Quick note switcher (KnowledgeUI.tsx:56)","Command palette (:57)","implemented, toolbar only (Toolbar.tsx:102)"],["frontmatter prototype","Commands (prototype:315)","Files (:315)","not shown"],["Typora, Bear, iA, Obsidian, VS Code","Insert link (CRITIQUE.md:614)","Switcher or palette","⌘K"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"The interaction floor this sits inside","items":[["Authoring keys bound today","3","CodeMirrorEditor.tsx:224-226 — no ⌘1–6, no list, no quote, no task"],["`toggleTaskAtLine`","written, unbound","toolbar-transforms.ts:112"],["`insertLink`","written, unbound","toolbar-transforms.ts:234"],["Cost of the whole hotkey group","0.5 day for two people","CRITIQUE.md:602, item 1 of 8; r24-v1's table header states its costs are for two founders"],["Occurrences of \"hotkey\" or \"keymap\" in the current plan","0","grep of PRODUCT-BRIEF.md"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"The whole floor into MVP-0, bindings moved to markdown convention","what":"All eight measured items ship before the ten strangers see anything.","gains":["The pilot judges the review idea, not the editor","No item is left to be named by a stranger"],"costs":["MVP-0 goes from about 70 to about 87 days","Roughly fourteen more calendar weeks at the measured rate"],"system":"Table editing needs splice-backed writes, which is engine work.","screens":"Adds a hotkeys screen, a table toolbar and a richer palette.","money":"None directly; the delay is the cost."},{"k":"b","label":"The cheap half only: hotkeys, outline key, palette, switcher deltas","what":"Cmd-K becomes insert-link, the switcher moves to Cmd-O, and the palette indexes everything.","gains":["Buys the first ninety seconds for about 4% of the budget","Two of the four items call functions that already exist"],"costs":["Leaves table editing and HTML paste out","Both are called disqualifying in the survey"],"system":"A keymap table over existing transforms. No engine work.","screens":"The palette gains a hotkey column and recents; no new screen.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Ship the pilot on the current floor and the current bindings","what":"Nothing is scheduled; the ten strangers name what they miss.","gains":["Fastest to the exit test","The feedback is real rather than surveyed"],"costs":["A reviewer who pastes a URL gets a file switcher","The exit test cannot separate the editor from the idea"],"system":"No change.","screens":"No change.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Resolve the form factor first — an extension inherits floor and keymap","what":"A VS Code extension gets the whole interaction floor from the host.","gains":["Deletes the floor and the keymap question at once","Deletes the bring-your-own-key work as well"],"costs":["Forfeits Live mode, which has no view-zone API","The name is held in that store by an 82,265-install incumbent"],"system":"A different shell around the same engine.","screens":"Kills the launcher, the tree and the mode switcher.","money":"Removes the certificate costs of a desktop build."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["Three days buys the part of the floor a reviewer meets in the first two minutes, and that is where the exit test is decided.","Cmd-K to insert-link is the cheapest credibility available, because the function is already written and bound to nothing.","Booking the days explicitly stops table stakes and polish from being a one-day line after 69 days are spent.","Cmd-O over Cmd-P for the switcher, because the markdown editors the free tier aims at all use Cmd-O."],"flip":"If decision 6 resolves toward a VS Code extension, the host owns the keymap and the floor, and (d) is strictly better.","linked":["FF1","FL12","FL2"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:227","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:231","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:364","docs/CRITIQUE.md:602","docs/CRITIQUE.md:614","docs/CRITIQUE.md:616","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r24-v1-table-stakes.md:31","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r24-v1-table-stakes.md:37","src/modules/editor/presentation/toolbar-transforms.ts:234","src/modules/editor/presentation/Toolbar.tsx:102","src/modules/app-shell/presentation/KnowledgeUI.tsx:56","docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:315","merged: FL17"],"dupes":{"dropped":["F24"],"why":"Do the table-stakes interaction days go into MVP-0 and does Cmd-K move to insert-link. Near-verbatim option sets, both rec (b) the cheap half. Flow & interaction owns the interaction floor."}},{"id":"FL5","cat":"Flow & interaction","sub":"Bulk actions","weight":"high","q":"Does a one-click Mark all read ship in MVP-0, and what is it allowed to clear?","lede":"The prototype draws two bulk-clear buttons, and the same corpus names a bulk clear as the condition under which the interaction is theatre.","visual":{"kind":"ba","before":{"title":"Launcher, as drawn","lines":[{"t":"3 projects, 128 documents","mark":"neutral"},{"t":"7 unreviewed","mark":"warn"},{"t":"sorted unreviewed first","mark":"neutral"}]},"after":{"title":"One click later","lines":[{"t":"3 projects, 128 documents","mark":"neutral"},{"t":"0 unreviewed","mark":"good"},{"t":"nothing was read","mark":"stop"},{"t":"the sidecar cannot tell","mark":"stop"}]},"via":"Mark all read","note":"The counter is retention lever one and the pilot's exit measure. Both go to zero together.","caption":"The counter emptied without a document being read."},"stakes":"A button that zeroes the counter without reading removes both the reason to return and the evidence that anyone reviewed.","state":["The prototype ships Mark all read on the clarify screen (`docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:523`) and accept all in file on the refactor screen (`:648`).","F2's feature row specifies tint, one-key revert and a panel with a counter, and no bulk action (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:56`).","The sidecar line records reviewed-by and reviewed-at and no action kind (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:135`)."],"path":["The buttons were drawn to make the screens feel complete.","The flow research had already ruled the other way: accept-all is disabled while any uncited paragraph remains (`r21-s7-flow-design.md:61`)."],"tension":["Opening frontmatter is how the count goes to zero (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:425`), so a bulk clear removes the daily trigger.","The week-2 gate is at least one review action, and a bulk clear cannot be told from a reading (`docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:22`).","Clinical alerting shows the shape of no escape: 12,659 of 14,612 alerts overridden, with 88.3% of the typed reasons meaningless.","A returning user facing a large backlog with no escape abandons the file instead."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"What each artefact says about bulk clearing","cols":["Artefact","Position"],"rows":[["Prototype S3 (`prototype:523`)","\"Mark all read\" — one click, whole file, no gate"],["Prototype S8 (`prototype:648`)","\"accept all in file\" alongside per-hunk accept/skip"],["r21-s7:61, flow 2 step 5","\"`Accept all` is **disabled** while any uncited paragraph remains\""],["CRITIQUE.md:643","\"If ≥5 hit 'accept all' in both, the interaction is theatre and MVP-0 has no demo\""],["PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:56 (F2 spec)","No bulk action specified at all"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"What the counter is load-bearing for","items":[["Retention lever #1","the counter","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:425 — \"opening frontmatter is how the count goes to zero\""],["Exit measure input","spans reviewed (accept, revert, skip)","WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:19"],["Pilot gate","≥1 review action in week 2","WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:22"],["States the drawer already offers","3 — accept, revert, skip","prototype:459; the sidecar spec at :135 names none of them"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"No bulk clear in MVP-0","what":"Every span is cleared by an act on that span, or by whatever the seen rule turns out to be.","gains":["The counter means exactly one thing","The pilot measurement is trustworthy"],"costs":["A 200-span backlog has no escape","The user may abandon the file rather than the span"],"system":"No change.","screens":"Removes two buttons from the prototype.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Ship Mark all read, recorded in the sidecar as a bulk clear","what":"The escape exists and every bulk clear is a distinguishable line in the store.","gains":["Users get an escape and the data stays honest","Bulk clears are countable and separable in the pilot"],"costs":["One field and one line of panel copy","A clicker still clears the counter"],"system":"The sidecar grows an action kind, which it needs anyway.","screens":"Keeps the button; adds a line of copy under it.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Ship it gated: enabled only when every span has been scrolled into view","what":"The button lights up once the document has actually passed under the eye.","gains":["Closest to what a review is meant to mean","The nearest thing here to the citation gate in the flow research"],"costs":["Needs viewport tracking the code does not have","A disabled button reads as broken unless it is explained"],"system":"Requires the seen state, so it depends on that decision.","screens":"The button gains a disabled state and a reason.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Ship Mark all read ungated, as drawn","what":"One click clears the file with no record of how.","gains":["Matches the prototype","The least surprising affordance"],"costs":["The counter, the lever and the exit measure clear in one click","The pilot cannot tell a reader from a clicker"],"system":"No change.","screens":"No change.","money":"None."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["A backlog with no escape is the fastest way to lose a returning user, so some bulk clear has to exist.","The honest version costs one field, and the sidecar has to learn an action kind regardless, because it cannot tell accept from revert from skip today.","Recording bulk clears distinctly keeps the week-2 gate meaningful, because at least one review action can then exclude one."],"flip":"If the pilot's local counts show bulk clears dominating individual clears, the interaction has failed the falsifier and the unit changes.","linked":["FL18","FL20","FL4"],"sources":["docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:523","docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:648","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r21-s7-flow-design.md:61","docs/CRITIQUE.md:643","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:425","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:135","docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:22","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38658357/"]},{"id":"FL6","cat":"Flow & interaction","sub":"The counter","weight":"high","q":"What does the review counter count, and is it allowed to be a dot?","lede":"One prototype screen shows four numbers for the same document, and the plan and the PRD take opposite positions on the badge.","visual":{"kind":"screen","title":"S3 clarify, one document","panes":[{"label":"Body and breadcrumb","w":36,"rows":[{"label":"written by spec-kit, 3 questions for you","meta":"prototype:495","tone":"warn"},{"label":"6 tinted spans in the body","meta":"prototype:503-510","tone":"neutral"}]},{"label":"Outline","w":30,"rows":[{"label":"Functional requirements 5 of 5","meta":"prototype:520","tone":"neutral"},{"label":"Non-goals 1 of 1","meta":"prototype:520","tone":"neutral"},{"label":"total 6","meta":"agrees with the body","tone":"accent"}]},{"label":"Status bar","w":34,"rows":[{"label":"7 unreviewed spans, 92%","meta":"prototype:514","tone":"stop"},{"label":"2 questions open","meta":"prototype:514","tone":"warn"}]}],"note":"7 divided by 0.92 is 7.61 spans, so the printed percentage has no possible span base.","caption":"Four surfaces, four numbers, one document."},"stakes":"The counter is the launcher sort key, the tree bar, the panel headline and the exit measure, so an undefined unit propagates into all four.","state":["The prototype prints four different numbers for one document, and each status-bar percentage implies a fractional span count.","The plan makes the counter retention lever one (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:425`); PRD v2 bans red-dot unread counts (`docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:1783`).","The count appears in five places at once, including a dot on the editor tab (`docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:329`).","The sidecar is one line per span, which fixes the numerator and never states a denominator (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:135`)."],"path":["Each surface was drawn for its own screen, and nothing reconciled them afterwards.","The ban was written from the retention evidence in August; the counter as a lever was added in September. Neither cites the other."],"tension":["Spans are the sidecar's own unit, so they cost nothing to compute and cannot drift from the store.","A bar that reads like progress implies bytes, because a one-word span and a 400-word section are not equal work.","PRD 18.5 bans dots as a discovery strategy, which a count of your own repo is not (`docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:2029`).","Anthropic's extension already ships an unread dot and a tab badge, so the mechanic differentiates nothing (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:560`)."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"The percentage cannot be a span ratio on any screen (computed from the prototype's own printed numbers)","items":[["S2 editor, auth.md","3 unreviewed · 64% → 4.69 total spans","prototype:394"],["S4 review","3 unreviewed · 88% → 3.41 total spans","prototype:455, :458"],["S3 clarify, spec.md","7 unreviewed · 92% → 7.61 total spans","prototype:514"],["S2c split","2 unreviewed · 31% → 6.45 total spans","prototype:591"]]},{"type":"table","title":"Three counts of one document on one prototype screen","cols":["Surface","Reads","Line"],"rows":[["Status bar","7 unreviewed spans · 92%","prototype:514"],["Outline","5 + 1 = 6 unreviewed","prototype:520"],["Document body","6 tinted spans (`class=\"m1\"`)","prototype:503-510"],["Breadcrumb","3 questions for you","prototype:495"],["Status bar and right rail, questions","2 questions open / 2","prototype:514, :517"],["Tree bar, spec.md","92% (width, no unit); plan.md and tasks.md both 100%","prototype:484-486"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"Everywhere the number appears","items":[["Launcher card bars","8 cards: 64%, 88%, 31%, 12%, 45%, 22% unreviewed; two read \"all reviewed\"","prototype:304-311"],["Launcher status","7 unreviewed across 128 documents","prototype:315"],["File tree","per-file bar","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:409"],["Editor status bar","3 unreviewed spans · 64%","prototype:394"],["Review drawer headline","3 unreviewed in this file","prototype:458"],["Exit measure","spans reviewed","WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:19"]]},{"type":"table","title":"The two positions, both current","cols":["Document","Says","Line"],"rows":[["Plan v15, §17 retention","The counter is lever #1; the return trigger is created by the user's own agent, daily","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:425"],["PRD v2, §17 retention","\"Banned outright: streaks · badges · XP or levels · … · red-dot unread counts\"","FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2:1783"],["PRD v2, §18.5 affordances","\"no badges, dots or status-bar chips **as a discovery strategy**\" — scoped to discovery, not to the number itself","FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2:2029"],["Plan v15, threats","Anthropic's extension already ships \"a missing unread dot\" and \"the editor tab badge showing unread\" (CHANGELOG 2.1.261)","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:560"],["Prototype","Count shown in 5 places simultaneously","prototype:315, :304, :329, :394, :458"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"What the plan claims for the counter, and its evidence class","items":[["Retention levers listed in §17","7","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:425-431"],["Levers with evidence that they retain","0","GAPS-2026-09-08.md:24 — \"Reasoning. No evidence that any lever retains\""],["Editors publishing retention data","0","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:417"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Spans everywhere, plain number, never a dot","what":"The percentage is unreviewed spans over total spans, printed as a number, never red and never on an icon.","gains":["Matches the store exactly, so the number cannot drift","Honours the ban's styling while keeping the information"],"costs":["A one-word span counts the same as a 400-word section","Every printed percentage in the prototype is recomputed"],"system":"No store change. One counting function, used by four surfaces.","screens":"Recomputes four status bars; deletes the tab dot.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Bytes for the bar, spans for the count","what":"The progress bar is proportional to how much there is to read; the action unit stays the span.","gains":["The bar means what a progress bar implies","The sidecar already stores byte start and end"],"costs":["The headline stops being a number a person can hold","Two units on every surface"],"system":"No store change; two derived figures instead of one.","screens":"The bar and the count disagree by design, so both need labels.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Files at the launcher and the tree, spans inside the document","what":"The top level counts documents with anything unreviewed; the panel counts spans.","gains":["One small integer at the top level","Matches GitHub's per-file Viewed state"],"costs":["Loses the per-span claim exactly where a buyer compares","Two units again, split by surface"],"system":"A per-file rollup over the sidecar.","screens":"Launcher and tree change; the panel does not.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"No persistent count — the panel lists what is unread when opened","what":"Nothing on the launcher, the tree or the tab. You see the state when you go looking.","gains":["Honours the ban outright","Cleanest against the visible-controls budget"],"costs":["Removes the plan's only daily return trigger","Retention then rests on the scan and answer-in-place"],"system":"No change.","screens":"Deletes the launcher bars, the tree bars and the tab dot.","money":"The retention argument in the plan has to be rewritten."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["The sidecar is one line per span, so spans are the only unit that costs nothing and cannot drift from the store.","The ban is aimed at the styling, and 18.5's own wording is scoped to discovery, so a plain number is inside it.","Whichever unit wins, the four status bars have to be recomputed before the five-second test, because none of them is self-consistent today.","A person shown contradictory counts reports on the contradiction rather than on the tint."],"flip":"If the 40-hunk test moves the review unit to files or sections, the counter follows it and (c) is correct.","linked":["FL19","FL4","FL5"],"sources":["docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:514","docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:520","docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:495","docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:329","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:135","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:425","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:560","docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:1783","docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:2029","docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:19","merged: FL7"]},{"id":"FL11","cat":"Flow & interaction","sub":"Kill lines","weight":"high","q":"Which review numbers stop the build — the five-second tint test, and a live dismissal rate?","lede":"Every other week 1-2 test carries a number that stops the build. The one test of whether the core signal is legible carries none.","visual":{"kind":"flow","perRow":3,"nodes":[{"label":"Five people, S2 screenshot, 5 s","tone":"neutral"},{"label":"They name the tint","note":"changed, provenance, highlighted, error","tone":"neutral"},{"label":"No threshold stated","note":"the plan names the words, not a count","tone":"stop","edge":"today"},{"label":"Build proceeds either way","tone":"warn"},{"label":"Ten people, 6 of 10 line","note":"matches every other arm and the exit test","tone":"accent","edge":"proposed"},{"label":"Redesign the treatment","note":"a treatment change, not a scope change","tone":"good"}],"note":"Tricorder puts an analyser on probation at a 10% not-useful rate; nothing here is instrumented at all.","caption":"The one test with no line, and the line proposed for it."},"stakes":"A test with no threshold can be run and then argued with, which is how three refuted headlines survived as long as they did.","state":["The test is listed in weeks 1-2: five people shown the S2 screenshot for five seconds (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:352`).","Section 16 names the failure words and no count and no consequence (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:411`).","The week-3 gate is the 4-of-10 review-state signal only (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:321`, `:337`).","Nothing in the plan instruments how often a surfaced span is ignored once the product is live."],"path":["The test was added in v14 from the F-pattern reasoning, which labels its own prediction as something the test replaces.","The kill lines elsewhere were written earlier, and this one was never backfilled."],"tension":["Five people is a small sample to hang a redesign on; ten matches every other arm and the exit test.","Tricorder puts an analyser on probation at a 10% not-useful rate and observed about 5%.","Clinical alerting shows the end state of no threshold: override between 55% and 98% across 34 studies.","Weeks 1-2 already carry 35 conversations, so five more people is a real cost (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:352`)."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"Kill lines in the plan, and the one without","cols":["Test","Threshold","Line"],"rows":[["Ten developers, review mock","under 4 of 10 unprompted → stop","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:321, :337"],["Engine refusal class","over 10 of 7,969 by day 24 → falsified","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:327"],["Ten strangers, MVP-0 exit","6 of 10 keep it","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:206"],["Obsidian plugin channel","under 200 installs in 14 days → kill — but the channel is CUT at :304, so the line is stale","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:204"],["Five-second tint test","none stated","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:352, :411"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"What the tint is competing against, in the one population with a vote","items":[["Nested-code-block rendering bug","501 likes, 117 posts, 18,331 views","Obsidian forum, PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:410"],["\"List of changes made to shared vault since last view\"","0 likes, 251 views, 1 post in nearly 3 years","same forum, same date"],["\"Tracking changes within notes\"","1 like","same"],["\"Suggestion Mode like Google Docs/Word\"","3 likes","same"],["People already scheduled for weeks 1–2 conversations","35","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:352 — 10 developers + 5 who bill + 20 team conversations"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Both get a line: 6 of 10 on the tint test, and a live dismissal rate","what":"The screenshot test gates the build, and a span class that is ignored past a stated rate stops being surfaced.","gains":["The signal is checked before build and after ship","Tricorder's threshold is a precedent for the second half"],"costs":["Five more conversations in a full week","The dismissal counter has to exist in the local usage file"],"system":"Adds a per-class dismissal count to the opt-in local counts.","screens":"No new screen; a rule about what stops appearing.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"The tint test only, widened to ten people at 6 of 10","what":"One consequential test before build, and nothing measured afterwards.","gains":["Comparable with the other arms","Cheap to act on, because it changes a treatment"],"costs":["Nothing catches the signal decaying after ship","Habituation is invisible"],"system":"No change.","screens":"No change.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"The dismissal rate only, instrumented from the first pilot week","what":"Skip the screenshot test and let live behaviour decide.","gains":["Measures action rather than naming","No extra week-1 load"],"costs":["The treatment is built before it is checked","A failure is found after 18 days are spent"],"system":"Adds the dismissal count.","screens":"No change.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Both advisory — signals that feed the design, not gates","what":"Run them, read them, decide by judgement.","gains":["Schedule certainty","No arbitrary number to defend"],"costs":["A test with no line gets argued with","The one thing the whole surface rests on stays unfalsifiable"],"system":"No change.","screens":"No change.","money":"None."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["Ten and 6-of-10 match the plan's existing sampling, so the tint result sits alongside the other arms.","The failure is cheap to act on, because it changes a treatment rather than a roadmap.","The dismissal rate is the only thing that catches the signal decaying after ship, and the local counts file already exists to hold it.","One population in the corpus already votes 501 to 0 against this feature's legibility as a problem, so a threshold is warranted."],"flip":"If the mock test returns under 4 of 10 first, the product stops at week 3 and neither line is ever reached.","linked":["D18","FL19"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:352","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:411","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:410","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:321","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:206","docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:19","https://static.googleusercontent.com/media/research.google.com/en//pubs/archive/43322.pdf","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/35673040/"]},{"id":"FL20","cat":"Flow & interaction","sub":"Lifecycle","weight":"medium","q":"Does clearing a span require a typed reason, and on which acts?","lede":"Two evidence lines point opposite ways: alert fatigue says one keystroke, and the compliance buyer wants to know why.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":132,"cols":[{"title":"No reason"},{"title":"Reason on every act"},{"title":"Reason on rejects only","tone":"accent"}],"rows":[{"label":"Keystrokes per span","cells":["one","one plus a sentence","one, or a sentence on a revert"]},{"label":"The sidecar records","cells":["who and when","who, when and why","who, when, and why on reverts"]},{"label":"A compliance reader gets","cells":["a list of hashes","a justification per span","the exceptions carry a reason"]},{"label":"What the evidence says","cells":["fatigue evidence favours it","88.3% of typed reasons were meaningless","exception reporting is adjudicated"]},{"label":"Cost","cells":["none","a text field on the common path","a text field on the rare path"]}],"note":"No regulation opened requires a reason, or per-span review at all.","caption":"Where a typed reason is worth its keystroke."},"stakes":"A reason field on the common act is the mechanism that made 88.3% of clinical justifications meaningless.","state":["The sidecar records reviewed-by and reviewed-at and no reason (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:135`).","The drawer offers accept, revert and skip with no text field (`docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:459`).","Nothing in the plan asks a reviewer to say why."],"path":["The store was written for a single-person loop, where a reason has no reader.","The paid tier's buyer is the person answerable for a document, and that buyer reads the sidecar rather than writing it."],"tension":["Of 14,612 overridden clinical alerts, 88.3% of the typed justifications were meaningless.","No regulation opened requires a reason, or per-span review at all; pharma mandates whole-document approval and aviation a per-page revision date.","MHRA permits an audit trail to be reviewed by exception reporting rather than as a full list, which is an argument for reasons on exceptions.","A revert is the only place the product learns what the agent got wrong, and nothing else holds that."],"evidence":[],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"No reason anywhere — one keystroke clears a span","what":"The sidecar records who and when, and nothing about why.","gains":["The fastest possible act, which the fatigue evidence favours","Nothing to build"],"costs":["A revert records no lesson about the agent","A compliance buyer gets a list of hashes"],"system":"No change.","screens":"No change.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"A reason on rejections and overrides, optional on approvals","what":"Accepting stays one keystroke; reverting or overriding a refusal asks for a sentence.","gains":["Keeps the common path at one keystroke","The rare path carries the only information worth storing"],"costs":["Two acts behave differently, which has to be learnt","A revert becomes slower at the moment of annoyance"],"system":"One optional string on the action line.","screens":"The drawer gains an inline field on revert.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"A reason on every act, stored in the sidecar","what":"Nothing clears without a typed justification.","gains":["The strongest record for a buyer answerable for the document","Uniform behaviour"],"costs":["This is the design that produced 88.3% meaningless reasons","It makes every span a form"],"system":"A required string on every line.","screens":"A field on every act, in the panel and the hover card.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"No reason in MVP-0; add the field when a compliance buyer asks","what":"Ship the fast path and wait for the five conversations with people who bill for documents.","gains":["No design work now","The field is shaped by a real requirement"],"costs":["The pilot's reverts carry no reason to learn from","A later field change rewrites every reader"],"system":"No change now, a format change later.","screens":"No change.","money":"None."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["The cheap act stays one keystroke, so the fatigue evidence is respected on the path taken most often.","A revert is the only place the product learns what the agent got wrong, and it is rare enough to carry a sentence.","Exception reporting is already adjudicated by a regulator, so a compliance reading survives without a field on approvals.","Say plainly in the pitch that no regulation opened requires per-span review, because a compliance buyer punishes the missing caveat."],"flip":"If the five people who bill for documents say an approval without a stated basis is worthless to them, (c) is the ask.","linked":["FL18","FL5"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:135","docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:459","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38658357/","https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5aa2b9ede5274a3e391e37f3/MHRA_GxP_data_integrity_guide_March_edited_Final.pdf","https://www.ecfr.gov/api/versioner/v1/full/2026-01-01/title-21.xml?part=11"]},{"id":"D1","cat":"Design, UI & attention","sub":"The tint","weight":"critical","q":"Does the review tint stay a colour-only wash at 1.11:1, or does it get a second, non-colour channel?","lede":"The tint is the only mark this product draws, and as built it is quieter than the divider lines it sits between.","visual":{"kind":"file","name":"auth.md — Live mode, left gutter","lines":[{"t":"  ## Token lifetime","mark":"","note":"reviewed"},{"t":"| Refresh tokens expire after 30 days.","mark":"unreviewed","note":"wash 1.111:1"},{"t":"| Rotation is silent and unlogged.","mark":"unreviewed","note":"same wash"},{"t":"  Sessions end on sign-out.","mark":"","note":"reviewed"}],"note":"The gutter bar is the proposed second channel; the wash inside the text stays as designed.","caption":"Where a non-colour channel would sit, outside the reading line."},"stakes":"If nobody registers the mark, every review number after it measures a screen the reader never saw.","state":["§10 says changed spans carry `a light tint and nothing else` (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:247).","The prototype ships `.m1{background:var(--wash);box-shadow:0 0 0 1px var(--wash) inset}`, so the shadow is the fill's own hex (docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:116).","Measured from the declared hexes, the wash is 1.111:1 on white, under the 1.24:1 hairline beside it (docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:13).","§22 already promises `the tint is never colour alone`, which a wash plus a same-colour shadow does not keep (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:540)."],"path":["§16 read Tang et al. as saying provenance awareness improves validation and raises workload (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:408).","The plan answered the workload half by making the mark as quiet as it could be.","It never asked what quiet costs on the perception side, and no eye-tracking has been run on our screens (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:402)."],"tension":["Quiet enough to ignore at rest and loud enough to be seen are the same dial when colour is the only channel.","The scheduled test asks what the tint means, so someone who never saw it still produces an answer (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:411).","Whether a text wash falls under SC 1.4.11 is contested; a margin mark makes the argument unnecessary."],"evidence":[{"type":"bars","title":"How loud each mark is against its own background","note":"Contrast ratios derived by me from the prototype's declared hexes (docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:13, :14, :16, :22) using the WCAG 2.x relative-luminance formula. The 3:1 line is the floor the plan's own PRD applies to borders that identify a control (docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:3357). Whether a text-background wash falls under that rule is contested — the same PRD row says \"do not raise decorative dividers\" — so read the line as the standard the design is being argued against, not a settled verdict.","data":[["Review tint #eef3ff on white",1.111],["AI proposal tint #f4efff on white",1.127],["Selected span #dfe8ff on white",1.226],["Hairline divider #e4e7ec on white",1.24],["Tab identity colour #cfe0ff on white",1.333],["Review tint #15213d on dark #0f1115",1.185]],"unit":":1 contrast","threshold":3,"thresholdLabel":"WCAG 2.2 SC 1.4.11 floor the PRD applies to an identifying boundary"},{"type":"table","title":"What the plan says about the tint, in three places","cols":["Where","What it says"],"rows":[["§10, docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:247","\"a light tint and nothing else\""],["§16, docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:408","\"ignorable at rest (no border, no icon)\""],["§22, docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:540","\"the tint is never colour alone\""]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Ship the colour-only wash and let the five-second test decide","what":"Nothing changes; the mark stays a background wash with no second channel.","gains":["Cheapest; nothing to build, redraw or re-test","Defensible if a document wash reads as decoration, not as a control boundary"],"costs":["Someone who missed the tint still answers the meaning question","§22's colour-alone promise stays false"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Add one gutter mark at 3:1 and keep the text wash quiet","what":"A left-margin bar marks the span; the wash inside the text is unchanged.","gains":["Keeps §22's promise and ends the SC 1.4.11 argument","Puts the mark in the left column §16 says is scanned first","One CodeMirror gutter decoration"],"costs":["Gutter width is also wanted by line numbers and git marks","A second element to draw in every mode and both themes"],"system":"One gutter decoration in the review-state layer; no sidecar or engine change.","screens":"S2, S4, split and Read gain a gutter column.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Raise the wash itself to 3:1","what":"The tint becomes a visible highlight behind the text.","gains":["One token change and impossible to miss"],"costs":["The document reads as highlighted, the exact failure the test exists to catch","Rejected by §16's own workload argument"],"system":"One token.","screens":"Every screen carrying the tint changes character.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Make the channel a setting: wash, wash plus gutter, or gutter only","what":"The reader picks how the mark is drawn.","gains":["Nobody has to be right first time"],"costs":["Three states to design, test and screenshot","The promise rests on whichever is default, so the default is still this decision"],"system":"A preference, plus the gutter work anyway.","screens":"One more control on S11, which the wireframes want short.","money":"None."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["§22 already commits to never colour alone, and a gutter mark is the cheapest way to keep that promise.","Tang's workload cost is about attention inside the text; a margin mark sits outside it.","The gutter also has room for the count, so this and D4 can share one column."],"flip":"If the rewritten noticing test in D18 finds people spot the wash unprompted at 1.111:1, the gutter mark is decoration.","linked":["D18","D2","D21","D4"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:247","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:402","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:408","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:411","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:540","docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:13","docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:14","docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:116","docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:3357"],"dupes":{"dropped":["FL10"],"why":"Does the 1.11:1 tint get a second, non-colour channel. Same options with the same rec (tint plus one non-colour mark). Design, UI & attention owns the tint."}},{"id":"D2","cat":"Design, UI & attention","sub":"The tint","weight":"critical","q":"Do we keep two washes for proposed and unreviewed, or does the bordered highlight already in the codebase become the proposal mark?","lede":"One tint means the bytes are on your disk, the other means nothing was written, and only hue separates them.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":150,"cols":[{"title":"Review tint #eef3ff","tone":"accent"},{"title":"Proposal tint #f4efff","tone":"neutral"},{"title":"Shipped .cm-ai-suggestion","tone":"warn"}],"rows":[{"label":"Contrast on white","cells":["1.111:1","1.127:1","1.280:1"]},{"label":"Border","cells":["none","none","1px inset, about 1.95:1 on the page"]},{"label":"Corners","cells":["square","square","3px radius"]},{"label":"Means","cells":["written, unreviewed","proposed, not written","proposed, not written"]},{"label":"Bytes on disk","cells":["yes","no","no"]},{"label":"Built today","cells":["no","no","yes, merged"]}],"note":"The two planned washes are 4.10 apart on delta-E76, against a just-noticeable difference near 2.3.","caption":"Three span treatments: two are drawn, one is already shipping."},"stakes":"Confusing the two states means reverting bytes that never changed, or accepting text believing it is already saved.","state":["The wireframes are explicit: purple is proposed, blue is written but unreviewed (docs/_wireframes.md:29).","Both wash hexes are declared on one line and differ by delta-E76 4.10 (docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:14).","`.cm-ai-suggestion` is merged with a blue fill, a 1px inset border, 3px corners and a pulse (src/app/globals.css:833, :835, :836, :844).","The planned tint is unbuilt: no file in `src/` carries review-tint state."],"path":["F2 marks what an agent already wrote; F5 and F8 deliver text that has not been written (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:56, :59).","Both were given a tinted span because tinting is the product's one visual idiom.","`.cm-ai-suggestion` arrived with the sibling app's inline accept and reject, before §16's tint rules were written."],"tension":["The distinction with a data consequence is carried by the weakest channel available.","Working code already gives the proposal a border, which is the non-colour channel the distinction needs.","Keeping it breaks §16's `no border, no icon` rule for one of the two marks (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:408).","The pulse runs with `prefers-reduced-motion` absent from the whole stylesheet (docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:3366)."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"The two tints, measured against each other","items":[["Light mode, review #eef3ff vs proposal #f4efff","ΔE76 = 4.10","derived by me from docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:14; JND is about 2.3"],["Dark mode, #15213d vs #22193a","ΔE76 = 8.85","derived from docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:22"],["Contrast against the page, review vs proposal","1.111 vs 1.127","the two are indistinguishable by luminance; only hue separates them"],["Scheduled tests that show both states","0","the five-second test names one screenshot and one tint (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:352, :411)"]]},{"type":"table","title":"What each state means for the file","cols":["Tint","State","Bytes on disk","What accepting does"],"rows":[["Blue #eef3ff","written, unreviewed","yes","flips a flag, changes zero bytes (docs/_wireframes.md:29)"],["Purple #f4efff","proposed","no","writes new bytes"]]},{"type":"table","title":"The shipped highlight against the planned tint","cols":["Property","Shipped .cm-ai-suggestion","Planned review tint"],"rows":[["Fill","#0055ff at 16% → #d6e4ff on white (1.280:1); #d2e0fb on the app's #fafafa (1.274:1)","#eef3ff → 1.111:1 on white; 1.065:1 on #fafafa"],["Border","inset 1px at 30% over that fill → ≈#93b6fc, 1.53:1 against the fill and 1.95:1 against the page","none — \"no border, no icon\""],["Corners","3px radius","square (border-radius:0 in the prototype, :116)"],["Hue","blue — for a proposal","blue means written-and-unreviewed; purple means proposal"],["Motion","sgnk-ai-pulse keyframes, unguarded","none specified"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"Motion, measured","items":[["@keyframes blocks in globals.css","4","measured"],["animation: declarations","3","measured"],["prefers-reduced-motion guards","0","measured — also flagged at docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:3366"],["Files in src/ carrying review-tint state","0","the planned tint is unbuilt; the competing treatment is merged"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Keep both washes as drawn and delete the shipped highlight","what":"One quiet idiom; the proposal is a purple wash with no border.","gains":["One vocabulary, and §16's rules stay enforceable","Nothing on the page competes with the review tint"],"costs":["The data-consequence distinction rests on a 4.1 delta-E hue difference","F8's inline accept and reject has to be redrawn"],"system":"Delete `.cm-ai-suggestion` and its keyframes; build the proposal decoration.","screens":"S3b and S4 keep their drawn treatment.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Adopt the shipped bordered highlight as the proposal mark, and correct the plan","what":"Proposals are blue with a border, review state is the quiet wash, and the wireframes' purple goes.","gains":["The difference survives greyscale, dark mode and colour-blindness","Reuses code that works, at close to no build cost"],"costs":["The `no border` rule then applies to one mark only and must be written down","Two blue marks of different loudness in one editor"],"system":"Keep the class, wrap the pulse in `prefers-reduced-motion`, rewrite the wireframe note.","screens":"S3b and S4 redraw the proposal span.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Keep both washes and add a dashed left rule to the proposal","what":"The purple stays and gains a non-colour mark of its own design.","gains":["Keeps the drawn palette and makes the distinction non-hue"],"costs":["Builds a second treatment when one is already merged","Adds an element to the surface §16 tried to keep clear"],"system":"One more decoration, plus deleting `.cm-ai-suggestion`.","screens":"S3b, S4.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Take the proposal out of the document; it lives in the review panel","what":"Nothing unwritten is ever tinted in the text.","gains":["Removes the confusion by removing the second state from the page","One tint to test and one meaning to teach"],"costs":["Forfeits proposal-arrives-in-place, which F5 and F8 were designed around","S3b answer-in-place is redrawn from scratch"],"system":"Proposals render in the panel only.","screens":"S3b changes shape; S4 grows.","money":"None."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["A border is the second channel the distinction needs, and it is already merged and working.","Correcting a wireframe note costs less than rebuilding the same idea in a different colour.","The motion guard is due either way, since `prefers-reduced-motion` appears zero times in the stylesheet."],"flip":"If the inline accept and reject flow is being replaced by the review panel, delete the class and take option a.","linked":["D1","D18","D21","D9"],"sources":["docs/_wireframes.md:29","docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:14","docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:22","docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:116","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:56","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:59","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:352","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:408","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:411","src/app/globals.css:833","src/app/globals.css:835","src/app/globals.css:836","src/app/globals.css:844","docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:3366","merged: D17"]},{"id":"D8","cat":"Design, UI & attention","sub":"Editor scope","weight":"critical","q":"Do we ship four editor modes for MVP-0, or cut to three?","lede":"Four modes is the largest surface that exists only because editors ship the editor first, at 1.21 engineering days a week.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":170,"cols":[{"title":"Ship four","tone":"neutral"},{"title":"Three, cut Split","tone":"accent"},{"title":"Two, Live and Read","tone":"neutral"}],"rows":[{"label":"Modes that render the tint","cells":["3 of 4 — Edit does not","2 of 3 — Edit does not","2 of 2"]},{"label":"Raw source available","cells":["yes","yes","no"]},{"label":"Dedicated screens to keep","cells":["S2 and the split screen (:530)","S2","S2"]},{"label":"Stated purpose that is not review","cells":["2 of 4 — Edit and Split","1 of 3 — Edit","0"]},{"label":"What the developer buyer misses","cells":["nothing","a side-by-side render","the source view; reads as a toy"]}],"note":"Purposes quoted from docs/_wireframes.md:17; F1 costs the modes as inherited, not as new build.","caption":"What each cut keeps, and what it costs the buyer."},"stakes":"Table-stakes surface is the cost the audits called larger than the novel-feature gap, and it is being paid before the novel feature exists.","state":["F1 ships Live, Edit, Split and Read, costed as `Exists. NF-1/NF-3 fixes (7d), engine wiring (8d)` (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:55); §21 repeats the four (:524).","The prototype ships a four-button control on S2 (docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:361) and a dedicated split screen (:530).","Edit does not render the tint at all, by the wireframes' own rule (docs/_wireframes.md:17).","About 70 engineering days at a measured 1.21 a week is 58 calendar weeks (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:227)."],"path":["The earlier master plan specified three states; the screens report reconciled to four on the founder mockup as a superset (docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-28/c6-screens.md:21).","That was a superset argument, not a cost argument.","The ten-week schedule that made the cost look small was withdrawn as arithmetically impossible (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:229)."],"tension":["The gap register records the audits calling the standalone editor's table-stakes cost larger than the novel-feature gap (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:48).","Two of the four modes have a stated purpose that is not review (docs/_wireframes.md:17).","F1 costs the modes as inherited, but 25 files across `src/` have already diverged from the sibling (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:223).","Four platforms now ship an agent-diff pane free, so mode count is not what a buyer is choosing between."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"The schedule the mode count is spent against","items":[["Engineering days for MVP-0","about 70","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:227"],["Measured engineering days per calendar week, 2026-07-13 to 2026-09-08","1.21","10 of 58 calendar days touched src/, src-tauri/ or test/ — docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:227"],["Sibling repo's best-ever rate","1.91/week","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:227"],["Last 30 days on this repo","0.23/week","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:227"],["Calendar weeks implied at 1.21","58","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:227"],["What F1's own estimate covers","\"Exists. NF-1/NF-3 fixes (7d), engine wiring (8d)\"","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:55 — the modes are costed as inherited, not as new build"]]},{"type":"table","title":"What each mode is for, and whether the tint shows there","cols":["Mode","Stated purpose (docs/_wireframes.md:17)","Tint renders?"],"rows":[["Live (default)","\"the default and the one that matters\"","yes"],["Edit","\"when the markdown itself is the thing you are working on\"","no"],["Split","\"for learning the syntax or checking a render\"","yes, in the rendered pane"],["Read","\"for review and printing\"","yes"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Ship all four","what":"Full table stakes on day one.","gains":["Nothing a developer expects is missing","The widest surface to keep working as the engine lands"],"costs":["Four modes across two themes is the test matrix on a 58-week schedule","Two of them are not where the tint does its work"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Ship two for MVP-0 — Live and Read — and add Edit and Split in MVP-1","what":"Only the modes that render the tint ship first.","gains":["Both remaining modes carry the product's one claim end to end","Smallest surface to build and test"],"costs":["A markdown editor with no raw-source mode reads as incomplete to the developer buyer"],"system":"Two modes wired.","screens":"The mode control loses two buttons; the split screen goes.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Ship three — Live, Edit, Read — and cut Split","what":"Raw source stays; the side-by-side render goes.","gains":["Keeps what the developer buyer looks for first","Cuts the mode with the weakest stated job and its own screen","Roughly the original three-state design"],"costs":["The saving is small if the modes really are inherited untouched","Split is the one place the same bytes are shown twice"],"system":"One mode and one screen removed.","screens":"The split screen goes.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Ship all four and budget zero days, as F1 already implies","what":"Modes are treated as fixed inherited code.","gains":["Consistent with F1's own Needs column","Makes the assumption explicit instead of leaving it inferred"],"costs":["Assumes the tint and the splice engine land under them for free","25 diverged files say the fork is not free"],"system":"No change; the estimate is restated.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"c","recCase":["Edit is the mode a developer looks for first, and its absence reads as a toy; Split has the weakest stated job and costs a whole screen.","Cutting one mode is a small saving, and it is the cheapest place to start applying the schedule finding rather than only reporting it.","The buyer's own editor now ships an agent-diff pane free, so the argument for breadth here is weaker than it was a month ago."],"flip":"If the fork audit shows all four modes work untouched by the tint work, d is the honest answer and the estimate should say zero out loud.","linked":["D11","D20","D9","FF2"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:55","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:223","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:227","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:229","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:524","docs/_wireframes.md:17","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-28/c6-screens.md:21","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:48","docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:361","docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:530"]},{"id":"D3","cat":"Design, UI & attention","sub":"The tint","weight":"high","q":"Should the tint be switchable at all, and is it on by default?","lede":"The settings page ships a toggle that turns off the one thing this product adds to a markdown editor.","visual":{"kind":"screen","title":"S11 Settings, as built","panes":[{"label":"Five toggles on one page","w":1,"rows":[{"label":"Hide all AI features","meta":"evidence-backed","mark":"keep","tone":"good"},{"label":"Mark machine-written text until a person reviews it","meta":"default on","mark":"removes the product","tone":"stop"},{"label":"Show the unreviewed bar in the file tree","meta":"default on","mark":"chrome","tone":"warn"},{"label":"Theme, keymap and the rest","meta":"appearance","mark":"","tone":"neutral"}]}],"note":"The settings copy already says the tint is file state, not AI.","caption":"Which switches remove chrome, and which remove the product."},"stakes":"A pilot participant who switches the tint off is counted as a user of a product they are not using.","state":["S11 ships `Mark machine-written text until a person reviews it` and a tree-bar toggle, both on (docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:615, :616).","The hide-all-AI switch already draws the line: the review tint stays, because it is file state (docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:608).","The MVP-0 exit measure counts days opened, spans reviewed and proposals accepted (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:431)."],"path":["The hide-all switch is evidence-backed: Zed, VS Code and Telegram shipped theirs after 412-, 30- and 181-reaction issues (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:298).","The tint toggle followed from the settings page's habit of making every visual behaviour optional."],"tension":["The wireframes state the rule being broken: every toggle we add is a decision we failed to make (docs/_wireframes.md:47).","With the tint off, 41 of 43 editor files are byte-identical to the sibling app, so nothing distinct is left (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:223).","Removing a control that already works is the kind of change those three reaction counts were about."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"Settings toggles on S11, counted","items":[["Toggles on the settings page","5","counted in docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html at :608, :612, :615, :616, :619"],["Of those, toggles that disable the product's core signal","2",":615 \"Mark machine-written text…\" and :616 \"Show the unreviewed bar in the file tree\""],["The stated constraint","\"Every toggle we add is a decision we failed to make\"","docs/_wireframes.md:47"],["Editor files byte-identical to the sibling app","41 of 43","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:223 — what is left when the tint is off"],["What the MVP-0 exit test counts","\"days-opened, spans reviewed, proposals accepted\"","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:431 — all three read zero for a user who switched the tint off"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Keep both toggles, default on","what":"Nothing changes; the reader can switch off the tint and the tree bar.","gains":["Maximum control, and nobody can call the mark forced"],"costs":["The exit measure reads zero for a user who switched it off","Two more states in every test and screenshot"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Remove the tint toggle; keep the tree-bar toggle","what":"The tint is not optional; the tree bar stays chrome that can be hidden.","gains":["Two fewer states to design, test and support","The pilot measures one product"],"costs":["A vocal user can reasonably object to a removed control","Someone who wants a clean document has only the file itself"],"system":"Delete one preference.","screens":"S11 loses a row.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Make the tint per-document, stored in frontmatter","what":"A finished document can be marked as no longer needing marks.","gains":["Matches the projection law: the setting lives in the file","A shipped document reads clean without a global switch"],"costs":["A new frontmatter key to read, write and refuse on","SAFE_KEY governs what can be addressed there (splice-frontmatter.ts:53)"],"system":"One key in the reader and writer, plus a refusal path.","screens":"The properties panel gains a row.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Replace both with one quiet mode","what":"A single switch dims every review signal at once.","gains":["One decision instead of two, and an answer to reviewer fatigue"],"costs":["Still ships an off switch for the product","A dimmed state has to be designed and measured too"],"system":"One preference applied across surfaces.","screens":"S11 loses a row; every surface gains a dimmed state.","money":"None."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["The hide-all switch already says the right thing out loud: AI is optional, file state is not.","A second switch that contradicts it hands the pilot a way to be a non-user without leaving.","The tree bar is chrome and can stay optional at no cost to the exit measure."],"flip":"If a pilot participant asks for it unprompted the need is real, and option c is the right shape for it.","linked":["D1","D4"],"sources":["docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:608","docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:615","docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:616","docs/_wireframes.md:47","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:223","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:298","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:385","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:431","src/modules/share/domain/splice-frontmatter.ts:53"]},{"id":"D4","cat":"Design, UI & attention","sub":"Attention","weight":"high","q":"How many surfaces carry the unreviewed count, and where does the total sit?","lede":"S2 states one fact in five places, and the total sits in the two regions §16 itself predicts are read last.","visual":{"kind":"screen","title":"S2 — every surface stating the same fact","panes":[{"label":"Top bar and left rail, read first","w":1,"rows":[{"label":"Dot on the active tab","meta":"6px, title=unreviewed","mark":"cut","tone":"warn"},{"label":"Per-file bars in the tree","meta":"§17's return trigger","mark":"keep","tone":"good"},{"label":"No total anywhere in this zone","meta":"","mark":"gap","tone":"stop"}]},{"label":"Document, read second","w":1,"rows":[{"label":"The tint","meta":"1.111:1 on white","mark":"keep","tone":"accent"}]},{"label":"Right rail and status bar, read last","w":1,"rows":[{"label":"Drawer counter, 3 unreviewed","meta":"S4 :458","mark":"move","tone":"warn"},{"label":"Status bar, 3 unreviewed spans · 64%","meta":":394","mark":"move","tone":"warn"},{"label":"Per-heading counts in the outline","meta":":398","mark":"cut","tone":"warn"}]}],"note":"Amber does three jobs: a lot unreviewed, an open question, a STALE verdict.","caption":"Five surfaces for one fact, with the total in the last-read column."},"stakes":"Repeating the count on every surface teaches the reader to stop seeing all of them, and the tint is on the same list.","state":["S2 carries the count five times: tab dot (docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:329), tree bars (:346, :351), outline counts (:398), status bar (:394), and the tint.","Both totals sit in the last-read zone: the status bar (:394) and the S4 drawer (:458). §16 never mentions a status bar (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:413).","The tree bar turns amber at no stated threshold, and the same file at 88% is amber on S2 (:351) and plain on S0 (:305).","Amber also marks an open question (:495) and a STALE verdict (:716)."],"path":["Each surface had a local reason: the tree bar is §17's return trigger (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:425); the status bar came with the sibling editor.","§16 puts the counter top-left of the panel, then predicts the right rail is read last, and the built screen satisfies both (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:409, :413).","Nobody counted the surfaces together."],"tension":["§16 justifies the tint by requiring it to be ignorable at rest; five simultaneous indicators of one fact is the opposite (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:408).","Clinical alerting is the mature form of a repeated count: 55–98% override across 34 studies, and 86.6% of 14,612 alerts overridden.","The one alerting system that earned 57.5% acceptance fired 31 rules in 0.19% of 500,274 sessions. Scarcity, not coverage.","Claude Code v2.1.260 opens its own diff panel beside the conversation, so a second count competes with a surface already free."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"§16's predicted reading order against where the counter actually is","cols":["Region","§16's predicted order","Carries the counter?"],"rows":[["Top bar (tabs)","first","no — only a 6px dot on the active tab, `title=\"unreviewed\"` (:329)"],["Left rail (tree)","first","no — per-file percentage bars, no total (:346–:353)"],["Document body","second","the tint itself"],["Right rail","last","yes — the S4 drawer counter (:458)"],["Bottom status bar","not mentioned in §16","yes — \"3 unreviewed spans · 64%\" (:394)"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"How well sourced the placement rule is","items":[["Evidence rows in §16's exhibit 23","3 plus one scheduled test","Tang et al. (:408), NN/g F-pattern (:409), Obsidian forum (:410); the five-second test (:411) is untested"],["Of those, rows that bear on where things go","2","Tang and NN/g; the Obsidian row is about demand, not placement"],["Of those two, carrying a URL or a fetch date","1","the Tang arXiv id at :408; the NN/g F-pattern row at :409 carries neither, while other NN/g citations in the corpus do (e.g. docs/REFERENCES.md:274, with URL and [fetched])"],["Eye-tracking runs on our own screens","0","§16 opening line, docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:402"],["Gap register's grade for §16","Medium","\"Two sources, one of them a lab study on code, not prose. No measurement on our screens\" — docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:26"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"Surfaces carrying unreviewed state, counted on the prototype","items":[["On S2","5","tab dot :329, tree bars :346–:353, outline counts :398, status-bar total :394, the tint"],["On S4","5","tab dot :415, tree bars :426–:431, status-bar total :455, drawer counter :458, the tint — the outline is replaced by the drawer"],["On S0 launcher","3","per-card bar :304–:311, per-card \"NN% unreviewed\" label, footer \"7 unreviewed\" :315"],["Amber threshold, stated in the plan","none","and it is applied inconsistently: 88% is amber on S2 (:351) and not amber on S0 (:305), for the same file"],["Distinct meanings carried by `--warn` amber","3","a lot unreviewed (:351), open questions (:495, :514), STALE verdict (:716)"]]},{"type":"table","title":"The colours doing semantic work across the prototype","cols":["Colour","Meaning","Where"],"rows":[["Accent blue #1a5cff","unreviewed share, and every primary control, and every link","tree bars (:87), buttons, links (:37)"],["Wash blue #eef3ff","this span is unreviewed","the tint (:116)"],["Tab blue #cfe0ff","nothing — decorative tab identity, one of four","`--t-blue` (:16), tab underline"],["Amber #b7791f","a lot unreviewed, and open questions, and STALE","tree bar over threshold (:88, :351); S3b questions (:495, :514); S13 verdict (:716)"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Leave all five surfaces and both totals where they are","what":"Nothing changes; the count stays repeated and the totals stay in the last-read zone.","gains":["No work, and no screenshot has to be redrawn"],"costs":["The retention story rests on a number in the coldest region of the screen","Amber keeps three meanings and a threshold that fires two ways"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Cut to three: the tint, the tree bars, and one total above the tree","what":"The outline count and the tab dot go; the total moves to the head of the left rail.","gains":["The total sits above the bars it summarises, in the early-read zone","Two surfaces with no stated job disappear","One bar colour, so amber is freed for one meaning"],"costs":["A reviewer inside a long document loses the per-heading count","The number disappears when the tree is collapsed"],"system":"No engine or sidecar change; a rail header and two deletions.","screens":"S2 and S4 lose the outline count and the tab dot; the left rail gains a header.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Cut to two: the tint and one total, tree bars included in the cut","what":"Only the document and one number carry review state.","gains":["The quietest possible surface, and the smallest thing to test"],"costs":["Removes §17's return trigger, which is the bar visible before a file is opened","Nothing tells you which file to open"],"system":"Deletions only.","screens":"S0 and the tree lose their bars.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Keep five, but give amber one meaning and a stated threshold","what":"The surfaces stay; the colour rules are written down and applied consistently.","gains":["Fixes the provable inconsistency without cutting anything"],"costs":["Five surfaces for one fact remain","Still forces a choice about which of amber's three jobs survives"],"system":"A token rule and one threshold constant.","screens":"Every screen carrying amber is re-checked.","money":"None."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["The tree bar earns its place because §17 makes it the reason the app is opened; the outline count and the tab dot appear in no exhibit.","Moving the total above the bars makes it a summary, not a fifth surface, and puts it where both halves of §16 agree scanning starts.","One bar colour removes a threshold applied two ways for the same file and frees amber for one job."],"flip":"If the rewritten test in D18 finds people read the status bar first in a document tool, the total stays there and the rule is written down.","linked":["D1","D18","D23","D3","FL19"],"sources":["docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:26","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:408","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:409","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:413","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:425","docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:305","docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:329","docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:346","docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:351","docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:394","docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:398","docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:455","docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:458","docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:495","docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:716","docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:88","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34450669/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/35673040/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38658357/","https://raw.githubusercontent.com/anthropics/claude-code/main/CHANGELOG.md","merged: D5"]},{"id":"D23","cat":"Design, UI & attention","sub":"Attention","weight":"high","q":"Does any surface ever state a share of a repository as unreviewed?","lede":"The percentage badge is the element with the least evidence behind it and the most published evidence against it.","visual":{"kind":"funnel","steps":[{"label":"Alerts shown to clinicians","n":14612,"unit":"alerts","tone":"neutral"},{"label":"Overridden","n":12659,"unit":"alerts","tone":"stop"}],"note":"86.6% overridden; 88.3% of the typed justifications carried no meaning.","caption":"The mature version of an always-on badge, measured."},"stakes":"A number nobody can act on in one sitting trains dismissal, and the tint rides on the same habit.","state":["S0 states a share three times: a bar per card, a percentage label per card, and `7 unreviewed` in the footer (docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:304, :305, :315).","S2 and S4 add one to the status bar: `3 unreviewed spans · 64%` and `· 88%` (:394, :455).","§17 makes that count the daily return trigger (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:425); S11 lets you switch the tree bar off (:616).","No source in the plan produces a repository-level share. The 18% figure circulating today has no method behind it and is unverified."],"path":["The bar came from the retention argument: the user's own agent creates the count, so opening the app is how it clears.","The launcher repeated it per card so folders could be sorted unreviewed-first (docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:304).","Nobody asked what the number is for once it is larger than one sitting."],"tension":["Almanac shipped read receipts on $45M and switched off on 2025-01-31, so the general-document form of this surface has a corpse behind it.","This repo alone holds 4,446,724 markdown words. At 240 wpm any double-digit share is weeks of reading, which is a debt, not a task.","Google measured a 3.2 hour weekly review budget against a 24-line median change: the unit people act on is small and specific.","A share is the one number that cannot be finished, and §17 asks the reader to return to it daily."],"evidence":[],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Keep every share and count as built","what":"Launcher cards, tree bars and both status bars keep their percentages.","gains":["Demonstrates well: the launcher reads as a queue at a glance"],"costs":["A repository share is unactionable, and unactionable warnings are overridden","Sets the pilot's first impression on the least-evidenced element"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Counts only; no percentage anywhere","what":"Every surface states a number of spans and never a share.","gains":["A count of spans is a thing that can reach zero","Removes the figure with no method behind it"],"costs":["A count without a denominator is hard to compare across files","Loses the sorted-by-worst launcher order"],"system":"Drop the share from the projection.","screens":"S0 cards, S2 and S4 status bars.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"A share inside an open file only; the tree keeps a bar with no number","what":"Folders and repositories state nothing numeric; the open file may.","gains":["The file is the unit a person can finish in a sitting","Keeps the return trigger without publishing a debt figure","Nothing on screen makes a claim the corpus cannot support"],"costs":["The launcher loses its at-a-glance ranking","Two rules to explain: why a file has a number and a folder does not"],"system":"The share is computed per open file only.","screens":"S0 cards lose their labels; the tree bar keeps its fill.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Nothing outside an open review session, tree bars included","what":"Review state is invisible until you ask for it.","gains":["The strongest answer to the override evidence: no standing badge at all"],"costs":["Deletes §17's only mechanical reason to return","Nothing tells a returning user that an agent has written since"],"system":"Review state renders only in a session.","screens":"S0 and the tree lose every mark.","money":"None."}],"rec":"c","recCase":["A file is finishable in a sitting; a repository is not, and the override literature is about warnings nobody can clear.","The tree bar survives as a fill without a number, so §17's return trigger is kept and the unsupported figure is not published.","It costs nothing today, because no percentage is computed anywhere in `src/` yet."],"flip":"If a pilot participant reads a folder share and then opens that folder because of it, the figure is a task and a stays.","linked":["D3","D4"],"sources":["docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:304","docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:305","docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:315","docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:394","docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:455","docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:616","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:425","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38658357/","https://get.almanac.io/go-forward","https://sback.it/publications/icse2018seip.pdf","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34516216/"]},{"id":"D6","cat":"Design, UI & attention","sub":"Hover card","weight":"high","q":"Do we ship the attribution hover card in MVP-0, when neither MVP-0 source can fill it on the tree the product is defined by?","lede":"Attribution is now the one claim of ours nobody has shipped, and both readers that land in MVP-0 need a commit that has not happened.","visual":{"kind":"screen","title":"Hover card on an uncommitted working tree","panes":[{"label":"Four rows, as drawn (:383–:386)","w":1,"rows":[{"label":"Changed — since you last reviewed, 2h ago","meta":"sidecar hash","mark":"fills","tone":"good"},{"label":"Bytes — the span's range","meta":"splice engine","mark":"fills","tone":"good"},{"label":"Author — claude-sonnet-5, trailer a3f9c2","meta":"needs a commit","mark":"empty","tone":"stop"},{"label":"Prompt — not recorded","meta":"needs MCP, MVP-1","mark":"empty","tone":"stop"}]}],"note":"The prototype mocks the card on a committed span, so the empty case never appears.","caption":"Which rows can be filled in the window the tint marks."},"stakes":"The only claim nobody else occupies gets its first demonstration as two rows reading `not recorded`.","state":["F3 ships trailer and note readers in MVP-0 and MCP in MVP-1; the card has four rows (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:57; docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:383, :385, :386).","§1 defines the container as a working tree with no pull request, where no trailer and no note exist yet (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:20).","MCP is the only source carrying a prompt, and its own row records the assumption as untested (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:65).","The readers cost 3 days against a measured 1.21 engineering days a week (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:57, :227)."],"path":["F3 was kept because Google sells span-level authorship at Workspace Business Standard and above (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:57).","The earlier demotion of authorship marking rested on iA Writer's consumer failure, and that reasoning is now weaker than it was.","Trailers and notes were scoped first because they are cheap to parse."],"tension":["Today's research puts attribution as the only one of our four claims no platform has shipped, so the demotion should be reopened.","Zed Delta went into private beta on 2026-08-12 and commits publicly to attribution down to the span.","The one shipped implementation found is a VS Code extension with 88 installs, which is either the opening or the size of it.","Three days of readers that return nothing on our own defined container is the wrong three days either way."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"What each hover-card row can be filled from, and when","cols":["Row","Source","Available on an uncommitted working tree?","Ships"],"rows":[["Changed","sidecar hash comparison","yes","MVP-0"],["Bytes","splice engine","yes","MVP-0"],["Author (carries the model name too)","commit trailer or git-ai note; MCP","no — needs a commit","MVP-0 readers / MVP-1 MCP"],["Prompt","MCP write only","no","MVP-1, and marked untested (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:65)"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"The gap between the card and the container","items":[["The product's stated container","\"a working tree that has no pull request\"","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:20"],["MVP-0 attribution readers","commit trailer, git-ai note","both post-commit only, docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:57"],["Estimated cost of those readers","3 engineering days","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:57"],["Measured engineering days available per calendar week","1.21","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:227"],["Sidecar filename in the plan vs the prototype","review.jsonl vs provenance.jsonl","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:56 against docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:617 — two names for one file, unreconciled"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Ship the card as designed, blank rows and all","what":"Four rows, two of which read `not recorded` on an uncommitted tree.","gains":["Honest, and it says why the row is empty"],"costs":["Advertises an absence on the claim we most need to land","Three days for rows that fill only after a commit"],"system":"Trailer and note readers as planned.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Two rows now; add author and prompt only when a source exists","what":"The card shows when it changed and which bytes, and grows when a write carries more.","gains":["The card is always full and never advertises an absence","Saves most of the three days for the engine work"],"costs":["Gives up the Google-precedent story until MVP-1","A two-row card invites the question of why it is a card"],"system":"Card renders from the sidecar only.","screens":"The hover card loses two rows.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Bind the author row to the file's last commit and label it as file-level","what":"Something shows on a committed repo, without claiming span precision.","gains":["Fills the row on any repo with history"],"costs":["Invites reading a file-level fact as a span-level one, the confusion F3 exists to remove"],"system":"Git log per file instead of per span.","screens":"The row changes label.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Cut the post-commit readers and pull the MCP write path into MVP-0","what":"Attribution means something the first time it appears, because the write carried it.","gains":["The only path that fills author and prompt inside the window the tint marks","Puts the unoccupied claim on a real source"],"costs":["6 days, desktop only, and the plan records the routing assumption as untested","Nothing to show in the web app, which is the trial"],"system":"MCP server moves into MVP-0; trailer readers drop out.","screens":"The card is unchanged but full.","money":"None."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["The two rows that always work are the two that prove the engine, and they are the rows the fifteen-second demo needs.","Adding rows only when they have content means the card never advertises an absence in front of a stranger.","Settle the sidecar's name in the same pass: the plan says review.jsonl and the prototype says provenance.jsonl (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:56; docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:617)."],"flip":"If the meeting confirms attribution as the surviving claim, the card is not the question — the source is, and d is the only option that supplies one.","linked":["D1","F3"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:20","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:227","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:247","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:56","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:57","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:65","docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:385","docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:617","https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=dfarkash.claude-edits-scm","https://zed.dev/blog/agentic-xanadu"]},{"id":"D7","cat":"Design, UI & attention","sub":"AI placement","weight":"high","q":"Does the AI prompt summon at the cursor, or stay as the docked strip under the document?","lede":"Our own screen report says every shipped product puts the prompt at the cursor; the prototype ships a docked strip and a second button.","visual":{"kind":"screen","title":"S2 — where the AI prompt can be asked for","panes":[{"label":"Under the document","w":1,"rows":[{"label":"AI · this file · collapsed · ⌘J opens","meta":":391","mark":"prompt","tone":"warn"},{"label":"Carries the your-key reassurance copy","meta":"nothing runs until you ask","mark":"","tone":"neutral"}]},{"label":"Right rail, bottom","w":1,"rows":[{"label":"AI edit · ⌘J","meta":":405","mark":"prompt","tone":"warn"},{"label":"No review tab for pending AI hunks","meta":"what the report asked for","mark":"missing","tone":"stop"}]},{"label":"At the cursor","w":1,"rows":[{"label":"Nothing","meta":"where every named incumbent puts it","mark":"","tone":"stop"}]}],"note":"Both existing affordances are bound to the same shortcut.","caption":"Two entry points to one feature, and neither is at the cursor."},"stakes":"Two AI affordances on a screen whose stated design goal is that AI does not compete for attention.","state":["S2 ships a collapsed strip under the document (docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:391) and an `AI edit · ⌘J` button in the rail (:405).","The wireframes defend the strip: a sidebar makes AI a place you go, under the document it is a thing you do (docs/_wireframes.md:11).","The screens report asked for the opposite — prompt at the selection, rail keeps a review tab (docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-28/c6-screens.md:22).","§15's evidence row describes the incumbent norm as one collapsed affordance present on load (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:381)."],"path":["The docked strip came from the founder mockup.","The report's reconciliation was recorded and never applied; what shipped in the rail is a prompt button, not the review tab it asked for.","So the plan disagrees with its own report and no argument is on the record."],"tension":["This is the one screen-placement question in the plan where a report gave a clear answer with named comparables.","The strip is also where the `your key · nothing runs until you ask` copy lives, so deleting it moves the trust line.","Discoverability is the real argument for the strip: without it a first-run user must know ⌘J or select text.","If the form factor goes to a VS Code extension, the host decides this and the question dissolves (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:48)."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"Three positions on where the AI prompt goes, all in the corpus","cols":["Source","Position","Reason given"],"rows":[["c6-screens.md:22, 2026-08-28","prompt at the cursor; rail keeps a review tab","every shipped convention; a docked prompt \"reads as bolted-on\""],["_wireframes.md:11","docked strip under the document","\"a thing you do to what you are looking at\""],["prototype S2 (:391, :405)","both — docked strip and a rail prompt button, both ⌘J","not stated"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"What the incumbent evidence actually establishes","items":[["Incumbents opening an AI panel expanded on load","0 of 5 named","Google Docs, Notion, Cursor, Zed, Obsidian Copilot — docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:381"],["Google Docs' stated behaviour","\"By default, the Gemini bar automatically minimizes to clear your screen.\"","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:381"],["AI affordances on our S2 today","2","the strip (:391) and the rail button (:405), both bound to ⌘J"],["Reaction counts behind the hide-all-AI switch","412 (Zed), 30 (VS Code), 181 (Telegram)","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:298, :382"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"At the cursor only; the rail button becomes the review surface for pending hunks","what":"The docked strip goes; the prompt appears at the selection.","gains":["Matches every product the buyer already uses","Frees the space under the document and leaves one entry point","Turns the rail element into the review surface the report asked for"],"costs":["A first-run user has to discover ⌘J or a selection","The trust copy needs a new home"],"system":"One deletion and one relocation.","screens":"S2 loses the strip; the rail gains a hunk list.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Docked strip only; delete the rail button","what":"One affordance, in the founder's position.","gains":["Keeps the discoverability the strip was built for","One entry point, one shortcut"],"costs":["Ships against the only screen-level convention evidence we have"],"system":"One deletion.","screens":"The rail loses a button.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Keep both","what":"Nothing changes.","gains":["No work"],"costs":["Two doors to one feature on the screen we most want quiet","No decision is recorded, so it recurs"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"At the cursor, with the strip shown on first run and dismissed after first use","what":"The strip becomes onboarding rather than furniture.","gains":["Discoverability without a permanent surface"],"costs":["One more state to build, explain and screenshot","A dismissed-forever element is hard to find again"],"system":"A first-run flag.","screens":"S2 gains a first-run variant.","money":"None."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["The researched answer costs one deletion and one relocation, and the prototype went the other way with no reason recorded.","It also gives the rail the job the report wanted it to have, which is review rather than a second prompt.","One entry point is what §15's own evidence row describes as the incumbent norm."],"flip":"If the ten-developer walkthrough shows people never find ⌘J, discoverability is the real problem and d is the fix, not the strip.","linked":["D20","D3"],"sources":["docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-28/c6-screens.md:22","docs/_wireframes.md:11","docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:391","docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:405","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:381","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:298","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:48"]},{"id":"D11","cat":"Design, UI & attention","sub":"Design system","weight":"high","q":"Do we reconcile the shipped stylesheet to the canonical system before the pilot, or ship the sibling project's?","lede":"The application's stylesheet is a copy of another product's and says so in its own header comment.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":150,"cols":[{"title":"Canonical system","tone":"accent"},{"title":"Prototype the pilot sees","tone":"neutral"},{"title":"Shipped app","tone":"stop"}],"rows":[{"label":"Accent","cells":["#1a5cff","#1a5cff","#18181b (globals.css:34)"]},{"label":"Corners","cells":["square","square, border-radius:0","6 / 8 / 12px (:56)"]},{"label":"Icons","cells":["inline SVG","inline SVG, 110 uses","Material Symbols web font (:2)"]},{"label":"Self-description","cells":["frontmatter","frontmatter","\"sgnk-md design system\" (:12)"]},{"label":"On the record as a defect","cells":["—","—","three times since 2026-08-29, fixed zero"]}],"note":"The tint's meaning is carried by the accent, so the two palettes disagree about the product's one signal.","caption":"Three visual systems; the pilot sees one and installs another."},"stakes":"Every visual reaction the pilot gives is about a palette we do not intend to ship.","state":["`src/app/globals.css:12` reads `sgnk-md design system — Linear-style modern SaaS`; it ships `--accent: #18181b` (:34) and rounded corners (:56).","The prototype uses the canonical `--accent:#1a5cff` and `border-radius:0` on the tint (docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:14, :116).","PRD v1 recorded the divergence, PRD v2 repeated it, PRODUCT.md called it free to fix (docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-2026-08-29.md:815, :817; docs/PRODUCT.md:997).","The current plan does not mention globals.css, the design system, icons or corners at all."],"path":["The editor was cloned from the sibling app and the stylesheet came with it (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:223).","The defect was recorded three times in two PRDs and fixed zero times.","It then dropped out of the plan entirely in the move to v15."],"tension":["The five-second test would be run on a palette the product does not ship, which makes its result unattributable.","The two stylesheets disagree on the colour that carries the tint's meaning, not only on taste.","PRODUCT.md's own verdict is that this is free to fix and embarrassing to charge money in front of (docs/PRODUCT.md:997).","If the form factor goes to a VS Code extension, the host supplies the theme and most of this file stops mattering (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:48)."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"Three descriptions of the same product's visual system","cols":["Where","Accent","Corners","Status"],"rows":[["Canonical system (quoted at docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-2026-08-29.md:819)","#1a5cff","square, three rounding exceptions","the intended system"],["Clickable prototype (docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:14, :116)","#1a5cff","square (`border-radius:0` on the tint)","what the pilot is shown"],["Shipped app (src/app/globals.css:12, :34, :56)","#18181b","6 / 8 / 12px","what the pilot would install"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"How long the divergence has been on the record","items":[["First recorded","PRD v1 §16.3, 2026-08-29","docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-2026-08-29.md:815, :817"],["Recorded again","PRD v2 §7.4 and PRODUCT.md","docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:430, docs/PRODUCT.md:997"],["PRODUCT.md's own verdict","\"Free to fix, embarrassing to charge money in front of\"","docs/PRODUCT.md:997"],["Mentions in the current plan (v15)","0","no occurrence of globals.css, design system, icons or corners in docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md"],["Fork state the plan does report","181 of 226 src/ files identical, 25 already diverged; 41 of 43 editor files identical","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:223 — note the plan's own two figures leave 20 files unaccounted for"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Reconcile the tokens before the pilot: accent, corners, failing contrast","what":"One stylesheet pass, so the pilot sees and installs the same product.","gains":["A single-file edit that PRODUCT.md already calls free to fix","The five-second test then runs on the real palette","Can be done in the same pass as D12's contrast work"],"costs":["Any component that assumed the near-black accent needs a look","One review pass to check the chrome still reads"],"system":"Token edits in one file.","screens":"Every screen changes colour and corner radius.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Ship the sibling's stylesheet and reconcile after the pilot","what":"Nothing changes now.","gains":["Zero work before the pilot"],"costs":["Any visual feedback from the pilot has to be discarded","The header comment naming another product ships"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Adopt the sibling's stylesheet as canonical and retire the other one","what":"One system, honestly chosen; the prototype is redrawn instead of the app.","gains":["Ends the divergence in the direction with the least code to change"],"costs":["Gives up the blue that carries the tint's meaning on every surface","The prototype and every screenshot are redrawn"],"system":"No code change; the design system document is rewritten.","screens":"The prototype is redrawn.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Reconcile only the tokens the tint depends on","what":"Accent and wash move; corners and the rest stay.","gains":["Smallest change that makes the tested and shipped screens agree on the one signal"],"costs":["The app still looks like the sibling everywhere else","A second pass is still owed"],"system":"Two token edits.","screens":"The tint and every accent control.","money":"None."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["It is one file's edit, on the record since 2026-08-29 and missing from the current plan, so doing it costs about what re-recording it costs.","Doing it before weeks 1–2 means the five-second test and the developer walkthrough run on the real palette.","It shares a pass with D12's contrast fixes and D13's icon work."],"flip":"If the form factor goes to a VS Code extension, the host supplies the theme and only the tint tokens matter — so decide the form factor first if it is imminent.","linked":["D1","D12","D13","D21"],"sources":["src/app/globals.css:12","src/app/globals.css:34","src/app/globals.css:56","docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-2026-08-29.md:815","docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-2026-08-29.md:819","docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:430","docs/PRODUCT.md:997","docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:14","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:223","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:48","src/app/globals.css:2"]},{"id":"D12","cat":"Design, UI & attention","sub":"Accessibility","weight":"high","q":"Do the failing contrast tokens get fixed and gated in CI before the pilot, or after?","lede":"Six shipped tokens fail AA today, one of them on live error text, in a product whose operating rules promise WCAG 2.2 AA.","visual":{"kind":"ba","before":{"title":"Shipped tokens on --bg #fafafa","lines":[{"t":"--muted #9b9ba3 — 2.64:1","mark":"fail"},{"t":"--danger #b2625e — 4.19:1, live alert text","mark":"fail"},{"t":"--success #4f8b6b — 3.84:1","mark":"fail"},{"t":"--ring focus — 2.14:1","mark":"fail"},{"t":"§22 names body-faint, which is not in the build","mark":"fail"}]},"after":{"title":"After one pass and the gate","lines":[{"t":"Every text token at or above 4.5:1","mark":"pass"},{"t":"Every focus ring at or above 3:1","mark":"pass"},{"t":"§22 rewritten to name shipped tokens","mark":"pass"},{"t":"~30-line arithmetic check, blocking in CI","mark":"pass"}]},"via":"about half a day","note":"The gate is arithmetic over globals.css, so it cannot flake (docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:3404).","caption":"What fails today, and what one pass plus a gate would fix."},"stakes":"A procurement conversation reads §22, and §22 currently promises a standard the build does not meet.","state":["§22 promises WCAG 2.2 AA and names `body-faint`, a token that is not in the shipped set at all (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:540; docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-2026-08-29.md:819).","Six shipped tokens fail against `--bg #fafafa` (src/app/globals.css:25; docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:3370, :3374).","`--danger` is used for `role=\"alert\"` error text at 12px, so SC 1.4.3 fails in production now (docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:3383).","The CI gate exists on paper, about thirty lines, blocking and zero-flake, and is not built (docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:3404)."],"path":["PRD v1 quoted `body-faint` at 2.14:1 from the canonical system.","The r12 agent recomputed it and then found the larger problem: that hex is not in the app, and the shipped palette fails worse and is live (:3370).","The plan carried the corrected number forward and the wrong token with it."],"tension":["§22 makes two AA-adjacent promises and keeps neither: the token it names is absent, and the tint is colour alone (see D1).","Raising `--muted` and `--ring` changes a lot of chrome at once, so the fix wants one deliberate review pass.","Both competitors treated this as table stakes in six weeks: Notion shipped high contrast on 2026-07-30, Obsidian system text scaling in 1.14.x.","Fixing without the gate means the next stylesheet edit puts it back."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"Shipped tokens against the WCAG floors, on --bg #fafafa","cols":["Token","Value","Ratio","AA text 4.5","Non-text 3.0"],"rows":[["--fg","#18181b","16.97:1","PASS","PASS"],["--fg-muted","#6b6b73","5.06:1","PASS","PASS"],["--muted","#9b9ba3","2.64:1","FAIL","FAIL"],["--danger","#b2625e","4.19:1","FAIL — used on live 12px role=\"alert\" text","PASS"],["--success","#4f8b6b","3.84:1","FAIL","PASS"],["--border","rgba(10,10,10,.06) → #ececec","1.13:1","n/a","FAIL"],["--ring (focus)","rgba(91,33,182,.40) → #baa3df","2.14:1","n/a","FAIL"],["dark --muted","rgba(237,237,237,.40) → #6e6e6e on #1a1a1a","3.41:1","FAIL","PASS"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"The prototype has its own failures, separate from the app's","items":[["--faint #9aa3b2 on white","2.544:1","derived by me from docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:13; `var(--faint)` used 6 times, including the launcher footer line"],["--warn #b7791f on white","3.641:1","derived from :14; `var(--warn)` used 6 times, including the S13 STALE verdict label"],["--good #0d8a4f on white","4.407:1","derived from :14; just under the 4.5 floor; `var(--good)` used 7 times"],["dark --faint #6b7480 on #0f1115","3.991:1","derived from docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:22"],["prefers-reduced-motion in globals.css","0 occurrences, against 4 @keyframes and 3 animation declarations","measured in src/app/globals.css; also recorded at docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:3366"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Fix the tokens now and add the contrast gate to CI as blocking","what":"One arithmetic pass over both palettes, plus a thirty-line check.","gains":["Makes §22 true instead of aspirational, for about half a day","An arithmetic gate never flakes, so this class cannot come back","The pilot screenshots are then the ones that ship"],"costs":["Raising --muted and --ring changes the look of a lot of chrome at once"],"system":"Token edits plus one CI check.","screens":"Chrome across every screen.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Fix --danger only, which is a live production failure, and defer the rest","what":"The one failure a user meets today is removed.","gains":["An hour of work removes a live SC 1.4.3 failure"],"costs":["Leaves the focus ring at 2.14:1, which every keyboard user meets on every screen"],"system":"One token.","screens":"Error text.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Change §22 to say what is true and schedule the fix for MVP-1","what":"The promise is restated as a target with the failures named.","gains":["Honest, and costs nothing now"],"costs":["Any B2B or procurement conversation reads that sentence","PRODUCT.md already calls the divergence embarrassing to charge money in front of"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Fix the tokens now and defer the CI gate","what":"Correct today, ungated tomorrow.","gains":["The visible failures go away immediately"],"costs":["It regresses on the next stylesheet edit, which is the whole reason for a gate"],"system":"Token edits only.","screens":"Chrome.","money":"None."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["The fix is arithmetic on one file and the gate is thirty lines that cannot flake, so this is the cheapest promise in the plan to make true.","Correct §22 in the same edit; it currently names a token that is not in the build.","It shares a pass with D11's reconciliation, so doing both at once costs one review rather than two."],"flip":"If D11 goes to option c and the sibling palette becomes canonical, do both edits in one pass rather than twice.","linked":["D1","D11","D21","E12"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:540","src/app/globals.css:25","src/app/globals.css:31","docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:3370","docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:3374","docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:3383","docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:3404","docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-2026-08-29.md:819","docs/PRODUCT.md:997"]},{"id":"D13","cat":"Design, UI & attention","sub":"Accessibility","weight":"high","q":"Do icons and export fonts stop depending on Google's CDN, or ship as they are?","lede":"When the icon font does not arrive, 28 controls display the words `check_circle` and `close`; exports call Google on the reader's machine.","visual":{"kind":"screen","title":"The same toolbar, font present and font absent","panes":[{"label":"Font present","w":1,"rows":[{"label":"Icon, icon, icon","meta":"ligatures resolve","mark":"","tone":"good"},{"label":"28 call sites across 20 files","meta":"GoogleIcon.tsx:63","mark":"","tone":"neutral"}]},{"label":"Font absent","w":1,"rows":[{"label":"check_circle","meta":"ligature text","mark":"","tone":"stop"},{"label":"close","meta":"ligature text","mark":"","tone":"stop"},{"label":"download","meta":"ligature text","mark":"","tone":"stop"}]},{"label":"Where that happens","w":1,"rows":[{"label":"Desktop app offline","meta":"advertised at :99","mark":"","tone":"stop"},{"label":"Exported HTML on a reader's machine","meta":"F13, :67","mark":"","tone":"stop"},{"label":"Strict CSP or a blocked font host","meta":"not considered","mark":"","tone":"warn"}]}],"note":"No font-display and no preload anywhere in the stylesheet or the layout.","caption":"One failure mode, and the three places the plan already promises."},"stakes":"The offline case the product advertises is the case where the interface prints the names of its own icons.","state":["`globals.css:2` imports `material-symbols/rounded.css` and `GoogleIcon` renders the name as ligature text (src/shared/presentation/GoogleIcon.tsx:60, :63).","The export template emits two preconnects and a Google Fonts stylesheet link, on both export paths (src/modules/export/presentation/print-css.ts:27, :29; export-doc.ts:97; pdf-doc.ts:131).","PRD v1 already banned the web font in favour of inline SVG (docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-2026-08-29.md:817); the prototype uses inline symbols.","F13 export is MVP-0, already built and never run, with an hour budgeted to verify it (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:67)."],"path":["Both came from the sibling clone; the icon component keeps the sibling's shape on purpose.","A CDN font link is the normal way to make exported HTML look right, and nobody re-read it against the offline claim.","The current plan mentions neither icons nor fonts."],"tension":["The desktop app advertises offline for everything except the model, and both defects fire exactly there (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:99).","An export is the artefact most likely to leave the buying organisation, and every reader's request reaches a third party.","F13's one-hour verification budget is already allocated, which is the window in which this is cheap.","Whether the fonts' licence permits embedding in a redistributed file has not been checked, and it decides half of this on its own."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"Icon delivery, as built","items":[["Delivery method in the shipped app","Material Symbols web font, ligature text","src/app/globals.css:2, src/shared/presentation/GoogleIcon.tsx:60 and :63"],["JSX call sites","28 across 20 files","measured across src/"],["Inline <svg> elements in src/","4","measured"],["font-display declarations","0","measured in src/app/globals.css and src/app/layout.tsx"],["preload hints for the icon font","0","measured in the same two files"],["Delivery method in the prototype the pilot sees","inline SVG symbols, 110 <use href=\"#i-…\"> references","docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html"]]},{"type":"table","title":"When the font is absent, and what shows","cols":["Scenario","In the plan?","What the user sees"],"rows":[["Desktop app offline","yes — \"Everything except the model\" works offline (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:99)","the icon name as text"],["Exported HTML opened on a reader's machine","yes — F13 export (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:67)","the icon name as text"],["Web app, slow first load","yes — the web app is the trial","the icon name, then icons"],["Strict CSP or a blocked font host","not considered in the plan","the icon name as text"]]},{"type":"table","title":"What the export template does against what the plan promises","cols":["Plan statement","Where","What the export does"],"rows":[["Desktop works offline for \"Everything except the model\"","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:99, exhibit 2","exported HTML needs a network for its fonts"],["\"No document byte ever passes through a Zephyrus server\" (proposed)","docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:35","still true — but a third party sees each reader's request"],["F13 already built and never run","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:67","the template has not been reviewed against either claim"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"The export path, measured","items":[["External font requests per exported document","1 stylesheet plus the font files it pulls","src/modules/export/presentation/print-css.ts:29"],["Preconnect hints to third parties","2","fonts.googleapis.com and fonts.gstatic.com, print-css.ts:27–:28"],["Export paths that include them","2 of 2","export-doc.ts:97 and pdf-doc.ts:131"],["Export code, written and never executed","945 lines across 8 files","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:67"],["Verification budget in the plan","0d + 1h to verify it runs","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:67"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Inline SVG for the 28 call sites, and embed the export fonts as base64","what":"Neither the app nor an exported file needs a network for its typography.","gains":["The failure mode disappears and the app matches the screenshots","No third party sees a reader of an exported document","The prototype has already drawn the sprite"],"costs":["28 mechanical edits plus a sprite, and a few hundred kilobytes per export","Needs the licence check before embedding"],"system":"Icon component rewritten; export template inlines the faces.","screens":"None visually, if the sprite matches.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Keep the web font with font-display and a preload; use a system stack in exports","what":"Mitigate in the app, drop the fonts from the export.","gains":["Much cheaper, and the export gains no network call and no licence question"],"costs":["font-display only hides the text during its block period; the offline case still fails","The exported document stops looking like the product"],"system":"Two stylesheet edits.","screens":"Exported documents change typeface.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Change nothing","what":"The font and the CDN link ship as they are.","gains":["No work"],"costs":["The product ships a defect that fires first in the case it advertises"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Do only the surfaces other people see: the demo icons and the export template","what":"The demo path and the export are fixed; the rest stays on the font.","gains":["Protects the two surfaces a stranger looks at, at a fraction of the work"],"costs":["Two delivery mechanisms in one codebase, which is how the current state happened"],"system":"Partial migration.","screens":"Demo path and exports.","money":"None."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["It is 28 mechanical edits against a defect recorded in PRD v1 that fires in the exact scenario the product advertises.","The prototype has already drawn the sprite, so the assets exist.","Embedding keeps the export looking like the product and removes a third party from a file a user may send to a client."],"flip":"If the fonts' licence does not permit embedding in a redistributed file, the export half is forced to a system stack — check the licence before the meeting.","linked":["D11","D12"],"sources":["docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-2026-08-29.md:817","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:67","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:99","docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:35","merged: D14","src/app/globals.css:2","src/modules/export/presentation/export-doc.ts:97","src/modules/export/presentation/pdf-doc.ts:131","src/modules/export/presentation/print-css.ts:27","src/modules/export/presentation/print-css.ts:29","src/shared/presentation/GoogleIcon.tsx:60","src/shared/presentation/GoogleIcon.tsx:63"]},{"id":"D15","cat":"Design, UI & attention","sub":"Accessibility","weight":"high","q":"Does Tab indent in the editor, or move focus?","lede":"The PRD records this binding as absent and says keep it that way; it is bound in four places across two files.","visual":{"kind":"flow","perRow":4,"nodes":[{"label":"Keyboard user tabs into the editor","tone":"neutral"},{"label":"indentWithTab inserts an indent","note":"bound in 2 files, 4 lines","tone":"warn","edge":"Tab"},{"label":"Focus never leaves","note":"SC 2.1.2, Level A","tone":"stop","edge":"Tab again"},{"label":"No hint, nothing announced","note":"EditorView.announce: 0 call sites","tone":"stop"}],"note":"The PRD's own row forbids fixing a trap by documenting the escape key in a help modal.","caption":"The Level A failure the corpus records as already avoided."},"stakes":"A keyboard user who reaches the editor cannot leave it, and the plan believes this was never introduced.","state":["`indentWithTab` is imported and bound in the main editor (src/modules/editor/presentation/CodeMirrorEditor.tsx:18, :233) and the inline block editor (live/InlineBlockEditor.tsx:13, :64).","The PRD states it appears zero times in `src/` and marks that measured (docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:3358).","SC 2.1.1 and 2.1.2 are Level A, the strictest tier in the whole accessibility set.","`EditorView.announce` has zero call sites, so no escape route can be announced (docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:3395)."],"path":["Tab-to-indent is the default expectation for a code-shaped surface and came with the cloned editor (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:223).","The accessibility section then wrote the opposite as a measured fact and built a recommendation on it.","That is the false-green class this codebase's own rules exist to catch, so the PRD line has to be corrected either way."],"tension":["Removing Tab-to-indent will be noticed by exactly the developer buyer §14's buyer decision is choosing.","The PRD's own anti-recommendation says 2.1.2 needs discoverability at the point of the trap, not a help modal.","An escape hint has to be announced as well as shown, and the announce plumbing has zero call sites.","Whichever way it goes, the measurement that said zero when the answer is four must be corrected."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"The claim against the code","cols":["Source","Statement"],"rows":[["docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:3358, §35.2","\"`indentWithTab` appears 0 times in `src/`\" [measured] — keep it that way"],["src/modules/editor/presentation/CodeMirrorEditor.tsx:18, :233","imported and bound in the main editor keymap"],["src/modules/editor/presentation/live/InlineBlockEditor.tsx:13, :64","imported and bound in the inline block editor"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"What the criterion requires","items":[["SC 2.1.1 Keyboard, SC 2.1.2 No Keyboard Trap","Level A","docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:3358"],["Occurrences claimed in the PRD","0","measured wrongly"],["Occurrences in the code today","4 lines across 2 files","measured by me"],["PRD's stated anti-recommendation","do not \"fix\" a trap by documenting the escape key in a help modal","same row — 2.1.2 requires discoverability at the point of trap"],["EditorView.announce call sites in src/","0","so no escape route can be announced to a screen reader today"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Remove indentWithTab from both keymaps; Tab moves focus","what":"Two edits, and the trap is gone.","gains":["Clears a Level A failure outright","No new UI, nothing to announce"],"costs":["Writers who Tab to indent a list lose a common habit","Enter-continuation of lists covers only part of it"],"system":"Two keymap edits.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Keep Tab-to-indent and add Escape-then-Tab with a visible hint on focus","what":"The conventional CodeMirror escape, shown at the trap.","gains":["Keeps the editing behaviour a developer expects","Satisfies 2.1.2 if the hint is genuinely at the point of the trap"],"costs":["Only clears the criterion if it is right, and a screen-reader user needs it announced","Needs the announce plumbing that has zero call sites today"],"system":"A keymap addition plus the first announce call sites.","screens":"A hint on editor focus.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Keep it in the main editor only; remove it from the inline block editor","what":"Halves the exposure.","gains":["Keeps the habit where a developer chose to be, removes it where a click put them"],"costs":["The main editor is still a trap, so the Level A failure remains"],"system":"One keymap edit.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Make it a setting under Keymap","what":"The reader picks, alongside the existing keymap options.","gains":["S11 already has a Keymap group, so it fits (docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:606)"],"costs":["The default is still this decision, and a default that traps keyboard users is the failure"],"system":"One preference.","screens":"S11 gains a row.","money":"None."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["Escape-then-Tab is the conventional CodeMirror answer and keeps the habit the developer buyer expects.","It only clears 2.1.2 if the hint sits at the trap and is announced, so budget the first announce call sites with it.","Correct the PRD line in the same commit: a measurement that says zero when the answer is four is a false green."],"flip":"If the announce work does not land with it, b does not clear the criterion and a is the only honest option.","linked":["D12","D9","FL2"],"sources":["src/modules/editor/presentation/CodeMirrorEditor.tsx:18","src/modules/editor/presentation/CodeMirrorEditor.tsx:233","src/modules/editor/presentation/live/InlineBlockEditor.tsx:64","docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:3358","docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:3395","src/modules/editor/presentation/live/InlineBlockEditor.tsx:13","docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:606"]},{"id":"D18","cat":"Design, UI & attention","sub":"Testing","weight":"high","q":"What does the five-second test measure, at what sample size, and what result stops the build?","lede":"The one test that could settle every tint question is five people, one question, and no pass line.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":170,"cols":[{"title":"As specified","tone":"neutral"},{"title":"As proposed","tone":"accent"}],"rows":[{"label":"Participants","cells":["5","15"]},{"label":"First question","cells":["what does the tint mean?","did you notice anything marked?"]},{"label":"Tints shown","cells":["1","2 — written and proposed"]},{"label":"Pass line","cells":["none; two failing words named","10 of 15 notice unprompted, 2 or fewer read it as an error"]},{"label":"Build days gated on the result","cells":["0","review-state rendering waits"]},{"label":"Decisions it can answer","cells":["none, since it cannot fail","D1, D2, D4, D23"]}],"note":"Asking what the tint means presupposes it was seen, so a participant who missed it still produces an answer.","caption":"The test as written cannot fail; the test as proposed can."},"stakes":"The gate that decides whether MVP-0's headline feature is visible is a phrase, not a measure.","state":["§14 and §16 specify five people, one screenshot, and the question what the tint means (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:352, :411).","Only two failing answers are named; there is no pass line and no protocol.","No build day depends on the result: review-state rendering is in weeks 5–7 either way (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:355).","The gap register grades §16 Medium: two sources, one a lab study on code, no measurement on our screens (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:26)."],"path":["The test was written as a cheap way to falsify the tint before building it.","Five sits beside ten developers, five people who bill for documents and 20 team conversations in the same row (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:352).","Nobody wrote the criterion that would make it a gate rather than an anecdote."],"tension":["Comprehension is the wrong measure. The transferable literature is about dismissal: 55–98% override, and 86.6% in a 14,612-alert audit.","Those figures come from clinical alerting and code review; no evidence exists on reviewing AI-written prose, so every transfer is an analogy.","Five participants cannot separate a marginal design from a bad one, so a 3-of-5 result says nothing.","The row promises a kill signal at day 14, and a test with no pass line cannot produce one."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"What the test asks, against what the tint decisions need to know","cols":["Question the design needs answered","Asked by the test as specified?"],"rows":[["Did you notice anything marked on this page?","no — the question presupposes the tint was seen (D1)"],["What do you think the mark means?","yes"],["Can you tell these two marks apart?","no — only one tint is shown (D2)"],["Where did you look first?","no — this is what would test §16's F-pattern prediction (D4, D5)"],["What is the pass line?","not stated — only two failing answers are named"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"The test as scheduled","items":[["Participants","5","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:352"],["Stated pass criterion","none","only \"highlighted\" and \"error\" named as failures, docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:411"],["Observable outcome the row promises","\"Kill signals at day 14\"","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:352"],["Build days gated on the result","0","review-state store and rendering are in weeks 5–7 regardless, docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:355"],["Gap register severity for §16","Medium","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:26"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Run it as written: five people, one screenshot, one question","what":"An hour, and the tint work proceeds either way.","gains":["Cheapest, and it may still surface the word `error`"],"costs":["Produces an anecdote that cannot fail","Answers a question that presupposes the mark was seen"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"About an hour."},{"k":"b","label":"Rewrite it: n=15, noticing first, both tints, a stated pass line","what":"Three questions in order, with a criterion written before the run.","gains":["Produces numbers that can kill the design","Feeds D1, D2, D4 and D23 from one recruitment","Still unmoderated and still about a day"],"costs":["Recruiting 15 in the same fortnight as the other tests is the real cost","Somebody has to own the pass line before the data arrives"],"system":"No change.","screens":"Two screenshots instead of one.","money":"Recruitment for 15."},{"k":"c","label":"Keep n=5 but make it a noticing test with a 4-of-5 line","what":"The cheapest change that makes the test falsifiable.","gains":["Falsifiable for the same hour"],"costs":["n=5 still cannot separate a marginal design from a bad one"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"About an hour."},{"k":"d","label":"Drop it and decide the tint on the contrast floors alone","what":"Arithmetic replaces five opinions.","gains":["Removes a week-2 item and grounds the decision in numbers we already have"],"costs":["Loses the only chance to learn that people read blue-on-white as an error"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["Four decisions on this list are answered by the same fifteen-minute screenshot exercise, so the marginal cost of doing it properly is ten more participants.","Noticing is the measure that matters, because the failure the literature documents is dismissal, not misreading.","A test with no pass line cannot produce the kill signal at day 14 that the same row promises."],"flip":"If the ten-developer walkthrough in the same fortnight can carry these questions, fold it in and run one recruitment rather than two.","linked":["D1","D2","D23","D4","FL11"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:352","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:355","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:411","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:413","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:26","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/35673040/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38658357/"]},{"id":"D9","cat":"Design, UI & attention","sub":"Editor scope","weight":"medium","q":"Click a tinted span in Live mode and both the mark and the actions break. Which half do we fix?","lede":"The editable unit is a whole top-level block, and the editor that opens on click carries no tint at all.","visual":{"kind":"file","name":"spec.md — clicking a tinted word inside a list","lines":[{"t":"## Acceptance criteria","mark":"","note":"reviewed"},{"t":"- The token refreshes silently.","mark":"unreviewed","note":"tinted"},{"t":"  - Rotation is not logged.","mark":"unreviewed","note":"tinted"},{"t":"- Sessions end on sign-out.","mark":"","note":"reviewed"}],"note":"splitIntoSegments iterates tree.children only, so the whole list is one editable unit; the inline editor it opens carries no decoration.","caption":"Where the mark and the byte range stop agreeing."},"stakes":"The revert-one-span demo works on a paragraph and degrades on a list item, which is what spec files are mostly made of.","state":["`splitIntoSegments` iterates `tree.children` only, so every editable segment is a top-level block (src/modules/editor/presentation/live/block-split.ts:45, :48).","Clicking a block swaps it into a raw CodeMirror instance that carries no review decoration (src/modules/editor/presentation/live/InlineBlockEditor.tsx:64).","The wireframes rule the tint out of Edit mode as information about the document, not the source (docs/_wireframes.md:17).","No file in `src/` carries review-tint state yet; F2 costs the rendering at 5 days (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:56)."],"path":["The splitter guarantees `reassemble(splitIntoSegments(src)) === src`, and top-level tiling is the simplest way to prove it (block-split.ts:16).","It arrived from the sibling codebase with the rest of the editor (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:223).","The rendered-views-only tint rule was written before anyone clicked a tinted span."],"tension":["§21 claims nested constructs render correctly; rendering does, editing granularity does not (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:524).","Nobody in the redlining category sells below word level, so byte granularity already sits under the floor any buyer was taught to want.","The splice engine is byte-range native, so the review actions never needed the block splitter — only click-to-edit does.","Nothing is announced either way: `EditorView.announce` has zero call sites (docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:3395)."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"The split, as implemented","items":[["Nodes iterated","tree.children only","src/modules/editor/presentation/live/block-split.ts:48"],["Editable unit","one top-level markdown block","heading, paragraph, list, fenced code, blockquote, table, frontmatter"],["Lines in the splitter","93","the property it guarantees is loss-less reassembly, not fine granularity"],["Obsidian's equivalent limitation","\"The Live Preview tree is depth-1 by construction\"","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:127, in a row that grades the plugin channel \"Not viable\""],["Measurement of how often review spans sit inside nested constructs","unmeasured","no report in the corpus counts this"]]},{"type":"table","title":"Where the tint renders, against where byte-level truth is most visible","cols":["Surface","Tint renders?","Shows raw bytes?"],"rows":[["Live (rendered)","yes","no"],["Live, block open for editing","no","yes"],["Edit (raw source)","no","yes"],["Split","yes, in the rendered pane","yes, in the source pane"],["Read","yes","no"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"What is built today","items":[["Files in src/ carrying review-tint state","0","measured: no file matches unreviewed / reviewTint / reviewState"],["Estimated cost of review-state rendering","5 engineering days","F2 row, docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:56"],["CodeMirror version installed","@codemirror/view ^6.43.0","package.json:47 — decorations are native"],["EditorView.announce call sites in src/","0","measured; also recorded at docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:3395"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Keep block granularity and the rendered-views-only rule, and document both","what":"Nothing changes; the limits are written down.","gains":["Zero build, and the loss-less property is untouched"],"costs":["The mark disappears under the cursor in the default mode","Revert lands on a block that may be forty lines"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Actions on byte ranges, and carry the tint into the inline block editor","what":"Mark-reviewed and revert work on the span; the decoration follows the click.","gains":["Uses the engine's native unit and leaves the splitter's proof alone","Fixes the case a user meets by accident, in the default mode","One decoration set reused in two places"],"costs":["A forty-line block still opens as raw source","Two behaviours to explain: the tint follows you here and not into Edit"],"system":"Review actions bind to byte ranges; the decoration set is shared.","screens":"S2 Live keeps the tint while editing.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Extend the splitter one level: list items and blockquote children","what":"The editable unit gets finer where specs actually need it.","gains":["Covers the two constructs spec files are made of"],"costs":["The loss-less reassembly property has to be re-proved at the new granularity","That property is the file's whole reason for existing"],"system":"Splitter change plus a corpus re-proof.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Render the tint everywhere, Edit mode included, as one decoration set","what":"The mark never disappears, in any mode.","gains":["One implementation, used three times","Puts the mark in the view where byte-level truth is most visible"],"costs":["Adds the source view to the contrast and test matrix","A wash behind monospace source is a different legibility problem"],"system":"One decoration set across all modes.","screens":"Edit and the inline editor gain the tint.","money":"None."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["The disappearing mark is a defect rather than a scope choice: it happens in the default mode, to a user who did not choose it.","Binding the actions to byte ranges costs nothing new, because the engine already works that way.","Edit staying plain is a position someone can argue for; a mark that vanishes under the cursor is not."],"flip":"If the weeks 3–4 hash prototype shows most spans are whole paragraphs, a is enough and c is wasted work.","linked":["D1","D12","D8"],"sources":["docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:3395","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:127","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:352","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:354","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:524","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:56","docs/_wireframes.md:17","merged: D10","src/modules/editor/presentation/live/InlineBlockEditor.tsx:64","src/modules/editor/presentation/live/block-split.ts:16","src/modules/editor/presentation/live/block-split.ts:45"]},{"id":"D20","cat":"Design, UI & attention","sub":"Prototype scope","weight":"medium","q":"What does the prototype owe before the pilot — the three undrawn screens, a benchmark against shipped products, or neither?","lede":"Nine screens exist, three that carry claims do not, and no screen has ever been held against a shipped product.","visual":{"kind":"screen","title":"Prototype coverage before the pilot","panes":[{"label":"Drawn — 9","w":1,"rows":[{"label":"S0, S2, S4, S3b, S2c","meta":"MVP-0","mark":"","tone":"good"},{"label":"S11 settings, S13 repo docs","meta":"MVP-0","mark":"","tone":"good"},{"label":"S8 refactor, S12 generate","meta":"MVP-1 and MVP-2","mark":"","tone":"sunk"}]},{"label":"Undrawn — 3","w":1,"rows":[{"label":"S1 open a folder, first run","meta":"§17's retention lever","mark":"","tone":"stop"},{"label":"S9 conflict, the only blocking modal","meta":"the sync doctrine","mark":"","tone":"stop"},{"label":"S10 team view, behind the paywall","meta":"the whole paid tier","mark":"","tone":"stop"}]},{"label":"Never compared","w":1,"rows":[{"label":"Ten screen queries, written 2026-08-28","meta":"refused twice by the taint gate","mark":"","tone":"warn"},{"label":"Screens seen outside this session","meta":"0","mark":"","tone":"stop"}]}],"note":"Every placement decision so far was made from written conventions rather than from interfaces.","caption":"What the pilot sees, and what nothing was compared with."},"stakes":"The screens that decide first-week retention, data safety and the entire paid tier are the three nobody has drawn.","state":["The prototype holds nine screens, of which S8 is MVP-1 and S12 is MVP-2 (docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:281, :624, :660).","The wireframes' map names three more: first run, conflict, and team view (docs/_wireframes.md:51, :37).","The screen benchmark was attempted twice and refused by a session-scoped taint gate; the ten queries are written (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:375, :387).","The gap register costs it at one fresh session with no founder time, item 11 of 12 (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:39, :109, :112)."],"path":["The prototype was built to demonstrate the review loop, so the review-path screens were drawn first.","S1, S9 and S10 each belong to a part of the product that is pre-review, exceptional, or paid.","The benchmark was deferred twice while nine screens were drawn (docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-28/c6-screens.md:12)."],"tension":["§17 stakes retention on a first-session screen that has never been drawn (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:429).","S9 is the product's only blocking modal and the visible face of the sync doctrine; shipping it undesigned is the worst moment to improvise.","S10 is the whole of Pro, which the gap register already grades High (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:25).","Four platforms shipped an agent-review pane in the last six weeks, so there is now something concrete to compare against."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"The three undrawn screens and what each carries","cols":["Screen","Stated role","What depends on it"],"rows":[["S1 open a folder","\"first run only\" (docs/_wireframes.md:51)","§17's first-session retention lever: edit in thirty seconds, no account (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:429)"],["S9 conflict","\"the only blocking modal\" (docs/_wireframes.md:51)","the sync doctrine — git merge, never a CRDT, divergence surfaced not guessed"],["S10 team view","\"the only screen behind the paywall\" (docs/_wireframes.md:37)","the entire paid tier, graded High in docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:25"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"Prototype coverage","items":[["Screens in the clickable prototype","9","section markers at docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:281–:686"],["Screens named in the wireframes","13, S0 through S12","docs/_wireframes.md; the map at :51 covers S0–S10, and S13 appears only in the plan and the prototype"],["Of the nine, screens after MVP-0","2","S8 is marked MVP-1 (:624), S12 is marked MVP-2 (:660)"],["People outside the authoring session who have seen any of them","0","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:27"]]},{"type":"table","title":"The ten queries already written, and which decisions they would settle","cols":["Maps to","Decision it would inform"],"rows":[["S0 launcher, 2 queries","the empty state and first-run shape (D20)"],["S2 editor, AI placement, 3 queries","D7 — prompt at the cursor or docked"],["S2 right rail and S13 evidence rail, 1 query","D4, D5 — where the counter lives, how many surfaces"],["S4 review panel, 1 query","the accept/reject grammar"],["S11 settings, 1 query","D3 — which toggles are conventional"],["Pricing and upsell, 2 queries","outside this area"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"Cost and standing","items":[["Cost to run","one fresh session","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:39"],["Rounds on which it was attempted and refused","at least 2","2026-08-28 (c6-screens.md:12, h1-design-patterns.md:2) and 2026-09-08 (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:375)"],["Screens drawn without it","9","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:27 — \"seen by nobody outside this session\""],["Position in the ordered list of what makes the plan solid","item 11 of 12","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:109"],["Founder involvement required","none","one of seven founder-independent items, docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:112"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Draw S1 only, before the pilot","what":"The first-run screen every participant meets gets designed.","gains":["Covers the retention claim with the least evidence behind it","One screen, on a schedule that cannot afford three"],"costs":["The conflict modal ships undesigned into the user's worst moment","Nothing is compared against a shipped product"],"system":"None.","screens":"S1 added.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Run the benchmark in a fresh session, then draw S1","what":"Comparables first, then the one missing screen everyone reaches.","gains":["Every placement question gets a reference from a shipped product","One session, no founder time, and the queries are already written","The screens then tested are the revised ones"],"costs":["Delays the prototype revision by about a day","Comparables are conventions, not evidence about our own users"],"system":"None.","screens":"S1 added; the nine revised against references.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Draw all three undrawn screens and skip the benchmark","what":"Complete visual coverage of every claim the plan makes.","gains":["Nothing the plan promises is missing from the pilot"],"costs":["Three screens to build and keep consistent at 1.21 engineering days a week","The nine go into the pilot compared against no interface at all"],"system":"None.","screens":"S1, S9, S10 added.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Neither; test on the nine that exist","what":"The pilot sees the prototype as it stands.","gains":["No delay at all"],"costs":["The retention, sync and paid-tier claims have no visual","§15's scope caveat becomes permanent"],"system":"None.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["The benchmark costs one session, needs no founder, and is the only input that answers a placement question from something other than reasoning.","S1 is the one undrawn screen every pilot participant is guaranteed to reach, and it carries the retention claim.","Running the benchmark first means the screenshots the five-second test uses are the revised ones."],"flip":"If the Pro tier enters the twenty team conversations in weeks 1–2, S10 becomes the artefact those conversations need and is drawn first.","linked":["D18","D21","D4","D7"],"sources":["docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:109","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:25","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:27","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:39","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:375","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:387","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:429","docs/_wireframes.md:37","docs/_wireframes.md:51","docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:281","docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:624","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-28/c6-screens.md:12","merged: D19"]},{"id":"D21","cat":"Design, UI & attention","sub":"Dark mode","weight":"medium","q":"Does dark mode ship at the pilot, given the tint is quieter there and nothing in it has been reviewed?","lede":"Two themes doubles every visual decision on this list, and the review tint is 1.185:1 in the one nobody has looked at.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":170,"cols":[{"title":"Light","tone":"neutral"},{"title":"Dark","tone":"warn"}],"rows":[{"label":"Review tint against the page","cells":["1.111:1","1.185:1"]},{"label":"Review tint against proposal tint","cells":["ΔE76 4.10","ΔE76 8.85"]},{"label":"Prototype --faint secondary text","cells":["2.544:1 FAIL","3.991:1 FAIL"]},{"label":"Shipped app --muted","cells":["2.64:1 FAIL","3.41:1 FAIL"]},{"label":"Screenshots reviewed by anyone","cells":["9","0"]}],"note":"Ratios derived from the prototype's and the app's declared hexes; §16 names no theme anywhere.","caption":"The same decisions, measured in the theme nobody has looked at."},"stakes":"Shipping two themes without saying which was tested means no visual feedback from the pilot can be attributed to either.","state":["The shipped stylesheet carries a full dark palette and a `prefers-color-scheme` fallback (src/app/globals.css:89, :129); the prototype adds a `data-theme` override (docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:22, :28).","S11's first control is Theme: System, Light, Dark (docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:605).","The five-second test names one screenshot and no theme (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:411).","The canonical system is described as a single accent on white (docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-2026-08-29.md:819)."],"path":["Both themes came with the cloned sibling app; nobody chose to ship dark mode, it was already there.","The prototype mirrored it so the screenshots would look complete.","No exhibit, screenshot or test has ever named a dark render."],"tension":["Every question on this list has a second answer in dark, and none of them has been checked.","A developer audience looks for dark mode within a minute, and removing a control that works is its own regression.","The dark palette carries its own AA failures, so D12's pass has to cover it either way.","Adding dark renders is close to free, because the prototype already has the toggle (docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:28)."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"The same decisions, measured in both themes","cols":["Measure","Light","Dark"],"rows":[["Review tint against the page","1.111:1","1.185:1"],["Review tint vs proposal tint","ΔE76 4.10","ΔE76 8.85"],["Prototype --faint secondary text","2.544:1 FAIL","3.991:1 FAIL"],["Prototype hairline divider","1.240:1","1.312:1"],["Shipped app --muted","2.64:1 FAIL","3.41:1 FAIL"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"What has been reviewed in dark","items":[["Screenshots specified for the five-second test","1","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:411 — no theme named"],["Themes named anywhere in §16","0","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:400–:413"],["Exhibits or files in docs/ that name a dark render","0","the nine prototype PNGs in docs/screens/ carry no theme in their names or captions"],["Contrast failures in the dark palettes","at least 2","prototype --faint 3.991:1 and shipped --muted 3.41:1; derived by me"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Ship both and fix the dark contrast failures alongside the light ones","what":"Two themes, one arithmetic pass over both palettes.","gains":["Meets the developer expectation and clears both palettes at once"],"costs":["Doubles the test matrix for a design nobody has reviewed in that theme"],"system":"Token edits in both palettes.","screens":"All, in dark.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Ship light only for the pilot; keep the dark tokens unreachable","what":"One theme to test, one set of screenshots, one answer per question.","gains":["Every result is attributable to one design"],"costs":["A developer audience notices within a minute and some will say so","Removing a control that already works reads as a regression"],"system":"The theme control is hidden.","screens":"S11 loses a control.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Ship both, and run the five-second test in dark because it is the harder case","what":"Test the weaker design and let the light case follow.","gains":["Measures the case most likely to fail"],"costs":["Answers one theme's questions while the launch screenshots are in the other"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Ship both and add dark renders of the nine screens to the prototype","what":"The untested theme gets looked at by the same people.","gains":["Close to free: the prototype already has a data-theme toggle","Turns an unreviewed surface into a reviewed one without cutting anything"],"costs":["A review is not a measurement, so it does not settle the contrast question","Nine more images to keep in step"],"system":"No change.","screens":"Nine dark renders.","money":"None."}],"rec":"d","recCase":["Cutting dark mode from a developer tool costs more goodwill than it saves work, and the tokens are already written.","What is missing is that nobody has looked at them, and looking is the cheap part.","The contrast failures in the dark palette are fixed by D12's pass whichever option wins."],"flip":"If the extended test in D18 finds the dark tint unnoticed, b is the honest answer and the control comes off until the design is fixed.","linked":["D1","D12","D18","D2"],"sources":["src/app/globals.css:89","src/app/globals.css:129","docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:22","docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:28","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:411","docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-2026-08-29.md:819","docs/prototype/frontmatter-prototype.html:605","src/app/globals.css:31"]},{"id":"D22","cat":"Design, UI & attention","sub":"Reader adaptation","weight":"medium","q":"What is v1's stated scope for CJK, RTL, text scaling and high contrast, and does the plan say it on the page?","lede":"The plan owes one written scope line; both competitors shipped three of these four inside six weeks.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":170,"cols":[{"title":"Settled in the record","tone":"neutral"},{"title":"In the plan","tone":"warn"},{"title":"Shipped elsewhere","tone":"sunk"}],"rows":[{"label":"Byte-to-UTF-16 map","cells":["the highest-risk seam","named as engine work (:233)","—"]},{"label":"CJK search","cells":["character bigrams","one clause (:540)","—"]},{"label":"RTL content","cells":["dir=auto on both panes (:4057)","not mentioned","Obsidian 1.14.x"]},{"label":"RTL chrome mirroring","cells":["out for v1 (:4062)","not mentioned","—"]},{"label":"System text scaling","cells":["not covered","not mentioned","Obsidian 1.14.x"]},{"label":"High contrast","cells":["not covered","not mentioned","Notion, 2026-07-30"]}],"note":"Record references are docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md; plan references are docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md.","caption":"What was settled, what the page carries, what shipped elsewhere."},"stakes":"An unsupported non-English user does not get a refusal, they get a silently damaged file.","state":["§22 owes `a written v1 scope decision` and carries one clause of what §43 settled (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:540).","§9 calls the byte-to-UTF-16 map the highest-risk seam, corrupting Chinese, Japanese, Korean and Arabic text silently (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:233).","The record settled RTL as a layout problem, with `dir=\"auto\"` on both panes and chrome mirroring out for v1 (docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:4057, :4062, :4064).","The gap register says to state it out of the pilot; nobody Chinese, Japanese or Korean has been asked (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:42)."],"path":["§43 settled the engineering: bigrams for search, direction attributes on both panes, no chrome mirroring, no UI localisation (docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:4088).","The plan carried one clause of it and none of the reasoning.","`A written v1 scope decision` has been outstanding since v14, which makes it a task standing in for a decision."],"tension":["The failure mode is asymmetric: unsupported and unstated means corruption, not refusal, which contradicts the whole refusal posture.","Obsidian shipped RTL and system text scaling in 1.14.x and Notion shipped high contrast on 2026-07-30, so these read as table stakes now.","The record's rule is that the editor and the preview share a base direction, ship both or neither, and the plan says which for neither.","Every UI string is English and the record says do not translate for v1, so scope has to be stated in two halves."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"What the record settled, and what the plan carries","cols":["Decision","In the record (§43)","In the plan"],"rows":[["Search tokenisation","character bigrams, not Intl.Segmenter — a segmenter mismatch gives silent zero-recall (§43.5)","one clause: \"a bigram search tokeniser\" (:540)"],["RTL content","dir=\"auto\" on both panes plus perLineTextDirection; ship both or neither (:4057, :4058, :4064)","not mentioned"],["RTL chrome mirroring","explicitly out for v1 — \"weeks, not days\" (:4062)","not mentioned"],["UI localisation","do not do it for v1; no reviewers for ar/ja/zh copy (:4088)","not mentioned"],["Byte-to-UTF-16 map","the highest-risk seam; silent corruption if unmapped","named as engine work at :233, no scope statement"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"Standing of the decision","items":[["Status","outstanding since v14","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:540 lists it as owed"],["Non-English users consulted","0","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:42"],["Gap register's recommendation","\"Out of the pilot; state it\"","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:42"],["Failure mode if unsupported and unstated","silent corruption, not refusal","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:233"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"State it out of scope: Latin-script content only, on the page and in the app","what":"One paragraph, and non-Latin files are marked unsupported.","gains":["Honest, free, and it closes the owed decision today"],"costs":["A visible narrowing against the plan's own thesis that markdown belongs to everyone","Discards RTL work the record shows is nearly free"],"system":"No change.","screens":"A line in Settings and on the page.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Support CJK and RTL content plus text scaling; the interface stays English","what":"Byte map, bigram index, direction on both panes, and system text size respected.","gains":["Matches what §43 already settled and what the engine is being built for","The byte map is on the MVP-0 list regardless, so the margin is small","Text scaling and high contrast are now expected of any editor"],"costs":["Commits the byte map to MVP-0, which is a schedule claim","Adds two more states to the contrast and screenshot work"],"system":"Direction attributes, bigram index, the both-panes rule.","screens":"Editor and preview gain a shared base direction.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Refuse non-Latin files until the byte map is verified","what":"The safest posture under a byte-exactness thesis.","gains":["Refuse rather than corrupt, the same rule as malformed repos refused"],"costs":["Refusing a file because of its language will be read badly","Turns a scope gap into a visible rejection"],"system":"A refusal path on non-Latin content.","screens":"A refusal panel.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Leave it open and decide after the pilot","what":"The owed line stays owed.","gains":["Nothing to write now"],"costs":["Two plan versions old already","The corruption risk ships with no statement beside it"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["Most of b is already being paid for: the byte map is MVP-0 engine work and the search decision is made.","What is missing is one paragraph in §22 and one rule that the editor and preview share a base direction.","Text scaling and high contrast now sit alongside RTL as things both competitors shipped in six weeks."],"flip":"If the byte map slips out of MVP-0, c is the only honest position — corrupting a Chinese document silently is worse than refusing to open it.","linked":["D12","E33"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:233","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:540","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:42","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:4053","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:4057","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:4062","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:4064","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:4088","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:4064"]},{"id":"E1","cat":"Engine & technical","sub":"Write path","weight":"critical","q":"Do we patch the refusing branch now and let the measured residual decide whether a structural fix follows, and is that fix the `yaml` CST or our own lexer?","lede":"Five of six flows open with a write that refuses 83% of real vaults, and three committed documents price the fix three different ways.","visual":{"kind":"file","name":"note.md","lines":[{"t":"---","mark":"neutral"},{"t":"tags:","mark":"good","note":"top-level key: the locator finds it"},{"t":"- obsidian","mark":"stop","note":"column zero: the writer refuses here"},{"t":"- vault","mark":"stop"},{"t":"---","mark":"neutral"},{"t":"# Note body","mark":"sunk"}],"note":"A dash at column zero continues the key above it. The branch reads it as a bare line and returns the input unchanged.","caption":"The shape 6,613 of 7,969 corpus frontmatter blocks emit"},"stakes":"Publish, share and every property edit fail silently on the vaults our own corpus is made of.","state":["The refusal is one branch at src/modules/share/domain/splice-frontmatter.ts:197, over any line that is neither indented nor a comment.","6,615 of 7,969 frontmatter files refuse a single `set` — 83.01% (docs/ENGINE.md:487).","`yaml@2.9.0` is already a direct dependency (package.json:81) and nothing imports its CST layer (docs/ENGINE.md:320).","NF-1's spec sets the post-fix ceiling at 2 refusals of 7,969 (specs/engine/nf-001-zero-indent-sequence.md:47)."],"path":["The writer was line-wise on purpose. It locates a key, it does not parse YAML, and that is what makes it byte-exact.","The refusal is right in spirit and wrong in fact: a column-zero dash is what Obsidian emits under `tags:`.","ENGINE §72.2 reads the patch as moving the rate and leaving the class alive (docs/ENGINE.md:646)."],"tension":["The patch is a day. The structural fix is priced at 2.0 founder-weeks and marked inference, not measurement (docs/ENGINE.md:622).","`CST.stringify` round-trips the refused shape byte-identically, but adopting a YAML library for mutation is anti-recommended (docs/ENGINE.md:650).","No residual has been agreed as the trigger, so the structural question gets argued under deadline."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"The refusal, reproduced at HEAD today","items":[["Files in pinned corpus","8,513","test/corpus/foreign/SOURCES.json"],["Files with frontmatter","7,969","docs/ENGINE.md:487"],["Refused on a single `set`","6,615 = 83.01%","docs/ENGINE.md:487"],["Of those, zero-indent block sequence","6,611 by first-offending-line attribution; 6,613 by the §75 count","docs/ENGINE.md:487, docs/ENGINE.md:1101 — the doc explains the gap as an attribution-method difference, not corpus drift, and names `node scripts/corpus-foreign.mjs verify` as the authority"],["Throws / corruptions among the 1,354 that proceeded","0 / 0","docs/ENGINE.md:146"],["Reproduced in this session","yes — `set` on `---\\ntags:\\n- a\\n- b\\n---` returns the input unchanged","live run against src/modules/share/domain/splice-frontmatter.ts at HEAD"]]},{"type":"table","title":"Three documents, three prices — and the disagreement is not the one that was reported","cols":["Document","Scope","Price"],"rows":[["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:214-215","NF-1 (4 d) + NF-3 (3 d)","7 engineering days"],["docs/ENGINE.md:622","E1 — all four YAML defects","2.0 founder-weeks; CRITIQUE reads that as 10 working days"],["docs/DECIDE.md:82-83","NF-3 (4 pts) + NF-1/NF-2 (6 pts)","10 pts, which at DECIDE's own stated rate of 38 pts ≈ 41 days (docs/DECIDE.md:73) is ≈ 10.8 days"],["docs/CRITIQUE.md:795","calls it \"a ~2× disagreement… unnoticed. SERIOUS\"","It derives those same 10 points as \"≈ 2.7 focused days\". That does not follow from DECIDE §3.1's only stated rate, and re-deriving it puts DECIDE and ENGINE within a day of each other. The real outlier is the brief's 7 days, on narrower scope"]]},{"type":"table","title":"Three ways to locate a key's bytes","cols":["Approach","Handles zero-indent","Refusal policy","New dependency"],"rows":[["Hand-rolled line scan (today)","no — 6,613 files refused","ours, 20 sites","none"],["`yaml` CST tokens for the range, our refusal on top","yes, measured byte-identical round trip","ours, unchanged","none — already a direct dep"],["Two-phase lexer of our own","yes, by design","ours","none, and a second YAML implementation to keep in agreement with the installed one"],["`yaml` Document layer / full parse-and-emit","yes","the library's","none, but it regenerates bytes"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"What is already paid for and unused","items":[["`yaml` version declared","^2.9.0","package.json:81"],["Imports of `Parser` or `CST` across src/ and scripts/","0","docs/ENGINE.md:320"],["CST round trip on the refused shape","68 B → 68 B, byte-identical, every token carrying an absolute offset","docs/ENGINE.md:288"],["Publish refusals the shape causes","6,613 files","docs/ENGINE.md:1101"],["What ENGINE §72.2 actually anti-recommends","handing over mutation to a value tree, not reading token offsets","docs/ENGINE.md:650"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Patch, and pre-commit to our own two-phase lexer if the residual exceeds 10","what":"Same gate as b, with a hand-written lexer as the structural answer instead of the CST.","gains":["No obligation to bound someone else's grammar","Full control of the refusal set"],"costs":["A second YAML implementation to keep in step with the installed one","Unmeasured, where the CST route is measured"],"system":"New lexer beside the writer.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Patch the branch, ship, accept whatever residual it leaves","what":"One-line fix to the block scanner, no measurement gate behind it.","gains":["Front door opens this week","Smallest possible diff in the one file with product traffic"],"costs":["The spec's own exit condition becomes decorative","Reopens mid-MVP with no branch pre-agreed"],"system":"One branch in the block scanner.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Patch, red-proof it first, pre-commit to the CST route above a residual of 10","what":"Same patch, but the red proof must fail against today's writer, and the CST route is agreed now rather than later.","gains":["The residual decides, not an opinion","CST offsets come with non-ASCII keys for free","No new dependency: `yaml` is already paid for"],"costs":["Adds about a day","We inherit the duty to refuse every construct the CST accepts"],"system":"CST supplies the byte range; refusal and replacement stay in our code.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Skip the patch and build the CST-backed locator first","what":"No interim fix; the writer stays refusing until the structural work lands.","gains":["One rewrite instead of two","Addresses the class rather than the case"],"costs":["Two founder-weeks before the front door opens","On an estimate ENGINE marks as inference"],"system":"Replaces the block scanner outright.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"c","recCase":["The patch is the availability fix and it is cheap. The structural fix is unmeasured and belongs behind a number.","Pre-committing the branch means nobody re-argues it at the point where the deadline decides.","The CST is the only structural route where the round-trip is already measured and the dependency already installed.","Settle the estimate in the same meeting: DECIDE and ENGINE land near 10 days, the brief says 7 on narrower scope."],"flip":"A patched writer still refusing more than 10 of 7,969 makes the structural fix mandatory rather than conditional.","linked":["E12","E18","E3","FL12"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:214","docs/ENGINE.md:622","docs/ENGINE.md:646","docs/ENGINE.md:487","docs/ENGINE.md:650","docs/ENGINE.md:288","docs/ENGINE.md:320","docs/DECIDE.md:73","docs/DECIDE.md:82","docs/CRITIQUE.md:795","specs/engine/nf-001-zero-indent-sequence.md:47","src/modules/share/domain/splice-frontmatter.ts:197","package.json:81","merged: E4"]},{"id":"E2","cat":"Engine & technical","sub":"Write path","weight":"critical","q":"Does the splice writer get a discriminated-union return before any other engine work, or does the bare string ship one more release?","lede":"A refusal and a successful no-op are the same value, so the product hands out a share link that cannot resolve.","visual":{"kind":"flow","nodes":[{"label":"set public_slug","tone":"neutral"},{"label":"writer refuses","note":"one of 20 `return src` sites","tone":"warn","edge":"same value as success"},{"label":"share-writer commits `next`","note":"no check on the return","tone":"stop"},{"label":"empty commit, slug never written","tone":"stop"},{"label":"makeSetShare returns publicUrl","tone":"stop"},{"label":"the link 404s","tone":"stop"}],"perRow":3,"note":"Every step reports success. Nothing in the chain can tell a refusal from a no-op.","caption":"How a refusal becomes a broken public link"},"stakes":"A stranger is handed a URL that cannot work, from a product whose pitch is that it refuses rather than guesses.","state":["`spliceFrontmatterValue` returns the unmodified input on refusal, at 20 sites (docs/CRITIQUE.md:556).","src/modules/share/infrastructure/share-writer.ts:25 computes `next` and commits it with no check.","The properties panel funnels every edit through one `emit` and drops the refusal at `next === content` (src/modules/preview/presentation/PropertiesPanel.tsx:95).","ENGINE traces the whole chain to a 404 and calls the string return the load-bearing defect (docs/ENGINE.md:502)."],"path":["The string return was the original shape and nothing forced it to change.","The two callers behave differently, so neither one made the gap visible.","The union shape already exists elsewhere in mdmax, so this is alignment rather than invention (docs/ENGINE.md:961)."],"tension":["It is the cheapest fix on the engine list and it is not in MVP-0's 38 points.","Fixing NF-1 first lowers the refusal rate, but the dead-link path stays live while it does.","You cannot tell whether NF-1 worked if success and refusal are the same value."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"What each caller does with a refusal today","cols":["Call site","Behaviour on refusal","User sees"],"rows":[["share/infrastructure/share-writer.ts:25","computes `next`, commits it unconditionally","a public URL that 404s; commit log says it worked"],["preview/presentation/PropertiesPanel.tsx:95, 106, 111, 130","every write goes through `emit`, which returns early at `next === content`","nothing at all — the edit vanishes; the file's own comment concedes it"],["Total `return src` sites in the writer","20","re-counted at HEAD this session; docs/CRITIQUE.md:556"],["Product code paths through the writer","2 files — share-writer.ts and PropertiesPanel.tsx","grep over src/"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"How often the silent path fires","items":[["Foreign-vault publish refusal rate","83.01%","docs/ENGINE.md:487"],["Refusals distinguishable from success today","0","the return type has no room for one"],["Named failure codes mdmax already emits elsewhere","19 typed codes among 32 uppercase symbols","docs/ENGINE.md:978"],["Where the refusal copy already exists and is unrendered","`explainFailure` in shape-gate.ts — zero callers","docs/ENGINE.md:467"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Leave it; treat refusal as out of scope for the pilot","what":"Ship the share button as it behaves today.","gains":["Nothing to build"],"costs":["A pilot user can hand a stranger a broken link on 83% of vaults","Contradicts the one sentence the pitch rests on"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Union return now, before NF-1","what":"`{ ok: true, text } | { ok: false, reason, at, hint }`, with both callers branching on `ok`.","gains":["Every later refusal becomes renderable","NF-1's fix becomes directly measurable","Kills the dead-link path today"],"costs":["Two call sites change","A refusal now needs copy, which nothing renders yet"],"system":"Signature change in the writer; `share-writer` stops committing on refusal.","screens":"Adds a refusal state to the properties panel.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Fix NF-1 and NF-3 first, then the union","what":"Lower the refusal rate before making refusals visible.","gains":["Fewer refusals to render when the union lands","Keeps fix order by user-visible impact"],"costs":["The dead-link path stays live, and it is live today","The NF-1 result is inferred from a byte diff rather than read off a return"],"system":"No change until the fixes land.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Keep the string; add a traced sibling for tests only","what":"A second entry point that returns the union, used by properties and benches, not by the product.","gains":["Unblocks the locality and refusal-safety properties","Zero call-site risk"],"costs":["Leaves the product's silent failure exactly where it is","Two writers to keep in agreement"],"system":"New test-facing export.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["It is the cheapest item on the engine list and the one that makes every other engine fix observable.","It is the only defect here that hands a user a wrong artefact rather than doing nothing.","Do not fix it in the panel: two definitions of one rule is how they drift (docs/ENGINE.md:1012)."],"flip":"Cutting the share path from MVP-0 entirely, which makes option c sufficient for the pilot.","linked":["E1","E16","E3"],"sources":["docs/ENGINE.md:502","docs/ENGINE.md:961","docs/ENGINE.md:1012","docs/ENGINE.md:576","docs/CRITIQUE.md:556","docs/CRITIQUE.md:660","src/modules/share/infrastructure/share-writer.ts:25","src/modules/preview/presentation/PropertiesPanel.tsx:95"],"dupes":{"dropped":["FL8","D16"],"why":"Does the splice writer return a discriminated union so a refusal and a successful no-op stop being the same value. Same spine in all three, with recs a/a/d. Engine mechanism. FL8's placement ladder and D16's rendering site are sub-questions that survive under E2's answer."}},{"id":"E5","cat":"Engine & technical","sub":"Byte claim","weight":"critical","q":"Do we fix the trailing-comment deletion before \"we change only the bytes you touched\" goes on a public page?","lede":"The product's single sentence is refuted by the one engine file carrying real traffic, and it reproduces in one line.","visual":{"kind":"ba","before":{"title":"On disk","lines":[{"t":"share: old  # keep me","mark":"good"},{"t":"b: 2","mark":"neutral"}]},"after":{"title":"After set share=new","lines":[{"t":"share: new","mark":"stop"},{"t":"b: 2","mark":"neutral"}]},"via":"spliceFrontmatterValue","note":"The value emitter replaces from the colon to end of line, so the comment goes with it.","caption":"Reproduced at HEAD: the comment is deleted, silently"},"stakes":"The first person who tests the byte claim on a commented key finds the counter-example in five seconds.","state":["`spliceFrontmatterValue('---\\nshare: old  # keep me\\nb: 2\\n---\\n','share','new')` drops the comment (docs/ENGINE.md:59).","The sibling `spliceFrontmatterKey` promises in its own doc comment that a trailing comment is preserved.","CRITIQUE grades it SEVERE because it is a silent rewrite in the only file with product traffic (docs/CRITIQUE.md:757).","It is not in MVP-0's 38 points."],"path":["The value emitter was written to replace a line, not a token.","No corpus file exercised it, because the byte gate hashes files rather than running the writer.","The demo's beat 5 renames a key and shows the diff, which is exactly the test that finds this (docs/ENGINE.md:1000)."],"tension":["The positioning, the demo and DECIDE's one-paragraph description all rest on this one sentence (docs/DECIDE.md:60).","The fix is confined to the value emitter and its red proof is a two-line fixture.","Narrowing the claim to the key's own line is defensible and gives up the property that makes the engine different."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"The claim and the measured behaviour","cols":["Where the claim is made","Wording","Status"],"rows":[["docs/DECIDE.md:60","\"edits them byte-exactly, changing only the bytes you touched\"","refuted by D10"],["src/modules/share/domain/splice-frontmatter.ts header","the module's stated contract is to leave every other byte untouched","refuted by D10, in the same file"],["docs/ENGINE.md:1000, demo beat 5","\"Everything else in the file is the same byte it was.\"","refuted for any `key: value # comment`"],["`spliceFrontmatterKey` doc comment, same file","\"any trailing comment … preserved\"","the sibling function keeps it; the value setter does not"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"Severity and reach","items":[["CRITIQUE severity","SEVERE","docs/CRITIQUE.md:757"],["Reaches a user today","yes, on any `key: value # comment`","docs/CRITIQUE.md:757"],["In MVP-0's 38 points","no","docs/CRITIQUE.md:757; docs/DECIDE.md:73"],["Product code paths through this function","2 — share-writer.ts and PropertiesPanel.tsx","grep over src/"],["Reproduced at HEAD in this session","yes, with a clean control","live run"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Narrow the public claim to \"only the key's own line\"","what":"Weaken the sentence to what the writer actually does.","gains":["True as written, no engineering"],"costs":["Gives up the property that separates the engine from a serialiser","Every downstream claim gets weaker with it"],"system":"No change.","screens":"Positioning copy.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Fix it, and state the exception in the copy until it lands","what":"Publish the claim with a named exception, remove the exception when the fix ships.","gains":["Honest in the interim"],"costs":["A caveat on the one sentence the whole pitch rests on"],"system":"None.","screens":"Caveat on the landing copy.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Fix it before any public copy makes the byte claim","what":"The emitter replaces the value token, leaving whitespace and any trailing comment intact.","gains":["The sentence becomes true","The demo survives a sceptic re-running it","Two-line red proof"],"costs":["Half a day inside the file with the most traffic"],"system":"Value emitter replaces a token, not a line.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Ship the copy now and fix later","what":"Make the claim, carry the defect.","gains":["No delay"],"costs":["The demo invites the exact test that refutes it","A refuted byte claim is unrecoverable in this category"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"c","recCase":["Everything in the pitch is downstream of one sentence, and this is the only defect that makes it false with no setup at all.","The writer's own doc comment contradicts the behaviour one function away, so the file already disagrees with itself.","The red proof must be shown failing against today's emitter before its pass means anything."],"flip":"Nothing short of dropping the byte claim from the positioning.","linked":["E18","E2","E23","P3"],"sources":["src/modules/share/domain/splice-frontmatter.ts:118","docs/ENGINE.md:59","docs/ENGINE.md:1000","docs/CRITIQUE.md:757","docs/DECIDE.md:60"]},{"id":"E6","cat":"Engine & technical","sub":"Certificate","weight":"critical","q":"Do we run the five-regex bake-off and sharpen the detectors before the certificate is priced into a tier?","lede":"The engine's own audit says the honest product may be a 200-line linter and names the one-day test that settles it. Nobody has run it.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":200,"cols":[{"title":"Certificate as built","tone":"neutral"},{"title":"Five-regex linter","tone":"warn"}],"rows":[{"label":"Explains of all findings","cells":["100%","99.8% on the sample"]},{"label":"Top three constructs cover","cells":["93.8%","93.8%"]},{"label":"DESTROY verdicts in 10,176 blocks","cells":["0","0"]},{"label":"Ruby dependency","cells":["yes, for GitHub Pages","none"]},{"label":"Build cost","cells":["two days, spent","one day, unspent"]},{"label":"Largest attribution bucket","cells":["`__unattributed__`, 392 of 845","n/a"]}],"note":"If agreement exceeds about 95%, the certificate's product claim is whatever is left over.","caption":"What the paid tier is being priced on, against the cheap alternative"},"stakes":"Two tiers are priced on an apparatus that may reduce to five regexes, and the buyer most likely to run the test is a technical one on the second call.","state":["Pro sells `mdmax cert` and review gates at $4–5 per user per month (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:288), and Max sells it again (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:475).","Kill condition 4 fires at 99.8% and three constructs cover 93.8% of attributions (docs/ENGINE.md:899).","DESTROY occurs zero times in 10,176 blocks (docs/ENGINE.md:816, docs/ENGINE.md:899).","`__unattributed__` is the top bucket at 392 of 845 attributions, so the kill condition is currently unreadable (docs/ENGINE.md:540)."],"path":["The certificate was built in two days as a differential apparatus across seven engines.","Only later did anyone run it over third-party vaults and count what the findings reduce to.","Six of 19 detectors carry `provenance: invented`, because no spec defines them (docs/ENGINE.md:578).","The plan's own risk box already quotes the counter-case back at itself (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:512)."],"tension":["Sharpening the detectors is a precondition for reading the kill condition at all, and the audit prices it at two founder-weeks.","Dropping unattributed blocks from the histogram would make the condition fire by construction, which is why it is anti-recommended.","Publishing the result tells a competitor that five regexes approximate us, which §73.5 already concedes."],"evidence":[{"type":"bars","title":"What the certificate's findings reduce to (800-file corpus sample)","note":"Kill condition 4 fires when the top five constructs exceed 80% of BROKEN attributions — the apparatus reduces to a static rule set. docs/ENGINE.md:816-828, 899.","data":[["Top-5 constructs' share of attributions",99.8],["Top-3 constructs (html-comment, yaml-frontmatter, pipe-in-prose)",93.8],["Kill-condition-4 threshold",80]],"unit":"%","threshold":80,"thresholdLabel":"kill condition 4 fires above this"},{"type":"stat","title":"The numbers that make the counter-case","items":[["Blocks / cells in the 800-file run","10,176 / 61,056","docs/ENGINE.md:816"],["DESTROY verdicts","0","docs/ENGINE.md:828, docs/ENGINE.md:899"],["Files carrying a BROKEN block","94.25%","docs/ENGINE.md:820"],["Cost of the bake-off","1 day","docs/ENGINE.md:899"],["Tiers currently priced on the certificate","2 — Pro gates and the Max B2B line","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:288, docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:475"],["Blocker underneath the test","the CLI does not start — see E10","reproduced this session"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"Attribution quality in the completed runs","items":[["`__unattributed__` share, 405-file run","392 of 845 attributions","docs/ENGINE.md:540"],["`__unattributed__` share, four-vault run","393 of 852","docs/ENGINE.md:138"],["Constructs defined","19","counted live in constructs.ts"],["Carrying an `invented` provenance","6 of 19","counted live in constructs.ts"],["Known false-positive shapes that reproduce","6","docs/ENGINE.md:217"],["Detector cost","0.09 ms mean, 11.0 ms worst over 400 files","docs/ENGINE.md:349"],["Audit's own cost for construct completeness","2.0 founder-weeks","docs/ENGINE.md:628"]]},{"type":"table","title":"The six false positives that reproduce today (docs/ENGINE.md:217)","cols":["Shape","Found","Should be"],"rows":[["`html-comment` inside indented code","1","0"],["`angle-bracket-text` inside indented code","1","0"],["`a || b`","1","2"],["`[[A]][[B]]`","1","2"],["one-column table","6","0"],["`coffee` fence","1","0"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Sharpen the detectors, run the bake-off, price only on the residual","what":"Fix the six reproducing false positives, then run both instruments over the same 800 files and compare.","gains":["The kill condition becomes readable","The paid claim becomes a measured residual","Corpus and both instruments are on disk"],"costs":["One day for the bake-off plus the detector work","If agreement is high, two tiers need rewriting before they are sold"],"system":"Detector fixes plus a throwaway linter.","screens":"None.","money":"Decides whether Pro and Max can be priced on the certificate."},{"k":"b","label":"Run it and publish the result whichever way it falls","what":"Same test as a, with the comparison table made public.","gains":["Strongest public position available","Forces the detector work to be defensible"],"costs":["Publishes the five regexes that approximate us","Commits us before the residual is understood"],"system":"Same as a.","screens":"A published comparison page.","money":"None directly."},{"k":"c","label":"Drop the certificate from the paid tiers and ship the five-rule linter","what":"Concede the reduction and sell the cheap thing.","gains":["Cheap, honest and fast","No ruby, no bench, no reproducibility burden"],"costs":["Forfeits the one artefact the plan calls categorically different","A linter has no third-party replay story"],"system":"Deletes the bench and the certificate path.","screens":"Removes the certificate surface.","money":"Removes the Max line as written."},{"k":"d","label":"Price now, run the bake-off later","what":"Keep the tiers as written and test the claim after it is on a pricing page.","gains":["No delay to the commercial plan"],"costs":["A tier built on the apparatus is hard to unwind","The person most likely to run the test is the buyer"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"Prices a tier on an untested claim."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["The test costs a day, both instruments are on disk, and it decides whether a team is paying for an apparatus or a rule set.","Kill condition 4 cannot be read while the biggest bucket means \"we did not look\", so the detector work is part of the same answer.","Pricing first is the expensive order, because a tier on a pricing page is hard to unwind."],"flip":"A large and specific residual, such as the lone-tilde case the construct list did not predict, which keeps the certificate's claim and the tier as written.","linked":["E10","E7","E9","PR21"],"sources":["docs/ENGINE.md:899","docs/ENGINE.md:816","docs/ENGINE.md:828","docs/ENGINE.md:820","docs/ENGINE.md:540","docs/ENGINE.md:578","docs/ENGINE.md:217","docs/ENGINE.md:118","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:288","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:475","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:512","src/modules/mdmax/domain/constructs.ts","merged: E27"],"dupes":{"dropped":["F30","MK22","P21"],"why":"All four ask whether the five-regex bake-off runs before the rendering certificate is priced into a tier. Near-identical options (run the test first / fix the CLI and price now / ship the five-rule linter instead / drop the certificate from the tiers). Engine mechanism, so it belongs in Engine even though Features, Market and Product each ask it; the pricing consequence survives as an edge to PR21."}},{"id":"E7","cat":"Engine & technical","sub":"Certificate","weight":"critical","q":"Do we replace the modal-consensus reference with declared per-construct expectations, keep modal, or stop reporting MUTATE?","lede":"The certificate reports PASS when the engines disagree most, and marks the spec-correct engines corrupt when they are outvoted.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":150,"cols":[{"title":"The engines","tone":"neutral"},{"title":"The certificate says","tone":"stop"},{"title":"What is true","tone":"good"}],"rows":[{"label":"`~~gone~~`","cells":["split 3 / 2 / 2","PASS on all seven cells","three visibly different renderings"]},{"label":"`- [x] done`","cells":["split 4 / 1 / 1 / 1","the three correct ones are CORRUPT","the four have no GFM task lists"]},{"label":"Task lists in the vault run","cells":["172 of 484 attributions","—","not a corner case"]}],"note":"A reference set by majority inverts precisely where the majority is uninformed.","caption":"Two measured cells, wrong in opposite directions"},"stakes":"Every published number and every priced gate inherits a verdict that is inverted at both ends.","state":["A reference is set only when one folded output holds a strict majority with no tie (src/modules/mdmax/application/certify.ts:256).","With no reference, `classify` never reaches MUTATE and every cell reports PASS.","ENGINE records both ends and calls the mechanism symmetric (docs/ENGINE.md:165).","Task lists are 172 of 484 attributions in the vault run (docs/ENGINE.md:141)."],"path":["An earlier design used CommonMark as the oracle and produced 356 MUTATEs on a five-file sample, nearly all false, because the spec has no tables.","The reference moved to the modal folded output, which fixed the false positives and created a symmetric problem.","`void oracle` survives as a caller-settable option that provably changes nothing (docs/CRITIQUE.md:766)."],"tension":["The per-construct map has to be written by hand and maintained, and it needs the CommonMark ambiguity catalogue the gap register says is missing.","Suppressing MUTATE keeps the false PASS, which is the half that makes a PASS meaningless.","Showing divergence with no verdict is always true and gives up the only thing the artefact sells."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"Two measured cells, both wrong (docs/ENGINE.md:149-150)","cols":["Input","Engine split","Certificate says","Truth"],"rows":[["`~~gone~~`","3 / 2 / 2 (`<del>`, `<s>`, literal `~~`)","all 7 cells PASS","maximum disagreement, reported as agreement"],["`- [x] done`","4 / 1 / 1 / 1","remark-app, github-pages and marked = CORRUPT/MUTATE","those three are the ones implementing GFM correctly"],["Share of vault-run attributions that are `task-list`","172 of 484","—","the second-largest attributed construct"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"How much the answer moves with the question","items":[["`AGENTS.md`, 7 targets","PASS 326 / CORRUPT 38","docs/ENGINE.md:808"],["Same file, 4 targets","PASS 202 / CORRUPT 6","docs/ENGINE.md:808 — both MUTATE rows gone"],["Reason","`--targets` is not a filter; consensus is computed over the selected set","docs/ENGINE.md:808"],["Dead option in the code","`void oracle` — a caller-settable `oracleEngineId` that provably changes nothing","src/modules/mdmax/application/certify.ts:259; graded MINOR at docs/CRITIQUE.md:766"],["What the plan already commits to","\"Replace the modal reference with a declared per-construct expectation named in `targets.ts`\"","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:506"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Fall back to the CommonMark oracle","what":"Judge every construct against the spec, tables included.","gains":["One reference, no per-construct map"],"costs":["Produced 356 MUTATEs on a five-file sample, nearly all false","Anti-recommended in the engine doc"],"system":"Reverts an earlier design.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Keep modal consensus, suppress MUTATE in every product surface","what":"Report PASS and CORRUPT only.","gains":["Cheap; nothing structural changes"],"costs":["Keeps the false PASS on maximum disagreement","Loses the only verdict that catches loss with the characters intact"],"system":"Verdict filter at the surface.","screens":"Fewer rows shown.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Report divergence with no verdict","what":"Show the cells and name no winner.","gains":["Always true","No reference to defend"],"costs":["Never actionable","Gives up the stamped verdict a third party can replay"],"system":"Removes `classify`.","screens":"Matrix without verdicts.","money":"Removes the artefact's claim."},{"k":"d","label":"Declared per-construct expectation, named in `targets.ts`","what":"The reference is the set of engines implementing the spec that defines the construct.","gains":["Fixes both ends of the inversion","Makes the verdict explicable to a third party","Keeps MUTATE, which catches structural loss"],"costs":["A construct-to-spec map to write and maintain","Needs the missing CommonMark ambiguity catalogue"],"system":"Reference selection moves out of `certify.ts` into the target table.","screens":"Certificate surface shows why a cell failed.","money":"Precondition for pricing the certificate."}],"rec":"d","recCase":["A PASS that fires precisely where the engines disagree most is not a weaker verdict, it is an inverted one.","The per-construct expectation is the only option that fixes both directions.","Delete `void oracle` in the same commit: a settable option that changes nothing is a trap for the next reader."],"flip":"E6's bake-off showing the apparatus reduces to a rule set, at which point the reference question stops mattering.","linked":["E6","E9"],"sources":["src/modules/mdmax/application/certify.ts:256","src/modules/mdmax/application/certify.ts:259","docs/ENGINE.md:149","docs/ENGINE.md:165","docs/ENGINE.md:141","docs/ENGINE.md:808","docs/CRITIQUE.md:766","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:506"]},{"id":"E12","cat":"Engine & technical","sub":"Enforcement","weight":"critical","q":"Does a CI workflow land in week one before NF-1, and which benches are required on every push?","lede":"There is no continuous verification at all, so every engine fix on the roadmap is riskier than it needs to be.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":180,"cols":[{"title":"Every push","tone":"accent"},{"title":"Nightly","tone":"neutral"},{"title":"Weekly","tone":"sunk"}],"rows":[{"label":"Unit tests and typecheck","cells":["yes","—","—"]},{"label":"Corpus byte pin","cells":["yes, and not in `verify` today","—","—"]},{"label":"Splice oracle over 7,969 files","cells":["yes, as a band not an equality","—","—"]},{"label":"Quadratic canary","cells":["yes, red on purpose until E17","—","—"]},{"label":"Certificate over the corpus","cells":["no","yes","—"]},{"label":"Seven-engine bench with kramdown","cells":["no","yes","full sweep"]}],"note":"A slow required check is a check people learn to skip; the audit names that as the way to train it.","caption":"The split the eight benches are proposed under"},"stakes":"Nothing can stop a regression from being committed, in a repo where four gates have already reported green while blind.","state":["There is no `.github` directory; `npm run verify` chains six steps and does not invoke `corpus` (package.json:19).","ENGINE ranks CI first of nine roadmap items at half a founder-week (docs/ENGINE.md:732).","CRITIQUE independently says the first thing to ship is a workflows file, not NF-1 (docs/CRITIQUE.md:862).","The plan puts it third at one day (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:216); DECIDE prices it at 2 points (docs/DECIDE.md:84)."],"path":["The repo has been audited more often than released; the test suite runs locally and gates nothing.","The eight benches were designed alongside the performance measurements and never wired, because there was no CI to wire them to.","`clean-architecture-report.mjs` once reported zero violations whether it scanned 208 files or none (docs/ENGINE.md:2168)."],"tension":["Writing all eight benches costs more than the CI file itself, and CI is the thing with a multiplier on everything else.","An equality-pinned refusal count goes red the moment a file is added to the corpus, which punishes coverage growth (docs/ENGINE.md:660).","A gate that has never been observed failing is not evidence, which is why the red run matters more than the file."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"What exists and what enforces it","cols":["Artifact","State","Enforced by"],"rows":[["The vitest suite under test/","green locally","nothing"],["`npm run arch` — 208 files, 0 violations, MIN_SCANNED_FILES = 50","green and honest","nothing on push"],["`npm run corpus` — the 8,513-file byte pin","exists as a script","not in the `verify` chain"],["`npm run budget`","`echo 'No bundle budget configured yet — skipping'`","a gate that always passes"],[".github/workflows","does not exist","—"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"How the two reviews rank it","items":[["ENGINE roadmap rank","1 of 9","docs/ENGINE.md:732"],["Cost","0.5 founder-weeks","docs/ENGINE.md:623"],["Plan's fix-list position","#3, 1 day","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:216"],["CRITIQUE's one-sentence verdict","\"the first thing to ship is not NF-1, it is a `.github/workflows` file\"","docs/CRITIQUE.md:862"],["Gates that have reported green while blind","4","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:216; docs/DECIDE.md:84"]]},{"type":"table","title":"The eight benches and what they cost (docs/ENGINE.md:414-423)","cols":["Bench","Corpus","Proposed cadence","Cost / assertion"],"rows":[["gate-throughput","all 8,513","every push","63.5 ms total for the whole corpus"],["gate-ceilings","7 synthetic fixtures","every push","milliseconds"],["quadratic-canary","`[[` × 10–80 KB","every push","asserts slope < 1.3 and 80 KB < 250 ms — today 80 KB measures 2,575.7 ms, so this bench is red against current code until E17 lands"],["offset-integrity","the 475 non-BMP files","every push","fast"],["splice-oracle","all frontmatter files","every push","309 ms measured for set-then-delete across all 8,513"],["fold-idempotence","rendered HTML for all 8,513","nightly","~100 ms of fold over 2.3 MB, measured on 946 files"],["cert-matrix","400-file stratified sample","nightly","minutes"],["cert-full","all 8,513","weekly","unsettled — ENGINE gives 5.6 min, ≈45 min and 92.4 min in three sections; see E8"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"CI first, per-push limited to unit tests plus the corpus byte pin","what":"Ship the workflow in a day; everything else nightly until written.","gains":["Lands this week","No bench authoring on the critical path"],"costs":["The splice oracle and the quadratic canary move off the merge path","Those two are aimed at defect classes that have actually shipped"],"system":"Workflow plus two checks.","screens":"None.","money":"One day."},{"k":"b","label":"No CI; rely on `npm run verify` locally","what":"Today's state.","gains":["Nothing to build"],"costs":["A green local suite cannot stop a bad commit","The corpus gate is not even in the chain"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"CI first with a deliberate red run, and the five-per-push split as written","what":"Workflows file, then the §70.6 split: five benches per push, two nightly, one weekly.","gains":["Every subsequent fix lands with evidence","Per-push cost stays under a second on the green benches","The red run answers this repo's history of blind gates"],"costs":["All eight benches must be written before the split is real","The quadratic canary starts red"],"system":"`.github/workflows`, eight bench scripts, `corpus` added to `verify`.","screens":"None.","money":"Half a week to a day of founder time."},{"k":"d","label":"Everything per push","what":"Every bench required on every merge.","gains":["Nothing can regress unnoticed"],"costs":["Puts a multi-minute certificate on every merge","Trains people to skip the check, which the audit names outright"],"system":"One workflow, no split.","screens":"None.","money":"CI minutes."}],"rec":"c","recCase":["Two independent reviews put this first, for the same reason and at roughly the same price.","The deliberate red run is the part that matters: four gates here have reported green while scanning nothing.","Land the quadratic canary red on purpose until E17 fixes the regex, so the canary is seen failing once.","Three rules travel with the split: assert bands not equalities, preflight the environment, and make each guard fail against the unfixed code first."],"flip":"Bench authoring pushing CI past week one, in which case ship option b's subset and add the rest as they are written.","linked":["D12","E1","E17","E23","E25","PR23"],"sources":["package.json:19","package.json:20","docs/ENGINE.md:656","docs/ENGINE.md:732","docs/ENGINE.md:623","docs/ENGINE.md:414","docs/ENGINE.md:418","docs/ENGINE.md:425","docs/ENGINE.md:427","docs/ENGINE.md:660","docs/ENGINE.md:2168","docs/CRITIQUE.md:862","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:216","docs/DECIDE.md:84","merged: E13"]},{"id":"E17","cat":"Engine & technical","sub":"Correctness","weight":"critical","q":"Do we wire the shape gate at ingress now and replace the quadratic wikilink regex, or accept a 41-second parse on a hostile file?","lede":"The guard the whole performance story rests on has never been called, and the regex it exists to bound runs on every vault open.","visual":{"kind":"flow","nodes":[{"label":"Vault open","tone":"neutral"},{"label":"walk every file","tone":"neutral"},{"label":"WIKILINK_RE, two live copies","note":"quadratic in the number of `[[`","tone":"warn"},{"label":"320 KB of `[[` occupies the app 41 s","tone":"stop"},{"label":"shapeGate: 4 MB, 200,000 lines","note":"written, tested, zero call sites","tone":"sunk"},{"label":"explainFailure: nothing renders it","note":"the refusal copy already exists","tone":"sunk"}],"perRow":3,"note":"Three of the seven ShapeFailure variants have no producer, because the gate they belong to is never called.","caption":"The path every user takes, and the guard that is not on it"},"stakes":"A single hostile file blocks the app on the one path every user takes, and the fix is already written and measured.","state":["`shapeGate`, `MAX_BYTES`, `MAX_LINES` and `BUDGET_MS` have zero product call sites; only `decodeStrict` is imported (docs/ENGINE.md:49).","`WIKILINK_RE` is live at src/modules/vault/infrastructure/markdown-parser.ts:12 and again as `COMBINED_WIKILINK_RE` in the preview.","BUDGET_TIME, PARSER_THREW and WORKER_DIED are declared, rendered and unreachable (docs/ENGINE.md:371).","The gate is measured at 16 ms on a 4 MB string against a 5 ms budget (docs/ENGINE.md:344)."],"path":["Only `decodeStrict` was ever imported, as a `continue` in the snapshot and search-index loops.","The wider gate was written, tested and left.","`explainFailure` produces the refusal copy already and nothing renders it (docs/ENGINE.md:467)."],"tension":["An atomic-group rewrite is not available: JavaScript has none, and the linear scanner is simpler and faster.","Wiring the gate alone refuses the hostile file and leaves the quadratic for everything under the ceiling, which is every corpus file.","Fixing the regex alone leaves the ceilings unenforced and BUDGET_MS documented as enforced by a caller that does not exist."],"evidence":[{"type":"bars","title":"Wikilink regex cost against input size (docs/ENGINE.md:362)","note":"markdown-parser.ts, live and ungated today. Fitted log-log slope k = 1.98 — quadratic. BUDGET_MS.keystroke is 250 ms.","data":[["10 KB",42.9],["40 KB",649.2],["160 KB",10384.3],["320 KB",41527.3]],"unit":"ms","threshold":250,"thresholdLabel":"keystroke budget, 250 ms"},{"type":"stat","title":"What is wired and what is not","items":[["Symbols of 13 engine files reachable from product code","1 — `decodeStrict`","verified by grep over src/"],["`shapeGate` call sites","0","verified"],["ShapeFailure variants no code can produce","3 of 7","docs/ENGINE.md:371"],["Corpus files that reach any gate limit","0 — the corpus proves the happy path only","docs/ENGINE.md:392"],["Gate throughput when it does run","8,513 files in 63.5 ms = 286 MB/s, 0 refusals, 0 throws","docs/ENGINE.md:344"],["Largest corpus file","939,763 bytes — 22.4% of MAX_BYTES","docs/ENGINE.md:392"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Neither; ship and watch","what":"Today's behaviour.","gains":["Nothing to build"],"costs":["A 320 KB file of `[[` occupies the app for 41 seconds","On the path every vault open takes"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Replace the regex only","what":"Remove the worst case without introducing a gate.","gains":["Kills the availability problem","No new refusal states to design"],"costs":["The 4 MB and 200,000-line ceilings stay unenforced","BUDGET_MS keeps being documented as enforced by nobody"],"system":"One scanner.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Wire the gate only","what":"Refuse oversized files, leave the regex.","gains":["Refuses the hostile file before the parse","Smallest change"],"costs":["The quadratic stays for everything under the ceiling","That is every file in the corpus"],"system":"Two call sites.","screens":"Refusal state.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Wire `shapeGate` at both ingress sites, replace the regex with a scanner","what":"Two call sites and one scanner, plus rendering `explainFailure` in the file tree.","gains":["Bounds the hostile case at O(limit) instead of quadratic","Gives the three unreachable refusal variants a producer","The gate is written and measured already, so the cost is wiring"],"costs":["Two ingress sites change","Refusal copy must be rendered somewhere"],"system":"Gate at snapshot and search-index; one scanner replaces two regex copies.","screens":"File tree shows a refused file with a reason.","money":"None."}],"rec":"d","recCase":["This is the only engine defect that is a live availability problem on a path every user takes.","The gate that fixes it is already written and measured, so the cost is wiring rather than design.","Render `explainFailure` at the same time; the copy exists and nothing shows it."],"flip":"A pilot that ships without vault ingest, which shrinks the exposure enough for option c alone.","linked":["E12","E15","E23"],"sources":["src/modules/vault/infrastructure/markdown-parser.ts:12","src/modules/preview/presentation/markdown/wikilinks.tsx:10","src/modules/vault/application/get-snapshot.ts:172","src/modules/vault/infrastructure/search-index.ts:175","docs/ENGINE.md:49","docs/ENGINE.md:344","docs/ENGINE.md:362","docs/ENGINE.md:371","docs/ENGINE.md:467","docs/ENGINE.md:469"]},{"id":"E18","cat":"Engine & technical","sub":"Measurement","weight":"critical","q":"What has to be true before any engine number is published — a second population, the two remaining gates, or nothing?","lede":"Every engine number is measured on seven Obsidian vaults, one wiki is 77% of the files, and the plan's own buyer is not in that population.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":190,"cols":[{"title":"Seven Obsidian vaults","tone":"warn"},{"title":"READMEs, prior audit","tone":"neutral"}],"rows":[{"label":"Blocks BROKEN on at least one target","cells":["18.74%","5.78%"]},{"label":"Ratio between the two populations","cells":["3.24× on the same code","—"]},{"label":"YAML frontmatter present","cells":["7,969 of 8,513 files","none"]},{"label":"Task lists in the attributions","cells":["172 of 484","none"]},{"label":"Contains the plan's buyer","cells":["no","closer"]}],"note":"The population moved the headline number by 3.24× with the code untouched.","caption":"What the pinned corpus is answering, against what the plan is asking"},"stakes":"Three headline numbers have already been withdrawn in this programme, and the next one is measured on an audience the route abandons.","state":["`SOURCES.json` pins 7 vaults, 8,513 files; one wiki contributes 6,586 of them.","The plan states the caveat itself: the refusal rate is a property of those vaults (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:514).","The record forbids publishing a fidelity or coverage percentage until four gates land (docs/ENGINE.md:207).","Gates 1 and 2 are done, with both red proofs on disk, and §68.5 still calls them ghosts (docs/ENGINE.md:211)."],"path":["The vaults were chosen because they were real, third-party and pinnable by commit. Nobody chose them to represent the buyer.","The ban was written after every fidelity percentage in circulation turned out to be measured on a population the product does not serve (docs/ENGINE.md:134).","NF-4's residual assertion does not exist, and the whole-corpus behavioural sweep exists only as a scratch script (docs/ENGINE.md:214)."],"tension":["The corpus contains zero BOM, zero CRLF, zero bare-CR and zero unterminated-frontmatter files, so three of four named defects sit in rows with a count of zero.","A fidelity percentage with the refusal rate omitted is the exact shape of the three claims already withdrawn (docs/ENGINE.md:220).","Adding a second pinned population is cheap and keeps the existing byte gate, which is the only standing regression net."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"The pinned corpus, by vault (test/corpus/foreign/SOURCES.json, recomputed)","cols":["Vault","Files","Share"],"rows":[["community-archive_obsidian-hub","6,586","77.36%"],["oldwinter__knowledge-garden","961","11.29%"],["quanru_obsidian-example-lifeos","540","6.34%"],["s-blu_obsidian_dataview_example_vault","264","3.10%"],["kepano_kepano-obsidian","103","1.21%"],["erazlogo_obsidian-history-vault","40","0.47%"],["CyanVoxel_Obsidian-Vault-Template","19","0.22%"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"What the corpus cannot see (docs/ENGINE.md:1746-1756)","items":[["Files with a leading BOM","0","the BOM defect was unreachable from the corpus"],["Files with CRLF anywhere","0","the CRLF branch is corpus-untested"],["Files with a bare CR","0","NF-3 is corpus-unreachable and still broken"],["Files with unterminated frontmatter","0","that refusal is corpus-unreachable"],["Files with a zero-indent block sequence","6,613","the refusal driver — an Obsidian default"],["Same code, README population","5.78% blocks BROKEN","docs/ENGINE.md:134"],["Same code, Obsidian vault population","18.74%","docs/ENGINE.md:139"]]},{"type":"table","title":"The four gates that lift the ban (docs/ENGINE.md:211-214), re-checked at HEAD","cols":["Gate","State today","Evidence"],"rows":[["NF-1 zero-indent red proof","exists — 99 lines","test/corpus/foreign/nf-001-red-proof.test.ts; ENGINE §68.5 still calls it a ghost"],["NF-3 bare-CR red proof","exists — 82 lines","test/corpus/foreign/nf-003-red-proof.test.ts; same stale row"],["NF-4 unaddressable-key residual","does not exist","docs/ENGINE.md:213"],["Whole-corpus behavioural sweep","scratch script only","docs/ENGINE.md:214"],["`npm run spec`","4 specs, 0 errors, 0 warnings","run in this session"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"Why the ban exists","items":[["Headline numbers withdrawn in this programme","3","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:13"],["Same code, README population","5.78% blocks BROKEN","docs/ENGINE.md:134"],["Same code, Obsidian vault population","18.74%","docs/ENGINE.md:139"],["Ratio","3.24x, from the population alone","docs/ENGINE.md:141"],["Files the writer can currently address","17%","docs/ENGINE.md:220"],["What the audit says not to gate on","tests 5–8 — they protect the certificate, which is not yet customer-facing","docs/ENGINE.md:220"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Keep the standing ban; describe the mechanism only","what":"No measured percentage leaves the building.","gains":["No withdrawal risk"],"costs":["No falsifiable claim, which is the one thing separating the engine from an assertion"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Publish now, always with the denominator and the population named","what":"State the number and the vaults it came from in the same sentence.","gains":["Gets a checkable number out","Free"],"costs":["Risks a fourth withdrawal","Qualifies every headline with an audience the plan is not targeting"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Second population and the two remaining gates, then publish as one fraction","what":"Pin agent-written repos and third-party READMEs, land NF-4's residual assertion and the corpus sweep, publish fidelity and refusal together.","gains":["The number becomes about the buyer","Both populations publishable side by side","Keeps the existing 8,513-file byte gate"],"costs":["Delays the first public engine number by days","§68.5's stale rows have to be corrected in the same pass"],"system":"A second pinned corpus and two tests.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Replace the corpus with an agent-written one","what":"Retire the vaults and measure only the buyer's files.","gains":["Aligns the measurement with the route"],"costs":["Discards the pinned byte gate that took real work to assemble","Loses the population where the hard cases live"],"system":"New corpus, new hashes.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"c","recCase":["The corpus answers a question about Obsidian users while the plan asks one about developers running agents.","The same code moved 3.24× when the population changed, so the population is the finding.","Two of the four gates already exist, which the audit text has not caught up with, so the remaining cost is small.","Hold to the single-fraction form: fidelity without the refusal rate is the shape of the three withdrawals."],"flip":"The pilot buyer turning out to be the Obsidian user, in which case the corpus is already right and option b is enough.","linked":["E1","E23","E5","R7"],"sources":["test/corpus/foreign/SOURCES.json","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:514","docs/ENGINE.md:134","docs/ENGINE.md:139","docs/ENGINE.md:141","docs/ENGINE.md:207","docs/ENGINE.md:211","docs/ENGINE.md:213","docs/ENGINE.md:214","docs/ENGINE.md:220","docs/ENGINE.md:1746","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:13","merged: E19"]},{"id":"E3","cat":"Engine & technical","sub":"Write path","weight":"high","q":"Do we replace SAFE_KEY with the addressability predicate, or keep an ASCII allowlist that cannot address 942 files?","lede":"The key grammar excludes a space, which is the shape two of the corpus's largest vaults use for their commonest keys.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":190,"cols":[{"title":"Keep SAFE_KEY","tone":"warn"},{"title":"Widen the class","tone":"stop"},{"title":"Addressability predicate","tone":"accent"}],"rows":[{"label":"`date created`","cells":["refused","writable","writable"]},{"label":"`分类`","cells":["refused","writable","writable"]},{"label":"Files made writable of 942","cells":["0","most","936"]},{"label":"Sequence item mis-spliced","cells":["never","5 corpus files","never"]},{"label":"Definitions of the rule","cells":["two: engine and panel","two","one"]}],"note":"Widening the character class buys the same files and introduces a structural corruption path.","caption":"Three ways to decide whether a key can be addressed"},"stakes":"Two vaults in our own corpus stay read-only, and the CJK population that produced the hardest cases cannot be written at all.","state":["`SAFE_KEY = /^[A-Za-z0-9_.$-]+$/` at src/modules/share/domain/splice-frontmatter.ts:53, copied at five sites in the panel.","942 files carry at least one unaddressable key, 11.8% of frontmatter files (docs/ENGINE.md:1093).","ENGINE §75 designs the replacement and measures it: 936 files become writable, 6 stay refused (docs/ENGINE.md:1115).","0 keys in the corpus are quoted on disk, so the quoting cases are theoretical today (docs/ENGINE.md:1094)."],"path":["The regex is narrow on purpose: the module scans lines it did not write.","Widening it naively lets a sequence item at column zero be read as a key.","The panel grew a second copy of the rule because the engine's copy was not exported as a decision."],"tension":["The honest boundary is what the locator can find unambiguously, not which characters are safe.","Codepoint equality with NFC normalisation of the request is the spec-conformant answer, and it is a commitment.","The predicate costs about what widening the class costs, and does not add a corruption path."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"What SAFE_KEY cannot address, measured on the pinned corpus","items":[["Top-level key lines","29,293","docs/ENGINE.md:1089"],["Occurrences failing SAFE_KEY","2,452 = 8.4%","docs/ENGINE.md:1092 (§68.5 quotes 2,447/8.35% — the 5-line gap is the aliases sequence items counted below)"],["Files with at least one unaddressable key","942 = 11.8% of frontmatter files","docs/ENGINE.md:1093"],["`date created` / `date modified`","812 / 811 files","docs/ENGINE.md:1105"],["`分类`","232 files","docs/ENGINE.md:1105"],["Files unlocked by the §75.5 predicate","936 of 942 = 99.36%","docs/ENGINE.md:1115"],["— of which the predicate alone is enough","750","docs/ENGINE.md:1113-1120"],["— of which NF-1 must also land before publish succeeds","186","docs/ENGINE.md:1113-1120"],["Quoted keys anywhere in 8,513 files","0","docs/ENGINE.md:1094"]]},{"type":"table","title":"Why widening the character class is not the same fix","cols":["Approach","Unlocks","Fails on"],"rows":[["Widen the class to allow spaces and non-ASCII","most of the 942","5 corpus lines that are sequence items under `aliases:` would be read as top-level keys and spliced into"],["Predicate: NFC, one line, no control char, no edge space, no `: `, no ` #`, no leading indicator","936 of 942","6 files — 5 sequence items and one template line, all correct refusals"],["Keep SAFE_KEY","0","942 files, and the panel keeps a second copy of the rule"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Widen the character class to permit spaces and non-ASCII","what":"Same regex, more characters allowed.","gains":["Cheapest possible change","Reaches most of the same files"],"costs":["Splices into a sequence item on 5 corpus files","That is structural corruption, not a refusal"],"system":"One regex.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Predicate, but ASCII-only for the pilot","what":"Ship addressability for spaces and dots, defer non-ASCII keys.","gains":["Reaches the 1,623 `date created` and `date modified` occurrences"],"costs":["Leaves the Chinese vault refused","That vault generated most of the CJK evidence"],"system":"Predicate with a character gate.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Adopt the §75.5 predicate, one definition, both modules","what":"Addressability becomes a function over what the locator can find, returning a typed refusal.","gains":["936 of 942 files become writable, measured","One definition of the rule, not two","Non-ASCII keys come with it"],"costs":["Commits us to codepoint equality with NFC on the request","The test that must fail first has to be shown failing"],"system":"New `addressableKey` in the engine; the panel's five call sites move to it.","screens":"Properties panel renders a refusal kind instead of a red border.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Keep SAFE_KEY and refuse those keys with a named message","what":"No new capability; the refusal becomes explicable.","gains":["Honest, and cheap once E2's union lands"],"costs":["11.8% of frontmatter files stay unwritable","Two corpus vaults are effectively read-only"],"system":"Refusal reason only.","screens":"Refusal copy in the panel.","money":"None."}],"rec":"c","recCase":["The design is written, measured against the corpus and carries its own test set, including the one test that must fail first (docs/ENGINE.md:1250).","It costs about what option b costs and does not introduce a corruption path.","Three quarters of the gain lands without waiting on NF-1, which is worth carrying into the sequence."],"flip":"A real vault with in-file case-duplicate or non-NFC keys, which forces the equality rule to be re-decided first.","linked":["E1","E33","E36"],"sources":["src/modules/share/domain/splice-frontmatter.ts:53","src/modules/preview/presentation/PropertiesPanel.tsx:105","docs/ENGINE.md:1043","docs/ENGINE.md:1092","docs/ENGINE.md:1093","docs/ENGINE.md:1094","docs/ENGINE.md:1115","docs/ENGINE.md:1250","docs/ENGINE.md:213"]},{"id":"E8","cat":"Engine & technical","sub":"Certificate","weight":"high","q":"What does it take for a third party to recompute a certificate — which engines run when, and which dependencies get declared and pinned?","lede":"One of seven engines costs forty times the other six combined, and the function that defines what PASS means is not in our dependency list.","visual":{"kind":"arch","layers":[{"label":"Ambient on the machine","items":["ruby at /opt/homebrew","kramdown 2.5.2 gems"],"side":"no Gemfile.lock","tone":"stop"},{"label":"Hoisted, undeclared","items":["entities@8.0.0","marked"],"side":"resolve out of node_modules","tone":"stop"},{"label":"Declared in package.json","items":["yaml","github-slugger"],"side":"pinned","tone":"good"},{"label":"Stamped in the certificate","items":["mdmax/fold@1","benchId"],"side":"does not move when the above do","tone":"accent"}],"note":"`escapeText` from `entities` is the definition of PASS. A silent major bump changes every verdict without moving the stamp.","caption":"What a verdict actually depends on, against what the stamp records"},"stakes":"A stamped verdict whose meaning can change without the stamp moving is not an auditable artefact, and it is the thing we would sell.","state":["`kramdown-jekyll` is in `BENCH_ENGINE_IDS` and runs through `spawnSync` on an ambient ruby (src/modules/mdmax/infrastructure/bench.ts:52).","103 files take 338 ms with six engines and 14,020 ms with seven — 41.5× (docs/ENGINE.md:542).","`entities` and `marked` appear in neither `dependencies` nor `devDependencies` (docs/ENGINE.md:229, docs/ENGINE.md:230).","There is no Gemfile, no Gemfile.lock and no .ruby-version, so gem versions come from the machine (docs/ENGINE.md:231)."],"path":["GitHub Pages is the one target no JS engine models, which is why `Engine.options` is hashed into `benchId` at all.","`entities` was never declared because it always resolved; nothing distinguishes a hoisted dependency from a declared one.","`marked` has exactly one dependent in the lockfile, `mermaid`, so a diagram-library upgrade silently changes `benchId`."],"tension":["Interactive surfaces need single-digit milliseconds per file; the published artefact needs the GitHub Pages row.","Under `npm ci --omit=dev` the production domain layer loses its import entirely.","ENGINE gives three different whole-corpus cost figures in three sections, so the nightly cannot be sized until one basis is picked."],"evidence":[{"type":"bars","title":"Wall time for the same certification run (docs/ENGINE.md:542)","note":"kepano vault, 103 files. The seven-engine number is 41.5x the six-engine one; the difference is one spawnSync per block.","data":[["6 JS engines (ms)",338],["7 engines with kramdown (ms)",14020]],"unit":"ms"},{"type":"stat","title":"Cost, reproducibility, and one unresolved number","items":[["kramdown share of wall time","96.9%","docs/ENGINE.md:830"],["Per-block cost","51.2 ms","docs/ENGINE.md:830"],["Whole corpus, JS only","34.9 s","docs/ENGINE.md:870"],["Whole corpus, with kramdown","the document gives three answers — ≈45 min (docs/ENGINE.md:542), 92.4 min (docs/ENGINE.md:871), and 5.6 min (docs/ENGINE.md:354, quoted again at :427)","all three are marked [derived] from different bases; this must be re-derived once before it is used to size a nightly job"],["Gemfile.lock / .ruby-version in repo","absent","docs/ENGINE.md:231; verified — no such files"],["Cost if one ruby process is kept alive","~2 ms/block","docs/ENGINE.md:356"]]},{"type":"table","title":"The engine's real dependency graph vs the declared one","cols":["Package","Used by","Declared in package.json","Failure it enables"],"rows":[["`entities@8.0.0`","fold.ts, verdict.ts","no — hoisted from parse5 and markdown-it, marked dev","`escapeText` changes; every verdict changes; `mdmax/fold@1` does not move"],["`marked`","one of seven bench engines","no — one lockfile dependent, `mermaid`","a mermaid upgrade silently changes `benchId`"],["`github-slugger@2.0.0`","slug.ts","yes, package.json:55","—"],["ruby + kramdown 2.5.2 + kramdown-parser-gfm 1.1.0","bench.ts","no Gemfile, no Gemfile.lock, no .ruby-version — verified","the seventh engine's version is whatever the machine has"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"Cost to close","items":[["Declare `entities` and `marked`","2 lines of package.json","docs/ENGINE.md:229-230"],["Add the entities version to the fold stamp","1 field","docs/ENGINE.md:218"],["Add a Gemfile.lock","1 file","docs/ENGINE.md:231"],["Reproducibility gaps closed by those three","3 of the 5 in the table","docs/ENGINE.md:228-232 — the other two are the CLI (E10) and the certificate schema, which needs a version bump"],["What the plan already budgets","0.5 days, for the dependency half only","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:225"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Build the persistent-ruby protocol first","what":"Keep one ruby process alive behind a line-delimited protocol.","gains":["Takes the cert from 60.7 ms/block to roughly 2 ms","Makes kramdown affordable everywhere"],"costs":["New infrastructure before the first certificate has run end to end","Does not touch the undeclared dependencies"],"system":"New subprocess protocol in infrastructure.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Six JS engines interactively, the seventh nightly, every dependency pinned","what":"Split the bench by surface, add a Gemfile.lock, declare `entities` and `marked`, and put the `entities` version in the fold stamp.","gains":["Interactive paths stay in single-digit milliseconds per file","Three of five reproducibility gaps close for about half a day","The GitHub Pages row survives in the published artefact"],"costs":["Two run modes to keep in step","One whole-corpus figure must be picked and re-derived"],"system":"Bench split by mode; dependency and stamp changes.","screens":"None.","money":"Precondition for selling a replayable certificate."},{"k":"c","label":"Keep all seven everywhere and declare nothing","what":"Today's behaviour, unchanged.","gains":["Nothing to build"],"costs":["A 16-second run behind a single large file rules out every interactive surface","Any claim that the engine drops into another host fails on the first `npm ci`"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Drop kramdown; mark github-pages declared rather than local","what":"Six JS engines everywhere, no ruby anywhere.","gains":["Removes the ruby dependency and the reproducibility hole","One run mode"],"costs":["Gives up measurement on the surface most users publish to","Uncertifiable share goes from 8 of 15 to 9 of 15"],"system":"Bench loses an engine; `targets.ts` changes a fidelity value.","screens":"One fewer row.","money":"Weakens the certificate's claim."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["The numbers already say it: interactive surfaces need the six, the published artefact needs the seven, nothing needs both at once.","The dependency half is the cheapest item on the engine list and the plan already budgets it (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:225).","Do not let three conflicting whole-corpus figures survive the meeting; pick a basis and re-derive once."],"flip":"The certificate never becoming a published artefact, which makes option b cheaper and turns GitHub Pages into a declaration like the other eight.","linked":["E10","E6","E9"],"sources":["src/modules/mdmax/infrastructure/bench.ts:52","src/modules/mdmax/infrastructure/bench.ts:74","docs/ENGINE.md:542","docs/ENGINE.md:354","docs/ENGINE.md:356","docs/ENGINE.md:229","docs/ENGINE.md:230","docs/ENGINE.md:231","docs/ENGINE.md:218","docs/ENGINE.md:2125","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:225","package.json:55","merged: E11"]},{"id":"E9","cat":"Engine & technical","sub":"Certificate","weight":"high","q":"Which certificate surface reaches an outsider first — the MCP tool, a public web checker with the dataset, a GitHub Action, or none until the bake-off?","lede":"The certificate is a wedge only if a stranger can run it on their own files, and every candidate surface imports a CLI that does not start.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":170,"cols":[{"title":"MCP tool","tone":"accent"},{"title":"Web checker","tone":"neutral"},{"title":"GitHub Action","tone":"warn"}],"rows":[{"label":"Effort, engineer-days","cells":["2","4","3"]},{"label":"Consumer","cells":["the agent, before it writes","a stranger, once","someone else's CI"]},{"label":"Rendering work","cells":["none","a full UI","a log format"]},{"label":"First impression","cells":["a summary and non-PASS cells","94.25% of real files show BROKEN","a red build on adoption day"]},{"label":"Blocked by","cells":["the CLI fix","the CLI fix and the dataset","the CLI fix and a baseline"]}],"note":"Returning a whole certificate from an MCP call is a 24.4× blowup on the source, so the tool must summarise.","caption":"The three live surfaces, priced in the engine doc"},"stakes":"Build the wrong surface first and we spend a week making a claim reachable that the bake-off may retire.","state":["No certificate surface exists; the engine doc ranks five and prices each (docs/ENGINE.md:836).","94.25% of real files carry a BROKEN block, so a default-failing Action goes red on adoption day (docs/ENGINE.md:820, docs/ENGINE.md:841).","The badge is anti-recommended outright: a verdict is a function of the target set, the bench id and the fold version (docs/ENGINE.md:905).","The dataset would be derived verdicts keyed by the source sha256, never the source text (docs/ENGINE.md:866)."],"path":["The certificate was built as an audit tool, so its artefact is already machine-shaped.","That is why the agent-facing surface is the cheapest of the five.","Our own `frontmatter-app` target is the loudest offender on hand-authored prose, 25 of 38 CORRUPT cells on AGENTS.md (docs/ENGINE.md:830)."],"tension":["The dataset is the strongest top-of-funnel artefact and it publishes our own renderer as the loudest row until the hard-wrap choice is recorded in the target's options.","Publishing also dates the eight declared rows, which is the only forcing function `DECLARED_LAST_VERIFIED` currently has.","Every surface here is downstream of one day of CLI work."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"What publishing costs and exposes","items":[["Compute, JS only","34.9 s","docs/ENGINE.md:870"],["Compute, with kramdown","unsettled — see E8; ENGINE gives 92.4 min, ≈45 min and 5.6 min in three places","docs/ENGINE.md:871, :542, :354"],["Artifact size uncompressed","0.35–0.43 GB","docs/ENGINE.md:872"],["Surfaces that are declarations, not measurements","8 of 15 = 53.3%","docs/ENGINE.md:69; src/modules/mdmax/domain/targets.ts:125"],["Declaration staleness today","39 days","DECLARED_LAST_VERIFIED = 2026-08-01, computed against 2026-09-09"],["Files carrying a BROKEN block","94.25%","docs/ENGINE.md:820"],["`frontmatter-app` CORRUPT cells on AGENTS.md","25 of 38, all from our own soft-line-break choice","docs/ENGINE.md:830"]]},{"type":"table","title":"The five surfaces, ranked (docs/ENGINE.md:836-843)","cols":["Surface","Days","For","Measured failure mode"],"rows":[["Make the CLI executable","1","everything else imports it","fails today with ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND; do not ship as npx until the frontmatter-app MUTATE row is fixed or excluded"],["MCP tool `certify_markdown`","2","an agent that can act on VOID and LEAK before writing","whole certificate is 24.4x source size — return summary plus non-PASS cells"],["Public web checker","4","top of funnel; 4.1 ms/file makes a request free","kramdown must not sit behind it synchronously at 51.2 ms/block"],["GitHub Action","3","repeat exposure inside someone else's CI","default-fail is a red build on adoption day for 94.25% of files"],["In-editor panel","8","retention; the fix is one keystroke away","a panel showing 25 MUTATEs trains its own dismissal"],["Badge","1","nothing defensible","anti-recommended outright — target subsetting alone moved AGENTS.md from 38 CORRUPT to 6"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Public web checker, with the corpus dataset published beside it","what":"Paste or drop a file, get the block-by-target matrix, with the pinned-corpus verdicts published as a citable dataset.","gains":["Best top-of-funnel and a citable number","Dates the eight declared rows publicly"],"costs":["Four days of UI","A stranger's first impression is a 94% broken rate on their own files","Publishes our own renderer as the loudest row until it is fixed"],"system":"Web surface plus a 0.35–0.43 GB artefact to host.","screens":"A checker page and a dataset page.","money":"Hosting cost for the artefact."},{"k":"b","label":"GitHub Action first, with a baseline file, failing only on new CORRUPT and worse","what":"Runs inside someone else's CI and reports regressions rather than state.","gains":["Repeat exposure inside a repo we do not own","Closest surface to the priced Max gate"],"costs":["Needs the baseline mechanism built or the default is a red build","Three days plus the CLI fix"],"system":"Action wrapper plus baseline storage.","screens":"CI output only.","money":"The surface the Max line is priced on."},{"k":"c","label":"None until the bake-off settles what the certificate claims","what":"No distribution surface until E6 returns.","gains":["No channel built for a claim that may reduce to five regexes"],"costs":["Delays every distribution surface by the bake-off","Nothing for a stranger to run"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"MCP tool first, returning a summary plus non-PASS cells","what":"One tool call that certifies a path and returns the verdict the agent can act on.","gains":["Cheapest of the four at two days","No rendering work","Puts the verdict in front of the agent before it writes"],"costs":["Reaches only people already running agents","No public artefact to cite"],"system":"MCP tool over the CLI path.","screens":"None.","money":"None directly; it is the integration story."}],"rec":"d","recCase":["The MCP tool is the cheapest, needs no rendering, and its consumer is the one that can act on a verdict before the bytes are written.","It depends on nothing but the CLI fix, which is already recommended first.","Sequence whichever surface goes first behind E6, so we are not building a channel for an untested claim.","If the dataset ships, record that `frontmatter-app` hard-wraps in the target's option set rather than widening the fold until the finding disappears."],"flip":"A pilot buyer who does not run agents, which moves the web checker's top-of-funnel value ahead of the MCP tool.","linked":["E10","E6","E8","G20"],"sources":["docs/ENGINE.md:836","docs/ENGINE.md:839","docs/ENGINE.md:840","docs/ENGINE.md:841","docs/ENGINE.md:862","docs/ENGINE.md:905","docs/ENGINE.md:866","docs/ENGINE.md:870","docs/ENGINE.md:872","docs/ENGINE.md:820","docs/ENGINE.md:830","docs/ENGINE.md:911","docs/ENGINE.md:69","src/modules/mdmax/domain/targets.ts:24","src/modules/mdmax/domain/targets.ts:125","merged: E30"]},{"id":"E10","cat":"Engine & technical","sub":"Wiring","weight":"high","q":"Is making `mdmax cert` runnable, and running the fold over the whole corpus, the first engine commit?","lede":"The certificate is the only thing that can execute twelve of thirteen engine files, and it has never executed them.","visual":{"kind":"flow","nodes":[{"label":"node scripts/mdmax-cert.mjs","tone":"neutral"},{"label":"ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND","note":"domain/offsets, missing extension","tone":"stop"},{"label":"ts-resolve.mjs: no importer","tone":"warn"},{"label":"12 engine files unreachable","tone":"stop"},{"label":"bake-off, fold run, MCP tool, dataset","note":"all blocked behind one day","tone":"sunk"}],"perRow":3,"note":"Every corpus number in circulation was produced by hand-writing the resolve hook the repo already contains.","caption":"One missing register, five blocked decisions"},"stakes":"Every engine number going into the other decisions is produced by a hook nobody has committed.","state":["`node scripts/mdmax-cert.mjs` fails with `ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND` on `.../mdmax/domain/offsets` (docs/ENGINE.md:526).","`cert` is not one of package.json's 26 scripts (package.json:8).","`scripts/mdmax-cert.mjs:195` calls `paint(s.padEnd(18))` and `paint` compares against the unpadded value, so every verdict prints red (docs/ENGINE.md:1004).","`mdmax/fold@1` has been run four times, never over all 8,513 files, and the samples disagree by nine points (docs/ENGINE.md:819, docs/ENGINE.md:138)."],"path":["The commit that shipped the CLI met its two-day estimate and the artefact has never run.","`scripts/ts-resolve.mjs` was written to supply the missing extension and the `@/` alias, and no file imports it.","The audit hand-wrote a resolve hook to produce any number at all (docs/ENGINE.md:718)."],"tension":["The plan lists this as fix #10 at one day, behind nine other items (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:224).","The full JS-only fold costs 34.9 seconds of compute, so the only real cost is the CLI fix (docs/ENGINE.md:870).","Four samples give 24.35%, 25.26%, 33.45% and 18.74%, and there is no principled reason to pick one."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"State of the CLI at HEAD","items":[["`node scripts/mdmax-cert.mjs <file>`","ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND on `.../mdmax/domain/offsets`","reproduced this session"],["`cert` in package.json scripts","absent — 26 scripts, none is cert","verified; package.json:8"],["Importers of scripts/ts-resolve.mjs anywhere in the repo","0 — it is named only in prose","verified by grep"],["Works with `node --import ./scripts/ts-resolve.mjs`","yes — all seven engines load, including kramdown 2.5.2","docs/ENGINE.md:526"],["Second defect found while demoing","`paint(s.padEnd(18))` compares against the padded string, so every verdict renders red including PASS","scripts/mdmax-cert.mjs:195; docs/ENGINE.md:1004"],["Days since the commit claiming it landed","37 at the time the plan was written","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:224"]]},{"type":"table","title":"Four fold runs, four answers","cols":["Sample","Files","Blocks BROKEN","Source"],"rows":[["Every-nth stride","300","24.35%","docs/ENGINE.md:819"],["Every-nth stride","800","25.26%","docs/ENGINE.md:819"],["Three vaults (kepano, erazlogo, s-blu)","405","33.45%","docs/ENGINE.md:534"],["Four vaults, all seven targets","419","33.48%","docs/ENGINE.md:138"],["Four vaults, excluding frontmatter-app","419","18.74%","docs/ENGINE.md:139"],["Whole corpus","8,513","never run","docs/ENGINE.md:718"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"What it costs to settle","items":[["Full corpus, JS engines only","34.9 s","docs/ENGINE.md:870"],["Full corpus, with kramdown","unsettled — see E8","docs/ENGINE.md:871, :542, :354"],["Prerequisite","a runnable CLI — E10","reproduced failing this session"],["Roadmap rank of running it","2 of 9, ahead of the YAML defects","docs/ENGINE.md:733"],["Audit's framing","\"an unknown, not a task — the corpus exists, the fold exists, nobody has pressed the button\"","docs/ENGINE.md:718"],["What the result also sizes","the 1.5 founder-weeks costed for fixing the fold, which may turn out to be zero","docs/ENGINE.md:718"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Register the resolve hook, add a `cert` script, fix padEnd, run the full fold","what":"One day of wiring, then one 35-second run that replaces four disagreeing samples.","gains":["Unblocks the bake-off, the dataset, the MCP tool and twelve unreachable files","Replaces four numbers with one carrying a corpus id","Also sizes the fold-fix budget, which may be zero"],"costs":["One day ahead of user-visible fixes"],"system":"Node register hook, one script entry, one comparison fix.","screens":"The demo stops printing every verdict red.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"After NF-1 and NF-3","what":"Keep fix order by user impact; wire the CLI in week two.","gains":["User-visible refusals fall first"],"costs":["The corpus numbers going into the NF-1 decision stay hand-produced","Five other decisions stay blocked"],"system":"No change until then.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Delete the CLI; certify only under vitest","what":"Remove the surface that does not work.","gains":["Removes a broken entry point","The tests already reach the code"],"costs":["Gives up third-party reproducibility, which is the certificate's whole basis","Every distribution surface in E9 dies with it"],"system":"Deletes the script.","screens":"None.","money":"Removes the certificate as a sellable artefact."},{"k":"d","label":"Accept the 800-file stride sample as the standing fold figure","what":"Wire the CLI later and publish the sample in the meantime.","gains":["A number today with defensible sampling"],"costs":["Differs from the vault-specific runs by nine points","Any reader comparing them sees a contradiction"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["One day converts twelve unreachable files into runnable ones, and the padEnd bug currently prints every verdict red, including the passes.","The fold run is the cheapest information on the roadmap and has been outstanding for months.","Both the engine audit and the certificate section rank this first, because everything in either list imports this path.","Update the \"never been run\" line in the same commit; §70.5 already contradicts it."],"flip":"Cutting the certificate from the product entirely, which makes option c the honest cleanup.","linked":["E6","E8","E9"],"sources":["scripts/mdmax-cert.mjs:195","docs/ENGINE.md:526","docs/ENGINE.md:838","docs/ENGINE.md:1004","docs/ENGINE.md:718","docs/ENGINE.md:733","docs/ENGINE.md:819","docs/ENGINE.md:870","docs/ENGINE.md:138","docs/ENGINE.md:139","docs/ENGINE.md:412","docs/ENGINE.md:228","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:224","package.json:8","merged: E34"]},{"id":"E15","cat":"Engine & technical","sub":"Correctness","weight":"high","q":"Do we fix the two defects that return a wrong answer and report success, or defer them until a caller reads the value back?","lede":"One returns end-of-document with `ok: true`; the other prints a wrong column in the only engine error a user sees today.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":190,"cols":[{"title":"The engine reports","tone":"stop"},{"title":"What is true","tone":"good"}],"rows":[{"label":"Probe past the last checkpoint, length 512","cells":["end of document, `ok: true`","a real offset"]},{"label":"Same at length 1024 and 1536","cells":["end of document, `ok: true`","a real offset"]},{"label":"`é` + 0xFF","cells":["column 2","column 2"]},{"label":"`éé` + 0xFF","cells":["column 1","column 3"]},{"label":"`ééé` + 0xFF","cells":["column 4","column 4"]}],"note":"Both failures are silent: one carries `ok: true`, the other is a plausible number in an error message.","caption":"Two defects reproduced at HEAD, both reporting success"},"stakes":"Per-hunk accept and reject reads byte anchors back, so a conversion that lies becomes a wrong byte range in the flagship.","state":["The checkpoint table is sized `Math.floor(text.length / BLOCK) + 1` and filled only inside a loop over the text (src/modules/mdmax/domain/offsets.ts:127).","At lengths that are exact multiples of 512 the last slot is never assigned, and every probe at or past it returns end-of-document (docs/ENGINE.md:41).","`decodeStrict` bisects on \"longest valid prefix\", which is not a monotone predicate on multi-byte input (docs/ENGINE.md:47).","The wrong column reaches users through `search-index.ts` and `get-snapshot.ts` (docs/CRITIQUE.md:762)."],"path":["`offsets.ts` was already patched once for an off-by-three; this is the same class in the same file.","The bisection was written for speed, about 22 decodes instead of a full scan on a 4 MB file (docs/ENGINE.md:346).","The offsets suite contains no document whose length is an exact multiple of 512."],"tension":["`toByte` is unaffected, so nothing reaches a user from the offset defect today.","A naive test at 512, 1024 and 1536 that probes only low offsets passes against the unfixed code (docs/ENGINE.md:1863).","The impact of the column defect is minor; the signal is not — a binary search over an unsorted property shipped and passed its tests."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"Reproduced at HEAD in this session — the shape matters","items":[["Length 512","512 of 513 probes wrong; first wrong at byte 0","live run"],["Length 1024","512 of 1025 probes wrong; first wrong at byte 512","live run"],["Length 1536","512 of 1537 probes wrong; first wrong at byte 1024","live run"],["Length 2048","512 of 2049 probes wrong; first wrong at byte 1536","live run"],["Every wrong answer","`{ok: true, value: <document length>}` — indistinguishable from a valid result","live run"],["Length 513 (control)","0 of 514 wrong","live run"],["Fix","size the table `Math.ceil(text.length / BLOCK) || 1`","docs/ENGINE.md:99"],["Existing offsets test cases","16, none on a 512-multiple document","docs/ENGINE.md:99; counted live (the §68.1 and §68.3 tables say 22, which does not match the file)"]]},{"type":"table","title":"Which test shape finds it (docs/ENGINE.md:1863)","cols":["Generator","Offsets checked","Failures against the unfixed code"],"rows":[["Uniform random (emoji every 7th, lengths 400–2000)","4,966","0"],["Boundary-straddling (surrogate low unit on a 512 boundary)","9,363","600, first at pad=511, delta exactly +3"],["Same generator against the fixed code","9,363","0"],["A test at 512/1024/1536 that probes only low offsets","—","0 at 1024 and 1536 — it must probe at or past the last checkpoint"]]},{"type":"table","title":"Measured columns, reproduced live this session","cols":["Input","Reported column","Correct column"],"rows":[["`é` + 0xFF","2","2"],["`éé` + 0xFF","1","3"],["`ééé` + 0xFF","4","4"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"Reach and cost","items":[["Reaches a user today","yes — the only mdmax defect that does","docs/ENGINE.md:47; docs/CRITIQUE.md:762"],["CRITIQUE grading","MINOR in impact, SERIOUS as signal","docs/CRITIQUE.md:762"],["Where it surfaces","search-index.ts and get-snapshot.ts, via explainFailure","docs/ENGINE.md:47; verified by grep"],["Failure-locate performance today","10.6 ms for an invalid byte at offset 4,194,303","docs/ENGINE.md:346"],["Budget for that operation","coldOpen, 50 ms","docs/ENGINE.md:346"],["Headroom","4.7x on the current bisect; a bounded forward decode fits the same tier","docs/ENGINE.md:346"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Fix both now, with tests shown failing against the unfixed code first","what":"One character-class change in the checkpoint fill, and a bounded forward decode from the last known-good boundary.","gains":["Closes two defects that report success","Keeps the refusal message useful to someone opening the file","Both fixes are contained to one file each"],"costs":["The offset test must walk every offset, not sample three lengths"],"system":"Two domain files.","screens":"The ingress refusal can carry a correct location.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Fix both, and adopt the boundary-straddling generator with them","what":"Cover the whole class rather than the two known instances.","gains":["Catches the next instance of the same class","A uniform generator reports zero failures, so the generator shape is the finding"],"costs":["Pulls the property-testing decision in as a dependency"],"system":"Adds a generator file.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Fix the offset map now; drop line and column from the UTF-8 message","what":"Report a byte offset instead of a location for invalid UTF-8.","gains":["Always correct and cheaper","No bisection to maintain"],"costs":["A byte offset is less useful to a person opening the file in an editor"],"system":"One domain file plus a message change.","screens":"Refusal copy loses the location.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Defer both until a caller reads offsets back","what":"Leave them; nothing breaks today.","gains":["No work now"],"costs":["Ships the flagship on a conversion that can silently return end-of-document","Leaves a wrong column in the one engine path that reaches users"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["A wrong answer that reports `ok: true` is the failure shape this engine's type system exists to make impossible.","The offset fix is one character class; the column fix is contained and keeps the message the ingress refusal needs.","Do it now rather than under the anchor work, because that is where a wrong offset first becomes a wrong byte range."],"flip":"The property-testing decision landing in the same week, which gets the whole class for barely more effort under option c.","linked":["E17","E22","E23"],"sources":["src/modules/mdmax/domain/offsets.ts:127","src/modules/mdmax/domain/shape-gate.ts","docs/ENGINE.md:41","docs/ENGINE.md:47","docs/ENGINE.md:99","docs/ENGINE.md:346","docs/ENGINE.md:1863","docs/ENGINE.md:467","docs/CRITIQUE.md:761","docs/CRITIQUE.md:762","merged: E29"]},{"id":"E16","cat":"Engine & technical","sub":"Correctness","weight":"high","q":"Do we rewrite `safeInsert`, delete it, or ship review state without a placement gate?","lede":"The gate meant to stop a write from changing what a document means refuses the safe case, permits the unsafe one, and has never been called.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":200,"cols":[{"title":"safeInsert says","tone":"stop"},{"title":"What is true","tone":"good"}],"rows":[{"label":"After a heading, before a thematic break","cells":["ADJACENT_TO_SETEXT_UNDERLINE","safe: no insertion converts it"]},{"label":"After a paragraph, before a thematic break","cells":["ADJACENT_TO_SETEXT_UNDERLINE","safe"]},{"label":"Inside a fenced code block","cells":["ok: true","the marker lands as visible text"]},{"label":"Inside an inline code span","cells":["ok: true","the marker lands as visible text"]},{"label":"Callers in `src/`","cells":["zero","the flagship needs one"]}],"note":"The pre-check ORs over a two-line lookback and treats a bare `---` as a setext underline.","caption":"The placement gate, measured both ways"},"stakes":"Per-hunk accept and reject is priced at 16 points and its write gate refuses the flagship's primary case.","state":["`placement.ts` has zero callers anywhere in `src/`.","Both refusals and both permissions reproduce today (docs/ENGINE.md:45).","CRITIQUE grades it SEVERE the moment `land()` ships (docs/CRITIQUE.md:760).","The generalisation already has a name in the record, `SKELETON_CHANGED_OUTSIDE_SPAN` (docs/ENGINE.md:1464)."],"path":["It was written for the AI-marker case, where the whole block skeleton should be unchanged.","That rule is right for an invisible marker and wrong for anything visible.","`placement.test.ts` never asserts what the gate accepts beyond markers, so the refusals went unnoticed (docs/ENGINE.md:198)."],"tension":["Both defects are small and both have reproducible red proofs available today.","The architecturally right shape is per-span-kind permitted skeleton deltas, which belongs to the body-span decision and is three founder-weeks.","Leaving it unwired puts a late rewrite on the flagship's critical path."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"The gate's measured behaviour (docs/ENGINE.md:45)","cols":["Input","What it should do","What it does"],"rows":[["`# Title\\n\\n---\\n\\nBody\\n` — insert at the break","allow: the `---` is a thematic break","refuses, ADJACENT_TO_SETEXT_UNDERLINE"],["`Body text\\n\\n---\\n\\nMore\\n`","allow","refuses, same reason"],["Insert inside a ```js fence","refuse","{ok:true} — the marker becomes visible code"],["Insert inside an inline code span","refuse","{ok:true}"],["Paragraph, callout or heading at a true block boundary","allow","SKELETON_CHANGED"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"Standing","items":[["Product call sites","0","verified by grep over src/"],["Test assertions","16, opening with a genuine red proof","docs/ENGINE.md:121, docs/ENGINE.md:198"],["What the tests never assert","what it accepts beyond markers","docs/ENGINE.md:198"],["CRITIQUE severity","SEVERE the moment `land()` ships","docs/CRITIQUE.md:760"],["Is `land()` built","no — no `land()`, no splice journal, no review sidecar anywhere in src/","verified by grep"],["Points MVP-0 assigns the feature it gates","16","docs/DECIDE.md:87"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Rewrite both defects now, before `land()` is designed","what":"Fix the setext lookback and add the skip-region check for fences and code spans.","gains":["Makes the gate usable for the flagship","Two contained changes with red proofs available today","Keeps it decoupled from the body-span decision"],"costs":["Work on a file nothing calls yet"],"system":"One domain file, then wired by `land()`.","screens":"None yet.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Fold the rewrite into the body-span work","what":"Each span kind declares its permitted skeleton delta.","gains":["The architecturally right shape","One design instead of two"],"costs":["Makes the flagship wait on a three-founder-week item rated High risk"],"system":"Placement becomes part of the span contract.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Leave it unwired until a caller exists","what":"Defer; discover the rewrite when `land()` is built.","gains":["Costs nothing now"],"costs":["Puts the review flow's write gate on the critical path of a late rewrite"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Delete it; gate writes on block-skeleton equality alone","what":"Remove 154 lines and rely on the coarser check.","gains":["Removes code nothing calls"],"costs":["Gives up the check that distinguishes a real boundary from one that changes the parse"],"system":"Deletes a domain file.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["Both defects are small, both have red proofs today, and the gate stands between an accepted hunk and a document whose meaning changed.","Fixing it now keeps it decoupled from the body-span decision, which is much bigger and much less certain.","The plan prices the flagship at 16 points and does not price its gate."],"flip":"Per-hunk accept and reject slipping out of MVP-0, which makes option c defensible if it is written down.","linked":["E21","E22","E26"],"sources":["src/modules/mdmax/domain/placement.ts","docs/ENGINE.md:45","docs/ENGINE.md:121","docs/ENGINE.md:198","docs/ENGINE.md:1464","docs/CRITIQUE.md:760","docs/DECIDE.md:87"]},{"id":"E20","cat":"Engine & technical","sub":"Parsing","weight":"high","q":"Does the engine adopt @lezer/markdown for incremental parsing, or stay on remark with a typed one-way boundary?","lede":"Two committed documents give opposite answers, and the premise the plan's answer rests on was measured and does not hold.","visual":{"kind":"arch","layers":[{"label":"Bytes on disk","items":["the file","the only source of truth"],"tone":"neutral"},{"label":"Engine","items":["remark / micromark","OffsetMap","splice writer"],"side":"cold, once, per document","tone":"accent"},{"label":"Editor","items":["CodeMirror","@lezer/markdown decorations"],"side":"viewport-budgeted, per keystroke","tone":"sunk"},{"label":"Boundary","items":["typed, one-way, lint-enforced"],"side":"an editor offset cannot reach the splice","tone":"good"}],"note":"Lezer offsets are UTF-16 code units, the same unit mdast reports, so adopting it buys nothing against the byte contract.","caption":"Which layer owns parsing, and what the boundary refuses"},"stakes":"A stale editor offset reaching the splice writes correct-looking bytes at the wrong place, in a file committed on every save.","state":["The plan says lezer is vendored for incremental parsing so review spans survive every keystroke (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:233).","ENGINE §79.1 says the opposite: keep remark, keep lezer inside CodeMirror, make the boundary one-way and typed (docs/ENGINE.md:1927).","On `\"# 🌊 tide\"` both report [0,9) and neither reports 11, the byte length (docs/ENGINE.md:1970).","Lezer's default parser reads a frontmatter block as a horizontal rule plus a setext heading (docs/ENGINE.md:2007)."],"path":["Lezer is already installed and already used, in three presentation files, through CodeMirror.","The question was only ever whether it moves down into the engine.","It also collapses a bare-CR document into a single heading, the same family as the bare-CR set-destruction (docs/ENGINE.md:2017)."],"tension":["The engine has no keystroke loop to make incremental: its work is cold, once, per document.","The two numbers that drive the product, the 83% refusal and SAFE_KEY, live below the markdown grammar entirely.","Being wrong one way costs 4,849 ms per full-corpus pass; being wrong the other way writes bytes at the wrong offset."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"Measured, on the same inputs (docs/ENGINE.md:1962-2017)","cols":["Question","@lezer/markdown","remark / micromark"],"rows":[["Position unit","UTF-16 code units","UTF-16 code units"],["`# 🌊 tide` heading span","[0,9)","offset 0..9 — identical; byte length is 11"],["Frontmatter block","HorizontalRule + SetextHeading2","addressable, via remark-frontmatter"],["Bare-CR document, 21 units","one ATXHeading1 covering everything","heading[0,3) paragraph[4,8) list[9,20)"],["Emits HTML for the certificate","no","yes"],["Full-corpus parse, 8,513 files","566 ms","4,849 ms"],["Incremental reparse, 50 largest docs","0.46 ms with fragment reuse (1.83 ms cold)","51.37 ms full"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"Cost of each answer","items":[["Adopt lezer in the engine","rewrite 3 domain files plus the bench","docs/ENGINE.md:1940"],["Typed one-way boundary","~60 lines plus one lint rule","docs/ENGINE.md:1940"],["Do nothing (today)","0 lines, and a stale-tree splice stays representable","docs/ENGINE.md:1938"],["Engine parse cost either way","the engine is cold, once, per document, in a worker — there is no keystroke loop in it","docs/ENGINE.md:1996"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Leave both trees with no declared boundary","what":"Today's state.","gains":["Costs nothing"],"costs":["Keeps available the one failure the contract exists to prevent","A viewport-budgeted offset can reach a byte write"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Keep remark; add the typed tree boundary and the import lint rule","what":"About 60 lines and one rule, plus correcting the plan's line.","gains":["A stale editor offset reaching the splice becomes unrepresentable","No new parse layer to keep in agreement","Both documents stop contradicting each other"],"costs":["Keeps the slower full-corpus parse","One more lint rule to maintain"],"system":"A branded editor-offset type and one import rule.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Vendor lezer into the engine for incremental parsing","what":"The plan's line as written.","gains":["566 ms per full-corpus pass instead of 4,849 ms"],"costs":["Buys throughput for a consumer that does not exist","Makes the frontmatter misparse and the bare-CR collapse structural"],"system":"Rewrites three domain files and the bench.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Defer until a feature needs sub-100 ms structural reparse","what":"Decide when a consumer appears.","gains":["Honest deferral"],"costs":["Leaves the plan and the engine doc contradicting each other in writing"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["Incrementality is an editor property being bought for an engine consumer that does not exist.","The asymmetry decides it: one way costs seconds per corpus pass, the other writes correct-looking bytes in the wrong place.","Whichever way this goes, one of the two documents has to change in the same session."],"flip":"A shipped feature that genuinely needs sub-frame structural feedback on a 900 KB document.","linked":["E15","E21","E22"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:233","docs/ENGINE.md:1927","docs/ENGINE.md:1938","docs/ENGINE.md:1940","docs/ENGINE.md:1962","docs/ENGINE.md:1970","docs/ENGINE.md:1996","docs/ENGINE.md:2007","docs/ENGINE.md:2017","docs/ENGINE.md:2102"]},{"id":"E21","cat":"Engine & technical","sub":"Scope","weight":"high","q":"Do we commit to body-span splicing in the MVP, or is the render lane read-only until a profile needs it?","lede":"The splice contract covers one region of the file, so every rendered view that lets you edit has nowhere to write back.","visual":{"kind":"file","name":"spec.md","lines":[{"t":"---","mark":"neutral"},{"t":"status: draft","mark":"good","note":"addressable today"},{"t":"---","mark":"neutral"},{"t":"- [ ] ship the gate","mark":"accent","note":"one code unit, atomic, leaf span"},{"t":"> [!note] carrier","mark":"accent","note":"no closer to lose"},{"t":"```ts","mark":"warn","note":"an unclosed fence swallows the document"},{"t":"Free prose that an agent rewrote.","mark":"stop","note":"boundary genuinely ambiguous"}],"note":"Leaf, delimited spans are safe to address first; the ambiguous prose case is the expensive half.","caption":"What the writer can address, and what it cannot"},"stakes":"With no body locator the projection law holds for one region, and every render profile is a viewer rather than an editor.","state":["`spliceFrontmatterValue` addresses one thing: a top-level key inside the frontmatter block. There is no body locator.","ENGINE prices the body-span contract at 3.0 founder-weeks and rates it High risk (docs/ENGINE.md:624).","It ranks 5 of 9, behind CI, the fold run, the YAML defects and detector work (docs/ENGINE.md:736).","Five product write-backs have no path at all today (docs/ENGINE.md:1270)."],"path":["Frontmatter was the easy case: one delimited region, known offsets, line-oriented targets.","The body is the general case and was deferred.","The task marker is measured as exactly three code units for every marker shape tested (docs/ENGINE.md:1348)."],"tension":["A checkbox toggle, a kanban card status, a calendar drag, an accepted hunk and a section restore all need a body write.","An unclosed fence swallows the rest of the document, and on a product where every save is a commit that intermediate state is publishable (docs/ENGINE.md:1350).","This is the highest-risk item on the engine roadmap, and High risk is honest: a body span boundary can be legitimately ambiguous (docs/ENGINE.md:677)."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"Write-backs with no path today (docs/ENGINE.md:1270-1276)","cols":["Write-back","Target span","Today"],"rows":[["Kanban drag to a new status","a field inside a list item, or a frontmatter key","frontmatter only; a card whose status is in the body has no write path"],["Checkbox toggle","the three units `[ ]` in a TaskMarker","none"],["Calendar drag to a new date","a date token in a list item or heading","frontmatter only"],["Accepted AI hunk","an arbitrary block range","none"],["Section-level restore","heading through the next heading of depth ≤ d","none"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"What makes the leaf spans the safe first target","items":[["TaskMarker span, all marker shapes tested","exactly 3 code units, state char at from+1","docs/ENGINE.md:1348"],["A checkbox toggle is therefore","a one-unit splice, not a line rewrite","docs/ENGINE.md:1348"],["Why a fence is the opposite case","CommonMark 0.31.2 §4.5 — an unclosed fence swallows every line to end of document, and every save is a commit","docs/ENGINE.md:1350"],["List items followed by a lazy continuation","19,135 of 60,000 = 31.9%","docs/ENGINE.md:1378"],["Setext headings in the corpus","15 across 11 of 8,513 files = 0.129% of headings","docs/ENGINE.md:1388"],["Roadmap position","rank 5 of 9, behind CI, fold run, YAML defects, detectors","docs/ENGINE.md:736"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Leaf, delimited spans only in MVP-1 — task marker, fenced block, callout body","what":"Address the span kinds whose boundaries are unambiguous, and refuse free prose.","gains":["Delivers the checkbox toggle and the callout carrier","Proves the address model on real traffic first","Defers the genuinely ambiguous case"],"costs":["Render profiles stay partly read-only","Two contracts to maintain until the general case lands"],"system":"A span enum with three kinds and a locator per kind.","screens":"Checkbox toggles and callout edits write back.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Build the full span enum now","what":"The whole §76 contract in one go.","gains":["Opens every render profile at once"],"costs":["Three founder-weeks of the highest-risk work","No CI underneath it unless E12 lands first"],"system":"Full body locator.","screens":"Every render profile becomes editable.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Task marker only","what":"One span kind, one code unit.","gains":["Smallest possible commitment","Proves the model where duplicate content is worst"],"costs":["Leaves the callout carrier, which the render design already depends on, unwritable"],"system":"One locator.","screens":"Checkbox toggles only.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Render lane stays read-only, no body writes at all","what":"Keep the guarantee narrow and true.","gains":["Nothing new to guarantee","No ambiguous boundary to defend"],"costs":["Every render becomes a viewer, which the projection law was written to avoid"],"system":"No change.","screens":"Rendered views lose edit affordances.","money":"None."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["Atomicity picks the order: a task marker cannot disturb indentation, tags or a trailing comment, and a callout has no closer to drop.","A fence is the opposite case, and an intermediate broken state is publishable on a product where every save is a commit.","Shipping the leaf spans proves the address model on real traffic before the prose case is attempted."],"flip":"A corpus replay showing path-plus-ordinal resolving below 99.5%, which collapses the model back to content plus refusal.","linked":["E16","E22","E26"],"sources":["docs/ENGINE.md:624","docs/ENGINE.md:677","docs/ENGINE.md:736","docs/ENGINE.md:1270","docs/ENGINE.md:1333","docs/ENGINE.md:1348","docs/ENGINE.md:1350","docs/ENGINE.md:1378"]},{"id":"E22","cat":"Engine & technical","sub":"Scope","weight":"high","q":"Do review anchors carry the structural triple, or a content hash alone?","lede":"Review state is the product, and the published re-anchoring number describes a pointer nobody has written yet.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":190,"cols":[{"title":"Content hash only","tone":"stop"},{"title":"Hash plus multiplicity","tone":"accent"}],"rows":[{"label":"False positives, 43,056 attempts","cells":["141","16"]},{"label":"Of those, in the exact-hash lane","cells":["115, undetectable","0"]},{"label":"Resolve rate","cells":["about half a point higher","98.65%"]},{"label":"Task lines unique within their file","cells":["67.4%","67.4%"]},{"label":"Cross-document resolve without a scope check","cells":["35.1%","0 with the check"]}],"note":"One integer field converts an 8.8× worse false-positive rate into zero errors in the lane where nothing can catch them.","caption":"The multiplicity ablation, everything else identical"},"stakes":"A false positive here replaces bytes the user never pointed at, in the feature the whole product is named for.","state":["§68.1 row 12 classifies the 99.627% re-anchoring claim as ASPIRATIONAL: no anchor store, no re-anchor function (docs/ENGINE.md:124).","Nothing in `src/` contains a `land()`, a splice journal or a review sidecar.","A task line's trimmed text is unique within its own file for 67.4% of items (docs/ENGINE.md:1291).","Anchors from one corpus file resolve into a different file 35.1% of the time with the scope check off (docs/ENGINE.md:1516)."],"path":["The published number came from a prototype harness whose mutation mix is not recorded beside it.","Two harnesses now exist and are not comparable: 43,056 attempts against 41,642, and a mix that manufactures ambiguity on purpose (docs/ENGINE.md:1714).","The ablation was run to find out which field was carrying the result."],"tension":["Eight fields to persist and version means every threshold change becomes a migration.","A hash-only anchor refuses about one task item in four on the span kind the product writes to most.","Structural path and ordinal alone are silent on reorder, which is the worst outcome because it succeeds."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"Uniqueness by anchor kind, measured over the corpus","items":[["Task-line trimmed text unique within its file","2,278 of 3,378 = 67.436%","docs/ENGINE.md:1291"],["Same, plus one line of context","2,554 of 3,378 = 75.607%","docs/ENGINE.md:1291"],["ATX heading full ancestor path unique within its file","37,413 of 37,489 = 99.797%","docs/ENGINE.md:1291"],["Corpus blocks sitting in a same-hash group of 2 or more","6.73%","docs/ENGINE.md:1596"],["Anchors from one corpus file resolving into a different file","1,401 of 3,992 = 35.095%","docs/ENGINE.md:1628"],["Same, with the quote gate raised to 64 characters","31.06% — length gates do not separate them","docs/ENGINE.md:1628"]]},{"type":"table","title":"The multiplicity ablation — 448 files, 43,056 attempts (docs/ENGINE.md:1593-1596)","cols":["Configuration","Resolve rate","False positives","FP in the exact-hash lane"],"rows":[["With `multiplicity`","98.6505%","16 (0.0372%)","0"],["Without — unique hash means accept","99.1410%","141 (0.3275%)","115"],["Cost of the field","0.49 points of resolve rate","—","—"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Structural path and ordinal only","what":"Address by heading path and position.","gains":["99.797% unique for headings","Small record"],"costs":["Silent on reorder: a moved section relocates the anchor with full confidence","Confident wrong answers are the worst class"],"system":"Path index.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Content hash plus refusal whenever two or more blocks match","what":"Refuse the ambiguous case rather than resolving it.","gains":["Much simpler to persist and version","The refusal is honest"],"costs":["Refuses roughly one task item in four","On the span kind the product writes to most"],"system":"Hash store plus a duplicate check.","screens":"Frequent unresolvable spans.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"In-session offsets only, re-derived on every load","what":"No persistence; map positions within a session.","gains":["Correct within a session and cheap"],"costs":["An agent's proposal cannot survive a save","That is the scenario the product exists for"],"system":"No store.","screens":"Review state resets on reload.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Full record: hash, multiplicity, ordinal, docId, quote, context, heading path","what":"The §77 anchor as specified, with scope checked before any content is examined.","gains":["Zero false positives in the exact lane at 98.65% resolve","Survives rename and reorder","The scope check is measured as load-bearing"],"costs":["Eight fields to persist and version","Every threshold change becomes a migration"],"system":"Anchor record plus resolver, versioned.","screens":"Review panel can explain why a span could not be found.","money":"None."}],"rec":"d","recCase":["One integer field converts an 8.8× worse false-positive rate into zero errors in the undetectable lane, for half a point of resolve rate.","The scope check is equally load-bearing, and it must run before any content is examined.","Publish both harnesses under one manifest with the mutation mix stated, rather than reconciling them by argument."],"flip":"A harness reproducing the mutation mix with zero exact-lane false positives and no multiplicity field, which would make the duplicate population an artefact of the block segmenter.","linked":["E21","E36","E37","F1"],"sources":["docs/ENGINE.md:124","docs/ENGINE.md:1291","docs/ENGINE.md:1516","docs/ENGINE.md:1529","docs/ENGINE.md:1593","docs/ENGINE.md:1596","docs/ENGINE.md:1628","docs/ENGINE.md:1714"]},{"id":"E26","cat":"Engine & technical","sub":"Refusals","weight":"high","q":"Do we declare non-locality a refusal condition, or keep splicing near reference-link definitions?","lede":"There are edits where every byte in the changed range is correct and the meaning of prose elsewhere in the file changes anyway.","visual":{"kind":"file","name":"guide.md","lines":[{"t":"See the [spec][s] before you start.","mark":"accent","note":"renders as a link only because of line 9"},{"t":"","mark":"neutral"},{"t":"…","mark":"sunk"},{"t":"","mark":"neutral"},{"t":"[s]: https://example.com/spec","mark":"stop","note":"delete this and line 1 becomes literal text"}],"note":"Measured across four CommonMark engines, unanimous in both directions. No byte in the edited range changes.","caption":"An edit at the bottom that changes the meaning at the top"},"stakes":"The engine keeps a silent failure of exactly the kind it exists to eliminate, in a product whose pitch is refuse rather than guess.","state":["The plan states the class and states that nothing implements it (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:510).","The gap register reaches the same conclusion independently (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:128).","The same class covers HTML block condition 7 and setext underlines, where the spec records four different interpretations (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:488).","The corpus has 15 setext headings across 11 of 8,513 files, so that member is rare (docs/ENGINE.md:1388)."],"path":["The refusal set was built from what the writer can address.","Non-locality is the opposite shape: it is about bytes the writer did not touch.","The boundary rule already exists — the engine may do anything decidable from the bytes and must refuse otherwise (docs/ENGINE.md:767)."],"tension":["Nothing measures how often the shape occurs, so the availability cost of refusing is unknown.","The writer already refuses 83% of vaults, and stacking an unmeasured refusal rate on that is where careful becomes unusable.","Auto-normalising the ambiguous case is anti-recommended outright (docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:5829)."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"The three non-local classes named","cols":["Class","Mechanism","Status"],"rows":[["Reference links","`[foo][bar]` means link or literal text depending on a definition elsewhere, perhaps later","measured unanimous across four engines; undeclared"],["HTML block condition 7","block boundaries depend on surrounding context","named, unmeasured"],["Setext underlines","the spec records four possible interpretations","placement.ts already refuses near them, with a parse-verified fixture; 15 in the corpus, 0.129% of headings"],["Corpus incidence of the first two","unmeasured","no figure exists in the record"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"Why it belongs to the engine and not the UI","items":[["Engine boundary rule","\"the engine may do anything that is decidable from the bytes and refusable when it is not\"","docs/ENGINE.md:767"],["Source of the diagnosis","CommonMark's own author, on why he built Djot","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:488"],["Standing anti-recommendation","do not build an auto-fixer that silently normalises ambiguous indentation, reference-link placement, or a bare-CR line ending","docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:5829"],["Refusal codes mdmax already emits","19 typed failure codes","docs/ENGINE.md:978"],["Refusal rate the writer already carries","83.01%","docs/ENGINE.md:487"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Declare all three; refuse only the destructive case and warn on the rest","what":"Refuse deleting or moving a reference-link definition; warn where the other two are touched.","gains":["Closes the one case where meaning is lost silently","Adds no refusals to ordinary edits","Keeps the classes named in writing"],"costs":["A warning is weaker than a refusal and can be ignored","Two behaviours to explain instead of one"],"system":"One refusal reason, two warnings, one pre-scan.","screens":"A warning state beside the refusal state.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Leave it undeclared","what":"Today's state.","gains":["No refusals added"],"costs":["A silent failure of the exact class the engine exists to eliminate","Contradicts the plan's own §20 item 5"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Measure corpus incidence first, then set the refusal set","what":"One day of counting before declaring anything.","gains":["Makes the availability cost a number rather than a guess","The corpus is on disk"],"costs":["Delays the declaration","Leaves the silent case live for another week"],"system":"A counting script.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Declare all three classes and refuse edits that touch them","what":"Reference-link definitions, HTML block condition 7 and setext underlines all become refusals.","gains":["The strongest correctness position available","One rule, no case analysis"],"costs":["Adds an unmeasured number of refusals on top of 83%","Refuses ordinary edits to prove a rare point"],"system":"Three new refusal reasons and a whole-file pre-scan.","screens":"More refusals in the panel.","money":"None."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["Deleting a definition at the bottom and changing a paragraph at the top is the failure this contract is written against, and the user cannot see it happen.","Refusing the whole class before measuring its incidence stacks an unknown rate on an already high one.","Declare all three in writing either way, so the next reader does not rediscover them."],"flip":"The corpus measurement in option c: if the three classes together touch under a percent of files, refuse all three.","linked":["E16","E2","E21"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:510","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:488","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:128","docs/ENGINE.md:767","docs/ENGINE.md:1388","docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:5829"]},{"id":"E32","cat":"Engine & technical","sub":"Strategy","weight":"high","q":"Do we adopt a dated kill condition for the engine, and which one?","lede":"The engine doc wrote its own falsifiers, none carries a date, and the one number that decides them is not instrumented.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":200,"cols":[{"title":"Under 1 in 20 hit a refusal","tone":"warn"},{"title":"1 in 5 or more hit one","tone":"stop"}],"rows":[{"label":"What it proves","cells":["nobody meets the guarantee","the guarantee is met constantly"]},{"label":"Which defence dies","cells":["the six engine moments are theatre","refusal UX becomes a churn risk"]},{"label":"Where the budget belongs","cells":["projections, not the engine","refusal copy and recovery"]},{"label":"Readable today","cells":["no","no"]}],"note":"There is no value of this number at which both defences survive, and nobody can currently read it.","caption":"The refusal-rate pincer, per activated user per 30 days"},"stakes":"The engine is a conviction with no way to be wrong, in a programme that has already withdrawn three headline claims.","state":["§74.6 states the risk plainly: the product works today with the engine almost entirely disconnected (docs/ENGINE.md:1023).","Five falsifiers are listed with thresholds and none has a date (docs/ENGINE.md:1025).","The plan imports exactly one of them: patched corpus still refusing over 10 of 7,969 by day 24 (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:327).","The Z metric, foreign-vault open rate, has a threshold of 99.9% and sits at 17% today (docs/ENGINE.md:1030)."],"path":["The falsifiers were written into the engine doc as an honesty exercise.","The plan's kill-condition table then imported one of them.","CRITIQUE proposes the pincer and names `cert_refusal` as the instrument (docs/CRITIQUE.md:662)."],"tension":["Instrumenting requires the measurement decision, and the architecture keeps counts in a local file the user can read.","CRITIQUE's 40-person survey by 2026-12-31 is the only line in the record with both a date and a stated consequence (docs/CRITIQUE.md:330).","The Z metric moves directly with the fix list and says nothing about whether anyone values the guarantee."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"The falsifiers already written (docs/ENGINE.md:1025-1031)","cols":["Claim","Measurement","Threshold","State"],"rows":[["Deterministic guarantees retain","Obsidian projection plugins vs AI capability installs","7,289,307 against 1,005,651 = 7.25x in favour of projections","already refuted, from outside the thesis"],["Nobody hits the refusal, so nobody values it","`cert_refusal` per activated user, 30 days","fewer than 1 in 20 means the six moments are theatre","not instrumented"],["The refusal is the ceiling, not the floor","foreign-vault open rate, the Z metric","target 99.9%; today 17%","measured, far from target"],["Users want the guarantee but not visibly","day-7 return split by whether the byte diff was shown, as a release cohort","activated users must retain 2x","no cohort exists"],["Buyers pay for consolidation, not fidelity","the first 25 sales conversations","—","zero conversations held"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"The alternative kill line in the record","items":[["CRITIQUE's proposal","40 strangers on their own repos by 2026-12-31, Ellis wording","docs/CRITIQUE.md:330"],["Its threshold","under 40% \"very disappointed\" and fewer than 5 of 40 naming whole-file rewrites","docs/CRITIQUE.md:330"],["Its consequence","stop the editor, keep the engine, ship it as a free plugin","docs/CRITIQUE.md:330"],["The plan's only engine kill line","patched corpus still refusing over 10 of 7,969 by day 24","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:327"],["The pincer, stated in the record","\"There is no value of that metric at which both the refusal-UX defence and the engine-as-differentiator defence survive\"","docs/CRITIQUE.md:662"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Adopt the 40-person survey by 2026-12-31","what":"Test demand rather than mechanism, on the record's only dated line.","gains":["Has a date and a stated consequence","Executable without any instrumentation"],"costs":["Tests interest rather than the engine","Forty strangers is a real recruiting cost"],"system":"None.","screens":"None.","money":"Recruiting time."},{"k":"b","label":"Adopt the falsifier table with dates, and instrument `cert_refusal` in the pilot","what":"Every falsifier gets a date, and refusals per activated user per 30 days become observable.","gains":["Makes the engine falsifiable on its own terms","The pincer becomes a reading rather than an argument","Pairs with the Z metric the fixes move directly"],"costs":["Depends on the measurement decision being settled","Adds a local counter and the copy explaining it"],"system":"A refusal counter in the local usage sidecar.","screens":"Nothing new; the count lives in a readable file.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Adopt the Z metric alone","what":"Foreign-vault open rate to 99.9%, nothing else.","gains":["One number, already measured at 17%","Tied directly to the fixes on the list"],"costs":["Says nothing about whether anyone values the guarantee","Cannot fire the pincer"],"system":"A corpus assertion.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"No engine kill condition","what":"Today's state.","gains":["Nothing to run"],"costs":["The engine cannot be wrong","Three headline claims have already been withdrawn here"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["The falsifiers are already written and measured against; what is missing is dates and one instrument.","The pincer is the reason to instrument rather than argue: the same number decides whether refusal is the differentiator or the churn risk.","Pair it with the Z metric, which is the falsifier the fix list moves directly."],"flip":"A measurement decision that lands on self-reporting rather than a usage file, which makes `cert_refusal` uninstrumentable and option c the only executable line.","linked":["E18"],"sources":["docs/ENGINE.md:1023","docs/ENGINE.md:1025","docs/ENGINE.md:1027","docs/ENGINE.md:1028","docs/ENGINE.md:1030","docs/CRITIQUE.md:330","docs/CRITIQUE.md:662","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:327"]},{"id":"E33","cat":"Engine & technical","sub":"Scope","weight":"high","q":"Is non-English correctness in scope for the pilot, or declared out?","lede":"The plan calls the byte-to-UTF-16 seam the highest-risk part of the engine, and the vault where it matters most cannot be written at all.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":190,"cols":[{"title":"Solid","tone":"good"},{"title":"Broken","tone":"stop"}],"rows":[{"label":"Astral characters","cells":["round-trip correctly","—"]},{"label":"Surrogate splits","cells":["refused, not rounded","—"]},{"label":"A CJK key such as `分类`","cells":["—","SAFE_KEY cannot address it"]},{"label":"Documents whose length is a multiple of 512","cells":["—","wrong offset with `ok: true`"]},{"label":"Files with a non-BMP character in a key","cells":["20, 0.25%","—"]}],"note":"The arithmetic is in good shape; the two things that make non-English writing work are the key predicate and the offset fix.","caption":"Which half of the non-English story is actually broken"},"stakes":"A written scope decision is cheap now and a discovered one is a defect report from the population that produced our hardest cases.","state":["The plan names the offset map as the highest-risk seam and says an unmapped crossing corrupts CJK and Arabic silently (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:233).","The gap register records CJK scope as \"a written decision\" and that nobody Chinese, Japanese or Korean has been asked (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:42).","`offsets.ts` records that only 67 of 1,080 corpus files have bytes equal to UTF-16 units equal to code points (docs/ENGINE.md:398).","20 corpus files carry a non-BMP character inside a key (docs/ENGINE.md:1100)."],"path":["The branded offset types and `OffsetMap` were built precisely for this seam.","`u16` refuses rather than rounds, which is the right default.","What was never decided is which keys and which surfaces we support."],"tension":["The two fixes that make non-English writing work are already on the list for unrelated reasons.","The search tokeniser is genuinely separate and can be deferred without deferring correctness.","Declaring it out writes off the population that generated most of the corpus's hardest cases."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"Non-English exposure in the pinned corpus","items":[["Files containing surrogate pairs","475 of 8,513 = 5.6%","docs/ENGINE.md:398"],["Files where bytes equal UTF-16 units","6,568 of 8,513 — so 22.8% diverge","docs/ENGINE.md:398"],["Files with a non-BMP character inside a frontmatter key","20 = 0.25%","docs/ENGINE.md:1100"],["`分类` as a key","232 files","docs/ENGINE.md:1105"],["`器械` / `主要训练肌肉`","54 / 53 files","docs/ENGINE.md:1105"],["Chinese vault size","oldwinter__knowledge-garden, 961 files, of which 905 carry an unaddressable key","test/corpus/foreign/SOURCES.json; docs/ENGINE.md:1105"],["`SAFE_KEY.test('分类')`","false","verified live this session"]]},{"type":"table","title":"Which parts are solid and which are not","cols":["Part","State"],"rows":[["Branded U16Offset / ByteOffset, one conversion point","built and tested against Buffer.byteLength at every offset"],["`u16` refuses rather than rounds inside a surrogate pair","built; a splice of `title: a😀b` round-tripped correctly"],["`OffsetMap.toU16` at 512-multiples","returns end-of-document with ok:true for the last 512 bytes — reproduced today (E15)"],["Addressing a CJK frontmatter key","refused by SAFE_KEY — the whole Chinese vault (E3)"],["A CJK-aware search tokeniser","not built"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Defer the decision until a user asks","what":"Leave it open.","gains":["Nothing to decide now"],"costs":["The plan names this the highest-risk seam and then leaves it undecided","That is the state that produced the caveat"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"In scope: the key predicate and the offset fix, both already scheduled","what":"Non-English documents are writable in the pilot; the CJK search tokeniser is explicitly deferred.","gains":["Opens the Chinese vault using two fixes already on the list","Scope costs coordination rather than engineering","Keeps the highest-risk seam owned"],"costs":["Ties the pilot to two fixes landing","Search quality for CJK stays poor and must be said"],"system":"E3 and E15, no new work.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"In scope for reading, out for writing","what":"Files open and render; keys cannot be edited.","gains":["Close to today's behaviour, said out loud","Zero engineering"],"costs":["A read-only editor for a whole language group","Feels like a bug to anyone who meets it"],"system":"A named refusal.","screens":"Refusal copy on those keys.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Out of the pilot, stated in writing","what":"English-language repos only, said plainly.","gains":["Honest and narrow","No scope creep in the pilot"],"costs":["Writes off the population that produced the hardest cases","The decision has never been tested with anyone in it"],"system":"None.","screens":"A stated limitation.","money":"None."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["Both fixes are already scheduled for unrelated reasons, so scope here costs coordination rather than engineering.","The arithmetic is already correct; the two defects are addressability and one off-by-one.","Defer the search tokeniser explicitly, so deferral is a decision rather than an omission."],"flip":"Ten English-language pilot repos, which makes option c a defensible boundary as long as it is written down rather than discovered.","linked":["D22","E15","E3"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:233","docs/ENGINE.md:398","docs/ENGINE.md:1100","docs/ENGINE.md:1105","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:42","src/modules/mdmax/domain/offsets.ts:127","src/modules/share/domain/splice-frontmatter.ts:53"]},{"id":"E35","cat":"Engine & technical","sub":"Sidecar","weight":"high","q":"Does Zed Delta's CRDT bet reopen \"never a CRDT\", and do we answer them by name?","lede":"A team with ten years of CRDT work reached the opposite conclusion in public. Our position is one table row.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":190,"cols":[{"title":"Delta, on CRDTs","tone":"neutral"},{"title":"frontmatter, on git","tone":"accent"}],"rows":[{"label":"Where the state lives","cells":["a database beside the editor","a plain-text file in the repo"]},{"label":"What convergence guarantees","cells":["all replicas agree","nothing; git surfaces a conflict"]},{"label":"A write from outside the tool","cells":["not in the model","the case the product exists for"]},{"label":"A concurrent prose edit","cells":["merged automatically","refused and shown"]},{"label":"What a reader needs installed","cells":["their client","nothing"]}],"note":"Our objection is about document bytes, where interleaving produces byte-identical garbage. It has never been argued for the sidecar.","caption":"Same thesis, opposite architecture"},"stakes":"The competitive set now contains a purpose-built rival, and our answer to their architecture is unwritten.","state":["\"A CRDT\" sits in the engine's not-this table as settled, with one sentence of reasoning (docs/ENGINE.md:759).","The plan states \"Git merge, never a CRDT\" in the F12 sync row and nowhere else (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:66).","Delta went to private beta on 2026-08-12 on DeltaDB, and its 2026-09-01 post stakes attribution down to the span on CRDTs [research 2026-09-09].","Launch drew 679 HN points, DeltaDB 529 and the between-commits post 319 [research 2026-09-09]."],"path":["The ban was written for document bytes, where interleaving concurrent edits produces convergent garbage.","CRITIQUE argues the refusal of CRDTs was correct and was wrongly extended into refusing sync (docs/CRITIQUE.md:523).","The record's own reading is that git merge plus a splice journal is a sync design, not a refusal to sync (docs/CRITIQUE.md:1730)."],"tension":["The argument is being had in public and we are not in it.","The sidecar is append-only JSONL, where convergence is nearly free, so the ban's reasoning does not obviously reach it.","Answering by name commits us to a position a well-resourced team is actively trying to falsify."],"evidence":[],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Reopen it for the sidecar only","what":"Consider a CRDT for review records while prose stays git-merged.","gains":["Removes sidecar merge conflicts entirely","Convergence on append-only records is cheap"],"costs":["A binary or opaque sidecar breaks the readable-plain-text promise","Two merge models in one product"],"system":"A new sidecar format and a library.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Keep the ban for prose, rebut Zed by name, decide the sidecar separately","what":"A written position: no CRDT for prose, git merge for the sidecar, with Delta's design named and answered.","gains":["Answers the objection before it is raised in a room","Scopes the ban to where the reasoning holds","Costs writing, not engineering"],"costs":["Puts us on record against a team that may ship first","The rebuttal has to be right about their design, not a caricature"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Keep the ban everywhere, say nothing publicly","what":"Position unchanged and unstated.","gains":["No public commitment"],"costs":["The comparison gets made without us","A one-sentence table row is not an answer"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Reopen the whole position","what":"Re-argue CRDTs for document bytes.","gains":["Takes the competitor's evidence seriously"],"costs":["Contradicts a settled decision with no new measurement","Convergence without correctness is worse than a refusal"],"system":"Rewrites the write path.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["The ban's reasoning is about prose interleaving and is sound there; it has never been argued for an append-only record.","Naming Delta is cheaper than being asked about it, and the objection will be raised by anyone who follows the space.","Keep the sidecar merge decision separate, so the two are not settled by one slogan."],"flip":"A demonstration that Delta's span anchors survive an out-of-band write our locator cannot follow.","linked":["E22","E37","F15"],"sources":["docs/ENGINE.md:759","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:66","docs/CRITIQUE.md:523","docs/CRITIQUE.md:1730","research briefing 2026-09-09"],"dupes":{"dropped":["MK28"],"why":"Does Zed Delta's CRDT bet reopen 'never a CRDT', and do we rebut them by name. Same options, both rec (a). Architecture position, so Engine & technical owns it; the market-table row is bookkeeping that follows."}},{"id":"E36","cat":"Engine & technical","sub":"Sidecar","weight":"high","q":"Where does document identity live — a key written into the file's own frontmatter, or a sidecar keyed by path?","lede":"A rename done in a terminal never fires our hook, and Bike documents the failure that follows: plain text cannot hold a stable item id.","visual":{"kind":"file","name":"spec.md","lines":[{"t":"---","mark":"neutral"},{"t":"title: Payments spec","mark":"neutral"},{"t":"fm_id: 8f2c4a1e","mark":"accent","note":"option a: one key we write into the user's file"},{"t":"tags:","mark":"neutral"},{"t":"- spec","mark":"neutral"},{"t":"---","mark":"neutral"}],"note":"Renders as an ordinary property everywhere. It is still a byte we added to a document nobody asked us to change.","caption":"Option a in bytes, against a promise to add nothing to the file"},"stakes":"Get identity wrong and a rename performed outside the app orphans every review record for that document.","state":["§77.6 settles that anchors carry `docId` and that `docId` is not the path (docs/ENGINE.md:1626).","It rejects path-keyed anchors with a rename hook, because `mv`, a git checkout and an Obsidian move never fire the hook (docs/ENGINE.md:1632).","It then places `docId` in the file's own sidecar without saying how the sidecar finds the file after a rename.","The sidecar as specified in the plan is keyed by file path (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:135)."],"path":["Path was the obvious key, because every editor addresses a file by path.","Anchors from one corpus file resolve into a different file 35.1% of the time with the scope check off, so identity has to be checked first (docs/ENGINE.md:1516).","Bike documents the same failure on plain text: no stable item id, so row links break on close and reopen [research 2026-09-09]."],"tension":["The plan's own rule is that nothing is added to markdown that breaks it elsewhere (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:527).","A key in YAML frontmatter breaks nothing and is still a byte we wrote into a document the user did not ask us to change.","Content-addressing the first-seen bytes needs no key and dies the moment the document is edited outside frontmatter."],"evidence":[],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"No stored id; content-address the first-seen bytes","what":"Identity is derived, never written.","gains":["Adds nothing to the file","No migration for existing documents"],"costs":["Dies the moment the document is edited outside frontmatter","Which is the scenario the product exists for"],"system":"A hash index.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Path first, content-address as a fallback, refuse on mismatch","what":"Resolve by path, fall back to a content match, refuse when neither is confident.","gains":["Nothing written into the file","Refusal is honest and visible"],"costs":["Refuses on rename-plus-edit, which is the common agent case","An unmeasured refusal rate on the core flow"],"system":"Two indexes and a refusal reason.","screens":"An unresolvable-document state.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Write one `fm_id` key into the document's frontmatter, once, on first review","what":"Identity lives in the file, so it travels with every copy, move and checkout.","gains":["Survives `mv`, a checkout and an Obsidian move","Renders as an ordinary property everywhere","The sidecar stops depending on the path"],"costs":["We write a byte nobody asked for, in a product that promises not to","A file with no frontmatter gets a block added","Blocked on the write path until E1 and E3 land"],"system":"A first-review write through the splice writer.","screens":"The properties panel shows a key we own.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Sidecar keyed by path, with a rename hook","what":"Today's specified shape.","gains":["Nothing written into the user's file","Simplest to implement"],"costs":["The hook never fires for the renames that matter","Anchors end up keyed to a path that no longer exists"],"system":"A path index plus a watcher.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"c","recCase":["It is the only option that survives all three out-of-band operations the engine doc already names.","One key in the frontmatter block is the smallest possible addition and renders as an ordinary property.","Write it on first review, never on open, so a read-only pass never modifies a file.","It also makes the sidecar independent of the path, which is what §77.6 assumes and does not provide."],"flip":"A corpus replay showing path plus content-address resolving above 99.5% across rename-and-edit pairs, which makes option d cheaper and leaves the file untouched.","linked":["E22","E3","E37"],"sources":["docs/ENGINE.md:1516","docs/ENGINE.md:1529","docs/ENGINE.md:1626","docs/ENGINE.md:1628","docs/ENGINE.md:1632","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:135","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:527","research briefing 2026-09-09"]},{"id":"E37","cat":"Engine & technical","sub":"Sidecar","weight":"high","q":"What wins when the sidecar and the document disagree, and how does `review.jsonl` merge across branches?","lede":"Two people review on two branches. On a fresh clone git has no driver for our sidecar, so the default is a conflict.","visual":{"kind":"flow","nodes":[{"label":"Branch A appends a record","tone":"neutral"},{"label":"Branch B appends a record","tone":"neutral"},{"label":"git merge","tone":"neutral"},{"label":"No .gitattributes","note":"conflict markers inside JSONL","tone":"stop","edge":"default"},{"label":"merge=union","note":"both lines kept, built in, no local config","tone":"good","edge":"shipped"},{"label":"Reader dedupes by span and hash","tone":"accent"},{"label":"Orphan record marked, never pruned","tone":"accent"}],"perRow":3,"note":"A custom merge driver needs config a clone does not carry, so it silently falls back to a conflict.","caption":"The two paths a merged sidecar can take"},"stakes":"The sidecar is the product's state, and a conflicted or pruned sidecar loses the only record of what a person read.","state":["The sidecar is one JSON line per span, plain text, in the repo (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:135).","Nothing writes it: no anchor store and no re-anchor function exists (docs/ENGINE.md:124).","No `.gitattributes` is shipped and no merge behaviour is written down anywhere.","The projection law makes the document authoritative, so the sidecar can only ever be stale."],"path":["The sidecar was specified as a format, not as a file under concurrent edit.","Git's built-in `union` driver needs only a shipped `.gitattributes`; a custom driver needs local config a fresh clone does not carry [research 2026-09-09].","A record whose hash no longer matches is the product's central event, which is why it must be marked rather than deleted."],"tension":["Union merge keeps every line and makes duplicates and superseded records the reader's problem.","Pruning records that match no span destroys the only evidence that something was reviewed and then moved.","Per-person files avoid merges entirely and split the state a team wants to read as one thing."],"evidence":[],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Ship `.gitattributes` with `merge=union`, dedupe on read, mark orphans","what":"Both branches' lines survive the merge; the reader resolves duplicates; a record with no matching span is marked, never removed.","gains":["Works on a fresh clone with no local configuration","No conflict markers in a file nobody edits by hand","Keeps the evidence that a span was reviewed and then moved"],"costs":["The reader must dedupe and order records","The file grows and needs a compaction story"],"system":"A shipped `.gitattributes`, a dedupe on read, an orphan flag.","screens":"The review panel shows records whose span moved.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"A custom merge driver registered on first run","what":"A driver that understands the record shape.","gains":["Semantic merges rather than line unions","Can resolve duplicates at merge time"],"costs":["Needs local config a fresh clone does not carry","Falls back silently to a conflict for everyone else"],"system":"A driver binary plus install steps.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"One file per person, so two people never touch one file","what":"`.frontmatter/review.<person>.jsonl`.","gains":["Merges cannot conflict","Trivial to reason about"],"costs":["The team view becomes a join across files","A rename of a person's identity splits their history"],"system":"Per-person file naming.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Leave it; resolve conflicts by hand","what":"Today's non-decision.","gains":["Nothing to build"],"costs":["A conflicted JSONL is the first thing a two-person pilot meets","Hand-resolving a machine file loses records"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["Union is the only merge that works on a fresh clone with nothing installed, which is the condition the sidecar has to survive.","Retain and mark is forced by the product: a record whose span moved is the event we exist to show.","Per-person files from option c are compatible with union and can be added later if a team asks for them."],"flip":"A pilot repo where union produces a sidecar the reader cannot dedupe, because two people reviewed the same span at the same hash with different verdicts.","linked":["E22","E35","E36","FL18","L13"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:135","docs/ENGINE.md:124","research briefing 2026-09-09"],"dupes":{"dropped":["FL16"],"why":"Is the review sidecar one shared JSONL with a merge strategy or one file per person. Same option set, both rec (a) but for opposite shapes (E37 merge=union on a shared file, FL16 one file per person) — the merge forces that contradiction into the open. Engine & technical owns the sidecar mechanism."}},{"id":"E14","cat":"Engine & technical","sub":"Enforcement","weight":"medium","q":"Do we replace the byte budget's `echo` with a real bundler budget, or delete the script?","lede":"A product that wants to sell document gates in CI ships a size gate that is a print statement.","visual":{"kind":"ba","before":{"title":"package.json today","lines":[{"t":"\"budget\": \"echo 'No bundle budget…'\"","mark":"stop"},{"t":"not called by `verify`","mark":"stop"}]},"after":{"title":"After a real bundler run","lines":[{"t":"mdmax core: measured gzip size","mark":"good"},{"t":"ceiling set after two weeks of readings","mark":"accent"}]},"via":"one bundler","note":"The proposed ceilings rest on a 15–18 KB estimate the engine doc says must be replaced by a real number first.","caption":"Two placeholders: a script that prints, a ceiling that was guessed"},"stakes":"The packaging story says the splice core is small enough to drop into someone else's host, and nothing has ever measured it.","state":["`\"budget\": \"echo …\"` at package.json:20, and nothing calls it inside `verify` (package.json:19).","The plan budgets two days to replace it (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:218).","ENGINE proposes 20 KB gzip and one runtime dep for the core, 45 KB and two for the certificate subpath (docs/ENGINE.md:2243).","Those ceilings rest on 57,318 stripped bytes across the browser-eligible files, which is a strip count, not a bundle (docs/ENGINE.md:2127)."],"path":["The script was added as a placeholder and never filled in.","The ceilings were derived from stripped source rather than from a bundler.","Nothing published, so nothing forced either number to become real."],"tension":["A gate that fails on day one for reasons nobody can act on trains people to ignore it.","A gate that always passes is the same disease from the other end.","The size number is load-bearing for E24's packaging argument and worth having either way."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"What is actually known about size","items":[["Engine source, all files","3,614 lines / 153,178 bytes","docs/ENGINE.md:2120"],["Comment and whitespace share","51.9%","docs/ENGINE.md:2126"],["Stripped code, browser-eligible files only","57,318 bytes","docs/ENGINE.md:2127"],["Estimated gzip after minification","15–18 KB","docs/ENGINE.md:2243 — marked [derived, estimate]"],["Proposed ceiling for the core","20 KB gzip, 1 runtime dep","docs/ENGINE.md:2243"],["Proposed ceiling for `mdmax/cert`","45 KB gzip, 2 runtime deps","docs/ENGINE.md:2244"],["Actual bundler measurement","none — no bundler is configured for the engine","package.json:20"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Real bundler, report the number, set the ceiling after two weeks of readings","what":"Measure now, gate later, once the real distribution of sizes is known.","gains":["Same work, no false red","Gives E24 a real number to argue from","Nothing is published yet, so the fortnight costs nothing"],"costs":["No enforcement for two weeks"],"system":"Bundler reports into CI output.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Real bundler, with the proposed ceilings as the gate from day one","what":"Measure and enforce immediately at 20 KB and 45 KB gzip.","gains":["A working gate this week"],"costs":["If the estimate is off, the first CI run is red with no plan","The basis is a strip count, not a bundle"],"system":"Bundler in the verify chain.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Leave it","what":"Today's state.","gains":["Nothing to do"],"costs":["Keeps a script whose only effect is to make `verify` look longer than it is","It is not even in that chain"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Delete the script","what":"Remove a gate that always passes.","gains":["Honest; one fewer thing pretending to be a check"],"costs":["Gives up the number the distribution story depends on"],"system":"Removes a script entry.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["The measurement is worth having and the ceiling is not worth guessing.","A harness reporting a false red trains people to ignore it, which is the failure this repo has already paid for.","Land it with the CI file, not as separate work."],"flip":"Deciding never to publish the engine as a package, which makes option c the honest cleanup and frees the two days.","linked":["E12","E24","E25"],"sources":["package.json:19","package.json:20","docs/ENGINE.md:2243","docs/ENGINE.md:2244","docs/ENGINE.md:2127","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:218"]},{"id":"E23","cat":"Engine & technical","sub":"Testing","weight":"medium","q":"Do we adopt fast-check and the twelve properties, adopt four of them, or widen the corpus instead?","lede":"Three of the four defects the engine has shipped live in corpus rows with a count of zero, so the gate cannot see the class.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":190,"cols":[{"title":"Corpus, a byte pin","tone":"warn"},{"title":"Properties","tone":"accent"}],"rows":[{"label":"Files with a BOM","cells":["0","generated"]},{"label":"Files with CRLF","cells":["0","generated"]},{"label":"Files with a bare CR","cells":["0","generated"]},{"label":"Catches the BOM class","cells":["no","only the locality property"]},{"label":"Catches the offset-map defect","cells":["no","only a boundary-biased generator"]},{"label":"In the `verify` chain today","cells":["no","n/a"]}],"note":"The corpus is a sample of what people wrote; a property is a statement about what the code must do.","caption":"Why the standing gate cannot see three of four shipped defects"},"stakes":"Two open byte-destructive defects have no instrument that can see them, and the gate that exists is blind to the class.","state":["No property tests exist; `npm run corpus` hashes files, does not run the writer, and is not in `verify` (package.json:19).","ENGINE §78 specifies twelve properties across four files on fast-check 4.9.0 (docs/ENGINE.md:1730).","The added suite is budgeted at 7.0 s with a build failure above 12 s (docs/ENGINE.md:1913, docs/ENGINE.md:1915).","The corpus has zero BOM, CRLF, bare-CR and unterminated-frontmatter files (docs/ENGINE.md:1746)."],"path":["The corpus was assembled as a fidelity oracle, from files people actually wrote.","A uniform generator reports zero failures against the unfixed offset map, so generator shape is the finding (docs/ENGINE.md:1863).","The zero-indent refusal is correctly invisible to every property, because it is specified behaviour (docs/ENGINE.md:1865)."],"tension":["Twelve properties plus four generator files is real authoring time in a repo measured at 1.21 engineering days per calendar week.","Four of the twelve would have caught every defect this engine has shipped; the other eight guard surfaces that do not exist yet.","Widening the corpus only ever finds what someone thought to add, and a corpus cannot state a contract."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"Which property catches which shipped defect (docs/ENGINE.md:1854-1859)","cols":["Defect","Round-trip","Locality","Idempotence","Offset map"],"rows":[["BOM (fixed, f47555f)","passes on the bug","catches it","passes on the bug","n/a"],["OffsetMap off-by-three (fixed, cc1d451)","n/a","n/a","n/a","catches it — 600 wrong answers"],["Zero-indent sequence (open)","passes","passes","passes","n/a"],["Bare CR (open, live today)","n/a","catches it","n/a","n/a"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"Generator shape decides whether it fires at all","items":[["Uniform generator vs the unfixed OffsetMap","0 failures in 4,966 offsets","docs/ENGINE.md:1863"],["Boundary-straddling generator, same code","600 failures in 9,363","docs/ENGINE.md:1863"],["Corpus-plus-properties, run together","surfaced 21 round-trip failures neither instrument reports alone","docs/ENGINE.md:1760"],["Proposed CI budget for all twelve","7.0 s, fail the build above 12 s","docs/ENGINE.md:1913, docs/ENGINE.md:1915"],["Zero-indent sequence caught by any property","no — and correctly so; properties encode the contract, and the contract is what is wrong","docs/ENGINE.md:1865"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Neither","what":"Today's state.","gains":["No authoring cost"],"costs":["Two open byte-destructive defects stay invisible","The standing gate stays blind to three of four shipped classes"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Widen the corpus instead — add BOM, CRLF and bare-CR files","what":"Extend the sample rather than state contracts.","gains":["Cheaper and familiar","Keeps one instrument"],"costs":["Only ever finds what someone thought to add","A corpus cannot state a contract"],"system":"Corpus additions and new hashes.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Adopt four: round-trip, locality, refusal safety, offset map","what":"The subset that covers every defect class that has actually shipped.","gains":["Covers every shipped defect class at about a third of the authoring","The rest land as the surfaces they guard get built","Corpus goes into `verify` in the same commit"],"costs":["Construct and fold properties wait","Two suites to grow rather than one"],"system":"New dev dependency and two test files.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Adopt fast-check and all twelve properties as specified","what":"The full §78 suite, including brand, fold and construct properties.","gains":["Covers the whole class including surfaces not yet built","One authoring pass instead of two"],"costs":["Four generator files is the real cost, not the 7 seconds of CI","Eight of them guard code that does not exist"],"system":"New dev dependency and four test files.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"c","recCase":["The four properties that would have caught every shipped defect are worth authoring now; the other eight guard nothing that exists.","Build documents from small structured parts, so a counterexample shrinks to a readable record rather than 3 KB of noise.","Store regressions as literal counterexamples, not seed-and-path pairs: a seed stops testing anything the first time the generator changes.","Add `npm run corpus` to the `verify` chain in the same commit; it is not there today."],"flip":"The body-span and anchor work landing, which makes the construct and fold properties concrete and option a the right size.","linked":["E12","E15","E18"],"sources":["docs/ENGINE.md:1730","docs/ENGINE.md:1746","docs/ENGINE.md:1760","docs/ENGINE.md:1854","docs/ENGINE.md:1863","docs/ENGINE.md:1865","docs/ENGINE.md:1889","docs/ENGINE.md:1913","docs/ENGINE.md:1915","package.json:19"]},{"id":"E24","cat":"Engine & technical","sub":"Distribution","weight":"medium","q":"If we publish the engine, what shape and what licence — and does the name survive?","lede":"The package name is free, the product name is taken in two registries, and the repo has no licence file at all.","visual":{"kind":"arch","layers":[{"label":"mdmax-cli","items":["bin","bench","ruby subprocess","MCP server"],"side":"node only","tone":"warn"},{"label":"mdmax/cert subpath","items":["constructs","fold","verdict"],"side":"pulls entities","tone":"neutral"},{"label":"mdmax core","items":["splice","anchors","admission"],"side":"browser-safe, no node built-ins","tone":"accent"},{"label":"Licence","items":["Apache-2.0 with a NOTICE"],"side":"§6 withholds trademark rights","tone":"good"}],"note":"A splice-only consumer must never pull `entities` or `node:child_process` into its graph.","caption":"Two packages from one repo, and what each consumer inherits"},"stakes":"Publishing the wrong shape freezes an API and a name we would then have to break.","state":["`mdmax` returns 404 on the npm registry and `frontmatter` returns 200 (docs/ENGINE.md:2128, docs/ENGINE.md:2130).","There is no LICENSE file in the repo (docs/ENGINE.md:2131).","The gap register records the VS Code incumbent at 82,265 installs and alive, and the `@frontmatter` npm scope held by it (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:132).","ENGINE proposes two packages under Apache-2.0 with a NOTICE (docs/ENGINE.md:2231, docs/ENGINE.md:2237)."],"path":["Nothing has ever been published, so no licence was ever needed.","`bench.ts` imports `node:child_process`, so one accidental barrel export pulls it into a browser bundle.","The name question is worse than the registry collision: \"Frontmatter Studio\" was taken on 2026-09-07."],"tension":["A single package pulls `entities` and a subprocess into a splice-only consumer's graph.","Three packages fragment the version vector for no gain.","Apache-2.0 §6 withholds trademark rights, which MIT would leave entirely to trademark law."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"Registry and licence state","items":[["`mdmax` on npm","HTTP 404 — unregistered","docs/ENGINE.md:2128, fetched 2026-08-30"],["`@sgnk/mdmax`","HTTP 404","docs/ENGINE.md:2129"],["`frontmatter` on npm","HTTP 200 — taken","docs/ENGINE.md:2130"],["`@frontmatter` npm scope","held by the VS Code incumbent","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md"],["VS Code incumbent","82,265 installs, alive at v10.12.0 (2026-08-21)","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md"],["LICENSE file in repo","absent","verified — no LICENSE* exists"],["Engine export declarations","88","docs/ENGINE.md:2121"],["External consumers","1 symbol, at 2 sites","verified by grep"],["Runtime deps of the core","github-slugger (ISC), entities (BSD-2-Clause, undeclared — see E11)","docs/ENGINE.md:2125"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Two packages, Apache-2.0 with a NOTICE, ship under `mdmax`","what":"A browser-safe core with a `mdmax/cert` subpath, and `mdmax-cli` for the bin, bench, ruby and MCP.","gains":["A splice-only consumer pulls neither `entities` nor a subprocess","§6 stops a fork issuing certificates under our name","`mdmax` is free in the registry we would ship to"],"costs":["Two release trains to keep in step","Commits to a public API surface"],"system":"Barrel, subpath exports, two package manifests.","screens":"None.","money":"Zero registry cost; a name decision it does not solve."},{"k":"b","label":"Do not publish; keep the engine inside the product","what":"No public package at all.","gains":["No public commitment to any API","Name question becomes moot for npm"],"costs":["Removes the one route where our reach is someone else's distribution"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"One package, MIT","what":"Everything in one, permissive licence.","gains":["Simplest to publish and to adopt"],"costs":["Pulls the ruby subprocess and certificate dependencies into every consumer","Leaves the certificate's name to trademark law alone"],"system":"One manifest.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Publish the CLI only, not the library","what":"Sell the checker without freezing a library API.","gains":["No API commitment","Smaller surface to support"],"costs":["Needs the CLI to run first, which it does not","No embedding story for another host"],"system":"One bin package.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["Apache-2.0 earns its keep on one point: the certificate is a published claim about seven third-party engines, and a fork must not issue it under our name.","The two-package split is what keeps the core small enough for the packaging story to be true.","Add the LICENSE file whatever else is decided — there is none today.","Resolve the name in the same meeting: `mdmax` is free where the engine would ship, `frontmatter` is not."],"flip":"Deciding never to publish, which leaves the licence file worth adding and everything else here moot.","linked":["E14","E25","FF12","L20"],"sources":["docs/ENGINE.md:2128","docs/ENGINE.md:2130","docs/ENGINE.md:2131","docs/ENGINE.md:2231","docs/ENGINE.md:2237","docs/ENGINE.md:2243","docs/ENGINE.md:2251","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:132"]},{"id":"E25","cat":"Engine & technical","sub":"Boundary","weight":"medium","q":"Do we cut the engine to a 31-symbol barrel, move the splice writer inside it, and enforce the boundary mechanically?","lede":"There is no API, there is a folder other folders reach into, and the engine's central function lives outside it.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":200,"cols":[{"title":"Today","tone":"warn"},{"title":"Barrel plus an engine element type","tone":"accent"}],"rows":[{"label":"Public symbols","cells":["88 exports, no index.ts","31 in six capability groups"]},{"label":"Where the splice writer lives","cells":["`share/domain`","`mdmax/domain`"]},{"label":"Copies of the key rule","cells":["two: engine and panel","one"]},{"label":"Would a gate catch mdmax importing vault?","cells":["no, all three permit it","yes"]},{"label":"Transitive `node:` leak into the browser","cells":["undetected","caught by the purity harness"]}],"note":"`export *` would freeze `unsafeU16` as public API forever, so the barrel has to be enumerated.","caption":"What the boundary costs to state, and what stating it buys"},"stakes":"A purity violation discovered after publication is a breaking change rather than a refactor.","state":["88 export declarations across 13 files, no index.ts, one external consumer deep-importing for a single symbol (docs/ENGINE.md:2121, docs/ENGINE.md:2133).","`splice-frontmatter.ts` lives in `share/domain` and the properties panel imports it across a module boundary (docs/ENGINE.md:575).","Every import inside `mdmax/` already resolves to a sibling, `entities`, `github-slugger` or `node:*` (docs/ENGINE.md:546).","`npm run arch` maps every module's domain folder to one element type, so all three gates permit mdmax importing vault (docs/ENGINE.md:548)."],"path":["Every other module has an index.ts; mdmax never got one because it never had a second consumer.","Nothing enforces the writer's purity because it sits in another module.","A second copy of SAFE_KEY grew in the UI for the same reason."],"tension":["`infrastructure/bench.ts` imports `node:child_process`, so one accidental barrel export reaches the client bundle.","A per-file lint rule structurally cannot see a transitive node built-in three files down.","The distribution story depends on a property nothing currently checks."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"The surface, measured","items":[["Engine files / lines","13 / 3,614","docs/ENGINE.md:2120"],["`export` declarations","88","docs/ENGINE.md:2121"],["Symbols consumed from outside","1 — `decodeStrict`","verified by grep"],["Imports mdmax makes from other modules","0 — the rule holds and nothing enforces it (see E28)","docs/ENGINE.md:546"],["Real `throw` sites","2","docs/ENGINE.md:2124"],["Proposed barrel","31 symbols in six capability groups","docs/ENGINE.md:2137"]]},{"type":"table","title":"Three structural moves that come with the barrel","cols":["Move","Reason","Risk if skipped"],"rows":[["Move splice-frontmatter.ts into mdmax/domain/","it is the engine's central contract living outside the module","nothing enforces its purity; the UI grew a second SAFE_KEY. Move it — do not copy it: two writers is how the shipped write paths diverged in the first place"],["bench.ts behind a node-only subpath","it imports node:child_process, node:fs, node:path","one barrel export pulls node built-ins into the browser bundle"],["Collapse slugStamp/foldStamp/normalizeStamp into one stamp()","a consumer recording three of four stamps has an unreproducible artifact","certificates that cannot be replayed"]]},{"type":"table","title":"Would each gate catch mdmax importing from vault? (docs/ENGINE.md:548-552)","cols":["Gate","What it checks","Catches it"],"rows":[["eslint-plugin-boundaries","maps every module domain to the single type `domain`; allows domain to domain","no"],["`npm run arch`","layer direction only; layerOf() discards the module name","no"],["import-boundary-report.mjs","substring ban on @/server, @/lib, @/components","no"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"Cost, and the traps to avoid","items":[["Fix","one boundaries element type, declared before the generic per-module patterns so it wins","docs/ENGINE.md:554"],["Anti-recommendation","do not move mdmax to src/shared — shared-domain is importable by everything and would still permit the reverse import","docs/ENGINE.md:554"],["What a per-file lint rule cannot see","a transitive `node:fs` three files down through a type-only-looking import — exactly how bench.ts would leak into a browser bundle","docs/ENGINE.md:2170"],["Why the new harness needs a denominator guard","clean-architecture-report.mjs once reported 0 violations and exit 0 whether it had scanned 208 files or zero; today it carries MIN_SCANNED_FILES = 50, so `arch` itself can no longer go blind","docs/ENGINE.md:2168, docs/ENGINE.md:554"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Leave it; deep imports are fine for one consumer","what":"Today's state.","gains":["No work"],"costs":["True until the second consumer","The packaging story assumes several"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Barrel and the eslint rule only","what":"State the API, catch direct imports.","gains":["One line of config","Catches the obvious case"],"costs":["Misses the transitive case, which is exactly how bench.ts reaches a browser bundle"],"system":"index.ts plus a lint rule.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"`export *` from a barrel","what":"One line, everything public.","gains":["Immediate"],"costs":["Freezes all 88 symbols including `unsafeU16`","Which can then never be removed"],"system":"One line.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Barrel, the three moves, and the transitive purity harness in `verify`","what":"An enumerated index.ts, the splice writer moved inside, an `engine` element type and a harness with a denominator guard.","gains":["One public surface instead of a folder","The rules apply to the file that matters most","Catches the transitive leak a lint rule cannot see"],"costs":["One more harness to maintain","It must not be able to pass by scanning nothing"],"system":"index.ts, one file move, one element type, one harness.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"d","recCase":["An enumerated barrel is the difference between an API and a folder, and the move puts the module's rules on the file with real traffic.","The rule already holds, so enforcing it costs nothing now and everything later.","The denominator guard is not decoration: a gate here once reported a clean pass while scanning zero files."],"flip":"Deciding the engine is never lifted out of this repo, which makes option b proportionate.","linked":["E14","E2","E24"],"sources":["docs/ENGINE.md:546","docs/ENGINE.md:548","docs/ENGINE.md:554","docs/ENGINE.md:575","docs/ENGINE.md:2120","docs/ENGINE.md:2121","docs/ENGINE.md:2133","docs/ENGINE.md:2137","docs/ENGINE.md:2149","docs/ENGINE.md:2159","docs/ENGINE.md:2168","docs/ENGINE.md:2170","merged: E28"]},{"id":"AC1","cat":"Access, offline & install","sub":"Web byte path","weight":"critical","q":"In the web app, does the browser read the repository, or does our server read it and hand the bytes on?","lede":"Zero document bytes in our control plane is the claim a server-side rival cannot copy, and the code breaks it in three places.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":210,"cols":[{"title":"Browser, per file","tone":"neutral"},{"title":"Browser, tarball","tone":"accent"},{"title":"Server tarball (today)","tone":"stop"}],"rows":[{"label":"Whole-vault read inside 5,000 req/hr","cells":["No: 5,833 calls","Yes, one call","Yes, one call"]},{"label":"Who touches the bytes","cells":["Browser only","Browser only","Our server, then the browser"]},{"label":"Claim survives","cells":["Until a feature reads everything","Yes","No"]},{"label":"Untested assumption","cells":["None","Zipball redirect under CORS","None: it already ships"]},{"label":"Ceiling","cells":["Per-file latency","88.1 MB unzipped in a tab","16.4x the Vercel body cap"]}],"note":"F7 reads every markdown file by definition, so the first column breaks on an MVP-0 feature.","caption":"Three read shapes against GitHub's rate limit and the byte claim."},"stakes":"Lose this and the web app is a hosted editor competing on features with free ones.","state":["The week-0 draft proposes browser-side only: no document byte passes through a Zephyrus server (docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:35).","The code does the opposite. One operator token on every call (`src/shared/infrastructure/github/client.ts:30`), a whole-repo zipball (`client.ts:78`), and a server-parsed vault from `GET /api/vault/snapshot`.","The plan lists the byte path as `Decision` with no days (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:221) and puts it in week 0 (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:368)."],"path":["The editor was forked from sgnk-md, a single-tenant hosted workspace that held documents by design.","An earlier round recommended the server lane: mint a 1-hour installation token, read a tarball (docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r20-q4-repo-and-folders.md:9).","The claim went into the architecture section later, and nobody reconciled it with the read path."],"tension":["The installation floor is 5,000 requests an hour and the founder's vault is 5,832 markdown files, so per-file reads cannot finish a whole-vault pass (r20-q4:38, :40).","The only whole-vault read that fits is a tarball, and 88.1 MB unzipped in a tab moves the cold-start problem rather than solving it.","Nothing here shows a browser can follow the zipball redirect to codeload; the draft admits one check is outstanding (docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:54).","Git-backed markdown editing is already free. Pages CMS is MIT with 3,976 stars and no paid tier, and it makes no claim about where the bytes go."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"The numbers that constrain the byte path","items":[["GitHub installation rate limit, floor","5,000 req/hr","r20-q4:38, fetched 2026-08-31; hard cap 12,500"],["Whole-vault per-file read of the founder's md vault","5,833 calls","5,832 .md + 1 tree call = 1.17× the floor; r20-q4:40"],["Markdown bytes in that vault","88.1 MB","88,137,142 bytes, measured by find/cat 2026-08-31, r20-q4:40"],["The same vault measured two days earlier","77.5 MB across 4,548 .md","r11 c2:19, measured 2026-08-29 — same vault, different date, not a contradiction"],["Installation token lifetime","1 hour","r20-q4:33; expired token returns 401, so mint per request"],["Whether a browser can follow api.github.com's zipball redirect to codeload","never tested in this corpus","the WEEK0 CORS note covers the REST API generally, not the zipball redirect"]]},{"type":"table","title":"Four read shapes, and what each costs","cols":["Read shape","Fits the rate limit?","Who touches the bytes","Preserves the claim?"],"rows":[["Browser, per file, lazy","For opening files as the user clicks them, yes. For any whole-vault pass — search index, F7 docs scan — no: 5,833 calls is 1.17× the floor","Browser only","Yes, until a feature needs the whole vault"],["Browser, tarball fetched and unzipped in the page","Yes, 1 call","Browser only","Yes; ceiling is browser memory at 88.1 MB, and the redirect is untested under CORS"],["Browser, raw.githubusercontent.com","Yes — unauthenticated, off the REST bucket, sends access-control-allow-origin: *","Browser only","Yes, but public repositories only (PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:310)"],["Server, tarball plus a server-rendered snapshot (today's code)","Yes, 1 call","Our server, then the browser","No — this is the shipped path"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Browser reads each file as you open it, with a published vault ceiling","what":"The browser fetches one file at a time with the user's installation token.","gains":["No document byte reaches us while you are opening files","No zipball redirect assumption to test","Cheapest thing to build once the App exists"],"costs":["5,833 calls is 1.17x the 5,000/hr floor, so a whole-vault pass cannot finish","F7's docs scan reads every file, so it breaks first","The refusal lands on the user, not on us"],"system":"A per-file adapter behind the same port the desktop filesystem uses.","screens":"A ceiling notice on the repo picker. No new screen.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Browser fetches the tarball and unzips it in the page","what":"One call returns the whole repository and the tab unzips it in memory.","gains":["One call, well inside the rate limit","Bytes never leave the browser","Whole-vault features keep working"],"costs":["88.1 MB of markdown in a tab, a ceiling we would have to publish","The zipball redirect has never been tested from a browser","Cold start moves into the tab rather than going away"],"system":"Unzip and parse in a worker. The snapshot route and its 3-entry LRU are deleted.","screens":"A loading state on first connect.","money":"Removes the server-side parse, so function time drops."},{"k":"c","label":"Our server reads the tarball, as today, and we drop the claim for the web","what":"Keep `/api/vault/snapshot` and rewrite the architecture section to say the web app is server-mediated.","gains":["Already built, so no days at all","No rate-limit or memory ceiling in the browser"],"costs":["Spends the one differentiator a server-side rival cannot copy","Makes us a processor of the user's documents under DPDP and GDPR","The snapshot is already 16.4x the Vercel body cap (r11 c2:24)"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"Function time scales with vault size."},{"k":"d","label":"No repo lane on the web at all","what":"The web app opens files you drop on it, and GitHub is a desktop feature.","gains":["The claim is true by construction","Nothing to build"],"costs":["The web app stops being a trial anyone can finish","Every repo user meets a download before seeing the product"],"system":"Delete the GitHub client from the web build.","screens":"The repo picker goes. Drag-in becomes the only entry.","money":"None."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["One tarball call is the only whole-vault read inside GitHub's own floor that keeps the bytes out of our server.","F7 reads every markdown file by definition, so per-file lazy reads break on a feature the plan ships in MVP-0.","Publish the memory ceiling. The plan already says the web app is the trial and the desktop app is the daily surface (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:106).","Spike the redirect for one day before this is recorded as decided."],"flip":"The spike shows a browser cannot follow the zipball redirect, or 88 MB kills a tab, in which case (c) is the only working option and the claim is rewritten in the same edit.","linked":["AC14","AC19","AC3","F25"],"sources":["docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:35","docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:39","docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:54","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:221","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:310","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:368","src/shared/infrastructure/github/client.ts:30","src/shared/infrastructure/github/client.ts:78","src/app/api/vault/snapshot/route.ts","src/modules/vault/infrastructure/snapshot-cache.ts","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r20-q4-repo-and-folders.md:9","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r20-q4-repo-and-folders.md:38","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r20-q4-repo-and-folders.md:40","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-29-r11/c2-architecture-decisions.md:19"],"dupes":{"dropped":["L2"],"why":"Does the browser read the repository or does our server hand the bytes on. Answering AC1 settles L2 in both directions (browser path keeps the zero-bytes claim; server path withdraws it). Access, offline & install owns the web byte path and states the three read shapes mechanically."}},{"id":"AC3","cat":"Access, offline & install","sub":"GitHub access","weight":"critical","q":"Does the GitHub App launch with three permissions, or four with `pull_requests: write`?","lede":"Every repository read uses one operator token against one allowlisted login, and the set that replaces it can never be widened quietly.","visual":{"kind":"flow","perRow":3,"nodes":[{"label":"A repo admin clicks Install","note":"no org owner, no ticket","tone":"neutral"},{"label":"Consent screen, three lines","note":"contents, metadata, emails","tone":"accent","edge":"then"},{"label":"Repo picker, one repo","note":"about forty seconds","tone":"neutral","edge":"then"},{"label":"Token minted per request","note":"one hour, never persisted","tone":"neutral","edge":"then"},{"label":"Later: add pull_requests","note":"every installation owner re-approves","tone":"warn","edge":"if"},{"label":"Unapproved installs keep the old set","note":"so the launch list is frozen in practice","tone":"stop","edge":"and"}],"note":"Any organisation permission replaces the first node with an org owner and a ticket.","caption":"Why the launch permission list cannot be widened quietly."},"stakes":"Ask one permission too many and every install needs an org owner; ask too few and widening it later means re-consenting the whole base.","state":["Every repository call carries one operator token (`src/config/env.ts:85`, `src/shared/infrastructure/github/client.ts:30`).","Sign-in is gated on a single login, defaulting to `sagnikmitra` (`src/config/env.ts:47`, `src/modules/auth/infrastructure/auth-options.ts:82`).","There is no installation code in `src/`, so a pilot with strangers cannot physically run today."],"path":["The app is a fork of sgnk-md, a single-tenant personal workspace.","The earlier round named this token the single largest unshipped liability in the repo (docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r20-q7-one-page.md:96)."],"tension":["Deleting the operator token is forced under every option but (d). The permission list is the part that is genuinely decidable.","Changing permissions later prompts every installation owner to re-approve, and unapproved installs keep the old set (r20-q4:37).","Zero organisation permissions is what lets a repo admin install alone in about forty seconds (r20-q7:46).","A team reviewer wants a real pull request with a title and a body, and that is the fourth line."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"The permission ladder, from GitHub's own docs (fetched 2026-08-31, r20-q4 §101.2)","cols":["Permission","Buys","Cost of asking"],"rows":[["contents: write","Read bytes, splice writes, blobs/trees/commits/refs, create a branch","Required for every save"],["metadata: read","Repo listing; force-granted with any other permission","None"],["emails: read","Billing contact","One line on the consent screen"],["pull_requests: write","We open the PR ourselves","A fourth line, and a re-consent campaign if added later"],["Any organization permission","Org-wide install, seat provisioning","Every install routes through an org owner and a ticket, instead of a repo admin acting alone in forty seconds"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"What is in the code today","items":[["Repository tokens in the product","1, operator-held","GITHUB_REPO_TOKEN, env.ts:85 and client.ts:30"],["Logins permitted to sign in","1","ALLOWED_GH_LOGIN default \"sagnikmitra\", env.ts:47, enforced at auth-options.ts:82"],["Installation-flow code in src/","0 occurrences","grep for \"installation\" returns nothing"],["Installation token TTL, if built","1 hour","mint per request, never persist (r20-q4:33)"],["Token format change already rolling out","stateless ghs_APPID_JWT since 2026-04-27","anything assuming a fixed ghs_ length breaks (r20-q4:36)"],["Permission changes after launch","every installation owner re-approves; unapproved installs keep the old set","r20-q4:37"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Three permissions, and no organisation permission, ever","what":"A repo admin installs alone and we hand the user GitHub's own compare banner instead of opening pull requests.","gains":["A three-line consent screen with a repo picker","Review before merge costs no extra permission","One sentence a security reviewer can check rather than take on trust"],"costs":["We cannot open a pull request with a title and a body","Adding that permission later means a re-consent campaign"],"system":"Branch and hand off, rather than a PR API call.","screens":"A consent screen, a repo picker, and a compare link after a save.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"The same three, plus pull_requests:write taken at launch","what":"We open the pull request ourselves, with a body listing the splices.","gains":["The flow a team reviewer actually wants","No re-consent campaign later"],"costs":["A fourth consent line at the moment we have the least trust","It can never be removed either"],"system":"A PR builder that renders the splice list.","screens":"A review-and-open-PR step after a save.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"OAuth with the repo scope","what":"One sign-in screen, no install step, one token across everything the user can reach.","gains":["Fewest steps to a first file","No installation flow to build"],"costs":["All or nothing across every repository the user can reach","Never expires, and invisible to an org owner per repo","It is the opposite of the promise the product sells"],"system":"No installation code, one long-lived token.","screens":"A sign-in screen instead of an install flow.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Keep the operator token through the pilot and build the App afterwards","what":"The ten strangers use our repository, not theirs.","gains":["Zero build cost now","The pilot can start a fortnight earlier"],"costs":["The pilot measures nothing about real repositories","The founder's credential sits in the read path for other people's work","It is the liability the research already named"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["Zero organisation permissions is a distribution decision that happens to also be a security decision.","Branch and hand off buys review before merge without asking for a fourth line.","Delete `GITHUB_REPO_TOKEN` before the first external user, whichever option wins."],"flip":"The buyer decision lands on the team rather than the solo developer, in which case take `pull_requests: write` at launch while the installed base is still ten people.","linked":["AC1","AC19"],"sources":["src/config/env.ts:47","src/config/env.ts:85","src/modules/auth/infrastructure/auth-options.ts:82","src/shared/infrastructure/github/client.ts:30","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r20-q4-repo-and-folders.md:22","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r20-q4-repo-and-folders.md:27","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r20-q4-repo-and-folders.md:37","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r20-q4-repo-and-folders.md:151","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r20-q7-one-page.md:96","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r20-q7-one-page.md:46"]},{"id":"AC8","cat":"Access, offline & install","sub":"Desktop shell","weight":"critical","q":"Do we rebuild the Tauri shell as a bundled local app before signing anything, or keep it as an unsigned internal artefact?","lede":"The desktop app as configured cannot open a local file, and signing it would attest to a shell any web deploy can swap.","visual":{"kind":"ba","before":{"title":"The shell today","lines":[{"t":"frontendDist points at https://md.sgnk.ai","mark":"remote"},{"t":"security.csp","mark":"null"},{"t":"tauri-plugin-fs","mark":"absent"},{"t":"Filesystem permissions in capabilities","mark":"none"},{"t":"Bundled assets, so a window offline","mark":"none"}]},"after":{"title":"After the rebuild","lines":[{"t":"Frontend bundled inside the app","mark":"local"},{"t":"Scoped filesystem capability","mark":"opens files"},{"t":"A real content security policy","mark":"set"},{"t":"Update channels","mark":"one, signed"},{"t":"Works with no network","mark":"yes"}]},"via":"4 to 8 weeks","note":"The research calls signing the current configuration security theatre.","caption":"What signing would attest to today, against what it should attest to."},"stakes":"Signing the shell as configured certifies a payload any web deploy can replace thirty seconds later.","state":["`src-tauri/tauri.conf.json` points frontendDist, devUrl and the window url at https://md.sgnk.ai, with `security.csp` null and every signing field null.","`src-tauri/Cargo.toml` carries plugins for shell, os, process, clipboard and dialog, and neither a filesystem nor an updater plugin.","`src-tauri/capabilities/default.json` grants no filesystem permission, so the app cannot open a file in the user's home directory."],"path":["The shell was inherited whole from sgnk-md, a hosted workspace in a native window.","Nothing about it was rebuilt for a local-first product."],"tension":["The remote origin is a second, unsigned update channel running beside the signed one, with no version gate and no rollback (k9:113).","The shell cannot do the product's core job, which is locating a byte range in a file on disk (k9:115).","The rebuild is the 4-to-8-week item AC2 shows the plan has no days for.","The research's anti-recommendation is a hybrid: bundle the editor, keep auth and the model as network calls, set a real policy (k9:121)."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"The shell as configured, read from the repo","items":[["frontendDist / devUrl / window url","https://md.sgnk.ai","tauri.conf.json — the shell loads remote content, not bundled assets"],["security.csp","null","the one mitigation Tauri offers for a remote-origin window is off"],["bundle.macOS.signingIdentity","null","nothing is signed; Tauri's hardened runtime default applies only when an identity exists"],["tauri-plugin-fs in Cargo.toml","absent","the desktop app cannot read a local file at all"],["tauri-plugin-updater in Cargo.toml","absent","no update channel of any kind"],["Filesystem permissions in capabilities/default.json","none","core, event, window, webview, shell, os, process, clipboard, dialog only"]]},{"type":"table","title":"What each path actually delivers","cols":["Path","Opens a local file?","One verified update channel?","Offline?"],"rows":[["Sign and ship the shell as it is","No","No — two channels, one unsigned","No — no bundled assets means no window content without a network"],["Bundle the frontend, add scoped fs, set a CSP, then sign","Yes","Yes","Yes"],["Keep it unsigned as an internal beta","No","n/a","No"],["Drop the desktop build from MVP-0","n/a","n/a","n/a"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Bundle the frontend, declare a scoped fs capability, set a real CSP, then sign","what":"The desktop product as designed: real files, offline, one verified update channel.","gains":["The only version worth shipping to a stranger","Offline becomes true rather than claimed","One update channel to reason about"],"costs":["4 to 8 weeks the schedule has no room for","Absorbing it into a one-day rename row is how it stays invisible"],"system":"Bundled assets, `tauri-plugin-fs` with a scoped capability, a content security policy.","screens":"A folder picker and an offline state that actually works.","money":"None beyond the days."},{"k":"b","label":"Keep the remote shell as an unsigned internal artefact only","what":"A wrapper we hand to people we can tell it is a wrapper, to smoke-test window chrome and menus.","gains":["Costs nothing and keeps the option open","Honest about what it is"],"costs":["It is not a shipping posture","It must never appear on a download page"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None public.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Sign and notarise the shell now, so there is a download to point at","what":"Buy the certificate, run notarisation, publish the current wrapper.","gains":["A download link exists","The signing pipeline gets exercised early"],"costs":["Ships a product that cannot open a file","Attests to a payload we can change from a web deploy","Mis-sells anyone who downloads a desktop markdown editor"],"system":"No change to the shell, only to the release pipeline.","screens":"A download page for something that does not work.","money":"99 USD/year spent to certify a URL wrapper."},{"k":"d","label":"Drop the desktop build from MVP-0 entirely","what":"No desktop artefact of any kind this cycle.","gains":["Consistent with a web-first MVP-0","Nothing to sign, rename or update"],"costs":["Removes offline and the local-folder lane from anything a user can hold this year","Leaves the shell rotting in the repo"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["Rule out (c) permanently. Signing a URL wrapper spends a certificate to certify whatever was deployed thirty seconds ago.","(b) costs nothing and keeps the option open while the schedule is decided.","When desktop is genuinely scheduled, (a) is the only version worth building, budgeted as the 4 to 8 weeks it is."],"flip":"AC2 sends the pilot to a desktop build, in which case (a) moves to now and the schedule has to admit it.","linked":["AC10","AC18","AC6","FF8"],"sources":["src-tauri/tauri.conf.json","src-tauri/Cargo.toml","src-tauri/capabilities/default.json","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-29-r12/k9-desktop-distribution.md:113","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-29-r12/k9-desktop-distribution.md:115","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-29-r12/k9-desktop-distribution.md:121","docs/research/prd-v2-sections/35-platform-surfaces.md:311","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r19-p2-offline-or-online.md"]},{"id":"AC14","cat":"Access, offline & install","sub":"Web byte path","weight":"critical","q":"Do we delete the server-side PDF route, or amend the zero-document-bytes claim to admit it?","lede":"Fixing the read path leaves one route that sends a whole file to a server by design rather than by accident.","visual":{"kind":"screen","title":"Export menu, as shipped","panes":[{"label":"Export","w":1,"rows":[{"label":"Download .md","meta":"Blob in the browser","mark":"local","tone":"good"},{"label":"Export HTML","meta":"Blob in the browser","mark":"local","tone":"good"},{"label":"Export Word (.doc)","meta":"Blob in the browser","mark":"local","tone":"good"},{"label":"Open PDF (print)","meta":"Blob, then window.print()","mark":"local","tone":"good"},{"label":"Download PDF","meta":"Headless Chromium on our server","mark":"server","tone":"stop"}]}],"note":"One of five items sends the whole file to us, and a browser PDF path already ships above it.","caption":"Where each export runs, read from the shipped menu."},"stakes":"A security reviewer finds a route that contradicts the published architecture, and the contradiction reads worse than the feature.","state":["`src/app/api/export/pdf/[...path]/route.ts:60` fetches the file server-side and renders it with headless Chromium, pulling mermaid and KaTeX from CDNs.","The route is gated on a Linux platform check (`route.ts:108`), so it can never run in the desktop app.","The plan says the control plane holds no document bytes in two places (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:123, :133).","A browser PDF path already ships one line above it (`src/modules/export/presentation/ExportMenu.tsx:159`)."],"path":["Export was inherited whole from sgnk-md, which did hold documents.","The plan already flags one contradiction this route creates, in F13's needs column (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:67), and not the byte-path one."],"tension":["Deciding AC1 for browser-side reads removes the zipball and the snapshot. This route survives, because rendering is its whole point.","Every future statement of the differentiator would carry a clause, and a clause is what a competitor quotes back.","Folder-to-one-PDF is the only export with demonstrated demand, and it makes a server renderer hard to avoid (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:67)."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"The five export menu items, and where each runs","cols":["Menu item","Where it runs","Document bytes reach our server?"],"rows":[["Download .md","Browser, Blob + object URL","No"],["Export HTML","Browser, Blob","No"],["Export Word (.doc) — Word opens HTML","Browser, Blob","No"],["Open PDF (print)","Browser, Blob + window.print()","No"],["Download PDF","Server route, headless Chromium on Linux","Yes — the whole file"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"What the route actually does","items":[["File fetched","server-side","container.getFile(vaultPath), route.ts:60"],["Renderer","@sparticuz/chromium + puppeteer-core","dynamically imported inside the handler"],["External calls at render time","mermaid via CDN, KaTeX via CDN","route.ts header, lines 4–13"],["Platform gate","process.platform === \"linux\"","route.ts:108 — cannot run in the desktop app"],["Browser PDF path already shipped","\"Open PDF (print)\" is a live menu item","ExportMenu.tsx:159 → export-doc.ts:130"],["Plan's claim","\"zero document bytes\" in the control plane","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:123 and :133"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Delete the server PDF route and keep the browser print item","what":"One route and one menu item go; the replacement already ships next to it.","gains":["The claim becomes true with no asterisk","Removes a route that can never run on desktop","Stops reaching two CDNs from our infrastructure while rendering a user's document"],"costs":["No server-controlled page setup","PDF output depends on the browser's print dialogue"],"system":"Delete `src/app/api/export/pdf/`.","screens":"The export menu loses one item, from five to four.","money":"Removes a Chromium cold start from the function bill."},{"k":"b","label":"Keep it and amend the claim to name the exception","what":"The claim becomes zero document bytes except a PDF you export, one file at a time, when you ask.","gains":["Honest and precise","Keeps the better PDF output"],"costs":["Every statement of the differentiator now carries a clause","The clause is quotable by anyone selling against us"],"system":"No change to code, one change to the architecture text.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Keep it for the web and build a native PDF path on desktop","what":"Two renderers, one per surface.","gains":["Best output on both surfaces","Desktop rendering never leaves the machine"],"costs":["Two rendering paths to keep byte-identical","The web claim still needs the clause from (b)"],"system":"A second renderer inside the Tauri build.","screens":"None visible.","money":"Desktop rendering costs nothing; the web route still bills."},{"k":"d","label":"Keep it and say nothing","what":"Leave the route and the claim as they are.","gains":["No work","The better PDF output stays"],"costs":["The first security review finds it","Being found is worse than the feature is worth"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["One export format is not worth an asterisk on the only claim a server-side rival cannot copy.","The replacement is already a shipped menu item directly above it.","It also removes a route that can never work in the desktop app, so the two surfaces stop diverging."],"flip":"Folder-to-one-PDF ships, at which point a server renderer is hard to avoid and the clause goes into the plan before the feature does.","linked":["AC1","F16"],"sources":["src/app/api/export/pdf/[...path]/route.ts:60","src/app/api/export/pdf/[...path]/route.ts:108","src/modules/export/presentation/export-doc.ts:115","src/modules/export/presentation/export-doc.ts:130","src/modules/export/presentation/ExportMenu.tsx:159","src/modules/export/presentation/ExportMenu.tsx:160","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:67","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:123","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:133","docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:35"]},{"id":"AC4","cat":"Access, offline & install","sub":"Browser lanes","weight":"high","q":"Do we ship the File System Access path on the web at all, when two earlier accepted rounds cut it?","lede":"The plan reversed a research decision without noting it, and the number that would settle the reversal can be measured for free.","visual":{"kind":"flow","perRow":3,"nodes":[{"label":"Someone opens the web app","note":"no install, no account yet","tone":"neutral"},{"label":"Chrome or Edge on desktop","note":"folder picker, direct writes","tone":"good","edge":"yes"},{"label":"Firefox, Safari, mobile","note":"no folder picker exists","tone":"stop","edge":"no"},{"label":"Connect a GitHub repo","note":"the one lane that works everywhere","tone":"accent","edge":"either"},{"label":"Download the desktop build","note":"a conversion step at peak intent","tone":"warn","edge":"otherwise"}],"note":"Chrome Android is unreconciled between two sources and should not be built on.","caption":"The fork a visitor with a plain folder hits, by browser."},"stakes":"Ship it and some share of desktop visitors meets a refusal from a product whose positioning is that its refusals are principled.","state":["The plan ships it. Exhibit 2 gives the web local-folder lane a full column and the API is desktop Chrome and Edge only (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:102).","The week-0 draft keeps it too (docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:41).","No `showDirectoryPicker` code exists in `src/`."],"path":["It is the only zero-install route to a plain folder, so it fills the hole left by users with no repository.","Two earlier reports cut it on the same facts (r20-q4:11, r20-q7:78), and the reversal was never noted."],"tension":["The refusal rate has never been measured. The only figure is an assumption chain marked derived by its own author.","Measuring it costs a script tag on the landing page and needs no adapter at all.","The corpus disagrees with itself on Chrome Android: BCD says 132, caniuse says no (s4-mobile-cross-device.md:202).","AC2's recommendation leaves no days for the roughly two-week adapter."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"Support, as three sources in this corpus report it","cols":["Source","Chrome/Edge desktop","Firefox","Safari / iOS","Chrome Android"],"rows":[["PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:102 (caniuse, 2026-09-08)","Yes","No","No","No"],["r20-q4 §101.1 line 11 (MDN BCD, 2026-08-31)","Chrome 86+, Edge mirrors","version_added: false","version_added: false","132+"],["s4-mobile-cross-device.md:202 (2026-08-31)","—","—","—","BCD 132 vs caniuse and_chr 151 \"n\" — recorded as unreconciled, do not build on either number without re-testing"],["18-simplicity.md:283 (2026-08-31)","—","—","BCD says safari 15.2 for the handle interfaces; caniuse says \"n\" for the feature at every iOS version through 26.6 — both correct at different granularity, so cite the picker, not the interface","same unreconciled note"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"The refusal rate is assumed, not measured","items":[["Chromium share of desktop browsing used in the estimate","~70%","r19-p2 §91.3, explicitly [derived] from an assumed input"],["Share assumed for our audience","80%","also assumed — the source's words are \"call it 80%\""],["Resulting refusal rate","1 in 5 desktop visitors","at 10,000 users, 2,000 first experiences that are a refusal"],["Times the real rate has been measured","0","no analytics on browser mix exists in the corpus"],["Cost of measuring it properly","a script tag on the landing page","the browser mix of people who arrive does not require the adapter to exist"],["API status flag in MDN BCD","experimental: true, secure-context only","fetched 2026-08-31"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Ship it on Chrome and Edge, labelled as limited before the click","what":"A folder picker appears for the majority browser and a refusal for the rest.","gains":["Zero-install access to a plain folder","Covers the users with no GitHub repository"],"costs":["A refusal on the surface where a broken promise is most expensive","About two weeks of adapter work the schedule has no room for"],"system":"A File System Access adapter behind the same port as the desktop filesystem.","screens":"A folder picker and a permission prompt, plus a browser-support line on the page.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Cut it: the desktop build owns plain folders, the web build owns GitHub","what":"Two honest promises instead of one hedged one.","gains":["What both earlier rounds recommended, on facts that have not changed","No adapter, no browser matrix, no unreconciled Android row"],"costs":["Every local-folder user meets a download at the moment of highest intent","That is a conversion cliff the plan has no distribution to absorb"],"system":"One fewer adapter to keep in step with the engine.","screens":"A download prompt where the folder picker would have been.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Instrument the landing page for browser mix now, decide when the number arrives","what":"Count what browsers actually turn up before building anything.","gains":["Turns an assumed refusal rate into a measured one","Costs a script tag, and the same instrumentation AC6 needs for the OS mix"],"costs":["Four weeks of waiting","Free only if MVP-0 is web-against-a-repo anyway"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Ship it, with drag-and-drop read-only as the Firefox and Safari fallback","what":"Nobody meets a dead end, but the fallback cannot persist anything.","gains":["No visible refusal on any browser","Firefox and Safari visitors can at least read"],"costs":["Review state silently does not work for those users","A silent failure is worse than a clear refusal","Two adapters instead of one"],"system":"A read-only session adapter alongside the folder one.","screens":"A drag target that quietly cannot save.","money":"None."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["Two prior rounds cut this lane on facts that have not changed, and there are no days to build the adapter.","Run (c) in the same week regardless. The deciding number does not exist anywhere in two weeks of research.","If it ever does ship, the page must say Chrome and Edge before the click, never after it."],"flip":"A measured Chromium share well above the assumed 80%, together with pilot candidates who keep documents in plain folders rather than repositories.","linked":["AC12","AC17","AC6"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:102","docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:41","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r20-q4-repo-and-folders.md:11","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r20-q4-repo-and-folders.md:80","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r20-q7-one-page.md:78","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r19-p2-offline-or-online.md","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-29-r8to10/s4-mobile-cross-device.md:202","docs/research/prd-v2-sections/18-simplicity.md:283"]},{"id":"AC6","cat":"Access, offline & install","sub":"Desktop platforms","weight":"high","q":"Does v1 of the desktop app ship macOS only, and when Windows comes, what does signing it actually cost?","lede":"The plan promises three installers and states a Windows price that matches nothing measured.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":210,"cols":[{"title":"macOS only","tone":"accent"},{"title":"+ Windows, Trusted Signing","tone":"neutral"},{"title":"All three, OV certificate","tone":"warn"}],"rows":[{"label":"Year-one certificates","cells":["99 USD","99 + 119.88 USD","99 + 219 USD"]},{"label":"CI, two releases a week, private repo","cells":["193.44 USD","216.53 USD","216.53 USD"]},{"label":"Hardware token","cells":["None","None, managed HSM","Yes, and no build machine to hold it"]},{"label":"Debuggable on hardware we own","cells":["Yes","No, Windows is not","No"]},{"label":"Unverified before it enters a budget","cells":["Nothing","Individual eligibility, signature quota","Reseller quotes, not CA lists"]}],"note":"The plan's 150 USD Windows floor is below every quote in this corpus.","caption":"What each platform mix costs in year one, at measured prices."},"stakes":"One person cannot debug a SmartScreen reputation climb on a machine they do not own.","state":["The plan promises a notarised .dmg, a code-signed .exe at 150 to 400 USD a year with a hardware token, and a Linux AppImage (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:104).","It repeats the Windows figure in the resources paragraph (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:231).","The config supports one of the three: `bundle.targets` is dmg and app, and package.json carries three Apple architectures and no Windows or Linux."],"path":["Three targets read as a complete product, so they entered the plan unpriced.","The desktop round costed them and recommended macOS only (k9:125). That recommendation never reached the plan.","Merged from AC7, because the Windows signing route is the price of the second column rather than a separate decision."],"tension":["The cheapest measured certificate is 219 USD a year, so the plan's 150 floor matches nothing (k9:17, k9:53).","Azure Trusted Signing is 119.88 USD a year with no dongle, which matters because there is no build machine to plug one into (k9:79).","Two things under that number are unverified: eligibility for individuals, and the included-signature quota (k9:131).","macOS is 89.3% of per-release CI cost, and the research's own falsifier is an OS mix nobody has measured (k9:137)."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"Year-one direct-distribution cost, three platforms, private repo","items":[["Apple Developer Program","99 USD/year","fetched 2026-08-29"],["Windows OV certificate, lowest measured quote","219 USD/year","Comodo/Sectigo via reseller; the plan's \"$150\" low end is below every measured quote"],["Microsoft Partner Center account","0 USD","no registration fee for either account type; the plan does not mention this"],["CI, two releases a week","216.53 USD/year","104 × 2.082 USD per release [derived]"],["Year-one floor, all three","534.53 USD","99 + 219 + 216.53 [derived]"],["macOS share of per-release CI cost","89.3%","1.860 of 2.082 USD — the only CI line worth optimising"],["macOS-only CI, private repo","193.44 USD/year","104 × 1.860 [derived]; on a public repo all CI is 0 USD"]]},{"type":"bars","title":"Per-release CI cost by platform, at GitHub's published rates","note":"Estimated build minutes (Linux 12, Windows 15, macOS universal 30) × published per-minute rates, fetched 2026-08-29. Minutes are inference — no release build was run; rates are fetched. Public repos are free.","unit":"USD per release","data":[["macOS universal",1.86],["Windows",0.15],["Linux",0.072]]},{"type":"table","title":"Windows signing routes, all fetched 2026-08-29","cols":["Route","Price","Hardware token","SmartScreen"],"rows":[["Azure Trusted Signing, Basic","9.99 USD/mo = 119.88/yr, plus 0.005 USD per signature above an unstated quota","None — managed HSM at FIPS 140-3 level 3","Not stated in what was fetched; eligibility for individuals unverified"],["OV certificate (Comodo/Sectigo)","219 USD/yr","Yes","Warns until reputation accrues, and reputation is per file hash — every release restarts the climb"],["OV (GoGetSSL / DigiCert)","289 / 400 USD/yr","Yes","Same"],["EV (Comodo/Sectigo → DigiCert)","287 → 685 USD/yr","Yes","Immediate reputation, no warning; business vetting from India is the real cost"],["Microsoft Partner Center account","0 USD one-time","n/a","n/a"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"What the plan says against what was measured","items":[["Plan's stated Windows range","150–400 USD/year","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:104 and :231"],["Lowest measured quote of any kind","119.88 USD/year","Azure Trusted Signing Basic, 12 × 9.99"],["Lowest measured certificate quote","219 USD/year","so the plan's \"$150\" floor matches nothing in the corpus"],["Plan's stated hardware requirement","\"hardware token required\"","false for the Trusted Signing route"],["Saving, Trusted Signing vs OV, year one","99.12 USD","435.41 against 534.53 [derived]"],["Recorded caveats","reseller quotes not CA list; SSL.com's own pages returned 404; token surcharge is a search summary, not fetched","k9:37, k9 cost table"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"macOS only in v1, said plainly on the download page","what":"One installer, notarised, debugged on the Mac the founder already owns.","gains":["The single biggest cost reduction available, since macOS is 89.3% of CI spend","Notarisation is debuggable on hardware we have","One support matrix"],"costs":["Every Windows visitor bounces, and nobody has counted how many that is","Contradicts what the plan currently promises"],"system":"Keep `bundle.targets` as it is.","screens":"A download page that says macOS only, for now.","money":"99 USD/year plus about 193 USD CI on a private repo. Zero CI on a public one."},{"k":"b","label":"macOS and Windows, with Windows signed through Azure Trusted Signing","what":"Two installers, and the Windows key lives in a managed HSM rather than on a dongle.","gains":["Cheapest measured Windows route, below the plan's own floor","No hardware token for a distribution with no build machine","Covers both desktop populations"],"costs":["Eligibility for individuals was never confirmed","The included-signature quota did not appear in the pricing response, so 119.88 is a floor","A second support matrix before there is one paying user"],"system":"A Windows target and a second signing path in CI.","screens":"A second download button.","money":"119.88 USD/year on top of Apple, gated on confirming eligibility."},{"k":"c","label":"macOS and Windows, with Windows signed by an OV certificate on a token","what":"The conventional route, available to individuals with certainty.","gains":["No eligibility question to resolve first","Well-trodden and documented"],"costs":["219 USD a year and a physical token nobody is there to plug in","SmartScreen reputation is per file hash, so a weekly shipper may never converge","99.12 USD more than the Trusted Signing route in year one"],"system":"A Windows target plus token-bound signing, which CI cannot do unattended.","screens":"A second download button, and a SmartScreen warning behind it.","money":"219 USD/year."},{"k":"d","label":"Measure the OS mix on the site for four weeks, then choose","what":"Instrument the download page before committing to a platform order.","gains":["Turns the deciding number into data at near-zero cost","Reuses the instrumentation AC4 already wants"],"costs":["Delays the desktop build by a month","Only acceptable if the pilot is on the web anyway"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["One person can debug notarisation on the Mac in front of them and cannot debug a SmartScreen climb on a machine they do not own.","macOS is 89.3% of the per-release CI cost, so shipping only it is the largest saving on the table.","Correct the plan's Windows line in the same edit. It is wrong on the price and wrong on the token.","Instrument the download page before the first build, so the falsifier can actually fire."],"flip":"The OS mix comes back Windows-first, which the research names as the case where macOS-only is vanity and the order inverts (k9:137).","linked":["AC10","AC18","AC4","AC8"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:104","src-tauri/tauri.conf.json","package.json:24","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-29-r12/k9-desktop-distribution.md:43","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-29-r12/k9-desktop-distribution.md:53","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-29-r12/k9-desktop-distribution.md:125","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-29-r12/k9-desktop-distribution.md:137","docs/research/prd-v2-sections/35-platform-surfaces.md:324","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:231","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-29-r12/k9-desktop-distribution.md:17","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-29-r12/k9-desktop-distribution.md:37","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-29-r12/k9-desktop-distribution.md:79","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-29-r12/k9-desktop-distribution.md:131","merged: AC7"]},{"id":"AC10","cat":"Access, offline & install","sub":"Updates","weight":"high","q":"Does the desktop app ship an auto-updater, and if it does, is the endpoint a Worker or a static file?","lede":"The signing key is unrecoverable, one person holds it, and the endpoint shape decides whether a bad release can ever be undone.","visual":{"kind":"state","states":[{"label":"No updater","meta":"where we are today","tone":"neutral","current":true},{"label":"Key generated","meta":"first public build, three copies held","via":"ship","tone":"warn"},{"label":"Updates flowing","meta":"one signed manifest per release","via":"release","tone":"good"},{"label":"Key lost","meta":"installed users unreachable, permanently","via":"one slip","tone":"stop"}],"note":"There is no revocation, no rotation and no second signer in the manifest format.","caption":"The one transition in this lifecycle with no way back."},"stakes":"Lose the key and every installed user can never be updated again.","state":["The plan requires it: the auto-updater must be signed and configured before the first public build (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:104).","Nothing is built. `tauri-plugin-updater` is absent from `src-tauri/Cargo.toml` and no endpoint is named anywhere.","The costed recommendation is a Worker-backed dynamic endpoint on R2, where egress is free (k9:125)."],"path":["Every desktop product ships one, so it entered the plan as an assumption rather than a decision.","Merged from AC11, because whether to ship and what to point at are one ladder: the static option cannot be upgraded afterwards."],"tension":["Signature verification cannot be disabled, and a lost key strands the installed base for good (k9:93, k9:101).","A null signing identity today is a recoverable mistake. A lost updater key is not (k9:105).","A static manifest cannot roll back, because the comparator override is compiled into the client binary (k9:99, k9:143).","The installed base at pilot is ten people (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:357)."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"The key liability, from Tauri's own docs via k9","items":[["Signature verification","cannot be disabled","k9:93 — the key is mandatory once the updater ships"],["Lost private key","installed users can never be updated again","k9:101 — no revocation, no rotation, no second signer in the manifest format"],["Where the key may live","env vars only — .env files do not work","k9:102, TAURI_SIGNING_PRIVATE_KEY / _PASSWORD"],["Recommended custody","3 independent copies","k9:103 — password manager + two offline media in two locations, plus the CI secret"],["Manifest validation order","whole file validated before the version check","k9:96 — one malformed platform entry breaks updates for every platform"],["The asymmetry, stated","signingIdentity null is recoverable; a lost updater key is not","k9:105"],["Installed base at pilot","10","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:357"]]},{"type":"table","title":"Static manifest against a dynamic endpoint (k9:99, k9:143)","cols":["","Static JSON on R2","Worker in front of R2"],"rows":[["Can serve a lower version (rollback)","No — the client refuses it","Yes, via version_comparator"],["Retrofit cost","Ship a new build to the stranded population","n/a"],["Egress","Free","Free"],["Operational surface","A file","One more deployable"],["Failure mode","Forward-only fixes; a bad release is fixed only by a newer release","A Worker outage stops update checks"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"Hosting cost either way","items":[["R2 storage","0.015 USD/GB-month; 10 GB-month free","fetched 2026-08-29"],["R2 egress","free, all storage classes","which is what makes download volume irrelevant"],["Artifact volume, 3 platforms × ~15 MB × 104 releases","4.68 GB/year cumulative","k9:55 [derived]; artifact size is an assumption, not a measurement"],["Manifest reads (Class B)","0.36 USD/million; 10M free","fetched"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"No auto-updater in v1: an in-app version check that opens the download page","what":"The app notices a newer version exists and links to it.","gains":["No key, no manifest, no permanent liability","Users still learn an update exists","Replaceable later without stranding anyone"],"costs":["Every update is a manual download","A footnote at a few hundred users and a support cost at ten thousand"],"system":"One version endpoint and a link. No signing key.","screens":"A one-line update notice.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Ship the updater against a Worker-backed endpoint from the first public build","what":"A dynamic endpoint that can serve a lower version through the comparator override.","gains":["Rollback exists the first time it is needed","Normal update experience","Free tier at this scale, and R2 egress is free"],"costs":["Creates a credential whose loss permanently strands every installed user","One more deployable to operate","A Worker outage stops update checks"],"system":"Updater plugin, signing key in CI secrets, a Worker in front of R2.","screens":"An update prompt and a restart.","money":"Free tier on Cloudflare at this volume."},{"k":"c","label":"Ship the updater against a static JSON manifest on R2","what":"The simplest possible endpoint, a file in object storage.","gains":["Nothing to operate","Free"],"costs":["Cannot roll back: the client refuses a lower version","A bad release is fixable only by a newer one","If the bad release breaks the updater, there is no path back"],"system":"Updater plugin, signing key, one file.","screens":"An update prompt and a restart.","money":"Free."},{"k":"d","label":"Static now, a Worker later","what":"Start with the file and add the dynamic endpoint when rollback is needed.","gains":["Reads as the prudent middle","Defers one deployable"],"costs":["It is the one option here that cannot work","The comparator override is compiled into the client, so later reaches nobody","Retrofitting means shipping a build to the population you are rescuing"],"system":"Same as (c), with a migration that does not exist.","screens":"Same as (c).","money":"Free, and worthless."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["The downside is not a bad release. It is a permanently unreachable installed base, held by one person.","A version check that opens the download page delivers most of the value with none of the permanent liability.","If an updater does ship, it must be (b). (d) looks prudent and is the only option that cannot work."],"flip":"The installed base grows past the point where manual re-download is a support cost, or a second person can hold a copy of the key.","linked":["AC6","AC8"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:104","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:357","src-tauri/Cargo.toml","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-29-r12/k9-desktop-distribution.md:93","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-29-r12/k9-desktop-distribution.md:96","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-29-r12/k9-desktop-distribution.md:101","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-29-r12/k9-desktop-distribution.md:105","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-29-r12/k9-desktop-distribution.md:55","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-29-r12/k9-desktop-distribution.md:99","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-29-r12/k9-desktop-distribution.md:125","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-29-r12/k9-desktop-distribution.md:143","merged: AC11"]},{"id":"AC12","cat":"Access, offline & install","sub":"Offline","weight":"high","q":"Do we build real offline reading for the web app, or say it is online-only and fix the exhibit that says otherwise?","lede":"The plan publishes an offline capability the code does not have, in the table a buyer reads to choose a surface.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":220,"cols":[{"title":"Exhibit 2 claims","tone":"warn"},{"title":"The code does","tone":"stop"}],"rows":[{"label":"Web, GitHub repo","cells":["Cached open files only","Nothing: content arrives via /api/, which the worker passes through"]},{"label":"Web, local folder","cells":["Cached","No File System Access code exists in src/ at all"]},{"label":"Web, Firefox, Safari, mobile","cells":["No","Correct"]},{"label":"Desktop","cells":["Everything except the model","No bundled assets, so no window content offline"]}],"note":"The service worker is 98 lines and caches two static assets.","caption":"The table a stranger reads to choose a surface, against the file."},"stakes":"A buyer picks a surface on a row that is wrong in two of four columns.","state":["Exhibit 2's offline row claims cached open files on the web-GitHub lane and cached on the local-folder lane (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:99).","`public/sw.js` treats navigations as network-only (`public/sw.js:63`) and never intercepts `/api/` (`public/sw.js:52`), which is where note content arrives.","The mobile round reached the same verdict independently: offline reading is impossible today (s4:18)."],"path":["The service worker came from sgnk-md as an installability shell, never as an offline story.","The exhibit was written from the intent rather than from the file."],"tension":["An earlier round refused this middle ground in writing: the web build is dead offline and we will not pretend otherwise (r20-q7:48).","The shipped model that works is Google Docs' opt-in shape, a per-file toggle and an N-most-recent cache, not a whole-vault sync (s4:60).","IndexedDB eviction is LRU and `persist()` is a heuristic, so the store can never be the record (s4:222).","The offline page already ships and names the sibling product's domain (`public/sw.js:70`), so there is a defect here under every option."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"The service worker as it exists","items":[["Lines","98","public/sw.js"],["Assets cached","2","/favicon.png and /theme-init.js, line 14"],["HTML navigations","network-only","line 63; req.mode === navigate is never served from cache"],["/api/ and /login","never intercepted","lines 52–58 — which is where note content arrives"],["Cache key","sgnk-md-v2","line 13, still the sibling product's name"],["Offline fallback that already exists","an inline HTML page saying \"md.sgnk.ai is unreachable\"","lines 63–76 — so the shell-offline courtesy is shipped, with the wrong product's domain in it"],["Offline reading today","impossible","s4:18, [derived] from the two /api/ rows above"]]},{"type":"table","title":"What the plan claims against what the code does","cols":["Surface","Exhibit 2 claims","Code does"],"rows":[["Web, GitHub repo","Cached open files only","Nothing — content comes from /api/, which the SW passes through"],["Web, local folder","Cached","No File System Access code exists in src/ at all"],["Web, Firefox/Safari/mobile","No","Correct"],["Desktop","Everything except the model","No filesystem plugin, no bundled assets — no window content without a network"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Build real offline reading: N most-recent files plus pins, in IndexedDB","what":"Google Docs' opt-in shape, per file, with a visible toggle.","gains":["Makes the published claim true","The shape a shipped product actually uses"],"costs":["Days AC2 shows the plan does not have","Eviction is LRU, so it can never be the record","Adds a second store to keep in step with the repo"],"system":"An IndexedDB cache with a pin list and an eviction policy.","screens":"A per-file offline toggle and an offline state in the tree.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"State that the web build is online-only, and correct Exhibit 2","what":"Two words in a table change, and the claim matches the code.","gains":["Costs an edit","Makes offline a real reason to download rather than a hedged half-promise"],"costs":["Removes a capability from the web column","Concedes that the trial surface is weaker than the daily one"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Keep the shell-offline page and fix its copy","what":"The app opens with no network and says honestly what is unavailable.","gains":["Nearly free, since the page already exists","Removes the sibling's domain from user-visible copy"],"costs":["The user still cannot read anything","It is a courtesy, not a capability"],"system":"Edit `public/sw.js`.","screens":"The offline page.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Leave the exhibit as written and revisit after the pilot","what":"Nothing changes.","gains":["No work","The web column keeps a capability on paper"],"costs":["The plan keeps publishing a capability that does not exist","In the one table meant to help someone choose a surface"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["Correct the exhibit. It is the table a stranger reads to choose a surface, and it is wrong in two of four columns.","Do (c) in the same pass. The offline page ships today naming the sibling product's domain, which is a defect either way.","Offline then becomes a real reason to download, which is cleaner than a half-working cache that makes both surfaces feel unreliable.","AC2 leaves no days for (a), and its store could never be the record anyway."],"flip":"Offline reading turns up in the ten-stranger pilot as a named reason people stop using the web app, and even then it is the opt-in per-file shape.","linked":["AC4","FF8"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:99","public/sw.js:13","public/sw.js:52","public/sw.js:63","public/sw.js:70","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r20-q7-one-page.md:48","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-29-r8to10/s4-mobile-cross-device.md:18","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-29-r8to10/s4-mobile-cross-device.md:60","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-29-r8to10/s4-mobile-cross-device.md:153","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-29-r8to10/s4-mobile-cross-device.md:222"]},{"id":"AC13","cat":"Access, offline & install","sub":"Keys and AI","weight":"high","q":"Where does the user's AI key live on the web, and does a local model ever ship so anything works offline?","lede":"The plan's web answer is an OS keychain the browser does not have, and its reason for deferring a local model cites only earlier drafts.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":190,"cols":[{"title":"Web","tone":"accent"},{"title":"Desktop","tone":"neutral"},{"title":"Our server","tone":"stop"}],"rows":[{"label":"Where the key rests","cells":["Nowhere: session memory, retyped","OS keychain via Tauri","Envelope-encrypted, held by us"]},{"label":"Worst case","cells":["One tab lifetime","Lost on a machine change","We run up your provider bill"]},{"label":"Friction","cells":["Retyped on every reload","Once per machine","None"]},{"label":"Works with no network","cells":["No","No: the model needs one","No"]},{"label":"Verdict in the research","cells":["Allow, with the friction visible","Recommended","Refuse at v1"]}],"note":"A local model is the only thing that would change the third row, and it is deferred.","caption":"Key custody by surface, with the failure mode each carries."},"stakes":"Persist a key in the browser and one flaw in a markdown renderer reads a credential to someone else's spend.","state":["Exhibit 1's F8 row budgets BYO key UI plus keychain at three days and marks the web column yes, with key (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:62).","Exhibit 2 repeats it for every web lane (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:97). No web custody is specified anywhere.","The local model is deferred on the line that constrained small models fabricate in 10 of 13 (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:173), repeated as settled (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:93)."],"path":["The F8 row was written for the desktop case, and the web column was filled in by analogy.","The local-model row entered as part of a vocabulary audit and was carried forward without its source.","Merged from AC16, because both halves answer how AI is powered on each surface."],"tension":["The provider round refuses browser persistence for a stated reason: we render user-supplied markdown by definition (r20-q3:30).","The browser is not the blocker. Anthropic allows browser calls behind a header it named dangerous, and OpenAI and Google reflect any origin.","That 10 of 13 figure appears in no research report and no fetched source, only in earlier versions of this plan.","What is traceable is different in both number and subject: constrained-decoding coverage of 41%, 39%, 28% and 3% (docs/engine/PLAN.md:1210)."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"Key custody, with the named failure mode for each (r20-q3 §100.2)","cols":["Where the key lives","Failure mode","Verdict in the research"],"rows":[["Browser localStorage","One XSS in a markdown renderer reads it; survives logout; readable by any script on the origin","Refuse"],["Browser session memory, retyped each session","Retyped on every reload; blast radius is one tab-lifetime","Allow on web, with the friction visible"],["OS keychain via Tauri","Lost on machine change; no team sharing","Recommended — desktop only"],["Our server, envelope-encrypted","A breach is not \"documents leaked\", it is \"we ran up your provider bill\"","Refuse at v1"],["Never stored","Nothing to leak, nothing to run","The default, and the free tier"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"Browser-origin calls, measured with curl 2026-08-30 (r20-q3 §100.1)","items":[["Anthropic, without the header","HTTP 400, no access-control-allow-origin","preflight to POST /v1/messages fails"],["Anthropic, with anthropic-dangerous-direct-browser-access","HTTP 200, ACAO *, credentials true, max-age 600","a real POST from evil.example.com returned 401 and the browser could read it"],["OpenAI","reflects any origin verbatim","tested 4 origins including literal null — all reflected, no opt-in, no warning"],["Google","identical behaviour","same 4 origins reflected"],["Conclusion recorded","the browser is not the blocker; the constraint is custodial","r20-q3 §100.1"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"What the plan cites against what the corpus holds","items":[["Cited in the plan","\"constrained small models fabricate in 10 of 13\"","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:173"],["Where else that figure appears","only in earlier versions of this same plan","PILOT-PLAN v10/v10.1/v11/v12 and PLAN v13/v14 print HTML — circular, not corroborating"],["Occurrences in any research report, PRD section or engine document","0","searched docs/research/ (235 reports) and docs/engine/"],["What is traceable — constrained-decoding coverage","Guidance 41%, llama.cpp 39%, XGrammar 28%, Outlines 3%","docs/engine/PLAN.md:1210; a coverage measure on \"GitHub Hard\" schemas, not a fabrication rate"],["Also traceable and adjacent","Grammar-Aligned Decoding (NeurIPS 2024): naive masking \"distorts the output distribution\"","engine/PLAN.md:1211 — valid and bad, which is the same shape of failure"],["The argument that needs no number","a local model in a refuse-rather-than-guess product is self-refuting","r19-p2 §91.4, stated as [inference]"],["Also true and unrelated to model size","no AI feature works offline in any architecture at our budget","r19-p2 §91.4"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Session memory on the web, OS keychain on desktop, no local model","what":"The key is typed each session on the web and stored once per machine on desktop.","gains":["Blast radius on the web is one tab lifetime","Nothing is at rest in the browser","The friction is honest, and the user can see why"],"costs":["Retyping a key on every reload, on the surface where most new users land","Two designs to build instead of one"],"system":"Split the F8 row: a keychain adapter on desktop, an in-memory holder on the web.","screens":"A key field in settings that says plainly it is not saved.","money":"None. Model spend stays on the user's account."},{"k":"b","label":"localStorage on the web, with the blast radius documented","what":"The key persists in the browser and a note explains the risk.","gains":["No friction after the first entry","Best conversion on connect-a-model"],"costs":["Puts a bearer credential inside a renderer whose job is rendering untrusted markdown","It survives logout and any script on the origin can read it","The research says refuse"],"system":"A browser store the security model does not permit.","screens":"A key field and a warning nobody reads.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"No AI on the web at all: a desktop feature, keyed from the OS keychain","what":"The web app is the editor and the review surface, with no model calls.","gains":["The cleanest custody story, and the one the research recommends","One implementation instead of two"],"costs":["Makes the web app strictly weaker at the moment the plan calls it the trial","F5, F6 and F8 disappear from the trial surface"],"system":"Remove the AI path from the web build.","screens":"The AI panel is absent on the web.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Bundle a small local model so desktop AI needs no key and no network","what":"Reopen the deferred local model and ship one in the desktop bundle.","gains":["Closes the one gap that survives every architecture, since AI is online in all of them","No key custody question on desktop"],"costs":["A product selling refusal cannot ship a component that guesses","Constrained decoding coverage is measured at 41% down to 3% on complex schemas","Adds a model to a bundle that currently contains none"],"system":"A bundled runtime and weights, and a much larger installer.","screens":"A model picker with a local option.","money":"Installer size and bandwidth, against zero model spend."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["Session memory is the only web option whose worst case is bounded by a tab.","Never our server. A breach there is not documents leaked, it is that we ran up your provider bill (r20-q3:36).","Keep the local model deferred, and replace the 10 of 13 citation with the coverage figures in `docs/engine/PLAN.md:1210`.","Split Exhibit 1's three-day row: a keychain is the desktop half, and the web half is a different design with a different risk."],"flip":"BYO-key setup completion below 40% among people who click connect a model, which the research names as its own falsifier (r20-q3:144).","linked":["AC1","AC12","F10"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:62","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:97","docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:45","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r20-q3-provider-keys.md:30","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r20-q3-provider-keys.md:36","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r20-q3-provider-keys.md:136","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r20-q3-provider-keys.md:144","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:173","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:93","docs/engine/PLAN.md:1210","docs/engine/PLAN.md:1211","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r19-p2-offline-or-online.md","merged: AC16"]},{"id":"AC19","cat":"Access, offline & install","sub":"Web byte path","weight":"high","q":"On the web against a GitHub repo, how does review state get written back: a commit per action, a batch, or a branch?","lede":"The headline artefact is a file in the user's repository, and on the web every review action is a repository write.","visual":{"kind":"flow","perRow":3,"nodes":[{"label":"You clear a span","note":"one line appended to review.jsonl","tone":"neutral"},{"label":"Commit per action","note":"the noisiest history a repo can have","tone":"stop","edge":"or"},{"label":"Batch on idle and on close","note":"lost if the tab dies first","tone":"accent","edge":"or"},{"label":"A sidecar branch","note":"invisible to git log on main","tone":"neutral","edge":"or"},{"label":"Browser only, never written","note":"not durable across machines","tone":"warn","edge":"or"}],"note":"On desktop this is one file write. On the web it is a git operation each time.","caption":"Four ways one cleared span reaches the repository."},"stakes":"Review state that is not written back is not durable across machines, which is the only form of the claim nothing observed reaches.","state":["Exhibit 2 says review state on the web-GitHub lane is a sidecar committed with the files (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:95).","The format is one JSON line per span in `.frontmatter/review.jsonl`, relocated by the splice locator on every edit (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:135).","Nothing specifies when that file is written on the web, or by what git operation."],"path":["On desktop the answer is obvious: write the file and let git see it. The web path was never separated from it.","The usage file hit the same wall and got a written decision (docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:20). The review file did not."],"tension":["Reading marks are generated far faster than edits, so a commit per action makes the history unreadable.","Batching loses state when a tab closes, on the surface AC2 recommends for the pilot.","Writes count against the same installation floor of 5,000 requests an hour as reads (r20-q4:38).","Durable in the repository, across sessions and machines, is the narrow form of the claim that survives. A browser-only cache is not that."],"evidence":[],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"One commit per review action","what":"Every cleared span appends a line and pushes it immediately.","gains":["State is durable the moment it is made","Nothing is lost when a tab closes"],"costs":["The user's history fills with commits they did not make","Writes count against the same hourly floor as reads","Contradicts the promise not to disturb your files"],"system":"A write per interaction through the GitHub client.","screens":"None, until the user opens their own git log.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Batch: write on idle, on file close and on tab close","what":"Marks accumulate in memory and land as one commit per session.","gains":["One commit a session instead of dozens","The user's history stays readable","Still lands in the repository, where the claim needs it"],"costs":["A killed tab loses that session's marks","The window in which two machines disagree is a whole session"],"system":"A flush scheduler and an unload path in the review store.","screens":"A saved indicator in the review panel.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Write to a sidecar branch, never to the working branch","what":"Review commits land on their own ref and merge on demand.","gains":["The user's branch history is untouched","Sidecar merge conflicts stay off the main line"],"costs":["Two refs to keep in step","A fresh clone without that branch shows no review state","More git surface than the product wants to expose"],"system":"A second ref and a merge policy for the sidecar.","screens":"None, unless a conflict surfaces.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Keep web review state in the browser, and write the file only on desktop","what":"The web app remembers marks per browser and never touches the repository.","gains":["No repository writes at all on the trial surface","Nothing to reconcile"],"costs":["Not durable across machines, which is the surviving form of the claim","Clearing site data erases it","The trial surface can no longer demonstrate the product"],"system":"A browser store with no git path.","screens":"A notice that marks are local to this browser.","money":"None."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["One commit a session keeps the history readable and still lands the state in the repository, where the claim needs it.","A commit per action turns the user's log into our telemetry, from a product that sells restraint.","(d) forfeits the one narrow claim nothing observed reaches, which is state durable across machines rather than per browser.","Decide it with AC17. The usage file and the review file hit the same wall on the same path."],"flip":"The pilot shows people review in short bursts and lose marks to closed tabs, in which case (a) is the honest answer and the commit noise is the price.","linked":["AC1","AC17","AC3","FF8"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:95","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:135","docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:20","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r20-q4-repo-and-folders.md:38"]},{"id":"AC17","cat":"Access, offline & install","sub":"Pilot surface","weight":"medium","q":"Where does the pilot's usage file live, when three of the four access paths cannot hold it as designed?","lede":"The measurement decision and the access model were written in the same document and never checked against each other.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":200,"cols":[{"title":"In the user's repo","tone":"neutral"},{"title":"Per surface","tone":"accent"},{"title":"Day-14 question","tone":"warn"}],"rows":[{"label":"Web, GitHub repo","cells":["A commit a day into a stranger's repo","Browser storage, no commit","Works"]},{"label":"Web, local folder","cells":["Yes, a silent disk write","Yes","Works"]},{"label":"Web, drag-in","cells":["Impossible: nothing persists","Browser storage","Works"]},{"label":"Desktop","cells":["Yes, once the fs plugin exists","Yes","Works"]},{"label":"What the gate then reads","cells":["Counted","Counted","Self-reported"]}],"note":"The gate is 6 of 10, and the draft's own fallback already concedes the self-report.","caption":"The exit measure against the four access paths."},"stakes":"The gate is 6 of 10, and on three of four paths the file that decides it cannot exist as designed.","state":["The draft puts it in one place: `.frontmatter/usage.jsonl` in the user's repo, one JSON line a day, user-readable (docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:20).","The gate is at least 6 of the last 10 working days plus one review action in week two (docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:22).","It reaches us only if a stranger pastes it once, on day 14 (docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:21).","There is no vendor usage database, by architecture (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:313)."],"path":["The location was chosen so the user owns the file, and that reason holds only where writing to the repo is normal.","The draft's own fallback already concedes the risk and replaces counting with a self-report (docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:27)."],"tension":["On the web-GitHub path this is a commit a day into a stranger's repository, from a product that promises not to disturb your files.","On drag-in nothing persists between sessions, so the file cannot exist at all.","On Firefox and Safari there is no local-folder path to write it to, and AC4 recommends cutting that lane anyway.","The narrow claim that survives is review state durable in the repository across machines, which is the same write problem at higher frequency."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"The usage file on each access path","cols":["Access path","Can hold .frontmatter/usage.jsonl?","Cost"],"rows":[["Web, GitHub repo","Only as a commit","One commit per day into the user's repo, from a product that promises not to touch it"],["Web, local folder (Chrome/Edge)","Yes","Silent local write; needs the File System Access adapter AC4 recommends cutting"],["Web, drag-in","No","Session only, not persisted"],["Desktop","Yes","Needs the filesystem plugin that is absent from Cargo.toml"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"What the gate needs to observe","items":[["Exit measure","opened on ≥6 of the last 10 working days, plus ≥1 review action in week two","WEEK0:22"],["Strangers","10","6 of 10 is the gate"],["How it reaches us","not at all by default — pasted once, on day 14","WEEK0:21"],["Stated fallback if local files are rejected","one message on day 14; \"accept that the gate is then self-reported\"","WEEK0:27"],["Vendor usage database","none, by architecture","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:313"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Keep it in the repo, batched to one commit a week","what":"The file stays where the user owns it, written seven times less often.","gains":["Preserves the ownership argument","Cuts the commit noise by seven"],"costs":["Still writes into a repository the user did not ask us to write to","Still cannot exist on drag-in or in Firefox"],"system":"A weekly flush through the GitHub client.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Store it per surface, and the stranger pastes whichever they have","what":"Browser storage on the web, a repo or local file on desktop.","gains":["Works on every access path, including drag-in and Firefox","Needs no commit into anyone's repository"],"costs":["Browser storage is not the user's repo, so the ownership argument weakens","Clearing site data erases it, and a zero reading becomes ambiguous"],"system":"One writer per adapter, behind a single measurement port.","screens":"A settings row showing the file and letting the user copy it.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Drop the file and use the day-14 question the draft already proposes","what":"Ask each stranger once, by message, whether they used it.","gains":["Zero build","Works everywhere"],"costs":["The gate becomes self-reported, which is what the measurement decision existed to avoid","Ten answers with no way to check them"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Opt-in upload of the daily line to the control plane, off by default","what":"The count reaches us directly, with consent.","gains":["The only path that gives a reliable count","No pasting, no missing files"],"costs":["Makes the counts personal data keyed to an account","Brings notice and consent duties with it","Contradicts the no-vendor-database line in the plan"],"system":"An endpoint and a consent record in the control plane.","screens":"A consent toggle in settings.","money":"Negligible, but it changes the compliance surface."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["The measure has to work on whatever surface AC2 chooses, and only per-surface storage does.","Keep everything the draft settled: counts only, no content, no file names, user-readable, pasted once on day 14.","Say in the recruiting script that clearing site data loses the file, so a zero reading is known to be ambiguous."],"flip":"AC2 sends the pilot to a signed desktop build, in which case the repo file works as originally designed and (a) is simpler.","linked":["AC19","AC4","B10"],"sources":["docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:20","docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:21","docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:22","docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:27","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:313","src-tauri/Cargo.toml"]},{"id":"AC18","cat":"Access, offline & install","sub":"Desktop platforms","weight":"medium","q":"Do we commit to direct download only and rule out the Mac App Store, or design for the sandbox now?","lede":"The store's sandbox forbids the one thing the product does, and the cost of keeping the door open is paid in architecture.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":210,"cols":[{"title":"Direct download only","tone":"accent"},{"title":"Direct, bookmarks built in","tone":"neutral"},{"title":"Mac App Store in v1","tone":"stop"}],"rows":[{"label":"App Sandbox","cells":["None","None yet","Mandatory"]},{"label":"Home folder","cells":["Full access","Full access","Container directory only"]},{"label":"Holding a folder across launches","cells":["A path","Security-scoped bookmarks","Security-scoped bookmarks"]},{"label":"Commission","cells":["None","None","15% or standard"]},{"label":"What the choice costs","cells":["Store discovery, never quantified here","A persistence layer nobody asked for","The seam the product is built around"]}],"note":"The bookmark mechanics are marked not opened in the source, so treat the specifics as unverified.","caption":"What the store's sandbox costs the file-access design."},"stakes":"Deciding late is expensive, because bookmarks are an architecture choice rather than a build flag.","state":["The plan does not mention stores at all. It describes direct artefacts only: a .dmg, an .exe and an AppImage (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:104).","App Sandbox is mandatory for the Mac App Store and grants a container directory, not the home folder (k9:135).","The current shell loads a remote URL, which is the shape guideline 4.2 targets (s4:114)."],"path":["Direct download was assumed, so the question never entered the plan.","It was answered in the desktop round (k9:135) and repeated at prd-v2-sections/35-platform-surfaces.md:384, and never surfaced."],"tension":["A vault-shaped editor that holds a folder open across launches would route every path through open panels and persisted bookmarks.","That is a real constraint on an engine whose premise is locating a byte range in a file.","The store also wants a provisioning profile, a bundle category, an encryption declaration and a separate Tauri config.","No evidence in two weeks of research shows store discovery matters for a category this narrow."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"What the Mac App Store requires","items":[["App Sandbox","mandatory for MAS","fetched, Apple App Sandbox doc, via k9:135"],["Home folder access under the sandbox","not granted","container directory only"],["Holding a folder across launches","security-scoped bookmarks via open panels","the source marks the bookmark mechanics as not opened — treat specifics as unverified"],["Commission","15% under the Small Business Program, else standard","fetched 2026-08-29"],["Extra MAS build requirements","embedded.provisionprofile, bundle.category, ITSAppUsesNonExemptEncryption, a separate tauri.appstore.conf.json, a universal build","fetched, Tauri App Store guide"],["Guideline 4.2, verbatim","an app \"should include features, content, and UI that elevate it beyond a repackaged website\"","fetched, s4:114 — and our shell loads https://md.sgnk.ai [derived from tauri.conf.json]"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Direct download only, stated on the site: no Mac App Store, no Microsoft Store","what":"One channel, and the engine keeps direct file descriptors.","gains":["No sandbox, no commission, no review queue on every release","The file-access design stays as simple as the engine needs"],"costs":["Forfeits store discovery, which nobody here has quantified","Closes a channel that a managed fleet might require"],"system":"No change.","screens":"A download page that says where the app comes from.","money":"No commission. No review cycle cost."},{"k":"b","label":"Direct download now, with security-scoped bookmarks designed in from the start","what":"Keep the store possible by building the persistence the sandbox would need.","gains":["The door stays open","Bookmarks are cheaper to design in than to retrofit"],"costs":["Adds a persistence layer for a channel nobody has asked for","More surface in the part of the system that must not be wrong"],"system":"A bookmark store in the file-access layer.","screens":"None visible.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Ship to the Mac App Store in v1","what":"Sandbox the app, add the store build configuration, and submit.","gains":["Store discovery and Apple-handled payments","Installs on machines that only allow store apps"],"costs":["Sandbox constraints land on the exact seam the product is built around","Commission and a review cycle on every release","The current shell is the shape guideline 4.2 rejects"],"system":"A separate store configuration, a universal build, and a bookmark layer.","screens":"A store listing and a first-run folder grant.","money":"15% under the Small Business Program, otherwise standard."},{"k":"d","label":"Leave it undecided","what":"Build file access without the constraint and revisit later.","gains":["No work now","No channel is formally ruled out"],"costs":["Reopening the store later means rebuilding the file-access design","The download page still cannot answer the question"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["The sandbox constrains the one mechanism the product exists to perform.","No evidence here shows store discovery matters for this category, so the constraint buys nothing measurable.","Say it on the download page rather than leaving people to guess."],"flip":"A buyer segment that can only install from a store, such as a managed fleet or a school, which would also be the first evidence the channel is worth an architecture constraint.","linked":["AC6","AC8"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:104","src-tauri/tauri.conf.json","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-29-r12/k9-desktop-distribution.md:35","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-29-r12/k9-desktop-distribution.md:135","docs/research/prd-v2-sections/35-platform-surfaces.md:384","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-29-r8to10/s4-mobile-cross-device.md:114"]},{"id":"MK4","cat":"Market & competition","sub":"Buyer","weight":"critical","q":"Which buyer does the first version serve, and does F5/F6 stay in MVP-0 while that is settled?","lede":"Two MVP-0 features were validated on a buyer who does not run an agent, and a third candidate segment sits unread in our own repo.","visual":{"kind":"matrix","x":["reachable in 90 days","not reachable this year"],"y":["no budget line","budget and liability"],"points":[{"label":"AI-native developer","x":0.12,"y":0.18,"us":true},{"label":"Obsidian user blocked at work","x":0.35,"y":0.3},{"label":"Startup docs owner","x":0.3,"y":0.5},{"label":"Liable services operator","x":0.75,"y":0.82},{"label":"Regulated QMS team","x":0.9,"y":0.9},{"label":"Compliance-adjacent writer","x":0.88,"y":0.75}],"note":"Persona ranking from CRITIQUE.md:233-242; the Obsidian segment from docs/research/frontmatter-segment-strategy.md.","caption":"Everyone with pain and a budget is out of reach inside 90 days"},"stakes":"Choosing wrong costs the first version rather than a sprint, and MVP-0 scope is committed in week 3.","state":["Exhibit 20 decision 2 puts the choice in week 1: AI-native developer, or the person liable when a document is wrong (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:366`).","F5 idea mode and F6 decision flow both ship in MVP-0 on founder user tests with no notes, participants or protocol attached (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:59-60`; `docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:23`).","A third candidate is in the repo and cited nowhere in the plan: `docs/research/frontmatter-segment-strategy.md` ranks Obsidian power users first."],"path":["The gap register named the contradiction as D3: F5 and F6 point at a buyer who does not run an agent (`docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:52`).","The persona review ranked six personas and found none of them burning (`docs/CRITIQUE.md:244`).","The segment study was synthesised on 2026-07-13 against a different product, browser vault plus git sync plus publish, and was never retired or contradicted."],"tension":["The two segments in real pain sit outside the product: the compliance writer needs SOC 2 and nine to eighteen months; the services operator writes `.docx`.","The developer has `git diff` and appeared 0 times in the 355 highest-intent comments (`docs/CRITIQUE.md:242`).","The Obsidian segment has the largest verified pain artefact in the corpus, 246,568 views over six years, and voted 0 likes for review state.","The falsifier is already written: 20 outreach conversations, five or more naming whole-file rewrites unprompted (`docs/CRITIQUE.md:246`)."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"Six personas, ranked by how badly they hurt (CRITIQUE.md:233-242)","cols":["Persona","Pain today","Verdict"],"rows":[["P5 compliance-adjacent writer","A signed artifact that does not match its source is an audit finding","Fire exists — unreachable: no SOC 2, no attorney review, 9-18 month cycle"],["Liable services operator (not one of the six)","\"Two rounds of revisions\" silently becoming unbounded free labour","Fire exists — wrong substrate: their document is .docx, where dealfluence/adeu already ships this engine"],["P2 startup docs owner","Docs, changelog, roadmap drift","Warm; budgeted at $20-40/seat; needs multiplayer presence first"],["P3 agency lead","Notion export is 900 files of Untitled 3.md","Warm; blocked by the 83% publish refusal"],["P4 AI-heavy knowledge worker","Unreviewable agent diffs","The record's own v1 target; its only measured instance is the founder's machine"],["P1 solo dev","He has git diff","Cold — 0 of 355 in the highest-intent thread"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"Which archetype this is","items":[["Sequoia Arc classification","Hard Fact, not Hair on Fire","\"customers have resigned themselves to just living with the problem\" — CRITIQUE.md:244"],["What Hard Fact requires","market education","CRITIQUE.md:244"],["Education budget today","₹0 and two blog posts","one defective since 2026-08-10 — CRITIQUE.md:244"],["Falsifier already written","20 outreach conversations","if 5 or more name whole-file rewrites unprompted, P4 is a segment — CRITIQUE.md:246"],["Evidence attached to the F5/F6 founder tests","none","\"Founders' statement in chat. No notes, no participants, no protocol\" — GAPS-2026-09-08.md:23"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"The signal the segment study ranks first","items":[["Obsidian forum, \"Obsidian for web\"","246,568 views, 244 posts, 928 likes","six years, still active in 2026 — research/frontmatter-segment-strategy.md §1.1"],["Docker pulls of linuxserver/obsidian","414,917","streaming a whole desktop over VNC into a browser tab, as a workaround"],["obsidian-git stars","11,540","README warns mobile git is \"very unstable\""],["Stated willingness-to-pay band for that segment","$2-6 per month","anchored to Obsidian Sync $4"],["The study's own caveat on that segment","\"skews free-first — treat as acquisition and evangelism more than revenue\"","§1.1 honest verdict"],["Obsidian forum likes for review state","0","251 views, 1 post in nearly three years — PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:410"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"AI-native developer first; move F5 and F6 to MVP-1","what":"The plan commits to the developer and drops the two founder-tested features from the first release.","gains":["Consistent with the channels, the sidecar and the repo-native architecture","One buyer, one surface"],"costs":["Discards the only two features with any user test behind them","Leaves MVP-0 resting entirely on untested review state"],"system":"No change; F5 and F6 slip a tier.","screens":"S0's template cards and the decision-flow screens move out of MVP-0.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"The liable person first; keep F5 and F6 in MVP-0","what":"We aim at the buyer with real, priceable pain.","gains":["Keeps the founder-tested features","Points at a segment with a budget line"],"costs":["Their document is `.docx`, and an MIT competitor already ships this engine there","SOC 2 and a nine to eighteen month cycle, none of it in the 90-day plan"],"system":"A `.docx` path we have refused, or nothing to sell them.","screens":"The review screens stay; the repo tree becomes wrong.","money":"SOC 2 and legal review, both unbudgeted."},{"k":"c","label":"Put the Obsidian segment on the table as a third candidate","what":"The web app opens a vault from a repo, with review state on top.","gains":["The largest verified pain artefact in the corpus, 246,568 views","The watering holes accept a demo link into the asking thread"],"costs":["That population voted 0 likes for the feature we are building","The study calls the segment free-first, so it is acquisition, not revenue"],"system":"A vault-shaped web path, not the repo-shaped one.","screens":"S0 becomes vault-first.","money":"A $2-6 band, below every planned price."},{"k":"d","label":"Pre-register the rule: F5 and F6 stay, and the 20 conversations decide","what":"We write down before the answer what five or more unprompted mentions will change.","gains":["The only form of waiting that cannot be rationalised afterwards","Uses a falsifier the corpus already contains"],"costs":["Week-3 scope stays conditional","Binds us to act on a number we may not like"],"system":"No change until week 3.","screens":"No change.","money":"None."}],"rec":"d","recCase":["The plan already reserves weeks 1-2 for tests and already contains the exact falsifier. The meeting's job is to write down in advance what the count will mean.","Deciding before that test means deciding on a persona set whose own author wrote that the only measured instance of the target is the founder's machine.","Put the segment study on the table in the same sitting, if only to reject it on the record. The rejection is available and honest.","Attach the F5/F6 test notes in that meeting or relabel both features untested."],"flip":"If fewer than five of twenty name whole-file rewrites unprompted, option b is forced and the 90-day plan has to absorb a nine-month sales cycle.","linked":["MK16","MK31","PR1"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:59-60","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:366","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:410","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:23","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:52","docs/CRITIQUE.md:233","docs/CRITIQUE.md:242","docs/CRITIQUE.md:244","docs/CRITIQUE.md:246","docs/research/frontmatter-segment-strategy.md","merged: MK24"]},{"id":"MK16","cat":"Market & competition","sub":"Size","weight":"critical","q":"Do we accept that this is a few-hundred-customer business, or change the denominator before building?","lede":"Two independent routes land on the same buyer population, and it is one eighth of the revenue goal the same corpus carries.","visual":{"kind":"funnel","steps":[{"label":"Qualified humans at a 5x private multiplier","n":81000,"unit":"people","tone":"neutral"},{"label":"Payers, optimistic (20% switch x 8% pay)","n":1296,"unit":"payers","tone":"neutral"},{"label":"Payers, central (10% x 5%)","n":405,"unit":"payers","tone":"accent"},{"label":"Payers, pessimistic (2% x 2.5%)","n":41,"unit":"payers","tone":"stop"}],"note":"The ₹20 lakh a month figure carried elsewhere needs 3,339 payers. The central case is 12.1% of it.","caption":"Bottom-up from live GitHub counts, with the switch and pay rates swept"},"stakes":"This decides whether frontmatter is a product funded by services or a company, and every downstream plan follows.","state":["The plan states the monthly nut at about ₹1.09 lakh, covered by 54 to 78 consulting hours (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:292`). The MVP-1 exit is one team paying within 20 conversations (`:206`).","It states no target customer count anywhere.","The central case of 405 payers clears the nut with about ₹46,400 spare (`docs/CRITIQUE.md:292`)."],"path":["The TAM was computed bottom-up from live GitHub counts on 2026-08-31 with a private multiplier the author marked unmeasurable (`docs/CRITIQUE.md:266`).","It was cross-checked top-down through Stack Overflow usage rates, and the two routes agree within 0.5% at the generous end (`docs/CRITIQUE.md:288`).","The 2026-09-09 sweep found six firms publishing note-taking market sizes spanning $1.35B to $15.46B, one of them publishing two figures for the same base year."],"tension":["The measured spontaneous-concern rate is 0.032%, so even a 2% switch rate is 62 times the observed signal (`docs/CRITIQUE.md:279`).","At 4% monthly churn the stock asymptotes at 804 payers forever, inside the TAM band (`docs/CRITIQUE.md:295`).","The 1.26M-visitor requirement is a 24 to 36 month cumulative figure, and the plan is missing at least one channel of a size nobody has named (`docs/BUSINESS.md:1086`).","No top-down market size may be quoted. The 8.2x same-year disagreement between vendors is more useful than any of their figures."],"evidence":[{"type":"bars","title":"Buyer population, four scenarios, against what the revenue goal needs","note":"Bottom-up from api.github.com 2026-08-31, sensitivity on the private-repo multiplier and the switch and pay rates. CRITIQUE.md:281-286","data":[["Pessimistic (2% switch x 2.5% pay)",41],["Central (10% x 5%)",405],["Optimistic (20% x 8%)",1296],["Generous (20x private multiplier)",5184]],"unit":"paying customers","threshold":3339,"thresholdLabel":"payers needed for the ₹20L/month goal"},{"type":"stat","title":"The two independent routes, and the constraints on them","items":[["Bottom-up qualified population at a 5x private multiplier","81,000 humans","10,800 repos x 5 x 1.5 humans — CRITIQUE.md:277"],["Top-down cross-check, generous end","5,160 payers","against bottom-up 5,184 — the two routes agree within 0.5% — CRITIQUE.md:288"],["Measured spontaneous-concern rate","0.032%","even a 2% switch rate is 62x the observed signal — CRITIQUE.md:279"],["Central case against the ₹20L/month goal","12.1%","CRITIQUE.md:284, :293"],["Churn ceiling at c=4%/month","the stock asymptotes at 804 payers forever","inside the TAM band — CRITIQUE.md:295"],["Central case against the ₹1.09L/month nut","clears it with ₹46,400 spare","\"a real, if small, business\" — CRITIQUE.md:292"],["What the 1.26M visitor requirement actually is","a 24-to-36-month cumulative figure, not year one","and the plan is \"missing at least one channel of a size nobody has yet named\" — BUSINESS.md:941, :1086"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Accept the small shape: a few hundred customers, funded by services","what":"The plan stops carrying figures that only make sense at scale.","gains":["Arithmetically clears the nut with room","Deletes every decision that assumes growth we have no channel for"],"costs":["The ₹20 lakh figure and the 1.26M funnel go","Forecloses any outside funding conversation"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"Caps the business at roughly the nut plus a margin."},{"k":"b","label":"Change the denominator — sell to teams at a seat price","what":"The unit becomes a team, not a person.","gains":["The only path in the corpus with a different denominator","27,778 seats at $30 reaches the goal"],"costs":["The record's own trigger, three unsolicited inbound teams, has fired zero times","Nothing in Pro has been paid for yet"],"system":"Seat counting, team boundaries, invoicing.","screens":"A team admin surface that does not exist.","money":"Higher ceiling, no evidence."},{"k":"c","label":"Measure the private-repo multiplier before accepting either number","what":"The one unmeasured input gets measured.","gains":["It is the difference between 41 and 5,184"],"costs":["The corpus marks it unmeasurable from outside","The measurement may not exist"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Reject the gating assumption — the population is anyone with markdown in a repo","what":"The four gates are dropped and the denominator rises three orders.","gains":["Every number rises if it is true"],"costs":["The wider set has `git diff`","Five docs-drift Show HN launches scored 1, 2, 2, 2 and 4 points"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["Two independent routes agreeing within 0.5% is the strongest quantitative result in this corpus.","The central case clears the monthly nut, so the question is not whether to continue but what to stop claiming.","Accepting the small shape deletes the 1.26M funnel and the ₹20 lakh target, which is a week of editing and no engineering.","Publish no top-down market size at all. Six firms disagree by 8.2x for the same year, and that disagreement is the only honest thing to say about the category."],"flip":"A measured public-to-private ratio at 20x or above, with a switch rate at or above 20%, puts the generous branch in reach and option b becomes the plan.","linked":["MK29","MK4","PR3"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:206","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:292","docs/CRITIQUE.md:266","docs/CRITIQUE.md:277","docs/CRITIQUE.md:279","docs/CRITIQUE.md:281","docs/CRITIQUE.md:284","docs/CRITIQUE.md:288","docs/CRITIQUE.md:292","docs/CRITIQUE.md:295","docs/BUSINESS.md:941","docs/BUSINESS.md:1086"]},{"id":"MK27","cat":"Market & competition","sub":"Precedent","weight":"critical","q":"Do we name Almanac in the pitch, or wait for someone in the room to name it for us?","lede":"Almanac shipped our whole feature sentence, raised $45M, and switched off on 31 January 2025. It appears nowhere in the corpus.","visual":{"kind":"ba","before":{"title":"Almanac, at its height","lines":[{"t":"Read Receipts","mark":"ok"},{"t":"Version Control Mode, Layers, Approvals","mark":"ok"},{"t":"Doc History diffing, deprecation reviews","mark":"ok"},{"t":"$9M seed, $34M Series A, Tiger Global","mark":"ok"},{"t":"7-figure ARR, 50+ staff","mark":"ok"}]},"after":{"title":"get.almanac.io today","lines":[{"t":"Shut down 2025-01-31","mark":"x"},{"t":"Cause stated as capacity, not demand","mark":"!"},{"t":"Their AI content product took the team","mark":"!"},{"t":"The feature list is still on the live site","mark":"!"}]},"via":"four years","note":"Their 2020 Show HN, \"GitHub for Docs\", scored 6 points and drew no comments.","caption":"Our feature sentence, funded to $45M, switched off"},"stakes":"The read-receipt half of the headline has a well-funded corpse, and anyone who knows the space will raise it before we do.","state":["The plan's headline is review state across people and tools (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:20`), which is Almanac's Read Receipts feature in different words.","`Almanac` appears zero times in `docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md` and zero times in the market table (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:145-160`).","The company's own farewell page states the cause as capacity: their AI content product reached tens of thousands of users in months and consumed the team."],"path":["Almanac launched on Show HN in 2020 as GitHub for Docs and scored 6 points with no comments.","It raised a $9M seed and a $34M Series A led by Tiger Global in September 2021, and reached 7-figure ARR with 50 or more staff.","It shut down on 2025-01-31. Kortex died the same way. Neither is in this corpus."],"tension":["The stated cause is capacity, not demand, which is either an honest reason or the polite one. Nothing opened settles which.","Naming it first turns the strongest objection into evidence that we did the reading. Waiting means hearing it from a sceptic.","The general-document form of \"know what nobody has read\" is precisely what Almanac sold. The agent-scoped, in-repo form is not.","$45M and fifty people did not make the general form work, which is an argument for narrowing rather than for spending more."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"Almanac, from opened sources","items":[["Features still listed on the live site","Read Receipts, Version Control Mode, Layers, Approvals, Doc History diffing","get.almanac.io"],["Funding","$9M seed plus a $34M Series A led by Tiger Global, September 2021","thesaasnews.com"],["Scale before shutdown","7-figure ARR, 50+ staff","saasclub.io podcast summary — a secondary source, not the founder's writing"],["Shutdown date","2025-01-31","get.almanac.io/go-forward"],["Cause as stated","capacity, not demand","their AI content product \"grew to tens of thousands of users in a matter of months\""],["Their 2020 Show HN, \"GitHub for Docs\"","6 points, no comments","hn.algolia.com/api/v1/items/23339147"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Name Almanac first, in the plan and in the pitch, with the narrowing it forces","what":"A short paragraph naming the company, the money, the date and what we do differently.","gains":["Turns the strongest objection into evidence we did the reading","Forces the honest narrowing rather than deferring it"],"costs":["Puts a $45M failure in front of every reader","Invites the question of why two people succeed where fifty did not"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Add it to the market table only, not to the pitch","what":"A row in Exhibit 3 with the date and the stated cause.","gains":["The table becomes honest for the cost of one row","No change to what we say out loud"],"costs":["A sceptic who raises it in a meeting still catches us flat","The narrowing it forces goes unmade"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Say nothing and answer if asked","what":"Almanac stays out of the written plan.","gains":["Nothing to explain unprompted"],"costs":["Anyone who knows the space raises it, and silence reads as not having looked","We lose the framing of the answer"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Treat the shutdown as a demand verdict and drop the review-state direction","what":"We read $45M and four years as the market's answer.","gains":["Takes the strongest negative precedent seriously","Frees the direction to move"],"costs":["The stated cause is capacity, and nothing opened contradicts it","It would be a fifth pivot on a single data point"],"system":"F2 leaves the plan.","screens":"The whole review surface.","money":"None."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["The blind spot is the problem, not the company. A corpus that ran two adversarial rounds and missed a $45M precedent has a gap a reader will notice.","Naming it first is also the cheapest way to force the narrowing MK1 needs. Almanac sold the general form; the agent-scoped, in-repo form is what is left.","The stated cause is capacity, and that is worth quoting exactly. Do not upgrade it to a demand verdict, because nothing opened supports that."],"flip":"If a former Almanac customer or employee says demand was the real cause, option d is on the table and the direction has to move again.","linked":["MK16","MK29","P2"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:20","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:145-160","https://get.almanac.io/","https://get.almanac.io/go-forward","https://www.thesaasnews.com/news/almanac-raises-34-million-in-series-a/","https://hn.algolia.com/api/v1/items/23339147"],"dupes":{"dropped":["P23"],"why":"Do we name Almanac in the pitch or wait to be asked. Both rec naming it first. P23 is MK27 plus Zed Delta, and Delta's pitch treatment is already MK28/E35's option (a)."}},{"id":"MK7","cat":"Market & competition","sub":"Channels","weight":"high","q":"Two channels were cut on measured evidence and six places still ship them — what actually replaces each?","lede":"The Obsidian plugin and the Chrome extension are both marked CUT in one exhibit and remain load-bearing in five others.","visual":{"kind":"ba","before":{"title":"Plan v15 as published","lines":[{"t":"Exhibit 17: Obsidian plugin CUT","mark":"x"},{"t":"Exhibit 6: plugin is the week-2 channel","mark":"!"},{"t":"Exhibit 19: \"plugin shipped\" in weeks 1-2","mark":"!"},{"t":"Exhibit 24: plugin is a retention lever","mark":"!"},{"t":"Exhibit 26: plugin and Chrome extension ship","mark":"!"},{"t":"§21: the nested fix ships first as the plugin","mark":"!"}]},"after":{"title":"One coherent plan","lines":[{"t":"Additive review-state CodeMirror extension","mark":"+"},{"t":"?src= parameter with a written next action","mark":"+"},{"t":"Chrome extension deleted from Exhibit 26","mark":"x"},{"t":"Retention lever replaced or struck","mark":"x"}]},"via":"one edit","note":"All six locations verified in the v15 file.","caption":"Both cuts are correct; the document has not caught up with either"},"stakes":"Publishing a plan that cuts a channel on one page and schedules it on four others is the kind of thing a reader stops trusting.","state":["Exhibit 17 marks the free Obsidian plugin CUT with the technical reason (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:304`) and cuts the Chrome extension for a `?src=` parameter (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:310`).","The plugin still ships in Exhibit 6 with a 200-install kill line (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:204`), Exhibit 19 (`:352`), Exhibit 24 (`:428`), Exhibit 26 (`:477`) and §21 (`:524`).","Exhibit 26 still lists the Chrome extension as a family member shipping at MVP-1, in the same row (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:477`)."],"path":["The plugin was the week-2 channel through v14 on the strength of a 501-like rendering bug.","Round 2 spiked it and found the parse unreachable: Obsidian's Live Preview tree is a CodeMirror `StreamLanguage` tree, depth-1 by construction, verified twice (`docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:127`).","The Chrome extension was cut when its 1.5M figure turned out to sum a reader with a clipper. That clipper's tracker holds zero requests to read a `.md` URL (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:310`)."],"tension":["The two plugins that do change nested behaviour write `U+200C` into user files, which a byte-exact product cannot ship.","The additive route named in the same row needs no containment and rides the sidecar we are building anyway, so it is close to free.","A parameter that opens any public `.md` in our editor is a demo, not a channel, until someone writes down what the visitor does next.","GitHub already renders markdown and ships rich diff and per-file Viewed state free at the exact surface both cut channels targeted."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"The same document, five places, two answers","cols":["Location","What it says"],"rows":[["Exhibit 17, PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:304","Free Obsidian plugin — CUT. The parse is unreachable"],["Exhibit 6, PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:204","Channels: free Obsidian live-preview plugin, week 2; kill under 200 installs in 14 days"],["Exhibit 19, PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:352","Weeks 1-2 work: \"plugin shipped\""],["Exhibit 24, PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:428","Retention lever: the Obsidian live-preview fix stays installed in a vault they open daily"],["Exhibit 26, PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:477","Family member: Chrome extension, Obsidian plugin — free; channels; MVP-1, week 2"],["§21, PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:524","Nested constructs render correctly (the 501-like bug, shipped first as the free plugin)"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"Why round 2 cut it","items":[["Obsidian Live Preview parse tree depth","1, by construction","a CodeMirror StreamLanguage tree; \"this fence is inside a list item\" does not exist in it — PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:304"],["What a plugin can change","appearance only","on undocumented DOM classes Obsidian has already deleted once — PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:304"],["What the two plugins that do change nested behaviour write into user files","U+200C","which a byte-exact product cannot ship — PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:304"],["Closest measured analogue, first 14 days","115 installs","against our own 200 kill line — PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:304"],["Obsidian live-preview changelog lines in 2025","9 across 5 of 12 months","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:304. Flagged: CRITIQUE.md:362 measures the same surface as \"51 live preview hits in the 142 releases of 2025-26\" and calls Obsidian \"still actively fixing\" it — two readings of one question, unreconciled"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"Why the extension was cut","items":[["Claimed browser reading population","1.5M","summed a 500,000-user reader with a 1,000,000-user clipper — PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:310"],["Requests to read a .md URL in the clipper's tracker","0","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:310"],["Real reading population","~647,000","its leader has not shipped a store build in over two years — PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:310"],["raw.githubusercontent.com CORS header","access-control-allow-origin: *","so the web app needs no extension — PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:310"],["Cost of the replacement","hours","no store listing, no Manifest V3 — PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:310"],["What GitHub already ships at that exact surface","rendered markdown, rich diff, per-file Viewed state, free","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:310"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Accept both cuts and delete both from all six places","what":"The plan loses every Obsidian and browser surface.","gains":["One coherent document","Nothing to maintain that we cannot build"],"costs":["The retention strategy loses a lever and the family loses its free channel","MVP-0 has no channel at all before superpowers"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Ship the additive Obsidian extension and a `?src=` link with a stated job","what":"Review state as a CodeMirror decoration over the sidecar's byte ranges, plus a public read link that names its next action.","gains":["Needs no containment and reuses the sidecar we build anyway","The link is the only artefact we can paste into a spec-kit or superpowers thread"],"costs":["A different product in that vault, never sized","The audience that voted 501 for the rendering bug voted 0 for review state"],"system":"A CodeMirror decoration layer over the sidecar; hours for the URL parameter.","screens":"Adds a minimal read view; kills the plugin screens.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Ship `?src=` only and drop every Obsidian surface","what":"The browser read path survives, Obsidian does not.","gains":["Removes an inconsistency the plan repeats in §23","Hours of work, no store listing"],"costs":["Abandons the single largest measured demand signal in the corpus","Still leaves no week-2 channel we own"],"system":"Hours.","screens":"A read view on the web app.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Reject the cuts and spike the plugin again","what":"A third look at whether a plugin can fix nested live preview.","gains":["Would restore the plan as written if it succeeded"],"costs":["The spike is done and returned negative twice","A day that will not change the depth-1 finding"],"system":"No change.","screens":"No change.","money":"A day of the 1.21 available per week."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["Both cuts are correct. The depth-1 finding was verified twice, and the CORS header makes the extension unnecessary.","The additive route needs no containment and rides the sidecar already scheduled for F2, so it is close to free.","Write down what a `?src=` visitor does next. A reading surface with no next action repeats the mistake the extension was cut for.","Fix all six locations in one edit rather than six."],"flip":"If the additive extension cannot anchor spans in Obsidian's own editor either, option a is the only honest plan and MVP-0 has no channel.","linked":["MK4"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:204","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:304","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:310","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:352","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:428","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:477","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:524","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:62","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:127","merged: MK8"]},{"id":"MK12","cat":"Market & competition","sub":"Competitors","weight":"high","q":"Do we let the measured ceiling in this niche stand, or open the products behind it first?","lede":"Thirteen extensions and seven plugins already sit in this niche and nobody in the corpus has opened a single one of them.","visual":{"kind":"funnel","steps":[{"label":"All 13 markdown-review extensions","n":1217,"unit":"installs","tone":"neutral"},{"label":"Ceiling for any single one","n":400,"unit":"installs","tone":"warn"},{"label":"mddiff — our exact sentence, June 2026","n":74,"unit":"installs","tone":"stop"}],"note":"In Obsidian, Drift does the same job at 893 downloads against a 143 million download registry.","caption":"The VS Code niche enumerated, ending at our own sentence"},"stakes":"The difference between a market ceiling and thirteen bad listings decides how much weight the direction can bear.","state":["The plan's key figures carry it first: 1,217 total installs of all 13 markdown-review extensions, ceiling 400 (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:9`).","§23 Opportunities reads the same number the other way, as a niche that is real, narrow and small (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:559`).","Drift, an Obsidian plugin doing exactly this job at 893 downloads, is measured in `docs/CRITIQUE.md:355` and absent from the plan."],"path":["Round 2 enumerated the niche while attacking the direction, and found mddiff at 74 installs three months after publication (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:24`).","Drift was measured on 2026-08-31 and recorded as our MVP-0 demo as an Obsidian plugin (`docs/CRITIQUE.md:355`).","Nobody has opened, installed or assessed the listing quality of any of the twenty products."],"tension":["The same number drives two conclusions in one document: the headline did not survive, and the niche is empty and available.","The plan carries a 200-install kill line for a channel it has already cut, and no threshold for the niche it intends to enter.","Free software in an adjacent shape does travel: human-review reached 1,241 stars in six weeks, and 501 repos match \"agent diff review\" since May.","A ceiling and a distribution failure look identical from outside, and half a day separates them."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"The niche, enumerated","items":[["Purpose-built markdown-review extensions in the VS Code Marketplace","13","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:24"],["Their combined installs","1,217","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:9"],["Ceiling for any single one","400","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:9"],["mddiff, our sentence shipped 2026-06-03","74 installs","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:24"],["Obsidian plugins in the same niche","7, none above 1,540 downloads","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:559"],["SpecKit Companion, the nearest shipped sidecar pattern","9,367 installs","review state in .spec-context.json, spec-kit only — PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:135"],["git-ai, attribution after the fact","61,517 installs","commit granularity, nothing per span — PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:151"]]},{"type":"table","title":"The Obsidian registry, by what the plugin does (CRITIQUE.md:350-359)","cols":["Plugin","What it does","Downloads","Stars"],"rows":[["Obsidian Git","the JTBD incumbent, already installed","3,075,875","—"],["Claudian","embeds Claude Code and other agents in the vault","1,958,668","15,064"],["Copilot (Brevilabs)","runs agents inside the vault, paid tiers","1,783,652","7,651"],["Tag Wrangler","tag rename and merge","1,067,863","—"],["Global Search and Replace","vault-wide replace","65,569","—"],["Drift","detects external file changes, side-by-side diffs per chunk","893","8"],["Schema Refactor","renames properties across frontmatter","66","—"]]},{"type":"table","title":"The same number used two ways in one document","cols":["Location","Reading"],"rows":[["Key figures, PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:9","1,217 total, ceiling 400 — the headline did not survive"],["§1 risk callout, PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:24","mddiff is this sentence, shipped three months ago, at 74 installs"],["§23 Opportunities, PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:559","\"Real, narrow, and small\" — thirteen extensions and seven plugins already sit in it, none above 1,540"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Treat 400 as the ceiling and publish it as the threshold to beat","what":"The number becomes a falsifiable kill line for the product itself.","gains":["Makes the direction testable rather than arguable","Ends the two contradictory readings"],"costs":["Prices success at a level that does not clear the monthly nut","Passing the threshold would still not be a business"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"A published threshold below the nut."},{"k":"b","label":"Open the top three extensions and Drift before letting the number count","what":"Half a day of installing and using the twenty products behind the ceiling.","gains":["Separates a market ceiling from twenty bad listings","One task covers both stores"],"costs":["It may return that they are good and nobody wanted them","Half a day at 1.21 engineering days a week"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Discount the number because none of them does the cross-person, in-repo form","what":"The ceiling is declared irrelevant to the narrowed claim.","gains":["Consistent with the narrowed headline","Costs nothing"],"costs":["It is the argument every one of the thirteen could have made","Unfalsifiable without users"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Pick one reading and stop publishing both","what":"An edit that makes the plan internally consistent.","gains":["Removes a contradiction on page one","Costs an edit"],"costs":["Does not itself decide whether the ceiling is real"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["The gap between the market's answer and twenty bad listings is the difference between a direction and a dead end.","Nobody in this corpus has opened any of the twenty, and it is one half-day covering both stores.","Put Drift into Exhibit 3 either way, and fix the two contradictory readings once the answer is in.","The counter-signal is real: human-review took 1,241 stars in six weeks in an adjacent shape, so distribution clearly is not the constraint everywhere."],"flip":"If the leading extensions turn out well-made, well-listed and still under 400, the ceiling is real and option a is the honest threshold to publish.","linked":[],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:9","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:24","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:135","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:151","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:559","docs/CRITIQUE.md:350","docs/CRITIQUE.md:353","docs/CRITIQUE.md:355","docs/CRITIQUE.md:356","docs/CRITIQUE.md:367","docs/CRITIQUE.md:436","https://api.github.com/repos/petergyang/human-review","merged: MK19"]},{"id":"MK13","cat":"Market & competition","sub":"Incumbents","weight":"high","q":"What is the pre-committed response when a platform ships the half we are building?","lede":"Four platforms shipped agent-change review in nine weeks. The plan states what they have not built, not what we do when they do.","visual":{"kind":"timeline","items":[{"when":"2026-07-03","label":"VS Code merges review/unreview","note":"PR #324218, milestone 1.128.0, undocumented","tone":"warn"},{"when":"2026-07-19","label":"VS Code markdown feedback editor","note":"issues #326539 and #326540, milestone 1.130.0","tone":"warn"},{"when":"2026-08-24","label":"Antigravity ships Agent Edits pane","note":"agent edits, uncommitted and branch scopes","tone":"warn"},{"when":"2026-08-28","label":"Notion ships per-change approval","note":"agent edits approved one change at a time","tone":"warn"},{"when":"2026-09-03","label":"Claude Code v2.1.260 diff panel","note":"opens itself, three scopes, no reviewed marker","tone":"stop"}],"note":"The VS Code work is gated to an experimental Agents window and the live docs page documents neither feature.","caption":"Nine weeks of absorption; the plan watches one vendor"},"stakes":"The war-game gives this the shortest fuse on its list, three to nine months, and the response is not written down anywhere.","state":["Exhibit 18 says re-check at week 12 (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:322`). §23 Threats says re-check monthly, not at week 12 (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:560`). Both are in v15.","The response in both places is one sentence: persistence across sessions, people and tools is what they do not build.","The war-game's pre-committed response exists at `docs/BUSINESS.md:1156` and is not in the plan."],"path":["Round 2 read the Claude Code changelog and found persisted unread state already shipping, with a diff panel at 2.1.260 (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:560`).","Scenario D gave this the shortest fuse on the list: capability shipped, only packaging missing (`docs/BUSINESS.md:1154`).","The 2026-09-09 sweep widened it from one vendor to four, and added Microsoft merging a per-file reviewed marker into VS Code itself."],"tension":["The trigger the war-game named has partly fired: a first-party surface writing to a user-owned path (`docs/BUSINESS.md:1152`).","Re-checking one vendor's changelog is now the wrong instrument. Four platforms shipped in nine weeks and one of them was Microsoft.","The pre-committed response is a roadmap deletion, which a small team executes faster than a large one, but only if it is written before the trigger.","The war-game's own stated failure mode is refusing to make the deletion when the moment arrives."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"What Anthropic already ships","items":[["Claude Code VS Code extension installs","24.89M","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:150"],["Plans as a markdown document with inline comments","since 2.1.70, 2026-03-06","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:150"],["Persisted unread state","shipping","2.1.261 fixes a missing unread dot and the tab badge showing unread — PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:560"],["Diff panel","2.1.260","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:560"],["Open request for a diff-review UI","262 reactions","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:150"],["What is unbuilt by them","persistence across people and tools","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:560"],["The war-game's named trigger to watch","a first-party surface that writes to a user-owned path","BUSINESS.md:1152, :1236"]]},{"type":"table","title":"The two re-check cadences in the same document","cols":["Location","Cadence","Response stated"],"rows":[["Exhibit 18 risks, PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:322","week 12","\"persistence across sessions, people and tools is what they do not build\""],["§23 Threats, PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:560","monthly, not at week 12","same sentence"],["War-game scenario D, BUSINESS.md:1148-1157","3-9 months, shortest fuse on the list","stop building what a vendor could ship; reposition as the verification layer under their output; ship the certificate as an MCP tool they can call"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Monthly check across all four platforms, with the written response","what":"One cadence, one list of sources, and a deletion decided in advance.","gains":["The response is chosen while it is cheap, not in the week it fires","Reconciles the two cadences in the published plan"],"costs":["Commits us in advance to deleting features","Recurring work at 1.21 engineering days a week"],"system":"No change; it constrains the roadmap.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Weekly changelog check, no pre-committed response","what":"Earliest possible warning with no decision attached.","gains":["Cheapest possible early signal"],"costs":["The warning arrives and nothing happens","That is precisely the failure mode the war-game names"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Week 12 only, as Exhibit 18 says","what":"One check, at the end of the ninety days.","gains":["Least effort"],"costs":["The fuse is three to nine months and four platforms shipped inside nine weeks","A changelog line can land in any of the twelve"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Concede the working-tree half and build only the cross-person, in-repo half","what":"The roadmap deletion is made now rather than on a trigger.","gains":["Removes the dependency on four roadmaps","Matches the narrowed headline in MK1"],"costs":["Shrinks MVP-0's visible feature set to the part with the least evidence","Nothing left to demo that a free panel does not do"],"system":"F2's diff view stops being a feature and becomes a read of the host's.","screens":"The review panel keeps the counter and loses the diff.","money":"None."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["The two cadences in one published document have to be reconciled, and monthly matches a fuse measured at three to nine months.","Widen the watch from one vendor to the four that shipped, plus the VS Code milestones, because the absorption is not vendor-specific.","The valuable half is the written response, which already exists at `docs/BUSINESS.md:1156` and is a roadmap deletion.","A deletion decided in advance is the one move a two-person team executes faster than a platform team."],"flip":"If MK1 settles on the cross-person, in-repo clause, option d and option a converge and the deletion is already made.","linked":["MK17"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:150","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:322","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:560","docs/BUSINESS.md:1148","docs/BUSINESS.md:1152","docs/BUSINESS.md:1154","docs/BUSINESS.md:1156","docs/BUSINESS.md:1236","https://www.notion.com/releases","https://antigravity.google/blog/vcs-and-terminal","https://raw.githubusercontent.com/anthropics/claude-code/main/CHANGELOG.md"]},{"id":"MK17","cat":"Market & competition","sub":"Evidence","weight":"high","q":"What standing competitive discipline do we actually keep, and who owns it?","lede":"Three published numbers have already been withdrawn, and nothing in the plan says when any row of the market table is read again.","visual":{"kind":"state","states":[{"label":"Fetched","meta":"with a date","via":"","tone":"good"},{"label":"Quoted","meta":"date dropped","via":"in a doc","tone":"neutral","current":true},{"label":"Stale","meta":"nobody notices","via":"weeks pass","tone":"warn"},{"label":"Withdrawn","meta":"three so far","via":"a control","tone":"stop"}],"note":"62% of the record's load-bearing claims needed correction on first primary-source check.","caption":"How every number in the market table has actually decayed"},"stakes":"Without a discipline the table decays silently and the next correction happens in a meeting instead of in a file.","state":["Exhibit 3 is dated at table level and no individual row carries a read date (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:143`).","Exhibit 18 lists ten risks, each one line with a one-line response (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:319-330`). The full war-game sits at `docs/BUSINESS.md:1092` and is not carried into it.","The war-game's eight-signal instrumentation table has named sources and triggers, and none of it appears in the plan (`docs/BUSINESS.md:1229`)."],"path":["The war-game was built on 2026-08-31 when the pitch was byte-exactness, and its moat matrix ranks byte-fidelity, the certificate and provenance.","The pitch moved twice since and the plan was rewritten around review state without carrying the scenario work forward.","Exhibit 4 records three withdrawals in the same period: the marker count, stars as channel size, and \"uncopyable\" (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:176-178`)."],"tension":["Scenario F, nobody moves and the category never forms, is named the highest-probability outcome and is the one the current risk table omits.","Seven of the eight instrumentation signals watch someone else. The eighth watches our funnel and does not exist (`docs/BUSINESS.md:1238`).","Every number in Exhibit 3 is an install, star or active-repo count, and all of them move.","A cadence nobody keeps is worse than none, because it implies a freshness that is not there."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"The war-game's six scenarios, and their lead times (BUSINESS.md:1111-1185)","cols":["Scenario","Lead time","Still applies to the review-state thesis?"],"rows":[["A · Obsidian ships conflict review","6-12 months from trigger; the setting shipped 2025-08-18","Partly — it is about sync, not review state"],["B · Notion or Coda makes files on disk the store of record","18-36 months; base rate is never","Yes, unchanged"],["C · GitHub ships a real editor over repo markdown","12-24 months","Yes, and stronger — GitHub already ships Viewed state free"],["D · A model vendor ships a filesystem-backed document surface","3-9 months, the shortest fuse","Yes, and it has partly fired: persisted unread state is shipping"],["E · A funded rival ships the same thesis with eight people","6-9 months to parity, 0 to the claim","Yes, unchanged"],["F · Nobody moves and the category never forms","no trigger; highest probability","Yes, and it is the one the current risk table omits"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"What the instrumentation table found","items":[["Signals in the table","8","BUSINESS.md:1229-1238"],["Signals that watch someone else","7","recoverable by publishing a measurement or deleting a roadmap lane — BUSINESS.md:1240"],["Signals that watch us","1","zero paid checkouts after 60 days on our own funnel"],["Whether that one exists","no","\"our own funnel — does not exist yet\" — BUSINESS.md:1238"],["Scenarios recoverable in under a fortnight by one person","A through E","BUSINESS.md:1240"],["Scenarios not recoverable at all","F","and it is the most likely"]]},{"type":"table","title":"The three withdrawn numbers, and what replaced each (PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:176-178)","cols":["Withdrawn","Why","Replacement"],"rows":[["62,976 unanswered markers","49,408 were spec-kit's own checklist line","about 1,500 live markers; later measured at 3,368 files, 42% live in a 50-file sample (PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:58)"],["496,000 stars as channel size","stars measure attention to a CLI","active-repo counts: spec-kit 11,072 repos / ~1,660 active; superpowers 75-85k / 22-30k"],["\"Uncopyable\"","trailers and git-ai attribute at commit level","struck"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Monthly re-read of Exhibit 3, a fetch date on every row, plus the eight signals","what":"A standing sweep with an owner and a calendar.","gains":["Turns a snapshot into a series and makes decay visible","Carries the war-game's triggers into the plan"],"costs":["Recurring work for a team at 1.21 engineering days a week","A missed cadence reads as freshness that is not there"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Fetch date on every figure, no cadence, plus the two signals that have triggers","what":"Staleness becomes visible at the point of use, and only the two decision-changing signals are watched.","gains":["Zero standing cost and it works at this team size","The two signals are the ones that change the plan, not the table"],"costs":["Nothing gets noticed until someone happens to look","Five war-game scenarios stay unassessed against the current thesis"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Re-run the six scenarios against review state and replace Exhibit 18","what":"The current thesis gets the scrutiny the previous one got.","gains":["The only option that tests the scenarios against the thesis they now threaten","Would produce a real risk register"],"costs":["A day or two of writing","It will produce more risk rows than the plan wants to publish"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Retire the war-game and treat Exhibit 18 as the whole register","what":"One risk document instead of two.","gains":["No ambiguity about which governs"],"costs":["The ten one-line rows carry no lead times, triggers or pre-committed responses","That is exactly what made the war-game useful"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["A one-person team cannot hold a monthly market sweep, and a cadence nobody keeps implies a freshness that is not there.","Marking every figure with its own fetch date gives the same protection for the cost of an edit.","Add the two war-game signals that actually have triggers: a model vendor writing to a user-owned path, and our own funnel.","Carry scenario F into Exhibit 18. It is called the highest-probability outcome and the plan does not mention it at all."],"flip":"If a second person joins, option a is affordable and correct; if the form factor lands as an extension, scenarios C and D change shape and option c is forced.","linked":["MK12","MK13"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:58","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:143","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:176-178","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:227","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:319-330","docs/BUSINESS.md:1092","docs/BUSINESS.md:1111","docs/BUSINESS.md:1229","docs/BUSINESS.md:1238","docs/BUSINESS.md:1240","docs/DECIDE.md:212","merged: MK23"]},{"id":"MK29","cat":"Market & competition","sub":"Precedent","weight":"high","q":"Five products with this feature set are dead — do we publish why this one differs, or leave the graveyard unnamed?","lede":"The category has a repeated failure mode, and in three of the five cases the people who lived it said what it was.","visual":{"kind":"timeline","items":[{"when":"2014-05-30","label":"Editorially closes","note":"paying users would not have been enough","tone":"stop"},{"when":"2016-06-01","label":"Poetica dead","note":"acquired 1 March; goals stated as at odds","tone":"stop"},{"when":"2020-03-03","label":"Atrium shuts down","note":"after $75.5M raised","tone":"stop"},{"when":"2022-02-01","label":"Upsource, end of sales","note":"industry moving off standalone review tools","tone":"stop"},{"when":"2025-01-31","label":"Almanac switches off","note":"$45M; cause stated as capacity","tone":"stop"}],"note":"Codebrag, SpaceCode and Swimm sit alongside Upsource; Draft and Penflip are dead with the cause unverified.","caption":"Every product that sold this shape, and the date it stopped"},"stakes":"A plan that does not name its own graveyard is refuted by anyone who has been in the category five years.","state":["The plan carries no dead-product section. `docs/BUSINESS.md:1092` holds the war-game and its scenario F, and neither reaches the risk table.","Scenario F, nobody moves and the category never forms, is named the highest-probability outcome and has no trigger to watch.","The 2026-09-09 sweep opened five shutdowns with dates and, in three cases, a stated cause."],"path":["Editorially closed on 2014-05-30 saying that even universal payment would not have been enough.","Poetica was acquired on 2016-03-01 and dead by 1 June, with the two parties' goals described as at odds.","JetBrains ended Upsource sales on 2022-02-01, citing a gradual industry trend away from standalone code review tools."],"tension":["The stated causes are not one cause. Money, acquisition, category drift and capacity are four different failures.","Upsource's stated cause is the direct threat: standalone review tools lose to review inside the tool people already use.","That reading argues for the extension form factor and against the standalone editor, which is MK2's decision.","Publishing the graveyard makes the plan more credible and the product harder to sell in the same paragraph."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"The graveyard, from opened sources","items":[["Editorially","closed 2014-05-30","stated that even if all users paid, it would not have been enough — stet.editorially.com"],["Poetica","acquired 2016-03-01, dead 2016-06-01","goals described as at odds — blog.poetica.com via web.archive.org"],["Atrium","shut down 2020-03-03","after $75.5M — techcrunch.com"],["JetBrains Upsource","end of sales 2022-02-01","cited a gradual industry trend away from standalone code review tools"],["Almanac","shut down 2025-01-31","cause stated as capacity — get.almanac.io/go-forward"],["Draft and Penflip","dead, cause unverified","death confirmed; do not state a cause"],["Codebrag, SpaceCode, Swimm","dead","standalone code review, same shelf as Upsource"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Publish the graveyard with dates and stated causes, and answer Upsource directly","what":"A short section naming five products, the dates, and what we do that each did not.","gains":["Credible to anyone who has been in the category","Forces the form-factor answer rather than deferring it"],"costs":["Every reader now knows the base rate","The honest answer to Upsource points away from a standalone editor"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Publish only the ones whose cause we verified, and say the rest are unverified","what":"Three stated causes, two deaths without one.","gains":["Nothing overstated","Still credible"],"costs":["A shorter list reads as a curated one","The pattern is weaker with two of five missing"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Carry scenario F into the risk table and leave the graveyard out","what":"The highest-probability outcome gets a row; the dead products do not.","gains":["Fixes the risk table's largest omission for one row"],"costs":["A row is not an argument","The five names are the evidence for the row"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Say nothing about dead products","what":"The plan stays as it is.","gains":["Nothing to explain"],"costs":["Anyone who names Upsource or Almanac gets no answer","Silence reads as not having looked"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["The five names are the strongest available evidence for scenario F, and scenario F is the outcome the war-game calls most likely.","Upsource's stated cause is the one that bites: standalone review tools lose to review inside the tool people already use. That belongs in the form-factor decision.","Quote each cause exactly as stated and mark Draft and Penflip as cause-unverified. The dates are verified; the causes are not all."],"flip":"If the twenty conversations show teams already buying a standalone review surface, Upsource's stated trend does not apply here and the section becomes a footnote.","linked":["MK17","MK27"],"sources":["docs/BUSINESS.md:1092","docs/BUSINESS.md:1111","http://stet.editorially.com/articles/goodbye/","https://techcrunch.com/2020/03/03/atrium-shuts-down/","https://get.almanac.io/go-forward"]},{"id":"MK21","cat":"Market & competition","sub":"Positioning","weight":"medium","q":"Do we publish the Djot arithmetic as a public position, or say nothing about markdown dialects?","lede":"Djot is the improved-markdown design by CommonMark's own author and the first thing a technical reviewer will raise.","visual":{"kind":"file","name":"spec.md","lines":[{"t":"# Payment spec","mark":""},{"t":"","mark":""},{"t":"The runtime reads [foo][bar] before boot.","mark":"?","note":"a link, or literal text"},{"t":"","mark":""},{"t":"...400 lines...","mark":""},{"t":"","mark":""},{"t":"[bar]: https://example.com/bar","mark":"-","note":"delete this and line 3 changes meaning"}],"note":"Measured across four CommonMark engines, unanimous in both directions.","caption":"Non-locality: bytes elsewhere decide what these bytes mean"},"stakes":"Publishing teaches every reader that a better markdown exists and that we chose not to build it.","state":["§20 names Djot and states the verdict: no new format, and the reason is adoption, not architecture (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:486`).","It also records that the smart-punctuation objection was tested on 2026-09-08 and fails (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:490`).","Nothing in the go-to-market says whether any of this is stated publicly."],"path":["The gap register found the dialect landscape in the record with zero lines in the assembled plan (`docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:68`).","Round 2 restored it with numbers: 4,984 npm downloads against `marked`'s 275,363,833, a ratio of 55,250 to 1.","The section is now correct and entirely internal."],"tension":["Djot is right about CommonMark, and its diagnosis lands on us: we inherit seventeen numbered emphasis rules, five of them pure tie-breakers.","Non-locality is the engine's real refusal condition and none of the refusals is currently declared (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:510`).","Publishing the refusal instead of the format argument is the sharper claim, and it would be a promise rather than a fact today.","If the question turns out to be common, we have published nothing to point at."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"Djot against the incumbent, measured to 2026-09-06","items":[["@djot/djot npm downloads, one month","4,984","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:486"],["marked npm downloads, same window","275,363,833","ratio 55,250 : 1 — PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:486"],["Djot GitHub stars","2,038","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:486"],["Best Djot VS Code extension","247 installs","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:486"],["Djot support among Obsidian community plugins","0 of 7,422","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:486"],["Feature requests at Hugo, Astro or Jekyll","zero","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:486"],["The smart-punctuation objection against byte-exactness","tested 2026-09-08 and fails","source-to-source round-trips are byte-identical — PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:490"]]},{"type":"table","title":"What Djot is right about, and what it costs us to say so","cols":["Djot's diagnosis","Our position"],"rows":[["Seventeen numbered emphasis rules, five of them pure tie-breakers","We inherit all of them (PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:488)"],["`[foo][bar]` means different things depending on a definition elsewhere in the file, which makes accurate highlighting nearly impossible","Named in §20 item 5 as the engine's real refusal condition — and none of the refusals is currently declared (PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:510)"],["The fix is a new syntax","Refused on adoption: 55,250 : 1"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Publish the arithmetic as the standing answer to \"why not a better markdown\"","what":"The numbers go on a public page and the position is stated once.","gains":["Pre-empts the strongest technical objection with numbers","Shows the work, which is the house style"],"costs":["Puts a competitor's design in front of every reader","Concedes the format we build on is flawed"],"system":"No change.","screens":"A page or a section of one.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Keep it internal and answer only when asked","what":"The section exists so the answer is ready in a room.","gains":["Nothing in the marketing teaches anyone about Djot","The numbers hold when the question comes"],"costs":["If the question is common, there is nothing to point at"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Publish the non-locality refusal instead, framed as what the engine does","what":"A product claim about refusing to guess, not a format argument.","gains":["Turns a defensive answer into a differentiator","Uses the sharper half of the evidence"],"costs":["None of the refusals is declared in the engine today","Publishing before building is a promise, not a fact"],"system":"The refusal conditions must actually be declared and tested first.","screens":"A refusal state in the editor.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Say nothing about dialects at all","what":"The topic is absent from every public surface.","gains":["Keeps the message narrow"],"costs":["The first technical reviewer raises Djot and there is no prepared answer","That is the situation the gap register flagged"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["The section exists so the answer is ready, and that is its whole job.","A plan that can answer the Djot question in a room does not need to publish it, and publishing introduces a design most readers have never heard of.","Option c is the better public claim but must wait until the refusals are declared in the engine. §20 item 5 says none of them is today."],"flip":"If a technical reviewer raises Djot unprompted in more than one of the twenty team conversations, the question is common enough to answer in public.","linked":["MK25"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:486","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:488","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:490","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:510","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:68"]},{"id":"MK25","cat":"Market & competition","sub":"Positioning","weight":"medium","q":"Which shelf does the buyer file this under, and do we accept the price on that shelf?","lede":"The buyer does not invent a category, and on the shelf the plan currently sits on the price is zero.","visual":{"kind":"matrix","x":["the job is somebody else's","the job is ours"],"y":["price is $0","price is thousands a year"],"points":[{"label":"Markdown editor","x":0.12,"y":0.06},{"label":"AI code editor","x":0.35,"y":0.28},{"label":"AI review of machine changes","x":0.88,"y":0.72},{"label":"Redlining for law firms","x":0.6,"y":0.86},{"label":"Docs platform","x":0.28,"y":0.95},{"label":"frontmatter as positioned today","x":0.15,"y":0.06,"us":true}],"note":"Shelves and owners from CRITIQUE.md:252-260; the redlining prices from draftable.com/pricing.","caption":"Where the buyer files it now, against where the job actually sits"},"stakes":"Filing under markdown editor means the price is $0 and the team tier has to carry the whole business.","state":["The positioning leads with refusals: no plugins, no code execution, no holding files, no lock-in, a hide-all-AI switch (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:298`).","The market table is organised by what tools do, not by what a buyer would search for (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:145-160`).","Exhibit 3's price note states the editor is worth ₹0 in this category (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:161`)."],"path":["The shelf analysis was written on 2026-08-31, when the pitch was byte-exactness. It named the problem: an unrecognised category has no search volume, no grid and no budget line (`docs/CRITIQUE.md:258`).","It found one shelf where the job is genuinely ours, and its incumbents charge four to nine times our top tier (`docs/CRITIQUE.md:256`).","The 2026-09-09 sweep added a fifth shelf: prose redlining, where Draftable sells word-level diff alone at $129 to $261 per user per year."],"tension":["Leading with refusals reads as a markdown editor with fewer features, and the buyer then files it where the price is zero.","The review-of-machine-changes incumbents review code with a model. We review documents with a hash, which invites a capability question we cannot answer yet.","The redlining shelf has budgets and a trained buyer, and nobody in that thirty-year category sells below word level.","The docs-platform shelf implies hosting we refused, and Mintlify at $450 a month is not a shelf a one-person team enters."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"The shelves, and who owns each (CRITIQUE.md:252-260)","cols":["Shelf","Who owns it","The price on it"],"rows":[["Markdown editor / notes app","Obsidian — 16.1% of 30,065 SO devs, free without limits, 7,092 plugins","$0 for the editor; $4 for sync"],["AI code editor / agent surface","Cursor ($20 reference), Zed","$0-20"],["AI review of machine changes — the only shelf where the job is ours","CodeRabbit $24-48/seat, Greptile $30/seat","4-9x our top tier, sold to teams with budgets"],["Docs platform","Mintlify $450/mo, GitBook $65-249/site, ReadMe $100-150","not a shelf a solo founder enters"],["Source-of-truth workspace","nobody — that is the problem","no search volume, no grid, no budget line"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"What the category owner gives away","items":[["Obsidian editor","free, no limits","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:156"],["Obsidian Sync","$4","the one proven individual price — PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:161"],["Obsidian commercial licence","$50/user/year","confers no functional benefit, optional since Feb 2025, bought by 25+ seat organisations — PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:161"],["Zed","free","reviews per hunk — PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:157"],["Free OSS floor in the category","AppFlowy 76,040 stars, AFFiNE 71,976, SiYuan 46,023, Logseq 44,669","CRITIQUE.md:254"],["The corpus's own conclusion about the default filing","\"another markdown editor, and the price on that shelf is $0\"","CRITIQUE.md:260"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"File under AI review of machine changes, priced against that shelf","what":"The category line names review of machine output, not markdown editing.","gains":["The one shelf where the job is ours and budgets exist","Published prices four to nine times the intended one"],"costs":["Those incumbents review code with a model; we review documents with a hash","Invites a capability comparison we cannot yet answer"],"system":"Review gates in CI have to work, because that is the shelf's table stakes.","screens":"The landing page leads with the review panel, not the editor.","money":"Anchors at $24-30 a seat rather than $4."},{"k":"b","label":"File under markdown editor and accept $0, with a paid team tier on top","what":"We accept the category the buyer will actually search for.","gains":["Matches what the free tier genuinely is","No capability comparison to lose"],"costs":["The price on that shelf is zero","The team tier then has to carry the entire business"],"system":"No change.","screens":"No change.","money":"Editor revenue is zero by definition."},{"k":"c","label":"File under prose redlining and sell to teams that already pay for diff","what":"We enter the thirty-year category where diff alone has a budget line.","gains":["Draftable sells word-level prose diff at $129-261 per user per year","A trained buyer who already searches for this"],"costs":["Their substrate is Word and PDF, and we have no Word path","Nobody in that category sells below word level, so byte precision is unwanted"],"system":"A `.docx` path we have refused.","screens":"A redline view, which does not exist.","money":"The highest observed prices in the corpus."},{"k":"d","label":"Refuse to pick and lead with the refusals as today","what":"The buyer files it himself.","gains":["Distinctive and honest"],"costs":["On the available evidence he files it under markdown editor at $0"],"system":"No change.","screens":"No change.","money":"None."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["The current positioning leaves the filing to the buyer, and he files it where the price is zero.","The review-of-machine-changes shelf is where the job actually sits, and it is where the twenty team conversations should be held.","Keep the refusals as the second line rather than the first.","Name the redlining shelf in the market table as adjacent and declined, so a reviewer sees it was considered."],"flip":"If the form factor lands as a standalone editor for individuals, the buyer files it under markdown editor whatever the copy says, and option b is honest.","linked":["MK30","PR3"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:145-160","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:156","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:161","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:298","docs/CRITIQUE.md:252","docs/CRITIQUE.md:254","docs/CRITIQUE.md:256","docs/CRITIQUE.md:258","docs/CRITIQUE.md:260","https://draftable.com/pricing"]},{"id":"MK30","cat":"Market & competition","sub":"Adjacent markets","weight":"medium","q":"Do we go after prose redlining and the legal buyer this year, or state it as adjacent and decline?","lede":"Draftable sells word-level prose diff alone at $129 to $261 a user a year, which is thirty times what we plan to charge.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":150,"cols":[{"title":"Draftable","tone":"neutral"},{"title":"Diffchecker","tone":"neutral"},{"title":"frontmatter","tone":"accent"}],"rows":[{"label":"Price","cells":["$129/user/yr Business; $261 Legal","$15, $20 or $40 per user a month","Planned $4-5 per user a month"]},{"label":"Substrate","cells":["Word and PDF","Any text","Markdown in git"]},{"label":"Granularity sold","cells":["Word level","Word level","Byte level"]},{"label":"Buyer","cells":["Law firms with a budget line","Anyone with a card","Undecided"]},{"label":"Mac client","cells":["None","Web only","Web and desktop"]}],"note":"Nobody in this thirty-year category sells below word level, so byte precision sits under the category floor.","caption":"Prose diff alone sells for thirty times our planned price, to lawyers"},"stakes":"The legal vertical is where diff already has a budget line, and it is on a substrate we have refused.","state":["The market table has no redlining row at all (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:145-160`).","The corpus already found the segment with the most measured pain writes `.docx`, where an MIT competitor ships this engine (`docs/CRITIQUE.md:307`).","The plan's positioning and engine are both markdown-only (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:298`)."],"path":["The persona review put the liable services operator on the wrong substrate and left it there (`docs/CRITIQUE.md:307`).","The 2026-09-09 sweep opened the redlining category's live prices for the first time.","Atrium raised $75.5M selling software into law firms and shut down on 2020-03-03."],"tension":["Byte-exact splicing sits under the category floor. No trained buyer in redlining has been taught to want it.","The prices are the highest observed anywhere in the corpus, and the buyer already searches for the product.","Entering means a Word path, which contradicts the substrate the whole engine is built on.","Litera claims 15,000 customers and 99% of the Am Law 100. That is a self-claim, and it describes an incumbent nobody displaces from outside."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"The redlining shelf, from opened sources","items":[["Draftable","$129/user/yr Business, $261/user/yr Legal","draftable.com/pricing; no Mac client"],["Diffchecker","$15, $20 and $40 per user per month","diffchecker.com/pricing"],["Litera","$16M to about $250M revenue, 15,000+ customers, 99% of the Am Law 100","litera.com/our-story — a self-claim, undated at both ends"],["Atrium","shut down 2020-03-03 after $75.5M","techcrunch.com"],["Granularity sold anywhere in the category","never below word level","so byte precision is under the floor"],["Draftable's customer count","1,300, 1,500, 2,500 and 4,000 all appear on its own pages","use the prices, never a count"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Write the paragraph: redlining is adjacent, not competitive, and we decline it","what":"One stated boundary in the market table and the positioning.","gains":["A reviewer respects a boundary that is stated rather than missed","Costs a paragraph"],"costs":["Concedes the segment with the most measured pain","Gives up the highest observed prices in the corpus"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Add a redlining row to the market table and price against it","what":"The shelf enters the comparison set and informs what we charge.","gains":["Prose diff alone at $129-261 a year reframes our own price","Puts a fourth rung on the pricing barbell"],"costs":["We are comparing a markdown tool to a Word tool","Invites a substrate question we answer with a refusal"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"Raises the plausible ceiling on the paid tier."},{"k":"c","label":"Build a Word path and go after the legal buyer","what":"A `.docx` route so the liable buyer's actual document is served.","gains":["The one segment with measured, priceable pain","An existing budget line"],"costs":["Contradicts the substrate the engine is built on","Atrium burned $75.5M selling into this buyer and shut down"],"system":"A whole second substrate the splice engine does not handle.","screens":"A redline view that does not exist.","money":"A long enterprise sales cycle with no budget for it."},{"k":"d","label":"Ignore the category entirely","what":"Nothing changes.","gains":["No edit"],"costs":["A reviewer who knows Draftable asks why prose diff sells for $261 and we sell for $54","No prepared answer"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["The row costs nothing and the prices are the best pricing evidence in the corpus. Prose diff alone, with no review state, sells for thirty times our plan.","State the decline in the same row. We are not building a Word path, and Atrium is the reason to say so plainly.","Do not quote a Draftable customer count. Four different figures appear on their own pages."],"flip":"If the twenty conversations surface a team keeping contracts as markdown in git, option c stops being a substrate contradiction and becomes a segment.","linked":["MK25","MK31"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:145-160","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:298","docs/CRITIQUE.md:307","https://draftable.com/pricing","https://www.diffchecker.com/pricing/","https://www.litera.com/our-story","https://techcrunch.com/2020/03/03/atrium-shuts-down/"]},{"id":"MK31","cat":"Market & competition","sub":"Segments","weight":"medium","q":"Do we target regulated software teams keeping quality documents as markdown in git?","lede":"It is the only adjacent buyer whose documents are already markdown in git, and no regulation opened requires what we sell.","visual":{"kind":"state","states":[{"label":"Draft","meta":"in the repo","via":"","tone":"neutral"},{"label":"Reviewed","meta":"per span","via":"our sidecar","tone":"accent"},{"label":"Approved","meta":"whole document","via":"a signature","tone":"good","current":true},{"label":"Superseded","meta":"record retained","via":"21 CFR 11","tone":"neutral"}],"note":"21 CFR 11.10(e): record changes shall not obscure previously recorded information.","caption":"Regulation mandates the third step; our claim sits in the second"},"stakes":"Claiming a regulatory requirement that does not exist is the fastest way to lose a compliance buyer.","state":["The plan's buyer decision offers only the AI-native developer or the person liable when a document is wrong (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:366`).","The persona review found the compliance-adjacent writer unreachable without SOC 2 and a nine to eighteen month cycle (`docs/CRITIQUE.md:233`).","§22 names GST, IT Rules and DPDP, and no quality-management regime at all (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:535-551`)."],"path":["The regulated buyer's actual requirements were listed as untapped: design for, do not chase, was decided without asking what an audit trail must contain (`docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:41`).","The 2026-09-09 sweep opened the primary texts for the first time.","None of them mandates per-span review. Pharma mandates whole-document approval; aviation mandates a per-page revision date."],"tension":["MHRA has already adjudicated the exhaustive-list question and permits audit trails reviewed by exception rather than in full.","The EMA's 2024 reflection paper says model-generated text needs a quality review mechanism, and it is non-binding and names no granularity.","Selling into this buyer needs SOC 2, an outside security review and a sales cycle the ninety-day plan has no room for.","Their documents are already markdown in git, which is true of no other buyer with a budget line."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"What the regulators actually say, from opened texts","items":[["21 CFR 11.10(e)","\"Record changes shall not obscure previously recorded information.\"","ecfr.gov — retention, not per-span review"],["MHRA GxP data integrity guide","audit trails may be reviewed as a list \"or by an 'exception reporting' process\"","assets.publishing.service.gov.uk"],["EMA reflection paper, 9 Sept 2024","model-generated text needs a quality review mechanism","non-binding; names no granularity"],["Any regulation mandating per-span review","none found","pharma mandates whole-document approval; aviation a per-page revision date"],["What the compliance persona needs first","SOC 2, attorney review, a 9-18 month cycle","CRITIQUE.md:233"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Target regulated software teams whose quality documents live in git","what":"The buyer decision gains a third named candidate with its own evidence.","gains":["The only adjacent buyer already on our substrate","Exception reporting is exactly what our review panel does"],"costs":["SOC 2, an outside security review and a nine to eighteen month cycle","None of it fits inside ninety days"],"system":"Retention, audit export and an approval object none of which exist.","screens":"An approval and export surface.","money":"SOC 2 and legal review, unbudgeted."},{"k":"b","label":"Design for them, chase the developer, and say so in writing","what":"Retention and non-destructive records are built in; the sales motion is not.","gains":["Costs little today and keeps the door open","The retention floor is already forced by CERT-In and DPDP"],"costs":["Designing for a buyer we do not talk to is how the F5/F6 contradiction happened","No revenue from it this year"],"system":"The sidecar must never obscure a previous record.","screens":"None yet.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Ignore the segment until a customer asks","what":"No design accommodation and no claim.","gains":["Smallest surface"],"costs":["Retrofitting non-destructive records later is expensive","Loses the one adjacent buyer on our substrate"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Quote the regulators in the marketing and let readers infer a requirement","what":"21 CFR and MHRA appear in the pitch as validation.","gains":["Reads as authority to a non-specialist"],"costs":["No regulation opened mandates per-span review","A compliance buyer punishes the missing caveat harder than the missing claim"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["Their documents are already markdown in git, which is true of no other buyer with a budget line. The design cost of never obscuring a previous record is near zero today.","The sales cost is the blocker, not the fit. SOC 2 and a nine to eighteen month cycle do not fit inside ninety days.","Whenever a regulator is quoted, say plainly in the same sentence that none of them requires per-span review. The caveat is what a compliance buyer checks for."],"flip":"If two or more of the twenty conversations are with regulated teams already keeping quality documents in git, option a becomes the segment and the schedule changes.","linked":["MK30","MK4"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:366","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:535-551","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:41","docs/CRITIQUE.md:233","https://www.ecfr.gov/api/versioner/v1/full/2026-01-01/title-21.xml?part=11","https://www.ema.europa.eu/en/documents/scientific-guideline/reflection-paper-use-artificial-intelligence-ai-medicinal-product-lifecycle_en.pdf"]},{"id":"PR1","cat":"Pricing & tiers","sub":"Tier contents","weight":"critical","q":"What does Pro actually gate on, and how long does the journal have to be kept?","lede":"The two things v15 put behind the gate have no feature row, and one of them is a command that exits with a module-not-found error.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":190,"cols":[{"title":"Retained journal","tone":"warn"},{"title":"CI gate, mdmax cert","tone":"warn"},{"title":"Attribution, F3","tone":"accent"}],"rows":[{"label":"Feature row with days","cells":["None. Line 289 says so itself","None; 1 day to wire, line 224","3 days for the readers, line 57"]},{"label":"Runs today","cells":["No","No. ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND","No. Estimated, unbuilt"]},{"label":"In the free tier now","cells":["Current state only","n/a","Yes, inside F1-F8"]},{"label":"Someone charges for it","cells":["Obsidian 1 month to 12 months","Docs-as-code CI seats, line 443","Google Workspace Business Standard"]}],"note":"Google gates span-level authorship and gives the file-level signal away free.","caption":"Three candidate gates, against whether they exist and whether anyone sells them."},"stakes":"A price published against two objects that have no feature row is a price the build team cannot deliver against.","state":["Pro is $4-5 per user per month for a splice journal kept 90 days and review gates that block in CI (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:288).","Neither gate exists. The plan's own Max row says no feature row builds retention at all (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:289), and `mdmax cert` was never wired to a runnable command (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:224).","Shared review state and MCP sit inside Pro but are disclaimed as the gate. They carry 16 estimated days between them (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:288).","Attribution is free today, inside F1-F8 (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:287)."],"path":["Round 2 found the tiers inverted: Pro held what comparables give away, Max held what they charge for (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:131).","So enforcement was pulled forward into Pro and retention was named as the paid object, a day before the meeting.","The same round found Google sells span-level authorship at exactly our intended tier, and the plan had demoted that feature as unsellable (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:139).","The 90-day number predates the CERT-In work, which now sets a 180-day floor and tells us to delete the 90-day rule (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:545)."],"tension":["Two other rows of the same document still route CI gates to Max (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:202, docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:443).","The retention comparable does not fit the offer: Obsidian's ladder is 1 month to 12 months, and we ship one rung at 90 days.","Retention gets more expensive as a paid object the moment the journal carries prompts, because CERT-In sets a floor we cannot delete below.","Attribution is the only one of the four claims nobody has shipped, and it is currently given away."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"What Pro charges for, and whether it exists","cols":["Pro object","F-row","Days estimated","Runs today"],"rows":[["Retained splice journal, 90 days","none - PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:289 says so itself","none","no"],["Review gates in CI (mdmax cert)","none","1d to wire (§9 item 10, line 224)","no - ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND, re-run in this audit"],["Shared review state, comments (F10) - in Pro, disclaimed as the gate","F10","10d","not built"],["MCP server (F11) - in Pro, disclaimed as the gate","F11","6d","not built"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"What the cert gate's absence looks like on disk, re-checked in this audit","items":[["`node scripts/mdmax-cert.mjs --bench-info`","ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND","cannot resolve `src/modules/mdmax/domain/offsets`, imported from certify.ts"],["`cert` in package.json scripts","absent","26 scripts present; none is `cert`"],["`.github/` directory","does not exist","so no GitHub Action can be required on any path"],["Plan's own estimate to wire it","1 day","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:224"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"The same document routes CI gates to two different tiers","items":[["Exhibit 16 §11","Pro","\"pulled forward from Max, because enforcement is what GitHub sells at $4\" (line 288)"],["Exhibit 6 §8","Max","AI row, MVP-2 column reads \"Document gates in CI\" (line 202)"],["Exhibit 25 §18","Max","upsell row for CI gates routes to Max (line 443)"]]},{"type":"table","title":"The anchor ladder against the offered ladder, with what is actually verified","cols":["Product","Lower rung","Upper rung","Status of the price step"],"rows":[["Obsidian Sync","1 month history","12 months history","retention step fetched (s4:63); price mapping [SS], recorded as a discrepancy (x5:236)"],["HackMD","free tier version cap","unlimited, Prime $5 annual / $8 monthly","prices fetched (r7/g1:115); the \"Recent 10 versions\" free cap appears in no research file"],["frontmatter as written","current state only, free","90 days, $4-5","one rung; nothing between 90 days and Max's \"beyond a year\""]]},{"type":"stat","title":"Where 90 days came from, and what the law now requires","items":[["§22 operating rules","\"Delete the record's 'no row-level retention beyond 90 days' rule\"","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:545 - the notified text refutes it"],["Live log floor today","180 days of ICT logs, rolling, inside Indian jurisdiction","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:544 (CERT-In)"],["From 2027-05-13","one year of access logs, and processing logs surviving account deletion","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:545 (DPDP Rules 6(1)(e), 8(3))"],["Retention as a feature row","does not exist","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:289"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","what":"Retention stays the paid object and becomes a scheduled feature with a day estimate before any price is published.","label":"Keep retention as the gate, write it as an F-row first","gains":["It is the plan's own written instruction, in its own Max row","Retention is one of only two things the comparables actually charge for"],"costs":["Adds unestimated work to a schedule already at 58 calendar weeks","The price cannot be quoted until the estimate exists","90 days collides with the CERT-In floor, so the number moves again"],"system":"New store: an append-only journal with a retention policy and a deletion job.","screens":"A history view over the journal, which no screen currently shows.","money":"No revenue until the F-row lands. Storage cost scales with retention length."},{"k":"b","what":"Free keeps attribution from commit trailers; Pro gates per-span, prompt-bearing provenance from the MCP write path.","label":"Gate on attribution, the one claim nobody else shipped","gains":["Google sells exactly this at exactly this tier, and gives the file-level half away","It is the only one of four claims no platform has occupied","F3 and F11 already carry estimates"],"costs":["Takes a feature out of a free tier the distribution strategy depends on","Prompt-bearing writes need F11 MCP, which is 6 days and untested","Attribution is absent whenever the write carried nothing"],"system":"The split runs through F3's readers: trailers free, MCP-carried prompts paid.","screens":"The hover card gains a locked state on the paid half.","money":"No new build beyond F11. Ties the price to a feature with a live paid precedent."},{"k":"c","what":"Pro is simply the second seat on a repo, with every feature included and nothing withheld.","label":"Gate on people, not features","gains":["Nothing new to build and one sentence to explain","Matches what the seats are actually for"],"costs":["Honour-system at best, which is PR2's problem in full","Gives up the argument that we charge for something specific"],"system":"No change.","screens":"A seat count in settings. Nothing else.","money":"Fastest to charge for. Revenue depends entirely on goodwill."},{"k":"d","what":"No Pro gate is named until the twenty team conversations come back.","label":"Name no gate until the conversations return","gains":["Publishes no price with nothing behind it","The conversations are already scheduled for weeks 1-2"],"costs":["Leaves the plan with no revenue line for the whole build","Every other card on this page stays a hypothesis until then"],"system":"No change.","screens":"No pricing page.","money":"None."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["Attribution is the only claim in the plan that no platform occupied in the last nine weeks, and Google already sells it at this exact tier.","It costs nothing new: F3's readers are estimated and F11 is already inside Pro.","Retention fails three ways at once. No feature row, a comparable that does not fit the offer, and a 90-day number the CERT-In work has already told us to delete.","Whatever is chosen, fix the two rows that still send CI gates to Max in the same edit."],"flip":"If the twenty conversations name shared review state or history rather than provenance as the thing a team would pay for, the gate is (a) or (c).","linked":["F1","MK4","PR2","PR21","PR23","PR3"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:57","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:202","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:224","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:287","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:288","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:289","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:443","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:545","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:131","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:139","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-29-r8to10/s4-mobile-cross-device.md:63","merged: PR6"],"dupes":{"dropped":["F12","PL15"],"why":"One decision — what Pro gates on, and whether retention gets built before the price is published — asked three times with three different answers (PR1 gate on attribution, F12 scope retention inside the review store, PL15 don't price Pro until the conversations return). Pricing & tiers owns tier contents."}},{"id":"PR2","cat":"Pricing & tiers","sub":"Enforcement","weight":"critical","q":"Where does the retained journal live, and what happens to it when a team stops paying?","lede":"The paid object is a plain-text file the free client writes, so either the gate is honour-system or the zero-bytes promise is not true.","visual":{"kind":"flow","perRow":4,"nodes":[{"label":"Payment lapses","note":"The journal is already on their disk","tone":"neutral"},{"label":"Client stops appending","note":"Past history intact and readable","tone":"good","edge":"a"},{"label":"Client truncates the file","note":"Deletes a file the user owns","tone":"stop","edge":"b"},{"label":"Server-held, then dropped","note":"Zero document bytes stops being true","tone":"warn","edge":"c"},{"label":"Rule: features, never files","note":"docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:449","tone":"accent"}],"note":"Only one branch leaves every stated promise standing.","caption":"The three things that can happen to a journal in the customer's own repo."},"stakes":"Either the pricing page describes a gate nobody can enforce, or the architecture line the whole pitch leads with is false.","state":["The sidecar is `.frontmatter/review.jsonl`, plain text, beside the documents in the user's repo, readable without frontmatter (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:135).","Pro's journal is the same file plus history, with prompts and per-span hashes, kept 90 days (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:288).","The control plane holds identity, teams, entitlements and billing, and no document bytes (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:133).","The only lapse rule written is one sentence: downgrading loses features, never files (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:449)."],"path":["The sidecar-in-the-repo design came from the refusal to hold documents, which is the strongest positioning line in the plan.","The retained journal was added as a price gate a day later, and the two were never reconciled.","BUSINESS.md has a full lapse table, but every hosted item in it was removed from the architecture in v15 (docs/BUSINESS.md:618).","The proposed week-0 decision is browser-side only, no document byte through a Zephyrus server (docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:35)."],"tension":["If the journal sits in the repo, the free client writes it and nothing is withheld. The gate is an honour system.","If it sits on our server it carries prompt text and per-span hashes, and the zero-bytes line goes.","Obsidian ran this experiment: the licence was mandatory for five years and became optional because a local app with no sign-up cannot enforce it (r26-c8:21).","BUSINESS.md already settled the principle: a product whose thesis is that the file is the only source of truth cannot hold the file hostage (docs/BUSINESS.md:632)."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"Where the journal can live, and what each costs","cols":["Location","Enforceable","Zero-bytes claim survives","Plain-text promise survives"],"rows":[["User's repo, plain text","no - honour system","yes","yes"],["Our server","yes","no - carries prompts and per-span hashes","n/a"],["User's repo, encrypted to a control-plane key","yes","yes","no - stops being readable without frontmatter"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"The precedent the corpus already measured","items":[["Obsidian commercial licence","mandatory until Feb 2025","made optional because it was unenforceable on a local app (r26-c8:21)"],["What the founder says the money comes from","Sync and Publish, not the licence","\"Obsidian makes money from its add-on services\" - Steph Ango (r26-c8:20)"],["Named orgs on the licence wall","84 or 146","two agents read the same server-rendered page a day apart and disagreed (r26-c8:39)"],["Amazon's share of the named floor","61.8%","r26-c8:37, own parse 2026-08-31"]]},{"type":"table","title":"The three possible lapse behaviours, and what each breaks","cols":["Behaviour","Journal after lapse","Rule broken"],"rows":[["Stop writing history; file stays","complete up to the lapse date, then frozen","none - but Pro becomes a subscription to future history only"],["Truncate to current state","user loses history they already had","\"loses features, never files\" (line 449) and BUSINESS.md:632"],["Journal held server-side, read-only 30 days then dropped","deleted from our systems","\"No document byte ever passes through a Zephyrus server\" (WEEK0-DECISIONS:35)"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"What BUSINESS.md's lapse table still describes that v15 no longer has","items":[["Hosted sync across devices","stops at lapse","F12 is MVP-2, 15d+, not built"],["Published pages on *.frontmatter.page","live, frozen, indefinitely","hosting is a refusal in v15 (§12 positioning)"],["Hosted version history","read-only 30 days, then dropped","no retention F-row exists (PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:289)"],["Hosted AI credits","zero at lapse","hosted AI is an unspecified add-on (PR10)"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","what":"The journal stays in the repo; on lapse the client stops appending and everything already written stays.","label":"Repo, honour-system by design, and lapse only stops new entries","gains":["Breaks no promise the plan makes in bold elsewhere","Nothing to build for the lapse path","Trivial to explain at checkout"],"costs":["Pro becomes a licence rather than a lock, the exact shape line 161 dismisses","Makes plain that Pro buys future retention, not access to the past"],"system":"One entitlement check before appending. No server storage.","screens":"A pricing-page line: your history stays, we stop adding to it.","money":"Revenue is voluntary in effect. No storage cost."},{"k":"b","what":"The journal is held on our server and dropped after a read-only window when payment stops.","label":"Server-held journal, and rewrite the zero-bytes promise","gains":["A real gate with real enforcement","Matches the lapse table BUSINESS.md already drafted"],"costs":["Loses the positioning line the plan leads with","Drags prompt text into DPDP and CERT-In scope, including the 180-day floor","Adds an intermediary-status question under the IT Act"],"system":"A hosted store, a retention job, and processor agreements.","screens":"A lapse banner and a read-only history state.","money":"Storage and compliance cost from the first paying team."},{"k":"c","what":"The journal stays in the repo but is encrypted to a key held by the control plane.","label":"Repo, encrypted to a control-plane key","gains":["Enforceable, and the bytes never leave the machine"],"costs":["Breaks readable without frontmatter, which is what makes the sidecar safe to adopt","A key server is a new failure mode for a file the user owns"],"system":"Key management on top of the sidecar writer.","screens":"An opens state nobody has designed.","money":"Key infrastructure, small but permanent."},{"k":"d","what":"Retention is dropped as the paid object and something else carries the price.","label":"Drop retention as the gate entirely","gains":["Removes the contradiction at its root","Follows automatically if PR1 goes to attribution"],"costs":["Pro is left with the CI gate, which does not run today either"],"system":"No journal store at all.","screens":"No history view.","money":"None until another gate is named."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["It is the only option that breaks no promise the plan makes in bold on another page.","The lapse behaviour falls out of it: stop appending, keep everything, say so at checkout.","Accept that the price is then a licence, price it that way, and stop calling it a gate.","Rewrite BUSINESS.md's lapse table to describe the product that exists rather than the hosted one it was written for."],"flip":"If the twenty conversations show teams will not buy without an enforced entitlement, (b) is the honest answer and the zero-bytes line must be rewritten in the same edit.","linked":["L17","PR1","PR21","PR23","PR8"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:133","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:135","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:161","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:288","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:289","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:449","docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:35","docs/BUSINESS.md:618","docs/BUSINESS.md:632","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r26-c8-b2b.md:21","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r26-c8-b2b.md:39","merged: PR14"]},{"id":"PR3","cat":"Pricing & tiers","sub":"Price level","weight":"critical","q":"What is the price, and which category is it anchored to - editors, diff tools, or docs platforms?","lede":"Draftable sells prose comparison alone at $129-261 per user a year. Our band is $48-60, anchored to sync and to a price nobody fetched.","visual":{"kind":"matrix","x":["$30 per user per year","$300 per user per year"],"y":["bought by a person","bought by an organisation"],"points":[{"label":"Obsidian Sync","x":0.07,"y":0.15},{"label":"frontmatter Pro","x":0.09,"y":0.45,"us":true},{"label":"Draftable Business","x":0.37,"y":0.85},{"label":"GitBook, per user","x":0.42,"y":0.8},{"label":"Diffchecker","x":0.56,"y":0.5},{"label":"Draftable Legal","x":0.86,"y":0.95}],"note":"Draftable and Diffchecker sell comparison alone, with no editor and no review state.","caption":"Annual price per user against buyer. Every figure from the vendor's own page."},"stakes":"Price against the wrong category and the number is either not worth collecting or not credible, and twenty conversations will only ever test the one we ask about.","state":["Pro is $4-5 per user per month with no billing period stated (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:288), which is $48-60 a year.","The anchors were GitHub Team $4, Obsidian Sync $4, HackMD $5, Confluence $6.70. Two of those are annual-billed rates and one has no fetched source in 237 research files (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:25).","The plan says the tier is a hypothesis until twenty team conversations return seat counts (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:292), and those conversations only carry the low number.","On the basis that pays the founder for support time, $5 needs 1,018 subscribers to cover the monthly nut (r26-c6:178)."],"path":["The band was picked to sit inside the category's published prices rather than derived from cost or from anyone's willingness to pay.","Earlier plan versions priced in rupees and were corrected after round 25 showed Indian companies selling globally quote dollars.","The 114-seats-at-$8 claim was withdrawn because the feature was GitHub's at $4 and the retention band would not hold it (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:292).","Nothing in the record ever compared us with the tools that sell prose comparison on its own."],"tension":["Draftable charges $129 a year for Business and $261 for Legal, per user, for comparison with no editor attached (draftable.com/pricing).","Diffchecker charges $15 to $40 per user per month for the same narrow job (diffchecker.com/pricing).","Round 2 named the failure directly: pricing below the category's credibility floor, or charging for what GitHub bundles (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:85).","$5 a month is the modal consumer price in a 940-comment corpus and sentiment there splits 11 positive against 10 negative (r25-w3:84)."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"Anchors, split by billing period, with provenance","cols":["Comparable","Annual rate","Monthly rate","Provenance in the record"],"rows":[["Obsidian Sync","$4/user/mo","$5/user/mo","r7/g1:114, fetched 2026-08-29"],["Obsidian Publish","$8/site/mo","$10/site/mo","r7/g1:114, fetched 2026-08-29"],["HackMD Prime","$5/seat/mo","$8/seat/mo (stated 37.5% annual discount)","r7/g1:115, fetched 2026-08-29"],["Confluence","-","$6.70 and $13.20 per user/mo","r25-w3:42, read 2026-08-31"],["GitHub Team","-","$4 asserted","no fetched source in 237 research files; GAPS:25 credits \"the refuter\""],["frontmatter Pro, as written","not stated","$4-5","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:288 - no period declared"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"What the price implies against founder cost and category discourse","items":[["Break-even India monthly price at Rs1,700/h founder time","Rs333.25","r26-c6:45, from support cost 0.1445 h per paying user per month"],["$4 at USD/INR 95.39","Rs381.56","derived; ECB rate date 2026-08-28 via frankfurter"],["$5 at USD/INR 95.39","Rs476.95","derived"],["Modal price in the HN pricing corpus","$5/mo, 75 of 259 mentions (29.0%)","r25-w3:77, measured"],["Sentiment at $5/mo in that corpus","11 positive vs 10 negative","r25-w3:84 - \"$5 is already the contested zone, not the safe one\""]]},{"type":"bars","title":"Paying seats needed to cover the Rs1,08,918 two-founder monthly nut","note":"Gross at USD/INR 95.39 (ECB rate date 2026-08-28). Contribution uses r26-c6's measured World Pro $5 contribution of Rs352.66. The eff rows are r26-c6:178-180's own table, which nets out founder support time at Rs1,700/h; the $30 row is its 8.6 teams x 5 seats. Nut from r26-c6:171, matching PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:292.","data":[["$4/seat, on gross revenue",286],["$5/seat, on gross revenue",229],["$5/seat, on contribution (Rs352.66)",309],["$5/seat, after founder support time (eff Rs107.01)",1018],["$30/editor in 5-seat teams, same eff basis",43]],"unit":"seats","threshold":114,"thresholdLabel":"the 114 seats the plan already withdrew as too many"},{"type":"stat","title":"Support load per rupee, from r26-c6:184","items":[["One 5-seat team at $30/seat","contributes Rs12,622/month","consumes 0.5 founder-hours/month"],["58 India Pro subscribers, same revenue","Rs12,622/month","consume 8.4 founder-hours/month - 17x worse"],["Teams to fund one founder at $30/editor","5.1","r26-c6:180, at a Rs63,918 one-founder nut"],["Individual seats to fund one founder at $5","598","same table, same eff basis"],["Live comparables at the $30 level","CodeRabbit $24 and $48/seat; Greptile $30/seat/mo","r25-w3:47-48 - AI code review, not markdown editors"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","what":"$5 per seat monthly with $4 billed annually, matching Obsidian's actual structure rather than half of it.","label":"$5 monthly, $4 annual, per seat - the editor anchor","gains":["Parity with the anchor the plan already chose, in full","Makes the annual discount an explicit lever the Indian rail needs","Settles the billing-period question by implication"],"costs":["Needs 1,018 subscribers on the basis that pays the founder","Sits at the contested $5 mode, not below it","Anchors us to editors when the closest functional comparables are diff tools"],"system":"Two SKUs and a proration path.","screens":"A pricing page with a period toggle.","money":"$48-60 per seat per year."},{"k":"b","what":"Price per person who reviews, in the band the prose-comparison tools already occupy.","label":"$10-20 per editor per month - the diff-tool anchor","gains":["Draftable already sells less than this for $129-261 per user a year","Far fewer subscribers to cover the nut","Supports a thicker offer instead of a cheaper one"],"costs":["No markdown editor charges this, so the offer must be a gate rather than an editor","PR1 says the gate is unbuilt","Untested with anyone"],"system":"Same billing, different number.","screens":"The pricing page has to justify the level, not just state it.","money":"$120-240 per editor per year."},{"k":"c","what":"One price per repository or per organisation, with no seat accounting at all.","label":"Flat, per repository or per organisation","gains":["No seat accounting and no proration, which suits a product with no enforcement","Matches how the docs platforms sell a check"],"costs":["Kills seat expansion permanently; r25-w4:61 calls the flat licence out as disabling the main growth engine","One number has to fit a two-person team and a fifty-person one"],"system":"No seat model. One entitlement per repo.","screens":"No invite-and-count flow.","money":"Predictable per logo, capped per logo."},{"k":"d","what":"Both the seat price and the editor price go into the twenty conversations, and the price is set afterwards.","label":"Carry both numbers into the twenty conversations","gains":["The conversations are the only pricing instrument that exists and cost nothing to run twice","A rejection of $5 becomes distinguishable from a rejection of paying at all"],"costs":["A two-price script is longer and can read as unserious","The answers are noisier at n=20"],"system":"No change.","screens":"No pricing page until the answer lands.","money":"Defers revenue by the length of the conversations, which is two weeks."}],"rec":"d","recCase":["The plan's own position is that the price is a hypothesis until twenty teams are asked, and it is about to ask a question with only one possible answer.","The cost of learning that the higher band is buyable is one extra sentence per conversation. The cost of not asking is a thousand seats.","Two edits regardless of the outcome: state the billing period, and strike GitHub Team from the anchor list until someone opens the page and dates it.","When the price does go on a page, publish the founder-time basis beside the gross one, so nobody reads 229 seats and thinks the nut is covered."],"flip":"If fewer than five of twenty will engage with the higher number at all, (a) is settled honestly rather than by default.","linked":["MK16","MK25","PR1","PR11","PR12","PR17"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:288","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:292","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:352","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:25","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:85","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-29-r7/g1-business-model-unit-economics.md:114","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-29-r7/g1-business-model-unit-economics.md:115","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r25-w3-willingness-to-pay.md:77","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r25-w3-willingness-to-pay.md:84","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r25-w4-retention-and-growth.md:61","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r26-c6-unit-economics.md:178","https://draftable.com/pricing","https://www.diffchecker.com/pricing/","https://obsidian.md/pricing","merged: PR9"],"dupes":{"dropped":["B4","MK10"],"why":"Which price rung, anchored to what. All three carry the $4-5 rung against a higher anchor and a 'take no number in' option; recs d/c/c. Pricing & tiers owns the price. MK10's second half (is cross-person review state the gate) is already PR1's question."}},{"id":"PR4","cat":"Pricing & tiers","sub":"Time to revenue","weight":"critical","q":"Do we ship a checkout before MVP-1, or is the first sale a conversation about eighteen months from now?","lede":"MVP-0 has no sign-up and no billing, and at the plan's own measured velocity the first chance to be paid is about 81 weeks out.","visual":{"kind":"timeline","items":[{"when":"Now","label":"No sign-up, no billing in MVP-0","note":"docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:205","tone":"neutral"},{"when":"Weeks 1-2","label":"Twenty team conversations","note":"Opinions, no money, no threshold","tone":"warn"},{"when":"About 58 weeks","label":"MVP-0 ships","note":"70 engineering days at 1.21 a calendar week","tone":"warn"},{"when":"About 81 weeks","label":"First point a team can pay","note":"F9, F10, F11 and folder-to-PDF add 28 days","tone":"stop"}],"note":"Every date derives from the density the plan measured on this repo.","caption":"The gap between the plan's first revenue event and today."},"stakes":"Eighteen months of building against a price nobody has ever been asked to pay is the failure mode the whole plan is meant to avoid.","state":["MVP-0's absent row reads sign-up, billing, sync, mobile, hosting, hosted AI, local model (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:205).","The MVP-1 exit test is a team paying within twenty conversations, so the first sale is a human conversation by construction (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:206).","MVP-0 is about 70 engineering days against a measured 1.21 engineering days per calendar week (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:227).","Across 105 reports and 374,866 words the record contains zero instances of customer-discovery or willingness-to-pay work (r26-c7:22)."],"path":["MVP-0 was scoped as a ten-stranger pilot with nothing asked of the user before value, which is the right instinct and is stated as a rule.","The elapsed time was re-derived in v15 and came out far longer than earlier versions assumed.","The previous ten-week schedule was withdrawn as arithmetically impossible in the same edit (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:229).","The corpus wrote a pre-order design with its own kill number and it was never carried into a plan version (r26-c7:122)."],"tension":["The services engagement is available now: four a year at ₹3,00,000 is the ₹1L monthly milestone, and one client equals 63,060 visitors of funnel (r23-u4:62).","Editorially, a collaborative prose editor, closed on 2014-05-30 writing that even if all of its users paid up it would not have been enough.","That arithmetic is a pre-build question. Running it after 81 weeks of building is running it too late.","A failed pre-order is public, and a public failure at week 2 is cheaper than a private one at week 81."],"evidence":[{"type":"bars","title":"Calendar weeks to a sellable product at measured velocity","note":"70 engineering days for MVP-0 plus 28 estimated MVP-1 days (F9 8d + F10 10d + F11 6d + folder-to-one-PDF 4d), divided by the density in each label. Densities measured on this repo 2026-07-13 to 2026-09-08 (PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:227).","data":[["At 1.21 eng-days/week (measured here)",81],["At 1.91 eng-days/week (sibling repo best ever)",51],["At 0.23 eng-days/week (last 30 days here)",426]],"unit":"calendar weeks","threshold":52,"thresholdLabel":"one year"},{"type":"stat","title":"What is not sellable during that window, and what is","items":[["MVP-0 billing and sign-up","both absent","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:205"],["First paid signal in the plan","a team paying after 20 conversations","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:206"],["Instances of waitlist, pre-order or willingness-to-pay work in the record","0 each, across 105 reports and 374,866 words","r26-c7:22 (finding D6), measured"],["The corpus's own pre-order proposal","a refusal-contract page with a paid $49 pre-order button","r26-c7:122"],["Its kill number","zero pre-orders from 100 qualified conversations kills the price, not the product","r26-c7:125"],["Revenue available now instead","Rs3,00,000 per 10-day engagement, 4/yr = Rs12,00,000","r23-u4:62, r23-u4:84"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","what":"Billing stays out until MVP-1, exactly as the plan is written today.","label":"Keep billing out until MVP-1","gains":["Cleanest pilot and no billing code to maintain","Nothing asked of a stranger before value"],"costs":["No money and no price evidence for roughly 81 weeks","Every pricing card here stays a hypothesis for that whole period"],"system":"No change.","screens":"No checkout, no account.","money":"None until MVP-1."},{"k":"b","what":"A refusal-contract page with a named price, a real checkout, a full refund promise and no feature gate.","label":"Ship the pre-order page the corpus already specified","gains":["One falsifiable demand test in front of the build instead of after it","The kill number is already written: zero pre-orders from 100 qualified conversations","Costs a page, not a product"],"costs":["Needs a payment rail and a refund policy earlier than planned","A failed pre-order is public","Takes money for something that does not exist yet"],"system":"A checkout and a refunds path. No product changes.","screens":"One page: the refusals, the price, the button.","money":"$49 per pre-order, refundable, and a real answer either way."},{"k":"c","what":"An optional licence purchase from the pilot: a button and an invoice, with nothing withheld from anyone.","label":"Optional licence and a supporters wall from day one","gains":["Revenue from day one and no engineering, because nothing is enforced","Composes with PR2's honour-system answer"],"costs":["Voluntary money on a product with no users may be nothing for years","Sets the anchor low and hard to move"],"system":"A payment link. No entitlement checks.","screens":"A supporters page.","money":"Small, unpredictable, immediate."},{"k":"d","what":"The product is not priced at all until MVP-1, and the services engagement carries revenue meanwhile.","label":"Sell the services engagement instead","gains":["Revenue this month from clients who already exist","It is what the funding line already assumes"],"costs":["The product gets no price evidence at all","The founder's hours split, and the plan already caps client work at 78 a month"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"₹2,40,000 to ₹3,00,000 per engagement."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["The corpus made this exact criticism and it was not acted on: the demand test is scheduled after the build, not before it.","A pre-order page is a page, not a product. It is the only instrument that converts a pricing opinion into a fact inside two weeks.","Use the price and the kill number already in the record, so the test cannot be re-scored after the answers arrive.","If the founders will not take money before the product ships, (c) tests nearly the same thing with no obligation attached."],"flip":"If the twenty conversations produce a signed intent to buy at MVP-1 from more than five teams, the pre-order adds nothing the conversations did not already give.","linked":["PR13","PR16","PR17","PR20"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:205","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:206","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:227","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:229","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:292","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r26-c7-d2c.md:22","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r26-c7-d2c.md:122","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r26-c7-d2c.md:125","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r23-u4-consultation-and-services.md:62","http://stet.editorially.com/articles/goodbye/"]},{"id":"PR7","cat":"Pricing & tiers","sub":"Free tier","weight":"high","q":"Does the free tier stay uncapped, and which founder-hour figure do we budget against?","lede":"The free tier's cost is founder time, and the plan, the unit-economics report and the AI-economics report give three different numbers.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":200,"cols":[{"title":"The plan, §4","tone":"neutral"},{"title":"r26-c6","tone":"accent"},{"title":"r19-p1","tone":"warn"}],"rows":[{"label":"Founder-hours at 10,000 users","cells":["About 90 a month","76.8 a month","300, cumulative across signups"]},{"label":"Priced in rupees","cells":["No","₹1,30,560 a month at ₹1,700/h","No"]},{"label":"Against the whole cloud bill","cells":["Not stated","₹25,930 a month","n/a"]},{"label":"How it is tagged","cells":["Stated","Modelled, derivation shown","Marked as inference"]}],"note":"The same population, three answers, and no line converts any of them into rupees in the plan.","caption":"What the free tier costs, according to three documents in one repo."},"stakes":"A free tier whose real cost is unmeasured is a free tier that can consume the only person building the product.","state":["Exhibit 16 row one reads Individual, free, no limits, F1-F8, own key (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:287).","The plan budgets support at about 90 founder-hours a month at 10,000 users (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:137).","The free tier has no service commitment, stated on the page (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:537).","Nine rows below the tier table an upsell moment names a free quota that no-limits says does not exist (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:444)."],"path":["Free-forever is the distribution strategy, and the category evidence supports it: the editor is worth nothing in this market (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:161).","Obsidian funds eight people from add-ons on a free app with no sign-up, which is the shape the plan copied.","Round 26 modelled the same population and got a different founder-hour figure with a shown derivation (r26-c6:62).","Round 19 estimated a third number for onboarding friction on the bring-your-own-key path and tagged it as inference."],"tension":["Founder time is five times the entire infrastructure bill at 10,000 users, and the profit line is worse there than at 100 (r26-c6:62).","The support coefficient is stated as 0.10 and as 0.30 in the same repo, a threefold spread the report says would move its verdict (r26-c6:50).","Editorially closed in 2014 saying that even full conversion of its users would not have covered the team.","The free tier cannot be both no limits and subject to a quota."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"Three founder-hour figures for the same free tier","items":[["Plan, §7 cost rules","about 90 founder-hours/month at 10,000 users","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:137 - no rupee figure, no free/paid split"],["r26-c6, modelled","76.8 founder-hours/month at 10,000 users (400 paid) = Rs130,560","r26-c6:62, at Rs1,700/h; founder time is 5.0x total cloud+AI (r26-c6:66)"],["r19-p1, BYO-key support only","300 founder-hours across 10,000 signups","r19-p1:63 - cumulative onboarding, tagged [inference], not a monthly rate"],["Support coefficient underlying all of it","stated as 0.10 and 0.30 tickets/paid-user/month in the same repo","r26-c6:50 - a 3x spread that moves Rs299 from FATAL to SEVERE"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"What a free user costs, per r26-c6","items":[["Median free user, total","Rs7.87/month","r26-c6:115; 86% of it is founder time"],["Founder time at 10,000 free users","Rs68,000/month","r26-c6:117, at Rs1,700/h"],["Total cloud + AI at 10,000 users","Rs25,930/month","r26-c6:62"],["Hosted inference on free","Rs0.00","BYO-key only, zero by construction (r26-c6:114)"],["Plan's own infra figure","about $0 at 100 users, about $390/month at 10,000","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:137"]]},{"type":"table","title":"The contradiction inside Exhibit 16 and Exhibit 25","cols":["Line","Text","Implication"],"rows":[["PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:287","\"Free, no limits\"","no quota exists"],["PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:444","\"asks for more than their free quota allows\"","a quota exists"],["PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:537","\"the free tier has no service commitment\"","support is disclaimed but the hours are still spent"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","what":"Free stays uncapped, the contradictory quota line goes, and one founder-hour figure is adopted and priced in rupees.","label":"Keep free uncapped; adopt one number and price it on the page it appears","gains":["Keeps the distribution story intact","Forces three estimates into one number a reader can argue with","Costs one deletion and one line"],"costs":["Deflection through docs and precise error text is unbuilt and unestimated","Commits to absorbing a cost whose input is uncertain threefold"],"system":"No change.","screens":"Delete the free-quota line from the upsell exhibit.","money":"₹1,30,560 a month of founder time at 10,000 users, stated rather than implied."},{"k":"b","what":"Free with a stated soft cap on whatever actually drives support, such as repo size or vault count, never on features.","label":"Free with a soft cap on the support driver, never on features","gains":["Bounds the worst case without crippling the product","Keeps every feature free"],"costs":["Any cap makes no limits untrue","The cap needs a number nobody has measured"],"system":"One counter and one threshold.","screens":"A cap notice that has to read as generous, not punitive.","money":"Caps the tail. Costs nothing directly."},{"k":"c","what":"Free for individuals, with an unenforced commercial-use licence asked for above a named seat count.","label":"Free for individuals, licence asked for above a seat count","gains":["The only B2B motion the corpus says two people can run","Composes with PR2 and PR8"],"costs":["Voluntary, so revenue is unpredictable","Obsidian tried the mandatory version and gave it up"],"system":"No enforcement code by definition.","screens":"A licence page and a supporters wall.","money":"Unpredictable, and it is the only measured B2B mechanism in the category."},{"k":"d","what":"Ship to the ten pilot users, count tickets for sixty days, and decide the cap afterwards.","label":"Measure the support coefficient before deciding","gains":["It is the one input r26-c6 says would change its own verdict","The pilot is happening anyway"],"costs":["Ten users will not resolve a threefold spread","Defers the page copy past the meeting"],"system":"A local, opt-in ticket count.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["The plan and the corpus agree that support, not compute, is the cost structure, and disagree by a factor of four on how much.","Uncapped is right for a product whose distribution is the free editor, but the number has to be published in rupees and someone has to say what absorbs it.","r26-c6's ₹1,30,560 is the figure with a shown derivation, so use it and mark the plan's ninety hours as superseded.","Delete the free-quota line in the same edit; it contradicts the tier table nine rows above it."],"flip":"If the ten pilot users generate more than the 0.02 tickets per free user per month the model assumes, put a soft cap in before the public launch.","linked":["B6","PR10","PR17","PR8"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:137","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:161","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:287","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:444","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:537","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r26-c6-unit-economics.md:50","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r26-c6-unit-economics.md:62","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r19-p1-ai-economics.md:26","http://stet.editorially.com/articles/goodbye/"]},{"id":"PR8","cat":"Pricing & tiers","sub":"Commercial licence","weight":"high","q":"Do we ship an optional commercial licence alongside seats, or keep the plan's dismissal of it?","lede":"Obsidian made the only measured B2B licence in this category optional because it could not enforce it, and kept growing anyway.","visual":{"kind":"ba","before":{"title":"Obsidian licence, 2020 to Feb 2025","lines":[{"t":"Mandatory for commercial use","mark":"ok"},{"t":"$50 per user per year","mark":"ok"},{"t":"No functional benefit attached","mark":"warn"},{"t":"Unenforceable: local app, no sign-up","mark":"x"}]},"after":{"title":"From 2025-02-20","lines":[{"t":"Optional. A supporter payment","mark":"ok"},{"t":"Over 10,000 organisations, on their own page","mark":"ok"},{"t":"Money comes from Sync and Publish","mark":"ok"},{"t":"Eight staff, no investors","mark":"ok"}]},"via":"made optional, unenforceable","note":"The vendor with the largest measured base in the category stopped requiring it and did not shrink.","caption":"What happened to the only B2B licence anyone in this category has run."},"stakes":"This is the only B2B revenue mechanism in the category anybody has actually measured, and the plan dismisses it in one sentence.","state":["The plan dismisses it in a single line: no functional benefit, optional since February 2025, bought by 25-plus seat organisations (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:161).","No licence appears anywhere in the tier table (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:285).","r26-c6 calls the current pricing the largest recoverable error in the plan and prescribes $50 per user per year at Obsidian's exact unit (r26-c6:220).","r26-c8 refutes the transfer: the licence was mandatory for five years, so the wall of logos is the residue of that period (r26-c8:21)."],"path":["v15 narrowed the buyer to small teams on a working tree with no pull request, so a 25-seat licence was read as the wrong buyer.","Two reports from the same round reached opposite conclusions and the plan sided with one without saying it was contested.","The two agents could not reproduce each other's count of the licence wall: 146 named organisations one day, 84 the next (r26-c8:39).","Obsidian's own page for the change says over 10,000 organisations use it, which makes the wall a poor proxy for anything."],"tension":["A licence confers no features, so it costs nothing to ship, and it is the shape PR2's answer turns Pro into anyway.","The precedent had five mandatory years behind it. We would be starting at the voluntary end with no users.","Obsidian's founder says on record the money comes from Sync and Publish, not the licence (r26-c8:21).","Voluntary revenue is unpredictable, and the plan needs a number it can put in a script."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"The two readings, and the number neither could reproduce","cols":["Report","Recommendation","Key figure","Read on"],"rows":[["r26-c6 unit economics","Ship $50/user/year at Obsidian's exact unit","Flat licence is 59.6x under at 50 people, 119.3x at 100","2026-08-31"],["r26-c8 B2B","Do not copy it; the precedent does not transfer","Mandatory until Feb 2025; made optional because unenforceable","2026-08-31"],["r21-s5","Ship the licence motion first","146 named orgs, 17,725 licences, $886,250/yr floor","2026-08-30"],["r26-c8 recount","-","84 named orgs, 16,175 licences, $808,750/yr floor; Amazon 61.8%","2026-08-31"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"What the licence would need to be worth","items":[["Monthly nut","about Rs1.09L","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:292"],["Licences at $50/user/yr to cover it at USD/INR 95.39","274 user-years","derived: 1,08,918 x 12 / (50 x 95.39) = 274.1"],["Named orgs holding 500+ licences on the largest wall","5 of 84 (6.0%)","r26-c8:29-31, measured 2026-08-31"],["Median named logo on that wall","$1,250/yr; 11 such logos is our survival year","r26-c8:165, derived"],["Deal size a $50 unit can reach","$25,000 ACV needs 500 licences at one company","derived from the same tier table"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","what":"An optional commercial licence at Obsidian's unit, sold alongside seats, with a supporters wall.","label":"Ship an optional commercial licence alongside seats","gains":["Costs no features: no SSO, no SCIM, no audit log, no SOC 2 behind it","Composes with PR2, which makes the seat price honour-system regardless","The only B2B motion two people can run"],"costs":["Voluntary revenue on a product with no users may earn nothing for years","The precedent had five mandatory years we will not have"],"system":"A payment link and a name on a page. No entitlement code.","screens":"A licence page and a supporters wall.","money":"Unpredictable upside at no build cost."},{"k":"b","what":"No licence at all; teams buy seats and nothing else is offered.","label":"No licence; teams buy seats only","gains":["One SKU and one story","Nothing extra to explain at checkout"],"costs":["Forgoes the only B2B revenue mechanism anyone in the category has measured"],"system":"No change.","screens":"No change.","money":"Seat revenue only."},{"k":"c","what":"The licence replaces seats entirely: the team motion is one licence and one invoice.","label":"Licence instead of seats","gains":["Removes seat accounting, proration and enforcement, which PR2 says cannot work anyway","One number to quote a procurement team"],"costs":["Caps revenue per logo and gives up seat expansion permanently","r25-w4:61 names the flat licence as disabling the main growth engine"],"system":"No seat model at all.","screens":"No invite-and-count flow.","money":"Predictable per logo, capped per logo."},{"k":"d","what":"Re-count the Obsidian licence wall, then decide alongside the twenty conversations.","label":"Re-count the wall first, decide after the conversations","gains":["One hour settles which of two reports is right before a strategy is built on it"],"costs":["Delays the decision past the meeting","The wall was never the measure: the vendor's own page says over 10,000 organisations"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["The re-count objection has been overtaken. Obsidian's own page for the change names over 10,000 organisations, so a disputed wall of 84 or 146 logos was never the measure.","What the precedent actually shows is that the licence is not load-bearing revenue for them, and that it costs nothing to offer.","PR2 turns the Pro price into a licence in effect. Naming one explicitly costs a page and no code.","Do not build a strategy on it, and do not put it in the revenue model."],"flip":"If a team in the twenty conversations asks how to pay for commercial use and then asks what it enforces, the honest answer is (b) plus a real entitlement.","linked":["PR2","PR21","PR3","PR7"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:161","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:285","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:292","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r26-c6-unit-economics.md:220","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r26-c8-b2b.md:21","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r26-c8-b2b.md:39","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r25-w4-retention-and-growth.md:61","https://obsidian.md/blog/free-for-work/"]},{"id":"PR10","cat":"Pricing & tiers","sub":"Hosted AI","weight":"high","q":"What unit does hosted AI meter in, and where is the ceiling in dollars?","lede":"Hosted AI is priced at cost plus margin over model costs that three reports in the same week disagree about having read.","visual":{"kind":"flow","perRow":3,"nodes":[{"label":"User's own key","note":"Free, uncapped, the MVP-0 default","tone":"good"},{"label":"Hosted, cheap lane","note":"Unmetered up to the daily ceiling","tone":"accent"},{"label":"Daily dollar breaker","note":"Server-side, checked before the vendor call","tone":"accent"},{"label":"Frontier lane","note":"Metered in actions, shown as a count","tone":"neutral"},{"label":"Ceiling reached","note":"Refuse and say so; never bill through","tone":"stop"}],"note":"One call a minute for 24 hours is $1,254 a month on the cheap model alone.","caption":"Where the ceiling has to sit for the abuse case to be bounded at all."},"stakes":"A price with no unit and no cap is not a price, and the abuse case is unbounded until the breaker exists.","state":["The tier table's last row reads hosted AI, metered at cost plus margin, optional, off by default (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:290).","The word capped appears three times in the plan and no cap number appears anywhere (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:133, docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:202, docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:444).","No unit is specified. r19-p4 works through tokens, actions, weighted credits and dollars and recommends actions with a server-side daily dollar breaker (r19-p4:82).","One UI call a minute for 24 hours is $1,254 a month on the cheap model and $2,507 on the frontier one (r26-c6:124)."],"path":["AI is bring-your-own-key in MVP-0 by design, so hosted AI was never specified beyond the phrase.","It was added to MVP-1 as an optional add-on and inherited the cost-plus-margin wording from an earlier plan.","r19-p1 attempted all eight vendor pricing pages on 2026-08-31 and got JS shells or 403s on every one, declaring zero fetched prices (r19-p1:26).","Two other documents cite fetched prices for the same pages in the same week (docs/BUSINESS.md:719)."],"tension":["A margin over an input the record cannot agree it read is not a margin.","The abuse case lives in the lane nobody meters: the cheap surface called on a timer.","Metering in tokens is honest and illegible; metering in dollars publishes our unit cost and invites comparison with the raw API.","Describing the cheap lane as free rather than as unmetered up to a ceiling is the difference between a bounded and an unbounded liability."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"The abuse ceiling against a seat price","items":[["1 call / 60s, 24h, Haiku 4.5","$1,254/month","r26-c6:124, derived from p90 restructure cost"],["Same pattern on Sonnet 5","$2,507/month","same"],["Against a Rs599 subscription grossing $6.28","199x gross revenue","r26-c6:129, the corpus's own comparison"],["Against a $5 seat","about 251x gross","derived from the same figure; the corpus does not state this one"],["Control that stops it","server-side daily dollar breaker, checked before dispatch","r19-p4:76 and :82; rate limits and concurrency-1 do not"]]},{"type":"table","title":"Whether the record has read a model price","cols":["Claim","Date","What it says"],"rows":[["r19-p1:13-28, eight vendor pages","2026-08-31","anthropic.com/pricing and docs.claude.com pricing both HTTP 200 JS-shell; OpenAI 403; \"zero [fetched] prices\"; every model price tagged [SS]"],["r19-p4:19","2026-08-31","\"Haiku 4.5 rates - $1/MTok in, $5/MTok out [fetched, anthropic.com/pricing, 2026-08-31]\""],["BUSINESS.md:719","2026-08-30","\"Claude Sonnet 5 is $2/MTok input and $10/MTok output ... [fetched, docs.claude.com pricing, read 2026-08-30]\""],["Net effect","-","every downstream cost number rests on which of these is true, and nobody has reconciled them"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","what":"Actions as the unit, the cheap surface unmetered up to a server-side daily dollar breaker, only the frontier lane metered.","label":"Actions, with a server-side daily dollar breaker","gains":["Legible to the user and bounded for us","r19-p4 has already done the design work","Survives a tokenizer change without repricing"],"costs":["Needs a proxy, a ledger and a breaker, none of which any exhibit estimates","Actions have to be defined and then defended"],"system":"A metering proxy, a per-account ledger, and a breaker checked before every vendor call.","screens":"A usage line in settings and a refusal state when the ceiling is hit.","money":"Bounded downside per account per day. Margin over a re-dated input."},{"k":"b","what":"Meter in dollars spent and show a running float.","label":"Dollars spent, shown as a running float","gains":["Impossible to mis-price","No repricing when a model or tokenizer changes"],"costs":["Publishes our unit cost","Invites the user to compare against the raw API and leave"],"system":"A ledger and a breaker. No action taxonomy.","screens":"A live spend readout.","money":"Thin margin, fully visible."},{"k":"c","what":"No hosted AI at any tier; bring-your-own-key stays the only path.","label":"No hosted AI; bring your own key forever","gains":["Zero inference cost and zero abuse surface","Matches what MVP-0 already ships"],"costs":["Loses the first run for anyone who has never held an API key","r19-p1 names that friction as the cost of key-only"],"system":"Nothing to build.","screens":"The key field, already planned.","money":"No AI revenue, no AI cost."},{"k":"d","what":"Keep the cost-plus-margin wording and specify it when MVP-1 arrives.","label":"Keep the wording, specify at MVP-1","gains":["No work now"],"costs":["Leaves an unbounded liability described as capped","A price with no unit and no ceiling cannot go on a page"],"system":"No change.","screens":"No change.","money":"Unbounded in the worst case."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["Actions plus an unmetered cheap surface is the only shape that stays legible while staying bounded, and the design already exists in the record.","The wording is load-bearing: unmetered up to a daily ceiling, never free. That one phrase is the whole liability.","Before any price is published on top of a model cost, one person opens the vendor pages in a browser and re-dates the table.","The record currently contains both zero fetched prices and two fetched prices for the same pages in the same week."],"flip":"If the pilot shows nobody without a key ever reaches the AI panel, (c) is cheaper and the whole surface goes away.","linked":["PR21","PR3","PR7"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:133","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:202","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:290","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:444","docs/BUSINESS.md:719","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r19-p4-credits-and-limits.md:82","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r19-p1-ai-economics.md:26","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r26-c6-unit-economics.md:124"]},{"id":"PR11","cat":"Pricing & tiers","sub":"Billing period","weight":"high","q":"Do we default to monthly or to annual, and which half of BUSINESS.md do we keep?","lede":"BUSINESS.md tells us to default to annual on one page and to monthly on another, and the fee gap between them is 466 basis points.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":200,"cols":[{"title":"Monthly, ₹299","tone":"accent"},{"title":"Annual, ₹2,499","tone":"neutral"}],"rows":[{"label":"All-in payment cost","cells":["9.29% of gross","4.63% of gross"]},{"label":"Renewal events a year","cells":["Twelve","One"]},{"label":"Retries on a failed debit","cells":["One attempt, no ladder","One attempt, no ladder"]},{"label":"Surprise-charge risk","cells":["Low: the amount is small","High: bank SMS, one attempt, ₹2,499"]},{"label":"UK withdrawal windows","cells":["One, at purchase","A fresh fourteen days each renewal"]}],"note":"The annual plan is a 466-basis-point fee reduction, not a retention device.","caption":"What the billing period costs on the rail we actually run on."},"stakes":"A build team reading the two halves of BUSINESS.md will implement whichever it opens first.","state":["The plan states a per-user-per-month price and says nothing about billing period (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:288).","BUSINESS.md §82.3 says default Indian customers to annual and price it that way (docs/BUSINESS.md:229).","BUSINESS.md §84.2's drafted pricing page defaults the toggle to monthly and shows the saving in rupees (docs/BUSINESS.md:455).","All-in cost is 9.29% of gross on a ₹299 monthly charge against 4.63% on a ₹2,499 annual one (docs/BUSINESS.md:723)."],"path":["The period was never decided in the plan because the tier table was written as a comparison against list prices, not as a checkout.","BUSINESS.md reasoned it out twice, in two sections written for different purposes, and neither cites the other.","The RBI e-mandate work in round 17 established the one-attempt constraint on the Indian rail (docs/BUSINESS.md:203).","The UK withdrawal finding came later and cuts the other way on annual (docs/BUSINESS.md:543)."],"tension":["The fee arithmetic favours annual outright, by 466 basis points on every customer who takes it.","The rail favours fewer renewal events, because the bank sends a pre-debit notice and there is one attempt with no retry ladder.","Against both: on a one-attempt rail a surprising ₹2,499 charge is a declined card, not a support ticket.","In the UK an annual subscription gets a fresh fourteen-day withdrawal window at every renewal."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"What the Indian rail and the fee schedule do to each period","cols":["Constraint","Monthly","Annual"],"rows":[["Renewal events per year","12","1"],["Debit attempts per event","1, no retry","1, no retry"],["Bank pre-debit notification","12 chances to cancel","1"],["All-in payment cost (Rs299 vs Rs2,499, Dodo)","9.29% of gross","4.63% of gross - a 466 bps saving"],["Failure concentration","spread","one lumpy anniversary at the least persuadable moment"],["UK withdrawal windows","1 at purchase","1 at purchase, plus a fresh 14 days at each renewal"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"Numbers the period decision must clear","items":[["AFA-free per-transaction ceiling","Rs15,000","RBI/2022-23/73, CO.DPSS.POLC.No.S-518/02.14.003/2022-23, 16 June 2022 [fetched, BUSINESS.md:593]; §82.3's own recitation of the same circular is tagged [SS] at line 209"],["A $5 annual seat at USD/INR 95.39","Rs5,723","derived - clears the ceiling with 2.6x headroom"],["Grace after a failed debit","14 days, one reminder, not a sequence","BUSINESS.md:231 and :614 - matched to the statutory withdrawal window; there is no dunning ladder to build"],["Annual plans vs monthly, churn per unit time","about 40-60% lower","BUSINESS.md:184, tagged [SS] - Profitwell/Paddle, not opened"],["Involuntary churn floor for our ARPC band","about 1.30%","Recurly $10-25 ARPC band (r25-w4:33); our ARPC sits below Recurly's lowest band, so this is a floor, not an estimate"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","what":"Monthly is the default, annual is offered and priced, and the saving is shown as an absolute amount.","label":"Monthly default, annual offered and priced","gains":["Lowest checkout-failure rate on the rail we run on","No surprise charge on a one-attempt debit","Churn signal arrives twelve times faster"],"costs":["Concedes 466 basis points on everyone who does not choose annual","Twelve chances a year for an involuntary lapse"],"system":"Two SKUs and a proration path.","screens":"A period toggle above the tier columns, defaulting to monthly.","money":"9.29% of gross to the rail on the monthly mix."},{"k":"b","what":"Annual is the default with a monthly option, as §82.3 recommends.","label":"Annual default, monthly available","gains":["Captures the fee saving by default","Raises cash earlier and cuts involuntary churn"],"costs":["A surprised customer on a one-attempt rail is a declined card","The anniversary becomes one high-variance churn event"],"system":"Same two SKUs, different default.","screens":"Toggle defaults to annual, with the monthly price visible.","money":"4.63% of gross to the rail. Better cash position."},{"k":"c","what":"Annual only, one price and one renewal a year.","label":"Annual only","gains":["Simplest ledger and the best fee arithmetic","One renewal event to design well"],"costs":["Excludes anyone who will not commit a year to a product with no track record","That is everyone in the first cohort"],"system":"One SKU.","screens":"No toggle.","money":"Best rail economics, smallest addressable set."},{"k":"d","what":"Monthly only until twenty teams are paying, then revisit.","label":"Monthly only until twenty teams pay","gains":["Nothing to build and the fastest churn signal"],"costs":["Forgoes the fee saving and the retention benefit for the whole first year"],"system":"One SKU.","screens":"No toggle.","money":"9.29% of gross throughout."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["Offering annual captures most of the 466 basis points from the people who want it. Defaulting to it puts a surprise ₹2,499 on a rail that gets one attempt.","Publish the period in the tier table in the same edit, so the $4-5 band stops being ambiguous.","BUSINESS.md has to stop saying both. §82.3 and §84.2 contradict each other and a build team will implement whichever it reads first.","Take this with PR12: currency and period are the same checkout decision."],"flip":"If the measured annual mix is low enough that the fee saving is going unclaimed, or involuntary monthly churn runs above the corpus floor, switch the default.","linked":["PR12","PR13","PR16","PR3"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:288","docs/BUSINESS.md:203","docs/BUSINESS.md:229","docs/BUSINESS.md:455","docs/BUSINESS.md:543","docs/BUSINESS.md:719","docs/BUSINESS.md:723"]},{"id":"PR12","cat":"Pricing & tiers","sub":"Currency","weight":"high","q":"One USD price worldwide, or a published India price and PPP bands?","lede":"The plan quotes dollars for the price and rupees for the nut, and has no stated geo policy at all.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":200,"cols":[{"title":"Obsidian","tone":"neutral"},{"title":"Craft","tone":"neutral"},{"title":"frontmatter today","tone":"accent"}],"rows":[{"label":"Served to an Indian IP","cells":["USD only, no rupee string","₹526.70 a month","Not decided"]},{"label":"Geo-prices to India","cells":["No","Yes, upward","No policy written"]},{"label":"The withdrawn ₹299 against it","cells":["Below it","Well below it","Withdrawn in v15"]},{"label":"EU signal","cells":["n/a","n/a","USD and INR only is part of the Art 3(2)(a) argument"]}],"note":"The two live comparables measured from an Indian IP do opposite things, and both charge more than our band.","caption":"What Indian buyers are actually charged by the nearest comparables."},"stakes":"A rupee price on a global page reads as domestic-market software, and a screenshot of two prices is an argument we cannot win in public.","state":["Pro is quoted in USD (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:288) and the monthly nut in rupees (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:292).","Nothing in the pricing section says whether an Indian or a European buyer sees a different number.","§22 makes currency part of a legal argument: price in USD and INR only, do not localise into an EU language (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:550).","BUSINESS.md permits geographic PPP tiers only when disclosed and uniform within a country (docs/BUSINESS.md:409)."],"path":["Earlier versions priced in rupees at ₹299 and ₹599 and were corrected after round 25 showed Indian companies selling globally quote dollars.","That correction changed the currency and never addressed geo-pricing.","Round 26 measured both live comparables from an Indian IP and found they do opposite things (r26-c7:24).","The same round concluded ₹299 sat below Indian willingness to pay rather than being a concession to it."],"tension":["Obsidian serves no rupee string at all, so Indians pay the full dollar price for sync and evidently do.","Craft serves an Indian IP ₹526.70 a month, which is above our proposed band, not below it.","The same §22 row concedes that Art 3(2)(b) monitoring is a separate trigger and an Art 27 representative is due from the first EU seat.","That representative costs €420-852 a year, which is 3.6% to 7.2% of annual burn (r26-c8:70)."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"What comparables serve to an Indian IP, read 2026-08-31","cols":["Product","Shown to an Indian IP","Geo-priced"],"rows":[["Obsidian Sync","$4 / $5, zero rupee strings on the page","no"],["Craft Plus","Rs526.70/mo annual, Rs658.30 monthly","yes, automatically"],["Superhuman (at coda.io)","Rs1,250/mo Basic Pro","yes"],["Postman (founded Bengaluru)","USD - $9 / $19 / $49","no"],["BrowserStack, Chargebee","USD","no - Indian companies selling globally quote USD"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"Where a $4-5 seat lands against those","items":[["$5 at USD/INR 95.39","Rs476.95","derived, ECB rate date 2026-08-28"],["Craft Plus, India","Rs526.70","frontmatter Pro is 0.91x of it"],["Superhuman, India","Rs1,250","frontmatter Pro is 0.38x of it"],["EU representative, if we sell into the EU","EUR420-852/yr = Rs46,645-94,622","fetched prighter.com/pricing 2026-08-31 (r26-c8:70)"],["Corpus rule on wealth-signal pricing","never by device, IP-to-income or browser; geographic PPP tiers only if disclosed and uniform within a country","BUSINESS.md:409"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","what":"One USD price for everyone, everywhere, with no geographic variation.","label":"One USD price worldwide, no geo-pricing","gains":["One number to publish, defend and change","No screenshot argument on Hacker News","The category leader does exactly this"],"costs":["Indian buyers pay the full dollar price","Gives up whatever the home market would have converted at a lower number"],"system":"One SKU per period.","screens":"One pricing page.","money":"Highest revenue per Indian customer who converts, fewest who do."},{"k":"b","what":"A USD list price plus a published, disclosed India price.","label":"USD list plus a published India price","gains":["Meets the home market where the founder's network already is","Disclosed, so it is a policy rather than a test"],"costs":["A rupee price on a global page reads as domestic-market software","The corpus says ₹299 undercut Indian willingness to pay rather than meeting it"],"system":"Two price books and one currency decision at checkout.","screens":"A country selector, and the argument that comes with it.","money":"Lower per Indian customer, possibly more of them."},{"k":"c","what":"A USD list price plus published purchasing-power bands for a named set of countries.","label":"USD list plus published PPP bands","gains":["Standard practice and defensible when disclosed and uniform within a country"],"costs":["A policy, a table and an abuse surface, for a product with no customers","Every band is a number somebody will argue with"],"system":"A country-to-band table and VPN abuse handling.","screens":"A banded pricing page.","money":"More conversions, lower average, more support."},{"k":"d","what":"Quote USD only until the twenty conversations, then decide.","label":"USD only until the conversations return","gains":["No work now and no wrong answer published"],"costs":["Leaves the pricing page unfinished if a checkout ships early"],"system":"No change.","screens":"No pricing page.","money":"None."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["The one measured fact is that the category leader does not geo-price and Indians pay its full dollar rate anyway.","The two products that do geo-price to India charge more than our proposed price, not less.","A single dollar number is also the only version that cannot be screenshotted into an argument.","It keeps the §22 currency line intact without pretending that line settles the EU question, which it does not."],"flip":"If more than half of the twenty teams are Indian and name the dollar figure specifically as the objection, publish an India price as disclosed policy, never as a test.","linked":["PR11","PR16","PR3"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:288","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:292","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:550","docs/BUSINESS.md:409","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r26-c7-d2c.md:24","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r26-c8-b2b.md:70","https://obsidian.md/pricing"]},{"id":"PR16","cat":"Pricing & tiers","sub":"Merchant of record","weight":"high","q":"Do we sell through a merchant of record from the first sale, or bill direct and register for tax as it arises?","lede":"The plan files this under enterprise features to defer, but it is not a feature — it is whose name is on the invoice.","visual":{"kind":"arch","layers":[{"label":"Customer","items":["Sees an invoice","Disputes to a card network"],"side":"never sees the difference","tone":"neutral"},{"label":"Merchant of record","items":["Sales-tax registration and remittance","Invoice issuance","Card-network relationship","Dispute paperwork"],"side":"4% + 15¢, +0.5% subscription","tone":"accent"},{"label":"Studio Zephyrus","items":["Data-fiduciary duty, never transferred","Statutory rights above the refund floor","The product itself"],"side":"stays ours either way","tone":"sunk"}],"note":"Only the middle layer is optional, and it has to be chosen before the first sale.","caption":"What a merchant of record absorbs, and what stays ours regardless."},"stakes":"The first EU or US sale arrives with a tax obligation, and there is nobody to refuse the feature that would have prevented it.","state":["§22 groups a merchant of record with SSO and SOC 2 under no enterprise feature until a customer refuses to pay without it (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:535).","BUSINESS.md lists what an MoR absorbs and what stays ours regardless, including the data-fiduciary duty it never holds (docs/BUSINESS.md:576).","Dodo charges 4% plus 15¢ on Indian cards and UPI, 4% plus 40¢ US domestic, plus 1.5% international and 0.5% for subscriptions (docs/BUSINESS.md:719).","The fixed-cent component alone is 4.79% of a ₹299 charge at today's rate (docs/BUSINESS.md:723)."],"path":["The refusal list was written to keep enterprise cost out of a two-person plan.","The MoR was grouped with SSO and SOC 2 because all three come up in procurement conversations.","The fee schedules for both candidate rails were fetched on 2026-08-30 and have not been revisited.","The plan's own resources section says the team is one person on the commit record (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:231)."],"tension":["SSO and SOC 2 are features a buyer asks for. A merchant of record is a legal identity on every transaction.","It has to be decided before the first sale, not after the first refusal, so the refusal test cannot apply to it.","The cut is most expensive precisely at the price we intend to charge, because of the fixed-cent component.","The alternative puts cross-border VAT and GST registration and dispute paperwork onto one person."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"Fee exposure on each route, all fetched 2026-08-30","items":[["Dodo Payments, headline rate","4% + 15c India domestic; 4% + 40c US domestic; +1.5% international; +0.5% subscriptions","BUSINESS.md:719"],["Dodo, fixed-cent drag on a small monthly charge","15c is 4.79% of Rs299 at USD/INR 95.39, up from 4.15% at 82.69","BUSINESS.md:723, derived"],["Dodo, dispute","$30 = Rs2,861.70","6.0x a $5 monthly seat, 7.5x a $4 seat"],["Dodo, refund","$1 = Rs95.39","0.2x a $5 seat"],["Stripe India, dispute lost","Rs2,000 plus principal","Rs1,000 if won"]]},{"type":"table","title":"What the merchant of record absorbs, and what does not move","cols":["Absorbed by the MoR","Stays ours"],"rows":[["Sales-tax registration and remittance across jurisdictions","the reason the dispute happened"],["Invoice issuance and the card-network relationship","statutory rights above the MoR's own floor"],["Dispute paperwork and evidence submission","transitioning the workspace state, which only we can do"],["Payment-data controllership","data-fiduciary duty for content under DPDP and GDPR"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","what":"A merchant of record handles every sale from the first one, in every jurisdiction.","label":"Merchant of record from the first sale","gains":["One counterparty handles global sales tax, invoices and disputes for a known cut","No jurisdiction arrives as a surprise","Nothing to build when the first EU seat lands"],"costs":["4% to 5.5% plus a fixed cent charge that is 4.79% of a small monthly seat","Expensive precisely at the price we intend to charge","One more party between us and the customer"],"system":"One integration, one webhook, one reconciliation surface.","screens":"Their checkout, our page.","money":"About 9.29% of gross on a monthly seat, 4.63% on an annual one."},{"k":"b","what":"Bill direct in rupees and dollars, and register for tax in each jurisdiction as it arises.","label":"Bill direct; register for tax as it arises","gains":["Keeps the margin and the direct customer relationship","No third party in the invoice chain"],"costs":["Puts cross-border registration and dispute paperwork onto one person","Every new country is a project","The first mistake is a tax mistake"],"system":"A billing integration plus tax logic we own.","screens":"Our own checkout.","money":"Lower percentage cut, unbounded administrative cost."},{"k":"c","what":"A merchant of record for sales outside India, direct billing inside it.","label":"MoR for non-India sales, direct for India","gains":["Keeps domestic margin and outsources the hard jurisdictions"],"costs":["Two checkouts, two ledgers, two reconciliation surfaces for a two-person team"],"system":"Two billing paths and a routing rule.","screens":"Two checkouts.","money":"Best blended rate, worst operational cost."},{"k":"d","what":"Defer the decision until the first EU or US team asks for it.","label":"Defer until a foreign buyer asks","gains":["No work now"],"costs":["The first EU sale arrives with a VAT obligation and no mechanism","That is exactly the situation the MoR exists to prevent"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"Nothing now, an unbounded obligation later."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["At this volume one dispute or one foreign tax registration costs more than the cut.","The concrete change is to move the MoR out of the no-enterprise-feature-until-refused list, because it is not a feature and there is nobody to refuse it.","The 15¢ fixed component makes a monthly seat the worst case for this fee schedule, which is a second argument for PR11's annual rung.","Revisit only when volume makes the percentage cut exceed the cost of running tax and disputes in-house."],"flip":"If a fetched comparison shows a direct rail plus an outsourced tax service beating the MoR cut at fewer than 200 seats, (b) is cheaper from the start.","linked":["L19","PR11","PR12","PR13","PR4"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:231","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:535","docs/BUSINESS.md:576","docs/BUSINESS.md:580","docs/BUSINESS.md:719","docs/BUSINESS.md:723"]},{"id":"PR17","cat":"Pricing & tiers","sub":"Evidence and kill number","weight":"high","q":"How do we get pricing evidence before MVP-1, and what result kills the paid tier?","lede":"Every other test in the plan carries a kill number. The one that decides whether there is a business does not.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":190,"cols":[{"title":"Randomised price test","tone":"stop"},{"title":"Twenty conversations","tone":"warn"},{"title":"Paid pre-order","tone":"accent"}],"rows":[{"label":"Time to a result","cells":["57 months at plausible traffic","Weeks 1 and 2","Weeks 1 and 2"]},{"label":"What it returns","cells":["An elasticity","Seat counts and opinions","Money, or nothing"]},{"label":"Kill number today","cells":["None; struck from the plan","None written","Zero from 100 qualified"]},{"label":"What it costs","cells":["Traffic we do not have","Hours already budgeted","A checkout and a refund policy"]},{"label":"Prices it can test","cells":["Three","Whatever is in the script","One"]}],"note":"The plan has scheduled the middle column and written the threshold for the right-hand one.","caption":"Three instruments, and the only one carrying a written kill number."},"stakes":"A test with no threshold cannot fail, and a threshold chosen after the answers arrive is not a threshold.","state":["The paid tier is a hypothesis until twenty team conversations return seat counts and what teams are gated on (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:292), scheduled for weeks 1-2 (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:352).","No threshold is written anywhere, while the plan sets kill numbers everywhere else: under 4 of 10 kills review state (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:321), under 200 installs in 14 days killed the plugin channel (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:204).","BUSINESS.md computed that the three-arm price test would take 57 months and must be struck (docs/BUSINESS.md:384).","Its replacement stack was specified and never carried into a plan version (docs/BUSINESS.md:399)."],"path":["An earlier plan said test ₹299 against ₹249 and ₹399, with no sample size, no minimum detectable effect and no stopping rule.","Round 17 computed what that sentence actually costs and struck it.","The conversations were added later, when the seat arithmetic was withdrawn, as the thing that would replace it.","The threshold was never written because the tier itself was still moving."],"tension":["What remains open after round 2 is whether anyone pays for review state in any shell; eleven gaps of desk research measured installs and attention, never payment (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:146).","As scheduled the conversations test only the $4-5 band, so nobody would pay $5 and they would pay more for a gate are indistinguishable outcomes.","The only affordable randomised measurement is free-signup rate, which answers price anchoring and must not be reported as willingness to pay.","Twenty conversations return opinions. A pre-order returns money. The plan currently has neither with a threshold."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"Power analysis at the plan's own funnel, from BUSINESS.md §83.2-83.3","cols":["Test","n per arm","Months at 5,000 visitors/mo","Viable"],"rows":[["Paid conversion, 20% lift, 3 arms","95,455","57","no"],["Paid conversion, 50% lift, 3 arms","17,341","10.4","no - 50% is not a real hypothesis"],["Revenue per visitor, 10% difference","347,000","208","no"],["Free-signup rate, 15% drop, 2 arms","6,570","2.6","marginal, and answers a different question"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"The inputs those numbers rest on","items":[["Visitor to free signup","9.0%","plan funnel assumption (BUSINESS.md:345)"],["Free to paid","5.0%","developer median, settled in the record"],["Baseline paid conversion per visitor","0.45%","derived: 0.09 x 0.05"],["Realistic month-6 traffic, solo founder, no paid acquisition","3,000-8,000 visitors/month","[inference] in BUSINESS.md:345, not measured"],["Traffic that makes the 20% test worth revisiting","about 40,000 visitors/month sustained","BUSINESS.md:386 - drops the three-arm test to 7.2 months"]]},{"type":"table","title":"Kill numbers the plan does write, and the one it does not","cols":["Test","Kill number","Where"],"rows":[["Review state as the product","under 4 of 10 unprompted","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:321"],["MVP-0 exit","under 6 of 10 strangers still using it after two weeks","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:206"],["Obsidian plugin channel","under 200 installs in 14 days","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:204"],["Pre-order page, if PR4 goes that way","zero pre-orders from 100 qualified conversations","r26-c7:125"],["Paid tier / 20 team conversations","none written","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:292"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"What the conversations have to establish","items":[["Seat counts per team","unmeasured","the input to every revenue number in §11"],["What teams are gated on","unmeasured","the input to PR1's tier contents"],["Whether anyone pays for review state in any shell","still open after two adversarial rounds","GAPS-2026-09-08.md:146"],["Willingness-to-pay work anywhere in the programme","0 instances across 105 reports and 374,866 words","r26-c7:22, measured"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","what":"Kill at fewer than five of twenty naming a gate they would pay for at a named price, with both prices in the script and the willingness-to-pay questions folded in.","label":"Kill under 5 of 20 naming a gate at a named price; both prices in the script","gains":["Falsifiable, and it tests the axis as well as the level","One protocol answers the price question and the kill question","Costs a week of conversations already scheduled"],"costs":["Twenty is a small sample and the signal is soft","Opinions, not money","The interview method over-reports acceptable prices"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None spent. The answer arrives in week 2."},{"k":"b","what":"Kill at fewer than three of twenty giving both a seat count and a budget line.","label":"Kill under 3 of 20 giving a seat count and a budget line","gains":["A harder bar that filters talk from procurement reality"],"costs":["Three of twenty is a thin thread to hang a tier on","A 15% hit rate is inside sampling noise at n=20"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","what":"Replace the conversations with a paid pre-order carrying the kill number already written in the record.","label":"Replace the conversations with a paid pre-order","gains":["The only instrument that returns a fact instead of an opinion","The kill number is already written and dated"],"costs":["Needs a checkout and a refund policy before the product exists","A public failure","Tests one price, not the axis"],"system":"A checkout and a refunds path.","screens":"One page.","money":"$49 a pre-order, refundable."},{"k":"d","what":"Run the free-signup-rate test only, and label it price anchoring rather than willingness to pay.","label":"Free-signup-rate test only, labelled price anchoring","gains":["The one randomised measurement that fits the traffic"],"costs":["It answers whether the price suppresses signup, not what anyone pays","2.6 months is most of the pre-launch window"],"system":"Two landing variants and a counter.","screens":"Two pricing pages.","money":"None, and no revenue evidence either."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["Write the number before the conversations start. Five of twenty naming a gate at a named price is high enough that a polite yes does not count and low enough that a real niche survives.","Put both PR3 prices in the script, so a rejection of $5 is distinguishable from a rejection of paying at all.","Fold the willingness-to-pay questions into the same conversations rather than running a second instrument; one protocol, one owner.","Label every output honestly: an interview brackets an acceptable band and over-reports, and no number from it may be reported as an elasticity."],"flip":"If PR4 goes to a pre-order page, (c) supersedes this gate entirely, because one card beats twenty opinions.","linked":["G15","PL7","PR20","PR3","PR4","PR7"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:204","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:292","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:321","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:352","docs/BUSINESS.md:384","docs/BUSINESS.md:399","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:146","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r26-c7-d2c.md:22","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r26-c7-d2c.md:125","merged: PR18"],"dupes":{"dropped":["R16"],"why":"Does a price go into the weeks-1-2 conversations and what result kills the paid tier. Both rec (a) — a price question in the script with a stated kill. Pricing & tiers owns whether there is a paid tier at all."}},{"id":"PR20","cat":"Pricing & tiers","sub":"Services line","weight":"high","q":"Do we sell the engagement as the first revenue line, at ten days or at eight?","lede":"The plan funds the build with consulting hours and lists the same engagement as its last upsell, without noticing they are one line.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":200,"cols":[{"title":"Ten days, ₹3,00,000","tone":"warn"},{"title":"Eight days, ₹2,40,000","tone":"accent"}],"rows":[{"label":"Sellable this month","cells":["Not without the kappa","Yes"]},{"label":"What days 7-8 sell","cells":["Eval discipline: kappa 0.1 against a 0.7 bar, n=9","Withheld until the kappa is honest"]},{"label":"Four a year","cells":["₹12,00,000, exactly the monthly nut","4 x ₹2,40,000 = ₹9,60,000"]},{"label":"Line item on the rate card","cells":["Absent","Absent"]},{"label":"Against the product funnel","cells":["One client equals 63,060 visitors","Same"]}],"note":"The engagement and the funding line are the same money, counted once.","caption":"The first revenue line, priced two ways, against what it can be defended on today."},"stakes":"The one revenue line available this month is priced on a discipline whose own measurement failed its own bar.","state":["The engagement appears as the bottom row of the upsell table (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:445) and in the family diagram at ₹3,00,000 fixed scope (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:465).","The funding line is stated separately: the monthly nut of about ₹1.09L, covered by 54-78 consulting hours (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:292).","Four engagements a year is ₹12,00,000, which is the same milestone, and one client equals 63,060 visitors of funnel (r23-u4:62).","The report's own shape withholds days 7-8 until the kappa is honest (r23-u4:105)."],"path":["Round 23 designed the engagement; round 22 established that services fund the company.","v15 kept both and connected them only through the narrative about the docs scan as a diagnostic.","The kappa was measured once at 0.1 against a bar of 0.7, n=9, and never re-run (r23-u4:10).","The studio's rate card still has no line item for the engagement."],"tension":["The upsell path runs through the docs scan, which is an MVP-0 feature that does not exist for about a year.","So the upsell has no source, while the same engagement could be sold directly this month.","Days 7-8 sell an eval discipline whose own measurement is dark, which is the exact self-flattery the audit exists to prevent.","Founder hours spent on engagements are hours not spent on the 81-week build."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"One engagement against the product funnel","items":[["Four engagements a year","Rs12,00,000 = Rs1,00,000/month","r23-u4:62"],["Product path to the same Rs1L/month","284 paying users, 5,675 free signups, 63,060 cumulative visitors","r23-u4:62, from the record's own conversion rates"],["Founder time for four engagements","360 hours = 16.6% of 2,172 annual engineering hours","r23-u4:62, derived"],["Price at eight days, days 7-8 withheld","Rs2,40,000","r23-u4:99"],["The kappa that gates days 7-8","0.1 against a 0.7 bar, n=9, dark 27 days","r23-u4:10, measured"],["Line item on the studio rate card today","none","r23-u4:105"]]},{"type":"table","title":"The two funding lines the plan carries separately","cols":["Line","Amount","Where"],"rows":[["Monthly nut","about Rs1.09L","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:292"],["Consulting hours to cover it","54-78/month","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:292"],["Productised engagement","Rs3,00,000 fixed scope, listed as an upsell","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:445, :465"],["Four of them a year","Rs12,00,000 = the Rs1L/month milestone","r23-u4:62"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","what":"Sell the ten-day engagement now as the first revenue line, and let the product price wait for MVP-1.","label":"Sell the ten-day engagement at ₹3,00,000 now","gains":["Revenue this month from clients who already exist","Four a year covers the whole monthly nut"],"costs":["Days 7-8 sell a discipline whose kappa is 0.1 against a 0.7 bar","Cannot be quoted from the rate card as it stands","Forty hours a month away from the build"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None; the docs scan becomes the diagnostic later.","money":"₹12,00,000 a year at four engagements."},{"k":"b","what":"Sell an eight-day version now, with the evals named as a later phase.","label":"Sell an eight-day version at ₹2,40,000, evals as phase two","gains":["Sellable this month with nothing outstanding","Eighty per cent of the revenue and none of the objection","It is the shape the report itself proposes"],"costs":["Leaves the highest-value days on the table until the kappa is honest","Still forty hours a month away from the build"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"₹9,60,000 a year at four engagements."},{"k":"c","what":"Keep it as a downstream upsell from the docs scan only, exactly as the plan has it.","label":"Keep it as a downstream upsell from the docs scan","gains":["Keeps the founder's hours on the build"],"costs":["The scan that generates the lead does not exist for about a year","No data exists on conversion from any productised diagnostic"],"system":"No change.","screens":"The scan's proposal list becomes the brief.","money":"None for about a year."},{"k":"d","what":"Do not sell it at all; it competes for the same hours as the product.","label":"Do not sell it; protect the build","gains":["Maximum product velocity"],"costs":["The plan's own funding line already assumes 54-78 client hours a month","So this contradicts the budget it appears in"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"No services revenue, and no funding for the build."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["Eight days at ₹2,40,000 is revenue this month at a scope the record says is defensible today.","It removes the one honest objection to the ten-day version: charging for a discipline whose own measurement is dark.","Add the line item to the rate card in the same week, because the engagement cannot be quoted today even if a client asks.","Move to (a) once the kappa has one dated artefact against a real gold set."],"flip":"If a client asks for the eval days specifically and will pay for them, re-run the kappa first and then sell (a) — never the reverse order.","linked":["PR17","PR4"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:292","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:445","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:465","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r23-u4-consultation-and-services.md:10","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r23-u4-consultation-and-services.md:62","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r23-u4-consultation-and-services.md:105"]},{"id":"PR21","cat":"Pricing & tiers","sub":"Tier ladder","weight":"high","q":"Which tier ladder ships, and does Max survive as a third rung?","lede":"Three committed artefacts name three different ladders, and the most specific one is a rules file that already encodes a billing webhook.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":175,"cols":[{"title":"The plan, v15","tone":"accent"},{"title":"firestore.rules, July","tone":"warn"},{"title":"BUSINESS.md","tone":"warn"}],"rows":[{"label":"Rungs","cells":["Individual / Pro / Max / Hosted AI","free | pro | team","Free / Pro / Power / Work"]},{"label":"Currency","cells":["USD","None","INR"]},{"label":"Encodes billing","cells":["No","Yes: priceId, provider, customerId","No"]},{"label":"Meters usage","cells":["No","Yes: aiTokens, noteCount, bytesUsed","No"]},{"label":"Holds documents","cells":["No","Yes: content up to 900,000 bytes","No"]}],"note":"A build team reading the repo finds the middle column first, because it is the most specific.","caption":"Three committed artefacts, three ladders, and which one describes a shipped design."},"stakes":"Whichever ladder is chosen, two of the three artefacts are wrong today and one of them is a security rules file.","state":["The plan runs Individual, Pro, Max and Hosted AI (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:285 to docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:290).","`firestore.rules:22` documents a server-owned plan enum of free, pro or team, with a billing collection and a usage meter (firestore.rules:29, firestore.rules:34).","BUSINESS.md runs Free, Pro, Power and Work (docs/BUSINESS.md:448).","Max holds retention beyond a year, admin and SSO when asked (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:289), while §22 defers SSO until a customer refuses to pay without it (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:535)."],"path":["The rules file dates from July, for a Firebase-backed product that held documents.","BUSINESS.md was generated on 2026-08-30 from round 17. The plan is 2026-09-08. None supersedes the others in writing.","Max was the home for sync, export and enterprise items before the round-2 inversion moved enforcement and retention forward.","Round 2 named the three-file contradiction and said no operating rule can be written until one of them is deleted (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:142)."],"tension":["The rules file caps note content at 900,000 bytes, which is the document-holding design decision 7 puts to the meeting (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:365).","Max's contents are one feature with no F-row and two the operating rules refuse to build.","Two other exhibits still send CI gates to Max after v15 moved them to Pro (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:202, docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:443).","The upsell table cannot decide whether a second device is a Pro or a Max moment (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:442)."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"Three ladders, three artefacts","cols":["Artefact","Ladder","Dated","Billing implied"],"rows":[["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:285-290","Individual / Pro, team / Max / Hosted AI","2026-09-08","none until MVP-1"],["firestore.rules:22","free | pro | team","file dated 2026-07-25","billing webhook, Admin SDK, usage meter"],["docs/BUSINESS.md:448-451","Free / Pro Rs299 / Power Rs599 / Work Rs3,999 flat","2026-08-30","monthly and annual, INR"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"What the rules file already designs","items":[["plan enum","free | pro | team","client may only ever write 'free'; upgrades via billing webhook (firestore.rules:22-24)"],["billing/{uid}","status, priceId, currentPeriodEnd, provider, customerId","owner-read only, no client writes (firestore.rules:29-32)"],["usage/{uid}/months","aiTokens, noteCount, bytesUsed","\"metered server-side\" (firestore.rules:34-36)"],["Note bodies","content: string, <= 900000 bytes","firestore.rules:61 - the document-holding design decision 7 puts to the meeting"]]},{"type":"table","title":"What the four exhibits say Max contains","cols":["Exhibit","Contents claimed","Line"],"rows":[["16 (§11 pricing)","retention beyond a year, admin, SSO when asked","289"],["6 (§8 tiers, MVP-2)","sync, multi-device, version-history retention, export, document gates in CI","199-203"],["25 (§18 upsell)","CI gates; and \"Pro or Max\" for the second device","442-443"],["22 (operating rules)","SSO is not a feature until a customer refuses to pay without it, at about 20 seats","535"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"Whether Max's contents can be built or priced","items":[["Retention beyond a year","no feature row exists","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:289 says so explicitly"],["Sync (F12)","15d+, MVP-2","\"sync is the one proven individual price\" (PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:66)"],["Export (F13)","already built, never run, 0d + 1h to verify","945 lines wired at EditorPane.tsx:907 (PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:67)"],["SSO / admin","deferred by rule until a customer refuses to pay without it","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:535"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","what":"Two tiers only, free and Pro, with Max deleted until a customer refuses to pay without SSO.","label":"Two tiers: free and Pro. Delete Max until someone asks","gains":["Removes three contradictory descriptions and a rung with no buyer","The reappearance trigger is already written into §22","One vocabulary to fix everywhere else"],"costs":["Gives up the anchoring a top tier gives the middle one","Anything currently parked in Max needs a new home"],"system":"One paid entitlement instead of two.","screens":"A two-column pricing page.","money":"Loses whatever a decoy tier is worth, which nobody here has measured."},{"k":"b","what":"Adopt the code's vocabulary of free, pro and team, and rename Max.","label":"free / pro / team, matching the code","gains":["Least code churn and the names a build team finds first"],"costs":["Loses Max, which the plan also uses as a product-family label","Adopts the vocabulary of a file that may be deleted outright"],"system":"The plan changes; the rules file does not.","screens":"Renamed columns.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","what":"Keep three rungs and fix the stale rows that describe Max differently.","label":"Keep three rungs and fix the stale rows","gains":["Cheapest edit and keeps the ladder intact"],"costs":["Max still holds one feature that does not exist and two the operating rules refuse to build","The incoherence is renamed rather than removed"],"system":"No change.","screens":"A three-column pricing page with a hollow third column.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","what":"Settle decision 7 first, delete the rules file if the Firebase design does not ship, then make the plan the only source.","label":"Settle decision 7 first, then the plan is the only source","gains":["Removes the contradiction at its root","Unblocks §22, which round 2 says cannot be written until one file goes"],"costs":["It is a deletion, so it needs the meeting","It does not by itself answer how many rungs there are"],"system":"Deletes a committed security rules file.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["A third rung whose contents are one unbuilt feature and two the operating rules refuse to build is not a rung.","Three rows describing it differently will confuse a reader before they confuse a buyer.","Do (d) in the same meeting as a prerequisite: do not let a July rules file remain the most specific tier definition in the repository.","Let Max reappear the first time a team refuses to pay without SSO, which is the trigger §22 already sets."],"flip":"If PR8 goes to a commercial licence, the third rung comes back as a per-organisation licence, which needs no features and has a measured precedent.","linked":["E6","PR1","PR2","PR23","PR8"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:202","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:285","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:289","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:290","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:365","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:442","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:443","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:535","docs/BUSINESS.md:448","firestore.rules:22","firestore.rules:29","firestore.rules:34","firestore.rules:61","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:142","merged: PR22"]},{"id":"PR23","cat":"Pricing & tiers","sub":"Unit of sale","weight":"high","q":"Is the CI gate priced per repository or per seat?","lede":"Every comparable that sells a documentation check prices per site or per project. The plan prices it per person.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":200,"cols":[{"title":"Per seat","tone":"neutral"},{"title":"Per repository","tone":"accent"}],"rows":[{"label":"Who buys it","cells":["Every reader on the team","The one person who wants the gate"]},{"label":"What the comparables do","cells":["GitBook: $12 per user per month","Mintlify Pro $450/mo; ReadMe Pro $250/mo"]},{"label":"GitBook charges both","cells":["$12 per user per month","plus $65 per site per month"]},{"label":"Enforceable at all","cells":["Honour system, per PR2","The Action runs or it does not"]},{"label":"Bills readers who never review","cells":["Yes","No"]}],"note":"The plan calls the gate the B2B line but never says what unit it sells in.","caption":"The unit an enforcement gate is bought in, against what the comparables charge."},"stakes":"Enforcement is the one paid object with a natural place to check an entitlement, and pricing it per seat wastes that.","state":["The upsell table routes the CI gate to Max and names the comparable as docs-as-code tooling and CI seats (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:443).","The family table calls `mdmax cert` and gates the B2B line, sold per team (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:475).","v15 then pulled the gate into Pro at $4-5 per user per month (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:288).","No document names the unit. Per team, per seat and per repo all appear."],"path":["The gate started life in Max, where it was priced per team.","Round 2 moved enforcement forward into Pro because enforcement is what GitHub sells at $4.","That move carried the object across without carrying its unit across.","The command itself still does not run: `mdmax cert` was never wired, one day of work (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:224)."],"tension":["A CI check is bought by whoever owns the repository, not by everyone who reads it.","Mintlify, GitBook and ReadMe all price a documentation product per site or per project, with seats as a second axis or none at all.","Per seat bills people who never look at a build. Per repo bills the person who wants the build to fail.","Per repo is also the only unit where an entitlement check has an obvious home, because the Action can ask for one."],"evidence":[],"options":[{"k":"a","what":"The gate stays inside the per-seat Pro price, exactly as v15 has it.","label":"Per seat, folded into Pro as written","gains":["One SKU and one price to explain","No new billing object"],"costs":["Bills readers who never see a CI run","Wastes the one place an entitlement could be checked","No comparable in docs tooling prices a check this way"],"system":"No change.","screens":"No change.","money":"Revenue scales with readers, not with repos."},{"k":"b","what":"The gate is sold per repository, separately from seats, with its own price.","label":"Per repository, sold separately from seats","gains":["Matches how every docs-platform comparable sells a check","The buyer is the repo owner who wants it, not the whole team","The Action is a natural entitlement checkpoint"],"costs":["Two paid objects to explain on one page","Needs a repo-level identity and entitlement, which nothing builds today","A team with many repos may be worse off"],"system":"A repo-scoped entitlement and an Action that asks for it.","screens":"A repos list with a per-repo toggle.","money":"Priced against $250-450 a month comparables rather than $4."},{"k":"c","what":"One flat organisation price covering any number of repositories.","label":"Per organisation, flat, any number of repos","gains":["One number for a procurement conversation","No counting of anything"],"costs":["One number has to fit a two-repo team and a two-hundred-repo one","Gives up expansion entirely"],"system":"An org-scoped entitlement.","screens":"One switch per organisation.","money":"Predictable per logo, capped per logo."},{"k":"d","what":"Do not price the gate until `mdmax cert` runs end to end once.","label":"Do not price it until the command runs","gains":["Refuses to price something that exits with a module error","One day of work settles it"],"costs":["Leaves Pro without the half of its offer that is meant to be enforceable"],"system":"Wire the command; no billing work.","screens":"None.","money":"None until it runs."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["The buyer of a build gate is the person who owns the build, and every comparable that sells one charges per site or per project.","It is also the only paid object in the plan where an entitlement has an obvious place to be checked, which PR2 says nothing else has.","Pricing it per repo lets the seat price stay low and honest while the gate carries a number the docs platforms already justify.","Do (d) first regardless: one day to make the command run, before either unit is published."],"flip":"If the twenty conversations show the same person buys the seats and the gate and wants one invoice, fold it back into (a) and price the seat higher.","linked":["E12","PR1","PR2","PR21","PR3"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:224","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:288","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:443","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:475","https://mintlify.com/pricing"]},{"id":"PR13","cat":"Pricing & tiers","sub":"Refunds and withdrawal","weight":"medium","q":"What refund and withdrawal terms ship at checkout?","lede":"One chargeback costs thirty dollars plus the principal. A refund costs one. The plan has neither policy written.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":210,"cols":[{"title":"Refund on request","tone":"accent"},{"title":"Non-refundable line","tone":"warn"}],"rows":[{"label":"Cost at a 2% refund rate","cells":["About 2.08% of gross","Nil"]},{"label":"Per dispute at Dodo","cells":["$1 per refund, dispute avoided","$30 per dispute, plus the principal"]},{"label":"EU fourteen-day right","cells":["Subsumed; no waiver flow needed","Waiver needed, and getting it wrong makes the supply free"]},{"label":"Fits the rest of the plan","cells":["Yes; the files are theirs either way","No; it contradicts every other trust position"]},{"label":"India e-commerce rules 2020","cells":["Policy must be displayed","Policy must be displayed"]}],"note":"At this price the refund is cheap and the dispute is not.","caption":"Refund posture, and what it does to the EU withdrawal question."},"stakes":"A waiver flow that is slightly wrong makes the supply free by law, and a missing refund policy turns remorse into a chargeback.","state":["The pricing section says nothing about refunds and nothing about withdrawal.","BUSINESS.md carries a complete drafted policy: full refund of a first payment within 30 days, prorated renewal refunds within 90 days, and a same-day refund offered in place of a chargeback (docs/BUSINESS.md:518, docs/BUSINESS.md:644).","It also specifies the three artefacts needed for the EU Art 16(m) waiver and then recommends against using them (docs/BUSINESS.md:552).","Art 14(4)(b) says the consumer bears no cost where any one of the three is missing (docs/BUSINESS.md:542)."],"path":["The refund policy was written in round 17 for a product with hosted sync and published pages.","v15 removed most of that hosted surface and never carried the policy forward.","No plan version since round 17 has carried a checkout at all, so the withdrawal question never came up again.","The dispute-fee figures were fetched on 2026-08-30 for both candidate rails (docs/BUSINESS.md:580)."],"tension":["The benchmark set is bimodal: Obsidian writes non-refundable and relies on statute; 37signals refunds on request and prorates.","One dispute costs six to seven and a half months of a seat at this price, before the principal.","With no free trial there is one withdrawal window per contract, except on UK annual plans where it returns yearly (docs/BUSINESS.md:543).","The 90-day prorated-renewal clause as drafted has no cap."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"What a refund and a dispute each cost at a $4-5 seat","items":[["Dodo refund fee","$1 = Rs95.39","fetched dodopayments.com/pricing, 2026-08-30 (BUSINESS.md:580)"],["Dodo dispute fee","$30 = Rs2,861.70","same; at USD/INR 95.39"],["Dispute against a $4 seat","7.50x the monthly charge","derived"],["Dispute against a $5 seat","6.00x the monthly charge","derived"],["Stripe India, dispute lost","Rs2,000 plus principal","BUSINESS.md:580, fetched 2026-08-30; Rs1,000 if won"],["Cost of the generous policy","2.08% of gross at a 2% refund rate","BUSINESS.md:518 - 2.74-3.51% of contribution (BUSINESS.md:524)"]]},{"type":"table","title":"The two shapes in the benchmark set","cols":["Product","Policy","Read"],"rows":[["Obsidian","\"All fees are non-cancellable and non-refundable and are based on Services purchased and not actual usage\"","obsidian.md/terms, 2026-08-30 (BUSINESS.md:530)"],["Paddle","non-refundable unless law requires; higher local consumer rights always apply","paddle.com/legal/refund-policy, 2026-08-30 (BUSINESS.md:531)"],["37signals","refund on request for a forgotten renewal; prorated \"for the remaining whole months\"; 60 days of data kept to migrate","basecamp.com/about/policies/refund, 2026-08-30 (BUSINESS.md:532)"],["frontmatter, drafted","30 days first charge, worldwide; 90-day prorated renewal; same-day refund instead of a chargeback","BUSINESS.md:644-664"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"What each path costs","items":[["Waiver taken correctly","0","needs three artefacts, all three, every time"],["Waiver taken incorrectly","the whole supply is free","Art 14(4)(b), fetched EUR-Lex 2026-08-30 (BUSINESS.md:542)"],["Right granted unconditionally","at most 14 days of one subscription per withdrawal","at $5/month that is about $2.30"],["EU representative, due from the first EU seat","EUR420-852/yr = Rs46,645-94,622","fetched prighter.com/pricing, 2026-08-31 (r26-c8:70)"],["UK annual renewals","a fresh 14-day window at every renewal","Paddle, fetched paddle.com/legal/refund-policy 2026-08-30 (BUSINESS.md:543)"]]},{"type":"table","title":"The three artefacts the exemption needs","cols":["Artefact","Requirement"],"rows":[["Prior express consent","separate unticked checkbox, not bundled into terms; store boolean, exact string version, timestamp"],["Performance actually begun","the provisioning event, timestamped"],["Durable-medium confirmation","receipt email repeating the acknowledgement text back (Art 7(2) / 8(7))"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","what":"Ship the drafted refund policy, cap the prorated clause, and grant the EU fourteen-day right unconditionally with no waiver checkbox.","label":"Ship the drafted policy; grant the withdrawal right unconditionally","gains":["Removes most of the dispute cost for about 2.08% of gross","Deletes a whole compliance surface and a checkout step","Consistent with a product whose files stay on the user's disk"],"costs":["Generous at a price where generosity is cheap but not free","Forgoes the revenue a waiver would have retained"],"system":"A refunds path in billing. No consent capture, no durable-medium receipt.","screens":"A refunds page and one line at checkout.","money":"About 2.08% of gross at a 2% refund rate."},{"k":"b","what":"Non-refundable as the published line, with the Art 16(m) waiver taken properly at checkout.","label":"Non-refundable, with the waiver taken properly","gains":["Costs nothing directly and is the category norm for file-first tools","Maximises revenue retention"],"costs":["Getting the waiver slightly wrong makes the supply free by law","Each dispute costs six to seven and a half months of the seat it came from","Needs storage and replay of exact consent text"],"system":"Consent capture, a timestamped performance-start event, a durable-medium receipt.","screens":"An unticked checkbox with exact statutory wording.","money":"Highest retained revenue, highest tail risk."},{"k":"c","what":"Thirty-day refund on a first charge only, with no renewal proration and no waiver flow.","label":"Thirty-day first-charge refund only","gains":["Covers buyer's remorse at a bounded cost","Simple to publish and to honour"],"costs":["Leaves the forgotten-annual-renewal case, which is what actually generates chargebacks"],"system":"A refunds path with a date check.","screens":"One line at checkout.","money":"Bounded, smaller than (a)."},{"k":"d","what":"No published policy until a paying customer exists.","label":"No published policy until there is a customer","gains":["No work now"],"costs":["India's e-commerce rules require the refund and cancellation policy to be displayed","So this stops being viable the moment a checkout exists"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None, and an obligation the first day a checkout ships."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["The asymmetry decides both halves. A refund at $5 is trivial, a dispute is $30 plus the principal, and a bad waiver makes the supply free.","The policy is already written and already checked against four fetched benchmark policies. Add a cap to the prorated-renewal clause and publish it.","With no free trial there is one withdrawal window per contract, so the exposure without a waiver is bounded and small.","The exception is UK annual plans, where the window returns every year, which is another reason to take this with PR11."],"flip":"If the measured refund rate goes materially above 2%, the thirty-day window is the dial to turn, not the policy to abandon.","linked":["PR11","PR16","PR4"],"sources":["docs/BUSINESS.md:518","docs/BUSINESS.md:531","docs/BUSINESS.md:542","docs/BUSINESS.md:543","docs/BUSINESS.md:552","docs/BUSINESS.md:580","docs/BUSINESS.md:644","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:550","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r26-c8-b2b.md:70","merged: PR15"]},{"id":"PR19","cat":"Pricing & tiers","sub":"Grandfathering","weight":"medium","q":"Do early subscribers keep their price forever, for three years, or only until the next announced change?","lede":"Break-even sits between what $4 and what $5 buy, so a perpetual price promise may be a perpetual promise to run near cost.","visual":{"kind":"state","states":[{"label":"Founding cohort","meta":"price held, stated at checkout","tone":"accent","current":true},{"label":"Continuous","meta":"price held","via":"keeps paying","tone":"good"},{"label":"Lapsed 60 days","meta":"price forfeit","via":"lapse","tone":"warn"},{"label":"Tier changed","meta":"current price applies","via":"upgrade","tone":"neutral"}],"note":"The drafted policy already names every transition; only the population it covers is open.","caption":"When a held price is forfeited under the policy BUSINESS.md drafted."},"stakes":"A perpetual promise made at a near-cost price cannot be withdrawn later without breaking it in public.","state":["v15 has one line, in §22: price changes, email before the next charge (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:536).","BUSINESS.md drafts a full policy: price held while the subscription is continuous, forfeit after a 60-day lapse, forfeit on upgrade (docs/BUSINESS.md:419).","Its own anti-recommendation says perpetual grandfathering caps blended revenue permanently (docs/BUSINESS.md:426).","Break-even at the founder's own rate is ₹333.25 a month (r26-c6:45), which sits between what $4 and what $5 buy."],"path":["The policy was written alongside the price-testing section, where sticky-by-account pricing made grandfathering a necessary companion rule.","The price test was then struck, and the grandfathering rule was never revisited on its own terms.","v15 kept a one-line notice rule and dropped the policy.","The break-even figure arrived later, in the round 26 unit-economics work."],"tension":["The standard alternative, a three-year sunset with 90 days' notice, costs goodwill precisely with the earliest users, who are the ones who talk.","The input to break-even is itself unsettled: the support coefficient is stated as 0.10 and as 0.30 in the same repo (r26-c6:50).","A price promise is one of the few reasons to buy early from a product with no track record.","Two policies published side by side invite the question of why customer 101 pays more."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"Why the promise is expensive here specifically","items":[["Break-even monthly price at Rs1,700/h founder time","Rs333.25","r26-c6:45, from 0.1445 founder-hours per paying user per month"],["$4 a seat at USD/INR 95.39","Rs381.56","derived; 1.14x break-even"],["$5 a seat at USD/INR 95.39","Rs476.95","derived; 1.43x break-even"],["Support cost per paying user per month","Rs245.65","r26-c6:22, the largest single line"],["Confidence in that line","low - the coefficient is stated as 0.10 and 0.30 in the same repo","r26-c6:50, a 3x spread"]]},{"type":"table","title":"The drafted policy's forfeit events","cols":["Event","Legacy price"],"rows":[["Subscription stays continuous","kept, for as long as it is continuous"],["Lapse over 60 days, then resubscribe","forfeit - stops churn-and-return arbitrage"],["Tier upgrade","forfeit; new tier at current list"],["Annual to monthly","forfeit; the annual discount was consideration for the commitment"],["Currency or PPP reassignment","never applied retroactively"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","what":"The price is held for as long as the subscription is continuous, for everyone, forever.","label":"Perpetual while the subscription is continuous","gains":["Strongest trust signal and easiest to state at checkout","Already drafted, with every transition named"],"costs":["Caps blended revenue permanently at a price near break-even","The break-even input is itself uncertain threefold"],"system":"A price snapshot per account.","screens":"One line at checkout.","money":"Locks early revenue at close to cost."},{"k":"b","what":"Held prices sunset after three years, with ninety days' notice before the change.","label":"Three-year sunset with ninety days' notice","gains":["Standard and defensible","Lets the price move once the cost base is understood"],"costs":["Costs goodwill with the earliest cohort, which supplies the word of mouth this product depends on"],"system":"A price snapshot plus an expiry date.","screens":"A notice in the in-product list.","money":"Recovers revenue at year three."},{"k":"c","what":"No grandfathering; announced changes apply to everyone at the next renewal.","label":"No grandfathering at all","gains":["Simplest ledger and no legacy prices to reason about"],"costs":["Removes a real reason to buy early from a product with no track record"],"system":"No snapshot needed.","screens":"The notice rule already in §22.","money":"Full flexibility on price."},{"k":"d","what":"Perpetual for the first hundred paying accounts, and no grandfathering for everyone after.","label":"Perpetual for the first hundred, then no grandfathering","gains":["Buys the founding cohort's loyalty at a bounded, countable cost","Leaves the price free to move afterwards"],"costs":["Two policies to publish and one number to defend","Invites the question from customer 101"],"system":"A snapshot on the first hundred accounts only.","screens":"Both policies visible at checkout.","money":"Caps the concession at a hundred accounts."}],"rec":"d","recCase":["The first hundred customers are worth more as advocates than as revenue, and their price should be a promise.","Everyone after should sit under a policy that lets the price move, because break-even is close to the launch number and its input is uncertain by a factor of three.","Publish both at checkout, so nobody discovers the distinction later.","This only matters once a price exists, so it is downstream of PR3 and PR17."],"flip":"If the pilot measures the support coefficient at the low end of that threefold spread, (a) becomes affordable and is the better story.","linked":["PR11","PR17","PR3"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:536","docs/BUSINESS.md:419","docs/BUSINESS.md:426","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r26-c6-unit-economics.md:45","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r26-c6-unit-economics.md:50"]},{"id":"G15","cat":"Go-to-market & channels","sub":"First hundred","weight":"critical","q":"Where do the ten pilot strangers and the twenty teams come from, and who makes the approach?","lede":"Everything after week 3 depends on ten people nobody has identified, and the query that would find them has never been run.","visual":{"kind":"funnel","steps":[{"label":"Visitors a loop would have to deliver","n":22222,"unit":"visitors","tone":"stop"},{"label":"Free signups at 9%","n":2000,"unit":"signups","tone":"warn"},{"label":"Paying customers at 5%","n":100,"unit":"customers","tone":"neutral"}],"note":"No measured loop produces the top figure at n=0 (r25-w4:92).","caption":"What a loop would owe, against zero measured loops."},"stakes":"The exit test, the price hypothesis and the whole fortnight rest on named humans this programme does not have.","state":["§9 says the pilot's ten users bring their own repos and agents, and names no source (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:231).","§11 makes the paid tier a hypothesis until twenty team conversations return seat counts (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:292).","The instrument exists on paper: public repos holding both a CLAUDE.md and a hand-written handover file (docs/THESIS.md:747).","It has never been run, by the record or by the auditor, for want of an authenticated token (docs/CRITIQUE.md:1191)."],"path":["Across 105 reports and 374,866 words there are zero instances of customer discovery, design partner or interview (docs/CRITIQUE.md:1102).","The twenty conversations were added as the instrument for the price and never staffed.","The founder is the one person holding the token, and the search costs an afternoon."],"tension":["Cold booking twenty conversations in a fortnight is optimistic at 1.21 working days a week (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:227).","Warm teams will not say the discouraging thing, and a warm no is indistinguishable from politeness.","Whether anyone pays for review state in any shell is the one thing eleven gaps of desk research never touched (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:146).","The ten test the product and the twenty test the price, and only the second tolerates a warm sample."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"The instrument, and its status","items":[["The query","Public repos containing both CLAUDE.md and a hand-written handover/context file","docs/THESIS.md:747"],["What it yields","A qualified lead with a visible email in git log","docs/THESIS.md:747"],["Times run","0 — \"has never been run, by the record or by me\"","docs/CRITIQUE.md:1191"],["Why not","Unauthenticated /search/code returns 401; gh fails TLS through the research proxy — the record said so and the auditor confirmed it","docs/CRITIQUE.md:1102"],["Customer-discovery vocabulary across 105 reports and 374,866 words","0 instances each of customer discovery, design partner, interviews, waitlist, beta tester, pre-order, user test, willingness to pay","docs/CRITIQUE.md:1102"],["What the critique says is missing","\"Ten named humans, with emails, in a file, who have said they want this\"","docs/CRITIQUE.md:1102"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"Why a loop cannot supply the ten, or the hundred","items":[["Visitors needed for the first 100 paying customers","22,222 — 100 ÷ 5% conversion = 2,000 signups ÷ 9% visitor-to-signup","r25-w4:90"],["Measured loops that produce them at n=0","None","r25-w4:92"],["Corpus conclusion","\"The first hundred cannot come from a loop; it must be hand-recruited, one at a time, from people the founder can name\"","r25-w4:94"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"What rests on the twenty conversations","items":[["Round-2 verdict on payment","\"Whether anyone pays for review state in any shell\" — eleven gaps measured installs and attention, never payment","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:146"],["What Pro sells at MVP-1","Shared review state, comments and MCP — the first is what GitHub Team bundles at $4, the other two untested","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:54"],["Retention band the tier sits in","Top-quartile annual gross retention 60–70% under $50/month; 23% for AI-native products under $50","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:292"],["Withdrawn earlier claim","\"114 seats at $8 covers the nut\" — withdrawn because the feature was GitHub's at $4 and the band would require replacing 34–46 of 114 seats a year","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:292"],["Monthly nut the tier would have to reach","about ₹1.09L, currently covered by 54–78 consulting hours","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:292"],["Founder capacity in the same fortnight","1.21 engineering days per calendar week measured; 0.23 in the last 30 days","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:227"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Run the code search now; recruit both cohorts cold from that list","what":"One authenticated query, fifty named repos with committer emails, both cohorts drawn from it.","gains":["Unbiased on both sides","Produces the first named humans this programme has had"],"costs":["Twenty cold conversations in a fortnight is not bookable at the measured rate","Contacting the list is a separate outbound decision"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"An afternoon, plus a token already held."},{"k":"b","label":"Recruit both cohorts from the studio's network","what":"Ten friendly users and twenty friendly teams.","gains":["Fastest to book","Everyone answers"],"costs":["Ten friendly reads falsify nothing, which is the point of the exit test","A warm no reads as politeness"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Cold list for the ten; ten warm and ten cold for the twenty","what":"The strangers stay strangers; the price conversations keep a control group.","gains":["The exit test stays a stranger test","Twenty conversations become bookable inside a fortnight","A warm-versus-cold split is itself a finding"],"costs":["Halves the sample on each side of the price question","Neither half alone is conclusive","Still depends on the search being run this week"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"An afternoon for the search."},{"k":"d","label":"Defer the twenty conversations until after MVP-0","what":"Build first, ask about the price later.","gains":["Removes a fortnight of load from a one-person team","The ten strangers still run on schedule"],"costs":["The build proceeds with the revenue hypothesis wholly untested","§11 already calls that the open question"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"The paid tier stays unevidenced through the build."}],"rec":"c","recCase":["The exit test needs strangers or it proves nothing, so the ten must come from the cold list.","Twenty cold conversations are not bookable in a fortnight at 1.21 working days a week; ten warm ones are.","Splitting the twenty keeps a control: if the warm half says yes and the cold half does not, that is the answer.","None of it happens unless the code search is run this week, by the one person with the token."],"flip":"If the code search returns fewer than fifty qualified repos with visible emails, the cold half has no source and the network is all there is.","linked":["G16","G22","G27","PR17"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:231","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:313","docs/THESIS.md:747","docs/CRITIQUE.md:1102","docs/CRITIQUE.md:1191","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r25-w4-retention-and-growth.md:90","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r25-w4-retention-and-growth.md:94","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:292","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:227","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:352","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:54","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:146","merged: G17"],"dupes":{"dropped":["R3"],"why":"Where the ten strangers and the twenty teams come from and who approaches them. Same cold/warm/panel/no-source fork; recs c vs a. Go-to-market & channels owns recruitment. G16 (contact sgnk-md's users) stays separate — it is one source, not the sourcing decision."}},{"id":"G22","cat":"Go-to-market & channels","sub":"Allocation","weight":"critical","q":"Which single channel gets the founder's launch hours in the first quarter?","lede":"The plan lists eight channels, two of them cut and three of them requests to strangers, at a measured one day a week.","visual":{"kind":"funnel","steps":[{"label":"Channel rows in §12","n":8,"unit":"rows","tone":"neutral"},{"label":"Still carrying a live channel","n":7,"unit":"rows","tone":"warn"},{"label":"Blocked by nobody and nothing unbuilt","n":1,"unit":"row","tone":"accent"}],"note":"The one unblocked row is published research. §23 calls every channel borrowed.","caption":"Eight channels, one that nothing blocks."},"stakes":"At 1.21 engineering days a calendar week the plan cannot run seven channels, and none of them produces the first cohort.","state":["§12's table has eight rows in order (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:300).","§23 lists \"every channel borrowed\" as a weakness in the same document (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:558).","No section allocates founder time to any channel.","Measured capacity is 1.21 engineering days a calendar week, 0.23 over the last thirty days (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:227)."],"path":["The table was built by ranking channels, not by budgeting hours against them.","Two rows were cut in the 2026-09-08 round and the ranking was not re-derived.","The corpus already concluded that the first hundred must be hand-recruited (r25-w4:94)."],"tension":["Hand recruitment is the only unborrowed channel and the only one that also produces research.","It does not compound, so quarter two starts from nothing.","Everything on the channel table, summed optimistically, reaches 350k–500k year-one visitors (r17-h7:153).","Two maintainers can end the toolchain channel with one reply each."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"The channel table's own status, row by row","cols":["Channel","Status in v15","Depends on"],"rows":[["Obsidian plugin","CUT (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:304)","—"],["superpowers","Week 2 (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:305)","A maintainer's permission and an unbuilt MCP server"],["spec-kit","Second (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:306)","A maintainer's permission and a 20-file sample"],["Plan mode","Demoted (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:307)","An untested file location — one hour to check"],["Published research","Now (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:308)","Nothing — the only unblocked row"],["Show HN","MVP-0 exit (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:309)","6 of 10, then 1.4% (all Show HN) to 5.7% (this category) odds of clearing 100 points"],["Chrome extension / Product Hunt","CUT / MVP-1 (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:310)","A ?src= parameter that is unbuilt; an exclusion the record already made"],["Exported pages with a mark","MVP-2 (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:311)","A deploy count that does not exist"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"The arithmetic the allocation has to survive","items":[["Visitors needed for the first 100 paying customers","22,222","r25-w4:90"],["Measured loops that produce them at n=0","None","r25-w4:92"],["Everything in the channel table, summed, optimistic, year one","350k–500k visitors; the 1.26M requirement is a 24-to-36-month cumulative figure","r17-h7:153"],["Corpus conclusion","\"The first hundred cannot come from a loop; it must be hand-recruited\"","r25-w4:94"],["Measured founder capacity","1.21 engineering days per calendar week; 0.23 in the last 30 days","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:227"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Hand recruitment: the code-search list, the ten users, the twenty teams","what":"Every launch hour goes to named humans.","gains":["The only unborrowed channel","It produces the interviews the programme has never had","It is the only thing that answers whether anyone pays"],"costs":["Does not scale and does not compound","Nothing is being built for quarter two","Consumes the same hours as the build"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"No spend. Founder hours only."},{"k":"b","label":"Toolchain documentation: superpowers, then spec-kit","what":"The week-2 channel becomes the quarter's channel.","gains":["Highest relevance per reader","Reaches 22–30k active repos if accepted"],"costs":["Entirely outside our control","Two maintainers can end it with one reply","Produces no interviews"],"system":"An integration page, and eventually an MCP server.","screens":"One integration page.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Content and the validator","what":"The only compounding channels, both slow.","gains":["Compounds, and the engine already produces the material","Neither depends on a stranger's permission"],"costs":["Nothing to show for three quarters","The validator is gated on fix-first"],"system":"The validator needs a client-side build of the engine.","screens":"A research index and a validator page.","money":"Seven engineering days before the validator can be honest."},{"k":"d","label":"Launch events: Show HN and Product Hunt","what":"A spike at the MVP-0 exit.","gains":["Visible, free, and confers credibility on a solo founder","One day of work for a whole quarter's channel"],"costs":["1.4% to 5.7% odds of clearing 100 points","Decays to zero in 96 hours","Leaves no owned asset behind"],"system":"No change.","screens":"A launch page.","money":"None."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["The arithmetic says no loop delivers 22,222 visitors at n=0, and none has been measured.","The one thing eleven gaps of desk research never touched is whether anyone pays, and only conversations answer it.","At 0.23 engineering days a week over the last month, a second channel is a wish rather than a plan."],"flip":"If the superpowers maintainer says yes in week 2, a channel reaching 22–30k active repos outranks hand recruitment for the quarter.","linked":["FF12","G15","G26","G6"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:300","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:558","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:227","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r25-w4-retention-and-growth.md:90","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r25-w4-retention-and-growth.md:92","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r25-w4-retention-and-growth.md:94","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r17-h7-content-seo-distribution.md:153"]},{"id":"G1","cat":"Go-to-market & channels","sub":"Headline","weight":"high","q":"Do the weeks 1–2 headline tests run three arms, two, or one?","lede":"The fortnight is the only thing between this plan and a build, and the plan gives two answers about what it tests.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":150,"cols":[{"title":"Arm 1 · what the AI wrote","tone":"accent"},{"title":"Arm 2 · what the agent changed","tone":"stop"},{"title":"Arm 3 · what nobody reviewed","tone":"warn"}],"rows":[{"label":"Already shipped by","cells":["iA Writer 7, 2023; nobody at span level","Claude Code, Antigravity, Codex, VS Code","Almanac, 2021 to 2025"]},{"label":"Free where it ships","cells":["No","Yes, in four editors","It was paid, and it closed"]},{"label":"Best pull measured","cells":["208 downloads for the Obsidian port","266 reactions, for a per-session panel","0 likes, 1 post in three years"]},{"label":"Reads per arm at ten people","cells":["3","3","4"]}],"note":"Arm 1 was demoted two rounds ago and is still in the test.","caption":"Three arms over ten people is three reads each, which is not a signal."},"stakes":"The day-14 kill signal is the plan's only gate, and three arms over ten people make it unattributable to any headline.","state":["§12 names three variants and says the upvoted pain matches the second and third (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:296).","Exhibit 19 says the ten developers see the mock \"in both framings\" — two, not three (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:352).","The gap register's own next-steps list also says three arms (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:110).","Arm 1 is carried as demoted, not deleted: \"Attribution is shown when available, not the headline\" (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:175)."],"path":["The three arms were written before the round that demoted authorship marking.","Exhibit 19 was rewritten on 2026-09-08 and §12 was not re-swept with it.","Today's research reopens arm 1 from the other side: authorship is the only one of four claims no platform occupies.","It also takes arm 2 away. Working-tree diff of agent changes shipped free in four places between 2026-08-24 and 2026-09-03."],"tension":["Arm 2 is now free in Claude Code v2.1.260, Antigravity, Codex and VS Code's Agents window.","Arm 3 is Almanac's feature sentence. Almanac raised $45M and switched off on 2025-01-31.","Arm 1 was demoted on iA Writer's consumer failure, and no platform has occupied it since.","Ten people split three ways cannot separate a bad arm from a bad product."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"Arm 1 has already been sold, twice, by other people","items":[["iA Writer 7 shipped authorship marking","2023","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:175"],["Obsidian port of it, downloads","208","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:175"],["Best VS Code extension in that niche, installs","366","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:175"],["Reddit demand — the plan says both things","§12 says the top twenty \"AI wrote\" posts contain no request for authorship marking; Exhibit 4 says \"one Reddit ask\". Different samples, same document","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:296 and :175"]]},{"type":"bars","title":"What the target buyer complains about — 300 unbiased posts, r/ClaudeAI + r/cursor + r/ChatGPTCoding","note":"Full table at docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r25-w1-reddit-recovered.md:78-87. All seven rows shown; percentage of 300 posts.","unit":"% of 300 posts","data":[["Price",15.7],["Reviewing agent output",14],["Context window / memory",11],["Usage limits / quota",9.7],["Agent broke something",4],["Markdown / docs files",3.3],["Byte-exact editing vocabulary",0.3]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Test all three arms as §12 and the gap register list them","what":"Ten people, three headlines, three or four reads each.","gains":["Keeps the plan internally consistent with §12","No argument to have before week 1"],"costs":["No arm reaches a readable signal","Day 14 returns an opinion, not a kill","Spends a third of the test on a headline four editors now ship free"],"system":"No change.","screens":"Three landing pages, one per arm.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Drop arm 1; test arms 2 and 3, five people each","what":"The version Exhibit 19 already assumes.","gains":["Five reads per arm","Matches the document that is most recent"],"costs":["Arm 2 is the claim four editors gave away this quarter","Arm 3 is verbatim a dead product's feature","Drops the only claim nobody occupies"],"system":"No change.","screens":"Two landing pages.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Drop arm 2; test authorship against unreviewed state, five each","what":"Tests the one unoccupied claim against the one with a $45M corpse behind it.","gains":["Both arms are still open questions in the market","Five reads per arm","Reopens a demotion that rested on one consumer product"],"costs":["Contradicts the demotion recorded in Exhibit 4","Authorship has no measured pull at all outside teams","Neither arm is the sentence §1 currently leads with"],"system":"No change.","screens":"Two landing pages, and the tint card must show an author.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"One arm, shown to all ten","what":"Ten reads of a single sentence, no comparison.","gains":["Strongest single read available in a fortnight","Closest to a real first impression"],"costs":["A bad arm is indistinguishable from a bad product","No second sentence to fall back to"],"system":"No change.","screens":"One landing page.","money":"None."}],"rec":"c","recCase":["Arm 2 shipped free in four editors this quarter, so testing it measures whether people can read, not whether they want it.","Arm 3 is the sentence Almanac shipped, and $45M did not save it.","Authorship at span level is the only one of the four claims nothing opened is occupying.","Five reads per arm is the most this fortnight can buy while still separating two headlines."],"flip":"If a platform ships span-level authorship marking before week 2, arm 1 joins arm 2 and the test collapses to one arm.","linked":["P2"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:296","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:352","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:175","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:110","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r25-w1-reddit-recovered.md:79"]},{"id":"G2","cat":"Go-to-market & channels","sub":"Obsidian","weight":"high","q":"Does any Obsidian surface ship, and do the four exhibits that still promise one get deleted?","lede":"The live-preview plugin was week 2's channel in every plan until this one, and four exhibits still carry it as live.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":170,"cols":[{"title":"The live-preview fix","tone":"stop"},{"title":"Additive review-state extension","tone":"warn"}],"rows":[{"label":"Forum demand, same population","cells":["501 likes, 117 posts, 18,331 views","0 likes, 1 post in three years"]},{"label":"Can a plugin do it","cells":["No. The tree is depth-1 by construction","Yes. Decoration over byte ranges"]},{"label":"Nearest measured launch","cells":["115 installs in 14 days, against our 200 kill line","Never sized"]},{"label":"What it costs to ship","cells":["U+200C written into the user's files","Obsidian owns the registry and the queue"]}],"note":"Both columns were measured in the same forum on the same day.","caption":"Demand sits on the surface we cannot build. The one we can has none."},"stakes":"Cutting the plugin removes MVP-0's only listed channel and one of seven retention levers, and neither has a replacement.","state":["§12 cuts the plugin because Obsidian's Live Preview tree is depth-1 by construction (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:304).","Exhibit 6 still lists it as MVP-0's channel with a 200-install kill line (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:204).","Exhibit 19 still schedules \"plugin shipped\" in weeks 1–2 (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:352); Exhibit 24 still counts it as a retention lever (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:428).","Exhibit 26 and the §19 diagram still carry it as a family member (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:464 and :477)."],"path":["Earlier rounds made the 501-like rendering bug the cheapest audience we would ever buy, and the free wedge.","Round 2 on 2026-09-08 killed the mechanism, not the demand (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:127).","§12 was rewritten in that round and the other four exhibits were not re-swept."],"tension":["Every engine claim we have is measured on seven Obsidian vaults, one wiki being 77% of the files (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:514).","Obsidian core shipped nothing about AI, agents, diffs or review across its last twenty releases, so the shelf is empty where ours would sit.","In that store, agent-writing plugins hold roughly forty times the downloads of the only review-shaped plugin.","Deleting the four survivors makes two holes visible rather than hidden: an MVP-0 channel and a retention lever."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"The Obsidian forum, one population, one metric, 2026-09-08","items":[["Nested-code-block rendering bug — likes / posts / views","501 / 117 / 18,331","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:410"],["Closest review-state request — likes / views / posts in ~3 years","0 / 251 / 1","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:410"],["\"Tracking changes within notes\" — likes","1","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:410"],["\"Suggestion Mode like Google Docs/Word\" — likes","3","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:410"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"What the plugin registry actually pays out","items":[["Community plugins","7,092","r25-w4:81"],["Median downloads per plugin","532","r25-w4:81"],["Plugins under 1,000 downloads","59.1% (4,194)","r25-w4:81"],["Share of all downloads held by the top 10%","91.7%","r25-w4:81"],["Relay, the exemplar the plan leaned on — rank","128 of 7,092 (p98.4)","r25-w4:19"],["Relay's real best single release vs the 191,997 cumulative figure","21,047 — a 9.1× inflation","r25-w4:18"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"The cost of conceding this audience, which §12 does not price","items":[["The corpus every engine claim rests on","test/corpus/foreign/SOURCES.json is seven Obsidian vaults; one wiki is 77% of the 8,513 files","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:514"],["What that makes the 83% refusal rate","\"A property of those vaults, not of markdown in the wild\"","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:514"],["Consequence","We would be cutting the only population against which the product is verified"]]},{"type":"table","title":"Where the cut channels still live in v15","cols":["Location","What it still says","Consequence if §12 governs"],"rows":[["§12 Exhibit 17, docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:304","Free Obsidian plugin — CUT","—"],["§12 Exhibit 17, docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:310","Chrome extension — CUT","—"],["§8 Exhibit 6, docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:204","\"Free Obsidian live-preview plugin, week 2; kill: under 200 installs in 14 days\"","MVP-0 loses its only listed channel"],["§8 Exhibit 6, docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:203","\"Chrome extension; MCP server\" as MVP-1 surfaces","MVP-1 loses a surface"],["§14 Exhibit 19, docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:352","\"plugin shipped\" in weeks 1–2","A fortnight deliverable disappears"],["§17 Exhibit 24, docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:428","\"The plugin … stays installed in a vault the user already opens daily\"","A retention lever disappears with no replacement"],["§19 diagram and Exhibit 26, docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:464 and :477","\"Chrome extension · Obsidian plugin — reading and distribution\"; \"Free; channels — MVP-1, week 2\"","A product-family member disappears"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"No Obsidian surface; delete the four surviving mentions","what":"§12 governs, and Exhibits 6, 19, 24 and 26 lose the plugin.","gains":["The plan stops saying both things","Two unreplaced holes become visible","No build days spent on an unreachable parse"],"costs":["Week 2 loses its only non-outbound action","The population the engine is verified against stops being a market"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None. Removes a family member from the §19 diagram.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Ship the additive review-state CodeMirror extension in week 2","what":"Review state drawn over the sidecar's byte ranges, with no re-parse.","gains":["Buildable, because it needs no containment","Keeps a foothold in the vaults the corpus is drawn from"],"costs":["Puts the 0-like feature in front of the 501-like audience","Obsidian owns the registry and the review queue","Adds build days to a fortnight meant to build nothing"],"system":"A CodeMirror extension reading `.frontmatter/review.jsonl`.","screens":"A tint layer inside Obsidian, no panel.","money":"None. Free plugin."},{"k":"c","label":"Ship the live-preview fix as an appearance-only repaint","what":"Repaint nested constructs without correcting the parse.","gains":["Reaches the one measured demand in that population","Would be the cheapest audience we ever bought, if it were possible"],"costs":["Depends on DOM classes Obsidian has already deleted once","The only working precedents write U+200C into user files","A byte-exact product cannot ship that"],"system":"No engine change; a rendering hack outside the engine.","screens":"None of ours.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Delete three mentions; keep the retention lever open in writing","what":"Exhibits 6, 19 and 26 lose the plugin; Exhibit 24 keeps it flagged as unreplaced.","gains":["Honest about the one loss with no replacement","Keeps the retention question visible instead of quietly dropped"],"costs":["Leaves a lever in the plan that depends on a cut channel","Same defect, smaller"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["The parse was verified unreachable twice, independently, so option (c) is not available at any price.","The additive extension is the feature that scored 0 likes in exactly this population.","Leaving the four mentions in guarantees somebody builds the cut thing from Exhibit 6 next month.","Naming the two holes is worth more than hiding them behind a channel that is gone."],"flip":"If the five-second screenshot test reads well and an Obsidian user asks for review state unprompted, the additive extension becomes the cheapest reach we have.","linked":["FF2","G22"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:304","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:410","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:514","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:127","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r25-w4-retention-and-growth.md:81","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r25-w4-retention-and-growth.md:18","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:203","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:204","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:310","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:352","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:428","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:464","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:477","merged: G3"],"dupes":{"dropped":["PL8"],"why":"Does any Obsidian surface ship, and do the stale references get deleted. Same options, both rec (a) delete everywhere. Go-to-market & channels owns the channel. MK7 is NOT a duplicate — it bundles the ?src= replacement as well."}},{"id":"G6","cat":"Go-to-market & channels","sub":"Toolchains","weight":"high","q":"What do we ship to the superpowers and spec-kit maintainers in week 2, and how do we ask?","lede":"Week 2's channel is a request to a stranger nobody has made, and its named artefact does not exist in the repository.","visual":{"kind":"flow","perRow":3,"nodes":[{"label":"Agent writes the spec","note":"architectural path only","tone":"neutral"},{"label":"Commits it","note":"the file is already in the repo","tone":"neutral"},{"label":"\"Please review it\"","note":"the terminal prints a path","tone":"warn"},{"label":"Terminal ends","note":"no review surface of its own","tone":"stop"},{"label":"A README line points here","note":"needs a maintainer's yes","tone":"accent","dashed":true},{"label":"An MCP entry","note":"no MCP server exists in src/","tone":"stop","dashed":true}],"note":"Spikes stay in chat and the bounded path writes no plan document.","caption":"Where superpowers stops, and which of our two artefacts exists."},"stakes":"The plan's first channel depends on a stranger's yes and on a server nobody has written.","state":["§12's week-2 action is a README line and an MCP entry, with a maintainer PR gated on approval (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:305).","Exhibit 6 puts the MCP server in the MVP-1 column (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:203), and F11 sits in the plan's own Untested row (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:188).","No approach has been made to either maintainer, and it is still open after round 2 (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:58 and :146).","Checked 2026-09-09: package.json has no MCP dependency, none of its 26 scripts mention one, and src/ has zero MCP references."],"path":["The channel was designed by reading what the toolchains write, not by asking their maintainers anything.","Round 2 ran both tools on a scratch repo and contacted nobody (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:126).","The artefact list and the feature list were written at the same time and never checked against each other."],"tension":["superpowers is the only toolchain that halts, names a path in the repo, and asks a human to review a file it has committed.","spec-kit's pitch is a critique of its own default artefact, which is an awkward first contact.","A rejected pull request is public and permanent; an issue asking first is neither.","Only the architectural path writes a document, and the share of sessions taking it is unmeasured (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:146)."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"The two targets, sized 2026-09-06 and 2026-09-08","cols":["Toolchain","Reach","What it writes","Where it stops"],"rows":[["obra/superpowers","75–85k public repos; 22–30k active in 30 days; marketplace counter 1,009,371 (cached)","Brainstorms, designs, writes the spec, commits it, then asks the human to review it","Terminal. No editor, no review state"],["github/spec-kit","11,072 public repos; about 1,660 active","specify/clarify/plan/tasks/implement; writes markdown then leaves","No review surface; its default checklist is ticked by the agent"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"What is still unknown about the channel","items":[["Whether either maintainer would accept a README line","Unmeasured — listed as still open after round 2","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:146"],["Share of superpowers sessions that take the architectural path (the only path that writes a document)","Unmeasured — listed as still open","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:146"],["Outreach made to date","None","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:58"],["A caveat §12 already carries","Only the architectural path writes a document; spikes stay in chat, bounded says \"no plan document\", and the plan document gets no review gate — only the spec does","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:305"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"What exists today for the week-2 artefact","items":[["MCP server in src/","None — no modelcontextprotocol dependency, no server module, zero MCP references in src/ (checked 2026-09-09)"],["MCP in package.json scripts","Absent from all 26: arch, budget, build, corpus, decide, dev, doc, format, format:check, lint, pdf, record, refs, spec, start, tauri (×6), test, test:watch, tree, typecheck, verify"],["MCP server scheduled","MVP-1","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:203"],["F11, agents writing through MCP","Listed in the plan's own Untested row","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:188"],["mdmax cert, the other CI-facing artefact","Never wired to a runnable command; exits 1 with ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND; cert is not one of the 26 scripts","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:224"],["Measured build rate","1.21 engineering days per calendar week; 0.23 in the last 30 days","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:227"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"What option (d) would have to overcome","items":[["src-tauri identity, checked 2026-09-09","productName \"sgnk-md\", identifier \"ai.sgnk.md\" — the desktop build still ships as the sibling app","src-tauri/tauri.conf.json:3, :5"],["Fix-first item 9","\"src-tauri carries the sibling app's identity\" — 1 day, not yet done","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:222"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Documentation PR to both, with the MCP server built first","what":"Build the server, then send two pull requests.","gains":["A working integration is stronger than a link","Reaches both populations at once"],"costs":["Adds build days to a fortnight meant to build nothing","A rejection is public and permanent in two repos","Pulls an Untested feature forward"],"system":"A local MCP server, currently scheduled for MVP-1.","screens":"None. A config entry in the user's agent.","money":"Six engineering days, at a measured 1.21 days a week."},{"k":"b","label":"superpowers only: ask in an issue, then a README line and one integration page","what":"No code. A question first, then a link and a page we own.","gains":["Highest relevance and the larger population","Reversible, and reads as courteous rather than promotional","Ships in hours, not days"],"costs":["Forgoes spec-kit's 11,072 repos for now","A link is weaker than a working integration","May get no answer at all"],"system":"No change.","screens":"One integration page on our own site.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"No outbound; publish our own integration page and wait to be found","what":"A page describing both toolchains, and no contact with either.","gains":["No permission needed and no rejection risk","The page is ours and stays useful whatever the maintainers say"],"costs":["Depends entirely on search, which contributes nothing for three quarters","Nobody in either community learns it exists"],"system":"No change.","screens":"One page.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Move the whole toolchain channel to MVP-1, where the MCP server lives","what":"Week 2 has no toolchain action.","gains":["Consistent with what is actually built","No outbound act while the MCP server is unwritten"],"costs":["Week 2 has no channel at all once the Obsidian plugin is cut","The maintainers are no closer to a yes in six months"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["The MCP entry cannot ship in week 2, because there is no MCP server anywhere in src/.","superpowers already halts and asks a human to review a committed file, so a review surface is on topic there.","An issue costs nothing, is reversible, and gets a yes or a no before a public pull request exists.","spec-kit's pitch depends on G8's re-measurement, so it should not be the first contact anyway."],"flip":"If the superpowers maintainer answers no, the channel is a page on our own site and week 2 has nothing outbound left.","linked":["G22","G24","G8"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:305","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:148","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:58","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:146","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:203","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:188","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:222","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:224","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:227","merged: G7"],"dupes":{"dropped":["B17","MK5"],"why":"Do we approach the superpowers and spec-kit maintainers, when, and with what ask. Three slices of one decision; recs b/a/b. Go-to-market & channels owns the channel."}},{"id":"G8","cat":"Go-to-market & channels","sub":"Toolchains","weight":"high","q":"Do we publish the agent-self-certification measurement by name, and at what sample size?","lede":"It is the sharpest sentence the research produced, and it is a public claim about somebody else's default artefact from twenty files.","visual":{"kind":"ba","before":{"title":"As measured, 2026-09-08","lines":[{"t":"Population 49,664 checklist files"},{"t":"20 sampled, 19 fully checked","mark":"warn"},{"t":"354 of 355 boxes ticked, 99.7%","mark":"warn"},{"t":"Anyone can run 200 and disagree in public","mark":"stop"}]},"after":{"title":"Re-measured at n of 200 or more","lines":[{"t":"Same population, defensible sample","mark":"good"},{"t":"Re-derivable by any reader","mark":"good"},{"t":"Meets §58's own standard","mark":"good"},{"t":"Costs one day, and delays the channel by it","mark":"warn"}]},"via":"one day","caption":"The claim is strong. The sample is what a critic attacks first."},"stakes":"A refuted marketing number refutes the product, whose one differentiator is that it refuses rather than guesses.","state":["§12 reframes the spec-kit channel as \"your checklist is green because the agent ticked it\" (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:306).","The measurement is population 49,664; 20 files sampled; 19 fully checked; 354 of 355 boxes ticked (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:306).","§58 permits numbers that are measured or fetched and re-derivable by anyone (docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:5022).","Three of our own published numbers were withdrawn when they failed a control (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:13)."],"path":["Round 2 found it on 2026-09-08 and ranked it among the five findings that change the most (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:140).","It replaced the older pitch, \"you have no review state\", which the same round refuted.","spec-kit is large enough that somebody will re-run this the day it is published."],"tension":["A 99.7% figure from twenty files is publishable only with its sample size in the same sentence.","The rule about our own fidelity percentages does not cover a third-party measurement, so this one turns on §58's re-derivable test.","The sentence is confrontational, and its target is the maintainer we would also be asking for a README line.","Removing the name removes the specificity, and readers identify the target anyway."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"The measurement as it stands","items":[["Population of checklists/requirements.md","49,664","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:306"],["Files sampled","20","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:306"],["Fully checked files in the sample","19 of 20","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:306"],["Boxes ticked","354 of 355 = 99.7%","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:306"],["Reviewer-owned checklist population, for contrast","4,536 — 11× rarer","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:306"],["spec-kit's size in the plan's own preferred unit","11,072 public repos, about 1,660 active — the plan struck star counts as a channel-size measure","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:148 and :176"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"The publication rules this would sit under — what §58 actually says","items":[["Rule that bites here","Any [SS]-tagged number, in any public asset — [SS] means \"search summary, nobody opened the page\" — verdict: \"No. Verify or omit\"","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:5022 and :100"],["Rule on fidelity percentages","Bans our own fidelity or coverage percentages until NF-1 and NF-3 land — it does not cover third-party measurements, so it is not the rule that governs this one","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:5022"],["What §58 explicitly permits","Numbers that are [measured] or [fetched] and re-derivable by anyone — which this becomes at a defensible n","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:5022"],["Precedent in this corpus","Three published numbers were withdrawn when they failed a control","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:13"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Publish it now, with the sample size and the method in the same sentence","what":"The line ships as measured, caveat attached.","gains":["Honest and immediate","The sentence is the strongest the research produced"],"costs":["A twenty-file sample invites a reader to run 200 and disagree","The disagreement would be public and about our rigour"],"system":"No change.","screens":"A published post and a spec-kit integration page.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Re-measure at n of 200 or more before publishing anything","what":"One day of counting, then the same sentence with a defensible denominator.","gains":["Meets §58's re-derivable standard","Turns the sharpest line we have into one that survives a re-run"],"costs":["Delays the spec-kit channel by a day","The larger sample may return a weaker number"],"system":"A counting script; nothing in the product.","screens":"Same as (a), later.","money":"One engineering day."},{"k":"c","label":"Publish the finding without naming spec-kit","what":"The pattern, not the product.","gains":["Removes the confrontation with a maintainer we also want a link from","The finding still lands with anyone running the toolchain"],"costs":["Removes the specificity that makes it land","Readers identify the target regardless"],"system":"No change.","screens":"A published post.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Do not publish; use it only with the ten and the twenty","what":"The line lives in conversation.","gains":["Zero public risk","Still does its work where the decision is made"],"costs":["Forgoes the one sentence likely to travel","Nothing accrues to the owned channel"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["One day buys the difference between a claim and a measurement, on the one line likely to be re-run.","The product's entire pitch is that it refuses rather than guesses, so a guessed denominator is self-refuting.","The corpus has already withdrawn three published numbers that failed a control."],"flip":"If a larger sample returns under 90%, the sentence goes and the spec-kit channel needs a different pitch entirely.","linked":["G6"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:306","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:148","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:140","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:13","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:5022","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:100"]},{"id":"G16","cat":"Go-to-market & channels","sub":"First hundred","weight":"high","q":"Do we contact sgnk-md's existing users?","lede":"If they exist, they are the only real users this codebase has ever had, and nobody has asked them anything.","visual":{"kind":"ba","before":{"title":"Today","lines":[{"t":"0 interviews across the whole programme","mark":"stop"},{"t":"Every demand claim inferred from public posts","mark":"warn"},{"t":"202 of 228 files shared with sgnk-md"}]},"after":{"title":"If a user list exists","lines":[{"t":"Ten people who have used this codebase","mark":"good"},{"t":"Note-takers, not agent operators","mark":"warn"},{"t":"Outbound to people who signed up for another product","mark":"warn"}]},"via":"one founder answer","caption":"The only real users this codebase may have, and their limit."},"stakes":"Every demand claim in the plan is inferred from public complaints, and a live user list may sit one directory away.","state":["The gap register lists sgnk-md's users as untapped and founder-gated (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:36, :112).","It is still open after round 2 (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:146).","202 of 228 files are shared with frontmatter (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:479); 41 of 43 editor files are byte-identical (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:141).","Interviews conducted across the whole programme: zero (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:35)."],"path":["The two products were never separated in anyone's mind.","Round 2 established that the editor shell is a fork rather than an asset.","The question was raised in the register and has waited for a founder answer since."],"tension":["They are note-takers, so their answers do not settle the agent-review question.","They signed up for a different product, so contacting them is outbound to a list with its own consent history.","Usage data answers how the editor is used and not why anyone would pay.","Talking to them first risks contaminating the stranger test the plan gates on."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"How closely the two products are the same thing","items":[["Shared source files","202 of 228 identical","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:479"],["Editor files byte-identical to sgnk-md","41 of 43","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:141"],["Files unique to frontmatter in the editor shell","0","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:141"],["Still visible in the shipped source, checked 2026-09-09","src/app/sitemap.ts opens \"sgnk-md sitemap\"; sgnk-md string literals in the drafts store, bookmarks, editor store, instrumentation and CodeMirrorEditor; src-tauri productName is \"sgnk-md\""],["Interviews conducted across the whole programme","0","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:35"],["What it would cost to tap","\"Founders: is there a user list, and may we contact ten?\"","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:36"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Establish whether a list exists, and ask ten of them","what":"Founders confirm the list, then ten short conversations.","gains":["The cheapest interviews available","The only people with a real usage history behind them"],"costs":["Wrong population for the agent-review question","Outbound to people who signed up for something else"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Look at usage data only; no outreach","what":"Read what the product already knows and contact nobody.","gains":["No consent question and no imposition","Available without waiting on a founder decision"],"costs":["Answers how, never why","Nothing about willingness to pay"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"No; sgnk-md's users are the wrong population for this buyer","what":"The list stays untouched.","gains":["Keeps the pilot clean","No outbound to a list collected for another product"],"costs":["Throws away the only existing users the codebase has","Leaves zero interviews standing"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Ask them, but only after the ten strangers","what":"Sequenced so the stranger test runs uncontaminated.","gains":["Preserves the exit test's independence","Both cohorts stay interpretable on their own"],"costs":["Two months of latency on the cheapest interviews available","The founder question stays open for two more months"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["Zero interviews is the largest hole in the programme, and this is the cheapest way to make it non-zero.","The founders can answer whether the list exists in a sentence, which is where this has been stuck.","Note-takers cannot settle the agent question, and they can settle how the editor is actually used."],"flip":"If the list is empty or was never collected, the question closes and the ten strangers are the only interviews available.","linked":["G15"],"sources":["docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:35","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:36","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:112","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:141","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:146","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:479"]},{"id":"G18","cat":"Go-to-market & channels","sub":"Services funnel","weight":"high","q":"Do we sell the ₹3,00,000 engagement off the docs scan before the scan has run for anybody?","lede":"Services fund the company, so this funnel matters more than the product's revenue, and it is the least evidenced thing in the plan.","visual":{"kind":"flow","perRow":4,"nodes":[{"label":"Team runs the free docs scan","note":"F7: ten engineering days, unbuilt","tone":"warn"},{"label":"Scan returns stale docs, broken links","note":"more than one person will work through"},{"label":"That list is the brief","note":"the §18 upsell moment","tone":"accent"},{"label":"₹3,00,000 fixed scope","note":"no team has ever done this","tone":"stop"}],"note":"F7 sits behind 24 days of fix-first, at 1.21 engineering days a calendar week.","caption":"The one bridge between studio and product, both ends unbuilt."},"stakes":"The diagnostic meant to generate the leads will not exist for months, and the nut is monthly.","state":["§19's diagram makes the docs scan the diagnostic for a ₹3,00,000 engagement (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:465).","§19 calls it the one place where the consultancy and the product are the same funnel (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:482).","§18 lists it as the services upsell moment (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:445).","The gap register calls it a design presented with the confidence of a finding (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:56)."],"path":["It was designed as the bridge between the studio and the product.","Nobody has tested whether a team that runs a scan wants an engagement.","The record holds no data on the studio's conversion from any productised diagnostic."],"tension":["F7 is ten engineering days behind twenty-four days of fix-first work (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:227).","At 1.21 engineering days a calendar week the scan is months away and the nut is about ₹1.09L a month.","Selling by hand now produces the missing conversion data before the feature exists.","The hours a hand-run scan consumes are the same hours the build needs."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"The funnel, and what stands behind it","items":[["Engagement price named in the plan","₹3,00,000 fixed scope","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:465"],["Monthly nut","about ₹1.09L, covered by 54–78 consulting hours","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:292"],["Evidence that a scan produces an engagement","None — untested","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:56"],["Studio's measured conversion from any productised diagnostic","No data in the record","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:56"],["When the scan ships","F7, 10 engineering days, after 24 days of fix-first work","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:227"],["Measured build rate","1.21 engineering days per calendar week; 0.23 in the last 30 days","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:227"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Sell the engagement now, with the scan run by hand","what":"The founder runs the diagnostic manually for a named team and quotes off it.","gains":["Revenue and the missing conversion data months before the feature","Tests the funnel where it is cheapest to be wrong"],"costs":["Consumes the hours the build also needs","A manual scan is not the product's scan","Two or three data points is all a quarter buys"],"system":"No change. The scan is done by hand.","screens":"None. A written report.","money":"₹3,00,000 per engagement against a ₹1.09L monthly nut."},{"k":"b","label":"Wait for the scan to ship before selling the engagement","what":"The funnel starts when F7 does.","gains":["Clean sequencing and one story to tell","The scan the client sees is the scan the product runs"],"costs":["Postpones the only revenue instrument in the plan","The nut is met from ordinary client work anyway meanwhile"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"No services revenue attributable to the product this year."},{"k":"c","label":"Sell a smaller paid diagnostic first, then price the larger engagement off it","what":"A fixed-fee docs audit as its own product.","gains":["Lowest-friction test of whether anyone buys the diagnosis at all","Produces cash inside the quarter"],"costs":["Anchors the studio at a low number the ₹3,00,000 figure must climb back from","A second offer to scope and deliver"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"A smaller fee, sooner, with an anchoring risk."},{"k":"d","label":"Drop the productised funnel; keep services as ordinary client work","what":"The two businesses stop being one funnel.","gains":["Removes an unevidenced claim from the plan","Client work stays scheduled the way it already is"],"costs":["Gives up the one place the product and the studio connect","§19's family diagram loses its bottom half"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"Services continue unchanged."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["The conversion claim can be tested by hand today and cannot be tested at all until F7 ships.","Two hand-run scans cost less than the plan currently spends asserting the funnel works.","It is the only item in this area that produces cash rather than spending it."],"flip":"If two hand-run scans in a month produce no engagement conversation, the funnel is a design and should leave the plan.","linked":["F7","G22"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:445","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:465","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:482","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:292","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:227","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:56"]},{"id":"G20","cat":"Go-to-market & channels","sub":"Owned surfaces","weight":"high","q":"Do we build the public frontmatter validator?","lede":"It is the only channel whose ceiling matches the size of the substrate, and it is in no version of the plan.","visual":{"kind":"ba","before":{"title":"Built today","lines":[{"t":"Refuses 83% of the seven pinned vaults","mark":"stop"},{"t":"NF-1: a column-zero list item in frontmatter","mark":"warn"},{"t":"The first thing a visitor sees is our defect rate","mark":"stop"},{"t":"§58 forbids publishing that as coverage anyway","mark":"warn"}]},"after":{"title":"Built after NF-1 and NF-3","lines":[{"t":"Seven of the twenty-four fix-first days","mark":"warn"},{"t":"The page shows the engine at its best","mark":"good"},{"t":"Client-side only, verifiable in the network tab","mark":"good"},{"t":"The search intent is unchanged and waiting","mark":"good"}]},"via":"7 days","caption":"The build order matters more here than the build."},"stakes":"It is the only lever in the corpus whose ceiling matches a 35-million-download-a-month substrate.","state":["The channel table does not mention it (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:300).","The research names it the one asymmetric move on the keyword map (r17-h7:72).","It is estimated at 30k–150k year-one visitors, the highest-variance line on that table (r17-h7:145).","The engine refuses 83% of real vaults today on the NF-1 defect (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:214)."],"path":["It came out of the SEO work, which earlier rounds never covered.","The plan was rewritten around channels rather than around search, so it never entered.","NF-1 and NF-3 are already the first two rows of fix-first, at four and three days."],"tension":["It must never send document content to a server, and that has to be visible in the network tab (r17-h7:72).","A validator built today shows a refusal rate §58 forbids publishing as a coverage claim.","That 83% is measured on seven Obsidian vaults; a paste box samples a different population entirely (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:514).","Fix-first is twenty-four engineering days away at 1.21 days a calendar week."],"evidence":[{"type":"bars","title":"Year-one visitor contribution by channel, optimistic end of each research estimate","note":"From the channel table at docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r17-h7-content-seo-distribution.md:144-151. Everything on that table sums to perhaps 350k–500k in year one (r17-h7:153). The ~1,260,000 visitor figure for ₹20L/month (r17-h7:8) is a 24-to-36-month cumulative number, not a year-one target.","unit":"visitors, optimistic end","data":[["Organic, marketing site",200000],["The free validator",150000],["Launch platforms (HN, Reddit)",100000],["Content, 24 pieces",60000],["Published-page organic",0]]},{"type":"stat","title":"Why the ceiling is the right order of magnitude — and the risk","items":[["gray-matter npm downloads per month","35,782,000 per r17-h7:9; independently recorded at 35,124,859 in docs/CRITIQUE.md:1728 — same order, two counts"],["front-matter npm downloads per month","3,041,000","r17-h7:10"],["Query the validator targets","\"yaml frontmatter invalid / parse error\" — problem-aware, huge latent volume, our strongest asset","r17-h7:69"],["Hard constraint","Client-side only, stated on the page, verifiable in the network tab","r17-h7:72"],["What it would currently reveal","The engine refuses 83% of real vaults on the NF-1 zero-indent defect","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:214"],["A second caveat on that number","It is measured on seven Obsidian vaults, one wiki being 77% of the files — a validator taking arbitrary pasted documents samples a different population","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:514"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Build it after NF-1 and NF-3 land","what":"Seven engineering days of fixes, then the page.","gains":["The validator shows the engine at its best","The refusal rate stops being the headline of our own page","The search intent does not expire"],"costs":["The channel starts three to six months later than it could","Fix-first is twenty-four days away at the measured rate"],"system":"NF-1 and NF-3 first; then a client-side build of the engine.","screens":"One page: paste, verdict, the byte that broke it.","money":"Seven engineering days already in the plan, plus the page."},{"k":"b","label":"Build it now; the refusal is the point","what":"A validator that refuses honestly, defects and all.","gains":["Fastest route to a channel that compounds","Refusing honestly is the product's own claim"],"costs":["The first thing a visitor sees is our defect rate","§58 forbids publishing it as a coverage percentage","Competes with fix-first for the same days"],"system":"A client-side build of the engine as it stands.","screens":"Same page, worse verdicts.","money":"The page, ahead of the fixes."},{"k":"c","label":"Do not build it; the plan is already over capacity","what":"No validator this year.","gains":["Protects the build entirely","No page whose first verdict is our own defect"],"costs":["Removes the only lever of the right order of magnitude","Nothing else in the table compounds"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Ship it as a CLI or npm package instead of a page","what":"The same check, distributed through the package registry.","gains":["Reaches developers where they already are","No hosting and no page to maintain"],"costs":["Forfeits the search intent, which is the entire reason the page exists","A public package is a support commitment nobody budgeted"],"system":"A published package with its own release process.","screens":"None.","money":"Maintenance of a public package."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["NF-1 and NF-3 are already the first two rows of fix-first, so the sequencing costs nothing extra.","A page whose first impression is our own defect rate is a worse asset than no page.","The search intent behind it is not seasonal and will still be there in a quarter."],"flip":"If NF-1 and NF-3 slip past a quarter, a validator that names the byte it refused is still a better page than no page.","linked":["E9","G22","G9"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:214","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:514","docs/CRITIQUE.md:1728","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r17-h7-content-seo-distribution.md:8","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r17-h7-content-seo-distribution.md:9","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r17-h7-content-seo-distribution.md:69","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r17-h7-content-seo-distribution.md:72","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r17-h7-content-seo-distribution.md:145"]},{"id":"G26","cat":"Go-to-market & channels","sub":"Allocation","weight":"high","q":"Do we write down that organic discovery contributes nothing in year one?","lede":"Two of the eight dead products in the graveyard died with nobody noticing, and one of them had raised $45M.","visual":{"kind":"timeline","items":[{"when":"May 2020","label":"Almanac's \"GitHub for Docs\" Show HN","note":"6 points, no comments","tone":"warn"},{"when":"Sep 2021","label":"$34M Series A, Tiger Global","note":"$45M raised in all","tone":"neutral"},{"when":"Jan 2025","label":"Almanac switched off","note":"cause stated as capacity, not demand","tone":"stop"},{"when":"Jul 2026","label":"petergyang/human-review published","note":"a free markdown review skill","tone":"neutral"},{"when":"Sep 2026","label":"1,241 stars in six weeks","note":"attention, with payment unmeasured","tone":"accent"}],"note":"Editorially closed in 2014: \"Even if all of our users paid up, it wouldn't be enough.\"","caption":"Money did not buy attention here. Free did. Neither is a plan."},"stakes":"If the plan quietly assumes any organic discovery, every channel number in it is optimistic by that whole amount.","state":["§23 lists \"every channel borrowed\" as a weakness (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:558).","No section states what organic discovery contributes; the research puts published-page organic at about zero (r17-h7:147).","Organic search is back-loaded to months 9 to 18 and cannot carry a launch (r17-h7:144).","Everything on the channel table, summed optimistically, reaches 350k–500k year-one visitors (r17-h7:153)."],"path":["The channel table was built by ranking channels, not by asking what happens if none of them fires.","Today's graveyard lens supplies the control: Almanac's own 2020 Show HN scored 6 points with no comments.","Draft has served 503 people since April 2023 and drawn no Hacker News comment at all.","Both products died anyway, and the category did not notice either."],"tension":["Free artefacts do get attention here: human-review went from nothing to 1,241 stars in six weeks.","Attention is not payment, and nothing in that repository's numbers says anyone would pay for it.","1.4% of the 1,000 most recent Show HN posts reach 100 points, and a spike decays to zero in 96 hours.","A plan whose only channel is hand recruitment is honest, and it does not compound."],"evidence":[],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"State that organic discovery contributes zero in year one, and budget nothing","what":"One paragraph, and every other channel number becomes a claim about hand-made effort.","gains":["Makes the rest of the table falsifiable rather than optimistic","Costs a paragraph","Removes the assumption that a good product gets found"],"costs":["Reads as pessimism to anyone who has not seen the graveyard","Nothing is being built that compounds"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None. It removes an implicit revenue assumption."},{"k":"b","label":"Keep the channel table as a ranking and add no such statement","what":"The plan stays as it is.","gains":["No argument to have","The table reads as a plan rather than a warning"],"costs":["The optimism stays hidden inside eight rows","Nobody can tell which number depends on being found"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Budget for organic on the research's own numbers, back-loaded to months 9 to 18","what":"Fifty to two hundred thousand cumulative visitors, arriving late.","gains":["Uses the research rather than a graveyard anecdote","Gives content hours a stated return to be judged against"],"costs":["Nothing arrives inside the decision window this plan lives in","It still assumes we are found"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"Commits content hours against a return in year two."},{"k":"d","label":"Make a free artefact the discovery plan: publish a skill and see if it travels","what":"Copy the one thing measured to travel in this category in 2026.","gains":["The only observed mechanism that produced attention from nothing","Reuses the engine we already have"],"costs":["Trains the audience that this is free","Says nothing about willingness to pay","Competes with fix-first for the same days"],"system":"A published package or skill with its own release process.","screens":"None.","money":"Engineering days against unmeasured payment."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["The two products in the graveyard that nobody noticed had no channel written down either.","Writing the zero down is what makes every other number in the table checkable.","The alternative that has evidence, option (d), buys attention rather than payment, which is the thing already in surplus."],"flip":"If a free artefact of ours draws a thousand stars in six weeks, discovery is real for artefacts and the statement needs a carve-out for them.","linked":["G22","G4"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:558","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r17-h7-content-seo-distribution.md:144","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r17-h7-content-seo-distribution.md:147","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r17-h7-content-seo-distribution.md:153","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r25-w4-retention-and-growth.md:82","https://get.almanac.io/go-forward","https://hn.algolia.com/api/v1/items/23339147","https://api.github.com/repos/petergyang/human-review","http://stet.editorially.com/articles/goodbye/","research briefing 2026-09-09, graveyard lens: Draft, 503 served since April 2023"]},{"id":"G4","cat":"Go-to-market & channels","sub":"Launch events","weight":"medium","q":"Do we spend the one Show HN shot at the MVP-0 exit, and does Product Hunt stay on the table?","lede":"Show HN is the only launch event left, and the plan sizes it with two anecdotes that appear nowhere else in the corpus.","visual":{"kind":"funnel","steps":[{"label":"Show HN posts, \"markdown editor\", 12 months","n":187,"unit":"posts","tone":"neutral"},{"label":"Cleared 50 points","n":12,"unit":"posts","tone":"warn"},{"label":"Cleared 100 points","n":7,"unit":"posts","tone":"stop"}],"note":"docs/CRITIQUE.md:1195. Every spike decays to zero in 96 hours.","caption":"What one Show HN in this category is worth, over twelve months."},"stakes":"One shot spent on the wrong title or the wrong week buys a 96-hour spike and nothing that lasts.","state":["§12 puts Show HN at the MVP-0 exit, one shot after 6 of 10, sized as \"Zed's scored 43, Cursor's 9\" (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:309).","Those two figures appear nowhere else in the docs tree. Five measured distributions do.","§12 keeps Product Hunt at MVP-1 as \"unchanged\" (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:310); the record excludes it in terms (docs/THESIS.md:752).","The corpus rule is never to put \"markdown editor\" in the title (docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:2533)."],"path":["Show HN entered the record as a single event, not a channel (docs/THESIS.md:750).","Product Hunt came from an early plan, was never re-examined, and its sweep was never run.","Today's graveyard lens adds the sharpest data point against a launch: Almanac's own 2020 \"GitHub for Docs\" Show HN scored 6 points with no comments."],"tension":["31% of the posts that cleared 50 points carry \"free\", \"open source\" or \"self-host\" in the title (docs/CRITIQUE.md:1728).","Our individual tier genuinely is free forever with no signup, so the title that works is also true.","A free title invites the free-alternatives thread, against a price floor of seven maintained editors at $0.","Product Hunt was excluded on an argument about paid acquisition, which does not cover a free launch day."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"Every Show HN measurement in the corpus, against the plan's sizing","cols":["Sample","n","Median points","Hit rate","Source"],"rows":[["\"markdown editor\", last 12 months","187","2","7 clear 100 = 3.7%; 12 clear 50 = 6.4%","docs/CRITIQUE.md:1195"],["\"markdown editor\", re-counted all-time","386","3","5.7% reach 100; 44% score ≤2","docs/CRITIQUE.md:1728"],["\"markdown editor\", r25-w3 count","609","3","—","docs/CRITIQUE.md:52"],["\"markdown editor\", 2024-08-18 → 2026-08-30","235","—","10 clear 100 = 4.3%; ~9.8 launches/month","docs/BUSINESS.md:1264"],["1,000 most recent Show HN, all topics","1,000","2","1.4% reach 100; 0.1% reach 500","r25-w4:82"],["The plan's own sizing","2","—","Zed 43, Cursor 9","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:309 — the only occurrence in the docs tree"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"What correlates with winning in this category","items":[["Of the 42 posts that cleared 50 points in 12 months, share with \"open source\"/\"self-host\"/\"free\" in the title","31% — and the top four all do","docs/CRITIQUE.md:1728"],["Of the 10 that cleared 100 in two years, how many announce free or open source in the title","Five products across six posts — OverType 471, OpenKnowledge 381, Rowboat twice at 219 and 205, Write.md 107, Ephe 143","docs/BUSINESS.md:1264"],["Spike decay","to zero in 96 hours","docs/BUSINESS.md:1082"],["Corpus rule on the category noun","\"Never say markdown editor\" — every Show HN with that name becomes a thread of free alternatives","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:2533"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"What the corpus actually holds on Product Hunt","items":[["Record's channel list verdict","Explicitly excluded: \"Not on the list: Product Hunt, LinkedIn, paid anything\"","docs/THESIS.md:752"],["Plan's verdict","\"Product Hunt unchanged\" at MVP-1","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:310"],["Research coverage of Product Hunt","\"NOT ATTEMPTED\"","docs/mdmax/tree/13-appendix.md:747"],["Launch-platform contribution, all platforms combined, year 1","30k–100k visitors in spikes, decaying to zero in 96 hours","r17-h7:149"],["What the exclusion was reasoned from","A ₹599 product cannot fund paid acquisition at any CAC a two-founder Indian company can absorb — an argument about paid, not about a free launch day","docs/THESIS.md:752"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"One shot at the MVP-0 exit, titled on the refusals","what":"No plugins, no code execution, no hosting, your key.","gains":["Differentiated against everything else in the list","Nobody else can claim it without admitting a backlash"],"costs":["Refusals are abstract to a stranger scrolling","Two of the five are currently disprovable","No measured winner reads like this"],"system":"No change.","screens":"A launch page built around the refusal list.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"One shot at the MVP-0 exit, titled on free; cut Product Hunt","what":"Lead the title with the free tier and drop the launch event the record already excluded.","gains":["Matches the only measured predictor of clearing 50 points","Honest: the individual tier is free with no signup","Removes an unevidenced row from the table"],"costs":["Invites the free-alternatives thread the record warns about","Forgoes a launch day that reaches non-developers"],"system":"No change.","screens":"A launch page whose first line is the free tier.","money":"None. It advertises the free tier, not a price."},{"k":"c","label":"Post at the end of the two-week test instead","what":"Use Show HN as a demand instrument rather than a launch.","gains":["A signal months earlier","Costs nothing to run"],"costs":["Burns the one shot on a mock","Cannot be repeated on the real product"],"system":"No change.","screens":"The mock becomes the landing page.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Do not post at all; put the hours into hand recruitment","what":"No launch event this year.","gains":["Every hour goes to the only channel that produces named humans","No thread to manage and no free-alternatives argument to have"],"costs":["Loses a free 30k–100k spike at 1.4–5.7% odds","Loses the credibility a good thread confers on a solo founder"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["Free is the one title feature that measurably correlates with clearing 50 points in this category.","The two figures the plan sizes the shot with exist in one row of one document and nowhere else.","Product Hunt has no evidence on either side, and the one place that treated it as a decision excluded it."],"flip":"If the twenty team conversations name a paying buyer who does not read Hacker News, the shot is better spent on a written case study.","linked":["G22"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:309","docs/CRITIQUE.md:1195","docs/CRITIQUE.md:1728","docs/CRITIQUE.md:52","docs/BUSINESS.md:1264","docs/BUSINESS.md:1082","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:2533","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r25-w4-retention-and-growth.md:82","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:310","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:227","docs/THESIS.md:752","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:11918","merged: G5","https://hn.algolia.com/api/v1/items/23339147"]},{"id":"G9","cat":"Go-to-market & channels","sub":"Owned surfaces","weight":"medium","q":"Do we publish the research, which slice, and at what rate?","lede":"It is the only channel available now that needs nobody's permission, and its measured supply is two posts ever.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":150,"cols":[{"title":"Engine measurements","tone":"accent"},{"title":"Market research","tone":"warn"},{"title":"Nothing yet","tone":"sunk"}],"rows":[{"label":"What one post costs","cells":["About 90 minutes; the build produces it","Re-derive every third-party number first","Nothing"]},{"label":"Who reads it","cells":["Engineers","Anyone tracking the category","Nobody"]},{"label":"What §58 permits","cells":["Yes, as a defect report, never as coverage","Only re-derived figures","Not applicable"]},{"label":"Cadence it can hold","cells":["A by-product of the build","Six to eight hours a fortnight","None"]}],"note":"Measured density is 1.21 engineering days a calendar week, 0.23 over the last thirty.","caption":"Which slice, and whether any cadence survives the measured build rate."},"stakes":"A cadence a solo founder cannot hold is worse than none, because the failure mode is a burst then months of silence.","state":["§12 lists published research as available now, unpublished, sized as \"the 157-source dataset\" (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:308).","Counted 2026-09-09: 235 report files and about 823,000 words under docs/research.","The \"157 sources\" traces to a verification round's source count, not to a publishable dataset.","Two marketing posts have ever shipped, one carrying a visible defect since 2026-08-10 (r17-h7:7)."],"path":["Two weeks of research produced a large corpus and no publication.","An earlier plan set a weekly cadence off a campaign system that shipped ten episodes in about a week.","The follow-up measurement found the supply was real and the shipping was not."],"tension":["Engine findings cost about 90 minutes because the build already produces them (r17-h7:28).","Content's year-one contribution is 20k–60k visitors, back-loaded to months 9 to 18 (r17-h7:144, :146).","§58 forbids publishing our own coverage percentage while the 83% refusal stands (docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:5022).","The proposed biweekly cadence with a bank of two commits six to eight hours a fortnight that fix-first also wants."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"What there is to publish, and what has shipped","items":[["Report files under docs/research","235 (counted 2026-09-09)"],["Words across those files","about 823,000 (counted 2026-09-09)"],["What \"157 sources\" actually refers to","The v12 plan's own line, \"I checked it against 157 sources this week\" — a verification count, not a dataset","docs/frontmatter-PILOT-PLAN-v12-2026-09-07-0756.print.html:86"],["Marketing posts ever shipped","2, one defective since 2026-08-10","r17-h7:7"],["Cost of a corpus post, from data the engine already produces","about 90 minutes","r17-h7:28"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"Engine findings that are publishable today, and the caveat each must carry","items":[["Zero-indent-sequence refusals across foreign vaults","83% of real vaults refused","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:214"],["Corpus the engine is verified on","8,513 third-party files, 7 vaults, 0 corruption, 0 throws — §58 names this as a may-say","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:5022"],["The caveat the plan itself attaches","Those 7 vaults are all Obsidian and one wiki is 77% of the 8,513 files — the refusal rate is a property of those vaults, not of markdown in the wild","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:514"],["Non-locality — same ten bytes, two meanings","Measured across four CommonMark engines, unanimous in both directions","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:510"],["Carrier finding","An unclosed fence swallows the document; a callout has no closer to lose — tested on four engines and GitHub","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:500"],["What §58 forbids here","Publishing our own fidelity or coverage percentage while the 83% refusal stands — so the refusal rate may be published as a defect report, never as a coverage claim","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:5022"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"Supply, shipping and capacity","items":[["Marketing posts ever shipped","2 — one with a visible defect since 2026-08-10","r17-h7:7"],["Cost of a corpus post from data the engine already produces","about 90 minutes","r17-h7:28"],["Proposed cadence","1 substantial piece per 2 weeks + 1 shallow in the off-week, bank of 2","r17-h7:19"],["Measured engineering days per calendar week","1.21; last 30 days 0.23; sibling repo's best-ever regime 1.91","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:227"],["Content's year-1 direct contribution at 24 pieces","20k–60k visitors; \"its real value is link acquisition and sales-page support, not raw traffic\"","r17-h7:146"],["When organic starts to matter at all","Back-loaded to months 9–18","r17-h7:144"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Engine measurements only, published when the build produces one","what":"The carrier finding and non-locality, with the refusal rate framed as a defect report.","gains":["Everything is ours and re-derivable","Cannot be missed, because nothing is scheduled","Supply really is a by-product of the build"],"costs":["Reaches engineers and nobody else","Gives search nothing predictable to crawl","Invisible to anyone tracking the channel"],"system":"No change. The engine already emits the numbers.","screens":"A research index on the marketing site.","money":"About 90 minutes a post."},{"k":"b","label":"Engine measurements on the biweekly-plus-bank cadence as written","what":"One substantial piece a fortnight, one shallow piece in the off-week, never publishing below a bank of two.","gains":["The most durable design in the corpus","Builds an internal link graph search can use"],"costs":["Commits six to eight hours a fortnight the build wants","At 0.23 engineering days a week it breaks in month one"],"system":"No change.","screens":"Same index, with dates.","money":"Six to eight founder-hours a fortnight."},{"k":"c","label":"Publish the market research too, after re-deriving every third-party number","what":"The refuted headlines and the install counts, verified again first.","gains":["The most interesting reading in the corpus","Draws links from people writing about the category"],"costs":["Several figures have a single source and must be re-derived","Publishes numbers about other people's products"],"system":"No change.","screens":"Same index.","money":"A day of re-derivation before the first post."},{"k":"d","label":"Publish nothing until the two-week test returns","what":"No owned channel this quarter.","gains":["Every hour goes to the test and the build","Nothing published that a later round has to withdraw"],"costs":["Loses three months on a channel that needs nine to eighteen to work","The corpus keeps growing and nobody outside sees any of it"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["The engine produces these numbers whether or not anybody writes them up, so the supply is genuinely free.","At 0.23 engineering days a week, a fortnightly commitment fails in its first month and the failure is public.","§58 already constrains how the refusal rate may be phrased, and a defect report is the phrasing it permits."],"flip":"If two engine posts in a quarter draw no links at all, the by-product is not worth the ninety minutes and the channel closes.","linked":["G20","G22"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:308","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:214","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:500","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:510","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:514","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:5022","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r17-h7-content-seo-distribution.md:7","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r17-h7-content-seo-distribution.md:28","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:227","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r17-h7-content-seo-distribution.md:19","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r17-h7-content-seo-distribution.md:144","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r17-h7-content-seo-distribution.md:146","merged: G19"]},{"id":"G12","cat":"Go-to-market & channels","sub":"Published pages","weight":"medium","q":"Do exported and shared pages carry a frontmatter mark?","lede":"The plan defers this until measured, and a mark already ships on one of the two surfaces with nobody having decided it.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":170,"cols":[{"title":"Our hosted note","tone":"warn"},{"title":"A page they deployed","tone":"stop"}],"rows":[{"label":"Whose domain","cells":["frontmatter.in","Theirs"]},{"label":"Mark today","cells":["\"Hosted on frontmatter.in\" footer","None, in 945 lines of export code"]},{"label":"Which research objection bites","cells":["Only file-is-truth: markup with no byte in the file","All three, including the link-scheme pattern"]},{"label":"Who decided it","cells":["Nobody. It arrived with the feature","§12 defers it as unmeasurable"]}],"note":"The research objects to a backlink on a user's own page. Only one column is that.","caption":"One mark ships unreviewed; the other is deferred as immeasurable."},"stakes":"An unreviewed footer on our own surface sits beside a deferred decision about somebody else's, and the two were never separated.","state":["§12 lists exported pages with a mark at MVP-2 as \"not a channel until measured\" (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:311).","The hosted public note already carries a \"Hosted on frontmatter.in\" footer (src/modules/share/presentation/PublicNoteView.tsx:30).","Checked 2026-09-09: the 945-line export module carries no mark of any kind.","The research position is no automatic backlink to our site from user pages (r17-h7:111)."],"path":["The footer came with the share feature and sits on our own domain.","The channel row came from a later analysis about pages a user deploys to their own domain.","The export cut was decided on Obsidian plugin-download ratios, a note-taker population (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:60)."],"tension":["The research's first two reasons describe a link on a user's own domain, which does not exist yet.","The third bites today: the footer is markup we inject with no representative in the user's file.","Developers deploy from repositories at scale, so the denominator behind the export cut was the wrong one (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:60).","Counting a deploy on somebody else's page is exactly what the telemetry position forbids."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"The two surfaces, and what the research actually objects to","items":[["Mark on the hosted public note","\"Hosted on frontmatter.in\", href=\"/\" — same domain as the note itself","src/modules/share/presentation/PublicNoteView.tsx:29"],["Mark on exported output","None — no mark anywhere in the 945-line export module (checked 2026-09-09)"],["Research position","\"No automatic backlink to our marketing site from user pages\"","r17-h7:111"],["Reasons given","The user's page becomes an advertisement they did not agree to run; tens of thousands of identical footer links is the classic link-scheme pattern; it contradicts file-is-truth because the footer is markup we inject with no representative in the user's file","r17-h7:113"],["Whether those reasons bite today","Only the third does. The first two describe a link on a user's own domain, which does not exist yet — every shared note is served from ours"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"The population the export cut was decided on","items":[["What the cut used","Obsidian plugin-download ratios — a note-taker population","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:60"],["What the refuter counted instead","443,392 root CNAME files; 113,536 astro configs","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:60"],["Gap register's verdict","\"The cut may be right for the wrong reason\"","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:60"],["Export code that already exists","Single-document export, 945 lines, wired, never run","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:133"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"No mark anywhere; remove the shipped footer too","what":"Nothing of ours appears on a page a reader opens.","gains":["Cleanest against the file-is-truth position","Nothing to opt out of"],"costs":["Forfeits the loop entirely","The §12 row should then be deleted rather than deferred"],"system":"Remove the footer from PublicNoteView.","screens":"The public note loses its footer.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Keep the footer, add a linked mark on exported pages, add an opt-out","what":"Both surfaces carry a mark, and settings can turn it off.","gains":["Keeps the loop with an escape hatch","Both surfaces finally say the same thing"],"costs":["The exported half is the one the research warns carries devaluation risk","Those links do sit on someone else's domain"],"system":"A mark in the export module and a settings toggle.","screens":"A settings row; a footer in exported HTML.","money":"Unmeasured. There is no deploy count."},{"k":"c","label":"Keep the hosted footer; a small unlinked wordmark on exports, off by default","what":"The research's own compromise, applied where its objection actually bites.","gains":["Leaves the shipped surface alone","No link scheme, because nothing is linked"],"costs":["Weakest growth effect of the three","Still injects markup with no representative in the file"],"system":"An optional wordmark in the export module.","screens":"A settings row, off by default.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Keep both marks and add a deploy counter so the channel is measurable","what":"Turns \"not a channel until measured\" into something measured.","gains":["Makes the §12 row falsifiable","Answers whether exported pages are a channel at all"],"costs":["Counts an event on a user's page, which the telemetry position forbids","Requires running a service for a channel of unknown size"],"system":"A counter endpoint we would have to run.","screens":"A dashboard nobody asked for.","money":"A server cost against a channel of unknown size."}],"rec":"c","recCase":["The objection the research actually makes is about somebody else's domain, and only the export half is that.","An unlinked wordmark cannot form the link-scheme pattern it warns about.","It leaves a shipped surface alone rather than deleting it in the same round as G10."],"flip":"If a custom-domain deploy path ships, an exported mark lands on somebody else's domain and the first two objections start to bite.","linked":["L6"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:311","src/modules/share/presentation/PublicNoteView.tsx:29","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r17-h7-content-seo-distribution.md:111","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r17-h7-content-seo-distribution.md:113","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:60","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:133"]},{"id":"G23","cat":"Go-to-market & channels","sub":"Loops","weight":"medium","q":"Do we ship the invite-only referral, or keep referral banned?","lede":"Referral sits in a banned list beside streaks and XP, and the research says it was banned by adjacency rather than argument.","visual":{"kind":"flow","perRow":4,"nodes":[{"label":"A second person opens the repo","note":"the moment the product can see","tone":"neutral"},{"label":"Invite link to a document","note":"the inviter gets nothing"},{"label":"Invitee lands on the document","note":"no signup wall","tone":"accent"},{"label":"Shared review state","note":"F10, MVP-1","tone":"warn"}],"note":"No credits, free months, leaderboards, counts or notifications.","caption":"The only referral shape consistent with the stated positions."},"stakes":"Shipping it early points the invitee at the public route this plan may be about to delete.","state":["Referral appears nowhere in the channel table or the upsell section (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:300, :437).","The research verdict is one form only: a workspace invite giving the inviter nothing (r17-h7:132).","The mechanic is an invite link to a document, landing on the readable document with no wall (r17-h7:134).","The team surface to invite into is F10, at MVP-1 (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:200)."],"path":["An earlier banned-patterns list grouped referral with streaks, badges and XP.","The research separates them: gamification manipulates a user's own work, a referral is a transaction between two people (r17-h7:119).","Nothing has been built either way, so the ban has never cost anything yet."],"tension":["The research says our version will underperform two-sided rewards, probably substantially (r17-h7:138).","There is no team surface until MVP-1, so today there is nothing to invite anyone into.","The landing surface would be the public route G10 is deciding.","The abandon threshold is already named: measured k below 0.03 after six months (r17-h7:138)."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"What referral is worth against the visitor requirement","cols":["Scenario","k-factor","Visitors still required for ₹20L/mo"],"rows":[["No referral","0","1,260,000"],["5% of free signups refer 1 who signs up","0.05","~1,200,000"],["10% refer 1","0.10","The source gives both ~1,150,000 in its table and 1,134,000 in its derivation — the stated saving of ~126,000 belongs to the second"],["20% refer 1 (optimistic ceiling, no cash incentive)","0.20","~1,050,000"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"The design and its limits","items":[["Proposed mechanic","An invite link to a document or workspace; the recipient lands on the readable document with no signup wall","r17-h7:134"],["The reward","The invitee's first five minutes are better; the inviter gets nothing","r17-h7:132"],["Explicitly excluded","Credits, free months, leaderboards, referral counts, notifications","r17-h7:132"],["Honest limitation","\"Ours will underperform two-sided rewards, probably substantially\"","r17-h7:138"],["Abandon threshold named by the research","Measured k below 0.03 after six months","r17-h7:138"],["When a team surface exists to invite into","MVP-1 — F10 shared review state and comments","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:200"],["Where the invitee would currently land","The public-note route, which is exactly what G10 and G11 are deciding"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Ship the invite form at MVP-1, when shared review state exists","what":"The invite becomes a work action rather than a growth mechanism.","gains":["The only version consistent with the product's stated positions","Lands on a surface that exists by then"],"costs":["Nothing happens for months","Underperforms two-sided rewards by design"],"system":"An invite token against shared review state.","screens":"An invite dialogue inside the review panel.","money":"None. It creates seats, which is the paid tier."},{"k":"b","label":"Keep referral banned","what":"The banned list stands as written.","gains":["Consistent with the existing list and needs no argument","No invite surface to design or support"],"costs":["Forgoes the one loop the research endorses","The ban was inherited by adjacency, not reasoned"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Ship it at MVP-0 as a document share link","what":"Available immediately, on the public route.","gains":["Something to measure this quarter","The share link already exists in the shipped feature"],"costs":["Collides directly with G10's hosting decision","The landing surface may not survive that decision"],"system":"Depends on the public route surviving G10.","screens":"A share dialogue.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Decide after the twenty team conversations","what":"Let the buyer say whether the invite is a real work action.","gains":["Costs nothing, since MVP-1 is the earliest build point anyway","The answer arrives before anything is built"],"costs":["One more open item carried into the build","Nothing measurable happens either way this quarter"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["MVP-1 is the first point at which there is anything to invite somebody into.","An invite that rewards the inviter is the pattern the banned list exists to keep out; this one does not.","It creates seats, which is the tier the whole price hypothesis rests on."],"flip":"If the twenty team conversations describe the invite as how work already starts, it belongs in MVP-0 and not MVP-1.","linked":["G15"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:200","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:437","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r17-h7-content-seo-distribution.md:119","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r17-h7-content-seo-distribution.md:130","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r17-h7-content-seo-distribution.md:132","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r17-h7-content-seo-distribution.md:134","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r17-h7-content-seo-distribution.md:138"]},{"id":"G24","cat":"Go-to-market & channels","sub":"Toolchains","weight":"medium","q":"Is plan mode really demoted, given it out-scores both named toolchains by two orders of magnitude?","lede":"The plan demotes the highest-attention population in the market on a file location that may be a one-line setting.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":150,"cols":[{"title":"Plan mode","tone":"accent"},{"title":"superpowers","tone":"neutral"},{"title":"spec-kit","tone":"neutral"}],"rows":[{"label":"Best Reddit score","cells":["1,776","38 or fewer","38 or fewer"]},{"label":"Where it writes","cells":["~/.claude/plans, outside the repo","Inside the repo, committed","Inside the repo"]},{"label":"File lifetime","cells":["Deleted after 30 days","Git","Git"]},{"label":"What we would ship","cells":["A plansDirectory recipe","A README line","A README line"]},{"label":"Cost to settle it","cells":["One hour, still unspent","Done","Done"]}],"note":"Exhibit 3 says the file location is untested; §12 demotes the channel on that location.","caption":"The largest attention pool, demoted on a detail nobody has checked."},"stakes":"We walk away from the biggest audience in the market on an unverified detail that costs an hour to verify.","state":["§12 demotes plan mode to at most a plansDirectory onboarding step (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:307).","Exhibit 3 records that plan mode out-scores both named tools on Reddit and that where the files live is untested (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:149).","The gap register priced the check at one hour before round 2 (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:40).","Round 2 ran the toolchains and found where each writes (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:126)."],"path":["Round 2 found plan mode writes outside the repository and deletes after thirty days.","That disqualified it under the working-tree framing before anyone checked whether the location is configurable.","§12 names the setting that would decide it and does not report having tried it."],"tension":["The plan carries two statements about the same channel in two sections.","Even inside a repository, a thirty-day deletion means the review anchor outlives the document it anchors to.","The artefact is small: a settings snippet and a paragraph.","One hour settles it, and blocks nothing while it is spent."],"evidence":[{"type":"bars","title":"Reddit attention: plan mode against the two named toolchains","note":"Recorded at docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:149. Points on the three highest-scoring plan-mode posts, against the best score for either named tool.","unit":"Reddit points","data":[["Plan mode, post 1",1776],["Plan mode, post 2",1409],["Plan mode, post 3",1329],["Best for superpowers or spec-kit",38]]},{"type":"stat","title":"Why it was demoted, and what is unchecked","items":[["Where plan mode writes","~/.claude/plans/<slug>.md — outside the repo","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:307"],["Retention of those files","Deleted after 30 days","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:307"],["The setting §12 names","plansDirectory","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:307"],["Whether it can point inside a repository","Untested — \"Where the files live is untested\"","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:149"],["What the gap register said before round 2","\"Plan mode out-scores the named toolchains on Reddit; where its files live decides whether they are a channel. One hour\"","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:40"],["Second unchecked leg","Even inside the repo, a 30-day deletion means the review anchor would outlive the document it anchors to"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Keep it demoted to an onboarding step","what":"A line in the docs and no channel.","gains":["Consistent with the working-tree framing","No hour spent and no recipe to maintain"],"costs":["Walks away from the largest attention pool on an unverified detail","Leaves two plan sections disagreeing"],"system":"No change.","screens":"An onboarding step.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Promote it to a week-2 channel and ship a plansDirectory recipe","what":"A settings snippet and a paragraph, published now.","gains":["Reaches the biggest population with the smallest artefact","No maintainer's permission required"],"costs":["Fails entirely if the setting cannot point into a repository","The 30-day deletion is a second unanswered problem"],"system":"No change. A documented setting.","screens":"One recipe page.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Spend the hour: confirm plansDirectory and the deletion behaviour, then decide","what":"One hour of testing, then promote or keep demoted on the answer.","gains":["Settles a two-section contradiction for an hour","Blocks nothing in the meantime"],"costs":["One more item on a week-0 list that is already long","The answer may simply confirm the demotion"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None yet.","money":"One hour."},{"k":"d","label":"Treat plan mode as a recruitment channel rather than a product channel","what":"Use the attention to find the ten strangers.","gains":["Uses the biggest pool for what the fortnight actually needs","No product claim to defend while the file question is open"],"costs":["Outbound into other people's communities","Still needs the file question answered before a product claim"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"c","recCase":["Two sections of the same document disagree, and one hour resolves which is right.","The attention gap is two orders of magnitude, which is worth an hour at any reading.","Nothing else waits on the answer, so spending the hour costs no schedule."],"flip":"If plansDirectory cannot point inside a repository, the demotion stands and the row should say so instead of naming the setting.","linked":["G22","G6"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:307","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:149","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:40","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:126"]},{"id":"G27","cat":"Go-to-market & channels","sub":"Adjacent audiences","weight":"medium","q":"Do we spend outreach on the git-backed CMS audience, where the review-shaped hole is already visible?","lede":"Pages CMS edits markdown in a repository, has no paid tier at all, and lists inline comments as \"Soon\".","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":170,"cols":[{"title":"Pages CMS","tone":"neutral"},{"title":"frontmatter","tone":"accent"}],"rows":[{"label":"What it is","cells":["Git-backed CMS for markdown, MIT","An editor over the same files"]},{"label":"Stars","cells":["3,976","Not published"]},{"label":"Price","cells":["No paid tier at all","Free individual; $4–5 team, untested"]},{"label":"Review","cells":["Inline comments listed as \"Soon\"","Review state is the product"]},{"label":"What the audience expects","cells":["Free","To be told why this is not"]}],"note":"Developers deploy from repositories at scale: 443,392 root CNAME files.","caption":"The right audience with the right hole, trained to expect it free."},"stakes":"It is the most reachable adjacent audience found and the one least likely to pay for filling its own gap.","state":["The channel table names no adjacent audience beyond the two agent toolchains (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:300).","Developers deploy from repositories at scale: 443,392 root CNAME files, 113,536 astro configs (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:60).","Pages CMS is MIT with 3,976 stars, no paid tier, and lists inline comments as \"Soon\".","The gap register calls the export cut right for the wrong reason, because it used a note-taker denominator (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:60)."],"path":["Earlier rounds sized markdown audiences on Obsidian plugin downloads, which measure note-takers.","Today's research opened the git-backed CMS shelf and found the review feature unshipped.","Nothing in the plan has ever named this audience."],"tension":["They already keep documents in a repository, so the sidecar needs no explaining at all.","There is no paid tier anywhere in view, so they are trained to expect this free.","Outreach hours here compete directly with the two toolchain maintainers in week 2.","Obsidian's shelf shows the same shape: agent-writing plugins outweigh the only review-shaped plugin roughly forty to one."],"evidence":[],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Add it as a week-3 channel with its own integration page","what":"A page addressed to people running a git-backed CMS.","gains":["The audience needs no education about repositories","The gap is visible and unfilled"],"costs":["Competes with the toolchain outreach for the same hours","An audience with no paid tier in view"],"system":"No change.","screens":"One integration page.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Ignore it; the audience does not pay","what":"The channel table stays as it is.","gains":["Protects week 2 for the toolchains","No new audience to learn or to write for"],"costs":["Gives up the only adjacency where the incumbent already names the hole","The hole stays open for whoever fills it first"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Use it as a recruitment pool for the ten strangers, not as a channel","what":"Their public repos join the code-search list, and nothing is published at them.","gains":["The fortnight needs named humans more than a channel","They already keep documents in a repository","No permission and no build"],"costs":["No compounding effect at all","Their expectations are set by a free tool"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Build the review feature Pages CMS lists as Soon, and offer it to them","what":"Fill somebody else's roadmap gap.","gains":["Directly addresses a stated need","The engine already does the hard part"],"costs":["Builds for a project that gives everything away","Ties our roadmap to their release schedule"],"system":"An integration against their storage model.","screens":"A view inside somebody else's product.","money":"Engineering days against an audience with no paid tier."}],"rec":"c","recCase":["The fortnight needs named humans, and these are people who already keep documents in a repository.","It costs no permission, no build and no channel hours.","Whether they would pay is exactly what the ten and the twenty are for."],"flip":"If a Pages CMS user in the pilot says they would pay, the audience is a channel and not only a recruitment pool.","linked":["G15","G22"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:300","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:60","https://pagescms.org/"]},{"id":"B1","cat":"Business & operations","sub":"Capacity","weight":"critical","q":"Do we strike the two-founder assumption from every number in the plan, or sign an agreement naming the second person, their start date and their hours?","lede":"Two governing documents give different answers, and every schedule, nut and break-even in the record is denominated in founders.","visual":{"kind":"ba","before":{"title":"The plan as written, two founders","lines":[{"t":"Monthly nut ₹1,08,918","mark":"warn"},{"t":"Default-alive at 501 paying users","mark":"warn"},{"t":"Client hours 54–78 a month","mark":"warn"},{"t":"Cumulative visitors 171,200","mark":"warn"},{"t":"Cost to the published calendar: zero","mark":"warn"}]},"after":{"title":"Re-derived at one founder","lines":[{"t":"Monthly nut ₹63,918","mark":"good"},{"t":"Default-alive at 294 paying users","mark":"good"},{"t":"Client hours 32.0–45.7 a month","mark":"good"},{"t":"Cumulative visitors 100,428","mark":"good"},{"t":"Cost to the calendar: a 1.46× stretch","mark":"stop"}]},"via":"strike the assumption","note":"Commit record: 80 of 80 here and 416 of 416 on the sibling, one author (PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:231).","caption":"Every downstream figure, re-derived at one founder"},"stakes":"Until this is settled no schedule, price or break-even in the plan can be quoted, because each moves by 41 to 70 per cent.","state":["The plan says one person: 80 of 80 commits here and 416 of 416 on the sibling, single author (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:231).","The decision layer says the opposite, settled 2026-08-31, two founders and a team (docs/DECIDE.md:156).","No signed agreement is in the repo. The critique set 2026-09-07 as the resolution date (docs/CRITIQUE.md:2100)."],"path":["The phrase entered the record once, in a session-pack constraint block pasted into a prompt (docs/CRITIQUE.md:1437).","Nine downstream reports then spent it on scope and capacity (docs/CRITIQUE.md:1447).","The one section with resourcing authority said one person and called it the binding constraint (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:231)."],"tension":["The nut moves 70 per cent, default-alive 41 per cent, and the calendar from zero cost to a 1.46× stretch (docs/CRITIQUE.md:1460).","The two-founder case is also the expensive one: a second draw doubles the nut from day one.","A decision written in a document does not create capacity. A signature with hours would, and there is not one."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"The commit record, re-counted 2026-09-08T18:27Z","items":[["frontmatter, this repo","82 of 82 commits, one author","git log --format='%an' | sort | uniq -c. The plan cites 80 of 80 at PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:231; two commits have landed since, both by the same author"],["Sibling md repo","416 of 416 commits, one author","git -C ../md log; matches PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:231 exactly"],["Cofounder named anywhere in the record","0","CRITIQUE.md:1437 — grep finds no cofounder in 16,189 lines"],["Signed founders' agreement in the repo","none found","CRITIQUE.md:2100 set the deadline at 2026-09-07"]]},{"type":"table","title":"What the answer changes (CRITIQUE.md:1453-1461)","cols":["Line","Two founders","One founder"],"rows":[["Monthly nut","₹1,08,918","₹63,918"],["Default-alive, paying users","501","294"],["Client hours per month to fund it","54–78","32.0–45.7"],["Cumulative visitors, 24 months","171,200","100,428"],["Cost to the published calendar","zero","1.46× stretch"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Strike it. One founder is the default; re-derive every figure before publishing","what":"The nut, break-even, client hours and traffic are recomputed at one person and the two-founder columns are deleted.","gains":["Default-alive falls to 294 paying users and about 4,185 visitors a month","Removes the largest untested assumption in the plan","Costs an afternoon of arithmetic and nothing else"],"costs":["No second person to absorb client work, so the calendar stretches 1.46×","The plan reads smaller, which is a real cost when you show it to anyone"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"Monthly nut falls from ₹1,08,918 to ₹63,918 (docs/CRITIQUE.md:1460)."},{"k":"b","label":"Sign this week: a named person, an equity split, a start date, hours a week","what":"The second founder becomes real on paper and the two-founder numbers stand as published.","gains":["Restores the reading in which client work costs no product velocity","Puts a second responder behind the six-hour statutory clock"],"costs":["Doubles the draw from day one, before any revenue exists","Requires a real commitment from a real person, which no document can manufacture"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"Nut returns to ₹1,08,918 a month; default-alive rises to 501 paying users."},{"k":"c","label":"Name the second person as a contractor with an hours floor, not a founder","what":"Capacity is bought by the hour under a written contract instead of by equity.","gains":["Buys hours without giving away equity","Reversible in a way a founder split is not"],"costs":["Adds a cash cost to a nut currently funded entirely by consulting","The IP assignment falls due before the first line is written"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"₹15,000–₹40,000 one-time for a lawyer-drafted agreement (docs/BUSINESS.md:759), plus the hours."},{"k":"d","label":"Carry both scenarios in the plan, labelled, until revenue decides","what":"Every capacity-dependent number stays a range with two columns.","gains":["Honest about what is unknown","Costs nothing today"],"costs":["The calendar cannot be committed to at all","The same argument returns at every review, with months spent"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["The only measurement available says one person, twice, across 498 commits.","The good half comes with it: 294 paying users and 4,185 visitors a month is a blog with traction, not a distribution miracle.","Striking it costs an afternoon; leaving it costs every number downstream."],"flip":"A signed agreement naming hours a week, at which point re-derive rather than assume the figures scale linearly, because two founders is not two of the same founder.","linked":["B18","B2","FF14","PL2"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:231","docs/DECIDE.md:156","docs/CRITIQUE.md:1437","docs/CRITIQUE.md:1447","docs/CRITIQUE.md:1459","docs/CRITIQUE.md:1460","docs/CRITIQUE.md:2100","docs/BRIEF.md:116","docs/BUSINESS.md:759"],"dupes":{"dropped":["PL18"],"why":"One founder or two, and does every number get re-derived. Same options, both rec (a) strike the assumption. Business & operations owns capacity."}},{"id":"B2","cat":"Business & operations","sub":"Funding","weight":"critical","q":"How is the build funded — services booked before it starts, one engagement a quarter alongside it, or a raise?","lede":"Services are the only funding line in the plan, and the plan's hour cap is nearly twice the ceiling the record measured from behaviour.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":200,"cols":[{"title":"Two engagements first","tone":"neutral"},{"title":"One a quarter","tone":"accent"},{"title":"₹4 Cr raise","tone":"stop"}],"rows":[{"label":"Money in","cells":["₹6,00,000 up front","₹3,00,000 every quarter","₹4 crore for 11%"]},{"label":"Months of the one-founder nut","cells":["9.4","continuous, 1.56× cover","367"]},{"label":"Founder hours it costs","cells":["180","30 a month averaged","none, but a board"]},{"label":"Build starts","cells":["after 4.5 months of client work","week 0","week 0"]},{"label":"Obligation taken on","cells":["two client SLAs","one client SLA at a time","a seven-year fund horizon"]},{"label":"Precedent in the record","cells":["—","Obsidian: 8 staff, no investors","Dendron: no fit for a venture-backed business"]}],"note":"Hours at the measured client-lane ceiling of 40 a month in one contiguous week (r23-u4:60).","caption":"Three ways to pay for the build, and what each costs in time"},"stakes":"Pick wrong and either the build stops for four months, or the company takes a seven-year obligation against a founder wall at 1,239 paying users.","state":["The plan caps client work at 78 hours a month and covers the nut with 54–78 of them (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:292, docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:329).","The 90-day calendar schedules no client hours at all (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:351).","The refusal to raise lives only in the decision layer; v15 has no funding section (docs/DECIDE.md:150)."],"path":["The money research concluded that services fund this, not investors and not the product (docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r22-t3-money.md:1).","The engagement was then designed in full: ten days, ₹3,00,000 or $8,000, 90 founder-hours, 73.5% repeatable (r23-u4:84, r23-u4:95).","The critique attached a condition, that revenue is booked before the build starts rather than alongside it (docs/CRITIQUE.md:1878)."],"tension":["The 78-hour cap is 1.95× the measured ceiling of 40 hours in one contiguous week (r23-u4:60).","Antler is ₹4 crore for 11% with a three-week decision, which is 367 months of runway against a fund that wants an exit in seven years (docs/DECIDE.md:150).","Almanac raised $45M, passed 50 staff and shut on 2025-01-31 with capacity, not demand, given as the cause.","Burn with no services at all is ₹4,700–9,300 a month, so runway is not what forces the choice (r23-u4:54)."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"The two lanes, priced","items":[["Two-year product success case, monthly","₹1,09,135","BRIEF.md:25 — 502 paying users, 171,200 cumulative visitors"],["The same money in consulting hours","78 hours a month","BRIEF.md:170, at the measured ₹1,400–2,000/hour"],["One productised engagement","₹3,00,000 / $8,000, 90 founder-hours","r23-u4:84 and r23-u4:95; 73.5% repeatable"],["Four engagements a year","₹12,00,000 = the ₹1L/mo milestone","r23-u4:62"],["Funnel equivalent of one client","63,060 visitors","r23-u4:62"],["Burn, if no services at all","₹4,700–9,300 a month","r23-u4:54 — runway is not the constraint"]]},{"type":"table","title":"The cap the plan sets, against the ceiling the record measured","cols":["Source","Client hours per month"],"rows":[["PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:329, the risk row","capped at 78"],["PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:292, to cover the ₹1.09L two-founder nut","54–78"],["CRITIQUE.md:1460, against the one-founder nut","32.0–45.7"],["r23-u4:60, measured ceiling from active-day clustering","40, in one contiguous week"],["r23-u4:62, four engagements a year averaged","30"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"The two routes, as priced","items":[["Antler India","₹4 crore for 11%, decision in 3 weeks; implied post-money ₹36.4 crore ≈ $3.81M","r22-t3-money.md:64, 70, fetched 2026-08-31"],["Y Combinator","$500K on two SAFEs, roughly 9.5% total at a $15M cap","r22-t3-money.md:65, fetched 2026-08-31"],["₹4 crore expressed in the nut","367 months of runway","DECIDE.md:150"],["Fund horizon","about 7 years","DECIDE.md:151"],["Trigger that would flip the verdict","three unsolicited inbound teams asking for multi-editor access","CRITIQUE.md:1075"],["Where that trigger appears in the plan","nowhere","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md, grep 2026-09-08"]]},{"type":"table","title":"What the alternative funds, with what it costs","cols":["Route","Buys","Costs"],"rows":[["₹4 crore raise","367 months of the two-founder nut","11% and a seven-year obligation against a founder wall at 1,239 paying users (BUSINESS.md:781)"],["Four engagements a year","₹12,00,000 = the ₹1L/mo milestone","360 founder-hours a year, 16.6% of annual engineering time (r23-u4:62)"],["One engagement","₹3,00,000 and 63,060 visitors of funnel equivalent","90 founder-hours (r23-u4:84, 62)"],["No funding at all","full ownership","a burn of ₹4,700–9,300 a month, which is survivable (r23-u4:54)"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Book two engagements before the week-3 go/no-go. No product code until invoiced","what":"The client lane runs alone until ₹6,00,000 is contracted, and the build waits.","gains":["₹6,00,000 is 9.4 months of the one-founder nut and takes cash off the risk list","Proves the ₹1,400–2,000 hourly rate is real before anything depends on it"],"costs":["180 founder-hours at a 40-hour contiguous-week pattern is 4.5 months of the client lane","The engine defects stay unfixed while the only measured demand signal ages"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"₹6,00,000 booked; zero product days in the same window."},{"k":"b","label":"Run both lanes from week 0 at the plan's 78-hour cap","what":"Client work and the build share every month at the cap the plan already published.","gains":["Fastest to a shipped product on paper","Keeps both lanes visible to anyone reading the plan"],"costs":["The cap is 1.95× the behaviourally measured ceiling, so one lane absorbs the other","That failure is already in the record at 10.9 to 1 substrate commits against product"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"Same ₹1L a month equivalent, at hours nobody has ever worked."},{"k":"c","label":"One engagement a quarter, cap hours from the nut, and a dated refusal to raise","what":"₹3,00,000 every quarter funds the nut at 30 hours a month, and the plan records a twelve-month no on funding with a named trigger.","gains":["₹1,00,000 a month equivalent is 1.56× the one-founder nut, inside the 40-hour ceiling","Settles the raise question in writing so it is not relitigated at the first cash scare","One client is worth 63,060 visitors of funnel that no other channel supplies"],"costs":["Never produces the lump that buys a year of not worrying about cash","Leaves nothing for a support hire when the coefficient lands badly"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"₹12,00,000 a year at 360 founder-hours (r23-u4:62)."},{"k":"d","label":"Apply to Antler or Y Combinator now","what":"Cash stops being a constraint and the company takes outside money and a board.","gains":["Buys a second person outright and removes the client lane","₹4 crore is 367 months of the two-founder nut"],"costs":["A seven-year obligation against a founder wall the record puts at 1,239 paying users","Almanac's $45M and Atrium's $75.5M both ended in a shutdown, not an exit"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"₹4 crore for 11%, implied post-money about $3.81M (r22-t3-money.md:64)."}],"rec":"c","recCase":["Corrected for the measured ceiling, (a) and (c) buy the same money, and only (c) buys it without stopping the build.","The argument against raising is already made in the record's own terms; writing it into the governing plan with a trigger costs a paragraph.","Send the proposals in week 0 whichever option wins, because the closes are the measurement, not the revenue."],"flip":"Three unsolicited inbound teams asking for multi-editor access, the record's own trigger for treating this as a category rather than a lifestyle business (docs/CRITIQUE.md:1075).","linked":["B1","B12","B21"],"sources":["merged: B20","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:292","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:329","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:351","docs/DECIDE.md:150","docs/CRITIQUE.md:1075","docs/CRITIQUE.md:1411","docs/CRITIQUE.md:1766","docs/CRITIQUE.md:1878","docs/BUSINESS.md:781","docs/BRIEF.md:170","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r22-t3-money.md:1","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r22-t3-money.md:64","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r23-u4-consultation-and-services.md:54","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r23-u4-consultation-and-services.md:60","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r23-u4-consultation-and-services.md:62","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r23-u4-consultation-and-services.md:84","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r23-u4-consultation-and-services.md:95"]},{"id":"B6","cat":"Business & operations","sub":"Support","weight":"critical","q":"Do we instrument the ten-stranger pilot to measure the support coefficient, or publish a price with a 3× error bar on the largest cost in the model?","lede":"Support is the cost structure of this business, and the number that drives it is written two ways in our own repo.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":210,"cols":[{"title":"0.10 per paid user","tone":"good"},{"title":"0.30 at 12 minutes","tone":"warn"},{"title":"0.30 at 20.72 minutes","tone":"stop"}],"rows":[{"label":"Where it is written","cells":["PRD §21.1","BUSINESS.md:771","r6's measured ticket mix"]},{"label":"Founder-hours per paying user","cells":["not derived","0.1445 a month","0.249 a month"]},{"label":"The founder wall","cells":["far out","1,239 paying users","well under 1,000"]},{"label":"What it does to ₹299","cells":["+₹47.43","−₹28.22","worse again"]},{"label":"Times measured on our users","cells":["0","0","0"]}],"note":"The 20.72-minute mean comes from the Obsidian forum tag histogram, weighted; 1.73× the flat 12 (r6:68).","caption":"One coefficient, three readings, none taken from a real user"},"stakes":"Every price, every hire trigger and the founder wall itself are computed from a number nobody has measured, and the pilot is the last cheap chance to take it.","state":["The plan states 90 founder-hours a month at 10,000 users with no denominator named (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:137).","The operating model uses 0.3 tickets per paying user a month at 12 minutes (docs/BUSINESS.md:771); the PRD uses 0.10 (docs/CRITIQUE.md:901).","The pilot as written asks the ten strangers nothing about how often they needed help."],"path":["The two figures were written into different documents at different times and never reconciled.","A later pass built a ticket mix from the Obsidian forum tag histogram and found a weighted mean handle time of 20.72 minutes (r6:68).","The critique ranked measuring it first among the things that would change its verdict (docs/CRITIQUE.md:1075)."],"tension":["At 0.30 the founder wall arrives at 1,239 paying users; at 0.10 an individual subscription flips from below cost to above it (docs/BUSINESS.md:781).","Ten users will not give a confidence interval, but they will separate two numbers that differ by 3×.","The deflection plan cuts the load 70.2 per cent and moves the hire trigger 5.83×, and it costs engineering days the schedule does not have (r6:87, r6:157-159).","Counting messages costs a spreadsheet; the price page waits for the pilot either way."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"The coefficient, three ways, none measured on our users","items":[["BUSINESS.md:771","0.30 tickets per paying user per month, 12 minutes each"],["PRD §21.1, quoted at CRITIQUE.md:901","0.10 tickets per paying user per month"],["r6 measured mix, weighted","20.72 minutes per ticket","r6-support-deflection.md:68 — 1.73× the flat 12"],["Times measured on our own users","0","CRITIQUE.md:901"],["No vendor publishes a per-user contact rate","confirmed against Zendesk's 2026 CX Trends and GitLab's public handbook","r6-support-deflection.md:12"]]},{"type":"table","title":"What the spread moves","cols":["Reading","Consequence"],"rows":[["0.30 at 12 minutes (BUSINESS.md:779-781)","0.1445 founder-hours per paying user; the wall at 1,239 paying users"],["0.10 (CRITIQUE.md:901)","₹299's effective contribution moves from −₹28.22 to +₹47.43"],["r6's 20.72 minutes, pre-deflection (r6:68)","80.45 founder-hours a month at 10,000 users"],["r6's deflection plan applied (r6:87)","23.97 founder-hours a month — a 70.2% cut bought with engineering"],["Support-hire trigger, without and with deflection (r6:157-159)","$14.18/hour against $82.64/hour of founder time — 5.83×"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Instrument the pilot: log every message with a category and a handle time","what":"For the full fortnight every message from the ten strangers is written down with what it was about and how long it took.","gains":["Separates 0.10 from 0.30 by an order of magnitude for the cost of a spreadsheet","Gives the deflection plan a target list drawn from our users, not Obsidian's forum"],"costs":["Ten users is a tiny sample and yields no confidence interval","Delays the pricing page by the length of the pilot"],"system":"None. A log, not a feature.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Ship the six deflection changes first, then measure","what":"Key validator, device-flow auth, never refuse an import, visible conflict state, self-serve billing and local history land before the coefficient is taken.","gains":["Moves the hire trigger 5.83× and removes the long-handle-time classes","Every change is one a user would want anyway"],"costs":["Real engineering days against a schedule with 1.21 a week","Optimises a number nobody has measured, so the ordering may be wrong"],"system":"Six changes across auth, import, billing and history.","screens":"Conflict state; billing.","money":"Cuts founder-hours at 10,000 users from 80.45 to 23.97 (r6:87)."},{"k":"c","label":"Adopt the pessimistic reading, 0.30 at 20.72 minutes, and price against it","what":"The model takes the worst supported number and every price is set above that cost.","gains":["Conservative, defensible, and pushes the business toward teams","No measurement needed, so nothing is delayed"],"costs":["If the true rate is 0.10 you have priced out of a market that existed","Makes every individual price look bad, which may be the wrong conclusion"],"system":"No change.","screens":"Pricing page.","money":"Raises the modelled cost per paying user by about 73 per cent."},{"k":"d","label":"Publish the 90-hour figure with its denominator stated, and measure later","what":"The plan keeps its headline support number and says which model produced it.","gains":["Cheapest, and it names the one thing that makes the figure unauditable","Nothing is delayed and no pilot design changes"],"costs":["The figure sits between two incompatible models, 80.45 hours and 1,464 at 10,000","The first real measurement then comes from paying customers, the expensive place"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["This is the largest cost in the model, the pilot is already happening, and counting messages costs nothing beyond writing them down.","Ten users will not give a precise coefficient, but telling 0.10 from 0.30 is the whole question.","The category gives no help: no vendor publishes a per-user contact rate (r6:12)."],"flip":"Fewer than about five messages in total across the fortnight, at which point the sample is too thin to read either way and (c) is the honest posture until 100 users exist.","linked":["B10","B7","PR7"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:137","docs/BUSINESS.md:771","docs/BUSINESS.md:777","docs/BUSINESS.md:781","docs/CRITIQUE.md:901","docs/CRITIQUE.md:1075","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-29-r11/r6-support-deflection.md:12","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-29-r11/r6-support-deflection.md:68","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-29-r11/r6-support-deflection.md:87","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-29-r11/r6-support-deflection.md:157"]},{"id":"B7","cat":"Business & operations","sub":"Support","weight":"high","q":"What does the free tier get — no service commitment, a public forum, or a response window — and does the pilot fortnight get an exception?","lede":"The free tier is the whole funnel and, at scale, the largest single consumer of the one resource that cannot be bought.","visual":{"kind":"screen","title":"What the page promises","panes":[{"label":"Free, individual","w":50,"rows":[{"label":"Public forum, category forms, indexed answers","meta":"$0 a month","mark":"✓","tone":"accent"},{"label":"No private queue, no response window","meta":"stated on the page","mark":"–","tone":"neutral"},{"label":"Every feature, no caps","meta":"F1–F8, own key","mark":"✓","tone":"good"},{"label":"Pilot fortnight only: 48-hour best effort","meta":"ten strangers","mark":"!","tone":"warn"}]},{"label":"Pro, team","w":50,"rows":[{"label":"One address, a published response window","meta":"per seat","mark":"✓","tone":"good"},{"label":"Same forum, same answers","meta":"shared","mark":"✓","tone":"neutral"}]}],"note":"Free users generate four of every seven tickets in the model (BUSINESS.md:787).","caption":"Bounding the time, not the product"},"stakes":"Promise too much and one person owes an answer to every free user; promise nothing and the pilot measures the support gap instead of the product.","state":["The operating rules give one address, a published window, and no service commitment on free (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:537).","The individual tier is free with no limits and stays free at MVP-0 (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:287, docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:196).","All ten pilot users are free users, because MVP-0 has no billing at all (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:205)."],"path":["The no-commitment line follows from the time budget: free users generate four of every seven tickets (docs/BUSINESS.md:787).","The support research reached a compatible answer, a support address plus GitHub Discussions at $0 a month to 1,000 users (r6:120).","The record's own anti-recommendation is not to cut the free tier, because that cuts the funnel and the ops bill together."],"tension":["A median free user costs about ₹7.87 a month, of which 86 per cent is founder time (docs/CRITIQUE.md:966).","At 10,000 free users that is ₹68,000 a month of founder time against ₹25,930 of cloud and AI (docs/CRITIQUE.md:968).","India to US Pacific is a 12.5-hour offset, so a sub-24-hour first response is not possible solo (r6:163).","A stranger who goes quiet because nobody answered is indistinguishable, in the exit measure, from one who did not want it."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"Who the free tier actually is, at MVP-0","items":[["Paying users in MVP-0","0 — billing is in the Absent row","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:205"],["Pilot users","10 strangers, all free","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:206"],["Share of tickets from free users in the model","4 of every 7","BUSINESS.md:787"],["Recommended channel to 1,000 users","support address plus GitHub Discussions, $0/month","r6-support-deflection.md:120"],["Sub-24-hour first response, solo, India to US Pacific","structurally impossible","r6-support-deflection.md:163"]]},{"type":"table","title":"What each phase costs (r6-support-deflection.md:120-121)","cols":["Users","Tickets/month","Tooling","Cost"],"rows":[["0 to 1,000","up to 23","support address + GitHub Discussions + docs","$0/month"],["1,000 to 10,000","23 to 232","Help Scout Standard, 1 seat, + AI Answers","$94.60/month at 40% AI resolution"],["Same volume, flat-price alternative","232","Crisp Essentials","$95.00/month"],["Break-even between the two","93.3 AI resolutions/month","—","derived, r6:121"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"What a free user costs","items":[["Hosted inference","₹0.00 — bring-your-own key only","CRITIQUE.md:963"],["Infrastructure","₹1.07 a month","CRITIQUE.md:964"],["Support at 0.02 tickets × 12 min at ₹1,700/hour","₹6.80 a month","CRITIQUE.md:965"],["Total, of which founder time","₹7.87, 86% founder time","CRITIQUE.md:966"],["At 10,000 free users","₹68,000 a month of founder time against ₹25,930 of total cloud and AI","CRITIQUE.md:968"],["Share of tickets from free users","4 of every 7","BUSINESS.md:787"]]},{"type":"table","title":"What is already banked as deflection, before any cap","cols":["Settled decision","What it removes"],"rows":[["No plugin marketplace, no client-side code execution","22.79% of the Obsidian-equivalent tagged forum volume (r6:90)"],["File is the only source of truth","\"where is my data\" has a filesystem-path answer (r6:91)"],["Byte-preserving splice","the mangling and diff-noise class (r6:92)"],["Certificate shown on import, not only export","converts a 90-minute forensic ticket into a pre-answered artefact (r6:94)"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"No commitment on free, stated plainly, in the pilot too","what":"The page says free users get no response window, and the pilot runs on the same terms.","gains":["Honest, unpurchasable-around, and it bounds the founder's time absolutely","One rule to write and one rule to keep"],"costs":["A pilot stranger who hits the 83 per cent refusal may get no answer at all","The exit test then measures the support gap rather than the product"],"system":"No change.","screens":"One line on the pricing page.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Unlimited features, bounded support: free goes to a public forum, never a queue","what":"GitHub Discussions with category forms is the free channel, standing, with the private address reserved for paying teams.","gains":["Bounds the only cost that scales with free users and leaves the product whole","Answers are indexed, so each one is spent more than once","It is the recommended channel to 1,000 users anyway, at $0 a month (r6:120)"],"costs":["Public questions from a product with ten users read as an empty room","Some fraction of free users will not ask, and go quiet instead"],"system":"Category forms that force OS, version and a repro file.","screens":"A support page; a forum link.","money":"$0 a month to 1,000 users; $94.60 a month from 1,000 to 10,000 (r6:121)."},{"k":"c","label":"Forum standing, plus a 48-hour best effort for the ten pilot users only","what":"The standing policy is the forum, and the pilot fortnight carries a stated, temporary response window.","gains":["Protects the one measurement the whole plan turns on","Ten users at 48 hours is a few hours a week, not a commitment at scale","The exception is visibly bounded to the fortnight from the start"],"costs":["Sets an expectation that has to be withdrawn in front of the same people","Past about fifteen messages a week the promise is already the constraint"],"system":"No change.","screens":"Pricing page plus a pilot welcome note.","money":"A few founder-hours a week for two weeks."},{"k":"d","label":"Cap the free tier by vault size or repository count instead of support","what":"Free stays a private queue but the product meters heavy use and prompts for a paid seat.","gains":["Bounds the heaviest users, who are also the likeliest to convert","Creates a paid moment the product can actually see"],"costs":["Contradicts free, no limits on the page and adds metering to a product that has none","Cuts the funnel and the ops bill in the same stroke, which the record advises against"],"system":"A metering surface where none exists.","screens":"An upgrade prompt at the ceiling.","money":"Unknown; no comparable in the category meters an editor this way."}],"rec":"c","recCase":["The cost that scales is time, not features, so bound the time and leave the product alone.","For the pilot fortnight support is not a cost centre, it is the instrument, and an unanswered stranger wastes the whole two weeks.","A public forum with category forms is free, indexed, and the channel the research recommends to 1,000 users."],"flip":"If the first hundred users show heavy vaults driving the long classes, import at 35 minutes and data loss at 90, then (d)'s ceiling becomes a real lever and the page stops saying no limits.","linked":["B10","B6"],"sources":["merged: B13","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:196","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:205","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:206","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:287","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:537","docs/BUSINESS.md:787","docs/CRITIQUE.md:963","docs/CRITIQUE.md:968","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-29-r11/r6-support-deflection.md:89","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-29-r11/r6-support-deflection.md:120","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-29-r11/r6-support-deflection.md:163"]},{"id":"B8","cat":"Business & operations","sub":"Communication","weight":"high","q":"How do we reach a user we hold no address for — a notice ledger in the repo, a vault folder, or an optional email field at first run?","lede":"A breach notice, a price change and a failed renewal all currently terminate at the same dead end, and the pilot needs a day-14 channel.","visual":{"kind":"file","name":"the user's repository, after frontmatter","lines":[{"t":".frontmatter/review.jsonl","mark":"keep","note":"the sidecar, already agreed"},{"t":".frontmatter/usage.jsonl","mark":"keep","note":"opt-in counts, B10"},{"t":".frontmatter/notices/2026-09-15-price.md","mark":"add","note":"one vendor directory, not two"},{"t":"Notices/2026-09-15-price.md","mark":"stop","note":"BUSINESS.md:121; breaks the one-sidecar rule"},{"t":"README.md","mark":"keep","note":"untouched"}],"note":"PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:508: the sidecar is the only thing frontmatter adds, and it is not in the markdown.","caption":"Where a required notice can live without a second vendor folder"},"stakes":"A notice class with no channel is a duty we cannot discharge, and a vendor folder at vault root breaks the one promise a byte-exact product is judged on.","state":["BUSINESS.md writes obligatory messages into the vault as read-only markdown under Notices/ (docs/BUSINESS.md:121).","The operating rules keep all notices in an in-product list instead (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:536).","The format section says the sidecar is the only thing we add (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:508).","Email is collected only on an obligation, never at first run, and first run collects nothing (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:430, docs/BUSINESS.md:48)."],"path":["The ledger was designed to satisfy DPDP Rule 7(1)'s user-account channel literally, for a product that collects no email (docs/BUSINESS.md:123).","The one-sidecar rule was written separately, as the answer to what we may add to somebody else's repository.","The email research found the governing PRD had no substantive coverage of sending infrastructure at all (docs/BUSINESS.md:17)."],"tension":["A folder at vault root appears in git status, in every diff and on GitHub, which is the addition the format section forbids.","The pilot is recruited, not organic, and the day-14 ask needs a channel the plan does not have (docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:21).","An explicit feedback field was filled 7 times in 694 opportunities, a 1.0 per cent response rate (docs/BUSINESS.md:281).","An email field at first run is the change most likely to depress conversion, by the plan's own reading (docs/BUSINESS.md:55)."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"Three answers in three documents","cols":["Location","Where specified","Consistent with the one-sidecar rule?"],"rows":[["`Notices/` at vault root, read-only markdown","BUSINESS.md:121","No — a second vendor directory in the user's repo"],["In-product list","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:536","Yes — writes nothing"],["`.frontmatter/` sidecar, plain text","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:508","Yes, if notices go inside the existing directory"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"What the ledger has to carry","items":[["Obligatory message classes","10","BUSINESS.md:25-34"],["Severities","2 — must-read and for-the-record","BUSINESS.md:130"],["Users with no address at all","a supported, permanent state","BUSINESS.md:53"],["Breach intimation channel named by DPDP Rule 7(1)","\"through her user account or any mode of communication registered by her\" — verbatim","BUSINESS.md:26, fetched 2026-08-30"],["When the DPDP substantive sections and penalties commence","2027-05-13; §2 and §§18–26 are live now","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:541"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"The channel the pilot needs and does not have","items":[["Collected at first run","nothing","BUSINESS.md:48"],["Sending infrastructure in the governing document","zero substantive occurrences of SPF, DKIM, DMARC or unsubscribe across the 120,539-word PRD v2","BUSINESS.md:17, measured 2026-08-30"],["Explicit feedback field, internal measurement","7 filled of 694 opportunities = 1.0%","BUSINESS.md:281"],["Day-14 ask in the measurement decision","paste the usage file into a message, or say no","WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:21"],["Vendor cost if we do send","Resend Pro, $20/month at 24,145 messages","BUSINESS.md:108, 115"]]},{"type":"table","title":"Obligatory classes that need a channel before the first charge","cols":["Class","Deadline","Channel available today"],"rows":[["Breach intimation to each affected user","without delay (DPDP Rule 7(1))","none — no address, no ledger built"],["Annual renewal pre-notice, California","at least 15 and not more than 45 days before renewal","email only; none collected"],["Price or terms change","before the next charge, never after","none"],["Payment failure and dunning","see BUSINESS.md:142-148","email only; none collected"],["Team invite and account recovery","immediate","email only, by definition"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Ledger in `.frontmatter/notices/`, no-email rule held, consent page for the ten","what":"Notices are plain files inside the sidecar directory that already exists, and the pilot users sign a one-page consent covering contact for the fortnight.","gains":["One vendor directory, not two, and the notice keeps the file-is-the-record property","The day-14 ask becomes a commitment rather than a hope","Nothing changes on the first-run screen the plan has protected hardest"],"costs":["Still lands in the user's git history, which some teams will object to","Does not solve the standing dead end for a breach notice at scale"],"system":"A notices writer inside the existing sidecar directory.","screens":"A status-line affordance; a notices list.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"`Notices/` at vault root, as BUSINESS.md specifies","what":"Obligatory messages are read-only markdown files at the top level of the user's vault.","gains":["Most visible to a user who never opens the sidecar directory","Reads as an ordinary note in whatever editor they already use"],"costs":["Puts vendor files at the top level of somebody's repository","Directly contradicts the plan's own only-thing-we-add rule"],"system":"A second vendor directory.","screens":"A notices folder in the tree.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"In-app list only, plus an optional email field at first run, purpose stated","what":"Nothing is written to the repo and a one-line optional field gives every obligatory class a real channel.","gains":["Solves breach, renewal and price-change delivery at once","Adds nothing to the user's files"],"costs":["Puts a field on the one screen the plan protects hardest, at an unmeasurable cost","For a user who declines, there is still no durable copy of a required notice"],"system":"An optional address on the identity record; a sending vendor.","screens":"First run gains a field.","money":"Resend Pro at $20 a month at 24,145 messages (docs/BUSINESS.md:108)."},{"k":"d","label":"Require an email at first run","what":"No editor until an address is given, which makes every message in the obligatory table deliverable.","gains":["Every notice class has a channel from day one","Team invites and account recovery stop being special cases"],"costs":["Contradicts the category convention the plan cites as a kill condition","Converts first run from opening the editor into filling a form"],"system":"Accounts before value.","screens":"A signup screen that does not exist today.","money":"Unknown conversion cost; the plan's own reading is that it is the largest one available."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["One directory is the rule the plan already committed to, and notices inside it keep every property the ledger was designed for.","The pilot is a study with ten named participants, so a consent page is the correct instrument and it costs nothing in the product.","It leaves the first-run screen exactly as the plan protects it."],"flip":"The standing dead end for breach and price-change notices at scale is untouched by this; that needs option (c) and it is due before the first charge, not before the pilot.","linked":["B10","B14"],"sources":["merged: B9","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:430","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:508","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:536","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:541","docs/BUSINESS.md:17","docs/BUSINESS.md:25","docs/BUSINESS.md:48","docs/BUSINESS.md:53","docs/BUSINESS.md:55","docs/BUSINESS.md:108","docs/BUSINESS.md:121","docs/BUSINESS.md:142","docs/BUSINESS.md:281","docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:21"]},{"id":"B10","cat":"Business & operations","sub":"Measurement","weight":"high","q":"Do we adopt the drafted local usage file as the exit measure, and do we interview every stranger whether or not they share it?","lede":"The headline exit test, six of ten strangers keep it, is unobservable under our own architecture unless the measure is designed in first.","visual":{"kind":"state","states":[{"label":"Installed","meta":"no account, nothing sent","via":"day 0","tone":"neutral","current":true},{"label":"Daily use","meta":"usage.jsonl gains a line a day","via":"days 1-13","tone":"good"},{"label":"Day-14 ask","meta":"paste the file, or say no","via":"day 14","tone":"accent"},{"label":"Counted or a hole","meta":"a decline is a tenth of the answer","via":"after","tone":"warn"}],"note":"Counts only: days opened, documents opened, spans reviewed, proposals accepted (WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:19).","caption":"The only measurement path the operating rules allow"},"stakes":"Without it the go/no-go at week 12 rests on recall, against a measured 1.0 per cent response rate for unprompted feedback.","state":["The draft puts counts only in `.frontmatter/usage.jsonl` in the user's repo, editable and deletable (docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:20).","The gate is 6 of the last 10 working days plus one review action in week two (docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:22).","The risk register still carries the measure as owed before week 10, and week 0 is tasked with writing it (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:324, docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:351).","The gap register lists it as flagged and still undecided (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:28)."],"path":["The constraint is self-imposed and correct: no vendor usage database, no document bytes (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:538).","Obsidian, with the same architecture, states on record that it does not measure churn (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:417).","The only compatible design is opt-in, local and readable by the user."],"tension":["A local file only reaches us if someone volunteers it, and with ten users one decline moves the gate by a tenth.","The interview gives the reason, which no count can supply, and costs ten conversations.","An opt-in upload keyed to an account makes the line personal data, pulling notice and consent duties into MVP-0.","Self-report alone produces a number that is not defensible to anyone, including us."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"The drafted measure","items":[["What is counted","days opened, documents opened, spans reviewed, proposals accepted, questions answered","WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:19 — counts only, no content"],["Where it lives","`.frontmatter/usage.jsonl` in the user's repo","WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:20"],["How it reaches us","it does not, by default; asked once on day 14","WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:21"],["The gate","6 of the last 10 working days plus one review action in week 2","WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:22"],["Never collected","session replay, keystrokes, content, file names, prompts, IP, device identifiers","WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:23; matches PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:538"]]},{"type":"table","title":"What each route can and cannot tell us","cols":["Route","Tells us","Cannot tell us"],"rows":[["Local file, pasted voluntarily","days opened and actions taken, exactly","why anyone stopped; anything about people who decline"],["Day-14 interview only","the reason, in their words","whether the reported usage happened"],["Opt-in upload from day one","the same counts, without an ask","nothing more; and once keyed to an account it is personal data, so the notice-and-consent duties come forward (WEEK0:24)"],["Nothing","—","the exit test cannot be run at all"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Adopt the draft as written: local file, one ask on day 14","what":"Counts are written locally and each stranger is asked once, at the end of the fortnight, to paste the file.","gains":["Consistent with every operating rule and cheap to build","The counts, when shared, are exact"],"costs":["Anyone who declines is uncounted","Says nothing about why anyone stopped"],"system":"A daily counts writer in the sidecar.","screens":"A settings line naming the file.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Adopt the draft and interview every stranger on day 14 regardless","what":"The file gives the count, the conversation gives the reason, and refusals stop being holes in the sample.","gains":["Every one of the ten is accounted for, shared file or not","The plan already calls the ten strangers the first interviews; this makes that literal","The reason is the input to whether the product is re-cut or killed"],"costs":["Ten conversations makes the pilot a two-week commitment, not a hand-off","It cannot be run by anyone but the founder, and it does not scale past this cohort"],"system":"Same writer as (a).","screens":"Same as (a).","money":"Founder time, roughly a day across the fortnight."},{"k":"c","label":"Self-report only. Skip the file","what":"Each stranger is asked what they did and the gate is read from the answers.","gains":["Nothing to build, and nothing lands in the user repository","The fortnight needs no instrumentation at all"],"costs":["Rests on recall against a measured 1.0 per cent baseline for unprompted feedback","The resulting number is defensible to nobody"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Opt-in upload, off by default, from day one","what":"Counts reach us without an ask, for anyone who switches it on.","gains":["Clean counts with no day-14 ask to chase","The only design that scales past ten users"],"costs":["Once keyed to an account the line is personal data","That pulls notice and consent forward for a product with no notice channel yet"],"system":"An upload path and a consent record.","screens":"A consent toggle at first run.","money":"None material at pilot scale."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["With ten users every refusal is a tenth of the answer, so the count and the reason both have to be collected.","The interview explains a number the counts cannot, and the plan already names the ten as the first interviews.","It is the cheapest version that produces a defensible go/no-go."],"flip":"At 100 users interviewing everyone stops being possible and (d) becomes the design, at which point the consent and notice machinery has to exist first.","linked":["AC17","B6","B7","B8","PL5"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:324","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:351","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:417","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:538","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:28","docs/BUSINESS.md:281","docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:19","docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:20","docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:21","docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:22"],"dupes":{"dropped":["L18"],"why":"Which measurement instrument ships for the pilot — local file, opt-in upload, or nothing. Recs b vs a. Business & operations owns the exit measure; L18's rotating-install-id option is the legally-loaded variant and must be carried forward as a named non-option, and AC17 (where the file can physically live) links in."}},{"id":"B12","cat":"Business & operations","sub":"Distribution","weight":"high","q":"Do we plan against ₹20 lakh a month and 1.26 million cumulative visitors, or replace the milestone with default-alive?","lede":"The channel audit sums every available channel at a third of the traffic the headline milestone needs, and the milestone has no churn term.","visual":{"kind":"funnel","steps":[{"label":"Cumulative visitors needed for ₹20L a month","n":1260000,"unit":"visitors","tone":"stop"},{"label":"Free signups implied at 9%","n":113507,"unit":"signups","tone":"warn"},{"label":"Paying users implied","n":6689,"unit":"paying","tone":"warn"},{"label":"Paying users for default-alive, one founder","n":294,"unit":"paying","tone":"good"}],"note":"Everything on the channel table reaches perhaps 350k–500k year-one visitors (BUSINESS.md:1086). Marketing posts ever shipped: 2.","caption":"The milestone against the only threshold that changes anything"},"stakes":"A target nobody can reach makes every honest report read as failure, and the plan stops being usable as a plan.","state":["The distribution work puts the requirement at about 1,260,000 cumulative visitors (docs/BUSINESS.md:941).","It then sums the channels at 350k to 500k year-one visitors and says the 1.26M figure is not a year-one number (docs/BUSINESS.md:1086).","The v15 plan carries neither figure and has no revenue milestone at all.","Marketing posts ever shipped: 2 (docs/BUSINESS.md:940)."],"path":["Every revenue milestone in the earlier plan was a gross-additions figure, with no term for anyone leaving (docs/BUSINESS.md:164).","The churn section then showed the stock has to be maintained: about 89,000 visitors a month at 6 per cent churn, in perpetuity (docs/BUSINESS.md:253).","Accounts under $50 a month sit in the worst-retaining band, 60 to 70 per cent top-quartile annual gross retention (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:292)."],"tension":["Default-alive at one founder is 294 paying users, about 100,428 cumulative visitors, against 6,689 for ₹20 lakh (docs/CRITIQUE.md:1459).","The published-page organic channel is about zero by choice, under the noindex default (docs/BUSINESS.md:1080).","The category cannot generate noise even when a loved product dies: Almanac's 2020 Show HN scored 6 points and no comments.","Editorially closed in 2014 saying that even if all of its users had paid, it would not have been enough."],"evidence":[{"type":"bars","title":"Cumulative visitors: what is needed against what the channels can reach","note":"Requirement from BUSINESS.md:941 and CRITIQUE.md:1459; channel capacity from BUSINESS.md:1086, summed at the optimistic end across organic, the validator, content, referral and launch spikes.","data":[["Default-alive, one founder",100428],["Default-alive, two founders",171200],["Optimistic year-one channel sum, low",350000],["Optimistic year-one channel sum, high",500000],["₹20 lakh a month",1260000]],"unit":"cumulative visitors","threshold":500000,"thresholdLabel":"the most every measured channel can reach in year one"},{"type":"stat","title":"What holding a stock costs, forever","items":[["Replacement visitors per month at 2% churn","~29,700","BUSINESS.md:249"],["At 4%","~59,500","BUSINESS.md:250"],["At 6%","~89,200","BUSINESS.md:251"],["Marketing posts ever shipped","2","BUSINESS.md:940"],["Published-page organic under the noindex default","about zero, by choice","BUSINESS.md:1080"],["ChartMogul band for accounts under $50/month","top-quartile annual gross retention 60–70%; 23% for AI-native","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:292"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Delete ₹20 lakh a month. Publish default-alive as the only target","what":"The plan's single traffic and revenue target becomes the point at which the founder is paid.","gains":["Every channel in the audit can reach it: about 4,185 visitors a month","Turns the traffic problem from a miracle into a modest blog","Makes an honest weekly report readable as progress"],"costs":["Removes the number that makes this look like a company worth years of a founder's life","A small target is harder to raise against, if that ever becomes desirable"],"system":"No change.","screens":"The milestone table is rewritten.","money":"Target falls from 6,689 paying users to 294."},{"k":"b","label":"Keep ₹20 lakh as a three-year figure, restated with the churn replacement flow","what":"The milestone stays but carries the perpetual visitor flow needed to hold the stock.","gains":["Honest about the flow the original figure omitted entirely","Keeps a number that means something to anyone reading the plan cold"],"costs":["Still 12× default-alive, with no channel of the right order of magnitude","Keeps a number that reads as failure every month for three years"],"system":"No change.","screens":"The milestone table gains a churn column.","money":"About 89,000 replacement visitors a month at 6 per cent churn."},{"k":"c","label":"Size the developer-tool distribution channel before publishing any target","what":"The npm, CLI and editor-integration surface is measured, and the target is set from what it can actually carry.","gains":["The only candidate whose ceiling is of the right order (docs/BUSINESS.md:1084)","Replaces an assumption with a measurement"],"costs":["It reaches developers, the record calls them the worst-converting paid-editor audience","May raise visitors and lower the blended rate at the same time"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None until sized.","money":"Unknown until measured, which is the point."},{"k":"d","label":"Publish no traffic target until the two-week tests return","what":"The plan carries no number for reach while the headline is still under test.","gains":["Avoids committing to a figure before the product is confirmed","Costs nothing and cannot be refuted"],"costs":["Leaves no way to say whether any channel is working","The same question returns at the week-3 go/no-go with nothing to point at"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["A target nobody can reach guarantees that every honest report reads as failure.","Default-alive at one founder is 4,185 visitors a month, which the content plan could plausibly produce (docs/BUSINESS.md:952).","Hitting it means the founder is paid, which is the only threshold that changes anything."],"flip":"If the developer-tool channel in (c) is sized and comes back large, the ceiling moves and ₹20 lakh becomes arguable; until someone sizes it, it is a hope with a big number attached.","linked":["B2"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:292","docs/BUSINESS.md:164","docs/BUSINESS.md:243","docs/BUSINESS.md:249","docs/BUSINESS.md:253","docs/BUSINESS.md:940","docs/BUSINESS.md:941","docs/BUSINESS.md:952","docs/BUSINESS.md:1080","docs/BUSINESS.md:1084","docs/BUSINESS.md:1086","docs/BUSINESS.md:1088","docs/CRITIQUE.md:1459"]},{"id":"B14","cat":"Business & operations","sub":"Compliance ops","weight":"high","q":"Which statutory work happens before the pilot — the CERT-In filing and runbook, the grievance officer, a written GST opinion, or none of it?","lede":"The obligations that bind today have no size floor, no owner and no artefact, and one of them runs on a six-hour clock.","visual":{"kind":"timeline","items":[{"when":"today","label":"CERT-In, six hours from noticing","note":"no size floor; Annexure II filing missing","tone":"stop"},{"when":"today","label":"SPDI Rules: policy, consent, grievance officer","note":"redress within one month; nobody named","tone":"warn"},{"when":"today","label":"SPDI Rule 7 transfer gate","note":"processor agreements due now, not in 2027","tone":"warn"},{"when":"2026-11-13","label":"DPDP §6(9) and §27(1)(d)","note":"first substantive tranche","tone":"neutral"},{"when":"2027-05-13","label":"DPDP §§3–17 and the penalty chapter","note":"247 days out from the plan's date","tone":"neutral"}],"note":"The register had this backwards until round 2; the live regime is the IT Act and the SPDI Rules (GAPS-2026-09-08.md:129).","caption":"What binds now, against what the plan was written against"},"stakes":"A missed statutory clock is a violation rather than a delay, and it attaches to the pilot, not to revenue.","state":["The plan names the six-hour CERT-In duty and records that the Annexure II point-of-contact filing is missing everywhere (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:543).","A grievance officer is due now under SPDI Rule 5(9) with a one-month window, and no name is published (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:548).","The GST risk row quotes only the harder of two rows in our own verification table (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:330).","None of it appears in the week-0 list (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:351)."],"path":["Round 2 found the register had the DPDP timeline backwards; the penalties commence 2027-05-13 (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:129).","That moved the IT Act and the SPDI Rules into the present tense (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:542).","On tax, one row was refuted and one revised, and they have never been reconciled (docs/VERIFICATION.md:40, docs/VERIFICATION.md:41)."],"tension":["CGST §24(iii) says reverse-charge payers shall be registered with no turnover floor; the other row says an unregistered recipient is charged GST by the vendor.","The company already buys foreign services, so whichever reading is right, it is operative now (docs/BUSINESS.md:719).","Registration adds monthly filing to a compliance load already priced at 17 hours a month, before any revenue.","A CA answers the tax question in an hour with the invoices; no document in this repository can."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"Live today, not in 2027","items":[["CERT-In breach report","within 6 hours of noticing, to incident@cert-in.org.in","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:543"],["Size floor","none","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:543"],["Annexure II point-of-contact filing","missing everywhere in our record","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:543"],["IT Act §70B(7) exposure","up to one year or ₹1 lakh; §70B(8) requires a CERT-In officer's complaint first","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:543"],["Grievance officer under SPDI Rule 5(9)","one named person, redress within one month","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:542, 548"],["Log residency","180 days of ICT logs inside Indian jurisdiction, NTP to NIC or NPL","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:544"]]},{"type":"table","title":"What a 21-day founder absence does to the clock (r26-c9-capacity.md:149-156)","cols":["Domain","Consequence"],"rows":[["Statutory","CERT-In's 6 hours from noticing; DPDP §8(6); GDPR Art. 33 at 72 hours — not recoverable"],["On-call","zero responders; Better Stack's free tier covers one"],["Support","103 to 144 tickets queue against a 24-hour email expectation"],["Billing","about 8 involuntary churns, on a rail with one attempt and no retry"],["The nut","client retainers carry their own SLA; missing three weeks risks the funding source"]]},{"type":"table","title":"The two rows, as recorded in VERIFICATION.md","cols":["Row","Verdict","What it says"],"rows":[["8 — RCM bounded by the registration threshold","REFUTED","CGST §24(iii): reverse-charge payers \"shall be required to be registered\", no turnover floor (VERIFICATION.md:41)"],["7 — RCM on imported services","REVISED","Notification 10/2017-IGST(R) Sl.1 excludes a \"non-taxable online recipient\"; unregistered means the vendor charges GST, registered means you self-assess (VERIFICATION.md:40)"],["The plan's risk register","quotes row 8 only","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:330"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"The foreign services already being bought","items":[["Model access","Claude Sonnet 5 at $2/$10 per MTok","BUSINESS.md:719, fetched 2026-08-30"],["Edge compute","Cloudflare Workers Paid, $5/month minimum per account","BUSINESS.md:719, fetched 2026-08-30"],["Object storage","R2 at $0.015/GB-month","BUSINESS.md:719"],["Payment rail","Dodo Payments, 4% + 15¢ on Indian cards","BUSINESS.md:719"],["Apple Developer Program","$99 per membership year","BUSINESS.md:719"],["CA retainer already budgeted","₹35,000–₹90,000 a year, quotes not yet obtained","BUSINESS.md:678"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Do the whole pack in week 0: file, runbook, grievance officer, CA opinion","what":"The point-of-contact filing, a six-hour incident runbook, a named grievance officer and a written GST position all land before the pilot.","gains":["Converts the only live criminal-adjacent exposure into a filed form and a page","The grievance name belongs on the site, so it costs no engineering","The CA retainer is already in the budget (docs/BUSINESS.md:678)"],"costs":["Hours taken from a schedule already short of engineering days","The runbook has to be revised once B16 settles what data we hold"],"system":"No change.","screens":"A grievance and privacy page on the site.","money":"₹35,000–₹90,000 a year CA retainer, already budgeted."},{"k":"b","label":"CERT-In filing and runbook now; grievance officer now; tax at first revenue","what":"The clock-bearing duties are discharged before the pilot and the GST position waits for a first invoice.","gains":["Deals with the only six-hour clock first, which is the one that cannot be recovered","Defers the item with the least immediate exposure"],"costs":["The GST obligation, if it exists, attaches to purchases already being made","Deferring accrues rather than avoids"],"system":"No change.","screens":"A grievance page.","money":"Nothing today; an accrued position of unknown size."},{"k":"c","label":"File everything at the first paying customer","what":"Nothing is filed until there is revenue to protect.","gains":["Defers all of it, at zero cost today","Nothing is written twice if B16 changes what we hold"],"costs":["The directions bind every body corporate with no size floor, so the pilot is covered","The work never gets cheaper, only more urgent at a worse moment"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None today."},{"k":"d","label":"Wait for B16, since the answer changes what data we hold","what":"The runbook and the filing wait until the Firebase question settles the incident surface.","gains":["Logical ordering: no documents held means a much smaller surface to write for","Avoids writing the runbook twice"],"costs":["B16 has no date, so this is deferral with a reason attached","The filing itself does not depend on the answer at all"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None today."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["The filing is a form and the runbook is a page, and both get more urgent rather than cheaper.","Two rows of our own verification table disagree on GST, and neither was written by anyone holding the invoices.","The grievance officer is due now and appears on the site rather than in code, so it costs no engineering day."],"flip":"If B16 lands within days, write the runbook after it rather than before, but file the point of contact first, because the filing does not depend on the answer.","linked":["B18","B8","L4"],"sources":["merged: B15","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:330","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:351","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:541","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:542","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:543","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:548","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:129","docs/VERIFICATION.md:40","docs/VERIFICATION.md:41","docs/BUSINESS.md:678","docs/BUSINESS.md:719","docs/BUSINESS.md:771","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r26-c9-capacity.md:149"]},{"id":"B21","cat":"Business & operations","sub":"Endgame","weight":"high","q":"What are we building toward — an independent business we keep, or a team and a codebase somebody buys?","lede":"Absorption is the modal outcome in this graveyard, and the plan has no sentence about the ending it wants.","visual":{"kind":"timeline","items":[{"when":"2014-05-30","label":"Editorially closes","note":"\"Even if all of our users paid up, it wouldn't be enough.\"","tone":"stop"},{"when":"2016-03-01","label":"Poetica bought by Condé Nast","note":"dead by 2016-06-01; the goals were at odds","tone":"stop"},{"when":"2020-03-03","label":"Atrium shuts after $75.5M","note":"raised, scaled, closed","tone":"stop"},{"when":"2025-01-31","label":"Almanac shuts after $45M","note":"cause stated as capacity, not demand","tone":"stop"},{"when":"today","label":"Obsidian: 8 staff, no investors","note":"per-seat licence made optional 2025-02-20","tone":"good"}],"note":"Four of the eight dead products in this set were bought as teams by organisations that already owned a publishing pipeline.","caption":"How this category ends, and the one that did not"},"stakes":"The ending decides the price, the ownership, the not-building list and whether the sidecar format is open, and none of those can be reversed cheaply later.","state":["The plan has no exit section. Strengths, weaknesses, opportunities and threats stop at the market (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:557).","The decision layer refuses a raise on the mismatch between 367 months of runway and a seven-year fund horizon (docs/DECIDE.md:150).","The family section already sells services around the product, which is an independent shape (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:482)."],"path":["The dead-product research assembled eight comparable products with dates and stated causes.","In one, the acquirer took the software and closed it to the users within three months.","Dendron's founder gave the cause of death as no product-market fit for a venture-backed business, which is a statement about the ending rather than the product."],"tension":["An acquirer that already owns a publishing pipeline wants the engine and the team, and has no use for the users.","Building to be bought argues for a proprietary sidecar and a closed format; building to keep argues for the opposite.","Litera consolidated this adjacent category, self-reporting growth from $16M to about $250M revenue and 15,000 customers.","Obsidian is the counter-case: 8 staff, no investors, and it made its per-seat licence optional rather than enforcing it."],"evidence":[],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Independent, permanently. Write it down, with the sidecar format published","what":"The plan states that the company is not for sale, and the sidecar schema is documented so anyone can read it without us.","gains":["Matches the architecture already chosen: files stay the user's and exit is free","Makes the refusal to raise coherent rather than a preference","An open format is the strongest promise a byte-exact product can make"],"costs":["Forfeits the modal outcome in this category, which is being bought","An open sidecar is the one asset an acquirer would pay for"],"system":"The sidecar schema is published and versioned.","screens":"A format page in the docs.","money":"No acquisition premium, ever."},{"k":"b","label":"Build to be acquired by a docs platform, CMS or agent vendor","what":"The engine, the sidecar and the team are shaped as something an acquirer can absorb, and the plan says so internally.","gains":["Absorption is what actually happens to products in this set","An acquirer with a pipeline gets distribution we cannot buy"],"costs":["Four of the eight dead products were bought as teams and the software went with them","In one case the acquirer took the software and refused the users","It argues against publishing the format, which contradicts the product's own promise"],"system":"Proprietary sidecar; no open format commitment.","screens":"None.","money":"One-time, unpredictable, and it ends the product."},{"k":"c","label":"Independent by default, with a written price at which we would sell","what":"The company is built to keep, the format is published, and one paragraph records what an offer would have to cover.","gains":["Removes the question from every future cash scare","Keeps the open-format promise, which is the product's differentiator","Costs a paragraph and settles a conversation that otherwise recurs"],"costs":["A written number can leak or age badly","It is a decision made without ever having met an acquirer"],"system":"Sidecar published; nothing else changes.","screens":"A format page.","money":"None today."},{"k":"d","label":"Leave it open","what":"No position is recorded and the question is answered when it arrives.","gains":["Costs nothing today","No position to defend to a buyer, a user or a fund"],"costs":["The format decision gets made by default, and defaults favour the closed version","The question returns under pressure, which is the worst moment to answer it"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"c","recCase":["The architecture already chose independence: files stay the user's, exit is free, and there is no lock-in to sell.","Publishing the sidecar schema is the one commitment that makes that architecture credible, and it is incompatible with building to be bought.","A written price costs a paragraph and stops the question returning at every cash scare."],"flip":"An approach from an acquirer that would keep the users and the format, which is the case none of the four absorbed products got.","linked":["B12","B2"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:482","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:557","docs/DECIDE.md:150","docs/CRITIQUE.md:1766"]},{"id":"B18","cat":"Business & operations","sub":"Continuity","weight":"medium","q":"Do we run a five-day laptop-off drill before the first paying user, or accept bus factor zero?","lede":"One person carries the funding, the calendar, the support queue and a six-hour statutory clock, and nobody has tested an absence.","visual":{"kind":"arch","layers":[{"label":"Funding","items":["Client retainers carry their own SLA"],"side":"0 responders","tone":"stop"},{"label":"Statutory","items":["CERT-In 6 hours","GDPR Art. 33 at 72 hours"],"side":"not recoverable","tone":"stop"},{"label":"Billing","items":["One debit attempt, no retry","About 8 involuntary churns in 21 days"],"side":"manual, after the fact","tone":"warn"},{"label":"Support","items":["103 to 144 tickets queue"],"side":"weeks to clear","tone":"warn"}],"note":"Figures for a 21-day absence at default-alive (r26-c9-capacity.md:149-156).","caption":"Four layers, one person, no cover on any of them"},"stakes":"An absence hits the funding source, the calendar, the support promise and the statutory clock at the same moment, because they are all the same person.","state":["The risk register lists ten risks and founder unavailability is not one of them (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:319).","The operating rules name no second responder (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:533).","The capacity research proposed the drill and it has not been scheduled (docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r26-c9-capacity.md:162)."],"path":["The capacity work modelled a 21-day absence across six domains and found every one exposed (r26-c9-capacity.md:149).","Its closing note is that a risk register with weekly checks and no checker is documentation of intent (r26-c9-capacity.md:181).","The same report proposed the cheapest possible test: five days off, with a written list of what broke."],"tension":["Indian card mandates get exactly one attempt, so a failed renewal during an absence is terminal for that cycle (docs/BUSINESS.md:140).","Before the pilot there is almost nothing running, so a drill would test very little.","Before the first paying user there is something to break and breaking it is still cheap.","Five working days is a real cost against a schedule that has few of them."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"What a 21-day absence costs at default-alive (r26-c9-capacity.md:149-156)","cols":["Domain","Consequence","Recovery"],"rows":[["Support","103 to 144 tickets queue against a 24-hour email expectation","weeks, arriving at a founder already behind"],["On-call","zero responders; Better Stack's free tier covers one","the page is simply not answered"],["Billing","147 monthly renewals × 8% single-attempt failure ≈ 8 involuntary churns in 21 days","manual, per user, after the fact"],["Statutory","CERT-In 6 hours; DPDP §8(6); GDPR Art. 33 at 72 hours","not recoverable — a missed clock is a violation"],["Roadmap","19.3 points = 9.8% of the 196-point plan","pushes every downstream date"],["The nut","client retainers carry their own SLA","the retainer is 100% of the funding"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"Why the rail makes it worse","items":[["Indian card e-mandate attempts per cycle","exactly one; no smart retries, no cascade","BUSINESS.md:140, 205"],["Assumed single-attempt failure rate","8%","BUSINESS.md:771"],["Pre-debit notice","sent by the issuer 24 hours ahead, in the bank's own wording, with a cancel affordance","BUSINESS.md:203"],["Dunning ladder length","T+0, T+3, T+7, T+10, terminal","BUSINESS.md:142-148"],["Founder-hours per paying user per month","0.1445","BUSINESS.md:779"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Run the five-day drill before the pilot starts","what":"The founder goes dark for five working days while ten strangers hold free accounts.","gains":["Cheapest possible moment, because nothing much can break","Happens before the schedule is under pressure"],"costs":["Tests almost nothing: no renewals, no queue, no incident surface","Spends five days of the pre-pilot schedule for a weak result"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"Five working days."},{"k":"b","label":"Run it before the first paying user","what":"The drill happens once billing, dunning, the support queue and the incident path exist, and what broke becomes the runbook.","gains":["Tests the systems that actually matter, at the last moment breaking them is cheap","The written list of what broke is a better runbook than anything written from imagination","Converts an argument into a measurement"],"costs":["Five working days from a schedule that has few","Some things will break in front of real users"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"Five working days, plus whatever the drill surfaces."},{"k":"c","label":"Write a continuity runbook without running a drill","what":"An afternoon of writing captures the obvious failure modes and names who covers what.","gains":["An afternoon, not a week, and it captures the obvious items","Something exists in writing before the first paying user"],"costs":["A runbook nobody has executed is documentation of intent","That is the exact pattern the capacity report already named twice"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"Half a day."},{"k":"d","label":"Accept it. One founder, no drill, no runbook","what":"Nothing changes and the exposure stands.","gains":["Free until it is not","Five working days stay in the schedule"],"costs":["Every clock in the compliance table keeps running during an absence","The funding line has its own SLA and no cover"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None until an absence."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["Before the first paying user is the last moment when a five-day outage is a test rather than an incident.","It is also the first moment when there is anything worth testing.","Write down what broke; that list is the runbook, and a better one than imagination produces."],"flip":"If B1 resolves to two people with a real split, the drill still runs but its result changes meaning, because one absence would then cost the calendar or the nut, not both.","linked":["B1","B14"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:319","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:533","docs/BUSINESS.md:140","docs/BUSINESS.md:142","docs/BUSINESS.md:203","docs/BUSINESS.md:205","docs/BUSINESS.md:771","docs/BUSINESS.md:779","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r26-c9-capacity.md:149","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r26-c9-capacity.md:162","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r26-c9-capacity.md:181"]},{"id":"L1","cat":"Legal, privacy & data","sub":"Data holding","weight":"critical","q":"Do we delete the Firebase document-holding design, or adopt it and take the fiduciary and intermediary duty that follows?","lede":"Three committed files give three answers, and every legal rule in §22 is a function of this one.","_ev":["L1"],"visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":190,"cols":[{"title":"Delete the design","tone":"accent"},{"title":"Adopt as written","tone":"stop"},{"title":"Keep, drop public read","tone":"warn"}],"rows":[{"label":"What we hold","cells":["identity, teams, billing","note bodies and revisions","note bodies and revisions"]},{"label":"Our status","cells":["no duty over documents","fiduciary and intermediary","fiduciary only"]},{"label":"Ceiling on content","cells":["none, no content held","₹250 crore, DPDP §8(5)","₹250 crore, DPDP §8(5)"]},{"label":"Publishing apparatus","cells":["none","74 founder-hours","none"]},{"label":"Engineering cost today","cells":["zero, nothing writes to it","build the store","build the store"]},{"label":"Forecloses","cells":["hosted viewer, server search","nothing","public share links"]}],"note":"Ceiling from the DPDP Schedule; 74 hours itemised at PRD v2 line 4194","caption":"What each answer holds, and what duty comes with it"},"stakes":"Adopting it puts document content under a ₹250 crore security ceiling and makes us an intermediary before there is one user.","state":["`firestore.rules:318` caps a note body at 900,000 characters, `:361` makes revisions undeletable, and `:393` allows an unauthenticated `get` on any public share.","`docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:4295` says we hold user documents. `docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:133` says the control plane holds no document bytes.","Nothing writes to Firestore. The rules file calls itself a prototype at `firestore.rules:7` and says harden before taking paid signups."],"path":["`firestore.rules` landed with the Firebase backend commit and nobody deleted it when the plan moved local-first.","The round-2 sweep found the contradiction on 2026-09-08 (`docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:142`) and made it decision 7 (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:365`)."],"tension":["Holding bytes confers intermediary status under IT Act §2(1)(w), which drags in the 74 founder-hours itemised at `docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:4194`.","The one claim a server-side rival cannot copy is that the documents never reach us (`docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:10104`).","Decision 3's hosted read-only viewer needs a server store, so closing this forecloses it (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:367`)."],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Defer past the pilot","what":"Leave the three files contradicting each other and decide after the ten-stranger test.","gains":["Costs nothing this week"],"costs":["§22 cannot be finalised, so no privacy policy can be written","A pilot with no published policy breaches SPDI Rule 4 today"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Delete `firestore.rules` and write zero document bytes into §22 as a constraint","what":"The control plane holds identity, team membership, entitlements and billing, and nothing else.","gains":["Legal surface collapses to identity and billing","Keeps the sentence a server-side rival cannot say","Costs no engineering: zero Firestore writes exist"],"costs":["Forecloses hosted publishing, server search and decision 3's viewer","Deletes the only written data model for a server store"],"system":"Firestore schema removed; §22 gains a hard architectural constraint.","screens":"Kills the hosted-viewer screen before it is drawn.","money":"None today. Forfeits any tier priced on server-side storage."},{"k":"c","label":"Adopt the Firebase design as written","what":"We store note bodies and an append-only revision history, and serve public reads to anyone.","gains":["Hosted sync, server-side search and publishing all become possible","A written data model already exists"],"costs":["Document content falls under §8(5), ceiling ₹250 crore","Intermediary status and 74 founder-hours before the first stranger"],"system":"Firestore becomes the store of record and every §22 row is rewritten.","screens":"Adds a share manager, a revision history and a moderation console.","money":"Storage and egress at scale, plus counsel for a policy saying we can read documents."},{"k":"d","label":"Hold documents server-side but delete the unauthenticated public-read path","what":"We keep a server store and drop the anonymous `get` at `firestore.rules:393`.","gains":["Intermediary duty mostly falls away","Hosted sync and server search stay available"],"costs":["Fiduciary duty over content stays, with the ₹250 crore ceiling","Still needs processor agreements, an Indian log store and breach cover"],"system":"One rule deleted. The store and its duties remain.","screens":"No share page for strangers; any hosted viewer stays behind sign-in.","money":"Storage cost plus the processor paperwork in L10."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["Nothing writes to Firestore across 226 source files, so deleting the design costs no engineering.","The cost model at 10,000 users and the strongest marketing claim both rest on holding no bytes (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:133`).","Adoption would be the largest available expansion of legal surface, taken before there is a user to justify it."],"flip":"If decision 3 lands on a hosted read-only viewer, or a paying team refuses to buy without server-side search, (c) is the honest minimum and the ₹250 crore surface must be budgeted.","linked":["F19","L16","L6","P13","PL12"],"sources":["firestore.rules:7","firestore.rules:318","firestore.rules:361","firestore.rules:393","docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:4194","docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:4204","docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:4295","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:133","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:365","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:367","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:142","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:9056","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:10100","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:10104"],"dupes":{"dropped":["B16","P8"],"why":"Do we hold user documents, i.e. does firestore.rules ship or get deleted. Same poles in all three (delete / adopt as written / keep server-side minus public read / defer). Recs split a/d/a. Legal, privacy & data owns it because the fiduciary and intermediary duty is the whole stake; P8's permalink option survives in F19."}},{"id":"L3","cat":"Legal, privacy & data","sub":"Live exposure","weight":"critical","q":"Do we treat every legal clock in §22 as already running, or as starting at the pilot?","lede":"sgnk-md is the same codebase and is listed as production. If it has users, the clocks started when the first one signed in.","_ev":["L3"],"visual":{"kind":"flow","nodes":[{"label":"sgnk-md listed as production","note":"202 of 228 files shared","tone":"warn"},{"label":"Google sign-in, not allowlisted","note":"collects email at first run","tone":"stop"},{"label":"Has any non-founder signed in?","note":"nobody has asked","tone":"warn"},{"label":"Yes: policy and officer overdue","note":"due at the first signup","tone":"stop"},{"label":"No: the pilot is the trigger","note":"every §22 deadline stands","tone":"good"}],"perRow":3,"note":"GitHub sign-in is allowlisted at auth-options.ts:80; Google sign-in is not","caption":"One unanswered question re-dates four other decisions"},"stakes":"If the answer is yes, the published policy, the consent step and the named officer were all due months ago and the six-hour clock ran with nobody on it.","state":["`docs/DECIDE.md:168` records that frontmatter is sgnk-md: 202 of 228 shared source files byte-identical, zero unique to `md`.","`docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:36` records the portfolio listing sgnk-md as production and asks the founders whether there is a user list.","`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:558` says zero users. Both statements cannot be true."],"path":["The fork was found in the round-2 sweep as a cost finding (`docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:141`), and nobody followed it through to the legal consequence.","`docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:146` still lists sgnk-md's own users among the things never measured."],"tension":["The GitHub sign-in gate is an allowlist on one login (`src/modules/auth/infrastructure/auth-options.ts:80`), which is evidence about HEAD, not about what the July deployment allowed.","Google sign-in is not behind that allowlist and collects email at first run (`src/modules/auth/infrastructure/firebase-auth-gateway.ts:30`).","Zero interviews have been conducted across the whole programme (`docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:35`), so nobody has asked those users anything either."],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Ask the founders first, then act on the answer in the same week","what":"One question in the meeting: has any non-founder ever signed in, and is there a user list.","gains":["Costs five minutes and settles which set of clocks is running","The same list is the only interview pool the product has"],"costs":["Nothing moves until the meeting happens","A verbal answer is not a deployment log"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Assume live: file the point of contact, publish the policy and the grievance page this week","what":"We act as if the duties are already overdue and close them before the meeting.","gains":["No downside if the assumption is wrong","Buys the pilot a clean starting position"],"costs":["About a day of work brought forward","A policy written before L1 and L2 are settled may need rewriting"],"system":"No change.","screens":"Adds /privacy, /terms and /grievance.","money":"None beyond founder time."},{"k":"c","label":"Take the sgnk-md deployment offline until the question is settled","what":"The sibling deployment stops serving anyone.","gains":["Removes any live exposure immediately"],"costs":["Kills the only real user population the product has ever had","Loses the interview pool GAPS:36 names"],"system":"One deployment paused.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Assume dormant because the GitHub allowlist gates sign-in","what":"We treat the pilot as the first collection of anyone's personal data.","gains":["Every §22 deadline stands as written","No work brought forward"],"costs":["Rests on one code path in the current HEAD","Says nothing about Google sign-in, which is not gated"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["This is the cheapest question on the list and it re-dates L4, L7 and L17.","It needs a founder, not research: is there a user list, and may ten of them be contacted.","If the answer is yes, (b) follows the same week; if no, the pilot is the trigger and nothing is brought forward."],"flip":"A deployment log showing non-founder sign-ins makes (b) mandatory rather than prudent.","linked":["L17","L4","L7"],"sources":["docs/DECIDE.md:168","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:35","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:36","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:141","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:146","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:558","src/modules/auth/infrastructure/auth-options.ts:80","src/modules/auth/infrastructure/firebase-auth-gateway.ts:30"]},{"id":"L4","cat":"Legal, privacy & data","sub":"Breach response","weight":"critical","q":"Who answers the six-hour clock, and do we file the CERT-In point of contact before there is anything to report?","lede":"A six-hour clock with no size floor, one person at 1.21 engineering days a week, and no filed contact.","_ev":["L4","L5"],"visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":180,"cols":[{"title":"File, runbook, best effort","tone":"warn"},{"title":"File, then shrink","tone":"accent"},{"title":"File and pay a rota","tone":"neutral"}],"rows":[{"label":"Who answers at 03:00","cells":["one founder, if awake","one founder","a paid second responder"]},{"label":"Reportable surface","cells":["25 routes, five AI vendors","identity and billing only","unchanged"]},{"label":"Detection today","cells":["none in package.json","little left to detect","alerting must be bought"]},{"label":"Six-hour clock","cells":["best effort, stated","rarely fires","genuinely covered"]},{"label":"Cost","cells":["one day","forecloses the web trial","money and a second credential holder"]}],"note":"Capacity from PRODUCT-BRIEF line 11; the clock from line 543","caption":"Three postures against a clock one person cannot staff"},"stakes":"A reportable incident with no filed contact, no runbook and no logs is the first thing an insurer, an acquirer or an enterprise buyer will find.","state":["`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:543` states the clock and then records the gap: the Annexure II point-of-contact filing is missing everywhere in our record.","The team is one person: 1.21 engineering days per calendar week and 80 of 80 commits by a single author (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:11`, `:12`).","No runbook, roster, pager or alert path exists, and `package.json` carries no Sentry, PostHog, Plausible or logging dependency."],"path":["The CERT-In Directions of 28.04.2022 were read into the record twice (`docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:4122`, `docs/BUSINESS.md:25`) and both passes missed the point-of-contact duty.","An incident runbook was written on 2026-08-29 (`docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:3697`) and never reached the plan.","The v15 sweep restored the six-hour clock to §22 and did not restore the runbook or ask who runs it."],"tension":["The clock starts on noticing, so detection gates everything, and there is no detection.","IT Act §70B(7) carries up to one year or ₹1 lakh, though §70B(8) needs a CERT-In officer's complaint first.","The surface that would generate an incident is server-side by construction, which is exactly what L1 and L2 propose to remove."],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"File nothing and rely on §70B(8) needing a CERT-In officer's complaint","what":"We treat the reporting duty as unenforceable at our size and leave the record's gap open.","gains":["Costs nothing"],"costs":["Fails the first security questionnaire and any insurer's proposal form","Leaves a named omission in a document a buyer will read"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"File the point of contact now, write the runbook, and state a best-effort clock","what":"The founder is named, an alert reaches a phone, and the plan says plainly that six hours is best effort.","gains":["About a day of work and honest on the face of it","Closes the one gap the record itself flags"],"costs":["A solo founder cannot guarantee six hours","Leaves the whole server-side surface reportable"],"system":"Adds alerting to the deploy and a runbook to the repo.","screens":"None.","money":"Free tier alerting; founder time."},{"k":"c","label":"File now, then shrink the surface until a reportable incident is near impossible","what":"No server-side documents, no publishing, no hosted AI, so a breach can expose only identity and billing.","gains":["Cuts the reportable surface to its smallest set","Costs nothing extra: L1 and L2 already point here"],"costs":["Forecloses the web trial and hosted publishing","Does not remove the duty, only the likely trigger"],"system":"Same change as L1(a) and L2(a); no new work.","screens":"Removes the share and hosted-AI surfaces.","money":"Forfeits any hosted tier."},{"k":"d","label":"File now and pay a second responder onto a rota before the pilot","what":"A contractor or the second founder shares an on-call schedule with production credentials.","gains":["Real coverage of a clock we otherwise cannot meet","Answers the first enterprise security questionnaire"],"costs":["Money, and a second holder of production credentials","Expands the access-revocation surface at `docs/BUSINESS.md:767`"],"system":"Credential issue and revocation runbook required.","screens":"None.","money":"A retainer before there is revenue."}],"rec":"c","recCase":["The only durable answer to a clock you cannot staff is a smaller surface, and L1 and L2 already point at it.","Filing is an hour of work and appears in three of the four options, so the real choice here is the surface, not the form.","Take (a) alongside it: the runbook and the named person are needed whatever the surface, and the filing requires the name anyway."],"flip":"The first paying team that requires hosted sync makes (c) compulsory, and its cost belongs in the team tier price rather than in the founder's nights.","linked":["B14","L1","L14"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:11","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:12","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:543","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:3697","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:4105","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:4122","docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:4198","docs/BUSINESS.md:25","docs/BUSINESS.md:767","package.json","merged: L5"]},{"id":"L6","cat":"Legal, privacy & data","sub":"Publishing","weight":"critical","q":"Do we close the shipped publishing surface to founder-only, and adopt noindex and system slugs as a standing rule?","lede":"A crawlable public page with user-chosen slugs makes us an intermediary, and none of the apparatus that comes with it exists.","_ev":["L6","L9"],"visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":180,"cols":[{"title":"Closed to founder","tone":"accent"},{"title":"Narrow shape","tone":"warn"},{"title":"As shipped today","tone":"stop"}],"rows":[{"label":"Who can publish","cells":["nobody but us","paying accounts","any signed-in user"]},{"label":"Indexable","cells":["not served","noindex, nofollow ugc","index true, follow true"]},{"label":"Slug","cells":["not applicable","system-assigned","user-chosen, 1 to 60 chars"]},{"label":"Grievance clock","cells":["none","24-hour ack, 15-day resolve","24-hour ack, 15-day resolve"]},{"label":"Preservation store","cells":["none","180 days","180 days, unbuilt"]},{"label":"Founder-hours due first","cells":["0","74","0, and none of it exists"]}],"note":"Controls from RECORD line 4181; the narrow shape from PRD v2 line 4204","caption":"The publishing surface: who reaches it, and what it drags in"},"stakes":"Open it as configured and we take a permanent 24-hour grievance clock, a 36-hour court-order clock and safe-harbour conditions we cannot meet.","state":["`src/app/(public)/[slug]/page.tsx:30` sets `robots: { index: true, follow: true }` and `src/app/robots.ts:18` allows crawlers at `/`.","`src/modules/share/domain/slug.ts:4` makes the slug user-chosen, and `src/app/api/share/route.ts:25` gates publishing on sign-in alone with no tier check.","Outbound links get `noopener noreferrer`, not `nofollow ugc` (`src/modules/preview/presentation/markdown/html-policy.ts:214`)."],"path":["The share surface is inherited from sgnk-md and predates the plan's no-hosting rule at `docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:43`.","The abuse ranking put SEO spam and backlink farms first and named the controls (`docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:4181`); PRD v2 then recommended exactly that narrow shape at `:4204`.","The plan's own §9 design already sets noindex, nofollow as the default (`docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:9392`), so the code contradicts the plan as well as the research."],"tension":["IT Act §79 safe harbour is conditional on the 2021 due-diligence set, and losing it makes the founder a co-defendant on the underlying claim.","74 founder-hours at 1.21 engineering days a week is about seven and a half weeks, and §14's twelve-week plan never schedules it.","Decision 3's hosted read-only viewer is unresolved, and closing publishing pre-empts it (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:367`)."],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Delete the share module","what":"The public route, the slug rules and the reserved list all come out of the repo.","gains":["Removes the exposure permanently","One less surface for L16's review to cover"],"costs":["Forecloses decision 3's hosted viewer, which the plan has not closed","Throws away code that mostly works"],"system":"Share module removed; reserved-slug list retired.","screens":"Kills the public note page.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Open it under PRD v2's narrow shape and build the 74-hour apparatus first","what":"Paid accounts only, noindex, system slugs, per-account cap, with a grievance flow and a preservation store.","gains":["Keeps the feature and cuts the abuse surface sharply","Produces the artefacts a B2B buyer asks for"],"costs":["74 founder-hours does not fit before week 1 of the pilot","The 24-hour clock then runs every day, permanently"],"system":"Adds a report form, a ticket store, a preservation store and an action log.","screens":"Adds a report page, a grievance page and a moderation console.","money":"Seven and a half weeks of founder time at the measured rate."},{"k":"c","label":"Open it as configured today and keep the indexable pages for distribution","what":"Any signed-in user publishes a root-level, crawlable page under a slug they choose.","gains":["Keeps the organic channel argument alive"],"costs":["Ships the shape the abuse research ranked first, with no takedown apparatus","Cloudflare terminates accounts for user-chosen deceptive names"],"system":"No change, which is the problem.","screens":"None.","money":"None, until a takedown arrives."},{"k":"d","label":"Gate publishing to founder-only, with noindex and system slugs as a standing rule","what":"The route stays in the code, serves nobody else, and the configuration rule binds the day it reopens.","gains":["One line of gating removes intermediary exposure during the pilot","Buys back roughly seven weeks of apparatus work"],"costs":["Loses whatever distribution a public page brings","Pre-empts decision 3 unless it is revisited"],"system":"One route gate, plus a written configuration rule in §21.","screens":"The public note page is unreachable for anyone else.","money":"None."}],"rec":"d","recCase":["Publishing is not on the MVP-0 critical path; §14's twelve-week plan never schedules it.","It is the single feature that turns a tool into an intermediary with a permanent 24-hour clock.","The standing rule costs nothing to hold while publishing is closed and binds automatically the day it opens, so it is worth setting once.","The plan already refuses a footer backlink for the same reason (`docs/BUSINESS.md:1046`), so indexable user pages would contradict settled reasoning."],"flip":"If decision 3 lands on the hosted viewer as the thing Pro sells, (b) is the shape, the 74 hours enter the schedule ahead of the pilot, and the tier price has to carry them.","linked":["G12","L1","L16","L7"],"sources":["src/app/(public)/[slug]/page.tsx:30","src/app/robots.ts:18","src/app/api/share/route.ts:25","src/modules/share/domain/slug.ts:4","src/modules/share/domain/slug.ts:26","src/modules/share/domain/slug.ts:43","src/modules/preview/presentation/markdown/html-policy.ts:214","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:43","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:365","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:367","docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:4194","docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:4204","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:4105","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:4115","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:4181","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:4187","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:9392","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:9403","docs/BUSINESS.md:1046","merged: L9"]},{"id":"L7","cat":"Legal, privacy & data","sub":"Policy pages","weight":"high","q":"Do we publish a privacy policy, terms and a named grievance officer before the pilot, and which redressal window do they promise?","lede":"SPDI Rule 4 requires a published policy today, the app has four pages, and none of them is a policy.","_ev":["L7","L8"],"visual":{"kind":"screen","title":"Pages served on the live app","panes":[{"label":"Exists today","w":1,"rows":[{"label":"/login","meta":"sign-in, the first screen","mark":"live","tone":"neutral"},{"label":"/<slug>","meta":"public note, unauthenticated","mark":"live","tone":"warn"},{"label":"/p/<slug>","meta":"301 redirect","mark":"legacy","tone":"sunk"},{"label":"/ vault","meta":"the editor","mark":"live","tone":"neutral"}]},{"label":"Due now, absent","w":1,"rows":[{"label":"/privacy","meta":"SPDI Rule 4, live regime","mark":"missing","tone":"stop"},{"label":"/terms","meta":"IT Rules 3(1)(a) once publishing opens","mark":"missing","tone":"stop"},{"label":"/grievance","meta":"named officer, SPDI Rule 5(9)","mark":"missing","tone":"stop"},{"label":"consent before collection","meta":"sign-in is the first screen","mark":"missing","tone":"stop"}]}],"note":"privacy and terms are reserved slugs with no route behind them; grievance is not reserved","caption":"Four pages exist; the three the live regime requires do not"},"stakes":"The pilot puts ten strangers into an app that takes an email at first run with no notice, no consent step and no page to point at.","state":["`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:542` lists as due now: a published privacy policy, consent before collection, a named grievance officer within one month, and a transfer gate.","`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:548` adds the ninety-day ceiling from 2027-05-13 and notes §13(3) makes our channel the mandatory first stop before the Board.","No person is named anywhere in the corpus, and `privacy` and `terms` are reserved slugs with no route behind them (`src/modules/share/domain/slug.ts:43`)."],"path":["The v15 sweep corrected a register that had assumed DPDP was operative, which moved the policy duty from 2027 to today.","The IT Rules version, 24-hour acknowledgement and 15-day resolution, was researched on 2026-08-29 (`docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:4115`) and never reached §22.","`docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:4194` budgets 12 founder-hours for terms, privacy policy and acceptable use together."],"tension":["The window depends on L6: closed publishing owes SPDI's one month, open publishing owes 24 hours and 15 days, 365 days a year.","A published window is a promise, and missing your own published window is worse than publishing a modest one.","`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:536` says email is collected only when an obligation exists and never at first run, which the sign-in screen already contradicts."],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"A written notice by hand to each of the ten, full pages at MVP-1","what":"Each pilot participant gets a one-page notice; nothing is published on the site.","gains":["Proportionate to ten known participants and cheap"],"costs":["Does not satisfy the published-policy duty while anyone else can reach the app","Today anyone can reach the app"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Publish all three before the pilot, self-drafted, one month, founder named","what":"Twelve hours of writing produces a policy, terms and a grievance page matching the duty that actually binds.","gains":["The pilot runs lawfully and costs less than one week of measured capacity","The window matches the live regime exactly"],"costs":["A self-drafted policy may say something we later correct","The page needs revisiting the day L6 changes"],"system":"Three static routes plus a monitored address.","screens":"Adds /privacy, /terms and /grievance, linked from the footer and from sign-in.","money":"Founder time now; counsel's fee deferred."},{"k":"c","label":"Publish the tightest window from day one: 24-hour ack, 15-day resolution","what":"We promise the intermediary-grade window whether or not publishing is open.","gains":["Simplest to explain and never wrong","No revisiting when L6 changes"],"costs":["Binds one person to a daily acknowledgement duty before anything requires it","A missed self-imposed window is worse than a modest one"],"system":"Needs a monitored inbox with a same-day rota.","screens":"Same three pages, tighter copy.","money":"None in cash; real in attention."},{"k":"d","label":"Counsel drafts them first, then the pilot","what":"An Indian firm writes the three documents before any stranger sees the app.","gains":["A reviewed document from the start","One review covers the CERT-In filing and the terms together"],"costs":["Spends ₹40,000–1,20,000 before any evidence anyone wants the product","Delays the pilot by whatever the review takes"],"system":"No change.","screens":"Same three pages, later.","money":"₹40,000–1,20,000, marked unverified in the record."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["Twelve hours of writing is less than one week of measured capacity and it removes a live breach.","Publish the window that binds and no tighter, because a published window is a promise we then have to keep.","The honest version is short, because the architecture genuinely holds very little.","§13(3) later turns this channel into a shield, so it is worth building properly rather than minimally."],"flip":"If L1 goes to (b) and we hold document content, the policy becomes a materially harder document and counsel should draft it first.","linked":["L1","L17","L6"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:536","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:542","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:548","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:357","docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:4194","docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:6041","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:4107","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:4114","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:4115","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:4116","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:4196","src/modules/share/domain/slug.ts:43","merged: L8"]},{"id":"L10","cat":"Legal, privacy & data","sub":"Processors","weight":"high","q":"Do we cut the vendor chain to bring-your-own key and bundled assets, or keep the server path and paper every processor?","lede":"Six AI routes send up to 200,000 characters to whichever of five foreign providers an environment variable selects.","_ev":["L10","L11"],"visual":{"kind":"flow","nodes":[{"label":"User's document","note":"up to 200,000 characters","tone":"neutral"},{"label":"POST /api/ai/*","note":"our server, six routes","tone":"warn"},{"label":"gateway-client reads env vars","note":"the user cannot see the choice","tone":"stop"},{"label":"One of five foreign providers","note":"Google, Groq, Cerebras, Mistral, OpenRouter","tone":"stop"},{"label":"Vercel AI Gateway if none set","note":"the silent default","tone":"stop"},{"label":"jsdelivr in the export renderer","note":"cut in the plan, still in the code","tone":"stop"}],"perRow":3,"note":"Providers listed at gateway-client.ts:34; the CDN at pdf-doc.ts:132 and export-doc.ts:98","caption":"Where a stranger's document goes on the path as shipped"},"stakes":"An undisclosed sub-processor chain under both regimes, invisible in the product, with the operator paying for every call.","state":["`src/modules/ai/infrastructure/gateway-client.ts:34` builds a provider list from five API-key environment variables, falling back to the Vercel AI Gateway at `:22`.","`src/app/api/ai/refine/route.ts:35` accepts 200,000 characters per call, and `docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:558` lists no bring-your-own key as a current weakness.","`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:549` names three vendors as needing agreements; the code has eight parties in the path and no agreement is referenced anywhere."],"path":["The AI routes are inherited from sgnk-md, where the operator and the user were the same person.","The plan's position, their key, their agent, their machine (`docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:83`), was reasoned on cost and trust and never implemented.","The v15 sweep corrected the assumption that cross-border rules wait for DPDP: SPDI Rule 7 is the live instrument."],"tension":["SPDI Rule 7 names password and payment instrument details, exactly what an auth provider and a payment provider hold, and those are the two we have not papered.","`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:171` cut a vendor CDN for breaking the no-bytes rule while both export renderers still load jsdelivr.","A published sub-processor list drifts silently from reality whenever an environment variable changes."],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Keep the five-provider fallback and publish a sub-processor list","what":"Nothing changes in the code and the list names every provider a key could select.","gains":["Truthful at the moment of writing","No engineering cost"],"costs":["The list drifts from reality whenever an env var changes","Five sub-processor relationships to paper"],"system":"No change.","screens":"Adds a sub-processor page.","money":"Unchanged."},{"k":"b","label":"Cut the chain: bring-your-own key, bundled CDN assets, then paper what is left","what":"Server-side AI routes are disabled, the user supplies a key, and KaTeX and mermaid ship in the bundle.","gains":["Removes five sub-processors and one CDN from the data path","Removes the operator's AI bill, which the plan already flags"],"costs":["Loses the with no extra step first-run AI demo that F5 and F6 rested on","Bundling the assets is an afternoon of work"],"system":"Six routes deleted or moved into the client; two CDN links vendored.","screens":"Adds a key field to settings; the AI panel needs a key before it works.","money":"Operator AI spend goes to zero."},{"k":"c","label":"Keep the server path, pin one named provider, sign the standard DPAs, publish the list","what":"One disclosed provider instead of five, plus a one-page sub-processor list on the site.","gains":["Keeps the zero-configuration demo","One relationship to paper rather than five"],"costs":["The operator still pays for every call","Fiduciary exposure over document content stays"],"system":"Provider selection pinned; the fallback chain removed.","screens":"Adds a sub-processor page and a disclosure in the AI panel.","money":"Operator AI spend continues and scales with use."},{"k":"d","label":"Defer the agreements to 2027 when DPDP commences","what":"We treat processor paperwork as a 2027 problem.","gains":["No work now"],"costs":["Reads the regime backwards: SPDI Rule 7 binds today and DPDP is the one that waits","Nothing to hand the first B2B buyer"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["Bring-your-own key is already the plan's stated position with the trigger before any stranger (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:328`).","It collapses five sub-processor relationships and an operator bill in one change.","Standard DPAs from the remaining vendors are click-through documents, and a sub-processor page is one page, so the residue is a day.","Bundling the two CDN assets closes a rule the plan already wrote down."],"flip":"If the pilot needs a zero-configuration AI demo to test F5 and F6 at all, (b) is the honest compromise, and the provider must be named on the page before a stranger types into it.","linked":["F10","L1","L19"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:133","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:171","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:328","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:542","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:549","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:551","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:558","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:83","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:4540","src/modules/ai/infrastructure/gateway-client.ts:22","src/modules/ai/infrastructure/gateway-client.ts:34","src/app/api/ai/refine/route.ts:35","src/modules/export/presentation/pdf-doc.ts:132","src/modules/export/presentation/export-doc.ts:98","package.json","merged: L11"]},{"id":"L12","cat":"Legal, privacy & data","sub":"EU","weight":"high","q":"Do we geo-exclude the EU for the pilot, or accept EU users and budget an Art 27 representative?","lede":"GDPR Art 3(2)(a) catches a free tool, and §22 concedes the targeting posture addresses that limb only.","_ev":["L12"],"visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":190,"cols":[{"title":"Geo-exclude for the pilot","tone":"accent"},{"title":"Appoint now","tone":"warn"},{"title":"Appoint at first EU seat","tone":"neutral"}],"rows":[{"label":"Annual cost","cells":["nil","€1,920 at EDPO's under-50 band","€468 at Prighter's €39 tier"]},{"label":"Art 27 representative","cells":["not engaged","in place before any user","in place on the trigger"]},{"label":"Art 30 record","cells":["not due","written now","written on the trigger"]},{"label":"DSA Art 13","cells":["falls away if publishing is closed","a second appointment","a second appointment"]},{"label":"Who spots the first EU seat","cells":["nobody needs to","nobody needs to","no measure exists, see L18"]}],"note":"Prices read live 2026-08-31; €200–500 is the 51–500 employee band, not ours","caption":"Three EU postures, priced at one-founder scale"},"stakes":"If any of the ten pilot strangers is in the EU, a representative is due before the test that decides whether the product lives.","state":["`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:550` sets the posture, then concedes it addresses Art 3(2)(a) only and that an Art 27 representative and an Art 30 record are due from the first EU seat.","The same row names our own telemetry plan, a persistent rotating install ID, as the Art 3(2)(b) monitoring fact pattern under Recital 24.","`docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r18-v2-compliance-legal.md:29` corrects the price: the one-founder band is €39–€160 a month, not €200–500."],"path":["The EU research was run on 2026-08-31 and corrected both the price band and the article: the one titled Legal representatives is DSA Art 13, a separate appointment (`docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r18-v2-compliance-legal.md:6`).","§22 states the conclusion and never prices or decides it."],"tension":["The Art 27(2)(a) occasional-processing escape was tested and fails for a subscription editor with sync (`docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r18-v2-compliance-legal.md:33`).","DSA Art 13 bites only for a provider of intermediary services, so it follows L6 rather than this card.","Spending €1,920 a year before there is demand is the sequencing `docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:6041` names as the most expensive ordering."],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Accept EU users and appoint at the first EU signup rather than pre-emptively","what":"The duty is matched to its trigger, with the representative contracted the day someone in the EU joins.","gains":["Matches spend to the obligation","Prighter's €39 tier is the floor if the trigger is early"],"costs":["Requires reliably detecting the first EU seat","L18's measurement design cannot currently detect it"],"system":"Needs a signup-country signal the architecture does not have.","screens":"None until the trigger.","money":"€468 a year from the trigger, at the cheapest tier."},{"k":"b","label":"Accept EU users and appoint an Art 27 representative now at €160 a month","what":"A representative and an Art 30 record are in place before the first user arrives.","gains":["No trigger to detect and no gap to explain","The record's own advice is to budget the ceiling, not the floor"],"costs":["€1,920 a year committed before any evidence of demand","Does not remove DSA Art 13 if publishing opens"],"system":"No change.","screens":"A representative named in the privacy policy.","money":"€1,920 a year, from now."},{"k":"c","label":"Geo-exclude the EU for the pilot; revisit at the first paying EU team","what":"The ten pilot strangers are recruited outside the EU and the exclusion is real, not just a terms clause.","gains":["Costs nothing and removes Art 27, Art 30 and DSA Art 13 from the pilot","Removes the Art 3(2)(b) telemetry question for the duration"],"costs":["Narrows the pool for a ten-stranger test that has not started","The exclusion has to be enforced, not merely written"],"system":"A recruitment rule, plus a sign-up check if the app opens beyond the ten.","screens":"None during the pilot.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Accept EU users and appoint nobody, arguing occasional processing","what":"We rely on Art 27(2)(a) and take no appointment at all.","gains":["Costs nothing"],"costs":["The research already tested this and it fails for a subscription editor with sync","A knowingly weak position on a public page"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"c","recCase":["The pilot is ten people we choose, so excluding the EU costs a sentence in the recruitment.","It defers a real annual commitment past the point where we learn whether the product survives.","It also removes the Art 3(2)(b) telemetry question entirely while L18 is still open."],"flip":"If the pilot cannot be filled without EU participants, (c) is right and the representative must be contracted the day the first one joins.","linked":["L6"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:550","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r18-v2-compliance-legal.md:5","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r18-v2-compliance-legal.md:6","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r18-v2-compliance-legal.md:29","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r18-v2-compliance-legal.md:33","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r18-v2-compliance-legal.md:34","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:4137","docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:6041"]},{"id":"L13","cat":"Legal, privacy & data","sub":"Sidecar","weight":"high","q":"Does the review sidecar carry a person's real identity into the user's git repository, or a pseudonymous id?","lede":"The one file the product exists to write is the one place nobody asked what personal data it carries.","_ev":["L13"],"visual":{"kind":"file","name":".frontmatter/review.jsonl","lines":[{"t":"{\"path\":\"docs/spec.md\",\"start\":1204,","mark":"neutral"},{"t":" \"end\":1631,\"hash\":\"9f2c…\",","mark":"neutral","note":"not personal"},{"t":" \"reviewed_by\":\"…\",","mark":"stop","note":"a natural person"},{"t":" \"reviewed_at\":\"2026-09-09T11:02Z\",","mark":"warn","note":"reading history"},{"t":" \"author\":\"…\",\"model\":\"…\",","mark":"warn"},{"t":" \"prompt\":\"rewrite the retention section\"}","mark":"stop","note":"the user's own text"}],"note":"Fields from PRODUCT-BRIEF line 135; the file is committed beside the documents","caption":"The one file the product writes, and what of it is personal data"},"stakes":"An erasure request against a sidecar in a repository we do not control has no answer, because git cannot forget without rewriting history.","state":["`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:135` specifies the sidecar as one JSON line per span carrying reviewed-by, reviewed-at and, when known, author, model and prompt.","It is committed alongside the documents, and the web byte path writes it by the same path as the documents (`docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:43`).","`reviewed-by` appears once in the whole plan and never in any legal section."],"path":["The sidecar was designed as an engineering artefact: a durable anchor that survives other tools writing to the file.","The legal sweep on 2026-09-08 covered breach, retention, residency, transfer, grievance and the EU, and never looked at the product's own output file."],"tension":["If the repository is public, the identity and every review timestamp are published; if private, they are shared with everyone who can clone.","DPDP §12(3) and GDPR Art 17 both give erasure on request, and we control none of it (`docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:8888`).","The prompt field is the user's own instruction text and may contain anything they would not knowingly commit."],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Keep the sidecar out of the repo, machine-local and synced separately","what":"Review state never travels with the documents.","gains":["Removes the exposure entirely"],"costs":["Destroys the central claim: review state across people and tools needs the file to travel","Turns a plain-text artefact into a sync problem"],"system":"A separate store and a sync path, which the plan says it does not want.","screens":"No shared review state.","money":"Sync infrastructure the plan defers to MVP-2."},{"k":"b","label":"Store real identity and say so plainly in the docs and at first write","what":"The sidecar carries an email or handle, and the product warns the first time a line is written.","gains":["Most legible to a team that wants to know who read what","No mapping layer to build or lose"],"costs":["Publishes a person's reading history into a repo forever, with no erasure route","Makes every rights request unanswerable"],"system":"No change to the format.","screens":"A first-write notice, prominent rather than buried in a policy.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Store a per-repo pseudonymous id by default, with a local map the user owns","what":"The file carries a stable id; the interface resolves it to a name only on the reader's own machine.","gains":["Removes the identifier from the artefact that leaves our control","Cross-tool review state still works: the id is stable within the repo"],"costs":["A team buyer wanting human-readable names in the file does not get them","Needs a local map and a rule for what happens when it is missing"],"system":"Adds an id-to-name map outside the repo and an id minting rule.","screens":"The review panel shows names; the file shows ids.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Drop the prompt field, keep identity, document the rest","what":"The highest-variance field goes; the identity and timestamp trail stays.","gains":["Removes the field most likely to carry something private","One-line change"],"costs":["Leaves the identity and timestamp trail intact and unerasable","Loses the prompt evidence that makes attribution useful"],"system":"One field removed from the writer.","screens":"The panel no longer shows what was asked.","money":"None."}],"rec":"c","recCase":["The product needs a stable per-span identity, not a person's name, so a pseudonymous id costs nothing functionally.","It removes the only irreversible personal-data flow the architecture creates.","Take (d) at the same time: the prompt field is the one most likely to carry something a user would never knowingly commit."],"flip":"If the team feature turns out to need human-readable attribution in the file for the buyer to trust it, then (b) with a prominent notice at the first sidecar write, never buried in a policy.","linked":["E37","L17"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:135","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:152","docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:43","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:8888"]},{"id":"L14","cat":"Legal, privacy & data","sub":"Log residency","weight":"high","q":"Do we build the India-resident 180-day log store now, or run with no logs at all and say so?","lede":"The plan says the log residency is already priced, and the store it was priced against is not the stack we run.","_ev":["L14"],"visual":{"kind":"ba","before":{"title":"What §22 prices","lines":[{"t":"R2, IN jurisdiction, object-lock","mark":"neutral"},{"t":"180 days rolling, NTP to NIC or NPL","mark":"neutral"},{"t":"no bytes, no filenames, no cleartext IP","mark":"neutral"}]},"after":{"title":"What the repo runs","lines":[{"t":"Vercel and Firebase, no region pinned","mark":"stop"},{"t":"no logging dependency in package.json","mark":"stop"},{"t":"zero logs, so nothing to capture","mark":"stop"}]},"via":"stack changed","note":"The R2 design is at PRD v2 line 3689; the residency conflict was recorded at RECORD line 4122","caption":"The log store was priced on infrastructure the product does not use"},"stakes":"A breach investigation with no log slice is an investigation with no evidence, and the 180 days is a floor rather than a ceiling.","state":["`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:544` states 180 days of ICT logs inside Indian jurisdiction and says it is already priced as R2 with object-lock.","The running stack is Vercel plus Firebase with no region pinned, and `package.json` carries no logging, error-reporting or analytics dependency.","`docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:3689` specifies the content: NTP-synced timestamp, request id, opaque user id, action verb, and no document bytes."],"path":["The residency duty was read from the CERT-In Directions on 2026-08-29 and `docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:4122` recorded the conflict with a default Cloudflare stack at the time.","The stack then changed to Vercel and Firebase and the pricing line did not."],"tension":["The real position is not a residency problem but an absence: there are no logs at all.","`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:545` states the 180 days as a floor, and adds a one-year access-log floor from 2027-05-13.","If L1 and L2 close the server surface, the log volume approaches zero and the store becomes almost empty by construction."],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Turn on the host's own logs and accept whatever region they land in","what":"Platform logging is enabled with default settings.","gains":["Cheapest way to have logs at all"],"costs":["Fails the residency clause","Default settings capture paths and IPs, which PRD v2 line 3689 forbids in this store"],"system":"A configuration change, no new code.","screens":"None.","money":"Platform log retention charges."},{"k":"b","label":"Run with no logs through the pilot and state that plainly in the runbook","what":"We hold nothing, and the plan says so rather than implying a store exists.","gains":["Zero cost and zero personal data at rest"],"costs":["Leaves the 180-day floor unmet and any incident un-investigable","The first security questionnaire finds it"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Correct §22 to name the real stack and defer the store to MVP-1","what":"The plan stops citing an R2 price for a Vercel and Firebase deployment.","gains":["Honest and free","Stops a wrong price being quoted as if it applied"],"costs":["Keeps the gap open","Fixes the document, not the duty"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Build the minimal India-resident append-only security log now","what":"Timestamp, request id, opaque user id, verb and outcome, and nothing else.","gains":["Satisfies the floor and gives a breach response something to capture","Five opaque fields hold no content and little personal data"],"costs":["Adds one vendor and one region decision to a one-person stack","Needs NTP sync and an object-lock equivalent"],"system":"A write-only store and a request-id middleware.","screens":"None.","money":"Small storage cost; one more vendor to paper under L10."}],"rec":"d","recCase":["The store is five opaque fields, append-only, with no content, and it is the one artefact a breach response cannot reconstruct afterwards.","Do (d) regardless of the answer: the priced design is R2 on Cloudflare and the running stack is not.","It also gives L4's runbook something to point at when the six-hour clock starts."],"flip":"If L1 and L2 close the server-side surface completely, the log volume approaches zero and (b) with a written statement becomes defensible for the pilot only.","linked":["L1","L4"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:544","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:545","docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:3689","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:4122","vercel.json","package.json"]},{"id":"L16","cat":"Legal, privacy & data","sub":"Security review","weight":"high","q":"Do we buy an outside security review before the first non-founder user, and does it cover the shipped code or only the Firestore design?","lede":"We assert our own safety, and the shipped code carries a defect two files revealed in one reading pass.","_ev":["L16"],"visual":{"kind":"flow","nodes":[{"label":"Anonymous visitor","note":"no account needed","tone":"neutral"},{"label":"GET /<slug>","note":"attacker-authored content","tone":"warn"},{"label":"Tight CSP bound to /p/:slug*","note":"that route is now a 301","tone":"stop","dashed":true},{"label":"Report-only policy applies","note":"permits unsafe-eval","tone":"stop"}],"perRow":4,"note":"Binding at next.config.ts:48; the report-only policy at proxy.ts:112 and :117","caption":"The defect two files revealed, with no outside review bought"},"stakes":"The people who wrote the code are judging whether it is safe, and the first B2B buyer will ask for the artefact we do not have.","state":["`docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:44` lists an outside security review as untapped, with the trigger set at before the first team customer.","`firestore.rules:7` labels itself a prototype and says harden before taking paid signups, and `docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:146` gives the review a concrete subject.","`next.config.ts:48` binds the enforced CSP to `/p/:slug*`, which is now only a redirect, so the live public page falls back to the report-only policy at `src/proxy.ts:112`."],"path":["The rules file carried its own warning from the commit that introduced it, and nobody acted on it.","The v15 sweep gave the review a subject and did not schedule or scope it.","The written trigger, before the first team customer, is later than the pilot, so ten strangers would use the product first."],"tension":["`src/proxy.ts:117` permits `unsafe-eval` in the policy that actually applies to untrusted content.","The comments in both files still describe the old arrangement as if it holds, which is how the defect survived.","If L1 and L2 both close the server surface, the thing to review shrinks to almost nothing."],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Buy a scoped external review of the shipped code and the Firestore design before the pilot","what":"An outside reviewer covers the routes, the CSP, the auth paths and the rules file.","gains":["Finds the class of defect above, which two files revealed in one pass","Produces the artefact the first B2B buyer asks for"],"costs":["A fee and about a week, before there is any revenue","Reviews a server surface L1 and L2 may be about to delete"],"system":"No change until findings land.","screens":"None.","money":"A review fee, unbudgeted."},{"k":"b","label":"Fix the known defects internally and defer the review to the first team customer","what":"We repair the CSP binding ourselves and keep the trigger as written.","gains":["Free now"],"costs":["Keeps the pattern that produced the defect","Ten strangers use the product before anyone outside has looked"],"system":"A two-line CSP fix.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Review only `firestore.rules`, the named concrete subject","what":"The scope is the design document and nothing that executes.","gains":["Cheapest scoping"],"costs":["Reviews a file nothing runs while the code that does run goes unreviewed","Pointless if L1 deletes the file"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"A small fee for little coverage."},{"k":"d","label":"Take L1 and L2 first, then buy a scoped review of a much smaller product","what":"Delete the Firestore design and close the server surface, then review what is left.","gains":["The cheapest real review is the one with the smallest subject","Aligns the spend with the architecture we intend to ship"],"costs":["Pushes the review past the pilot","Depends on two other decisions going the same way"],"system":"Follows L1(a) and L2(a); no new work here.","screens":"None.","money":"A smaller fee, later."}],"rec":"d","recCase":["The cheapest security review is the one with the smallest subject, and L1 and L2 already point at a product with almost no server.","Take those first and this becomes a modest scoped review rather than an audit of a document platform.","Fix the CSP binding this week regardless: it is two lines, and untrusted content is currently served under a policy that reports rather than enforces."],"flip":"If L1 goes to (b) or (c) and we hold documents server-side, the review moves ahead of the pilot and (a) stops being optional.","linked":["L1","L6"],"sources":["docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:44","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:146","firestore.rules:7","firestore.rules:393","next.config.ts:48","src/proxy.ts:112","src/proxy.ts:117","src/proxy.ts:138"],"dupes":{"dropped":["R12"],"why":"Buy an outside security review before the pilot or before the first team customer, and over what scope. Recs d vs a but both amount to 'settle the Firebase question first, then review a smaller product'. Legal, privacy & data owns it."}},{"id":"L17","cat":"Legal, privacy & data","sub":"Retention","weight":"high","q":"What does the privacy policy promise about deletion, given that retention now has a floor as well as a ceiling?","lede":"We cannot promise to delete what the law requires us to keep, and the record still carries the rule the v15 sweep says to delete.","_ev":["L17"],"visual":{"kind":"timeline","items":[{"when":"today","label":"CERT-In ICT logs, 180 days","note":"floor, inside India","tone":"warn"},{"when":"on publishing","label":"IT Rules 3(1)(g) and 3(1)(h), 180 days","note":"removed content, cancelled registrations","tone":"warn"},{"when":"2027-05-13","label":"Access logs plus the data they concern, 1 year","note":"Rule 6(1)(e)","tone":"stop"},{"when":"2027-05-13","label":"Processing logs survive deletion, 1 year","note":"Rule 8(3)","tone":"stop"},{"when":"superseded","label":"\"No row-level retention beyond 90 days\"","note":"still at RECORD line 4508","tone":"sunk"}],"note":"Floors from PRODUCT-BRIEF line 545; the superseded ceiling from RECORD line 4508","caption":"Every retention rule that binds today is a floor, not a ceiling"},"stakes":"A policy saying we delete what you delete is false the day it is published, and the user finds out at the moment it matters most.","state":["`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:545` sets the floors and instructs that the record's no-row-level-retention-beyond-90-days rule be deleted.","That rule is still in the record at `docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:4508`, so someone will quote it.","`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:546` separately kills the inactivity-erasure timer: the Third Schedule thresholds do not reach us."],"path":["The 90-day rule was written on 2026-08-29 from DPDP §8(7)(a) as a ceiling.","The v15 sweep read the notified Rules and found floors the earlier pass had not seen.","`docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:4123` already advised naming the conflict in the policy rather than letting a user discover it, and no policy exists to carry the advice."],"tension":["The floors that bind today are CERT-In's and the IT Rules', not DPDP's, so the schedule cannot wait for 2027.","A statutory books-of-account floor also applies and its period is unverified (`docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:3064`).","If L1, L2 and L14 all close the server surface, most of the table disappears and the honest claim gets shorter."],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Promise deletion on request with an except-where-law-requires clause","what":"The conventional short form, with the exceptions unnamed.","gains":["Short and conventional","Fast to write"],"costs":["The user discovers the exceptions when they matter, which RECORD:4123 advised against","Gives a rights request nothing to answer from"],"system":"No change.","screens":"One clause.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Defer the retention schedule until DPDP commences","what":"We treat retention as a 2027 problem.","gains":["No work now"],"costs":["Wrong direction: the binding floors today are CERT-In's and the IT Rules'","Leaves a superseded rule live in a governing document"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Publish a retention table naming the floors and what survives an account closure","what":"The policy carries a row per record type, its period, and the rule that sets it.","gains":["Doubles as the internal schedule, so it is written once and used twice","It is the artefact a rights request is answered from"],"costs":["A longer policy than the convention","Every row has to be true, which means checking the Companies Act floor"],"system":"Forces a written record inventory before the page can be published.","screens":"A table inside /privacy.","money":"Founder time; possibly one CA question."},{"k":"d","label":"Hold nothing that needs retaining, so the retention schedule is genuinely near-empty","what":"Deletion is trivial because there is almost nothing outside identity and billing.","gains":["The shortest honest policy available","The architecture does the work instead of the wording"],"costs":["Only reachable if L1, L2 and L14 all close the server surface","CERT-In's floor and the billing records still apply"],"system":"Follows L1, L2 and L14; no new work here.","screens":"A very short retention section.","money":"None."}],"rec":"c","recCase":["A retention table is the single most useful page a privacy policy carries and it doubles as the internal schedule.","Delete the superseded 90-day rule from the record in the same edit; a refuted rule left in a governing document is how a wrong number gets quoted six months later.","The floors are already written down, so the table is transcription rather than research."],"flip":"If (c) becomes true after L1, L2 and L14, the table gets much shorter and the honest claim gets stronger, not weaker.","linked":["L1","L14","L7","PR2"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:545","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:546","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:3064","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:4123","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:4508","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:8983"]},{"id":"L19","cat":"Legal, privacy & data","sub":"Tax","weight":"medium","q":"Do we register for GST now, stop buying foreign AI services until we do, or put the position to a CA first?","lede":"Buying API access from a foreign supplier is importing a service, and registration starts at the first rupee.","_ev":["L19"],"visual":{"kind":"flow","nodes":[{"label":"Company buys a foreign API key","note":"Google, Groq, Mistral, OpenRouter","tone":"neutral"},{"label":"Import of services","note":"supplier outside India","tone":"warn"},{"label":"Reverse charge applies","note":"CGST §24(iii)","tone":"warn"},{"label":"Registration due at the first rupee","note":"the ₹20 lakh floor does not apply","tone":"stop"}],"perRow":4,"note":"Stated as a fact about us at DECIDE line 213","caption":"Why the obligation attaches to buying, not to selling"},"stakes":"A known obligation left unmet accrues interest and penalty, and surfaces during diligence rather than on our own timetable.","state":["`docs/DECIDE.md:213` states it as a fact about us: buying Claude API access is importing a service, and registration starts at the first rupee.","`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:330` carries it as a risk with a one-line response and no owner.","Whether registration has happened is not stated in any document, either way."],"path":["It surfaced in the verification round as one of the corrections in `docs/DECIDE.md`, the section written after 62% of load-bearing claims needed correction (`docs/DECIDE.md:212`).","It was recorded and never actioned."],"tension":["`src/modules/ai/infrastructure/gateway-client.ts:34` reads keys for five foreign suppliers, and hosting is foreign too, so the trigger is concrete rather than hypothetical.","The adjacent export-of-services and LUT positions at `docs/BUSINESS.md:698` are marked inference-only because the source was unreachable.","Stopping the purchases removes the trigger and points the same way as L10's bring-your-own-key answer."],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Stop buying foreign AI services on the company account until registration is settled","what":"No foreign supplier is paid from the company until the position is clear.","gains":["Removes the trigger immediately","Points the same way as L10's bring-your-own-key answer"],"costs":["Conflicts with running server-side AI at all","Hosting is foreign too, so it does not remove every import"],"system":"Server-side AI off; keys removed from the deployment.","screens":"The AI panel needs the user's key.","money":"Operator AI spend to zero."},{"k":"b","label":"Register now and start filing, before any revenue","what":"The company takes a GSTIN and begins monthly returns.","gains":["Compliant from the first import","Removes the question from every future diligence pack"],"costs":["Monthly filing overhead on a company with no revenue","Permanent, not reversible when convenient"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"Filing overhead, monthly, from now."},{"k":"c","label":"Ask a CA to confirm the position and the exposure to date, then act","what":"One consultation settles registration, the exposure already accrued, and the export and LUT questions together.","gains":["Settles a factual question about our own filings that nobody has answered","Covers the BUSINESS.md:698 items marked inference-only"],"costs":["A short delay before acting","One fee"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"One consultation fee."},{"k":"d","label":"Treat it as immaterial at current spend and revisit at revenue","what":"We accept the position and carry on.","gains":["Cheapest today"],"costs":["Interest and penalty accrue on whatever is owed","Found later, by someone else, during diligence"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"Unquantified exposure."}],"rec":"c","recCase":["This is a factual question about our own filings that nobody in the record has answered, and it should not be guessed from a plan document.","One consultation settles it along with the export-of-services and LUT positions marked unverified at `docs/BUSINESS.md:698`.","The cost of asking is one fee; the cost of being wrong compounds quietly."],"flip":"If the CA confirms registration is already due, (a) follows immediately, and (c) becomes an attractive way to shrink the exposure while the paperwork catches up.","linked":["L10","PR16"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:330","docs/DECIDE.md:212","docs/DECIDE.md:213","docs/BUSINESS.md:680","docs/BUSINESS.md:698","src/modules/ai/infrastructure/gateway-client.ts:34"]},{"id":"L20","cat":"Legal, privacy & data","sub":"Licensing","weight":"medium","q":"Do we split the licence, Apache-2.0 for the engine and proprietary for the app, or license the repository one way?","lede":"The repo states no licence at all, so the default is all rights reserved and nobody may lawfully run the engine.","_ev":["L20"],"visual":{"kind":"arch","layers":[{"label":"Splice engine, OffsetMap, refusal logic","items":["Apache-2.0","NOTICE file","patent grant, trademark reserved"],"side":"engine","tone":"accent"},{"label":"CLI and the written spec","items":["Apache-2.0","per-directory LICENSE"],"side":"tools","tone":"accent"},{"label":"Editor, sync, billing","items":["proprietary, closed","data-portability promise"],"side":"app","tone":"neutral"}],"note":"Repo today: no LICENSE, no license field, 47 MIT runtime dependencies","caption":"The split the plan reasoned twice and never wrote to disk"},"stakes":"A certificate strategy whose value rises with third-party verification currently forbids third parties from running the engine at all.","state":["There is no `LICENSE` or `NOTICE` file, and `package.json` has no `license` field; it declares `private: true`.","`docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:4636` records the same measurement and calls all rights reserved the worst position for a spec others should implement.","The proposed split is set out at `:4640`, `:4641` and `:4645`, and again at `docs/ENGINE.md:2237`."],"path":["The licence was reasoned on 2026-08-29 around the certificate: Apache-2.0 §6 withholds trademark rights, so a fork could not issue certificates in our name.","FSL and BUSL were rejected because the Competing Use clause bars the independent reimplementation that would prove the engine correct."],"tension":["The repo shares 202 of 228 files with `sgnk-md` (`docs/DECIDE.md:168`), and nobody has checked what the sibling declares.","A root licence will not cover the spec prose, so per-path declarations are needed.","The split describes a boundary the code does not yet have, because the engine is not a separate package."],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Apache-2.0 with NOTICE for the engine, proprietary for the app, per-directory files","what":"The split already reasoned is written to disk, with a LICENSE in each directory it governs.","gains":["Matches reasoning written twice already","The trademark reservation is the mechanism the certificate needs"],"costs":["Requires actually separating the engine into its own package","Per-path declarations to keep in step as the tree moves"],"system":"Engine extraction, root and per-directory LICENSE files, a license field.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Leave it unlicensed until the engine is extracted","what":"The status quo, which is all rights reserved by default.","gains":["No work now"],"costs":["Every day nobody may lawfully verify the engine","The worst position for a spec we intend others to implement"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"One proprietary licence for the whole repository","what":"Everything is closed and nobody outside may run any of it.","gains":["Simplest, and true to the current code layout"],"costs":["Forecloses the third-party verification the certificate strategy depends on","Contradicts publishing a spec for others to implement"],"system":"One root LICENSE and a license field.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Apache-2.0 for everything","what":"The editor and the engine are both open.","gains":["Maximum adoption and the easiest verification story"],"costs":["Hands the whole editor to anyone, including the incumbent we may be colliding with","Nothing left to sell but the service"],"system":"One root LICENSE.","screens":"None.","money":"Removes any product licence revenue."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["The reasoning is done and written down twice; what is missing is the file.","Apache-2.0's trademark reservation is the specific mechanism that lets the engine be verified without letting a fork issue certificates in our name.","Check what the sibling repo declares in the same pass, because 202 files are shared."],"flip":"If the engine will not be extracted as a package in the next quarter, (b) plus a written intent to open it later is more honest than a licence describing a boundary the code does not have.","linked":["E24"],"sources":["docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:4636","docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:4640","docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:4641","docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:4645","docs/ENGINE.md:2237","docs/DECIDE.md:168","package.json"]},{"id":"L21","cat":"Legal, privacy & data","sub":"Citations","weight":"medium","q":"Do we adopt the rule that an unverifiable citation is dropped rather than repeated, and apply it to the gazette number now?","lede":"Four governing documents cite one instrument four ways, and every legal deadline in the plan derives from it.","_ev":["L21"],"visual":{"kind":"flow","nodes":[{"label":"PIB release, marked [SS]","note":"the registries were unreachable","tone":"warn"},{"label":"PRD v2: 846(E), 14 Nov 2025","note":"derives 14 May 2027","tone":"warn"},{"label":"BUSINESS and RECORD: 846(E), 13 Nov","note":"the marker was dropped","tone":"stop"},{"label":"PRODUCT-BRIEF v15: 843(E), 13 Nov","note":"a third number appears","tone":"stop"},{"label":"Every deadline in §22","note":"all of them derive from this date","tone":"stop"}],"perRow":3,"note":"The instruction to open the Gazette or drop the number is at PRD v2 line 5982","caption":"One unopened source, four citations, every legal deadline downstream"},"stakes":"A visible inconsistency in the documents shown to counsel, sitting on top of the date that fixes every deadline in §22.","state":["`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:541` cites G.S.R. 843(E) of 13 Nov 2025; `docs/BUSINESS.md:26` and `docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:8357` cite 846(E) of the same date.","`docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:4516` cites 846(E) and dates the notification 14 November 2025, deriving a commencement one day later.","`docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:5982` already recorded the instruction: open the Gazette or drop the number."],"path":["The number entered the record on 2026-08-29 from a PIB release, marked unverified because the primary registries were unreachable.","The instruction was not followed, and the v15 sweep then introduced a third variant."],"tension":["`docs/DECIDE.md:212` records that 62% of load-bearing claims needed correction once someone opened a primary source, so there are many more of these.","13 versus 14 November shifts the whole eighteen-month tranche by a day, and the 247-day headline with it.","A marker only works if it travels with the number, and three of four documents dropped it while copying."],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"No rule; treat each citation on its merits","what":"The status quo.","gains":["No process to maintain"],"costs":["The status quo produced four citations of one instrument","And a 62% correction rate on load-bearing claims"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Standardise on 846(E) because three documents use it","what":"The inconsistency is resolved by majority.","gains":["Fastest to apply"],"costs":["Resolves by majority rather than by source","That is exactly how a wrong number becomes a settled one"],"system":"A search and replace.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Adopt the rule but keep unverified details behind an explicit marker","what":"The number stays with an [SS] tag that must travel with every copy.","gains":["Preserves the lead for a later verification pass"],"costs":["The marker is only as good as the reader's attention","Three of four documents already dropped it while copying"],"system":"A marker convention and a check for it.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Adopt the rule and apply it now: one attempt at the Gazette, then one number or none","what":"Unverifiable detail is dropped rather than repeated, starting with the gazette number.","gains":["Fixes the date every legal rule derives from","Gives every future citation a default and removes a visible inconsistency"],"costs":["Loses the lead for anyone who later wants to verify it","About an hour, plus edits in four documents"],"system":"A citation rule in the docs conventions.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"d","recCase":["The rule is worth more than the number, because it generalises to every other unverified claim in the corpus.","The correction rate says there are many, and the gazette number is the test case.","It also settles whether the 247-day headline in §22 is right."],"flip":"If the founders want unverified leads preserved for a later verification pass, (b) is defensible, but only with a rule that the marker travels with the number, which is exactly what failed here.","linked":["L23","L7"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:541","docs/BUSINESS.md:26","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:8357","docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:4516","docs/FRONTMATTER-PRD-v2-2026-08-29.md:5982","docs/DECIDE.md:212"]},{"id":"L22","cat":"Legal, privacy & data","sub":"Children","weight":"medium","q":"Do we state 18-plus in the terms, build an age gate, or write down why the question is out of scope?","lede":"DPDP §9 carries a ₹200 crore ceiling, the plan never mentions children, and the code has no age field.","_ev":["L22"],"visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":190,"cols":[{"title":"Say 18-plus in the terms","tone":"accent"},{"title":"Build age assurance","tone":"stop"},{"title":"Stay silent","tone":"warn"}],"rows":[{"label":"Cost","cells":["one sentence","a field, a check and friction","nothing"]},{"label":"First-run friction","cells":["none","on the first screen","none"]},{"label":"§9(3) monitoring ban","cells":["satisfied, nothing is tracked","satisfied","satisfied in fact, unstated"]},{"label":"If a buyer asks","cells":["point at the clause","point at the gate","nothing to point at"]}],"note":"Ceiling from RECORD line 4517; the prohibition from RECORD line 4507","caption":"Three positions on an obligation the plan never mentions"},"stakes":"The current position is silence, which is the only one of the three that cannot be explained to anyone who asks.","state":["`docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:4507` quotes §9(3): no tracking or behavioural monitoring of children, and no targeted advertising directed at them.","`docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:4517` gives the ceiling: ₹200 crore for the §9 children obligations.","There is no age field, no date of birth and no terms acceptance anywhere in `src/`, and §22 does not mention children."],"path":["The children provisions were captured on 2026-08-29 as a never-collect line inside the telemetry section and never revisited.","The v15 legal sweep covered breach, retention, residency, transfer, grievance and the EU, and did not cover §9."],"tension":["A markdown editor for repositories has a small realistic child population, but small is an assumption nobody has written down.","The obligation does not scale with the number of children affected.","§9 commences 2027-05-13 with §§3–17 (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:541`), so the clause is cheap now and awkward later."],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Leave it unaddressed until DPDP commences","what":"The question waits until 2027-05-13.","gains":["No work now"],"costs":["Defers a clause that costs one sentence","Leaves a visible hole at a ₹200 crore penalty tier"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"State 18-plus in the terms and do no behavioural monitoring of anyone","what":"One clause in the terms, alongside the no-monitoring rule the plan already holds.","gains":["Costs one sentence and makes §9(3) trivially satisfied","Pairs with L18's no-telemetry answer at no extra cost"],"costs":["A clause nobody reads is weak evidence of anything","Needs the terms page from L7 to exist first"],"system":"No change.","screens":"One clause in /terms.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Build verifiable age assurance at sign-up","what":"A date-of-birth field and a check before the first screen.","gains":["The strongest position if the audience assumption is ever wrong"],"costs":["Real friction on the first screen, which the plan names as the worst place for it","Disproportionate to a developer-tool audience"],"system":"An age field, storage and a verification path.","screens":"Adds a step before the editor.","money":"A verification vendor if assurance is real rather than self-declared."},{"k":"d","label":"Write down that the product is not directed at children, and publish nothing","what":"The reasoning goes into §22 and no clause appears in the terms.","gains":["Documents the position internally at no cost"],"costs":["Publishes nothing, so the argument is not available to anyone who asks","The gap in the legal section stays visible"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["A terms clause costs one sentence and the substantive prohibition is already satisfied by an architecture that monitors nobody.","The reasoning belongs in §22 alongside the other legal rows rather than staying in the record.","It is the only position of the three that can be explained to a buyer or a regulator on sight."],"flip":"If the product ever ships a public publishing surface aimed at note-takers rather than developers, the audience assumption changes and (b) has to be re-argued on evidence.","linked":["L7"],"sources":["docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:4507","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:4517","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:538","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:541"]},{"id":"L23","cat":"Legal, privacy & data","sub":"Claims","weight":"medium","q":"Do we cite regulators at all, and do we say plainly that none of them requires per-span review?","lede":"Nothing opened in the 2026-09-09 research round mandates review below the whole document, and a compliance buyer will check.","_ev":[],"visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":200,"cols":[{"title":"What the source says","tone":"neutral"},{"title":"What it does not say","tone":"stop"}],"rows":[{"label":"21 CFR 11.10(e)","cells":["changes must not obscure previously recorded information","nothing about per-span human review"]},{"label":"MHRA GxP data integrity","cells":["audit trails may be reviewed by exception reporting","no granularity, no mandate"]},{"label":"EMA reflection paper, 2024","cells":["model-generated text needs a quality review mechanism","non-binding, says should, names no granularity"]},{"label":"Pharma practice","cells":["whole-document approval","not per span"]},{"label":"Aviation practice","cells":["a per-page revision date","not per span"]}],"note":"All five opened in the 2026-09-09 round; none mandates per-span review","caption":"What regulators require, against what a pitch might imply"},"stakes":"One implied mandate that a compliance buyer can refute kills the credibility of every other claim in the deck.","state":["The 2026-09-09 round opened 21 CFR 11.10(e), the MHRA GxP data integrity guide and the EMA reflection paper of 9 September 2024.","None mandates per-span review; pharma requires whole-document approval and aviation a per-page revision date.","`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:541` already carries the discipline for the adjacent case: claim neither compliance nor exposure before the dates."],"path":["Regulated-document buyers were reached for through desk research; nobody has asked one what an audit trail must contain (`docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:41`).","The same round found that a third of the researchers' quotation marks were paraphrases, so every regulator quote needs re-fetching before it is used."],"tension":["MHRA already permits exception reporting rather than a full list, which supports the product's design and undercuts an enumerate-everything pitch.","The EMA paper says should, is non-binding, and names no granularity, so quoting it as a requirement is the exact overreach a buyer will catch.","Saying plainly that nothing mandates per-span review is a weaker sentence and a stronger position."],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Cite them as pressure without the caveat","what":"Regulators are named to imply a requirement we do not spell out.","gains":["The strongest-sounding version"],"costs":["A compliance buyer refutes it from the source in one reading","One refuted claim discredits the rest of the deck"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Defer until five regulated-document buyers have been asked what they need","what":"The claim waits for the conversations the plan already schedules.","gains":["Evidence before wording, which is the right order"],"costs":["Leaves the pitch without a regulated story in the meantime","The conversations have not started"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Cite regulators only with the caveat that none mandates per-span review","what":"Every regulator reference carries the limit of what it actually requires, in the same sentence.","gains":["Compliance buyers reward the caveat and punish its absence","Keeps MHRA's exception-reporting line, which supports the design"],"costs":["A longer, flatter sentence than a mandate claim","Every quote must be re-fetched and string-matched first"],"system":"No change.","screens":"Wording on the regulated-buyer page, if one exists.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Do not cite regulators at all; sell on the working-tree case alone","what":"No regulatory language appears anywhere in the pitch.","gains":["Nothing to refute and nothing to re-fetch"],"costs":["Gives up the one adjacency where document review is already a habit","MHRA's exception-reporting support goes unused"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"Forgoes a buyer segment."}],"rec":"c","recCase":["The caveat costs a clause and it is the sentence a compliance buyer is testing for.","MHRA's exception-reporting line already argues for the product's design, so the honest citation is also the useful one.","Re-fetch and string-match before any regulator quote reaches a slide; roughly one in three of the researchers' quotation marks was a paraphrase."],"flip":"If the five regulated-buyer conversations turn up a written internal requirement for span-level review, the claim changes from none-mandates to buyers-require, which is a stronger and different sentence.","linked":["L21"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:541","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:41","https://www.ecfr.gov/api/versioner/v1/full/2026-01-01/title-21.xml?part=11","https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5aa2b9ede5274a3e391e37f3/MHRA_GxP_data_integrity_guide_March_edited_Final.pdf","https://www.ema.europa.eu/en/documents/scientific-guideline/reflection-paper-use-artificial-intelligence-ai-medicinal-product-lifecycle_en.pdf","added: L23"]},{"id":"N1","cat":"Name & identity","sub":"The word","weight":"critical","q":"Do we keep the word \"frontmatter\", qualify it, or leave it?","lede":"The name is taken in the store the buyer lives in, and every asset from week 1 spends it.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":200,"cols":[{"title":"Keep bare","tone":"stop"},{"title":"Qualify","tone":"warn"},{"title":"Coin","tone":"accent"}],"rows":[{"label":"Senior user since 2019","cells":["Unmanaged","Still adjacent","Gone"]},{"label":"Bare-word search","cells":["Owned by the concept","Brand-modified only","Ownable from day one"]},{"label":"The two best qualifiers","cells":["n/a","CMS and Studio both taken","n/a"]},{"label":"npm and GitHub","cells":["Both taken","Handles free 2026-08-29","stetfile 404 on both"]},{"label":"Teaching cost","cells":["None","A sentence per conversation","A sentence per asset"]},{"label":"What §52.3 calls it","cells":["Highest risk, extra steps","Rank 1 and 2","Rank 1 until clearance"]}],"note":"\"Frontmatter Studio\" was registered by somebody else on 2026-09-07.","caption":"The three routes, on the axes the naming reports actually measured"},"stakes":"Ship bare and we take the full confusion and clearance exposure of a live 2019 senior user and buy nothing back.","state":["v15 uses the word bare in every section, and its own keyfigure block leads with the collision: 82,265 installs of the extension that owns the name (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:13).","Exhibit 20 lists seven decisions and the name is not one of them (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:359-369). The week-0 doc files it under \"also open for the founders, not drafted here\" (docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:58).","The incumbent is alive, not abandoned: v10.12.0 on 2026-08-21, and the `@frontmatter` npm scope is his (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:132).","No channel in the plan is search. The four listed are superpowers, spec-kit, one Show HN and Product Hunt (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:305-310)."],"path":["Round r7 measured the collision on 2026-08-28 and rated it MEDIUM-HIGH, HIGH if shipped bare (e6-naming-risk.md:10).","Round r11 generated 41 candidates, probed 15 on npm and GitHub, and recommended the coinage `stetfile` (r4-naming-candidates.md:29, :63, :112).","The 2026-09-08 self-critique named it gap D2, \"Untreated\" (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:50). Round 2 the same day re-measured it worse (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:132)."],"tension":["The escape route the research reserved is gone. §52.3 ranked \"Frontmatter Studio\" the qualifier that separates us in speech, and it was taken on 2026-09-07 (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:132).","What remains is rank 1: handle qualified, spoken name bare (22-segments-disclosure-naming.md:219). Line 223 of the same section calls that the highest-risk option with extra steps.","The SEO half of the case is worth nothing this year, because nothing in the plan is a search channel. A rename bought on search grounds buys a channel we do not use.","Today's competitor sweep moves the collision closer. If distribution runs through the git-backed CMS shelf, the incumbent is a shelf neighbour as well as a name neighbour."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"The incumbent, re-measured","items":[["VS Code installs","82,265","GAPS-2026-09-08.md:132, round 2 on 2026-09-08; was 80,605 read 2026-08-29"],["Latest release","v10.12.0, 2026-08-21","GAPS-2026-09-08.md:132 — alive, not abandoned"],["Marketplace rating","5.0 from 20 ratings","22-segments-disclosure-naming.md:185"],["GitHub stars","2,539","e6-naming-risk.md:2 — estruyf/vscode-front-matter, created 2019-08-23"],["\"Frontmatter Studio\"","taken 2026-09-07","GAPS-2026-09-08.md:132 — the qualifier §52.3 ranked best in the spoken name"],["Marketplace listings the incumbent holds","3 — \"Front Matter CMS\", a \"(BETA)\" listing, \"Front Matter CMS - Theme\"","e6-naming-risk.md:87; named at COMPLETE-RECORD-2026-08-30.md:12496"]]},{"type":"table","title":"Where the name already lives","cols":["Surface","Holder","Source"],"rows":[["npm `frontmatter`","dead 2022 parser, v0.0.3, 11,212 dl/mo of transitive noise","22-segments-disclosure-naming.md:188"],["npm `@frontmatter` scope","the incumbent's","GAPS-2026-09-08.md:132"],["GitHub org `frontmatter`","Front Matter CMS, created 2021-09-21","22-segments-disclosure-naming.md:187"],["frontmatter.codes","the incumbent's homepage","e6-naming-risk.md:2"],["frontmatter.io","live company, Fremont CA, 11-50 staff","e6-naming-risk.md:7"],["frontmatter.cc","AI agent-skills / MCP config builder","e6-naming-risk.md:7"],["frontmatter.com","no product surfaced; registration unverified","COMPLETE-RECORD-2026-08-30.md:7755"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"How crowded the word is as a search term","items":[["gray-matter, npm downloads/month","35,782,970","COMPLETE-RECORD-2026-08-30.md:6386, api.npmjs.org 2026-07-29 to 08-27"],["front-matter, npm downloads/month","18,413,979","same source"],["The two combined","54,196,949","[derived] 35,782,970 + 18,413,979, computed 2026-09-09"],["GitHub repos with \"frontmatter\" in the name","564","e6-naming-risk.md:69"],["GitHub repos with \"front-matter\" in the name","319","e6-naming-risk.md:69"],["Incumbent's rank for the bare word after 7 years","not in the top results","e6-naming-risk.md:97"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"What the funnel would need if search ever mattered","items":[["Cumulative visitors for the plan's revenue target","1,260,000","BUSINESS.md:353 — settled figure"],["Free signups implied","113,507","BUSINESS.md:245"],["Channels in the plan that are search","0","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:305-310"],["Marketing-site keyword map","none written","r14-g1-final-gap-sweep.md:14 — MISSING"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Keep \"Frontmatter\" bare","what":"The product, the handles and any store listing all read Frontmatter, beside a live 2019 senior user.","gains":["No teaching cost; the word is the thesis in one token","Nothing to rewrite: 169 occurrences across 44 of 248 src files stay"],"costs":["Takes the full confusion and clearance exposure and buys nothing back","The one configuration all three naming reports argue against by name","Bare-word search is owned by the concept, not by any product"],"system":"No change.","screens":"No change.","money":"Nothing today; a possible rename later at a worse price."},{"k":"b","label":"Qualify the spoken name, and not with \"CMS\" or \"Studio\"","what":"The product is said as two words, so the incumbent's name is not our name in conversation.","gains":["Keeps the word's teaching value and the handles measured free on 2026-08-29","Cheaper than a coinage in every asset"],"costs":["The two best qualifiers are gone: CMS years ago, Studio on 2026-09-07","Leaves a near-identical mark in an overlapping class","A disambiguation sentence in every conversation, permanently"],"system":"Package and org handles change; the engine is untouched.","screens":"Wordmark, launcher title, desktop window title.","money":"One domain and a handle set."},{"k":"c","label":"Coin a name; keep \"frontmatter\" as the word for the block we edit","what":"A new word owns the product, and the old word stays the name of the YAML block the editor reads.","gains":["Kills the collision and the search problem outright","`stetfile` was 404 on npm and GitHub, measured 2026-08-29","Search becomes ownable if it ever turns into a channel"],"costs":["One sentence of category teaching in every asset","Nothing reserves it; re-run the 404 probe on registration day","`stetmark` shipped 2026-08-05 on the same metaphor, 5,753 dl/mo"],"system":"Rename two published packages and 169 string occurrences in src.","screens":"Every wordmark, the launcher, the desktop title.","money":"A domain, handles, and a second clearance search."},{"k":"d","label":"Flip the hierarchy — MDMAX becomes the brand","what":"The engine name already in inventory becomes the product name and the mark we defend.","gains":["No new clearance work; npm `mdmax` was 404 on 2026-08-30","Answers N4's mark question in the same move"],"costs":["\"md\" reads as a medical degree to non-developers (r4-naming-candidates.md:69)","The corpus rates it a library name, not a product you charge for"],"system":"One package name survives; the product's strings change.","screens":"Wordmark everywhere.","money":"The cheapest of the three changes."}],"rec":"c","recCase":["Both documented precedents for a same-market, same-channel senior user ended in a rename: Firefox twice while still small, Riot.im after launch and at community cost (e6-naming-risk.md:110-111).","Keep-and-outrank worked for Obsidian and Notion because their seniors were in other markets. Ours is in the same store, on the same shelf, and shipping.","The qualifier route lost both usable forms, and what is left is the configuration §52.3 calls highest-risk (22-segments-disclosure-naming.md:219, :223).","Renaming costs 169 string occurrences today. It costs a migration the moment somebody else holds one of our strings."],"flip":"A clean attorney knock-out on the incumbent's class plus an available qualifier; §52.3's own falsifier says a taught name then costs more (22-segments-disclosure-naming.md:225).","linked":["FF1","N2","N3","N4","N6"],"sources":["merged: N8","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:13","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:305-310","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:359-369","docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:58","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:50","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:132","docs/BUSINESS.md:245","docs/BUSINESS.md:353","docs/research/prd-v2-sections/22-segments-disclosure-naming.md:185","docs/research/prd-v2-sections/22-segments-disclosure-naming.md:187","docs/research/prd-v2-sections/22-segments-disclosure-naming.md:188","docs/research/prd-v2-sections/22-segments-disclosure-naming.md:219","docs/research/prd-v2-sections/22-segments-disclosure-naming.md:223","docs/research/prd-v2-sections/22-segments-disclosure-naming.md:225","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-28/e6-naming-risk.md:10","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-28/e6-naming-risk.md:69","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-28/e6-naming-risk.md:87","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-28/e6-naming-risk.md:97","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-28/e6-naming-risk.md:110-111","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-29-r11/r4-naming-candidates.md:29","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-29-r11/r4-naming-candidates.md:63","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-29-r11/r4-naming-candidates.md:112","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-29-r11/r4-naming-candidates.md:117","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r14-g1-final-gap-sweep.md:14","docs/FRONTMATTER-COMPLETE-RECORD-2026-08-30.md:6386"],"dupes":{"dropped":["MK3"],"why":"Keep the bare word, qualify it, or coin. Same options and same rec (c). Name & identity owns the name. MK3's fourth option (detente with the incumbent's author) is N9's question, already a separate card."}},{"id":"N2","cat":"Name & identity","sub":"Timing and order","weight":"critical","q":"When does the name freeze, and is it decided before or after the form factor?","lede":"The name is spent one asset at a time, and the form-factor decision is scoring a cost a rename would erase.","visual":{"kind":"state","states":[{"label":"Free to rename","meta":"169 strings in 44 of 248 src files","via":"","tone":"good","current":true},{"label":"Search seeded","meta":"three landing pages, weeks 1-2","via":"week 1","tone":"neutral"},{"label":"Installed","meta":"a signed build on a stranger's machine","via":"MVP-0","tone":"warn"},{"label":"Breaking","meta":"a customer CNAME to pages.frontmatter.app","via":"MVP-1","tone":"stop"}],"note":"Only the last two are strings somebody other than us is holding.","caption":"What a rename costs at each step, and where it stops being an edit"},"stakes":"Past the third state a rename migrates preferences, keychains and an update channel on other people's machines.","state":["A prototype is already public under the name (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:237), and weeks 1-2 put up three landing pages (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:352).","Exactly one string is declared permanent in writing: the API error-type URIs, \"stable forever — changing one is breaking\" (docs/DEV-PLAN.md:627).","The gap register orders the form factor first with the collision as an input (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:100), then the name (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:101).","The plan's decision 6 counts the collision as one of four arguments against the extension (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:364). Rename tripwires written into the plan: none."],"path":["§52 Option C proposed a tripwire list on 2026-08-28: counsel clean, no objection from the incumbent, listings accepted, handles secured (COMPLETE-RECORD-2026-08-30.md:12541; MASTER-PLAN-2026-08-28.md:182).","The Firefox lesson was attached to it: pre-launch renames are cheap, post-launch renames are Element (e6-naming-risk.md:110-111, :130).","The gap register and the plan were written in the same round and neither noticed the other's ordering. Round 2 then produced both as founder decisions in one sentence (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:150)."],"tension":["The cost of a rename is not flat, and the plan treats the name as an agenda item rather than a dated gate.","The ordering is circular: decision 6 counts the name as a cost, and the name is told to wait for decision 6.","Today's platform sweep weakens the extension route on other grounds. The working-tree diff of agent changes is now free in four editors, so the surface argument moved while the name argument sat still.","Three further strings are widely assumed permanent and the plan asserts it nowhere, so nobody has established where the line actually is."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"What a rename costs, by artefact — and how well each verdict is evidenced","cols":["Artifact","Cost of changing it later","Source and evidence class"],"rows":[["Source files carrying the word","Low — 169 occurrences in 44 of 248 src files","re-measured in src/ on 2026-09-09 [measured]"],["Public prototype URL","Low — one Vercel deployment","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:237"],["Three landing pages, weeks 1-2","Low, but they seed search results we would abandon","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:352 [inference on the seeding]"],["API error-type URIs at frontmatter.dev/errors/","Breaking — the plan's own words","docs/DEV-PLAN.md:627 [quoted — the only permanence the plan states]"],["`*.frontmatter.app` published pages","Breaking for customers who have CNAMEd to pages.frontmatter.app","docs/DEV-PLAN.md:1679, 1683 [the CNAME flow is specified; the breakage is inference]"],["Desktop bundle identifier `ai.sgnk.md`","Assumed permanent — it is the OS's key for preferences, keychain and the signed update channel","src-tauri/tauri.conf.json:5; the plan says only that it \"must be re-identified\" (PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:104) [unverified against platform docs]"],["GitHub App name \"Frontmatter\"","Assumed permanent — the plan registers 3 distinct App names across 4 environments, which implies a shared namespace","docs/DEV-PLAN.md:1104, 1610 [inference — the plan never says the App namespace is global, and it was not checked]"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"Precedent on rename timing","items":[["Firefox renames before dominance","2 (Phoenix, Firebird)","e6-naming-risk.md:110 — \"survivable and cheap\""],["Riot.im rename, post-launch","1, community reaction divided","e6-naming-risk.md:111"],["Strings the plan declares permanent in writing","1","DEV-PLAN.md:627"],["Rename tripwires written into the plan","0","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md — no gate in any exhibit"]]},{"type":"table","title":"The circle, in five lines","cols":["Document","Says","Line"],"rows":[["GAPS §G item 2","decide the form factor, with the name collision as one input","GAPS-2026-09-08.md:100"],["GAPS §G item 3","then resolve the name — keep, rename, or scope it to the desktop product","GAPS-2026-09-08.md:101"],["Plan, decision 6","the name collision argues against the extension","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:364"],["Plan, Exhibit 20","seven decisions listed; the name is not one of them","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:359-369"],["GAPS, founder decisions","\"the name, now a legal question and not only a marketing one\"","GAPS-2026-09-08.md:150"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"What decision 6 weighs","items":[["Arguments for the extension","4 — byte-exact writes 94/94 and 156/156; portable engine, 3,614 lines; free model picker and MCP; empty niche","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:364"],["Arguments against","4 — save pipeline rewrites; no view-zone API; untested data-loss path; the name","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:364"],["Of those, ones a rename removes","1","the name"],["Review-state install ceiling in that store","400","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:364"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Freeze the name this week, before the landing pages go up","what":"One sitting settles the word, and every downstream string becomes decidable at once.","gains":["Ends the circularity, so decision 6 can be scored honestly","Nothing is spent under a name we later abandon"],"costs":["Forces N1 before N3's register searches have been run","Decides the worst-evidenced question in the file in one sitting"],"system":"Every string in DEV-PLAN and src-tauri is settled the same week.","screens":"Wordmark on all nine prototype screens.","money":"Domains and handles bought once."},{"k":"b","label":"Freeze at the first artefact a third party holds","what":"Weeks 1-2 run under whatever name we have; the gate binds at the first signed build and the first customer CNAME.","gains":["Draws the gate where the evidence supports it, on strings we do not hold","Both artefacts already have dates in the build plan"],"costs":["The landing pages seed search results we may abandon","Tripwires only work if somebody owns watching them"],"system":"The bundle identifier and the publishing wildcard become the gate.","screens":"None until the gate fires.","money":"None now."},{"k":"c","label":"Write §52's tripwire list, rename when one fires, no date","what":"Counsel clean, no objection, listings accepted, handles secured — any one firing triggers the rename.","gains":["Keeps the option open while facts are still arriving","The list is already drafted (COMPLETE-RECORD-2026-08-30.md:12541)"],"costs":["A name gets spent by accident when nobody owns the watch","No date means no forcing function"],"system":"No change.","screens":"No change.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Form factor first; the name inherits whatever the surface requires","what":"The store or the desktop sets the name, and the gap register's ordering stands.","gains":["Follows the ordering already written down (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:100-101)","The surface, not the word, is what a buyer meets first"],"costs":["Scores the extension path with a cost that may not exist","Lets a surface choice set a company asset"],"system":"No change.","screens":"No change.","money":"None."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["Everything before the first installation is a search-and-replace across 44 of 248 files, 169 occurrences, measured 2026-09-09.","What cannot be undone is a string somebody else holds: a notarised app on a stranger's machine, a customer's CNAME to `pages.frontmatter.app` (docs/DEV-PLAN.md:1683).","Take the name inside the same sitting as the form factor, name first, then re-score decision 6. Both are already on that agenda (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:150).","Do not let this gate carry the error-type URIs. They move off the brand domain under N6 whatever the name turns out to be."],"flip":"If the weeks-1-2 landing pages are meant to generate press and backlinks rather than recruit ten people, they become the expensive asset and the freeze moves to this week.","linked":["N1","N3","N6"],"sources":["merged: N10","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:104","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:237","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:309","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:352","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:359-369","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:364","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:100","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:101","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:150","docs/DEV-PLAN.md:627","docs/DEV-PLAN.md:1104","docs/DEV-PLAN.md:1610","docs/DEV-PLAN.md:1679","docs/DEV-PLAN.md:1683","src-tauri/tauri.conf.json:5","docs/FRONTMATTER-MASTER-PLAN-2026-08-28.md:182","docs/FRONTMATTER-COMPLETE-RECORD-2026-08-30.md:12541","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-28/e6-naming-risk.md:110-111","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-28/e6-naming-risk.md:130"]},{"id":"N3","cat":"Name & identity","sub":"Clearance","weight":"critical","q":"Do we read the registers ourselves this week, buy an attorney search, or neither before the pilot?","lede":"One EU word mark has been reported, nobody has opened it, and every register is still unchecked.","visual":{"kind":"flow","nodes":[{"label":"Five registries blocked","note":"the research machine's allowlist","tone":"stop"},{"label":"Read them from an open network","note":"an hour, no money","tone":"accent","edge":"then"},{"label":"Does the EU mark exist?","note":"the only mark anyone has reported","tone":"neutral","edge":"then"},{"label":"Yes: attorney the same day","note":"no longer a cost question","tone":"warn"},{"label":"No: attorney on the shortlist","note":"the money follows a fact","tone":"good"},{"label":"Then anything public","note":"landing pages, listings, domains","tone":"neutral"}],"perRow":3,"note":"Nothing here substitutes for counsel, and none of it may be reported as clearance.","caption":"The blocker was a network allowlist, not a budget"},"stakes":"Choosing between a qualified word and a coinage without clearance risks paying for the rename twice.","state":["Nothing has been checked with any register. §52.4 lists USPTO TESS, EUIPO, IP India/TMR, WIPO Madrid, common-law rights and every domain as UNCHECKED (22-segments-disclosure-naming.md:229).","Round 2 left \"the FRONTMATTER EU word mark, reported but not reproduced from five blocked registries\" on the still-open list (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:146).","US registrability of the word is itself doubtful: a §2(e)(1) descriptiveness refusal is the read, tagged inference rather than counsel (e6-naming-risk.md:86).","The corpus holds no price for a knock-out search. Every hit is the recommendation, none a figure (grepped 2026-09-09)."],"path":["Three reports gave the same instruction and none was executed: a knock-out search before any spend on domains, logo or launch copy (r4-naming-candidates.md:154; 22-segments-disclosure-naming.md:229; r13-s6-remaining-unknowns.md:149).","Counsel was told to run EUIPO eSearch and Benelux BOIP, because the incumbent is Belgian and Benelux is his home registry (e6-naming-risk.md:85).","The trademark attorney then appeared in the record's own list of non-recoverable spend front-loaded before any demand signal (r13-s6-remaining-unknowns.md:177)."],"tension":["The blocker was the network, not the budget. Five registries were unreachable from the machine that ran the research.","So \"we have not cleared the name\" is a tooling fact being carried as if it were a cost decision.","If the word is too descriptive to register, we cannot defend it either, and that is the exact trigger that renamed Riot.im (e6-naming-risk.md:86, :111)."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"What is known about the mark, and what is not","items":[["US registration","none surfaced","e6-naming-risk.md:84 — search-summary only, \"snippets cannot prove a negative\""],["EU registration","one reported, never reproduced","GAPS-2026-09-08.md:146 — five registries blocked"],["Benelux (the incumbent is Belgian)","unchecked","e6-naming-risk.md:85 — named as the relevant home registry"],["India / IP India TMR","unchecked","22-segments-disclosure-naming.md:229"],["Cost of a knock-out search","no figure anywhere in the corpus","grepped 2026-09-09 — every hit is the recommendation, none a price"],["US registrability of \"frontmatter\"","§2(e)(1) descriptiveness refusal risk","e6-naming-risk.md:86 — tagged [inference], not counsel"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Pay an attorney for a knock-out search now, on two names","what":"Counsel runs TESS, eSearch and BOIP on the shortlist before any public asset carries a name.","gains":["Settles the question properly, and it is the only thing that can","Unblocks N1, N2 and N6 in one step"],"costs":["Spends money before any demand signal, on a name we may drop anyway","No price in the corpus to budget against"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"Unbudgeted; the corpus has no figure for it."},{"k":"b","label":"Read the registers ourselves first, then buy counsel on what survives","what":"An hour on an unblocked connection either produces the reported EU mark or refutes it.","gains":["The cheapest item on this entire list","The money then follows a fact rather than a rumour"],"costs":["Not clearance, and must never be reported as clearance","A free search cannot prove a negative"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"Nothing this week."},{"k":"c","label":"Skip clearance; rely on descriptiveness and no enforcement posture","what":"Ship on the read that confusion, not litigation, is the binding constraint.","gains":["Free, and defensible on the evidence we have","The incumbent shows no trade-mark symbol and no enforcement (e6-naming-risk.md:89)"],"costs":["The evidence we have is that nobody could open a register","Implies we cannot register anything either, which is the Riot.im trigger"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None, until a rename."},{"k":"d","label":"Defer until after the two-week tests","what":"Landing pages and conversations run first; the legal question waits for a demand signal.","gains":["Spends nothing before there is evidence anyone wants the product","The two-week tests do not need a cleared name to run"],"costs":["Puts public assets up under a name whose legal status is unknown","The one thing all three reports told us not to do"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None now, more later."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["What stopped the corpus was a network allowlist, not money, and one of the blocked registries holds the only mark anybody has reported.","An hour on an open connection either produces that record or kills it, and it is the cheapest item on this list.","Buy counsel afterwards, on the shortlist that survives, so the spend follows a fact.","Add MDMAX to the same shortlist under N4 rather than assuming a coined engine name is clean."],"flip":"A live mark in an overlapping class turns this from a cost question into an attorney engagement the same day.","linked":["N1","N4","N9"],"sources":["docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:146","docs/research/prd-v2-sections/22-segments-disclosure-naming.md:229","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-28/e6-naming-risk.md:84","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-28/e6-naming-risk.md:85","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-28/e6-naming-risk.md:86","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-28/e6-naming-risk.md:89","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-28/e6-naming-risk.md:111","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-29-r11/r4-naming-candidates.md:154","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r13-s6-remaining-unknowns.md:149","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r13-s6-remaining-unknowns.md:177"],"dupes":{"dropped":["L15","R10"],"why":"Do we buy a trademark knock-out search, and before or after the name is decided. Recs b/a/a. Name & identity owns clearance. L15's rename options duplicate N1; R10's are the same timing fork."}},{"id":"N4","cat":"Name & identity","sub":"Two names","weight":"high","q":"Do we keep two names, MDMAX for the engine and certificate and another for the product, or collapse to one?","lede":"The licence chosen for the engine only works if MDMAX is a mark we can defend, and nobody has checked that it is.","visual":{"kind":"arch","layers":[{"label":"Engine","items":["mdmax, 13 files, 3,614 lines","npm 404 on 2026-08-30"],"side":"the word the licence withholds","tone":"accent"},{"label":"Packages","items":["mdmax","mdmax-cli"],"side":"two published, one repo","tone":"sunk"},{"label":"Certificate","items":["mdmax cert","7 engines, 15 targets"],"side":"the published claim Apache-2.0 §6 protects","tone":"neutral"},{"label":"Product","items":["the editor"],"side":"the name under review in N1","tone":"warn"}],"note":"Product code reaches exactly one symbol of the engine today.","caption":"Which layer owns a name a fork cannot use"},"stakes":"Without a defensible engine mark, a fork can issue rendering certificates under a name we cannot contest.","state":["The engine already ships under its own name: two published packages, `mdmax` and `mdmax-cli`, from one repo (docs/ENGINE.md:2231).","`mdmax` was free on npm, confirmed 404 on 2026-08-30, while `frontmatter` returned 200 (docs/ENGINE.md:2235).","Apache-2.0 was chosen over MIT for one stated reason: §6 withholds trademark rights, so a fork cannot issue certificates under the word MDMAX (docs/ENGINE.md:2237).","The hierarchy is written down: \"frontmatter is Google Docs for markdown. MDMAX is the small library underneath it\" (docs/mdmax/PLAN.md:17)."],"path":["MDMAX was named before the product name came under review.","The r7 report offers this exact flip as Option B and calls it the legally cleanest option already sitting in inventory (e6-naming-risk.md:9).","The master plan then made that flip its recommendation for the naming item (FRONTMATTER-MASTER-PLAN-2026-08-28.md:182)."],"tension":["The licence decision assumes MDMAX is defensible, and it has had no more clearance than the product name. §52.4's UNCHECKED list covers every name (22-segments-disclosure-naming.md:229).","Two names double the teaching and the registration, and the one carrying the legal weight is the one nobody says out loud.","What the second name protects is under a live falsifier. DESTROY occurs zero times in 10,176 blocks, and the engine doc concludes a 200-line linter with five rules (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:512)."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"The two names, as measured","cols":["Name","npm","GitHub","Role today","Source"],"rows":[["mdmax","free (404), confirmed 2026-08-30","user taken — 2 repos, joined 2012-11-28; 18 repos named, none a product","engine, certificate, CLI, MCP server","ENGINE.md:2235; r4-naming-candidates.md:69"],["frontmatter","taken (HTTP 200) — dead 2022 v0.0.3 parser","org taken by the incumbent, created 2021-09-21","the product","ENGINE.md:2235; 22-segments-disclosure-naming.md:187-188"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"How much product depends on the engine name today","items":[["Files in src/modules/mdmax/","13, 3,614 lines","ENGINE.md:444"],["Symbols product code imports from it","1 (decodeStrict), in 2 files","ENGINE.md:444 — [measured]"],["Engine tests passing","851 across 23 files, 1.63s","ENGINE.md:444 — \"tested and unreached\""],["DESTROY verdicts on the pinned corpus","0 in 10,176 blocks","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:512 — the certificate's own falsifier"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Keep both; register MDMAX as the house mark","what":"The product name stays descriptive and MDMAX is the registrable word attached to the certificate.","gains":["The certificate gets a mark a fork cannot use, which is why Apache-2.0 was chosen","Costs nothing extra to keep: the packages are already named that way"],"costs":["Two clearance searches instead of one, and MDMAX has had none","Two names to teach, and the legal one is never spoken"],"system":"No change; the packages already exist.","screens":"A NOTICE and a mark line in the certificate output.","money":"A second knock-out search."},{"k":"b","label":"Collapse to one name — the product's name is also the engine's","what":"One word covers the editor, the packages and the certificate.","gains":["One mark, one story, one clearance search","Simplest thing to explain to anyone"],"costs":["Loses the trademark hook the licence rests on","A fork could then issue certificates under a name we cannot contest"],"system":"Rename two published packages and the CLI.","screens":"Certificate output and the CLI banner.","money":"One search instead of two."},{"k":"c","label":"Flip: MDMAX is the product, \"frontmatter\" stays the descriptive word","what":"The coined word becomes the brand, and the old word only names the block the editor reads.","gains":["Answers N1 for free with a name already in inventory","The legally cleanest option the r7 report found (e6-naming-risk.md:9)"],"costs":["\"md\" reads as a medical degree to non-developers (r4-naming-candidates.md:69)","The corpus rates it a library name, not a product name"],"system":"The engine keeps its packages; the product's strings change.","screens":"Wordmark everywhere.","money":"No new clearance beyond the one search."},{"k":"d","label":"Drop MDMAX; publish the engine under the product's scope","what":"One npm scope carries the editor and the engine, and the certificate has no separate identity.","gains":["Simplest packaging story","One npm scope to hold and one account to secure"],"costs":["Concedes the certificate mark entirely","Contradicts a licence decision already written down (docs/ENGINE.md:2237)"],"system":"Republish under a scope; every consumer's import path changes.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["The certificate is a published claim about seven third-party rendering engines, and the licence protecting it only functions if there is a mark to withhold (docs/ENGINE.md:2237).","A coined engine name is the strongest registrable thing in the inventory, and it costs nothing extra because the packages are already named that way.","Add MDMAX to N3's shortlist rather than assuming it is clean; §52.4's unchecked list covers it too."],"flip":"Cut the certificate and the second name loses its job. The test that settles it costs a day and is already specified (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:512).","linked":["N1","N3"],"sources":["docs/ENGINE.md:444","docs/ENGINE.md:2231","docs/ENGINE.md:2235","docs/ENGINE.md:2237","docs/mdmax/PLAN.md:17","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:512","docs/FRONTMATTER-MASTER-PLAN-2026-08-28.md:182","docs/research/prd-v2-sections/22-segments-disclosure-naming.md:229","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-28/e6-naming-risk.md:9","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-29-r11/r4-naming-candidates.md:69"]},{"id":"N5","cat":"Name & identity","sub":"Who decides","weight":"high","q":"Does the name need a second founder's signature, or does the commit author decide and register to the entity?","lede":"The name is listed as a founder decision while the founder count sits two days past its own deadline.","visual":{"kind":"ba","before":{"title":"Today","lines":[{"t":"The name is a founder decision","mark":"warn"},{"t":"Founder count open since 2026-08-31","mark":"stop"},{"t":"Its own deadline, 2026-09-07, passed","mark":"stop"},{"t":"Domain, npm scope and mark all wait","mark":"stop"}]},"after":{"title":"Registered to the entity","lines":[{"t":"The commit author decides","mark":"good"},{"t":"The company holds every string","mark":"good"},{"t":"An equity split can still change","mark":"good"},{"t":"No assignment to unwind later","mark":"good"}]},"via":"register to the company, never to a person","note":"The registrant and the equity split are different questions.","caption":"Why the founder count stops blocking the name"},"stakes":"A mark and a domain held personally are not compatible with a two-founder story later without an assignment.","state":["The plan's resourcing line reads \"One person, on the evidence\": 80 of 80 commits here and 416 of 416 on the sibling, one author (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:231).","The record's §53 says \"One person. This is the binding constraint on everything above\" (docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:4854).","Round 2 lists the name and \"one person or two\" as two separate founder decisions from the same round (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:150).","The gap register marks resolving the name as one of four items that cannot be done without the founders (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:112)."],"path":["\"Two founders\" entered the record as a pasted session-pack constraint and appears nowhere else with authority (docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:13652).","BRIEF.md:115 flagged the contradiction on 2026-08-31 and it is still open.","CRITIQUE.md:2100 set a resolution date of 2026-09-07 and the words \"No hybrid, no probably, no verbal\"."],"tension":["Waiting for a signature that is already overdue blocks the domain, the bundle identifier and the clearance search, all of which sit downstream of the name.","An assignment is cheaper before there is a mark than after.","Only one of these two questions has to be answered this week, and it is the smaller one."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"Who is on the record","items":[["Commits on this repo","80 of 80, one author","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:231"],["Commits on the sibling","416 of 416, one author","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:231"],["Total, one author","496","[derived] 80 + 416, computed 2026-09-09"],["Cofounder named anywhere in the record","0 — grepped across 16,189 lines when that audit ran; the file is 18,344 lines today and the claim has not been re-run","FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:13652"],["Deadline set for the founder count","2026-09-07","CRITIQUE.md:2100 — passed"],["Measured engineering days per calendar week","1.21","GAPS-2026-09-08.md:132 — a one-person rate"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"The commit author decides; every registration goes to the entity","what":"The company is the registrant of the mark, the domains and the handles, whoever ends up owning what.","gains":["Unblocks the name, the domains and the clearance search this week","Makes the founder count orthogonal: the split can change, the registrant need not"],"costs":["Needs the entity to exist before the first registration","Decides a founder-listed item without the second founder"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"Registrations billed to the company, not reimbursed later."},{"k":"b","label":"Hold the name until a signed founders' agreement exists","what":"Nothing is registered and nothing is decided until the second signature arrives.","gains":["No decision is taken that a second founder could reasonably object to","Removes any later argument about who agreed to what"],"costs":["Blocks four downstream decisions on a signature two days overdue","It has been asked for since 2026-08-31 (docs/BRIEF.md:115)"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None, and no progress."},{"k":"c","label":"Decide the name now, record it as reversible until the agreement exists","what":"The word is chosen but explicitly held open pending the founder question.","gains":["Progress on N1 without foreclosing the founder question","Keeps the founder question genuinely open while the word is chosen"],"costs":["Contradicts N2: the point of a freeze is that the name stops being reversible","A reversible name gets spent anyway"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Register personally, assign to the entity later","what":"One person holds the mark and domains now and transfers them when the entity is ready.","gains":["Cheapest thing to do today","The entity does not have to exist before the first registration"],"costs":["Most expensive if a second founder is real","Assignments of marks are a filing, not an email"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"A later assignment cost."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["There is one author on 496 of 496 commits and the record's own audit found no second name (docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:13652).","Registering to the entity rather than to a person is what makes the founder count irrelevant here: the company owns the mark whatever the split becomes.","The alternative blocks the domain, the identifier and the clearance search on a signature that is already late."],"flip":"A signed agreement naming a person with a start date and an hours commitment; even then nothing about registering to the entity has to be undone.","linked":["N1","N2","N6"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:231","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:4854","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:13652","docs/CRITIQUE.md:2100","docs/BRIEF.md:115","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:112","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:132","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:150"]},{"id":"N6","cat":"Name & identity","sub":"The permanent strings","weight":"high","q":"Do the bundle identifier and the permanent URIs carry the name, or a string that survives a rename?","lede":"The pilot's app identifies itself as another product, and the one permanent URI space points at a domain nobody has checked.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":200,"cols":[{"title":"Carries the brand","tone":"warn"},{"title":"Name-free","tone":"accent"}],"rows":[{"label":"Bundle identifier","cells":["A rename migrates preferences, keychain, updates","Survives every rename; odd in a crash report"]},{"label":"API error-type URIs","cells":["\"stable forever — changing one is breaking\"","Never moves, whatever the brand becomes"]},{"label":"Publishing wildcard","cells":["Customers CNAME to it; breaking to move","Plainer, and nobody types it"]},{"label":"Marketing site","cells":["The one string a brand should own","Loses the point of having a brand"]},{"label":"GitHub App name","cells":["3 names across 4 environments","Namespace never checked either way"]}],"note":"Only the first three end up held by somebody other than us.","caption":"Which strings other people end up holding"},"stakes":"Bind the brand into the bundle identifier or the error URIs and a rename becomes a migration on other people's machines.","state":["`src-tauri` still ships the sibling: productName `sgnk-md` (:3), identifier `ai.sgnk.md` (:5), window title (:18), frontendDist `https://md.sgnk.ai` (:9), and the crate name (src-tauri/Cargo.toml:2).","The plan says only that it \"must be re-identified\" and does not say to what (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:104).","DEV-PLAN carries `frontmatter.app` on 17 lines and `frontmatter.dev` on 6, measured 2026-09-09, and the thesis puts the web app on the second (docs/THESIS.md:956).","§52.2 records domains as UNCHECKED on every row, because no registrar or RDAP host was reachable (22-segments-disclosure-naming.md:194)."],"path":["The desktop identity came with the fork: 41 of 43 editor files are byte-identical to sgnk-md and none is unique to frontmatter (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:141).","The dev-plan sections and the thesis were written in different rounds, each assuming a domain, and nobody reconciled them.","The neighbouring TLDs were already occupied when r7 looked: `.codes` is the incumbent's, `.io` a live company, `.cc` an agent-skills builder (e6-naming-risk.md:2, :7)."],"tension":["The bundle identifier is the operating system's name for the app. It keys preferences, keychain entries and the signed update channel.","Exactly one string is declared permanent in writing, and it points at a domain nobody has checked (docs/DEV-PLAN.md:627).","Leaving `ai.sgnk.md` puts another product's identity into a notarised bundle and into the update channel.","The marketing name and the identifier do not have to be the same string. Making them the same is what turns a rename into a migration."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"What the desktop app calls itself today","cols":["Field","Value","File:line"],"rows":[["productName","sgnk-md","src-tauri/tauri.conf.json:3"],["identifier","ai.sgnk.md","src-tauri/tauri.conf.json:5"],["frontendDist","https://md.sgnk.ai","src-tauri/tauri.conf.json:9"],["window title","sgnk-md","src-tauri/tauri.conf.json:18"],["longDescription","\"sgnk-md is a markdown workspace…\"","src-tauri/tauri.conf.json:59"],["crate name","sgnk-md","src-tauri/Cargo.toml:2"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"What signing this identity will cost, and how deep the fork goes","items":[["Apple Developer ID","$99/year — budgeted, not yet spent","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:104, :231 — required to notarise the .dmg"],["Windows code signing","$150-400/year plus a hardware token — budgeted, not yet spent","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:104, :231"],["Auto-updater","must be signed and configured before the first public build","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:104"],["Editor files identical to the sibling","41 of 43","GAPS-2026-09-08.md:141"],["Files unique to frontmatter in the editor","0","GAPS-2026-09-08.md:141"]]},{"type":"table","title":"Who holds the neighbouring domains","cols":["Domain","Holder","Source"],"rows":[["frontmatter.codes","Front Matter CMS, the incumbent","e6-naming-risk.md:2"],["frontmatter.io","live creative-services company, Fremont CA, 11-50 employees; appears among the top results for the bare word","e6-naming-risk.md:7, :97"],["frontmatter.cc","\"Visual Builder for AI Agent Skills, Prompts & MCP Configs\"","e6-naming-risk.md:7"],["frontmatter.com","no product surfaced; registration status unverified","COMPLETE-RECORD-2026-08-30.md:7755"],["frontmatter.app / frontmatter.dev","assumed by the build plan; never checked","DEV-PLAN.md (17 + 6 lines); 22-segments-disclosure-naming.md:194"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"How deep the assumption goes","items":[["frontmatter.app — lines in DEV-PLAN","17 lines, 19 occurrences","measured 2026-09-09"],["frontmatter.dev — lines in DEV-PLAN","6 lines, 6 occurrences","measured 2026-09-09"],["GitHub App names planned","3 distinct, across 4 environments","DEV-PLAN.md:1610; manifest name \"Frontmatter\" at :1104"],["URI spaces the plan declares unchangeable","1 — the error-type URIs, on frontmatter.dev","DEV-PLAN.md:627"],["Domains actually checked","0","22-segments-disclosure-naming.md:194"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Bind everything to the product name now","what":"The identifier, both domains and the App name all carry whatever N1 decides, this week.","gains":["Clean and conventional; one string to remember","Every reference in DEV-PLAN becomes true at once"],"costs":["Forces N1 before N3's register searches have run","A later rename then migrates an installed app and a customer's DNS"],"system":"src-tauri, DEV-PLAN's 23 domain lines and the App manifest all change together.","screens":"Desktop window title, About panel, error pages.","money":"Two domains for a name N1 may replace."},{"k":"b","label":"Name-free identifier, and the permanent URIs on a domain we hold regardless","what":"The bundle identifier and the error-type URIs stop carrying the brand; the marketing domain stays replaceable.","gains":["Separates what cannot change from what is most likely to","Can be set before the first signed build without waiting for N1","Fixes the one string the plan itself calls breaking, in one line"],"costs":["One convention decision, and it looks odd in a crash report","A second domain to hold and renew"],"system":"One line in tauri.conf.json; the error-type base URI moves.","screens":"Nothing visible except the error URI in API responses.","money":"One extra domain a year."},{"k":"c","label":"Leave `ai.sgnk.md` and both domains until the name is settled","what":"Nothing changes until N1 concludes, and the pilot ships on whatever is in the config.","gains":["No work now, and no decision taken twice","Keeps every string open until N1 concludes"],"costs":["Ten strangers install an app that identifies itself as a different product","Any notarised build carries that identity into the update channel"],"system":"No change.","screens":"The desktop app keeps the sibling's title and description.","money":"None now."},{"k":"d","label":"Buy both domains today and collapse DEV-PLAN's 23 lines onto one","what":"Availability is checked, both are bought, and the plan stops disagreeing with itself about which is home.","gains":["Removes the unchecked assumption immediately","Ends the internal disagreement about which domain is home"],"costs":["Spends on two domains for a name N1 may replace","Still leaves the permanent URIs on the brand"],"system":"An hour of editing across 23 lines.","screens":"None.","money":"Two domain registrations."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["The identifier and the marketing name do not have to match, and making them match is what turns a naming decision into a migration.","One string in the build plan is declared unchangeable and it points at an unchecked domain. That is the single fixable mistake here, and it is one line (docs/DEV-PLAN.md:627).","The publishing wildcard is the second, because customers point their own DNS at it (docs/DEV-PLAN.md:1683).","Leaving `ai.sgnk.md` is worse than either alternative, because it writes another product's identity into a notarised bundle."],"flip":"If the name is frozen this week under N2, the identifier and the brand can be the same string and (a) is simpler.","linked":["N1","N2","N5"],"sources":["merged: N7","src-tauri/tauri.conf.json:3","src-tauri/tauri.conf.json:5","src-tauri/tauri.conf.json:9","src-tauri/tauri.conf.json:18","src-tauri/tauri.conf.json:59","src-tauri/Cargo.toml:2","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:104","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:231","docs/DEV-PLAN.md:627","docs/DEV-PLAN.md:1104","docs/DEV-PLAN.md:1610","docs/DEV-PLAN.md:1679","docs/DEV-PLAN.md:1683","docs/DEV-PLAN.md:2381","docs/BUSINESS.md:650","docs/THESIS.md:956","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:141","docs/research/prd-v2-sections/22-segments-disclosure-naming.md:194","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-28/e6-naming-risk.md:2","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-28/e6-naming-risk.md:7","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-28/e6-naming-risk.md:97","docs/FRONTMATTER-COMPLETE-RECORD-2026-08-30.md:7755"],"dupes":{"dropped":["AC9"],"why":"Do the bundle identifier and the permanent URIs carry the product name or a string that survives a rename. Same options, both rec the name-free identifier. Name & identity owns the permanent strings; the Gatekeeper/updater consequence links to AC8."}},{"id":"N9","cat":"Name & identity","sub":"The incumbent","weight":"high","q":"Do we contact the incumbent's author before deciding the name, and when?","lede":"He has publicly asked for company collaboration, the email has been on our open list since 2026-08-28, and nobody has sent it.","visual":{"kind":"timeline","items":[{"when":"2019-08-23","label":"Front Matter CMS created","note":"senior use in the same trade channel","tone":"neutral"},{"when":"2026","label":"Open Source Priorities Update","note":"invites a company commitment","tone":"good"},{"when":"2026-08-21","label":"v10.12.0 shipped","note":"alive, and 82,265 installs","tone":"neutral"},{"when":"2026-08-28","label":"Detente email logged as F6","note":"master plan open item","tone":"warn"},{"when":"2026-09-09","label":"Still unsent","note":"twelve days later","tone":"stop"}],"note":"He holds three \"Front Matter\" listings in the store an extension would ship into.","caption":"An open door, logged and not walked through"},"stakes":"An email cannot be unsent, and if a mark exists it changes what that email means.","state":["No approach has been made. The r7 report read his README and found a \"2026 Open Source Priorities Update\" (e6-naming-risk.md:52; x4-external-frontier-importer-naming.md:141).","In it, open source \"isn't providing me a sustainable income\", the project stays maintained, and major changes need \"a company commitment\" (e6-naming-risk.md:52).","The master plan logged it the day it was found, as \"F6 (new) the detente email to Elio Struyf\" (FRONTMATTER-MASTER-PLAN-2026-08-28.md:182).","The plan's rule for outbound acts is explicit: \"A maintainer PR is outbound; approval first\" (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:305)."],"path":["The r7 report called the priorities update \"a concrete detente/partnership/brand-acquisition opening\" (e6-naming-risk.md:52).","The same report found no trade-mark symbol and no enforcement posture anywhere, and concluded confusion rather than legal cost is the binding constraint (e6-naming-risk.md:89).","That conclusion is tagged as inference and was built from searches that could not open a single register (e6-naming-risk.md:84)."],"tension":["Contacting creates a dated written record that we knew about the collision before shipping, which is the fact a passing-off argument wants.","Not contacting leaves a 2019 senior user unmanaged, holding three \"Front Matter\" listings in the store an extension would ship into (e6-naming-risk.md:87).","Today's research makes him nearer, not further. Git-backed markdown CMS tools are the adjacency being considered as distribution, and his product is one."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"The incumbent, as a person","items":[["Author","Elio Struyf, Antwerp, Belgium","e6-naming-risk.md:3 — GitHub Star, Microsoft MVP, Google Developer Expert"],["Project created","2019-08-23","e6-naming-risk.md:2 — senior use in the same trade channel"],["Marketplace listings held","3 — CMS, a (BETA) listing, a Theme","e6-naming-risk.md:87; named at COMPLETE-RECORD-2026-08-30.md:12496"],["™ or ® anywhere in the README","none observed","e6-naming-risk.md:89"],["Enforcement posture observed","none — \"confusion cost, not legal cost, is the binding constraint\"","e6-naming-risk.md:89, tagged [inference]"],["The detente email as an open item","logged 2026-08-28, never sent","FRONTMATTER-MASTER-PLAN-2026-08-28.md:182"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Send a friendly heads-up now, before any public asset carries the name","what":"A short note saying what we are building and that we know his project exists.","gains":["The cheapest goodwill move available, and he is sympathetic","Removes the surprise if he later sees a listing next to his"],"costs":["Creates a dated record that we knew before we shipped","Cannot be unsent if a mark later turns up"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Open a sponsorship or brand-licence conversation on his own invitation","what":"Answer the priorities update directly and ask what a coexistence or licence would look like.","gains":["Could settle the whole question at freelance-budget scale","Uses an invitation that has been open since his 2026 update"],"costs":["Commits us to the name before N1 and N3 are answered","A sponsorship is a recurring cost with no revenue behind it"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"A sponsorship, sized by him."},{"k":"c","label":"Do nothing and avoid creating the record","what":"Ship, and deal with the incumbent only if he raises it.","gains":["No dated admission of prior knowledge","Costs nothing and needs no founder time"],"costs":["Leaves a live senior user unmanaged in the store a form-factor decision may send us to","Forfeits a door that has been open for a year"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Contact only after the registers have been read","what":"Run N3's free searches first, then write, knowing what the email actually commits us to.","gains":["Delays a friendly email by about a week and loses nothing","He has been asking since his 2026 update and is not going anywhere"],"costs":["One more week of a live collision going unmanaged","Depends on N3 actually being done"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"d","recCase":["The corpus reads confusion rather than litigation as the binding constraint, but that read is tagged inference and was built from searches that opened no register (e6-naming-risk.md:84, :89).","One EU mark has been reported and never reproduced, and if it exists the email means something different (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:146).","N3's free searches cost an hour, so the delay is a week at most.","Outbound acts need approval under the plan's own rule, so this is a founder send either way (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:305)."],"flip":"A clean clearance makes (b) genuinely attractive, because he is asking for exactly the kind of collaboration that would settle this permanently.","linked":["N1","N3"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:305","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:146","docs/FRONTMATTER-MASTER-PLAN-2026-08-28.md:182","docs/FRONTMATTER-COMPLETE-RECORD-2026-08-30.md:12496","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-28/e6-naming-risk.md:2","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-28/e6-naming-risk.md:3","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-28/e6-naming-risk.md:52","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-28/e6-naming-risk.md:84","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-28/e6-naming-risk.md:87","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-28/e6-naming-risk.md:89","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-29-r7/x4-external-frontier-importer-naming.md:141"]},{"id":"N11","cat":"Name & identity","sub":"Testing","weight":"medium","q":"Is the name a variable in the weeks-1-2 tests, or do we decide it without asking anyone?","lede":"Fifteen people are already being recruited, and not one of them will be asked what the name means.","visual":{"kind":"funnel","steps":[{"label":"Candidates generated","n":41,"unit":"names","tone":"neutral"},{"label":"Probed on npm and GitHub","n":15,"unit":"names","tone":"neutral"},{"label":"Scored against criteria","n":2,"unit":"names","tone":"warn"},{"label":"Shown to anyone outside this project","n":0,"unit":"names","tone":"stop"}],"note":"The zero is a search of the corpus, done 2026-09-09.","caption":"Forty-one names, and nobody outside the project has seen one"},"stakes":"The name gets settled on registry probes and taste, with no evidence from anyone who is not us.","state":["Weeks 1-2 run four tests across fifteen recruited people plus 20 team conversations (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:352).","The tested variable is three headline variants (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:296). The name is not a variable in any test.","There is already a five-second screenshot test in the script, asking what the blue tint means (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:411).","§64.6 scores two names against six criteria; four are pure judgment and the other two rest on registry probes (r13-s4-positioning-messaging.md:129-136)."],"path":["The tests were designed around the headline, because the headline is what the 2026-09-08 adversarial round attacked and did not leave standing (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:124).","Round r11 generated 41 candidates and pruned to 15 on handle availability alone (r4-naming-candidates.md:29, :63).","No record anywhere in the corpus shows a candidate name being read by a person outside the project (searched 2026-09-09)."],"tension":["Recruiting is already happening and the question costs ten seconds a person.","A landing-page arm would read the name cleanly, but the arms are what the two weeks exist to settle (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:296).","Five people is a weak signal and must never be reported as more than that.","If N2 freezes the name before week 1, asking becomes a post-hoc justification rather than evidence."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"Naming evidence in the corpus","items":[["Names scored against criteria","2 — a coinage and a qualified form","r13-s4-positioning-messaging.md:129-136 — 4 of 6 criteria are pure judgment, 2 rest on registry probes"],["Candidate names generated","41","r4-naming-candidates.md:29 — \"41 names, with strategy\"; an earlier draft of this card said 61, which the file does not support"],["Candidates probed for npm/GitHub availability","15","r4-naming-candidates.md:63 — \"Availability table — top 15\", measured 2026-08-29"],["Strangers asked what any candidate name means","0","no record found anywhere in the corpus, searched 2026-09-09"],["People already being recruited for weeks 1-2","10 developers, 5 who bill for documents, 20 team conversations","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:352"],["Existing five-second test in the script","1 — what the blue tint means","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:411"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Add one question to the script already running","what":"Ask what a tool called X would do, and whether they have seen it before.","gains":["No extra recruiting, ten seconds a person","It would be the only naming evidence anyone has"],"costs":["A weak signal from a small n, and it must be reported that way","Adds a question to a script already carrying four tests"],"system":"No change.","screens":"One line in the interview script.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Run one landing page per candidate name and compare","what":"The three landing pages become a name test instead of a headline test.","gains":["A cleaner read on the name than any interview gives","Reads the name against a real visitor, not an interview prompt"],"costs":["Burns a headline arm, and the arms are why the two weeks exist","Confounds the name with the headline it carries"],"system":"No change.","screens":"Three landing pages re-cut.","money":"None beyond the pages already planned."},{"k":"c","label":"Do not test the name; decide on clearance and collision alone","what":"The decision turns on the register searches and the incumbent, and on nothing anyone says.","gains":["Defensible: those are the arguments that actually carry weight","Keeps the two weeks pointed at the headline"],"costs":["Leaves a founder decision with zero evidence behind it"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Test only the confusion: show his listing and ask if it is the same product","what":"Five people see the incumbent's store listing beside ours and say whether they are one thing.","gains":["Measures the specific thing at issue rather than taste","Directly sizes the confusion cost the reports call binding"],"costs":["Answers nothing about whether an alternative name would land","Needs a mock listing that does not exist yet"],"system":"No change.","screens":"A mock store listing for the test.","money":"None."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["The test is already recruiting fifteen people and the question takes ten seconds, so it is the cheapest evidence available on a decision that has none.","Separate landing pages would spend a headline arm on a naming question, and the headline arms are the reason the two weeks exist (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:296).","The script already contains a five-second recognition test, so the format is proven within this study (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:411)."],"flip":"If the name is frozen before week 1 under N2, drop the question rather than run it for comfort.","linked":["N1","N2"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:296","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:352","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:411","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:124","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r13-s4-positioning-messaging.md:129-136","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-29-r11/r4-naming-candidates.md:29","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-29-r11/r4-naming-candidates.md:63"]},{"id":"PL2","cat":"Plan, scope & sequencing","sub":"Schedule","weight":"critical","q":"Which number does the plan publish as its schedule — twelve calendar weeks, or the measured 1.21 engineering days a week that makes the same scope 58 weeks?","lede":"One document carries both; they differ by a factor of five, and four competitors shipped the same surface in nine weeks.","visual":{"kind":"timeline","items":[{"when":"2026-07-03","label":"VS Code merges review/unreview","note":"PR #324218, milestone 1.128.0","tone":"warn"},{"when":"2026-08-24","label":"Antigravity ships Agent Edits pane","note":"working-tree diff, free","tone":"warn"},{"when":"2026-08-28","label":"Notion ships per-change approval","note":"agent edits, per change","tone":"warn"},{"when":"2026-09-03","label":"Claude Code v2.1.260 diff panel","note":"opens beside the conversation","tone":"warn"},{"when":"2026-09-08","label":"Our rate measured at 1.21 days a week","note":"10 of 58 calendar days touched src/","tone":"neutral"},{"when":"Week 12","label":"Twelve weeks buys 14.5 days","note":"the fix-first list alone is 25.5","tone":"stop"},{"when":"Week 58","label":"MVP-0 at the measured rate","note":"37 weeks at the best rate ever seen","tone":"stop"}],"note":"Competitor dates from the research briefing, all opened; rates from §9.","caption":"Nine weeks of shipping from the field, against a 58-week build."},"stakes":"A date nothing in the plan can meet turns every gate, kill line and pilot week into a number nobody will enforce.","state":["§9 measures 1.21 engineering days a calendar week here, and prices the same scope at 37 weeks best case and 58 measured (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:227`).","Exhibit 19 still puts ten strangers in weeks 10–12 (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:357`).","Twelve weeks at the measured rate buys 14.5 engineering days, less than the 25.5-day fix-first list (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:210`)."],"path":["The ten weeks was withdrawn in round 2 as impossible: 70 days in 10 weeks is 7.0 a week, seven days a week (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:229`).","The velocity paragraph was rewritten. The calendar under it was not (`docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:130`).","The gap register had already rated the day estimates unmethodical (`docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:22`)."],"tension":["Cutting does not rescue it: at the best-ever 1.91 a week, twelve weeks buys 22.9 days, still under the fix-first list.","Four competitors shipped working-tree agent diffs between 2026-07-03 and 2026-09-03, so the window is not static.","A plan with no date drifts, and `src/` here has not changed in 29 days.","CRITIQUE puts the failure mode at initiation rather than estimation (`docs/CRITIQUE.md:793`)."],"evidence":[{"type":"bars","title":"Engineering days per calendar week","note":"Re-measured here 2026-09-08 by git log: 10 distinct calendar days between 2026-07-13 and 2026-09-08 touched src/, src-tauri/ or test/, over a 58-day window = 1.21/week. Sibling best is the md repo's best-ever regime, per §9.","data":[["Last 30 days here",0.23],["Measured, whole project",1.21],["Sibling md, best ever",1.91],["Needed for 12 weeks",5.83],["Old withdrawn plan",7]],"unit":"eng days / week","threshold":1.21,"thresholdLabel":"measured rate"},{"type":"stat","title":"What twelve weeks actually buys","items":[["Engineering days in 12 weeks at 1.21","14.5","12 × 1.21"],["Engineering days in 12 weeks at 1.91","22.9","12 × 1.91, the best rate ever seen"],["Fix-first list alone","25.5 days","§9 table, rows summed"],["Full MVP-0 at 1.21/week","58 weeks","70 ÷ 1.21, plan's own figure"],["Full MVP-0 at 1.91/week","37 weeks","70 ÷ 1.91, plan's own figure"],["Independent estimate multiple on the earlier 41 days","1.6× central, 2.8×, 3.2× worst","CRITIQUE.md:791"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Keep twelve weeks and commit in writing to 5.8 engineering days a week","what":"The plan keeps its dates and the founder commits to a rate 4.8 times the one measured here.","gains":["Every existing gate date survives untouched","Simple to state and simple to check"],"costs":["Nothing in the capacity model supports 5.8 days a week","The last 30 days ran at 0.23 days a week"],"system":"No change.","screens":"No change.","money":"Honest only if client hours drop to near zero, which the nut does not allow."},{"k":"b","label":"Keep the scope and publish 37–58 weeks","what":"The scope stands and the plan states a pilot 37 to 58 weeks out.","gains":["Truthful, and it can be checked against the commit log","Forces the scope conversation immediately"],"costs":["The pilot lands in 2027 and dated kill lines lose meaning","Nobody can be held to a date that far out"],"system":"No change.","screens":"No change.","money":"Consulting must cover the nut for a year, not a quarter."},{"k":"c","label":"Re-cut MVP-0 to what 1.91 a week delivers in twelve weeks: 22.9 days","what":"MVP-0 shrinks to what the best rate ever observed buys inside the current calendar.","gains":["Keeps a twelve-week frame","Forces a hard cut now rather than a slip later"],"costs":["22.9 days is under the 25.5-day fix-first list","No pilot is left to put in front of ten strangers"],"system":"The cut lands below the engine floor rather than above it.","screens":"No feature screens ship.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Publish engineering days and a weekly rate; re-forecast the date at week 4","what":"The plan reports days achieved every Friday, and sets the pilot date at week 4 from four weeks of measurement.","gains":["Falsifiable on day 7 rather than at week 12","Produces a real date from real data at week 4"],"costs":["No external commitment for four weeks","A plan with no date is easy to let drift"],"system":"§9 already prescribes the weekly report; Exhibit 19's calendar goes.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"d","recCase":["A schedule needing 4.8 times the observed rate is not a schedule, and §9 already prescribes the report it contradicts (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:227`).","Option c cannot produce a twelve-week MVP-0 at all, because 22.9 days is below the fix-first list.","The week-4 re-forecast is the missing piece: it turns a weekly number into a date somebody can be held to.","Against a field that shipped four competing panes in nine weeks, a measured date beats a guessed one."],"flip":"A named second engineer with their own commit record makes 1.21 obsolete, and the density must then be re-derived rather than doubled.","linked":["B1","FF1","PL3"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:210","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:227","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:229","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:357","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:22","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:130","docs/CRITIQUE.md:779","docs/CRITIQUE.md:791","docs/CRITIQUE.md:793"],"dupes":{"dropped":["B3","P18"],"why":"Reconciling the twelve-week calendar with the measured 1.21 engineering days a week, by cutting scope or restating the date. Three of four options match in substance across all three cards; recs split d/b/a. Plan, scope & sequencing owns the schedule."}},{"id":"PL5","cat":"Plan, scope & sequencing","sub":"Exit test","weight":"critical","q":"What does \"the pilot passed\" mean, and how is it observed?","lede":"Three live documents set three different bars, and the proposed instrument is a request this workspace measured returning nothing.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":180,"cols":[{"title":"6 of 10 still using","tone":"neutral"},{"title":"3 ask unprompted","tone":"neutral"},{"title":"3 name it, 2 at day 30","tone":"accent"}],"rows":[{"label":"Measures","cells":["Retention only","Demand only","Demand and retention"]},{"label":"Passable by being polite","cells":["Partly","No","No"]},{"label":"Observed how","cells":["Local file, pasted","Session transcript","Transcript plus day-30 counts"]},{"label":"Needs the paste to work","cells":["Yes","No","For one half"]},{"label":"Where it is written","cells":["Exhibit 6","PRODUCT §95.2","the record's own rewrite"]}],"note":"Each bar carries the instrument it needs; the two cannot be chosen separately.","caption":"Three bars, and what each one can actually be read from."},"stakes":"The one gate allowed to stop the product is softer than the bar it replaced, and not measurable under the architecture.","state":["Exhibit 6's exit test reads \"6 of 10 strangers still using it after two weeks\" (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:206`).","The week-0 draft puts counts in `.frontmatter/usage.jsonl` and reaches us only if a stranger pastes it (`docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:21`).","The gap register rates the whole thing unobservable until the measurement decision exists (`docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:28`).","Zero interviews have been run across the whole programme (`docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:35`)."],"path":["PRODUCT §95.2 set it at six of ten running it plus three asking unprompted (`docs/PRODUCT.md:965`).","The record then attacked its own bar: six of ten measures politeness (`docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:12321`).","The current plan kept the six-of-ten half and dropped the unprompted clause.","The plan forbids a vendor usage database, so only a local opt-in design is compatible (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:313`)."],"tension":["Asking for a paste is the shape of ask that measured 7 fills in 694 opportunities on this workspace.","The marginal fill rate across three measurements was zero, not one percent (`docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-29-r11/r5-measurement-plan.md:14`).","A silent pilot reads as a failed one, and a false negative is the expensive direction.","Ten booked calls is under three hours of talking, and it collects the why counting cannot give."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"Three bars, three documents, all current","cols":["Bar","Source","What it measures"],"rows":[["6 of 10 still using after two weeks","plan Exhibit 6","Retention. Observable only via the week-0 measurement decision"],["6 of 10 run it once, and 3 ask unprompted","PRODUCT §95.2 (DECIDE §3.1 carries only the six-of-ten half)","Trial plus unprompted pull. The unprompted clause was dropped"],["3 of 10 name the review-cost problem before it is named, and 2 still using on day 30","the record's own rewrite, RECORD:12352","Demand plus retention. The bar written after attacking the other two"],["40 people, 40% 'very disappointed' and 5 of 40 naming whole-file rewrites, by 2026-12-31","record, Ellis wording, RECORD:12517","Product-market fit at n=40. Needs four times the recruitment"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"Where the current bar stands","items":[["Interviews run across the whole programme","0","gap register §C row 1"],["Strangers in the pilot","10","plan Exhibit 19, weeks 10–12"],["Measurement decision status","drafted, not accepted","WEEK0-DECISIONS §1"],["Draft's own definition of 'keeps it'","opened on 6 of the last 10 working days, plus one review action in week two","WEEK0-DECISIONS §1, exit measure row"],["Rated by the gap register","unobservable under the architecture","gap register §B row 8"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"What voluntary reporting measured on this workspace","note":"The 7 of 694 row is tagged [brief] in the source, supplied not re-measured; the 1 of 99 replication and the machine-row counts are tagged [measured] on that machine.","items":[["Explicit feedback field, fills","7 of 694","1.0086%"],["Marginal fill rate across three measurements","0","numerator frozen while the denominator grew"],["Machine-written rows in the same period","42,514","gate-tier 21,707 + turn-meta 15,786 + traces 5,021"],["Ratio, machine to human","6,073 : 1","42,514 ÷ 7"],["Preference-log routing_path filled","1 of 99","1.01%, the same number independently"]]},{"type":"table","title":"What each method can and cannot tell you","cols":["Method","Gives you","Does not give you"],"rows":[["Local file, pasted on request","Exact day counts, if they paste","Anything from the ones who do not reply"],["Local file plus a booked day-14 call","The counts read together, plus why","Ten calls of founder time"],["Opt-in upload toggle","Continuous data for those who opt in","Compliance with the no-vendor-database rule at scale, without a notice-and-consent path"],["Interview only","Why someone stopped","A number anyone can audit later"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Six of ten still using after two weeks, local file pasted on request","what":"The current wording stands, and the counts arrive if a stranger chooses to paste the file.","gains":["Cheapest to build","Measures the right half, which is retention"],"costs":["The paste is the method this workspace measured at effectively zero","Nothing in it catches a stranger being polite"],"system":"`.frontmatter/usage.jsonl` and nothing else.","screens":"No new screen; a settings line explaining the file.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Six of ten run it once, three ask unprompted; read from the session","what":"The bar returns to PRODUCT §95.2 and is read from what happens in the session itself.","gains":["Restores the demand clause","Observable with no file and no paste"],"costs":["Says nothing about whether anyone comes back","Ten sessions must be noted consistently"],"system":"No sidecar work needed for the gate.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Three of ten name the problem unprompted, two still using at day 30, booked call","what":"Both halves are required, the unprompted clause is read from the session, and the day-30 count is read together on a call.","gains":["Neither half is passable by a friendly stranger","Both halves are cheap to observe"],"costs":["Ten calls of founder time, booked at recruitment","The day-30 clause extends the pilot by two weeks"],"system":"The usage file stays; the call is scheduling, not engineering.","screens":"None beyond the settings line.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Ellis survey, forty people, 40% very disappointed, by year end","what":"A forty-person survey replaces the ten-stranger gate.","gains":["The strongest signal available","A published, comparable method"],"costs":["Recruiting forty strangers from zero interviews is a different project","Nothing is decided until year end"],"system":"None.","screens":"None.","money":"Recruitment cost, unbudgeted."}],"rec":"c","recCase":["It is the only bar written after somebody attacked the other two (`docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:12352`).","Both halves are observable: the unprompted clause in the session, the day-30 clause in the local counts.","Booking the call when the stranger is recruited turns a 1% ask into an appointment.","It collects the one thing the draft admits counting cannot give, which is why someone stopped (`docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:27`)."],"flip":"If strangers will not take a call, the opt-in upload toggle is the fallback and the usable n drops to whoever opts in.","linked":["B10","PL17","PL7"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:206","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:313","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:357","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:417","docs/DECIDE.md:92","docs/PRODUCT.md:965","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:12321","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:12352","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:12517","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:28","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:35","docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:20","docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:21","docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:22","docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:27","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-29-r11/r5-measurement-plan.md:9","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-29-r11/r5-measurement-plan.md:14","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-29-r11/r5-measurement-plan.md:17","merged: PL6"]},{"id":"PL3","cat":"Plan, scope & sequencing","sub":"Fix-first","weight":"high","q":"When does the fix-first list run, and in what order — the table's, the calendar's, or a split into demo-blockers and ship-blockers?","lede":"A table headed \"these block everything else\" schedules its largest row five weeks after the work it blocks.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":200,"cols":[{"title":"Table order","tone":"neutral"},{"title":"Exhibit 19","tone":"warn"},{"title":"Two named gates","tone":"accent"}],"rows":[{"label":"NF-1, 4 days","cells":["First","Weeks 3–4","Weeks 3–5, demo-blocker"]},{"label":"Engine wiring, 8 days","cells":["Fourth","Weeks 8–9","Weeks 3–5, demo-blocker"]},{"label":"Byte budget, cert, entities, Tauri id","cells":["In the list","In no week","Before the strangers"]},{"label":"Decision-independent rows","cells":["11.5 days","Not distinguished","Start now, in parallel"]},{"label":"First feature week","cells":["After 25.5 days","Week 5","Week 5"]},{"label":"Stated total","cells":["25.5","24, in the sequence line","25.5"]}],"note":"Rows and days from the §9 fix-first table; weeks from Exhibit 19.","caption":"Three artefacts in one document give three orders."},"stakes":"Twenty-nine days of no code have already passed, and the plan's own day-24 falsifier cannot run until NF-1 lands.","state":["§9 opens \"Fix first. These block everything else\" over twelve rows (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:210`).","Exhibit 19 puts CI, NF-3 and NF-1 in weeks 3–4 and engine wiring in weeks 8–9 (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:354`).","The sequence line still reads \"Fix-first (24 days)\" while the rows sum to 25.5 (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:227`).","Weeks 1–2 read \"build nothing\" (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:336`), and `src/` last changed 29 days ago."],"path":["Build-nothing-first was earned: three headlines were refuted by desk research before any code was written.","The table grew in round 2 with rows 0, 10 and 11, and neither the prose sequence nor the calendar followed (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:223`).","Round 2 then attacked the fourth headline and it came back negative too (`docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:124`)."],"tension":["Six rows depend on no open decision: NF-1, NF-3, CI, the byte budget, the cert CLI and the undeclared dependency.","Those six are 11.5 days, which is 9.5 calendar weeks at the measured rate.","Up to six days of the rest are deleted by one answer to decision 6 (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:364`).","The 83% refusal falsifier is dated day 24 and needs NF-1 first (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:327`)."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"Fix-first rows against the open decisions","cols":["Row","Days","Depends on decision 1, 6 or 7?"],"rows":[["1 NF-1 column-zero list item","4","No — engine, correct in any shell"],["2 NF-3 bare-CR fence","3","No"],["3 No CI","1","No"],["5 Byte budget is an echo","2","No"],["10 mdmax cert never runnable","1","No"],["11 entities undeclared dependency","0.5","No"],["4 Engine unwired (one symbol of thirteen files)","8","Yes — wiring target depends on the shell (decision 6)"],["6 No bring-your-own key","3","Yes — deleted if VS Code (decision 6)"],["7 LLM port returns a bare string","2","Yes — only needed if F5/F6/F7 stay (PL1)"],["9 src-tauri carries the sibling's identity","1","Yes — moot if no desktop app"],["0 The shell is a fork · 8 Web byte path","decision","Yes"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"Measured on this repo, 2026-09-08","items":[["Documentation file-changes, last 14 days","396","git log --since='14 days ago' --name-only -- docs"],["src/ file-changes, last 14 days","0","same command against src"],["Days since src/ last changed","29","last src commit cc1d451, 2026-08-10"],["Days since any engineering commit","8","last test commit 484f579, 2026-08-31"],["Decision-independent fix-first work","11.5 days","rows 1,2,3,5,10,11"],["That work at the measured rate","9.5 calendar weeks","11.5 ÷ 1.21"]]},{"type":"table","title":"Fix-first rows against the calendar in Exhibit 19","cols":["Row","Days","Week in Exhibit 19"],"rows":[["3 CI, deliberate red run","1","3–4"],["2 NF-3","3","3–4"],["1 NF-1","4","3–4"],["6 BYO key","3","5–7"],["7 LLM port structured output","2","5–7"],["4 Engine unwired","8","8–9"],["5 Byte budget is an echo","2","not scheduled"],["9 src-tauri identity","1","not scheduled"],["10 mdmax cert never runnable","1","not scheduled"],["11 entities undeclared","0.5","not scheduled"],["Sum of rows","25.5","sequence line still says 24"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"Verified against the code, 2026-09-08","items":[["Files in .github/workflows","0","the directory does not exist"],["package.json budget script","echo 'No bundle budget configured yet — skipping'","literal string at package.json:20, 26 scripts total"],["cert among the 26 scripts","absent","node scripts/mdmax-cert.mjs has no script entry"],["Engine symbols reaching product code","1 of 13 files","decodeStrict from shape-gate, imported in exactly 2 files"],["entities in package.json","absent from dependencies and devDependencies","imported at fold.ts:43 and verdict.ts:53"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Build nothing until week 3 and keep the calendar as written","what":"No code until the week-3 go/no-go, exactly as Exhibit 19 has it.","gains":["Keeps the discipline that refuted three headlines","One job at a time for the founder"],"costs":["Extends a 29-day code freeze to 43","The day-24 refusal falsifier cannot run"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Start the six decision-independent rows now, in parallel with the tests","what":"The six rows that are correct under every open decision start immediately, alongside the human tests.","gains":["Engine hygiene lands whatever the meeting decides","Answers the refusal falsifier on its own deadline"],"costs":["Splits the founder's attention across two jobs","Weeks 1–2 are already over-committed"],"system":"NF-1, NF-3, CI, the byte budget, the cert CLI and the entities dependency all land.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Start the six now; split the rest into demo-blockers and ship-blockers","what":"The remaining rows are separated into what blocks the demo working and what blocks handing it to a stranger.","gains":["Two named gates instead of one vague header","Forces the 4.5 unscheduled days onto a week"],"costs":["The same attention split as option b","Needs Exhibit 19 rewritten in the same edit"],"system":"Demo-blockers 18 days, ship-blockers 7.5 days, from the §9 rows.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Keep the calendar and demote the table to a defect list with no ordering claim","what":"The calendar stands and the table stops claiming to be an order.","gains":["Removes the contradiction in one edit","No new work this fortnight"],"costs":["Removes the argument that the engine must be right first","The 8-day wiring row still lands after what it blocks"],"system":"No change to the code.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"c","recCase":["Those six rows are true under every answer: an engine refusing 83% of real vaults is wrong in an app, an extension and a package alike (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:214`).","The split makes the header argue for itself, because some rows block the demo and others block the handover.","It forces the byte budget, the cert CLI, the entities dependency and the Tauri identity onto a week.","If PL1 cuts the AI block, rows 6 and 7 leave the list and the split gets cleaner."],"flip":"If the meeting concludes the engine is being abandoned for a different substrate, option a is right, and no option on the table does that.","linked":["PL2"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:210","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:212","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:214","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:223","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:224","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:225","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:227","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:327","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:336","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:354","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:356","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:364","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:83","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:124","package.json:20","merged: PL4"]},{"id":"PL7","cat":"Plan, scope & sequencing","sub":"Weeks 1–2","weight":"high","q":"What runs in weeks 1–2 — forty free contacts as written, or fewer tests and one that charges a card?","lede":"After two adversarial rounds nothing has tested whether anyone pays, and the fortnight is already booked at four contacts a day.","visual":{"kind":"timeline","items":[{"when":"Week 0","label":"Buyer, byte path and exit measure written","note":"Exhibit 19, week 0","tone":"neutral"},{"when":"Weeks 1–2","label":"Forty contacts and three landing pages","note":"four a day from a standing start","tone":"warn"},{"when":"Day 14","label":"Kill signals read","note":"under 4 of 10 stops the build","tone":"stop"},{"when":"Week 3","label":"Go or no-go","note":"needs only the developer sessions","tone":"accent"},{"when":"Weeks 1–4","label":"Team conversations and the priced arm","note":"the Pro price gates MVP-1, not week 3","tone":"accent"}],"note":"Weeks and contents from Exhibit 19; the priced arm from the record's Gate 1.","caption":"Which tests the week-3 gate needs, and which can run longer."},"stakes":"The commercial thesis stays untested into the build, which is where being wrong about it becomes expensive.","state":["Weeks 1–2 require ten developer sessions, five billers, twenty team conversations and five screenshot viewings (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:352`).","No checkout, no price and no card appear anywhere in the fortnight.","The same fortnight is labelled \"build nothing\" while it builds three landing pages and a cut plugin (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:336`).","The gap register still lists whether anyone pays as open after eleven gaps of desk research (`docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:146`)."],"path":["Each test was added by a different round to close a different gap, and nobody summed them.","An earlier ninety-day plan made a priced test the first gate: $19 refundable, a real card (`docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:14169`).","Gate 1 was twelve paid pre-orders on 1,200 visitors, and it was allowed to kill the product (`docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:14198`)."],"tension":["Zero interviews have been run, and the answer to zero is forty in ten working days (`docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:35`).","Only the developer sessions and the screenshot test gate the week-3 decision; the team conversations gate MVP-1.","Almanac raised $45M on this feature sentence and shut down on 2025-01-31, so attention is not payment.","A pre-order arm needs a checkout and 1,200 visitors that no budget line covers."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"What the scheduled tests can and cannot falsify","cols":["Test","Falsifies","Does not falsify"],"rows":[["Ten developers shown the mock, both framings","That the problem is recognised","That anyone would buy the answer"],["Five people who bill for documents","That approval is a felt cost","Price, seat count, or who signs"],["Three landing pages","Which headline reads best","Whether any headline converts to money"],["Twenty team conversations","What teams say they are gated on","What a team does when asked for a card"],["Five-second screenshot test","Whether the tint reads as a tint","Anything commercial"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"The priced test that was designed and then dropped","items":[["Gate 1 threshold","12 paid pre-orders","record's 90-day plan, RECORD:14193"],["Traffic required","1,200 visitors, 400 per arm","≥1.00% capture"],["Price point","$19, fully refundable on request","real card charged, RECORD:14169"],["Paid ads ceiling","₹20,000","₹16.67 per click at 1,200"],["What Gate 1 was allowed to kill","the entire product","stated in the plan's own words, RECORD:14198"],["Payment evidence gathered to date","none","gap register, still open"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"The fortnight, counted","items":[["Developers shown the mock","10","decision 1"],["People who bill for documents","5","decision 2"],["Team conversations","20","the Pro price"],["Five-second screenshot viewings","5","whether the tint reads"],["Total contacts","40","4 per working day"],["Builds inside 'build nothing'","3 landing pages, plus a plugin that no longer exists","Exhibit 19, weeks 1–2"],["Interviews run to date","0","across the whole programme"]]},{"type":"table","title":"What each test gates, and when that gate is actually needed","cols":["Test","Gates","Needed by"],"rows":[["Ten developer sessions","the week-3 go/no-go","week 3"],["Five-second screenshot","whether the tint design is wrong before building","week 3"],["Five billers","decision 2, first buyer","week 1, per Exhibit 20"],["Twenty team conversations","the Pro price and MVP-1's offer","MVP-1, months later"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Run all four tests as written, forty contacts in two weeks, free","what":"Every scheduled test runs in the ten working days, and price is left to the team conversations.","gains":["Every question closes at once if recruitment holds","No checkout to build"],"costs":["If recruitment slips, the week-3 gate runs on partial data","Nothing in the fortnight can falsify the price"],"system":"None.","screens":"Three landing pages.","money":"No revenue signal at all."},{"k":"b","label":"Sequence: developers and the screenshot test first, teams over four weeks","what":"The two tests the week-3 gate needs run on time, and the twenty team conversations get four weeks.","gains":["The go/no-go happens on time on the questions it needs","A realistic window for the price question"],"costs":["PL15's answer arrives later","Still no test that can return a refusal to pay"],"system":"None.","screens":"Three landing pages.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Sequence as in (b) and add a refundable pre-order arm to the landing pages","what":"The tests are sequenced and one landing-page arm charges a real, refundable card at a stated price.","gains":["The only test on the table that can return a hard no","Numbers for it already exist in the record"],"costs":["Needs a checkout and 1,200 visitors nobody has budgeted","Sells an artefact decision 6 may change"],"system":"A checkout and a refund path, neither in MVP-0's scope.","screens":"A pricing and checkout page outside the product.","money":"₹20,000 ad ceiling in the record's version; refunds on request."},{"k":"d","label":"Keep all four at lower n; ask teams for signed intent at a stated price","what":"Contact counts drop and teams are asked to sign an intent instead of paying.","gains":["Twenty-one contacts is deliverable","No checkout and no refunds"],"costs":["Every 'x of 10' threshold in §13 has to be restated","Signed intent has no measured conversion here"],"system":"None.","screens":"Three landing pages.","money":"None."}],"rec":"c","recCase":["It is the only test that can return a no, and it exists with numbers attached (`docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:14177`).","Sequencing is what makes room for it: only two of the four tests gate the week-3 decision.","Two rounds have proved that installs and attention do not predict purchase (`docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:146`).","A card returns a decision; twenty conversations return opinions."],"flip":"If decision 6 sends the form factor to a VS Code extension, the pre-order page sells a different artefact and the arms must be rewritten first.","linked":["PL17","PL5","PR17"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:336","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:352","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:366","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:14169","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:14177","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:14193","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:14198","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:35","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:146","merged: PL9"]},{"id":"PL10","cat":"Plan, scope & sequencing","sub":"Kill conditions","weight":"high","q":"Which kill set is live — the market conditions in the current plan, or the seven dated switches in the record, including the one tripped right now?","lede":"Not one condition in the current plan can ever fire on the founder.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":180,"cols":[{"title":"§13's four","tone":"neutral"},{"title":"KS5 to KS7","tone":"accent"}],"rows":[{"label":"Fires on","cells":["The market or the engine","The founder's own capacity"]},{"label":"Checked how","cells":["Interviews and corpus runs","Two git commands, no judgment"]},{"label":"Reading today","cells":["Not yet started","KS5 at 396 to 0 over 14 days"]},{"label":"Named action","cells":["Stop, or re-cut and retest","Freeze writing 14 days; cancel the month"]},{"label":"Attached to a live asset","cells":["One is attached to a cut plugin","Yes"]}],"note":"KS5 re-run here with the two commands the switch itself names.","caption":"Which kill set can fire on the person doing the work."},"stakes":"A kill switch nobody executes trains everyone to discount the rest of them.","state":["§13 carries four numeric conditions, all about the market or the engine (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:321`, `docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:327`).","A fifth, the plugin's 200-install line, sits in Exhibit 6 and is attached to a channel §12 has cut (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:204`).","KS5 to KS7 each carry a date, a condition and a named action, and none was carried into the plan (`docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:14295`).","KS5 reads 396 documentation file-changes against zero in `src/` over the last fourteen days."],"path":["The record's ninety-day plan wrote KS1 to KS7 on 2026-08-31.","The plan was rewritten and the three capacity switches were not carried across.","KS5 was already tripped on the day it was written, at 29.2 to 1, and has stayed tripped."],"tension":["KS5's action is a fourteen-day writing freeze, which is roughly what the last fortnight produced in code anyway.","Starting the clock today would freeze the week-0 measurement and byte-path pages PL5 depends on.","CRITIQUE names initiation, not estimation, as this project's failure mode (`docs/CRITIQUE.md:793`).","KS1 assumes a priced test, so adopting the whole set forces PL7's hand."],"evidence":[{"type":"bars","title":"KS5, measured on this repo 2026-09-08","note":"KS5 fires above 3:1 for two consecutive weeks. Re-run here with the two commands the switch itself names: git log --since='14 days ago' --name-only --pretty=format: -- docs, and the same for src.","data":[["docs/ file-changes, 14 days",396],["src/ file-changes, 14 days",0],["KS5 trip line",3]],"unit":"file changes","threshold":3,"thresholdLabel":"3:1 trip line"},{"type":"table","title":"The two kill sets","cols":["ID","Condition","Can it fire on the founder?"],"rows":[["§13 row 1","under 4 of 10 want review state","No — fires on the market"],["§13 row 7","patched corpus still refusing >10 of 7,969 by day 24","No — fires on the engine"],["§8 Exhibit 6","plugin under 200 installs in 14 days","No — and the plugin is cut (PL8)"],["KS5","docs:src file-changes >3:1 for two weeks → freeze writing 14 days","Yes — reading 396:0 today"],["KS6","logged product hours under 300 of 430 budgeted → drop client work or drop the product","Yes"],["KS7","a client month demands >60 client hours → the product month is cancelled in writing","Yes"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Keep §13's conditions and treat the record's seven as superseded","what":"The plan's four market conditions stand alone and the record's switches lapse.","gains":["Simplest, and no new bookkeeping","No risk of a freeze at a bad moment"],"costs":["Nothing can fire on the founder","One condition is attached to a channel that no longer exists"],"system":"None.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Adopt KS5, KS6 and KS7 alongside §13's four, KS5's clock from a named Monday","what":"Three capacity switches join the plan, and KS5's two-week clock starts once the week-0 pages are written.","gains":["The only conditions that can fire on the person doing the work","KS5 is checkable with two commands"],"costs":["A fourteen-day writing freeze at a moment nobody chooses","The start date must be named or it will drift"],"system":"None; a weekly check.","screens":"None.","money":"KS7 cancels a product month when client hours pass sixty."},{"k":"c","label":"Adopt the whole KS1 to KS7 set with new dates","what":"All seven switches return, including the paid and distribution gates.","gains":["A complete set with dates and actions","Forces the commercial gates back into the quarter"],"costs":["KS1 assumes a priced test PL7 has not chosen","Every date needs re-deriving against PL2"],"system":"None.","screens":"None.","money":"Ties the plan to a paid gate."},{"k":"d","label":"Keep §13's four and replace the cut plugin line with a live channel condition","what":"Only the dead plugin row is replaced, with a condition on a channel that exists.","gains":["Fixes the one row attached to nothing","A minimal edit"],"costs":["Still nothing measures the founder against the plan","Leaves the capacity failure mode unwatched"],"system":"None.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["§13's conditions all fire on the market; the three capacity switches are the only ones that fire on the founder.","KS5 is checkable with two commands and no judgment, and it is reading its most extreme possible value.","Starting the clock after the week-0 pages avoids freezing the work PL5 and the byte path depend on.","The record's own note says KS5 matters most and will be rationalised away (`docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:14299`)."],"flip":"If the founders decide the two-week tests are themselves the work, KS5's window must exclude that fortnight in writing, with an end date.","linked":["PL2","PL3"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:204","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:321","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:327","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:328","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:329","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:14295","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:14296","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:14297","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:14299","docs/CRITIQUE.md:793"]},{"id":"PL12","cat":"Plan, scope & sequencing","sub":"First run","weight":"high","q":"MVP-0 says there is no sign-up. The app shows a login screen before it shows a file. Which one changes?","lede":"The only non-engine work this repo owns is the thing MVP-0 says must not exist.","visual":{"kind":"flow","nodes":[{"label":"User opens frontmatter","note":"no actor, no file yet","tone":"neutral"},{"label":"LoginScreen","note":"layout.tsx:12, before any file","tone":"stop","edge":"today"},{"label":"Open a local folder","note":"needs no identity at all","tone":"accent","edge":"proposed"},{"label":"Drag files in","note":"read-only session","tone":"accent"},{"label":"Connect a GitHub repo","note":"needs the user's token","tone":"warn"},{"label":"Sign in","note":"only on the repo path","tone":"warn"}],"perRow":3,"note":"Paths from Exhibit 2; the login gate from the shipped code.","caption":"What each first-run path physically needs."},"stakes":"Removing the gate deletes shipped work; keeping it breaks the thirty-second first run the retention argument rests on.","state":["Exhibit 6 lists sign-up in MVP-0's Absent row (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:205`).","§17 makes the first session open a folder and edit in thirty seconds, no account (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:429`).","The vault layout returns a login screen whenever there is no signed-in actor (`src/app/(vault)/layout.tsx:12`).","`firestore.rules` is 419 committed lines with `allow delete: if false` and 900,000-byte note bodies (`firestore.rules:221`)."],"path":["The Firebase auth stack predates the no-account position.","It is five of the seven non-engine files this repo owns that the sibling does not.","Decision 7 asks whether that design ships at all, and it is unbuilt today (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:365`)."],"tension":["A local folder needs no identity; a GitHub repo needs a token. The gate matches neither.","Zero Firestore document writes exist across 226 source files, so the design is paper today.","Round 2 found three committed files contradicting each other on whether we hold documents (`docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:142`).","No operating rule can be written until one of the three is deleted."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"Verified in the code, 2026-09-08","items":[["Vault layout without an actor","returns <LoginScreen />","src/app/(vault)/layout.tsx:12-13"],["Non-engine files unique to this repo","7","5 are the Firebase auth stack"],["firestore.rules","419 lines, committed","note bodies bounded at 900,000 bytes"],["Revision history in those rules","allow delete: if false","append-only, with public content snapshots"],["Firestore document writes across 226 source files","0","the only Firestore code is an unused accessor"],["What Exhibit 6 says MVP-0 has","no sign-up","and §17 says no account"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Remove the gate for MVP-0 and keep the auth code behind a flag","what":"The login screen stops being the first thing anyone sees, and the code stays in the tree.","gains":["Restores the thirty-second first run","Nothing is deleted"],"costs":["Shelves the only non-engine work this repo owns","Leaves decision 7 answered on paper only"],"system":"A flag around the vault layout.","screens":"The S0 launcher becomes the first screen.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Keep sign-in and change §8 and §17 to admit an account is required","what":"The plan matches the code and the free tier begins with an account.","gains":["Honest about what ships today","No code to change"],"costs":["Loses the no-account first run retention depends on","Asking before value is the category's known failure"],"system":"None.","screens":"LoginScreen stays first.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Optional: local folder and drag-in with no account; a repo requires one","what":"Identity is asked for only on the path that physically needs a token.","gains":["Matches what each path actually needs","Preserves the thirty-second first run"],"costs":["Two first-run paths to design, test and document","The auth stack stays half-used until decision 7"],"system":"The vault layout branches on the storage adapter, not on the actor.","screens":"S0 gains a no-account path; sign-in moves into the repo connect flow.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Defer until decision 7 says whether the Firebase design ships","what":"Nothing changes until the document-holding question is answered.","gains":["Avoids deleting work that may be needed","One decision instead of two"],"costs":["MVP-0's first screen stays undecided as the pilot nears","Every legal rule waits on it too"],"system":"None.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"c","recCase":["It is the only answer that matches physics rather than preference.","It preserves the first run §17's whole retention argument rests on (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:429`).","It deletes no auth work, which decision 7 may still want.","It can be built without waiting for decision 7, because it branches on storage rather than identity."],"flip":"If decision 7 removes Firebase entirely, option a is right and the login screen goes with it.","linked":["L1"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:205","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:365","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:429","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:142","src/app/(vault)/layout.tsx:12","firestore.rules:221","firestore.rules:318","firestore.rules:361"]},{"id":"PL17","cat":"Plan, scope & sequencing","sub":"Ninety days","weight":"high","q":"Does the quarter end with ten strangers using a pilot, or with a launch on a bar written in advance?","lede":"As written the quarter produces no distribution and no revenue event, and its one channel needs permission nobody has asked for.","visual":{"kind":"timeline","items":[{"when":"2026-08-12","label":"Zed Delta launch: 679 HN points","note":"the visible bar in this category now","tone":"stop"},{"when":"Week 2","label":"superpowers README line","note":"outbound; maintainer not approached","tone":"warn"},{"when":"Weeks 10–12","label":"Polish; ten strangers","note":"the quarter's only outcome","tone":"neutral"},{"when":"After the exit","label":"Show HN, one shot","note":"outside the quarter, per §12","tone":"warn"},{"when":"Record's week 12","label":"Gate 3: 30 paid, or 50 for two","note":"the ending the plan dropped","tone":"accent"}],"note":"HN points from the research briefing, opened; weeks from Exhibit 19 and the record.","caption":"What the quarter ends with, against what it used to."},"stakes":"Ninety days can end with the only thing it can be wrong about being whether ten people liked something.","state":["Exhibit 19 ends at weeks 10–12, polish and ten strangers (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:357`).","§12 puts Show HN at MVP-0 exit, one shot, after six of ten (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:309`).","The one scheduled channel is a README line in superpowers, week 2 (`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:305`).","No approach has been made and the answer may be no (`docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:58`)."],"path":["An earlier ninety-day plan ended with a launch across five surfaces in week 10 (`docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:14217`).","Gate 3 was thirty paid purchases for one founder, or fifty for two (`docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:14226`).","Round 2 cut the Chrome extension and the Obsidian plugin, leaving one channel (`docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:134`)."],"tension":["Show HN is one shot by the plan's own reckoning, and a pilot-grade build is a poor thing to spend it on.","A launch bar chosen after the pilot result is a bar chosen under relief.","Zed Delta cleared 679 HN points on launch, so the floor should be written against something real.","The quarter has no revenue event, so PL7's priced arm is the only commercial evidence available inside it."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"Two ninety-day endings","cols":["Week","Current plan (Exhibit 19)","Record's 90-day plan"],"rows":[["1–2","four tests, build nothing","landing pages, checkout wired, ten stranger sessions, rename probe"],["3","go or no-go","GATE 1: 12 paid pre-orders on 1,200 visitors, or stop"],["8–9","revert, panel, answer in place, scan, engine wired","GATE 2: plugin live and 25 installs in 14 days; first non-founder paid purchase"],["10–12","polish; ten strangers; 6 of 10 by the week-0 measure","launch across five surfaces; GATE 3 at 30 paid (one founder) or 50 (two)"],["End state","a pilot result","a launch, a price, and a number"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"What the quarter currently commits to","items":[["Distribution events scheduled","1","superpowers README line, week 2"],["Maintainer approached about it","no","gap register D6"],["Channels cut in round 2","2","Obsidian plugin, Chrome extension"],["Revenue events scheduled","0","§14 Exhibit 19"],["Show HN, per §12","after the exit test","one shot, outside the quarter"],["Monthly nut","about ₹1.09L","covered by 54–78 consulting hours, §11"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"End at the pilot as written; launch is a separate quarter","what":"The quarter tests whether the product works, and nothing else.","gains":["Focused, and it matches the build capacity","No channel spent on an unfinished build"],"costs":["No distribution evidence in ninety days","The one channel still depends on an unasked permission"],"system":"None.","screens":"None.","money":"No revenue this quarter."},{"k":"b","label":"Add a week 13: Show HN and one community post, with a stated floor","what":"The quarter ends with a public number instead of a private one.","gains":["Puts a distribution number inside the quarter","Forces a floor to be written in advance"],"costs":["Spends a one-shot channel on a pilot-grade build","Adds a week to a schedule PL2 says cannot hold"],"system":"None.","screens":"A public landing page.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Add a payment event: the first paid team seat inside the ninety days","what":"The quarter cannot end without money changing hands.","gains":["The strongest possible ending","Forces the commercial question early"],"costs":["Billing, terms and a merchant path are outside MVP-0","Largely redundant if PL7 puts a priced arm in week 2"],"system":"Billing and entitlements, none of it in MVP-0's scope.","screens":"Checkout and account screens.","money":"Merchant fees and a compliance surface."},{"k":"d","label":"End at the pilot; pre-register the launch date and floor, and ask the maintainer","what":"The ending stays the pilot, and the launch bar is written before anyone knows the result.","gains":["Costs nothing and removes a bar chosen under relief","Turns one uncertain channel into an answered question"],"costs":["No revenue evidence this quarter","A pre-registered date can still slip with the schedule"],"system":"None.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"d","recCase":["Show HN is one shot, and a bar written after the result is not a bar.","Asking the maintainer this week is the difference between one scheduled channel and none (`docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:58`).","Writing the date and the floor costs nothing and can be done in the same edit as the plan.","Zed Delta's 679 points give the floor something real to be written against."],"flip":"If PL7 puts a priced arm in weeks 1–2, the quarter already carries commercial evidence and option c stops being necessary.","linked":["PL7"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:292","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:305","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:309","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:357","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:14208","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:14217","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:14219","docs/FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md:14226","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:58","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:134"]},{"id":"R1","cat":"Research & evidence","sub":"Programme","weight":"critical","q":"Do we stop the research rounds now and spend the next two weeks on people, or run a third round on the eleven open items first?","lede":"Every round has changed the headline and none has produced a user; a third costs the two weeks the human tests need.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":30,"cols":[{"title":"Two desk rounds, done","tone":"sunk"},{"title":"Weeks 1-2 tests, unstarted","tone":"accent"}],"rows":[{"label":"Findings","cells":["280 before 2026-09-08, plus 152 in round 2","None yet"]},{"label":"People asked anything","cells":["0","40 scheduled"]},{"label":"Effect on the headline","cells":["Four changes in two days","One go/no-go at week 3"]},{"label":"Source code touched","cells":["0 of 16 commits since 2026-08-31","None planned; build nothing"]},{"label":"Cost of one more","cells":["Two weeks, on the observed rate","Two weeks, and the first human contact"]}],"note":"Round 2 ran 23 agents over 11 gaps and sent the headline itself back to hypothesis.","caption":"What another desk round buys, against what the tests buy."},"stakes":"Another round moves the pitch again and the week-3 go/no-go is still decided by nobody who has used the thing.","state":["GAPS §G orders twelve items and says seven need no founder (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:112). Round 2 left eleven open (:146).","The week-0 row schedules token rotation, the buyer, the web byte path, the exit measure and the founder test notes, and none of the eleven (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:351).","`src/` was last touched on 2026-08-10. Of the sixteen commits dated after 2026-08-31, zero touch it."],"path":["280 findings before 2026-09-08 across two adversarial rounds; round 2 added 152, of which 75 confirmed, 60 revised, 16 refuted (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:13, :116).","The direction moved four times in two days on that evidence, and round 2 sent review state itself back to hypothesis (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:22).","Engineering days were assigned by inspection with no velocity data, which round 2 also corrected (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:22, :130)."],"tension":["Two of the eleven gate the build rather than the pitch: whether an anchor survives a foreign write (R2), and whether the forks honour the model APIs (R14).","The other nine change nothing about whether ten developers want this. Three are founder asks and proceed in parallel either way.","Stopping the rounds is not stopping the watch. Three of four claims moved in nine weeks: Antigravity 2026-08-24, Notion 2026-08-28, Claude Code v2.1.260 on 2026-09-03. The plan already says re-check monthly (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:560)."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"The research programme, measured 2026-09-09","items":[["Agent reports under docs/research/agent-reports-*","214","699,018 words; find + wc, re-measured 2026-09-09"],["User interviews across the whole programme","0","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:35"],["Findings before 2026-09-08, two adversarial rounds","280","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:13"],["Findings, round 2 (2026-09-08)","152","75 confirmed / 60 revised / 16 refuted, GAPS:116"],["Last commit touching src/","2026-08-10","git log -1 -- src/ — thirty days ago"],["Commits dated after 2026-08-31 touching src/","0 of 16","git log; 13 docs, 1 prototype, 1 deploy config, 1 decisions site"],["Measured engineering days per calendar week","1.21, and 0.23 over the last 30 days","the withdrawn schedule needed 7.0 — PRODUCT-BRIEF:11, :227"]]},{"type":"bars","title":"Words of tracked markdown per line of source","note":"Tracked .md excluding the pinned test corpus, summed per commit. The denominator, 25,407 lines of .ts/.tsx across 226 files, was verified identical at all three commits. The plan's own published series (87 at DECIDE:217, 92.2 at CRITIQUE:135) counts a wider file set that could not be reproduced here — the direction is the same, the absolute is not, so these are the reproducible figures.","data":[["2026-08-31, DECIDE commit 8fd0bf9",80.9],["2026-08-31, CRITIQUE commit a8ac822",84.8],["2026-09-08, HEAD f495376",85.7]],"unit":"words per line"}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Stop the rounds. Run the weeks 1-2 tests next","what":"The eleven open items stay open through the week-3 go/no-go and no further desk round runs.","gains":["First human contact in week 1 rather than week 5","Ends a programme that has never stopped early"],"costs":["A fatal anchor result lands after the tests, not before","The competitive watch stops with the rounds unless named separately"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"One bounded round 3 on the founder-independent items, capped at two days","what":"Two more days of desk research on the seven items that need no founder, then the tests regardless.","gains":["Closes the cheap items with a stated end date","Tests still start on day three"],"costs":["The cap has to be enforced against a programme that has never stopped early","Two days of the two weeks"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Run round 3 unbounded, as rounds 1 and 2 were","what":"A third adversarial round of the same shape, ending when it ends.","gains":["The rounds have caught real errors every time, including today's","Nothing is committed on an unattacked claim"],"costs":["On the observed rate, another 150-plus findings and another headline change","First human contact still unscheduled"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Split: two code experiments in week 0, the other nine accepted as risk","what":"R2 and R14 run in week 0; the remaining nine are signed off as open risk by a named person.","gains":["Cheapest. Both experiments are one person, one day","The tests and the gating evidence arrive together"],"costs":["Requires somebody to sign nine open risks, which nobody has done","The signature is meaningless if it is not written down"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"d","recCase":["Two of the eleven gate the build: the anchor test (R2) and the fork API test (R14). Both are one person for a day and both change a number the meeting is about to use.","The other nine change nothing about whether ten developers want this, and three of them are founder asks that run in parallel anyway.","The watch is separate from the rounds. Keep the monthly competitive re-check the plan already names (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:560); it is what caught Notion, Antigravity and Claude Code inside nine weeks."],"flip":"If the meeting picks the VS Code extension, R14 stops being optional and the split becomes three gating experiments and eight accepted risks.","linked":["R14"],"sources":["docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:13","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:22","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:35","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:112","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:116","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:130","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:146","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:11","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:22","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:227","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:351","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:560","docs/CRITIQUE.md:135","docs/DECIDE.md:217","https://www.notion.com/releases","https://antigravity.google/blog/vcs-and-terminal","https://raw.githubusercontent.com/anthropics/claude-code/main/CHANGELOG.md"]},{"id":"R7","cat":"Research & evidence","sub":"Corpus","weight":"critical","q":"Do we pin a second corpus of agent-written repositories before the engine fixes, or keep the seven Obsidian vaults?","lede":"Every engine number in the plan is measured on note-takers, and the pitch is now documents an agent wrote into a repository.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":28,"cols":[{"title":"Seven Obsidian vaults, pinned","tone":"sunk"},{"title":"Agent-written repos, unpinned","tone":"accent"}],"rows":[{"label":"Files","cells":["8,513, pinned 2026-08-29","None pinned"]},{"label":"Concentration","cells":["One wiki is 77.4% of the files","Unknown"]},{"label":"Files named spec.md","cells":["0","The population the pitch names"]},{"label":"AGENTS.md or CLAUDE.md","cells":["2 of 8,513","Unknown"]},{"label":"What it sizes","cells":["83% refusal, NF-1's four days","Nothing yet"]},{"label":"What it proves","cells":["Byte-exactness on real files","Nothing yet"]}],"note":"The weeks 3-4 row already names one spec-kit and one superpowers repo.","caption":"The corpus the engine is measured on, against the one in the pitch."},"stakes":"NF-1 is sized at four days against a refusal rate that describes one wiki, not the repositories in the pitch.","state":["`test/corpus/foreign/SOURCES.json` pins seven Obsidian vaults, 8,513 files, 19,047,891 bytes, pinned 2026-08-29.","The plan states the caveat and does not act on it: the refusal rate is a property of those vaults (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:514).","In the vendored corpus: zero files named `spec.md`, zero `specs` directories, two agent-instruction files in 8,513, both in one vault (measured 2026-09-09)."],"path":["The corpus was pinned when byte-exactness for note-takers was the product. Four direction changes later it has not moved.","The weeks 3-4 row already names one spec-kit and one superpowers repo (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:354), so the clone is scheduled anyway."],"tension":["One vault is 77.4% of the file count and two are 88.7%, so the 83% refusal figure mostly describes that wiki (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:214).","The population exists and is catalogued: AIDev records 932,791 agent-authored pull requests across 116,211 repositories (arXiv 2602.09185).","Discarding the vaults loses byte-exactness proven on 8,513 real files, which is the strongest verified asset in the project."],"evidence":[{"type":"bars","title":"Share of the 8,513-file corpus, from SOURCES.json","note":"Computed from md_files per vault; the seven sum exactly to 8,513, verified 2026-09-09","data":[["community-archive/obsidian-hub",77.4],["oldwinter/knowledge-garden",11.3],["quanru/obsidian-example-lifeos",6.3],["s-blu/dataview-example-vault",3.1],["kepano/kepano-obsidian",1.2],["erazlogo/obsidian-history-vault",0.5],["CyanVoxel/Obsidian-Vault-Template",0.2]],"unit":"% of corpus files"},{"type":"stat","title":"What the corpus does not contain","items":[["Files named spec.md","0","find over test/corpus/foreign/_vendor, 2026-09-09"],["Directories named specs","0","same"],["AGENTS.md or CLAUDE.md files","2 of 8,513","both in oldwinter/knowledge-garden"],["Repositories that are Obsidian vaults","7 of 7","SOURCES.json"],["Engine claims measured on it","refusal rate, byte-exactness, NF-1..4","PRODUCT-BRIEF:514"],["Days budgeted for NF-1, sized on its refusal rate","4","83% of real vaults refused — PRODUCT-BRIEF:214"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Pin a second corpus of agent-written repos before the engine fixes","what":"Clone and pin spec-kit, superpowers and similar repositories now, and size NF-1 against them as well.","gains":["Sizes the fixes against the population the pitch names","Every refusal figure gains its denominator"],"costs":["Delays the fixes by however long clone-and-pin takes","Two corpora to keep pinned and re-run"],"system":"A second SOURCES.json and a second gate run in CI.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Replace the vault corpus with the agent corpus","what":"The seven vaults go and the agent repositories become the only regression gate.","gains":["One corpus to maintain, matching the pitch","No stale refusal figures left to quote"],"costs":["Throws away byte-exactness proven on 8,513 real files","Loses the standing regression gate the engine already passes"],"system":"The existing gate is repointed; historical comparisons break.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Keep the vaults as the gate; add the agent corpus at weeks 3-4","what":"The clone happens on the row that already schedules it, and until then every refusal number is written as a vault number.","gains":["Costs nothing extra; the weeks 3-4 row names those repos already","Keeps the byte-exactness proof intact"],"costs":["Refusal figures stay vault-derived through the go/no-go","NF-1's four days remain sized on the wrong population"],"system":"One extra pinned source at weeks 3-4.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Keep as is; markdown is markdown","what":"The seven vaults remain the only corpus and the engine numbers keep their current basis.","gains":["No work","The gate is already green and understood"],"costs":["Every fidelity and refusal number describes a population the pitch does not address","The caveat at :514 stays true and unacted on"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"c","recCase":["The vault corpus is a good regression gate, and discarding it loses the one thing the engine can prove.","The weeks 3-4 row already names one spec-kit and one superpowers repo, so pinning them costs the same clone as the anchor test in R2.","Until then, write every refusal figure as a vault figure. The 83% is a property of seven vaults and mostly of one wiki."],"flip":"If the four-day NF-1 estimate is being defended with the 83% figure, the second corpus has to come first, because the fix may be sized against the wrong files.","linked":["E18"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:214","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:354","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:514","test/corpus/foreign/SOURCES.json","https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.09185"]},{"id":"R5","cat":"Research & evidence","sub":"Method","weight":"high","q":"Does the plan restore the evidence tags, or keep the three-word labels?","lede":"The document people actually read is the one with no way to tell a fetched number from a recalled one.","visual":{"kind":"ba","before":{"title":"The plan today","lines":[{"t":"83% of real vaults refused","mark":"unmarked"},{"t":"About 1,500 live markers","mark":"unmarked"},{"t":"at exactly our intended tier","mark":"unmarked"},{"t":"1.21 engineering days per week","mark":"unmarked"}]},"after":{"title":"Weak classes marked only","lines":[{"t":"83% of real vaults refused","mark":"silent = opened"},{"t":"About 1,500 live markers","mark":"silent = opened"},{"t":"at exactly our intended tier [SS]","mark":"marked"},{"t":"1.21 engineering days per week","mark":"silent = opened"}]},"via":"mark weak","note":"Silence has to be defined once at the top, or a bare number means nothing.","caption":"Tag where the errors are, not everywhere, so the marks stay visible."},"stakes":"An untagged number in the plan gets quoted as fact, which is how 62,976 was published the first time.","state":["The plan labels features public evidence, founder user test or untested (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:4, :186).","It carries zero instances of `[fetched]`, `[measured]`, `[derived]`, `[inference]` or `[SS]`, counted with grep -o on 2026-09-09.","The record carries 2,741 of them, and `docs/PRODUCT.md:1299` makes them mandatory on every claim."],"path":["The tag that mattered was `[SS]`, search-summary, which may never be published as fact (docs/PRODUCT.md:1299).","v15 was written fresh as a founder-facing document and the tags did not come with it."],"tension":["The error pattern is not random: where the source was a number quoted in prose, the record was wrong about half the time (docs/VERIFICATION.md:165).","Thirteen of twenty-one headline claims needed an edit before publication (docs/VERIFICATION.md:26).","Today's briefing ran on two marks, opened and inferred. The figure carrying neither, the 18% unreviewed claim, is the one nobody can source."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"Evidence tags, counted with grep -o on 2026-09-09","cols":["Tag","FRONTMATTER-RECORD.md","PRODUCT-BRIEF.md (v15)"],"rows":[["[fetched] — primary source opened","1,097","0"],["[measured] — executed here","863","0"],["[derived] — arithmetic shown","369","0"],["[inference] — reasoning","247","0"],["[SS] — may never be published as fact","165","0"],["Total","2,741","0"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"What the verification pass found the tags were catching","items":[["Load-bearing claims sent to six verification agents","21","VERIFICATION.md:17"],["Verifiable sub-claims they decomposed into","34","VERIFICATION.md:17"],["CONFIRMED","13 (38.2%)","VERIFICATION.md:21"],["REVISED","13 (38.2%)","directionally right, numerically or scopally wrong, :22"],["REFUTED","5 (14.7%)","false, must be deleted, :23"],["UNVERIFIABLE","3 (8.8%)","no openable source exists, :24"],["Headline claims needing an edit before publication","13 of 21","VERIFICATION.md:26"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Restore all five tags in the plan","what":"Every claim in the founder document carries its source class, as the record does.","gains":["Maximum discipline; no number is ever bare","One rule, no judgement call about which class is weak"],"costs":["A fifty-page document dense enough that readers stop seeing the tags","Retro-fitting 27 exhibits is a rewrite"],"system":"No change; a writing rule.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Restore [SS] and [inference] only — mark the weak, leave the strong bare","what":"Two marks in the plan, and a legend line saying an unmarked number was opened or measured.","gains":["Puts the mark where the verification pass found the errors","Costs one legend line and stays readable"],"costs":["Silence carries meaning, so the legend must be stated or it means nothing","A missed mark reads as a strong claim"],"system":"No change; a writing rule plus one line of front matter.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Keep the labels and add a source column to every exhibit","what":"Each exhibit grows a column naming where each row came from and when it was read.","gains":["More readable than inline tags","Puts the source beside the number, where it gets quoted from"],"costs":["A source column on twenty-seven exhibits is a rewrite","Wide tables break in the PDF"],"system":"The exhibit renderer takes another column.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Keep as is; the plan is a summary and the record carries the tags","what":"Nothing changes; anyone checking a number opens the record.","gains":["Free","The record is genuinely complete"],"costs":["Anyone quoting the plan quotes untagged numbers","Nobody opens a 325-page record to check a number they believe"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["Tagging every number makes the plan unreadable, and readers stop seeing marks that are everywhere.","Tagging the two weak classes puts the mark where the error rate actually is: prose-quoted numbers and reasoning (docs/VERIFICATION.md:165).","It costs one legend line, and today's briefing is the working demonstration — two marks, and the unmarked figure is the one that fell over."],"flip":"If the plan starts going outside the company, restore all five, because an external reader has no record to fall back on.","linked":["R18","R6"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:4","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:186","docs/PRODUCT.md:1299","docs/VERIFICATION.md:17","docs/VERIFICATION.md:21","docs/VERIFICATION.md:26","docs/VERIFICATION.md:165"]},{"id":"R6","cat":"Research & evidence","sub":"Method","weight":"high","q":"Do we gate the plan on a checker built from a withdrawals ledger, or keep correcting it by hand?","lede":"Round 2 applied twenty-two changes and left five decisions stated both ways inside the same file.","visual":{"kind":"flow","perRow":3,"nodes":[{"label":"Number published","note":"62,976, in a commit title","tone":"neutral"},{"label":"Corrected in one paragraph","note":"Now about 1,400 live markers","tone":"neutral"},{"label":"Old PDFs stay on disk","note":"v10 to v14, all under docs/","tone":"warn"},{"label":"Quoted again","note":"Nothing checks the rest of the file","tone":"stop"},{"label":"Ledger row written","note":"Exhibit 4 already does this for two","tone":"accent","edge":"instead"},{"label":"Grep gate on the PDF build","note":"Fails at the moment the plan leaves","tone":"good"}],"note":"The ledger is the input list the checker consumes; neither works alone.","caption":"How a withdrawn number comes back, and where to stop it."},"stakes":"The retention section still sells a channel that was cut, in a document going to a founder meeting.","state":["Exhibit 4 is a ten-row table of retired terms (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:165). It carries two of the six withdrawn numbers, at :176 and :178.","`docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md` is named by no npm script and checked by nothing; grep for it across `docs/build/` returns zero files.","The Obsidian plugin is struck at :304 and still live at :204, :352, :428 and :477. The marker count is about 1,400 at :58 and about 1,500 at :178."],"path":["v15 applied 22 plan changes from round 2 (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:118), each at the place the reviewer happened to be looking.","Exhibit 4 was built for retired vocabulary, so numbers withdrawn mid-rewrite went into prose instead (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:229, :292, :310)."],"tension":["Commit `94edca6` is titled in part \"62,976 public spec files carry an unanswered marker\", and every plan PDF from v10 to v14 is still on disk under `docs/`.","MAP.md routes any number to the record's §57 and notes twenty went stale (docs/MAP.md:108). Nobody opens a 325-page record to check a number they believe.","A hand re-read after every round is what produced these five contradictions."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"Numbers this programme published and then withdrew","cols":["As published","Where it went out","What it is now","In exhibit 4?"],"rows":[["62,976 public spec files with an unanswered marker","commit 94edca6 title, plan v10.1, 2026-09-06","3,368 files carry the marker; 42% of a read-every-hit sample of 50 were live, ≈1,400 (PRODUCT-BRIEF:58)","Yes, at :178 — but it says about 1,500"],["\"496,000 stars\" as channel size","earlier plans","replaced by active-repo counts; stars measure attention to a CLI (:176)","Yes, at :176"],["1.5M browser readers","earlier channel sizing","about 647,000; the figure summed a 500,000-user reader with a 1,000,000-user clipper (:310)","No"],["114 seats at $8 covers the nut","earlier pricing","withdrawn; the feature is GitHub's at $4 (:292)","No"],["Ten weeks to MVP-0","v14 schedule","withdrawn as arithmetically impossible; 70 engineering days is 37 weeks at the best rate ever observed, 58 at the measured one (:227, :229)","No"],["The 2.5x optimistic correction","the audits","withdrawn; the 41-day figure already had 25% active-day density baked in (:229)","No"]]},{"type":"table","title":"Round-2 decisions that survive in both states, same file","cols":["What round 2 decided","Struck at","Old position still stands at"],"rows":[["Obsidian plugin CUT","exhibit 17, line 304","§8 channels row :204; flowchart stop-branch :338; weeks 1-2 \"plugin shipped\" :352; retention lever :428; family diagram :464; exhibit 26 :477; §21 modes row :524"],["Chrome extension CUT","exhibit 17, line 310","§8 surfaces row :203; family diagram :464; exhibit 26 :477"],["Diff-review issue at 266 reactions, re-checked 2026-09-08","§1 :23 and F2 :56","262 reactions at :150, :322, :383"],["Web app indexes per open file, not server full-text","WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:50","\"move to server full-text search in the web app\" at :233"],["Live markers ≈1,400","F4 :58","\"About 1,500 live markers\" at :178"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"A withdrawals ledger, and a grep gate that fails the PDF build","what":"Exhibit 4 grows the four missing rows and becomes the list a checker greps the plan against before it renders.","gains":["Half a day; it fails at the moment the plan leaves the building","Six withdrawals in three days is the best evidence the process is honest"],"costs":["The list has to be maintained after every round","A gate that fires falsely trains you to skip it"],"system":"A script beside `build-plan-pdf.mjs`, and one npm run.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Extend the ledger; keep correcting by hand","what":"The four missing withdrawals are added to exhibit 4 and the plan is re-read after each round.","gains":["Free today, and minutes of work","The withdrawal count becomes visible, which is uncomfortable and correct"],"costs":["A hand re-read is what produced the five live contradictions","Nothing catches the sixth"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Inline [withdrawn] markers wherever an old number might still be quoted","what":"The mark travels with the number rather than living in a table.","gains":["Catches the number at the point of use","No build step to maintain"],"costs":["Scatters the record and leaves no index to check against","Cannot mark a number inside a PDF already shipped"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Generate the plan from the record, as the Tier-1 docs are generated","what":"One correction in the record propagates into every document that quotes it.","gains":["Correct in principle; the repo already has the build tree","Removes the whole class rather than catching instances"],"costs":["A rewrite of the build tree for a document that changes shape every two days","The plan's structure is not the record's"],"system":"The plan joins the generated docs pipeline.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["The repo already has the precedent: `npm run record` exists to prove the assembled record carries every tree file line for line. A retired-terms check is the same idea one size down.","The ledger is the checker's input, so building either alone wastes the other. Four rows and half a day covers both.","Fix the 1,400-against-1,500 disagreement in the same pass, and delete or re-file the superseded plan PDFs so the plan is the only quotable copy."],"flip":"If the plan is rewritten from scratch once more, do option d and stop hand-maintaining it.","linked":["R18","R5"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:58","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:165","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:176","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:178","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:203","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:204","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:227","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:229","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:233","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:292","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:304","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:310","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:352","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:428","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:477","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:118","docs/WEEK0-DECISIONS-2026-09-08.md:50","docs/MAP.md:108","merged: R9"]},{"id":"R14","cat":"Research & evidence","sub":"Form factor evidence","weight":"high","q":"Do we test whether Cursor and the other forks honour the model APIs before the form-factor decision?","lede":"Two of the savings that make the extension route attractive are proven on VS Code itself and nowhere else.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":26,"cols":[{"title":"VS Code","tone":"good"},{"title":"Cursor and other forks","tone":"warn"}],"rows":[{"label":"Byte-exact write","cells":["94/94 and 156/156, two harnesses","Untested"]},{"label":"Language-model API","cells":["Supplied by the host","Unknown"]},{"label":"Population in the plan","cells":["78.06M Copilot Chat, 24.89M Claude Code","No install count anywhere"]},{"label":"If the API holds","cells":["Fix #6 (3d) and F8's key UI deleted","Same saving, wider base"]},{"label":"If it does not","cells":["No effect","The key UI comes back for that share"]}],"note":"Live mode is standalone-only either way: there is no view-zone API.","caption":"The extension route's savings, and the host they were measured on."},"stakes":"The meeting decides the form factor on a saving that may apply to part of the population, and reversing it later costs the build sequence.","state":["Decision 6 records that an extension can write byte-exactly: 94/94 and 156/156 bytes on VS Code 1.135.0. The host supplies the model picker and MCP registration free (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:364).","Whether the forks honour those APIs is on the still-open list (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:146).","The plan carries no install count for Cursor or any fork; its five Cursor mentions are Reddit points, a price band, a Show HN score, a risk row and an exhibit-21 finding."],"path":["The harnesses ran against VS Code because round 2's question was whether byte-exact writing was possible at all (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:125).","No fork was installed and no fork was tested."],"tension":["Fix #6 is bring-your-own key at three days (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:219) and F8 carries the key UI. Both are deleted only where the host provides a model picker.","The size of the affected group is unmeasured, which is itself the finding: the plan quotes VS Code populations and none for the forks (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:48).","The host is moving in this direction anyway. VS Code merged a review/unreview operation on 2026-07-03 and a markdown feedback editor at milestone 1.130.0, both gated in an experimental window and undocumented."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"What is proven and what is assumed about the extension route","items":[["Byte-exact writes proven on","VS Code 1.135.0","94/94 and 156/156 bytes, two harnesses, PRODUCT-BRIEF:364"],["Forks tested","0","GAPS:146"],["Install count for Cursor or any fork, anywhere in the plan","none","grep: 5 Cursor mentions at :149, :157, :309, :326, :381 — none an install count"],["VS Code population measured","78.06M Copilot Chat, 24.89M Claude Code extension, 14.45M markdown-all-in-one","GAPS:48"],["Days deleted if the model API holds","3 (fix #6) plus F8's key UI","PRODUCT-BRIEF:219, :364"],["Live mode in an extension","not possible — no view-zone API","PRODUCT-BRIEF:364"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Test before the meeting: a stub extension in Cursor calling the model API","what":"One afternoon installing the forks and calling the two APIs the saving depends on.","gains":["Moves a number the form-factor decision rests on, before the decision","Count the fork population in the same sitting"],"costs":["An afternoon in a week already full of decisions","A negative result weakens the extension case just before the meeting"],"system":"A throwaway stub extension; no product code.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Decide on the VS Code numbers alone and treat the forks as upside","what":"The form factor is chosen against the population that is measured, and forks are a bonus if they work.","gains":["Defensible: VS Code is the population with real numbers","No delay"],"costs":["The saving quoted in decision 6 applies to a smaller base than the argument implies","The gap is discovered during the build"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Build the key UI regardless, so the extension works everywhere","what":"Fix #6 stays in the plan and the host's model picker becomes a nicety rather than a dependency.","gains":["Removes the dependency entirely","One code path across every host"],"costs":["Costs the three days back","The extension case gets weaker by exactly that much"],"system":"Fix #6 and F8's key UI stay in the sequence.","screens":"S11 keeps the key field.","money":"Three engineering days."},{"k":"d","label":"Defer the form factor until the two-week tests say which shell people want","what":"Ten developers are shown either mock and the decision waits for their answer.","gains":["Decides on demand rather than on savings","Both mocks already exist"],"costs":["Delays a decision that gates the whole build sequence","Ten people's preference is not a population measurement"],"system":"No change until week 3.","screens":"Both mocks stay live.","money":"None."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["One afternoon changes an input to a decision the meeting is about to take, and reversing that decision afterwards costs far more.","If the forks do honour the API, decision 6 gets stronger on a measured basis instead of an assumed one.","Count the fork population in the same sitting. The plan has no number for it at all, which is why the saving cannot currently be sized."],"flip":"If the meeting chooses standalone, the question dies with the option.","linked":["FF1","R1"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:219","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:364","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:48","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:125","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:146","microsoft/vscode#324218, merged 2026-07-03; issues #326539 and #326540, milestone 1.130.0"]},{"id":"R17","cat":"Research & evidence","sub":"Evidence class","weight":"high","q":"Do the F5, F6 and F7 founder tests get their notes attached this week, or get relabelled untested?","lede":"Three features carrying eighteen engineering days in MVP-0 rest on a class of evidence that is one sentence in a chat log.","visual":{"kind":"ba","before":{"title":"Exhibit 5 today","lines":[{"t":"F5, F6, F7: founder user test, reported","mark":"class"},{"t":"Participants recorded: none","mark":"gap"},{"t":"Protocol recorded: none","mark":"gap"},{"t":"18 of about 70 MVP-0 days ride on it","mark":"cost"}]},"after":{"title":"After one document","lines":[{"t":"Who, when, what they did, what they said","mark":"attached"},{"t":"The plan's strongest exhibit","mark":"if it exists"},{"t":"Or all three relabelled untested","mark":"if not"},{"t":"18 days move behind the week-10 pilot","mark":"if not"}]},"via":"one document","note":"The risk table already describes the fallback at PRODUCT-BRIEF:325.","caption":"The strongest label in the plan, or its weakest, decided by one file."},"stakes":"Eighteen of about seventy MVP-0 days are committed on an evidence class with no artefact behind it.","state":["Exhibit 5 gives idea mode, the decision flow and the docs-scan direction a class of their own, settled by the founders' notes then the pilot (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:187).","Week 0 schedules attaching the founder test notes for F5 and F6 (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:351).","The register rates the class High severity: a founders' statement in chat, with no notes, participants or protocol attached (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:23)."],"path":["The features were validated by the founders using them, and the validation was reported in conversation (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:69).","F5 and F6 carry 8 days and F7 carries 10, out of about 70 for MVP-0 (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:227)."],"tension":["Public evidence points the other way: standalone PRD generators number 512 repos and the top has 57 stars (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:155).","`/speckit.clarify`, Kiro and Claude Code plan mode ship the same step free (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:60).","D3 notes these two features point at a buyer who does not run an agent, the opposite of the buyer decision 2 recommends starting with (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:52)."],"evidence":[{"type":"stat","title":"What the founder-test class carries","items":[["Features in the class","3 of 13","F5, F6, F7 — PRODUCT-BRIEF:187"],["Engineering days those three carry","18 of about 70","F5+F6 8d, F7 10d — PRODUCT-BRIEF:227"],["Participants recorded","none","GAPS:23"],["Protocol recorded","none","GAPS:23"],["Notes attached to the plan","none","still a week-0 task, PRODUCT-BRIEF:351"],["Public evidence pointing the other way","512 PRD-generator repos, top has 57 stars","PRODUCT-BRIEF:155, and the same figure in the F5 row at :59"],["Free tools shipping the same step","/speckit.clarify, Kiro, Claude Code plan mode","PRODUCT-BRIEF:60"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Attach the notes this week: who, when, what they did, what they said","what":"The founders write up the tests they ran, and the class either gains an artefact or collapses.","gains":["A day of writing decides eighteen engineering days","The only evidence in the programme from a person using the thing"],"costs":["The write-up may show the test was informal","Founder time in a week already carrying four decisions"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Relabel all three untested and move them into the ten-stranger pilot","what":"The class disappears and F5, F6 and F7 join the untested row.","gains":["Matches what the risk table already anticipates (:325)","No claim rests on an unattachable artefact"],"costs":["Moves 18 days of MVP-0 onto evidence that arrives at week 10","Discards a real test because it was not written down"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Keep the label and attach nothing","what":"The founders' own test of their own product stands as reported.","gains":["Free","Nobody's time is spent on a write-up"],"costs":["An evidence class with no artefact, in a document whose method is that every claim opens","The first reader who asks for it finds nothing"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Cut F5 and F6 from MVP-0 and keep F7, which needs no model","what":"Generation leaves the pilot and the docs scan stays.","gains":["Removes 8 days and the buyer contradiction in D3","F7 needs no model and no key"],"costs":["Removes the two features a real person is reported to have used and liked","Cuts on the strength of the label, not the feature"],"system":"Structured output in the LLM port is no longer on the MVP-0 path.","screens":"The idea-mode and decision-flow screens leave MVP-0.","money":"None."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["This is one document that either exists or does not, and the answer moves eighteen engineering days inside MVP-0.","If the notes exist, this is the only evidence in the programme from a person using the thing. It should be the plan's strongest exhibit, not its weakest label.","If they do not, option b follows automatically and the risk table at :325 already describes the fallback."],"flip":"Nothing. No further research substitutes for the founders answering this one.","linked":[],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:59","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:60","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:69","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:155","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:187","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:227","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:325","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:351","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:23","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:52"]},{"id":"R18","cat":"Research & evidence","sub":"Method","weight":"high","q":"Do we adopt a verbatim-only rule — nothing in quotation marks that has not been re-fetched and string-matched?","lede":"Today's research got the substance right and invented the wording: about one quotation in three was a paraphrase in quote marks.","visual":{"kind":"flow","perRow":3,"nodes":[{"label":"Finding written from a source","note":"Substance is usually right","tone":"neutral"},{"label":"Quotation marks used?","note":"The only form that cannot be checked by reading","tone":"warn"},{"label":"Re-fetch and string-match","note":"One request, in the same pass","tone":"accent"},{"label":"Exact match: keep the marks","note":"Publishable on a slide","tone":"good"},{"label":"No match: drop the marks","note":"Say it in our own words, cite the URL","tone":"neutral"},{"label":"Cannot re-open the source","note":"Not on a slide, at any confidence","tone":"stop"}],"note":"Two quotations attributed to vendor blogs today were on neither page.","caption":"The gate a quotation passes before it reaches a founder meeting."},"stakes":"One fabricated quotation read aloud in a room destroys the only thing this plan sells, which is that every claim opens.","state":["Two quotations attributed to vendor blogs are on neither page. The findings they supported survived; the wording did not.","Strings attributed to VS Code's review documentation are absent from that page, which does not document the capability at all.","The plan's method is that every claim points at something openable (docs/PRODUCT.md:1299). A quotation is the one form where a paraphrase is indistinguishable from a fact."],"path":["Nine research lenses ran on 2026-09-09 and the fabrications were caught only by opening the page and matching the string.","The record already carries source-class discipline as tags (docs/PRODUCT.md:1299). It has no rule about quotation marks specifically."],"tension":["The error is invisible at read time. A paraphrase inside quotation marks looks exactly like a quotation, and usually reads better.","Four verbatim strings survived today's check and are safe to use: \"diff panel that opens beside the conversation\", \"comments attach to snapshots\", \"Agent Edits\", \"Uncommitted\".","Numbers fail the same way. The 18% unreviewed figure has no source, and six firms size the note-taking market between $1.35B and $15.46B."],"evidence":[],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Verbatim-only: re-fetch and string-match every quotation, or the marks come off","what":"A quotation may appear only where the exact string has been matched against the live source in the same pass.","gains":["Kills the only error class a reader cannot catch","One request per quotation, and nothing else"],"costs":["Slows any pass that quotes heavily","A changed or deleted page forces the sentence to be rewritten"],"system":"A quote-check list in the plan's build, beside R6's retired-terms gate.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"b","label":"Drop quotations: state every finding in our own words with the URL beside it","what":"No quotation marks anywhere in the plan, the deck or the record's user-facing layer.","gains":["Removes the failure entirely","Nothing to re-check later"],"costs":["Loses the force of a vendor stating its own behaviour, which is exhibit 21's whole method","Paraphrase invites its own drift"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Mark each quotation with its verification class and let the reader judge","what":"Quotations carry opened, reported or unverified, as the record's tags do for numbers.","gains":["Consistent with R5's tagging decision","Keeps quotations that cannot be re-opened, honestly marked"],"costs":["An unverified quotation still gets read aloud without its mark","Pushes the judgement onto the reader"],"system":"No change; a writing rule.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Nothing; the tag discipline already covers it","what":"Source-class tags stay the only rule and quotations are treated like any other claim.","gains":["Free","The record's tags have caught real errors"],"costs":["A tag says where a claim came from, never whether the words are the source's own","Today's round shows the tags did not catch it"],"system":"No change.","screens":"None.","money":"None."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["The failure was not laziness. Every fabricated quotation today had the finding right, which is why nobody caught it by reading.","It costs one request per quotation. R6 is already building a gate over the plan, so the quote list is another array in the same script.","Write option b into the rule as the fallback: where a source cannot be re-opened, the sentence loses its quotation marks and keeps its citation."],"flip":"If a source cannot be re-fetched, because it sits behind a login or has been deleted, the rule falls back to option b for that source.","linked":["R5","R6"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT.md:1299","docs/VERIFICATION.md:165","docs/MAP.md:108","https://zed.dev/blog/agentic-xanadu","https://antigravity.google/blog/vcs-and-terminal"]},{"id":"R11","cat":"Research & evidence","sub":"Measurement","weight":"medium","q":"Do we buy the two competitor benchmarks, screens and speed, before week 3?","lede":"Ten screen queries are written and unrun; the application has four named measures and no values.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":26,"cols":[{"title":"Mobbin screen benchmark","tone":"neutral"},{"title":"Speed against Obsidian","tone":"neutral"}],"rows":[{"label":"Cost","cells":["One fresh session","Two days (GAPS:43)"]},{"label":"Already answered by","cells":["Exhibit 21, four of six groups","Nothing; the app is unmeasured"]},{"label":"Left open","cells":["Launcher, onboarding, pricing, upsell","Cold start, typing at 10,000 words"]},{"label":"Needed before","cells":["The first screen a stranger sees","Only if a headline claims speed"]},{"label":"Blocked by","cells":["The injection-taint gate; a fresh session clears it","A 41,527 ms regex on an unguarded path"]}],"note":"Neither has been run. Exhibit 21 is vendor text, which beats a screenshot of the same behaviour.","caption":"Two unbought measurements, and what each would actually settle."},"stakes":"Either the launcher and pricing page get designed with no external reference, or two days go on a marketing number nobody is claiming.","state":["§15 says the screen benchmark \"was not conducted\": every Mobbin call was refused by the session's injection-taint gate (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:375).","Exhibit 21 answers four of the six screen groups from the incumbents' own documentation (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:379, :381, :382, :383).","§9 names four measures to publish and gives a value for none; the vault ships to the client at 77 MB parsed per cold start (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:233)."],"path":["The gate blocks outbound connectors for the rest of a tainted session, so a fresh session clears it (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:39).","The engine was benchmarked in detail on 2026-08-31; the application around it never was, and nothing has been compared with a competitor (docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:43)."],"tension":["A vendor's documented behaviour beats a screenshot of it, and exhibit 21 is vendor text. What it cannot answer is the launcher and the pricing page.","The same engine benchmark found a live quadratic: 41,527.3 ms on 320 KB of `[[`, log-log slope k = 1.98, and `shapeGate` has no product call site.","None of the three headline variants mentions speed (docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:296), so the Obsidian comparison answers a question nobody is asking yet."],"evidence":[{"type":"table","title":"Measured and unmeasured, engine versus application","cols":["Thing","Value","Source"],"rows":[["shapeGate over the corpus","8,513 files in 63.5 ms = 286 MB/s, none refused","r15-e4 §70.2, executed 2026-08-31"],["OffsetMap.toByte","465 ns over 20,000 random lookups","r15-e4 §70.2"],["Wikilink regex on 320 KB of \"[[\"","41,527.3 ms, slope k = 1.98, no guard on the path","r15-e4 §70.3 — shapeGate has no call site"],["Vault parsed per cold start","77 MB","PRODUCT-BRIEF:233"],["Time to first keystroke, cold","unmeasured","named as a measure to publish, :233"],["Typing latency at 10,000 words","unmeasured",":233"],["Anything compared with Obsidian","unmeasured","GAPS:43, priced at two days"]]},{"type":"stat","title":"The screen benchmark, and what already exists without it","items":[["Mobbin queries prepared","10, across 6 screen groups","exhibit 22, PRODUCT-BRIEF:387-396"],["Mobbin screens opened","0","refused by the injection-taint gate, 2026-09-08"],["Placement findings from primary docs","5 rows","exhibit 21, PRODUCT-BRIEF:379-385"],["Query groups exhibit 21 already answers","4 of 6","AI at rest :381, off switch :382, review placement :383, context scoping :384"],["Query groups it does not answer","2 — launcher/onboarding, pricing/upsell","4 of the 10 queries, :391 and :396"],["Global AI off-switch precedent","Zed after 412 reactions, VS Code after 30, Telegram after 181","exhibit 21, :382"],["Prototype screens built","9","seen by nobody outside this session, GAPS:27"],["Cost to run","one fresh session","GAPS:39"]]}],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Buy both in week 0: our four numbers, the Obsidian comparison, all ten queries","what":"Everything on the measurement list runs before the tests start.","gains":["Produces a speed number nobody is currently claiming","No screen is designed without a reference"],"costs":["Two days plus a session, out of a two-week window","Six of the ten queries re-derive what exhibit 21 already establishes"],"system":"A benchmark harness over the application, which does not exist yet.","screens":"Feeds S0, S4, S11 and the pricing page.","money":"None beyond time."},{"k":"b","label":"Our four numbers, plus the four queries exhibit 21 cannot answer","what":"Measure the app against itself in hours, and run only the launcher, onboarding, pricing and upsell queries.","gains":["Hours, not days, and aimed where no primary source answers","Answers whether ten strangers can use the build at all"],"costs":["No competitor speed claim available if a headline needs one","The review panel and settings screens keep only vendor-text references"],"system":"A small app benchmark; no new corpus.","screens":"S0 launcher and the pricing page.","money":"None."},{"k":"c","label":"Neither: exhibit 21 stands and five real people beat both benchmarks","what":"Skip both measurements and rely on the five-second screenshot test in weeks 1-2.","gains":["Frees the session and the two days","Real reactions outrank a reference library"],"costs":["The launcher and pricing page are designed with no external reference at all","No falsifiable performance commitment survives in §9"],"system":"The four published measures are dropped.","screens":"None.","money":"None."},{"k":"d","label":"Both, after the two-week tests, so the borrows answer what confused real people","what":"The benchmarks run once the five-second test has said which screens fail.","gains":["Best-targeted use of both","Avoids buying references for screens that get cut"],"costs":["The screens the test judges are built before the benchmark informs them","Pushes measurement past the go/no-go"],"system":"No change now.","screens":"None yet.","money":"None."}],"rec":"b","recCase":["Six of the ten queries ask about conventions exhibit 21 already establishes from the incumbents' own text, and vendor text beats a screenshot of the same behaviour.","Our own four numbers cost hours and answer whether a stranger can use the thing, which is the week-10 question. The Obsidian comparison costs two days and answers a marketing question nobody is asking.","Guard the quadratic regardless of who benchmarks. A 41-second regex on a keystroke path is a defect, not a benchmark input."],"flip":"If any tested headline claims speed, the Obsidian comparison becomes mandatory before that headline ships.","linked":["R1"],"sources":["docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:233","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:296","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:375","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:379","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:381","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:382","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:383","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:387","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:391","docs/PRODUCT-BRIEF.md:396","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:27","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:39","docs/GAPS-2026-09-08.md:43","docs/research/agent-reports-2026-08-30/r15-e4-performance.md","merged: R13"]}];
